choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Howard Stern began his tenure at WNBC in New York City in 1982, where he hosted the afternoon drive show. He remained at the station until he was fired in 1985.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 159}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:08:08.216309+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000101, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Celebrities_4096", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Neil Hamburger is played by which comedian?\n\nOptions: \nA. Gregg Turkington\nB. Nathan Fielder\nC. Tim Heidecker\nD. Todd Glass\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Neil Hamburger is a fictional comedic character created and portrayed by Gregg Turkington. The character is known for his awkward stand-up style and distinctive appearance, often featured in Turkington's performances and projects like \"Tom Goes to the Mayor\" and \"On Cinema.\" \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2928999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Celebrities_508", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When was Elvis Presley born?\n\nOptions: \nA. January 8, 1935\nB. July 18, 1940\nC. April 17, 1938\nD. December 13, 1931\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Elvis Presley was born on January 8, 1935, in Tupelo, Mississippi. This date is widely documented in biographies and historical records. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 124, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2904e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Celebrities_761", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What was James Coburn's last film role before his death?\n\nOptions: \nA. Monsters Inc\nB. Snow Dogs\nC. Texas Rangers\nD. American Gun\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "James Coburn's last film role before his death was in *American Gun*, released posthumously in 2002. He passed away in November 2002, and the film came out in 2005, making it his final credited role. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 163}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3428999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Celebrities_823", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which celebrity announced his presidency in 2015?\n\nOptions: \nA. Leonardo DiCaprio\nB. Donald Trump\nC. Kanye West\nD. Miley Cyrus\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is Donald Trump, who announced his candidacy for the U.S. presidency in June 2015. Although Kanye West also expressed interest in running for president, his official announcement came later, in 2020. Therefore, the most accurate answer based on the 2015 timeline is Donald Trump.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 175}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4571e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Celebrities_829", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What year was O.J. Simpson aquitted of his murder charges?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1995\nB. 1996\nC. 1992\nD. 1991\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "O.J. Simpson was acquitted of the murder charges in the criminal trial on October 3, 1995. The trial, which was highly publicized, concluded with a \"not guilty\" verdict after a lengthy jury deliberation. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 168}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3552e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Celebrities_929", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What was the cause of death for Freddie Mercury?\n\nOptions: \nA. Pneumonia\nB. HIV\nC. Brain Hemorrhage\nD. Stomach Cancer\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Freddie Mercury died from bronchial pneumonia, which was a complication resulting from his battle with AIDS. While he had been diagnosed with HIV, the immediate medical cause of his death was pneumonia.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 137}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:08:01.858902+00:00"}, "cost": 8.8e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Board Games_1314", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Angry Video Game Nerd's alter ego is \"Board James\".\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Angry Video Game Nerd, created by James Rolfe, does not have an alter ego named \"Board James.\" This name does not correspond to any known character associated with the series. The correct answer is therefore:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 88, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 138}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1248e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Board Games_1568", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"Magic: The Gathering\", what instant card has the highest converted mana cost?\n\nOptions: \nA. Assert Authority\nB. Blinkmoth Infusion\nC. Vitalizing Wind\nD.  Chant of Vitu-Ghazi\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. \n\nBlinkmoth Infusion has a converted mana cost (mana value) of 14, which is the highest among the options provided. The other cards listed have significantly lower mana costs.", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 160}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:12.906626+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0001025, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Board Games_1890", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the maximum level you can have in a single class in Dungeons and Dragons (5e)?\n\nOptions: \nA. 20\nB. 15\nC. 30\nD. 25\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In Dungeons & Dragons 5th Edition, the maximum level a character can achieve in a single class is 20. This is defined by the class advancement tables in the Player's Handbook. Multiclassing does not allow exceeding this limit per class.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 167}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.351e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Board Games_1971", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Yu-Gi-Oh, how does a player perform an Xyz Summon?\n\nOptions: \nA. Banish A Number of Monsters From Your Hand And Deck\nB. Overlay at least 2 Monsters of the Same Level\nC. Add the Monsters' Levels Together to Match the Xyz Monster\nD. Activate a Spell and Send Monsters to the Graveyard\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "To perform an Xyz Summon in Yu-Gi-Oh, a player must use two or more monsters of the same Level as Xyz Materials, which are then \"overlaid\" beneath the Xyz Monster. These materials are not sent to the graveyard but remain as overlays attached to the Xyz Monster. This process directly matches option B.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 138, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 214}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.7398e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Board Games_2127", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"Magic: The Gathering\", during the design for Planar Chaos, what color did the developers think of adding in as the sixth color?\n\nOptions: \nA. Orange\nB. Brown\nC. Purple\nD. Pink\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "During the design of *Planar Chaos* for *Magic: The Gathering*, the developers explored the idea of a sixth color, and conceptually considered purple as a potential addition, often associated with fate and alternate realities. Although never implemented, purple was the color most seriously discussed for this role. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 177}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4480999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Board Games_219", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Carcassonne is based on which French town?\n\nOptions: \nA. Paris\nB. Marseille\nC. Carcassonne\nD. Clermont-Ferrand\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question asks which French town the name \"Carcassonne\" is based on. Since \"Carcassonne\" is itself the name of a French town, the correct answer is the option that directly states this.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 151}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22