b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 9.645e-06, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Board Games_2869", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"Rich Uncle Pennybags\" from the board game \"Monopoly\" wears a monocle.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The character \"Rich Uncle Pennybags,\" also known as the Monopoly Man, is often mistakenly believed to wear a monocle, but he does not. He is depicted wearing a top hat, suit, and mustache, but never a monocle. This is a common misconception due to his stereotypical appearance as a wealthy businessman.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 166}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3903e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Board Games_3221", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Magic: The Gathering, what term for blocking was established in the Portal set?\n\nOptions: \nA. Shielding\nB. Resisting\nC. Blocking\nD. Intercepting\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The term established in the *Portal* set to describe the act of blocking was \"Intercepting.\" This was part of the set's attempt to simplify terminology for new players.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 142}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:12.335194+00:00"}, "cost": 8.8e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Board Games_3277", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Snakes and Ladders was originally created in India?\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The game Snakes and Ladders originated in ancient India, where it was known as Moksha Patam. It was used to teach moral lessons, with ladders representing virtues and snakes symbolizing vices. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 135}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1035e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Board Games_3430", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In standard Monopoly, what's the rent if you land on Park Place with no houses?\n\nOptions: \nA. $35\nB. $30\nC. $45\nD. $50\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In standard Monopoly, Park Place is a dark blue property, and its base rent with no houses is $35. This is the amount owed when landing on it if no houses or hotels are built and if the owner does not also own Boardwalk. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 173}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4139e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Board Games_3481", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Magic: The Gathering, what was a tribute card to Jamie Wakefield's late wife Marilyn, who loved horses?\n\nOptions: \nA. Vryn Wingmare\nB. Timbermare\nC. Sungrace Pegasus\nD. Loyal Pegasus\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is B. Timbermare. This card was printed as a tribute to Jamie Wakefield's late wife Marilyn, who loved horses, and it includes the nickname \"Marilyn\" in its flavor text. The card's design and sentimental details make it a well-known memorial card in the Magic: The Gathering community.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 117, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 188}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5407e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Board Games_3548", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What was the development code name for the \"Weatherlight\" expansion for \"Magic: The Gathering\", released in 1997?\n\nOptions: \nA. Decaf\nB. Mocha Latte\nC. Macchiato\nD. Frappuccino\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The development code name for the \"Weatherlight\" expansion in Magic: The Gathering was \"Mocha Latte.\" Wizards of the Coast often used coffee-themed code names for sets during that era. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 119, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3049e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Board Games_3678", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the game \"Racko\" you may pick up ANY card from the discard pile.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In the game \"Racko,\" players can only pick up the top card of the discard pile, not any card from below it. Therefore, the statement that you may pick up *any* card from the discard pile is incorrect. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 148}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2102999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Board Games_3765", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which ability from the \"Magic: The Gathering\" Scars of Mirrodin expansion involves having at least three artifacts in play?\n\nOptions: \nA. Living Weapon\nB. Imprint\nC. Metalcraft\nD. Affinity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The ability \"Metalcraft\" from the Scars of Mirrodin expansion triggers when a player controls at least three artifacts. This ability grants bonus effects to certain cards when the artifact threshold is met. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2552e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Board Games_3779", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the most challenging monster in the Dungeons & Dragons 5th Edition Monster Manual?\n\nOptions: \nA. Beholder\nB. Tarrasque\nC. Lich\nD. Displacer Beast\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Tarrasque is considered the most challenging monster in the Dungeons & Dragons 5th Edition Monster Manual, with a challenge rating (CR) of 30, the highest in the game. It is nearly unstoppable, featuring immense health, devastating attacks, and damage immunities. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 171}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Board Games_384", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Chess, the Queen has the combined movement of which two pieces?\n\nOptions: \nA. Rook and King\nB. Bishop and Rook\nC. Knight and Bishop\nD. King and Knight\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Queen in chess can move any number of squares vertically, horizontally, or diagonally, which combines the movements of the rook (horizontal and vertical) and the bishop (diagonal). The other options include pieces like the knight or king, which have different movement patterns not fully shared by the queen.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 172}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4126e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Board Games_520", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which character class in Dungeons and Dragons 5th edition gains it's powers from making a pact with a being of higher power?\n\nOptions: \nA. Sorceror\nB. Cleric\nC. Wizard\nD. Warlock\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Warlock class in Dungeons and Dragons 5th edition gains its powers by making a pact with a being of higher power, such as a fiend, fey, or other entity. This class is defined by its otherworldly patron, which grants abilities and spells in exchange for loyalty and service. The other options\u2014Sorcerer, Cleric, and Wizard\u2014derive their powers from innate magic, divine sources, or study, not pacts.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 99, "total_tokens": 211}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.7852e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Board Games_713", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many dots are on a single die?\n\nOptions: \nA. 21\nB. 15\nC. 24\nD. 18\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A standard die has six faces with the following number of dots: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, and 6. Adding these together gives 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 + 6 = 21. Therefore, the total number of dots on a single die is 21.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 178}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4928999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_101", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the Magic: The Gathering universe,  the Antiquities, Ice Age, and Alliances expansions take place on which continent?\n\nOptions: \nA. Shiv\nB. Aerona\nC. Terisiare\nD. Jamuraa\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Antiquities, Ice Age, and Alliances expansions in Magic: The Gathering are all set on the continent of Terisiare, located on the plane of Dominaria. These sets explore different time periods and events in Terisiare's history, including the Thran-Dwarven War and the Ice Age's climatic upheaval. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 189}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5623000000000003e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_1012", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which famous spy novelist wrote the childrens' story \"Chitty-Chitty-Bang-Bang\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. Graham Greene\nB. Ian Fleming\nC. John Buchan\nD. Joseph Conrad\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Ian Fleming, best known for creating James Bond, also wrote the children's book *Chitty-Chitty-Bang-Bang*, which was published in 1964. The story was later adapted into a popular musical film. Fleming is the only author among the options who wrote both spy novels and a children's story.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens"