ng to supplementary information from the Harry Potter wiki and Pottermore, his full name is Cornelius Oswald Fudge. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 161}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3257999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_1100", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the name of the gang that Ponyboy is a part of in the book, The Outsiders?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Mafia\nB. The Outsiders\nC. The Greasers\nD. The Socs\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Ponyboy is a member of a group known as the Greasers in S.E. Hinton's novel *The Outsiders*. This gang is defined by their socioeconomic status and distinct style, setting them apart from the wealthier Socs. The correct answer is C.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 172}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3981e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_1135", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the name of the protagonist of J.D. Salinger's novel Catcher in the Rye?\n\nOptions: \nA. Fletcher Christian\nB. Holden Caulfield\nC. Randall Flagg\nD. Jay Gatsby\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The protagonist of J.D. Salinger's novel *The Catcher in the Rye* is Holden Caulfield, a teenage boy known for his cynical view of the adult world. The other options are characters from different novels: Fletcher Christian from *Mutiny on the Bounty*, Randall Flagg from Stephen King's works, and Jay Gatsby from *The Great Gatsby*. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 200}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6780999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_1270", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which American author was also a budding travel writer and wrote of his adventures with his dog Charley?\n\nOptions: \nA. Ernest Hemingway\nB. John Steinbeck\nC. F. Scott Fitzgerald\nD. William Faulkner\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "John Steinbeck wrote about his cross-country road trip with his dog Charley in the book *Travels with Charley: In Search of America*. This work highlights his observations of American life during the journey. The correct answer is B.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 167}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3423e-05, "accu