outer", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2229e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2131", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which fictional English county was the setting for Thomas Hardy's novels?\n\nOptions: \nA. Barsetshire\nB. Wessex\nC. Fulchester\nD. Ambridge\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Thomas Hardy's novels are famously set in a fictional region he called Wessex, which is based on the south and southwest of England. This imaginative landscape appears in works like *Tess of the d'Urbervilles* and *Far from the Madding Crowd*. The other options are fictional counties from different literary or radio contexts.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 173}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4400000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2138", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What was the name of Captain Nemo's submarine in \"20,000 Leagues Under the Sea\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Nautilus\nB. The Neptune\nC. The Atlantis\nD. The Poseidon  \n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is A. The Nautilus is the name of Captain Nemo's submarine in Jules Verne's novel \"20,000 Leagues Under the Sea.\" It is a fictional submarine powered by electricity and is central to the story's exploration of the ocean depths. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 178}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4551999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2207", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is Ron Weasley's middle name?\n\nOptions: \nA. John\nB. Dominic\nC. Bilius\nD. Arthur\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Ron Weasley's full name is Ronald Bilius Weasley, as revealed in the Harry Potter series. His middle name \"Bilius\" comes from his uncle, Uncle Bilius, who was known for causing trouble at weddings. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 148}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2102999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_222", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the Beatrix Potter books, what type of animal is Tommy Brock?\n\nOptions: \nA. Badger\nB. Fox\nC. Frog\nD. Rabbit\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Tommy Brock is a character in Beatrix Potter's stories, specifically appearing in \"The Tale of Mr. Tod.\" He is depicted as a badger who lives in a dark, damp hole and is known for his gruff nature. \n\nThe correct answer is: \\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2957999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2241", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Stephen Chbosky wrote the book 'The Perks of Being A Wallflower'.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Stephen Chbosky is indeed the author of the novel *The Perks of Being a Wallflower*, which was published in 1999. The book is a coming-of-age story written in epistolary form and has gained widespread acclaim. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 154}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2760999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2357", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Romance of the Three Kingdoms, who was not a member of the Peach Garden Oath?\n\nOptions: \nA. Guan Yu\nB. Zhang Fei\nC. Zhao Yun\nD. Liu Bei\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Peach Garden Oath was a sworn brotherhood formed by Liu Bei, Guan Yu, and Zhang Fei at the beginning of the novel *Romance of the Three Kingdoms*. Zhao Yun, although a loyal and prominent general, did not participate in this oath. Therefore, the correct answer is Zhao Yun.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 178}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4668e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2384", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What position does Harry Potter play in Quidditch?\n\nOptions: \nA. Chaser\nB. Beater\nC. Seeker\nD. Keeper\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Harry Potter plays the position of Seeker in Quidditch, as he is known for his exceptional skill in catching the Golden Snitch. This role is central to his character throughout the series. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 142}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1416e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_241", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many Harry Potter books are there?\n\nOptions: \nA. 5\nB. 6\nC. 7\nD. 8\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "There are 7 main Harry Potter books written by J.K. Rowling, each chronicling one year at Hogwarts School of Witchcraft and Wizardry. The series begins with *Harry Potter and the Sorcerer's Stone* and concludes with *Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows*. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 157}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2974e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2418", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The novel \"Of Mice And Men\" was written by what author? \n\nOptions: \nA. Mark Twain \nB. George Orwell\nC. Harper Lee\nD. John Steinbeck \n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel \"Of Mice and Men\" was written by John Steinbeck, who is known for his works depicting the struggles of working-class Americans during the Great Depression. The story follows two migrant workers, George and Lennie, as they pursue their dream of owning a farm. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 167}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3684000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2435", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who was the original author of Frankenstein?\n\nOptions: \nA. Bram Stoker\nB. Mary Shelley\nC. H. P. Lovecraft\nD. Edgar Allan Poe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The original author of *Frankenstein* is Mary Shelley, who wrote the novel in 1818 when she was just 18 years old. The other authors listed\u2014Bram Stoker, H. P. Lovecraft, and Edgar Allan Poe\u2014are known for their contributions to Gothic and horror literature, but not for this work. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 177}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4771000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2465", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"Green Eggs and Ham\" consists of only 50 different words.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\"Green Eggs and Ham\" by Dr. Seuss is famously known for being written using only 50 distinct words. This was the result of a bet between Dr. Seuss and his publisher about how few words could be used in a children's book. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 89, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 155}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2919000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2497", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following authors was not born in England? \n\nOptions: \nA. H G Wells\nB. Arthur C Clarke\nC. Graham Greene\nD. Arthur Conan Doyle\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Arthur Conan Doyle was born in Edinburgh, Scotland, whereas the other three authors were born in England. Therefore, he is the correct choice.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 34, "total_tokens": 132}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:12.390460+00:00"}, "cost": 7.55e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2542", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What was the pen name of novelist, Mary Ann Evans?\n\nOptions: \nA. George Orwell\nB. George Bernard Shaw\nC. George Saunders\nD. George Eliot\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Mary Ann Evans used a male pen name to ensure her work was taken seriously in the 19th century literary world. The name she chose was George Eliot, under which she wrote famous novels like *Middlemarch* and *Silas Marner*. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 160}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.31e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2561", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the novel 1984, written by George Orwell, what is the name of the totalitarian regime that controls Oceania?\n\nOptions: \nA. Neo-Bolshevism\nB. Obliteration of the Self\nC. Earth Alliance\nD. INGSOC\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is D. INGSOC, which stands for \"English Socialism,\" the ideology of the totalitarian regime ruling Oceania in George Orwell's 1984. This regime enforces strict control over citizens through surveillance, propaganda, and thought control. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 121, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 183}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4791000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_258", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which famous book is sub-titled 'The Modern Prometheus'?\n\nOptions: \nA. Frankenstein\nB. Dracula\nC. The Legend of Sleepy Hollow\nD. The Strange Case of Dr. Jekyll and Mr. Hyde \n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is A. Frankenstein. Mary Shelley's novel \"Frankenstein\" is famously subtitled \"The Modern Prometheus,\" drawing a parallel between Victor Frankenstein and the Greek mythological figure who brought fire to humanity. The other options do not carry this subtitle.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 126, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 200}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6346e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2586", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the name of Sherlock Holmes's brother?\n\nOptions: \nA. Mederi Holmes\nB. Martin Holmes\nC. Herbie Hancock Holmes\nD. Mycroft Holmes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Sherlock Holmes's brother is named Mycroft Holmes, who is depicted as even more intelligent than Sherlock but less active in solving cases. This character appears in several of Sir Arthur Conan Doyle's stories, including \"The Adventure of the Greek Interpreter.\" \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 156}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2699999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2591", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows, Hermione destroyed the fourth Horcrux by stabbing it with the Sword of Gryffindor.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}\n\nThe statement is false because the fourth Horcrux was not destroyed by Hermione with the Sword of Gryffindor. The fourth Horcrux, Salazar Slytherin's locket, was destroyed by Ron Weasley, not Hermione, using the Sword of Gryffindor. Hermione destroyed Helga Hufflepuff's cup, which was the third Horcrux, using a basilisk fang.", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 192}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6213000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2637", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the Magic: The Gathering universe, which plane does the Homelands expansion take place in?\n\nOptions: \nA. Llanowar\nB. Tazeem\nC. Bant\nD. Ulgrotha\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Homelands expansion in Magic: The Gathering is set on the plane of Ulgrotha. This plane features a dark, gothic atmosphere with themes of decay and struggle. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 154}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2180999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2684", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the name of the three headed dog in Harry Potter and the Sorcerer's Stone?\n\nOptions: \nA. Spot\nB. Spike\nC. Fluffy\nD. Poofy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The three-headed dog in *Harry Potter and the Sorcerer's Stone* is named Fluffy. He guards the trapdoor leading to the chamber where the Sorcerer's Stone is hidden. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 149}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1884e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2835", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Abel Magwitch is a character from which Charles Dickens novel?\n\nOptions: \nA. Nicholas Nickleby\nB. Great Expectations\nC. The Pickwick Papers\nD. Oliver Twist\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result