ull, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3164999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2879", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the name of Eragon's dragon in \"Eragon\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. Glaedr\nB. Arya\nC. Saphira\nD. Thorn\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Eragon's dragon in the book \"Eragon\" is named Saphira. She is a blue dragon and plays a central role throughout the Inheritance Cycle. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 142}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1241999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2903", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: By what name was the author Eric Blair better known?\n\nOptions: \nA. Ray Bradbury\nB. Ernest Hemingway\nC. George Orwell\nD. Aldous Huxley\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Eric Blair was the real name of the author better known by his pen name George Orwell. He is famous for writing dystopian novels such as *1984* and *Animal Farm*. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 149}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1913000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2932", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is NOT a work done by Shakespeare?\n\nOptions: \nA. Trial of Temperance\nB. Cymbeline\nC. Titus Andronicus\nD. Measure For Measure\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is A. \"Trial of Temperance\" is not a work by William Shakespeare, while the other options\u2014Cymbeline, Titus Andronicus, and Measure for Measure\u2014are all authentic Shakespearean plays. There is no record of a Shakespeare play titled \"Trial of Temperance,\" making it the correct choice.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 178}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4754999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2992", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the \"Harry Potter\" novels, what must a Hogwarts student do to enter the Ravenclaw Common Room?\n\nOptions: \nA. Rhythmically tap barrels with a wand\nB. Speak a password\nC. Knock in sequence\nD. Answer a riddle\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "To enter the Ravenclaw Common Room in the \"Harry Potter\" novels, a student must answer a riddle posed by the door, as it does not use a password but instead tests the seeker's wit. This reflects Ravenclaw's emphasis on intelligence and wisdom. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 119, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 181}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4649000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2995", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the \"The Hobbit\", who kills Smaug?\n\nOptions: \nA. Frodo\nB. Bard\nC. Bilbo Baggins\nD. Gandalf the Grey\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In \"The Hobbit,\" Bard, a man from Lake-town, kills the dragon Smaug using a black arrow. Bilbo Baggins discovers Smaug's weak spot during their encounter, which helps Bard in the final attack. Frodo and Gandalf do not kill Smaug.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 170}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4013e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_30", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Under what pseudonym did Stephen King publish five novels between 1977 and 1984?\n\nOptions: \nA. J. D. Robb\nB. Richard Bachman\nC. Lewis Carroll\nD. Mark Twain\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Stephen King published five novels between 1977 and 1984 under the pseudonym Richard Bachman to test if he could succeed without his famous name and to publish more works than typically allowed by publishers at the time. The name Richard Bachman is well-documented as King's pen name during that period. The other options\u2014J. D. Robb (a pseudonym of Nora Roberts), Lewis Carroll, and Mark Twain\u2014are unrelated to Stephen King.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 103, "total_tokens": 218}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.8465e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3000", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The \"Berenstein Bears\" is the correct spelling of the educational children's book series' name.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct spelling of the children's book series is \"Berenstain Bears,\" not \"Berenstein Bears.\" The name is often misremembered due to a phenomenon known as the Mandela effect. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 143}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1545e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3056", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"Green Eggs And Ham\" is a book by which author?\n\nOptions: \nA. Dr. Seuss\nB. Beatrix Potter\nC. A.A. Milne\nD. Roald Dahl\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\"Green Eggs and Ham\" is a classic children's book known for its playful rhymes and whimsical illustrations, characteristic of Dr. Seuss's style. The author, whose real name is Theodor Seuss Geisel, wrote and illustrated the book under the pen name Dr. Seuss. It was published in 1960 and remains one of his most popular works.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 189}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5826e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3106", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: By what nickname is Jack Dawkins known in the Charles Dickens novel, 'Oliver Twist'?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Artful Dodger\nB. Fagin\nC. Bull\u2019s-eye\nD. Mr. Fang\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Jack Dawkins is a character in Charles Dickens' *Oliver Twist* who is famously known for his skill in pickpocketing and cleverness. He is commonly referred to by his nickname, \"The Artful Dodger,\" which reflects his cunning and agility. Fagin is the leader of the gang, Bull\u2019s-eye is Bill Sikes\u2019s dog, and Mr. Fang is a magistrate.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 200}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6751999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3157", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In The Lies of Locke Lamora, what title is Locke known by in the criminal world?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Thorn of the Marrows\nB. The Thorn of Camorr\nC. The Thorn of Emberlain\nD. The Rose of the Marrows\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In *The Lies of Locke Lamora*, Locke is known by a title that reflects his cunning and impact on the criminal underworld of Camorr. The correct title associated with him is \"The Thorn of Camorr,\" symbolizing how he pricks and disrupts the established powers. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 119, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 182}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4749e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3339", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The book \"The Little Prince\" was written by...\n\nOptions: \nA. Jane Austen\nB. Antoine de Saint-Exup\u00e9ry\nC. F. Scott Fitzgerald\nD. Miguel de Cervantes Saavedra\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The book \"The Little Prince\" was written by Antoine de Saint-Exup\u00e9ry, a French aviator and author. It was first published in 1943 and has since become one of the most beloved and translated books in the world. The other authors listed wrote different famous works but not this one.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 183}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5052e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3354", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Where does the book \"The Silence of the Lambs\" get its title from?\n\nOptions: \nA. The villain's favourite meal\nB. The main character's trauma in childhood\nC. The relation it has with killing the innocents\nD. The voice of innocent people being shut by the powerful\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The title \"The Silence of the Lambs\" refers to the protagonist Clarice Starling's traumatic memory of hearing lambs being slaughtered as a child, symbolizing her desire to protect the innocent and stop their suffering. This connects directly to her motivation and emotional drive throughout the story. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 126, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 189}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5246000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3456", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the Harry Potter universe, who does Draco Malfoy end up marrying?\n\nOptions: \nA. Astoria Greengrass\nB. Pansy Parkinson\nC. Hermione Granger\nD. Millicent Bulstrode\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Draco Malfoy marries Astoria Greengrass in the Harry Potter universe, as confirmed by J.K. Rowling in post-series interviews and writings. Astoria is the younger sister of Daphne Greengrass, a fellow Slytherin student. This makes option A the correct answer.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 180}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4751999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3490", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the name of the town in which Lily and James Potter are buried?\n\nOptions: \nA. Ottery St. Catchpole\nB. Godric's Hollow\nC. Hogsmeade\nD. Little Hangleton\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Lily and James Potter are buried in Godric's Hollow, the village where they lived before their deaths. This location is significant as it is also the birthplace of Harry Potter and the final resting place of other notable figures like Ignotus Peverell. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 172}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3951999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3516", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Alice in Wonderland, what is the name of Alice's kitten?\n\nOptions: \nA. Heath\nB. Oscar\nC. Dinah\nD. Smokey\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In *Alice's Adventures in Wonderland* by Lewis Carroll, Alice's kitten is named Dinah, who is mentioned frequently in the story as her beloved pet. The other options\u2014Heath, Oscar, and Smokey\u2014are not characters from the book. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2928999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3520", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the Lord of the Rings, who is the father of the dwarf Gimli?\n\nOptions: \nA. Dwalin\nB. Thorin Oakenshield\nC. Bombur\nD. Gloin\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The father of Gimli in The Lord of the Rings is Gloin, one of the dwarves who accompanied Thorin Oakenshield in *The Hobbit*. This is confirmed in both *The Hobbit* and *The Lord of the Rings*. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 167}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3568e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3570", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the Magic: The Gathering universe, the Fallen Empires expansion takes place on which continent?\n\nOptions: \nA. Sarpadia\nB. Shiv\nC. Terisiare\nD. Otaria\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The *Fallen Empires* expansion is set on the continent of Sarpadia, which was home to several warring empires that collapsed due to resource depletion and internal strife. The other options, such as Shiv and Terisiare, are distinct locations on the plane of Dominaria that are not the primary setting for this specific expansion.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 173}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:14.725589+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00013325, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3586", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which author co-wrote \"The Communist Manifesto\" alongside Karl Marx?\n\nOptions: \nA. Paul Lafargue\nB. Robert Owen\nC. Friedrich Engels\nD. Alexander Kerensky\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Friedrich Engels co-wrote \"The Communist Manifesto\" with Karl Marx in 1848. The pamphlet was commissioned by the Communist League and is one of the most influential political documents in history. Engels and Marx collaborated closely on many works, with Engels providing both intellectual and financial support.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 176}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4526e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3621", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What's the second book in George R. R. Martin's 'A Song of Ice and Fire' series?\n\nOptions: \nA. A Storm of Swords\nB. A Feast for Crows\nC. A Clash of Kings\nD. A Dance with Dragons\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The second book in George R. R. Martin's 'A Song of Ice and Fire' series is \"A Clash of Kings.\" The series follows the order: *A Game of Thrones*, *A Clash of Kings*, *A Storm of Swords*, *A Feast for Crows*, and *A Dance with Dragons*. Therefore, the correct answer is C.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 118, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 197}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6278e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3687", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who was the author of the 1954 novel, \"Lord of the Flies\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. Hunter Fox\nB. F. Scott Fitzgerald\nC. William Golding\nD. Stephen King\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The author of the 1954 novel \"Lord of the Flies\" is William Golding. This novel is a classic of British literature, exploring themes of civilization and savagery through the story of a group of boys stranded on an island. The correct answer is C.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 173}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4139e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_37", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the novel \"Lord of the Rings\", how many rings of power were given to the race of man?\n\nOptions: \nA. 11\nB. 9\nC. 13\nD. 5\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In \"The Lord of the Rings,\" the Rings of Power given to Men were part of a total of twenty rings: three to Elves, seven to Dwarves, and nine to Men. These nine rings eventually led to the creation of the Nazg\u00fbl when Sauron corrupted them. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 177}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.451e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_380", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is the world's best-selling book?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Lord of the Rings\nB. The Da Vinci Code\nC. The Little Prince\nD. Harry Potter and the Philosopher's Stone\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The world's best-selling book is not among the listed options in the way the question implies, but if considering standalone titles, *The Little Prince* has sold over 140 million copies worldwide, making it one of the best-selling books ever. While the Harry Potter series as a whole has sold more, the individual title listed, *Harry Potter and the Philosopher's Stone*, has sold fewer copies than *The Little Prince*. Therefore, the most accurate answer from the options is:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 105, "total_tokens": 215}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.831e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3816", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy book, the answer to life, the universe and everything else is...\n\nOptions: \nA. Loving everyone around you\nB. Chocolate\nC. 42\nD. Death\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is based on a famous plot point in *The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy* by Douglas Adams, where a supercomputer named Deep Thought calculates the Answer to the Ultimate Question of Life, the Universe, and Everything. After much anticipation, the answer revealed is simply \"42.\" This humorous and absurd result is central to the book's satire of the search for meaning.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 198}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6552e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3845", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The book \"Fahrenheit 451\" was written by whom?\n\nOptions: \nA. Stephen King\nB. R. L. Stine\nC. Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart\nD. Ray Bradbury\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The book \"Fahrenheit 451\" is a well-known dystopian novel about censorship and a future society where books are banned and burned. It was written by Ray Bradbury, a prominent American author of science fiction and fantasy literature. The other options are incorrect: Stephen King and R. L. Stine are authors of horror and children's books, respectively, and Mozart was a composer.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 196}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6439e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3886", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What book series published by Jim Butcher follows a wizard in modern day Chicago?\n\nOptions: \nA. A Hat in Time\nB. The Cinder Spires\nC. The Dresden Files\nD. My Life as a Teenage Wizard\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The book series that follows a wizard in modern-day Chicago is The Dresden Files by Jim Butcher. This series features Harry Dresden, a wizard who works as a private investigator. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 154}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2152e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3907", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What was the last message of the Dolphins in \"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. \"So long, and thanks for all the fish.\"\nB. \"Land of the brave.\"\nC. \"The answer is 42.\"\nD. \"Goodbye cruel world!\"\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The dolphins in \"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy\" left Earth just before its destruction and were known for their intelligence and appreciation of humanity. Their final message, as revealed in the story, was a humorous and poignant farewell. The correct answer is: \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 126, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 186}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4946e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_404", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In which classic novel by Mark Twain did a beggar and Prince of Wales switch clothes, and learn about social class inequality?\n\nOptions: \nA. A Modern Twain Story\nB. Wealthy Boy and the Schmuck\nC. The Prince and the Pauper\nD. Hamlet\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is C. The Prince and the Pauper, a novel by Mark Twain, tells the story of a poor beggar boy named Tom Canty and Prince Edward who switch places and experience each other's lives, highlighting disparities in social class. The novel explores themes of identity, justice, and inequality in 16th-century England.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 125, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 202}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6575e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_427", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the book series \"Odd Thomas\", Danny Jessup has what genetic disease? \n\nOptions: \nA. Spinocerebellar ataxia\nB. Adrenoleukodystrophy\nC.  Osteogenesis Imperfecta\nD. Cystic Fibrosis\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Danny Jessup is Odd Thomas's childhood friend who uses a wheelchair and suffers from extreme bone fragility with repeated fractures, which is the defining trait of osteogenesis imperfecta (brittle-bone disease). The other listed conditions produce different primary symptoms (neurodegeneration, lung/pancreatic issues, or ataxia) that do not match the character's portrayal across the novels.  \n\nThus the correct choice is C.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 238, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 324}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_444", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: J.K. Rowling completed \"Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows\" in which hotel in Edinburgh, Scotland?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Dunstane Hotel\nB. Hotel Novotel\nC. The Balmoral\nD. Sheraton Grand Hotel & Spa\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "J.K. Rowling completed \"Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows\" at The Balmoral Hotel in Edinburgh, where she famously stayed in a luxury suite to finish the final book. The hotel even commemorates this with a plaque and a suite named after her. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 119, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 180}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4548999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_478", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who wrote the children's story \"The Little Match Girl\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. Hans Christian Andersen\nB. Oscar Wilde\nC. Lewis Carroll\nD. Charles Dickens\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The story \"The Little Match Girl\" was written by Hans Christian Andersen, a Danish author known for his fairy tales. The other authors listed wrote different works: Oscar Wilde wrote \"The Happy Prince,\" Lewis Carroll wrote \"Alice's Adventures in Wonderland,\" and Charles Dickens wrote \"A Christmas Carol.\" Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 171}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4228999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_491", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who wrote the \"A Song of Ice And Fire\" fantasy novel series?\n\nOptions: \nA. George Eliot\nB. George Orwell\nC. George Lucas\nD. George R. R. Martin\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The \"A Song of Ice and Fire\" series was written by George R. R. Martin. The other authors listed are known for different works: George Eliot was a 19th-century novelist, George Orwell wrote dystopian fiction like *1984*, and George Lucas is a filmmaker known for *Star Wars*. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 180}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4925999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_521", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What was Sir Handel's original name in \"The Railway Series\" and it's animated counterpart \"Thomas and Friends?\"\n\nOptions: \nA. Eagle\nB. Swallow\nC. Kyte\nD. Falcon\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Sir Handel was originally named Falcon in \"The Railway Series\" by Rev. W. A. Awdry. The name was changed to Sir Handel when the character was introduced to avoid confusion with another character named Falcon in a different story. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 171}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3968e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_609", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is not a work authored by Fyodor Dostoevsky?\n\nOptions: \nA. Crime and Punishment\nB. Anna Karenina\nC. Notes from the Underground\nD. The Brothers Karamazov\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is B. Anna Karenina was written by Leo Tolstoy, not Fyodor Dostoevsky. The other options\u2014Crime and Punishment, Notes from the Underground, and The Brothers Karamazov\u2014are all well-known works by Dostoevsky.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 180}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4693999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_648", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The book 1984 was published in 1949.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The book *1984* by George Orwell was indeed published in 1949. This is a factual historical detail about the novel's release.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "s