e correct answer is C. Charles Dickens wrote \"A Tale of Two Cities,\" a classic novel set during the French Revolution. The other authors listed are known for different works: Charles Darwin for scientific theory, Mark Twain for American literature, and Roald Dahl for children's stories.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 160}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3187000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_725", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which is NOT a book in the Harry Potter Series?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Deathly Hallows\nB. The House Elf\nC. The Prisoner of Azkaban\nD. The Chamber of Secrets\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "B. The House Elf is not a book in the Harry Potter series, while the other options are official titles. The correct books are *The Deathly Hallows*, *The Prisoner of Azkaban*, and *The Chamber of Secrets*. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3367999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_737", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Originally, the character Charlie from Charlie and the Chocolate Factory was going to be black.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "According to Roald Dahl's widow, Liccy Dahl, the author originally envisioned Charlie Bucket as a black child. However, his agent at the time discouraged the idea, fearing it would not be well-received by readers.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 139}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:12.912318+00:00"}, "cost": 9.975e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_740", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What was the first ever entry written for the SCP Foundation collaborative writing project?\n\nOptions: \nA. SCP-173\nB. SCP-999\nC. SCP-1459\nD. SCP-001\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The first ever entry written for the SCP Foundation collaborative writing project was SCP-173. It was posted on the 4chan forum in 2007 and became the foundational piece for the entire SCP universe. This entry established the tone and format for future SCP articles.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 177}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4394e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_769", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the \"Harry Potter\" series, what is Headmaster Dumbledore's full name?\n\nOptions: \nA. Albus Percival Wulfric Brian Dumbledore\nB. Albus Valum Jetta Mobius Dumbledore\nC. Albus James Lunae Otto Dumbledore\nD. Albus Valencium Horatio Kul Dumbledore\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct full name of Headmaster Dumbledore in the \"Harry Potter\" series is Albus Percival Wulfric Brian Dumbledore, as confirmed by J.K. Rowling in interviews and writings.\n\nThis name is widely recognized and referenced in official Harry Potter sources, including the books and supplementary materials.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 144, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 227}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.8524e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_787", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these does Charlie NOT read in The Perks of Being a Wallflower?\n\nOptions: \nA. Peter Pan\nB. Hamlet\nC. The Grapes of Wrath\nD. The Great Gatsby\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Charlie reads several classic books throughout *The Perks of Being a Wallflower*, including *Hamlet*, *The Great Gatsby*, and *The Grapes of Wrath*, as part of his English class and personal growth. However, there is no mention of him reading *Peter Pan* in the novel. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 183}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5168e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_813", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following was the author of \"Username Evie\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. Joe Weller\nB. Zoe Sugg\nC. Alfie Deyes\nD. Joe Sugg\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The book \"Username Evie\" was written by Joe Sugg, who is a British YouTuber and author. It is a young adult novel released in 2018, co-written with Amelia Woodward. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 155}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2484e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_820", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Michael Crichton's novel \"Jurassic Park\", John Hammond meets his demise at the claws of which dinosaur?\n\nOptions: \nA. Velociraptor\nB. Tyrannosaurus Rex\nC. Dilophosaurus\nD. Procompsognathus\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In Michael Crichton's novel *Jurassic Park*, John Hammond is attacked and killed by a group of compies, which are *Procompsognathus*. This differs from the film adaptation, where Hammond survives. The correct answer is therefore D.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 121, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 180}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4490999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_826", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: George Orwell wrote this book, which is often considered a statement on government oversight.\n\nOptions: \nA. 1984\nB. The Old Man and the Sea\nC. To Kill a Mockingbird\nD. Catcher and the Rye\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "George Orwell is the author of *1984*, a dystopian novel that explores themes of totalitarianism and government surveillance. The book is widely recognized as a critique of oppressive government control and mass monitoring. The other options are works by different authors and do not match the context.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 117, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 180}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4607e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_83", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"Little Women\", which of the March sisters married Laurie?\n\nOptions: \nA. Amy\nB. Jo\nC. Beth\nD. Meg\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In \"Little Women,\" Amy March is the sister who marries Laurie. Jo initially has a close friendship with Laurie, but she declines his marriage proposal. Amy and Laurie eventually marry while in Europe.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 141}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1344999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_838", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Shub-Niggurath is a creature that was created by \tJ. R. R. Tolkien in his novel \"The Lord of The Rings\".\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Shub-Niggurath was not created by J. R. R. Tolkien, nor does it appear in \"The Lord of the Rings.\" It is a deity in the Cthulhu Mythos, created by H. P. Lovecraft.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 163}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3255e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_933", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who wrote the young adult novel \"The Fault in Our Stars\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. Stephenie Meyer\nB. Suzanne Collins\nC. Stephen Chbosky\nD. John Green\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is D. John Green is the author of the young adult novel \"The Fault in Our Stars,\" which was published in 2012 and became a bestseller. The other authors listed wrote popular YA novels but not this one\u2014Stephenie Meyer wrote \"Twilight,\" Suzanne Collins wrote \"The Hunger Games,\" and Stephen Chbosky wrote \"The Perks of Being a Wallflower.\"\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 190}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6042000000000003e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_956", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who wrote the novel \"Moby-Dick\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. J. R. R. Tolkien\nB. William Shakespeare\nC. Herman Melville\nD. William Golding\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel \"Moby-Dick\" was written by Herman Melville and published in 1851. It is a classic of American literature, known for its exploration of obsession and the complexities of human nature. The other authors listed wrote different famous works but not this novel.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 166}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3613e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Cartoon & Animations_100", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"Gravity Falls\", what does Quentin Trembley do when he is driven out from the White House?\n\nOptions: \nA. Release 1,000 captive salamanders into the white house.\nB. Jump out the window.\nC. Leave in peace.\nD. Eat a salamander and jump out the window.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In \"Gravity Falls,\" Quentin Trembley is a fictional U.S. president known for his eccentric behavior. When driven out of the White House, he dramatically eats a salamander and jumps out the window, showcasing the show's quirky humor. This matches option D.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 132, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 193}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5472e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Cartoon & Animations_1447", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Night on Bald Mountain was one of the musical pieces featured in Disney's 1940's film Fantasia.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Night on Bald Mountain, composed by Modest Mussorgsky and arranged by Leopold Stokowski, is indeed featured in Disney's 1940 film *Fantasia*. It appears in the segment depicting a dramatic portrayal of evil and supernatural forces on Mount Triglav. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 163}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3457999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Cartoon & Animations_1448", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When did the last episode of \"Futurama\" air before returning in 2023?\n\nOptions: \nA. September 4, 2013\nB. March 28, 1999\nC. November 4, 2021\nD. December 25, 2010\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The last episode of \"Futurama\" before its 2023 return aired as part of the show's seventh season, which concluded in 2013. This final episode was broadcast on September 4, 2013, marking the end of the original run before the series was revived. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 138, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 210}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Cartoon & Animations_1695", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What ability does Princess Sofia the First have from her amulet that allows her to breathe underwater?\n\nOptions: \nA. Bubble Shield\nB. Artificial Gills\nC. Bubble Head\nD. Mermaid Transformation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The amulet worn by Princess Sofia the First grants her magical abilities, including the power to breathe underwater through a transformation. This ability is specifically tied to her turning into a mermaid when near water. Therefore, the correct answer is D, as the Mermaid Transformation allows her to survive underwater.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 171}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Cartoon & Animations_1700", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"Avatar: The Last Airbender\" and \"The Legend of Korra\", Lavabending is a specialized bending technique of Firebending.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Lavabending is indeed a specialized bending technique, but it is an advanced form of Earthbending, not Firebending. It was first demonstrated by the badger moles and later used by character