hin 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Crescent Rose is the name of Ruby Rose's weapon in RWBY, which is a high-powered scythe that can transform into a sniper rifle. It is one of the most iconic weapons in the series and is closely associated with her character. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 160}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2984e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Cartoon & Animations_2146", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"My Little Pony: Friendship is Magic\", which of these ponies represents the quality of honesty?\n\nOptions: \nA. Rarity\nB. Pinkie Pie\nC. Twilight Sparkle\nD. Applejack\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Applejack is the pony who represents the Element of Honesty in \"My Little Pony: Friendship is Magic.\" She is known for her truthful nature and strong moral character. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 148}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1667999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Cartoon & Animations_2386", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which city did Anger berate for ruining pizza in \"Inside Out\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. Minnesota\nB. Washington\nC. California\nD. San Francisco\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In the movie *Inside Out*, Anger does not specifically berate a city for ruining pizza. The scene is a humorous moment where Anger expresses frustration, but it is not directed at any real city in the context provided. However, based on popular fan discussions and misremembered quotes, the intended joke is often misattributed to San Francisco.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 174}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4558e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Cartoon & Animations_2449", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the standard frame rate for animation?\n\nOptions: \nA. 60 FPS\nB. 30 FPS\nC. 12 FPS\nD. 24 FPS\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The standard frame rate for traditional film and most animation is 24 frames per second (FPS), as it provides a smooth motion appearance while being cost-effective. Although higher frame rates like 30 or 60 FPS are used in video games and digital content, 24 FPS remains the industry standard for cinematic animation. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 191}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Cartoon & Animations_2826", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"Avatar: The Last Airbender\", which element does Aang begin to learn after being defrosted?\n\nOptions: \nA. Earth\nB. Water\nC. Fire\nD. Air\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Aang is the Avatar and was born an Airbender, so he already mastered airbending before being frozen. After being defrosted, the next element he begins to learn is waterbending, starting with Katara as his teacher. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 163}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3225999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Cartoon & Animations_3210", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Nutcracker Suite was one of the musical pieces featured in Disney's 1940's film Fantasia.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Nutcracker Suite was indeed featured in Disney's 1940 film *Fantasia*. It is one of the eight segments in the film, set to Tchaikovsky's music and visually depicting dancing flowers, insects, and fairies. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 167}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.351e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Cartoon & Animations_3253", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following films was Don Bluth both the writer, director, and producer for?\n\nOptions: \nA. Anastasia\nB. The Land Before Time\nC. All Dogs Go To Heaven\nD. Titan A.E.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Don Bluth served as the writer, director, and producer for *All Dogs Go to Heaven* (1989). While he directed the other films listed, he did not hold all three roles simultaneously for those specific productions.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 162}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:13.420307+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00010675, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Cartoon & Animations_3681", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many episodes were in season five of Samurai Jack?\n\nOptions: \nA. 13\nB. 11\nC. 12\nD. 10\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Season five of *Samurai Jack* aired in 2017 and consisted of 10 episodes. This season was a revival of the original series and was structured as a single, cohesive story arc. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 151}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2171e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Cartoon & Animations_4042", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the \"Star Wars\" universe, what species is Grand Admiral Thrawn?\n\nOptions: \nA. Pantorans\nB. Twi'lek\nC. Gungans\nD. Chiss\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Grand Admiral Thrawn is a member of the Chiss species, known for their blue skin, red eyes, and strategic brilliance. He hails from the Unknown Regions and is one of the most intelligent military leaders in the \"Star Wars\" universe. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 162}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3126e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Cartoon & Animations_675", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What town was \"Springfield\" from \"The Simpsons\" originally named after?\n\nOptions: \nA. Springfield, Illinois\nB. Springfield, Oregon\nC. Springfield, Missouri\nD. Springfield, Massachusetts\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The fictional town of Springfield in \"The Simpsons\" was inspired by Springfield, Oregon. Matt Groening, the creator of the show, named it after the town of Springfield, Oregon, which he recalled from the TV show \"Father Knows Best.\" This fact was confirmed by Groening himself in various interviews.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 174}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4326e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Cartoon & Animations_69", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Blue Danube was one of the musical pieces featured in Disney's 1940's film Fantasia.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The musical piece featured in Disney's *Fantasia* was not \"The Blue Danube,\" but rather works by composers such as Bach, Tchaikovsky, and Stravinsky. Therefore, the statement is incorrect.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 145}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:12.931325+00:00"}, "cost": 9.875e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Cartoon & Animations_835", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In The Simpsons, which war did Seymour Skinner serve in the USA Army as a Green Beret?\n\nOptions: \nA. World War 2\nB. Cold War\nC. Vietnam War\nD. World War 1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Seymour Skinner, a character from The Simpsons, is depicted as a veteran who served in the Vietnam War. This is referenced multiple times throughout the series, including flashbacks and stories about his time as a prisoner of war. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 169}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3710000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Cartoon & Animations_946", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"Gravity Falls\", the character Bill Cipher remarks that \"the universe is what?\"\n\nOptions: \nA. An illusion \nB. A hologram \nC. Corrupting\nD. A simulation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In \"Gravity Falls\", Bill Cipher says, \"The universe is a hologram, mister.\" This quote is one of his most iconic lines, reflecting his surreal and chaotic nature. The correct answer is therefore:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 154}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2355000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Comics_1300", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The \"Pepe\" meme originated from a comic drawn by Matt Furie called \"Boy's Club\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The \"Pepe\" meme originated from a character named Pepe the Frog, created by cartoonist Matt Furie in his comic \"Boy's Club.\" The comic first appeared in 2005, and the character later became a widely shared internet meme. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 161}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3344999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Comics_1888", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What are the Three Virtues of Bionicle?\n\nOptions: \nA. Work, Play, Live\nB. Forge, Build, Fight\nC. Unity, Duty, Destiny\nD. Build, Play, Change\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Three Virtues of Bionicle are central themes in the Bionicle storyline, representing the core principles that guide the characters. These virtues are explicitly stated as Unity, Duty, and Destiny throughout the lore. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{C}.", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3338999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Comics_2125", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the Homestuck Series, what is the alternate name for the Kingdom of Lights?\n\nOptions: \nA. No Name\nB. Yellow Moon\nC. Prospit\nD. Golden City\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In the Homestuck series, the Kingdom of Light is one of two moons orbiting the planet Alternia, and it is home to dream-based interactions and associated with the color yellow. The alternate name for the Kingdom of Light is \"Prospit,\" which serves as a counterpart to the Kingdom of Doom, Derse. Prospit is represented by a yellow moon and hosts the White King and various dream selves.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 90, "total_tokens": 195}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6454999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Comics_2252", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What's the weakness of american vampires (Scott Snyder's American Vampire)?\n\nOptions: \nA. Sunlight\nB. Gold\nC. Silver\nD. Wood\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In Scott Snyder's *American Vampire*, the primary weakness of American vampires is not sunlight, as they are actually resistant to it, unlike traditional vampires. Instead, their key weakness is exposure to gold, which causes them severe harm. This distinguishes them from European vampires and is a central element in the series' lore.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 167}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3887000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Comics_2349", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following rings from the DC Comics' \"Lantern Corps\" are classified as Parasitic?\n\nOptions: \nA. Indigo (Compassion)\nB. White (Life)\nC. Yellow (Fear)\nD. Green (Willpower)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The parasitic rings in the DC Comics' Lantern Corps are those that forcibly bond to their hosts, impairing their free will. Among the options, the Indigo Ring of Compassion is known to be parasitic, as it often chooses unwilling hosts and alters their emotions. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "s