"The Adventures of Tintin was created by the Belgian cartoonist Herg\u00e9, whose real name was Georges Remi. He began the series in 1929 and it became one of the most influential and popular European comics. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 153}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2428999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Comics_3416", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who was the inspiration for Cuthbert Calculus in the Tintin series?\n\nOptions: \nA. Will Morris\nB. Jacques Piccard\nC. J. Cecil Maby\nD. Auguste Picard\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The character Professor Cuthbert Calculus in the Tintin series was inspired by the Swiss physicist Auguste Piccard, a real-life scientist known for his work in high-altitude balloon flights and deep-sea exploration. Herg\u00e9, the creator of Tintin, modeled Calculus's appearance and eccentric personality on Piccard. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 183}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5138999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Comics_3437", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In what Homestuck Update was [S] Game Over released?\n\nOptions: \nA. October 25th, 2014\nB. April 8th, 2012\nC. August 28th, 2003\nD. April 13th, 2009\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The flash animation \"[S] Game Over\" was released as part of the *Homestuck* update on October 25, 2014. This date corresponds to the anniversary of the comic's start, often referred to as \"Homestuck Day.\"\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 131, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 193}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:14.971690+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00012575, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Comics_3801", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the real name of the \"Master Of Magnetism\" Magneto?\n\nOptions: \nA. Pietro Maximoff\nB. Johann Schmidt\nC. Charles Xavier\nD. Max Eisenhardt\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The real name of Magneto, also known as the \"Master of Magnetism,\" is Max Eisenhardt. This name reflects his canonical backstory in Marvel Comics, where he is a Holocaust survivor with the ability to control magnetic fields. Pietro Maximoff is Quicksilver, Johann Schmidt is Red Skull, and Charles Xavier is Professor X.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 118, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 203}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "reque