Question: Which person from \"JoJo's Bizarre Adventure\" does NOT house a reference to a band, artist, or song earlier than 1980?\n\nOptions: \nA. Jolyne Cujoh\nB. Josuke Higashikata\nC. Giorno Giovanna\nD. Johnny Joestar\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The music references in JoJo are almost exclusively Stand (or occasionally character) names drawn from bands, albums, or songs.  \n\n- Jolyne\u2019s Stone Free (Hendrix, 1966/1972), Josuke\u2019s Crazy Diamond (Pink Floyd, 1975), and Johnny\u2019s Tusk (Fleetwood Mac, 1979) are all pre-1980.  \n- Giorno\u2019s Stand is named after Prince\u2019s 1995 album The Gold Experience\u2014the only post-1980 reference among the four options.  \n\nThus the character that does not contain a pre-1980 reference is C.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 248, "output_tokens": 129, "total_tokens": 377}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0006325, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Japanese Anime & Manga_4061", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How does the character Dragowizard, Qinus Axia's from the anime \"Buddyfight\" differ between the Japanese and English dubs?\n\nOptions: \nA. Different Appearance\nB. Different Body Proportions\nC. Different Backstory\nD. Different Gender\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The character Dragowizard, Qinus Axia from \"Buddyfight,\" does not undergo significant changes like appearance, body proportions, or backstory between the Japanese and English dubs. However, some voice actors and translations may lead to perceived differences, but none of those are officially documented as major alterations. The most commonly cited minor change in anime dubs involves character gender, but in this case, no credible sources confirm such a change for this character; thus, the correct answer is likely none, but based on typical dub differences, gender changes are rare and not applicable here\u2014still, if forced to choose from options, none are accurate, but D is sometimes cited in fan discussions erroneously.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 120, "output_tokens": 145, "total_tokens": 265}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.302e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Japanese Anime & Manga_680", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the last name of Edward and Alphonse in the Fullmetal Alchemist series.\n\nOptions: \nA. Eliek\nB. Elric\nC. Elwood\nD. Ellis\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is B. Elric, as Edward and Alphonse Elric are the main characters in the Fullmetal Alchemist series. Their last name is consistently referenced throughout the anime, manga, and related media. The other options are not associated with the characters.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 164}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3384000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Japanese Anime & Manga_800", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"The Melancholy of Haruhi Suzumiya\" series, the SOS Brigade club leader is unknowingly treated as a(n) __ by her peers.\n\nOptions: \nA. Alien\nB. Time Traveler\nC. God\nD. Esper\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In \"The Melancholy of Haruhi Suzumiya,\" the SOS Brigade club leader, Haruhi Suzumiya, is unknowingly treated as a god-like being because she has the power to unconsciously reshape reality. Her peers in the club\u2014representing an alien, a time traveler, and an esper\u2014believe she is a deity due to her immense, uncontrollable abilities. This makes \"God\" the most accurate answer.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 118, "output_tokens": 97, "total_tokens": 215}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.8078000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Japanese Anime & Manga_98", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: No Game No Life first aired in 2014.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The anime *No Game No Life* first aired in April 2014. This makes the statement accurate. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 30, "total_tokens": 117}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 9.177e-06, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Music_1103", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the  Rossini opera, what was the name of 'The Barber of Seville'?\n\nOptions: \nA. Angelo\nB. Fernando\nC. Figaro\nD. Dave\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The character known as \"The Barber of Seville\" in Rossini's opera is Figaro, a clever and resourceful barber who helps the Count win Rosina's love. This opera is based on the first play of the Figaro trilogy by Pierre Beaumarchais. The correct answer is therefore:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 170}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4013e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Music_1515", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is not a wind instrument?\n\nOptions: \nA. Viola\nB. Oboe\nC. Duduk\nD. Trombone\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The viola is a string instrument played with a bow, not a wind instrument. The oboe, duduk, and trombone all require air to produce sound and are classified as wind instruments. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 148}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2074e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Music_1525", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 1993, Prince changed his name to an unpronounceable symbol because he was unhappy with his contract with Warner Bros.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}\n\nThe statement is true. In 1993, Prince adopted an unpronounceable symbol, often referred to as the \"Love Symbol,\" as his name to protest his contractual disputes with Warner Bros. This act was a form of artistic protest against the label's control over his music and output.", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 169}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3913e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Music_1526", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Scatman John's real name was John Paul Larkin.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Scatman John's real name was indeed John Paul Larkin. He adopted the stage name \"Scatman John\" due to his scat singing style and international success. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 130}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0477e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Music_1600", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these Johns was murdered by gunshots outside the Dakota in New York in 1980?\n\nOptions: \nA. John Denver\nB. John Lennon\nC. Johnny Thunders\nD. John Cascella\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "John Lennon, a former member of The Beatles, was tragically killed on December 8, 1980, outside his apartment building, the Dakota, in New York City, after being shot by Mark David Chapman. The other individuals listed\u2014John Denver, Johnny Thunders, and John Cascella\u2014were not murdered in this manner or location. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 195}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6309999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Music_1718", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the name of Rivers Cuomo's wife?\n\nOptions: \nA. Kyoko Ito\nB. Kyary Pamyu Pamyu\nC. LiSA\nD. Yoko Ono\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is A. Kyoko Ito, who is the wife of Rivers Cuomo, the lead singer of Weezer. The other options are unrelated: Kyary Pamyu Pamyu is a Japanese pop artist, LiSA is a Japanese singer, and Yoko Ono is an artist and widow of John Lennon.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 180}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4925999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Music_194", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A Caixa Malacacheta is what kind of musical instrument which is commonly used in Latin American music?\n\nOptions: \nA. Bass Drum\nB. Maraca\nC. Snare Drum\nD. Cow Bell\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A Caixa Malacacheta is a type of snare drum commonly used in Latin American music, particularly in Brazilian samba and other percussion ensembles. It produces a sharp, crisp sound due to its snare wires, similar to a military drum. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 167}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3539e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Music_2223", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many strings are there on a cello?\n\nOptions: \nA. 8\nB. 6\nC. 5\nD. 4\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A cello has four strings, which are typically tuned to C, G, D, and A. This is standard across classical and modern music.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 35, "total_tokens": 131}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0315999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Music_2589", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The 2011 movie \"The Adventures of Tintin\" was directed by Steven Spielberg.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The 2011 movie \"The Adventures of Tintin\" was indeed directed by Steven Spielberg. It is a motion-capture animated film based on the comic series by Herg\u00e9. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 141}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1344999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Music_2658", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which classical composer wrote the \"Moonlight Sonata\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. Ludvig Van Beethoven\nB. Johannes Brahms\nC. Chief Keef\nD. Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The \"Moonlight Sonata\" was composed by Ludwig van Beethoven. It is one of his most famous piano sonatas, officially titled Piano Sonata No. 14 in C-sharp minor, Op. 27, No. 2. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 162}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3184000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Music_2805", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The key of sharps does the key of G# minor contain?\n\nOptions: \nA. 5\nB. 3\nC. 0\nD. 7\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The key of G# minor is the relative minor of B major, which contains five sharps (F#, C#, G#, D#, and A#). Therefore, G# minor shares the same key signature as B major.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 146}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:18.078568+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00010025, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Music_3027", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the British term for a 64th note?\n\nOptions: \nA. Demisemiquaver\nB. Hemidemisemiquaver\nC. Semihemidemisemiquaver\nD. Semiquaver\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The British term for a 64th note is \"hemidemisemiquaver.\" This corresponds to the American term \"64th note\" and is one-eighth the duration of a quarter note. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 166}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3265000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Music_3068", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A Saxophone is a brass instrument.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A saxophone is made of brass but is classified as a woodwind instrument because it uses a reed to produce sound. Despite its material, the method of sound production defines its family. Therefore, the statement is incorrect.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 82, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 132}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0821999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Music_3338", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Pamina and Papageno are characters in what Mozart opera?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Goose of Cairo\nB. The Magic Flute\nC. The Impresario\nD. The Marriage of Figaro\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Pamina and Papageno are central characters in Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart's opera *The Magic Flute*. This opera, first performed in 1791, is a singspiel that combines spoken dialogue with musical numbers. The other options listed are also Mozart works, but do not feature these characters.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 177}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4568e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Music_3412", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to the American rapper Nelly, what should you do when its hot in here?\n\nOptions: \nA. Drink some water\nB. Take a cool shower\nC. Go skinny dipping\nD. Take off all your clothes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer refers to the popular 2002 song \"Hot in Herre\" by Nelly, where the lyrics famously state, \"It's getting hot in here, so take off all your clothes.\" This line is the chorus and central theme of the song. Therefore, the most accurate answer based on the lyrics is:\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 184}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5181000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Music_3495", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"The Genius\" is the original and secondary name of which Wu-Tang Clan member?\n\nOptions: \nA. Raekwon the Chef\nB. GZA\nC. Ol' Dirty Bastard\nD. Ghostface Killah\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Wu-Tang Clan member known as \"The Genius\" is GZA, who adopted this nickname to reflect his lyrical intelligence and intricate rhyming style. While he is also referred to as \"The RZA's brother,\" \"The Genius\" is his most recognized alias. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 175}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4251999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Music_3807", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What country did Shirley Bassey originate from?\n\nOptions: \nA. Wales\nB. Canada\nC. England\nD. America\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Shirley Bassey is a renowned singer known for performing James Bond theme songs and was born in Wales. She was born in Cardiff, the capital city of Wales, making her Welsh by origin. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 137}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1061e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Music_3856", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Typically, how many keys are on a piano?\n\nOptions: \nA. 12\nB. 88\nC. 96\nD. 24\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A standard piano has 88 keys, which includes 52 white keys and 36 black keys, spanning 7 octaves plus a few additional notes. This configuration is consistent across most modern acoustic pianos. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 152}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.23e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Music_3921", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In what year was Tchaikovsky's 1812 Overture composed?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1840\nB. 1880\nC. 1790\nD. 1812\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Tchaikovsky composed the 1812 Overture in 1880 to commemorate Russia's defense against Napoleon's invasion in 1812. The piece was written for the dedication of the Cathedral of Christ the Saviour in Moscow. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 181}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4736e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_1269", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Andrew Lloyd Webber musical \"Cats\" is based off a book of poems written by which author?\n\nOptions: \nA. Emily Dickenson\nB. Andrew Lloyd Webber\nC. T.S. Elliot\nD. Robert Frost\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The musical \"Cats\" is based on a collection of poems titled *Old Possum's Book of Practical Cats* by T.S. Eliot. Andrew Lloyd Webber adapted these poems into the famous musical. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 127, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 184}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4716999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_1327", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Macbeth, the eyes of what animals were used in the Witches' cauldron?\n\nOptions: \nA. Sharks\nB. Squids\nC. Humans\nD. Newts\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In Macbeth, the Witches' cauldron includes \"eye of newt\" as one of the ingredients in their spell. This refers to the eye of a newt, a small amphibian, used symbolically in the potion. The correct answer is therefore D.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 166}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3583999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_1614", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What was George Bizet's last opera?\n\nOptions: \nA. Les p\u00eacheurs de perles\nB. Gris\u00e9lidis\nC. Carmen\nD. Don Rodrigue\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "George Bizet's last opera was *Carmen*, completed shortly before his death in 1875. Although *Don Rodrigue* and *Gris\u00e9lidis* were later works begun after *Carmen*, they were left unfinished due to his untimely death. *Carmen* remains his final completed opera.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 179}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4913000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_1861", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is Jean ValJean's first prisoner number?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1729\nB. 9430\nC. 32769\nD. 24601\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Jean Valjean's prisoner number in *Les Mis\u00e9rables* is famously 24601. This number is repeatedly referenced throughout the novel and its adaptations. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 152}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.201e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_1925", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"Doctor Who\" star David Tennant performed in a rendition of which Shakespearean play?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Taming of the Shrew\nB. Hamlet\nC. Othello\nD. The Tempest\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "David Tennant, known for his role in \"Doctor Who,\" performed in a critically acclaimed production of *Hamlet* with the Royal Shakespeare Company in 2008. His portrayal of the titular character received widespread praise. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 163}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3080999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_2132", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In which Shakespeare play does the character Marcellus say, \"Something is rotten in the state of Denmark\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. Twelfth Night\nB. King Lear\nC. Macbeth\nD. Hamlet\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quote \"Something is rotten in the state of Denmark\" is spoken by Marcellus in *Hamlet*, reflecting the moral corruption in the Danish court. This line occurs in Act 1, Scene 4, as Marcellus and Horatio witness the ghost of King Hamlet. The correct answer is therefore:\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 180}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4838999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_2137", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these musicals won the Tony Award for Best Musical?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Color Purple\nB. American Idiot\nC. Rent\nD. Newsies\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The musical *Rent* won the Tony Award for Best Musical in 1996. The other options, while popular, did not win in that category: *The Color Purple* (a revival) won for Best Revival, *American Idiot* was nominated but did not win, and *Newsies* won for Best Musical in a revival category much later but not the original Best Musical. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 94, "total_tokens": 194}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.65e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_2864", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Les Mis\u00e9rables, who is Prison Code 24601?\n\nOptions: \nA. Javert\nB. Jean Valjean\nC. Jean Claude Van Damme\nD. Marius Pontmercy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In *Les Mis\u00e9rables*, Jean Valjean is the protagonist who is imprisoned for stealing bread and is known by the prison number 246011 (often remembered as 24601). This number becomes a symbol of his past and identity throughout the story. Javert is the inspector who pursues him, Marius is a young revolutionary, and Jean Claude Van Damme is an actor with no connection to the novel.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 99, "total_tokens": 211}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.7852e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_2941", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who wrote the award winning musical \"In The Heights\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. John Phillips Sousa\nB. Lin-Manuel Miranda\nC. Francis Scott Key\nD. Steven Sondheim\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Lin-Manuel Miranda wrote the award-winning musical \"In The Heights,\" which premiered on Broadway in 2008 and won several Tony Awards, including Best Musical. The musical showcases Miranda's signature blend of hip-hop, salsa, and traditional show tunes. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 162}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3213e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_3001", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the play Oedipus Rex, Oedipus kills his father due to jealousy in loving his mother.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is false because Oedipus kills his father, Laius, without knowing their relationship, not out of jealousy over his mother. The act occurs at a crossroads due to a quarrel, not motivated by romantic jealousy. The tragic irony lies in the fulfillment of a prophecy, not intentional familial rivalry.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 169}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4058e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_3073", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Shakespeare's play Julius Caesar, Caesar's last words were...\n\nOptions: \nA. Aegri somnia vana.\nB. Et tu, Brute? \nC. Iacta alea est!\nD. Vidi, vini, vici.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Caesar's last words in Shakespeare's play *Julius Caesar* are famously depicted as \"Et tu, Brute?\" expressing his shock at being betrayed by Brutus. While historically inaccurate, this line is central to the play's dramatic impact. The correct answer is therefore:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 118, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 180}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4578e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_3672", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Jeff Wayne's Musical Version of War of the Worlds, the chances of anything coming from Mars are...\n\nOptions: \nA. A trillion to one\nB. A million to one\nC. A hundred to one\nD. A billion to one\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is based on the iconic opening narration of Jeff Wayne's Musical Version of War of the Worlds, where the lines clearly state the odds. The narrator, Richard Burton, says: \"But the chances of anything coming from Mars are a million to one.\" This exact phrase is well known from the production.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 183}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4965e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_3818", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: IMAX stands for Image Maximum.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "IMAX stands for \"Image Maximum,\" which is a motion picture film format and a set of cinema projection standards known for high-resolution and large-screen presentations. The name directly reflects its purpose of maximizing image quality and size. Therefore, the statement is true.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 81, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 138}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1451000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_3875", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The protagonist's names in 'Who's Afraid of Virginia Woolf', George and Martha, were derived from George Washington and his wife.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is true. The names George and Martha in *Who's Afraid of Virginia Woolf?* are indeed a reference to George Washington and his wife, Martha Washington, symbolizing the myth of the American family and national ideals, which the play deconstructs. This naming choice underscores the play's themes of illusion and disillusionment.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 177}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4741999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_3947", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The World Chess Championship in Chess, Act 1 is set in which Italian city?\n\nOptions: \nA. Milan\nB. Merano\nC. Venice\nD. Rome\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The World Chess Championship in the musical *Chess* is set in Merano, a city in northern Italy. This setting is specifically referenced in the context of Act 1 of the musical. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 144}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.15e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_407", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who played \"Charlie Price\" in the musical \"Kinky Boots\" on Broadway in New York from May 26th - Aug 6th 2017?\n\nOptions: \nA. Dallon Weekes\nB. Tom Cruise\nC. Ed Sheeren\nD. Brendon Urie\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Brendon Urie, the lead singer of Panic! at the Disco, played the role of Charlie Price in the Broadway musical \"Kinky Boots\" during the specified dates in 2017. The other options\u2014Dallon Weekes, Tom Cruise, and Ed Sheeran\u2014did not perform in the show. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 128, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 197}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5988e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_4088", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who wrote the lyrics for Leonard Bernstein's 1957 Brodway musical West Side Story?\n\nOptions: \nA. Oscar Hammerstein\nB. Himself\nC. Stephen Sondheim\nD. Richard Rodgers\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The lyrics for Leonard Bernstein's 1957 Broadway musical *West Side Story* were written by Stephen Sondheim. Although Bernstein composed the music, the lyrics were crafted by Sondheim, marking one of his earliest major contributions to musical theater. Arthur Laurents wrote the book, and the collaboration brought together several prominent figures in Broadway history.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 183}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5168e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_762", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The musical \"Dirty Rotten Scoundrels\" is set in what country?\n\nOptions: \nA. Germany\nB. Sweden\nC. USA\nD. France\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The musical \"Dirty Rotten Scoundrels\" is set in the French Riviera, which is in France. The story revolves around two con men operating in a luxurious coastal setting typical of southern France. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 146}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1758e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Musicals & Theatres_830", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: After England, more Shakespeare plays are set in this present day country than in any other.\n\nOptions: \nA. United States\nB. Greece\nC. Italy\nD. France\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Shakespeare set many of his plays in Italy, including *Romeo and Juliet*, *Othello*, *The Merchant of Venice*, and *Much Ado About Nothing*. More of his plays are set in Italy than in any other country after England. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 161}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3171e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_1393", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which country does the YouTuber \"SinowBeats\" originate from?\n\nOptions: \nA. England\nB. Scotland\nC. Germany\nD. Sweden\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The YouTuber \"SinowBeats\" is known to be from Germany. Therefore, the correct option is C.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 29, "total_tokens": 121}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:20.708278+00:00"}, "cost": 6.65e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_1415", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the Star Trek universe, what color is Vulcan blood?\n\nOptions: \nA. Green\nB. Purple\nC. Blue\nD. Red\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Vulcan blood is green due to the presence of copper-based hemocyanin, which oxygenates their blood. This is consistently shown throughout the Star Trek series whenever Vulcans are injured. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 141}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1373999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_1492", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Cesar Romero played which iconic Batman villain from the 1960's TV show?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Riddler\nB. The Penguin\nC. Mr. Freeze\nD. The Joker\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Cesar Romero portrayed the Joker in the 1960s Batman TV series. He is best known for bringing a flamboyant and humorous interpretation to the character. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 150}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1867999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_1524", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Klingons respect their disabled comrades, and those who are old, injuried, and helpless.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Klingons in Star Trek culture highly value honor, strength, and bravery in battle, but they do not typically respect those who are weak, old, or disabled, as such conditions are often seen as dishonorable. They believe that true respect comes from combat and personal achievement, not from age or suffering. Therefore, the statement is inaccurate.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 170}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4274000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_1666", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"Star Trek\", what is the Ferengi's First Rule of Acquisition?\n\nOptions: \nA. Never allow family to stand in the way of opportunity\nB. Greed is Eternal\nC. Never place friendship above profit\nD. Once you have their money, you never give it back. \n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Ferengi's First Rule of Acquisition is \"Once you have their money, you never give it back.\" This rule reflects the Ferengi culture's deep emphasis on profit and financial cunning. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 126, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 173}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3646000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_1799", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: British actor David Morrissey stars as which role in \"The Walking Dead\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. Rick Grimes\nB. Daryl Dixon\nC. The Governor\nD. Negan\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "David Morrissey portrays the character known as The Governor in \"The Walking Dead.\" This role is a major antagonist in the series, particularly during the third and fourth seasons. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 144}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1413e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_2345", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"Donkey Kong Country\", why does Donkey Kong want to know the secret of the crystal coconut?\n\nOptions: \nA. He's the big kahuna.\nB. Because Diddy Kong forced him.\nC. To find out where all the bananas are.\nD. He wants to punish brutes.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question contains fictional or nonsensical elements not aligned with the actual plot of \"Donkey Kong Country.\" In the real game, Donkey Kong does not seek a \"crystal coconut,\" nor is that part of the storyline. None of the options are factually correct, but based on absurdity and common meme culture, option A (\"He's the big kahuna\") is a humorous non-sequitur often associated with Donkey Kong memes.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 127, "output_tokens": 98, "total_tokens": 225}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.8817e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_2367", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which British writer wrote for both Doctor Who and Sherlock?\n\nOptions: \nA. Toby Whithouse\nB. Phil Ford\nC. Steven Moffatt\nD. Russell T Davies\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Steven Moffat is the British writer who contributed to both *Doctor Who* and *Sherlock*. He created *Sherlock* alongside Mark Gatiss and served as showrunner for *Doctor Who* from 2010 to 2017. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 160}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a