 series. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 151}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.22e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_3308", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"Star Trek: The Next Generation\", Data is the only android in existence.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "B. False\n\nIn \"Star Trek: The Next Generation\", Data is not the only android; others include Lore, his \"brother,\" and later introduced androids like B-4 and Soong-type androids. The show establishes that while rare, Data is part of a lineage of androids created by Dr. Soong.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 164}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3761e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_3329", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Klingons once had a period of Democracy in their history, they referred to it as the \"Dark Times\".\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The idea that the Klingons had a period of democracy referred to as the \"Dark Times\" is not supported by canonical Star Trek sources. The Klingon culture is traditionally depicted as feudal and warrior-based, with no historical period of democracy mentioned in official lore. Therefore, the statement is false.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 161}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3316e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_3479", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of following is rude and dishonorable by Klingon standards?\n\nOptions: \nA. Reaching over and taking his meal\nB. Insulting and laughing at him at the dinner table\nC. Punching him and taking his ship station position\nD. Taking his D'k tahg\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Klingon culture (as depicted throughout Star Trek) prizes direct confrontation, physical challenges, and overt displays of strength as honorable behavior. By that standard, punching a rival to seize a station (C) or openly insulting someone (B) aligns with accepted norms, and seizing a personal weapon (D) is treated as a legitimate act of conquest rather than covert theft. In contrast, silently reaching across the table to take another\u2019s food (A) is passive and non-confrontational, violating Klingon etiquette that requires either explicit permission or an open challenge.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 245, "output_tokens": 116, "total_tokens": 361}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00059625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_3963", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In season one of the US Kitchen Nightmares, Gordan Ramsay tried to save 10 different restaurants. How many ended up closing afterwards?\n\nOptions: \nA. 3\nB. 0\nC. 9\nD. 6\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Out of the 10 restaurants featured in season one of the US *Kitchen Nightmares*, the majority ultimately closed despite Gordon Ramsay's interventions. While some saw temporary improvements, long-term success was rare due to deep-rooted issues. Based on follow-up reports, 9 of the 10 restaurants eventually closed.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 186}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5236e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_4094", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Game of Thrones, what continent lies across the Narrow Sea from Westeros?\n\nOptions: \nA. Easteros\nB. Essos\nC. Westereast\nD. Esuntos\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The continent across the Narrow Sea from Westeros in Game of Thrones is Essos. This region is home to cities like Braavos, Pentos, and Vaes Dothrak, and plays a major role in the series. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 157}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2713000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_421", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Naruto: Shippuden, which of the following elements is a \"Kekkei T\u014dta?\"\n\nOptions: \nA. Ice Style\nB. Any Doujutsu\nC. Particle Style\nD. Shadow Style\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In Naruto: Shippuden, a Kekkei T\u014dta is an advanced nature transformation that combines three basic nature elements. Particle Style (F\u016bton: K\u016bsenp\u016b) is a Kekkei T\u014dta, combining Fire, Wind, and Lightning Release. Ice Style and Shadow Style are Kekkei Genkai, not Kekkei T\u014dta, and Doujutsu refers to eye techniques, not elemental combinations.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 102, "total_tokens": 214}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.8152000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_744", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Klingons express emotion in art through opera and poetry.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Klingons, a fictional warrior species from *Star Trek*, are known for expressing deep emotion through intense forms of art such as opera and poetry, despite their aggressive culture. These art forms are central to Klingon culture and often depict honor, battle, and legacy. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 152}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2735e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_955", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In which state of America was the Fresh Prince of Bel-Air born and raised in?\n\nOptions: \nA. Florida\nB. California\nC. Pennsylvania\nD. New Jersey\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The character Will Smith, known as the Fresh Prince of Bel-Air, was born and raised in West Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. This is explicitly mentioned in the show's iconic opening theme song. Therefore, the correct answer is Pennsylvania.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 153}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2370999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Television_99", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Battlestar Galactica (2004), Cylons were created by man as cybernetic workers and soldiers.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In Battlestar Galactica (2004), Cylons were indeed created by humans as cybernetic beings initially designed for labor and military purposes. Over time, they evolved and rebelled against their creators. This makes the statement accurate.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2871e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_1005", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Terraria, which debuff does the ankh charm not provide immunity to?\n\nOptions: \nA. Venom\nB. Bleeding\nC. Cursed\nD. Slow\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Ankh Charm in Terraria provides immunity to many debuffs, including Venom, Bleeding, and Cursed. However, it does not grant immunity to the \"Slow\" debuff. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 150}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.21e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_1029", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the fastest speed possible in Trackmania\u00b2: Stadium?\n\nOptions: \nA. 320 km/h\nB. 100 km/h\nC. 500 km/h\nD. 1000  km/h\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In *Trackmania\u00b2: Stadium*, there is no hard-coded speed cap, and cars can reach speeds well beyond 1000 km/h using boosters or specific map mechanics. Among the provided options, 1000 km/h is the only one that reflects the game's potential for extreme velocity.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 118, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 191}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:21.808625+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000139, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_1107", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In which U.S. state is Far Cry 5's fictional setting 'Hope County' located?\n\nOptions: \nA. Montana\nB. Wyoming\nC. Idaho\nD. North Carolina\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The fictional setting of Far Cry 5, Hope County, is located in the U.S. state of Montana. The game's environment, featuring vast rural landscapes, mountains, and a strong survivalist theme, closely mirrors real-life Montana. Additionally, the developers confirmed that the setting was inspired by rural Montana.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 171}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4113e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_1110", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Night in the Woods, which instrument did Casey play?\n\nOptions: \nA. Piano\nB. Sax\nC. Drums\nD. Bass\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Casey, a character in *Night in the Woods*, is known to play the drums in the band that Mae joins. This is shown during the band practice scenes in the game. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 139}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1145e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_1150", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Gordon Freeman is said to have burnt and destroyed what food in the break room microwave?\n\nOptions: \nA. Sub Sandwich\nB. Casserole\nC. Chicken Soup\nD. Pepperoni Pizza\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In the opening sequence of *Half-Life*, Gordon Freeman can interact with a microwave in the Black Mesa break room to heat up a meal. The item inside is a foil-wrapped casserole that begins to smoke and burn if left in too long.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 157}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:22.197274+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00010925, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_1160", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Terraria, what does the Wall of Flesh not drop upon defeat?\n\nOptions: \nA. Pwnhammer\nB. Breaker Blade\nC. Picksaw\nD. Laser Rifle\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. The Picksaw is dropped by the Golem in the Lihzahrd Temple, not the Wall of Flesh. The Wall of Flesh always drops the Pwnhammer and has a chance to drop the Breaker Blade and Laser Rifle.", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 155}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:22.232499+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00010875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_1177", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which \"Fallout: New Vegas\" quest is NOT named after a real-life song?\n\nOptions: \nA. Come Fly With Me\nB. Ain't That a Kick in the Head\nC. They Went That-a-Way\nD. Ring-a-Ding Ding\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quest \"They Went That-a-Way\" is not named after a real-life song, while the others are: \"Come Fly With Me\" (Frank Sinatra), \"Ain't That a Kick in the Head\" (also Frank Sinatra), and \"Ring-a-Ding Ding\" (a phrase popularized by Sinatra and used in music). The title \"They Went That-a-Way\" is a play on old Western tropes and not a reference to a known song. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 119, "output_tokens": 104, "total_tokens": 223}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.8849e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_1451", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: David Baszucki was a co-founder of ROBLOX Corporation.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "David Baszucki is indeed a co-founder of ROBLOX Corporation, along with Erik Cassel. He has served as the CEO of the company since its inception. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 132}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.059e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_1709", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Peter Molyneux was the founder of Bullfrog Productions.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Peter Molyneux co-founded Bullfrog Productions in 1987 alongside Les Edgar. He played a key role in developing influential games like *Populous* and *Theme Park* through the company. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 142}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1677e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_177", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How much does the 'AWP' cost in Counter-Strike: Global Offensive?\n\nOptions: \nA. $4500\nB. $4750\nC. $5000\nD. $4650\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The AWP in Counter-Strike: Global Offensive costs $4750. This price has remained consistent across official game updates and patches. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 36, "total_tokens": 151}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1764999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_1781", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the \"Half-Life\" series, \"H.E.V\" stands for \"Hazardous Evasiveness Vest\"\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is incorrect. In the \"Half-Life\" series, \"H.E.V\" stands for \"Hazardous Environment Suit,\" not \"Hazardous Evasiveness Vest.\" The suit is a protective exoskeleton worn by Gordon Freeman to protect against radiation, impacts, and other environmental hazards.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3657999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_1804", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When was the Valve Corporation founded?\n\nOptions: \nA. March 22, 1997\nB. March 13, 1997\nC. August 24, 1996\nD. December 26, 1994\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Valve Corporation was founded on August 24, 1996, by former Microsoft employees Gabe Newell and Mike Harrington. This date aligns with historical records of the company's establishment before the release of their groundbreaking game, Half-Life, in 1998. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 125, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 192}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5575e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_1820", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the \"S.T.A.L.K.E.R.\" series, which of these items can't be used to lower the player's accumulated radiation?\n\nOptions: \nA. Vodka\nB. Radioprotectant\nC. Anti-rad\nD. Medkit\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In the \"S.T.A.L.K.E.R.\" series, vodka, radioprotectant, and anti-rad are all items that can reduce radiation levels. A medkit, however, is used exclusively for restoring health and does not affect radiation. Therefore, the item that cannot be used to lower radiation is the medkit.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 118, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 191}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5678e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_1875", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who is the victim mentioned in the second KG-8 incident, in Ace attorney Investigations, Case 4?\n\nOptions: \nA. Frank Sahwit\nB. Shey De Killer\nC. Deid Mann\nD. Raymond Shields\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The second KG-8 incident in *Ace Attorney Investigations: Miles Edgeworth* Case 4 involves the murder of Deid Mann, a defense attorney who was investigating the smuggling ring connected to the KG-8 cases.\n\nThis incident occurs during a train ride, where Mann is found dead after being poisoned, making him a key victim in uncovering the larger conspiracy.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 191}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5852e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_1985", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to the lore of \"Starbound\", what does the \"Colony Deed\" do when it is placed down?\n\nOptions: \nA. Sends out an advertisement for someone to move in.\nB. Materializes a new being at it's location.\nC. Teleports a random person to the location.\nD. Teleports somebody from somewhere on the planet it is placed.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Colony Deed in \"Starbound\" is used to summon a new NPC settler to populate a planet. When placed, it sends out a signal that attracts a new colonist to move in and build a home. This function aligns most closely with option A.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 140, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 200}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.594e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_2013", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the PAYDAY series, who betrayed the PAYDAY gang that got Hoxton arrested?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Dentist\nB. Hector\nC. The Elephant\nD. Vlad\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In the *PAYDAY* series, Hector is the character who betrayed the gang to the FBI, which ultimately led to Hoxton's arrest. This betrayal is a central plot point revealed during the events of *PAYDAY 2*.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 153}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:22.806874+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00010575, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_2044", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Pok\u00e9mon Sun and Moon, a male Salandit can evolve to a Salazzle.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In Pok\u00e9mon Sun and Moon, only female Salandit can evolve into Salazzle; males cannot evolve at all. This is a unique trait specific to this species in the Alola region. Therefore, the statement is false.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 145}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1803e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_2108", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In vanilla Minecraft, which of the following cannot be made into a block?\n\nOptions: \nA. Wheat\nB. Charcoal\nC. Coal\nD. String\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In vanilla Minecraft, coal (option C) crafts into coal blocks, wheat (option A) crafts into hay bales, and string (option D) crafts into wool blocks. Charcoal shares many properties with coal but is a separate item with its own internal ID, and it has no dedicated storage block recipe (or compatibility with the coal block recipe). This leaves charcoal as the only item among the options that cannot be formed into a block.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 219, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 311}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00050375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_216", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Splatoon, what is the age that inklings can freely change between squid and humanoid forms?\n\nOptions: \nA. 10\nB. 13\nC. 16\nD. 14\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In the lore of the Splatoon series, Inklings gain the ability to freely transform between their humanoid and squid forms when they reach the age of 14. This milestone is a significant part of their development and is often referenced in the game's supplemental materials.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 168}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:21.933592+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00011825, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_2184", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"The Witness\", how many lasers must be activated to get into the mountain area?\n\nOptions: \nA. 8\nB. 5\nC. 12\nD. 7\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In \"The Witness\", players must activate a total of 11 laser panels to unlock the entrance to the mountain, but the final requirement to open the gate involves activating 7 of the 11 colored laser beams. The confusion often comes from the distinction between panels solved and lasers activated. The correct number needed specifically to unlock the mountain path is 7.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 183}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5254999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_2195", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: By how many minutes are you late to work in \"Half-Life\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. 60\nB. 30\nC. 15\nD. 5\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In the opening sequence of \"Half-Life,\" the tram announcement explicitly states that Gordon Freeman is 30 minutes late for his shift at the Black Mesa Research Facility. Therefore, the correct option is B.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 148}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:20.882340+00:00"}, "cost": 9.7e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_2238", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which one of these nations was added to Civilization V with the \"Gods & Kings\" expansion?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Ottomans\nB. The Zulu\nC. The Kongo\nD. The Netherlands\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The \"Gods & Kings\" expansion for *Civilization V* introduced nine new civilizations, including the Netherlands, the Celts, and the Maya. The Ottomans were part of the base game, while the Zulu and the Kongo were added in later expansions.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 163}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:21.584302+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0001145, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_2314", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Why were only only 300,000 copies of Uniracers were produced?\n\nOptions: \nA. It didn't sell well due to poor review scores\nB. DMA Designs was sued by Pixar, preventing more copies from being produced\nC. No public information is available\nD. There was a disagreement between DMA Designs and Nintendo\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is B. DMA Designs was sued by Pixar, preventing more copies from being produced. Pixar claimed that the unicycling racers in Uniracers resembled the characters from their short film \"Red's Dream,\" leading to a lawsuit that limited the game's production. This legal issue is widely cited as the reason for the limited release.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 135, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 213}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.7384999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_235", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many obsidian blocks are required to build a nether portal in Minecraft?\n\nOptions: \nA. 14\nB. 13\nC. 16\nD. 10\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A standard Nether portal requires a minimum of 10 obsidian blocks to form a 4x5 frame with the corners removed. While larger portals can be built, 10 is the smallest possible configuration.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 149}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:22.563137+00:00"}, "cost": 9.725e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_2381", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which city hosted the CS:GO Dreamhack Open 2015?\n\nOptions: \nA. Atlanta\nB. Cologne\nC. London\nD. Cluj-Napoca\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The CS:GO Dreamhack Open 2015 was held in Cluj-Napoca, Romania. This event took place in October 2015 and was one of the notable tournaments in the CS:GO competitive calendar that year. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 160}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3042e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_2445", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Terraria, you can craft the Cell Phone pre-hardmode.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Cell Phone requires the PDA, which includes the Fisherman's Pocket Guide, Weather Radio, and Sextant\u2014all of which are obtained from Angler quests. Since these items can be acquired regardless of world progression, the Cell Phone can indeed be crafted in pre-hardmode.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 148}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:21.665210+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00011575, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_2562", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"Magicka\", which two elements are combined to cast the spell, \"Nullify\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. Arcane + Shield\nB. Arcane + Life\nC. Lightning + Life\nD. Lightning + Shield\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In \"Magicka\", the spell \"Nullify\" is created by combining the Arcane and Shield elements. This defensive spell blocks incoming projectiles and certain spells. The correct combination is Arcane + Shield.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 160}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2752e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_2600", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Need For Speed Most Wanted (2005), what do you drive at the beginning of the career mode?\n\nOptions: \nA. Ford Mustang\nB. Nissan 240SX\nC. BMW M3 GTR\nD. Porsche 911 Turbo\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "At the beginning of the career mode in Need for Speed: Most Wanted (2005), the player starts with a BMW M3 GTR, which is used in the introductory race against Razor. This car is later taken from the player, prompting the journey to build a new one. The correct answer is therefore:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 121, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 192}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5691e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_261", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Without enchantments, which pickaxe in minecraft mines blocks the quickest.\n\nOptions: \nA. Obsidian\nB. Iron\nC. Golden \nD. Diamond\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The speed at which a pickaxe mines blocks in Minecraft depends on its material's mining speed. Without enchantments, a golden pickaxe has the fastest mining speed, even though it is less durable. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 149}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2087e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_2634", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What ingredients are required to make a cake in Minecraft?\n\nOptions: \nA. Milk, Sugar, and Wheat\nB. Milk, Sugar Cane, Egg, and Wheat\nC. Milk, Sugar, Egg, and Wheat\nD. Milk, Bread, Egg, and Wheat\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In Minecraft, to craft a cake, you need 3 milk, 2 sugar, 1 egg, and 3 wheat. These ingredients are arranged in a specific pattern in the crafting grid. The correct answer is C, as it lists all the required ingredients accurately.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 121, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 182}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4690999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_2681", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the Portal series, Aperture Science was founded under what name in the early 1940s?\n\nOptions: \nA. Aperture Science Innovators\nB. Aperture Fixtures\nC. Wheatley Laboratories\nD. Aperture Lavatories\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Aperture Science was originally founded as Aperture Fixtures, a company that manufactured shower curtains and lighting fixtures. The name \"Aperture Fixtures\" reflects its beginnings in architectural fixtures before transitioning into scientific research. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 117, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3107e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_270", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The creeper in Minecraft was the result of a bug while implementing which creature?\n\nOptions: \nA. Chicken\nB. Zombie\nC. Cow\nD. Pig\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The creeper in Minecraft was accidentally created when Markus Persson (Notch) was trying to implement a pig, but a coding error caused the model to be stretched incorrectly. This unexpected result led to the iconic creeper design. The creature was then repurposed into a hostile mob.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 162}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3358e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_2820", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Each piece in Tetris is called a tetris.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Each piece in Tetris is actually called a \"tetromino,\" not a \"tetris.\" The term \"Tetris\" refers to the game itself, not the individual pieces. Therefore, the statement is incorrect.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 148}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1957999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_2897", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Mirror's Edge Catalyst takes place in the City of...?\n\nOptions: \nA. Diamonds\nB. Glass\nC. Purity\nD. Mirrors\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Mirror's Edge Catalyst takes place in the City of Glass, a futuristic urban environment controlled by a corporate regime. The city's name reflects its sleek, transparent architecture and themes of surveillance and control. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 142}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1416e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_29", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What does Solid Snake use to hide himself with?\n\nOptions: \nA. Cloaking Device\nB. Metal Crate\nC. Cardboard Box\nD. Cardboard cut-out\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Solid Snake famously uses a cardboard box to hide himself in the Metal Gear series, often crawling behind or under it to avoid detection. This has become an iconic and humorous element of the franchise. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 145}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1599999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_2933", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: TF2: Sentry rocket damage falloff is calculated based on the distance between the sentry and the enemy, not the engineer and the enemy\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The sentry gun's rocket damage falloff in Team Fortress 2 is determined by the distance from the sentry to the target, not the engineer. This means that even if the engineer is far from the sentry, the damage falloff depends solely on where the sentry is located relative to the enemy. Therefore, the statement is correct.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 178}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4812999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_330", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"Minecraft\", gold tools are faster than diamond tools.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Gold tools in \"Minecraft\" are actually faster than diamond tools when it comes to mining speed, despite being less durable. However, they break much more quickly, which makes them less practical for extended use. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 135}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0977e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_3601", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"Team Fortress 2\", how much health does a scout have when overhealed?\n\nOptions: \nA. 195\nB. 225\nC. 215\nD. 185\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In \"Team Fortress 2\", the Scout has a base health of 125. When overhealed, he can reach up to 150% of his base health, which is 125 \u00d7 1.5 = 187.5, rounded down to 185. Therefore, the maximum overhealed health for a Scout is 185.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 199}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6652000000000003e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_3612", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Sid Meier's Civilization V, which World Wonder can only be built in cities on or next to a desert?\n\nOptions: \nA. Alhambra\nB. Petra\nC. The Pyramids\nD. Mausoleum of Maussollos\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is Petra, as it requires the city to be on or adjacent to a desert tile. This unique requirement is part of Petra's gameplay mechanic, giving bonuses related to trade routes. Other wonders like The Pyramids or Alhambra do not have such a desert-specific placement rule.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 119, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 185}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5049e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_3660", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What level do you have to be to get a service medal on CS:GO?\n\nOptions: \nA. 20\nB. 40\nC. 50\nD. 30\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In CS:GO, service medals are awarded at specific rank milestones based on your profile level. A service medal is granted every 10 levels, with unique medals at certain tiers. The first major milestone for a service medal is at level 40.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3397e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_3715", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the \"Ace Attorney\" series, what is the relationship between Apollo Justice and Trucy Wright?\n\nOptions: \nA. They're co-workers\nB. They're friends\nC. They're half-siblings\nD. They're both attorneys\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Apollo Justice and Trucy Wright are part of the Wright & Co. Law Offices, where they work together under Phoenix Wright. While they are close friends and act like siblings, it is later revealed in the series that they are not biologically related. However, they are considered half-siblings due to their shared connection to Phoenix Wright and their familial bond, though this is more symbolic than biological.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 200}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6665e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_3753", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Minecraft, which two items must be combined to craft a torch?\n\nOptions: \nA. Wood and Fire\nB. Wood and Coal\nC. Stick and Coal\nD. Stick and Fire\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "To craft a torch in Minecraft, you need one stick and one unit of coal or charcoal. The combination of stick and coal is the correct recipe. Fire is not a craftable item and cannot be combined in a crafting grid.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 156}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2584e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_3760", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If a \"360 no-scope\" is one full rotation before shooting, how many rotations would a \"1080 no-scope\" be?\n\nOptions: \nA. 3\nB. 2\nC. 5\nD. 4\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A \"360 no-scope\" refers to one full rotation, which is 360 degrees. Therefore, a \"1080 no-scope\" would be 1080 \u00f7 360 = 3 full rotations. \n\nThe correct answer is $\\boxed{A}$.", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 162}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2835999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_381", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Terraria, which of these items is NOT crafted at a Mythril Anvil?\n\nOptions: \nA. Ankh Charm\nB. Venom Staff\nC. Sky Fracture\nD. Orichalcum Tools\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}.\n\nThe Ankh Charm is crafted at a Tinkerer's Workshop, not a Mythril Anvil. The other items listed are all valid recipes that require a Mythril or Orichalcum Anvil to craft.", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:23.022251+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000107, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_3815", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"PUBATTLEGROUNDS\" which ammo type does the M24 use?\n\nOptions: \nA. 5.56mm\nB. 7.62mm\nC. 9mm\nD. .300 Magnum\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In \"PUBG: Battlegrounds,\" the M24 sniper rifle is chambered for 7.62mm ammunition. While it is a powerful bolt-action rifle, it does not use the .300 Magnum, which is exclusive to the AWM.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 173}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:22.815363+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0001195, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_4031", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which occupation did John Tanner, the main protagonist for Driver and Driver 2, had before turning into an undercover cop?\n\nOptions: \nA. Taxi Driver\nB. Racing Driver\nC. Delivery Driver\nD. Getaway Driver\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "John Tanner, the protagonist of Driver and Driver 2, was a getaway driver before becoming an undercover cop. This background explains his exceptional driving skills central to the gameplay. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 151}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1881e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_4047", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the maximum HP in Terraria?\n\nOptions: \nA. 500\nB. 400\nC. 100\nD. 1000\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The maximum health in Terraria is 500, which is achieved by using 15 Life Crystals (to reach 400 HP) followed by 20 Life Fruits (to add an additional 100 HP).\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 156}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:22.243076+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00010775, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_5", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the Half-Life universe, the Black Mesa Research Facility is located in which US state?\n\nOptions: \nA. New Mexico\nB. Nevada\nC. Arizona\nD. Wyoming\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Black Mesa Research Facility in the Half-Life universe is located in New Mexico. This is consistent with real-world references, as the name \"Black Mesa\" corresponds to a region in New Mexico, and the game's lore aligns with this setting. Additionally, the surrounding desert environment and government research themes match the Southwestern U.S. landscape.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 176}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4670999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_51", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the ARPG \"Path of Exile,\" what is the highest amount of sockets that an item can have?\n\nOptions: \nA. 8\nB. 5\nC. 6\nD. 4\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In \"Path of Exile,\" the maximum number of sockets an item can have is 6. This limit applies to most gear types, and items with 6 linked sockets (6L) are highly sought after for optimal skill gem setups. Some items can have fewer sockets depending on type and modifiers, but 6 is the highest possible.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 184}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5239e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_536", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The walls of the Goldenrod City Gym in \"Pok\u00e9mon Gold and Silver\" are arranged in the shape of which Pok\u00e9mon?\n\nOptions: \nA. Bulbasaur\nB. Pikachu\nC. Clefairy\nD. Pidgey\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The layout of the Goldenrod City Gym in \"Pok\u00e9mon Gold and Silver\" is designed to resemble the silhouette of a Clefairy. This unique floor plan is a notable detail of the Johto region's Normal-type gym.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 159}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:23.641006+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00010475, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_563", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Rust, how many Timed Explosive Charges does it take to destroy a Ladder Hatch?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2\nB. 1\nC. 5\nD. 3\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In Rust, a Ladder Hatch is a relatively weak structure compared to other building components. It requires only 1 Timed Explosive Charge (C4) to be destroyed. This is due to its low health and blast resistance.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2726e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_62", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What ingredient is NOT used to craft a cake in Minecraft?\n\nOptions: \nA. Wheat\nB. Bread\nC. Milk\nD. Egg\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In Minecraft, a cake is crafted using wheat, sugar, milk, and eggs. Bread is not an ingredient used in the cake recipe. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 135}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0774e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_637", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the title of the game \"Luigi's Mansion\", what is the only letter to not appear with a pair of eyes in it?\n\nOptions: \nA. n\nB. m\nC. s\nD. i\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question refers to the stylized logo of the game Luigi's Mansion, in which certain letters are drawn with a pair of eyes inside their shapes for visual effect. The letters M (two arches), n (two curves), and s (two loops) are each wide enough to contain such eyes in the logo, while the narrow vertical stroke of i has no room for a pair. Thus the answer must be option D.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 231, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 319}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00050875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_647", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Amazon acquired Twitch in August 2014 for $970 million dollars.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Amazon acquired Twitch in August 2014 for $970 million. This acquisition was officially announced in August 2014 and finalized later that year. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 134}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0732e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_707", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the \"Ace Attorney\" series, who was the truly responsible of the forging of the autopsy report of the pivotal IS-7 incident?\n\nOptions: \nA. Manfred Von Karma\nB. Bansai Ichiyanagi\nC. Gregory Edgeworth\nD. Tateyuki Shigaraki\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}.\n\nBansai Ichiyanagi, acting as the head of the Prosecutorial Investigation Committee, orchestrated the forgery of the autopsy report to ensure a conviction in the IS-7 incident. Manfred von Karma utilized this forged report, but the act of falsifying the document was directed by Ichiyanagi.", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 120, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 189}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:22.874496+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0001335, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_81", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Doki Doki Literature Club was developed in Japan.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Doki Doki Literature Club was developed by Dan Salvato, an American developer, not in Japan. Although the game has a Japanese art style and is inspired by visual novels from Japan, it was created independently in the United States. Therefore, the statement is false.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 171}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.42e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_853", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Night In The Woods, where does Gregg work?\n\nOptions: \nA. Ol' Pickaxe\nB. Food Donkey\nC. Video Outpost \"Too\"\nD. Snack Falcon\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Gregg, a character in *Night in the Ages*, works at the Snack Falcon, a convenience store in the game. This location is central to several interactions between Gregg and the protagonist, Mae. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 151}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2084e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_866", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What mainly favored rifle is used by the Terrorists in Counter Strike: Global Offensive?\n\nOptions: \nA. AK-74\nB. CZ-75 AUTO\nC. M4A4\nD. AK-47\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In Counter Strike: Global Offensive, the Terrorists are typically associated with using the AK-47 as their primary assault rifle. This weapon is iconic for the Terrorist faction and is more powerful than the M4A4 used by Counter-Terrorists. The AK-74 and CZ-75 AUTO are not standard primary rifles for Terrorists in the game.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 193}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6051999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Entertainment: Video Games_984", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In RuneScape, one must complete the \"Dragon Slayer\" quest before equipping Rune Platelegs.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In RuneScape, equipping Rune Platelegs requires a Defence level of 40, but there is no quest requirement to wear them. The \"Dragon Slayer\" quest is unrelated to the equipment requirements for Rune Platelegs. Therefore, the statement is false.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 154}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2645e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1030", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sitting for more than three hours a day can cut two years off a person's life expectancy.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Sitting for prolonged periods has been linked to various health risks, and some studies suggest that excessive sedentary behavior can negatively impact life expectancy. While the exact figure may vary, research has indicated that sitting for more than three hours daily could be associated with a reduction in life expectancy by approximately two years. Therefore, the statement is supported by scientific evidence.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 170}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4303e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1046", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The US emergency hotline is 911 because of the September 11th terrorist attacks.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "B. False\n\nThe US emergency hotline 911 was established in 1968, long before the September 11th terrorist attacks in 2001. The number was chosen for its simplicity and ease of memorization, not because of the date of the attacks.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 160}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3274e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1066", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Francis Bacon died from a fatal case of pneumonia while he was attempting to preserve meat by stuffing a chicken with snow.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Francis Bacon did indeed die from pneumonia after conducting an experiment involving stuffing a chicken with snow to test the effects of cold on preservation. This incident occurred in 1626, and he reportedly contracted the illness during the experiment, which ultimately led to his death. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 163}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3487e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1133", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The \u201cfairy\u201d type made it\u2019s debut in which generation of the Pokemon core series games?\n\nOptions: \nA. 4th\nB. 2nd\nC. 7th\nD. 6th\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Fairy type was introduced in the 6th generation of Pok\u00e9mon games, which includes Pok\u00e9mon X and Y. It was added to balance the dominance of Dragon-type Pok\u00e9mon in previous generations. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 154}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2210000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1178", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Waluigi's first appearance was in what game?\n\nOptions: \nA. Super Smash Bros. Ultimate\nB. Wario Land: Super Mario Land 3\nC. Mario Party (N64)\nD. Mario Tennis 64 (N64)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Waluigi made his first appearance in *Mario Tennis 64* for the Nintendo 64, where he was introduced as a doubles partner for Wario. He was created specifically for the Mario sports game series and did not appear in earlier titles like *Wario Land: Super Mario Land 3* or *Super Smash Bros. Ultimate*. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 118, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 196}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6178e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1196", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which iconic Disneyland attraction was closed in 2017 to be remodeled as a \"Guardians of the Galaxy\" themed ride?\n\nOptions: \nA. Peter Pan's Flight\nB. Pirates of the Caribbean\nC. The Haunted Mansion\nD. Twilight Zone Tower of Terror\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is D. The Twilight Zone Tower of Terror at Disney California Adventure was closed in 2017 and rethemed to become \"Guardians of the Galaxy \u2013 Mission: Breakout!\".\n\nThis change was part of Disney's effort to incorporate more Marvel-themed attractions into its parks.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 123, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 190}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5433e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1285", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following languages does NOT use gender as a part of its grammar?\n\nOptions: \nA. Polish\nB. Turkish\nC. German\nD. Danish\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Turkish does not use grammatical gender, unlike Polish, German, and Danish, which all have gendered noun systems. While Danish has common and neuter genders, and Polish and German have multiple grammatical genders, Turkish is gender-neutral in its grammar.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 157}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2858000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1357", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which company did Valve cooperate with in the creation of the Vive?\n\nOptions: \nA. Oculus\nB. Google\nC. Razer\nD. HTC\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Valve collaborated with HTC to develop the Vive, a virtual reality headset that combines Valve's software and tracking technology with HTC's hardware expertise. The partnership was announced in 2015 and led to the release of the HTC Vive. Other companies listed, such as Oculus, Google, and Razer, were not directly involved in the creation of the Vive.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 175}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4716e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_136", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The mitochondria is the powerhouse of the cell.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement \"The mitochondria is the powerhouse of the cell\" is a widely used phrase to describe the organelle's role in producing energy (ATP) through cellular respiration. This function is essential for powering various cellular activities. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 145}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2064e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1366", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Dihydrogen Monoxide was banned due to health risks after being discovered in 1983 inside swimming pools and drinking water.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Dihydrogen Monoxide is a scientific name for water (H\u2082O), and while the statement sounds alarming, it is a well-known hoax used to highlight scientific illiteracy. The claim that it was banned due to health risks is false, as water is essential for life and not banned. The mention of its \"discovery\" in 1983 in pools and drinking water is also misleading.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 90, "total_tokens": 192}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6241999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1392", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What kind of aircraft was developed by Igor Sikorsky in the United States in 1942?\n\nOptions: \nA. Stealth Blimp\nB. Space Capsule\nC. Helicopter\nD. Jet\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Igor Sikorsky is known for his pioneering work in vertical flight technology. In 1942, he developed the VS-300, one of the first successful helicopters in the United States. This makes the correct answer the helicopter.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 166}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3439e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1399", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Earth is located in which galaxy?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Galaxy Note\nB. The Black Hole\nC. The Milky Way Galaxy\nD. The Mars Galaxy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Earth is located in the Milky Way Galaxy, which is a barred spiral galaxy containing our Solar System. The other options are either fictional or incorrect astronomical terms. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 38, "total_tokens": 136}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0758e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_145", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The new One World Trade Center in Manhattan, New York City was designed by which architect? \n\nOptions: \nA. Michael Arad\nB. Bjarke Ingels\nC. David Childs\nD. Fumihiko Maki\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The new One World Trade Center was designed by David Childs of Skidmore, Owings & Merrill. While other architects contributed to the World Trade Center site, Childs was the lead designer for the main tower. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3194e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1450", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Apple co-founder Steve Jobs died from complications of which form of cancer?\n\nOptions: \nA. Stomach\nB. Liver\nC. Bone\nD. Pancreatic\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Steve Jobs died from complications of a rare form of pancreatic cancer, specifically a pancreatic neuroendocrine tumor, which is different from the more common and aggressive types of pancreatic cancer. This type of tumor tends to grow more slowly and is less aggressive. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 156}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2699999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1472", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these Marvel games was released on the Playstation 2?\n\nOptions: \nA. Silver Surfer\nB. Wolverine: Adamantium Rage\nC. Spider-Man 2\nD. Howard the Duck\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is C. Spider-Man 2 was released on the PlayStation 2 in 2004 and was a popular action-adventure game based on the Marvel superhero. The other options\u2014Silver Surfer, Wolverine: Adamantium Rage, and Howard the Duck\u2014were released on different platforms, not the PS2.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 179}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4826e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1504", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Sun rises from the North.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Sun does not rise from the North; it rises in the East due to Earth's rotation. This statement is therefore incorrect.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 81, "output_tokens": 33, "total_tokens": 114}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 9.051e-06, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1528", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Kissing someone for one minute burns about 2 calories.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Kissing for one minute typically burns around 2 to 3 calories, depending on intensity and individual metabolism. This makes the statement generally accurate. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 86, "output_tokens": 36, "total_tokens": 122}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 9.706e-06, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1617", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which river flows through the Scottish city of Glasgow?\n\nOptions: \nA. Tweed\nB. Clyde\nC. Tay\nD. Dee\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The River Clyde flows through the Scottish city of Glasgow, playing a significant role in the city's industrial history and development. The other rivers listed\u2014Tweed, Tay, and Dee\u2014flow through different parts of Scotland. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 150}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2303e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1639", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Nephelococcygia is the practice of doing what?\n\nOptions: \nA. Sleeping with your eyes open\nB. Finding shapes in clouds\nC. Swimming in freezing water\nD. Breaking glass with your voice\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Nephelococcygia refers to the practice of seeing shapes or figures in clouds. The term originates from Aristophanes' play \"The Birds\" and is derived from Greek roots meaning \"cloud\" and \"cuckoo.\" This whimsical term describes the imaginative act of identifying patterns in cloud formations.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 179}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4710000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1642", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Before the 19th Century, the \"Living Room\" was originally called the...\n\nOptions: \nA. Sitting Room\nB. Parlor\nC. Loft\nD. Open Room\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Before the 19th century, the term \"parlor\" was commonly used to describe the room in a home where guests were received and entertained. This space eventually became known as the living room in later centuries. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 153}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2312999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1674", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When someone is cowardly, they are said to have what color belly?\n\nOptions: \nA. Blue\nB. Green\nC. Red\nD. Yellow\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The phrase \"yellow-bellied\" is a common idiom used to describe someone who is cowardly. This expression has been widely used in English to associate the color yellow with fear or lack of courage. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 152}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2387e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1699", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which musician has collaborated with American producer Porter Robinson and released the 2016 song \"Shelter\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. Mat Zo\nB. Zedd\nC. deadmau5\nD. Madeon\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is D. Madeon collaborated with Porter Robinson to release the song \"Shelter\" in 2016. The track was part of a joint project between the two artists under the name \"Shelter.\" This collaboration was accompanied by an anime music video and a world tour.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 176}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4410000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1758", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When you cry in space, your tears stick to your face.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In microgravity, tears do not fall due to the lack of strong gravitational pull. Instead, they form small blobs that can stick to the eyes or face. This phenomenon has been reported by astronauts.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 133}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0777e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1807", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One of Donald Trump's 2016 Presidential Campaign promises was to build a border wall between the United States and Mexico.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "One of Donald Trump's central promises during his 2016 Presidential Campaign was to build a wall along the U.S.-Mexico border and have Mexico pay for it. This pledge received widespread media attention and was a key part of his immigration platform. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 164}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.35e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1812", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: NCIS stands for \"Navy Corps Investigative Service\"\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is false because NCIS stands for \"Naval Criminal Investigative Service,\" not \"Navy Corps Investigative Service.\" The correct name reflects its role in criminal investigations within the U.S. Navy and Marine Corps.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 86, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 137}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1205999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1839", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The New York Times slogan is, \u201cAll the News That\u2019s Fit to\u2026\u201d\n\nOptions: \nA. Print\nB. Look\nC. Digest\nD. Read\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The New York Times slogan is \"All the News That\u2019s Fit to Print.\" This phrase has been associated with the newspaper for over a century, emphasizing its commitment to publishing reliable and appropriate news. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 144}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1558e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1866", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a 1994 CBS interview, Microsoft co-founder Bill Gates performed what unusual trick on camera?\n\nOptions: \nA. Jumping over an office chair\nB. Jumping backwards over a desk\nC. Standing on his head\nD. Typing on a keyboard during a handstand\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In a 1994 interview with Connie Chung, Bill Gates famously demonstrated his agility by jumping over an office chair. This moment became an iconic piece of pop culture history regarding the Microsoft co-founder.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 119, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 167}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:58:20.699210+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00010175, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1891", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The vapor produced by e-cigarettes is actually water.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The vapor produced by e-cigarettes is not just water; it contains nicotine, flavorings, and other chemicals. While it may appear similar to water vapor, it is an aerosol with potentially harmful substances. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 132}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0763999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1894", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to Sherlock Holmes, \"If you eliminate the impossible, whatever remains, however improbable, must be the...\"\n\nOptions: \nA. Truth\nB. Answer\nC. Source\nD. Cause\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "According to Sherlock Holmes, the full quote is: \"If you eliminate the impossible, whatever remains, however improbable, must be the truth.\" This famous line emphasizes logical deduction and is central to Holmes's method of reasoning. The correct answer is therefore the option that matches \"truth.\"\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 166}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3583999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_192", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which logical fallacy means to attack the character of your opponent rather than their arguments?\n\nOptions: \nA. Tu quoque\nB. Post hoc ergo propter hoc\nC. Argumentum ad populum\nD. Ad hominem\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is D. Ad hominem refers to attacking the character or traits of a person instead of addressing the substance of their argument. This fallacy diverts attention from the actual issue to discredit the individual making the argument. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3222999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1927", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sciophobia is the fear of what?\n\nOptions: \nA. Bright lights\nB. Transportation\nC. Shadows\nD. Eating\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Sciophobia is the fear of shadows. The term comes from the Greek word \"skia,\" meaning shadow, and \"phobos,\" meaning fear. This phobia involves an irrational or excessive fear of shadows or dark areas.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 162}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3097e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1957", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When one is \"envious\", they are said to be what color?\n\nOptions: \nA. Yellow\nB. Green\nC. Red\nD. Blue\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "When someone is \"envious,\" they are said to be green, as in the phrase \"green with envy.\" This expression is commonly used in English to describe jealousy or envy. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 140}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1187e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1962", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What was the nickname given to the Hughes H-4 Hercules, a heavy transport flying boat which achieved flight in 1947?\n\nOptions: \nA. Noah's Ark\nB. Spruce Goose\nC. Trojan Horse\nD. Fat Man\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Hughes H-4 Hercules was nicknamed the \"Spruce Goose\" due to its construction primarily from wood, including spruce, and its massive size. Despite skepticism, it successfully flew once in 1947, piloted by Howard Hughes. The nickname became widely recognized, even though it was somewhat derisive at the time.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 191}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5736e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_1974", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Amsterdam Centraal station is twinned with what station?\n\nOptions: \nA. Paris Gare du Nord\nB. London Liverpool Street\nC. Frankfurt (Main) Hauptbahnhof\nD. Brussels Midi\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Amsterdam Centraal station is twinned with London Liverpool Street station, as part of a sister station agreement to promote cultural and operational exchanges. This partnership reflects the strong rail connections and historical ties between the Netherlands and the UK. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 161}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2968e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_199", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to the 2014-2015 Australian Bureau of Statistics, what percentage of Australians were born overseas?\n\nOptions: \nA. 20%\nB. 13%\nC. 7%\nD. 28%\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "According to the 2014-2015 Australian Bureau of Statistics data, approximately 28% of Australians were born overseas. This reflects Australia's significant level of immigration and cultural diversity. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3136e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2020", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A pasodoble is a type of Italian pasta sauce.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A pasodoble is not a type of Italian pasta sauce; it is actually a Spanish dance and musical form. The statement is therefore incorrect. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 86, "output_tokens": 36, "total_tokens": 122}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 9.706e-06, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2071", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 2010, Twitter and the United States Library of Congress partnered together to archive every tweet by American citizens.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The partnership between Twitter and the Library of Congress was announced in 2010 to archive all public tweets, not just those by American citizens, and included global data. However, the Library of Congress later changed its approach due to the volume and scope of data, eventually discontinuing the full archiving effort. Therefore, while the partnership existed, the statement is misleading because it did not exclusively archive American tweets and was later scaled back.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 94, "total_tokens": 193}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6428999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2106", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The British organisation CAMRA stands for The Campaign for Real Ale.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The British organisation CAMRA is indeed an acronym for The Campaign for Real Ale, which was founded in 1971 to promote and protect traditional cask ale and pubs in the UK. The statement is accurate and widely recognized. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 141}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1577e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2136", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In aerodynamics, which force pushes an object upwards?\n\nOptions: \nA. Drag\nB. Weight\nC. Thrust\nD. Lift\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The force that pushes an object upwards in aerodynamics is lift. Lift is generated by the motion of the object through the air, typically by wings. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 37, "total_tokens": 131}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0374e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2175", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: After how many years would you celebrate your crystal anniversary?\n\nOptions: \nA. 20\nB. 15\nC. 25\nD. 10\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The crystal anniversary is traditionally celebrated after 15 years of marriage. Among the options, 15 years corresponds to the crystal milestone. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 35, "total_tokens": 136}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0671e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2181", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Five dollars is worth how many nickles?\n\nOptions: \nA. 100\nB. 50\nC. 69\nD. 25\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Five dollars is equal to 500 cents. Since each nickel is worth 5 cents, dividing 500 by 5 gives 100 nickels. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 148}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.19e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2216", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The average woman is 5 inches / 13 centimeters shorter than the average man.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The average height difference between men and women is approximately 5 inches (about 13 centimeters) in many populations, with men being taller on average. This statistic is supported by numerous anthropometric studies across various countries. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 151}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2403e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2255", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Slovakia is a member of European Union-\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Slovakia joined the European Union in 2004 as part of the EU's enlargement. It is a full member and also part of the Eurozone, using the euro as its currency. Therefore, the statement is correct.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 82, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 136}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1222e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2273", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Computer manufacturer Compaq was acquired for $25 billion dollars in 2002 by which company?\n\nOptions: \nA. Dell\nB. Toshiba\nC. Asus\nD. Hewlett-Packard\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is D. Hewlett-Packard acquired Compaq in 2002 in a highly publicized merger valued at $25 billion, marking a major consolidation in the personal computer industry. This move significantly expanded HP's presence in the PC market. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 170}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3867999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2304", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"27 Club\" is a term used to refer to a list of famous actors, musicians, and artists who died at the age of 27.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The \"27 Club\" refers to a group of famous musicians and artists who died at the age of 27, including figures like Jimi Hendrix, Janis Joplin, and Kurt Cobain. While not an official club, the term is widely used in popular culture to highlight this tragic coincidence.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 177}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4626e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2311", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Scotland voted to become an independent country during the referendum from September 2014.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Scotland held a referendum on independence in September 2014, but the majority of voters chose to remain part of the United Kingdom. Therefore, Scotland did not vote to become an independent country. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 139}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1231999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2347", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"Number 16 Bus Shelter\" was a child's name that was approved by the New Zealand government.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The name \"Number 16 Bus Shelter\" was submitted as a joke and gained media attention, but it was not officially approved by the New Zealand government. New Zealand has strict naming laws, and such a name would not be legally permitted. Therefore, the statement is false.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3015999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2399", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Directly between the Washington Monument and the Reflecting Pool is a memorial to which war?\n\nOptions: \nA. Vietnam War\nB. American Civil War\nC. World War II\nD. American Revolutionary War\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The World War II Memorial is located on the eastern end of the Reflecting Pool, placing it directly between the pool and the Washington Monument. The other memorials listed are located in different areas of the National Mall.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 150}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:58:19.947127+00:00"}, "cost": 9.75e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2423", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Vietnam's national flag is a red star in front of a yellow background.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is incorrect because Vietnam's national flag features a large yellow star centered on a red background, not a yellow background. The red symbolizes revolution and bloodshed, while the yellow star represents the five main classes in Vietnamese society.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 89, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 142}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1619e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2429", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When someone is inexperienced they are said to be what color?\n\nOptions: \nA. Yellow\nB. Red\nC. Green\nD. Blue\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "When someone is inexperienced, they are often described as \"green,\" symbolizing inexperience or newness. This term originates from early 20th-century slang, where \"green\" referred to someone immature or unseasoned. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 147}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1974000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2463", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Area 51 is located in which US state?\n\nOptions: \nA. Arizona\nB. New Mexico\nC. Nevada\nD. Utah\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Area 51 is a highly classified U.S. Air Force facility located within the Nevada Test and Training Range. It is situated in southern Nevada, northwest of Las Vegas. The correct answer is therefore:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 140}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1274e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2467", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Frank Lloyd Wright was the architect behind what famous building?\n\nOptions: \nA. Sydney Opera House\nB. The Space Needle\nC. Villa Savoye\nD. The Guggenheim\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Frank Lloyd Wright was the architect known for designing the Guggenheim Museum in New York City. The other options were designed by different architects: the Sydney Opera House by J\u00f8rn Utzon, the Space Needle by John Graham, and Villa Savoye by Le Corbusier. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 173}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4312999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_249", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The commercial UK channel ITV stands for \"International Television\".\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is incorrect. ITV stands for \"Independent Television,\" not \"International Television.\" It was named to reflect its original structure as a network of independent regional broadcasters.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 38, "total_tokens": 123}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 9.835e-06, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2523", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the defining characteristic of someone who is described as hirsute?\n\nOptions: \nA. Funny\nB. Rude\nC. Hairy\nD. Tall\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The term \"hirsute\" is used to describe someone who has an abundance of hair. It is commonly used to refer to people, especially men, who are notably hairy. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 142}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1329e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2534", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: On average, Americans consume 100 pounds of what per second?\n\nOptions: \nA. Potatoes\nB. Donuts\nC. Cocaine\nD. Chocolate\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question is hyperbolic and likely meant to be humorous or misleading, as consuming 100 pounds of anything per second nationwide would be implausible. However, interpreting it as a per-year or per-capita average scaled up, chocolate is a commonly consumed item in large quantities in the U.S. Among the options, chocolate is the most reasonable answer, as Americans consume significant amounts of it annually.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 188}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.59e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2615", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Fields Medal, one of the most sought after awards in mathematics, is awarded every how many years?\n\nOptions: \nA. 4\nB. 5\nC. 3\nD. 6\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Fields Medal is awarded every four years to outstanding mathematicians under the age of 40. It is presented at the International Congress of Mathematicians. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 38, "total_tokens": 145}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1397e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2694", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How would one say goodbye in Spanish?\n\nOptions: \nA.  Hola\nB. Salir\nC. Au Revoir\nD. Adi\u00f3s\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\"Adi\u00f3s\" is the Spanish word for \"goodbye,\" making it the correct choice. \"Hola\" means \"hello,\" \"salir\" means \"to leave,\" and \"au revoir\" is French, not Spanish. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2987e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2722", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What country saw a world record 315 million voters turn out for elections on May 20, 1991?\n\nOptions: \nA. Poland\nB. United States of America\nC. India\nD. Soviet Union\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is India, which holds the world's largest democratic elections. On May 20, 1991, India conducted its general election with a record voter turnout of around 315 million people. This massive participation reflects the scale of India's electoral process.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 178}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4494e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2755", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Lego Group was founded in 1932.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Lego Group was indeed founded in 1932 by Ole Kirk Christiansen in Denmark. The company originally produced wooden toys and later transitioned to plastic bricks. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 86, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 126}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0106e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2839", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which film star has his statue in Leicester Square?\n\nOptions: \nA. Paul Newman\nB. Rowan Atkinson \nC. Alfred Hitchcock\nD. Charlie Chaplin\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statue in Leicester Square, London, honors Charlie Chaplin, one of the most iconic figures in film history. It was unveiled in 1981 to celebrate his contributions to cinema. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 146}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.17e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2852", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these banks are NOT authorized to issue currency notes in Hong Kong?\n\nOptions: \nA. HSBC\nB. Standard Chartered\nC. OCBC\nD. Bank of China\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The banks authorized to issue currency notes in Hong Kong are HSBC, Standard Chartered, and Bank of China. OCBC (Oversea-Chinese Banking Corporation) is not authorized to issue Hong Kong currency notes. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 159}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2913e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2894", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Popcorn was invented in 1871 by Frederick W. Rueckheim in the USA where he sold the snack on the streets of Chicago.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is false because popcorn was not invented in 1871 by Frederick W. Rueckheim. Popcorn has been used for centuries, with evidence of its consumption dating back to ancient indigenous peoples in the Americas. Frederick Rueckheim, however, did create a caramel-coated popcorn mixture later known as Cracker Jack in the 1890s.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 82, "total_tokens": 187}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5655000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_2922", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: French is an official language in Canada.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "French is one of the two official languages of Canada, alongside English, as established by the Official Languages Act. It is widely spoken, particularly in the province of Quebec. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 82, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 122}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 9.821999999999998e-06, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_3009", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How long did it take the motorized window washers of the original World Trade Center to clean the entire exterior of the building?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1 Month\nB. 2 Months\nC. 1 Week\nD. 3 Weeks\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The motorized window-washing platforms of the original World Trade Center took approximately one month to clean the entire exterior of each tower. Given the height and surface area of the buildings, this was a significant logistical task. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3136e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_3170", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The drug cartel run by Pablo Escobar originated in which South American city?\n\nOptions: \nA. Bogot\u00e1\nB. Cali\nC. Medell\u00edn\nD. Quito\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The drug cartel led by Pablo Escobar was based in Medell\u00edn, Colombia. This city became infamous during the 1980s and early 1990s for its association with the Medell\u00edn Cartel. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2812999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_3252", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Linus Pauling, one of the only winners of multiple Nobel Prizes, earned his Nobel Prizes in Chemistry and what?\n\nOptions: \nA. Economics\nB. Physics\nC. Peace\nD. Physiology/Medicine\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Linus Pauling won the Nobel Prize in Chemistry in 1954 and the Nobel Peace Prize in 1962 for his activism against nuclear weapons testing. He is one of the few individuals to win multiple Nobel Prizes in different fields. The correct answer is C.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 174}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4210000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_3266", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: You can legally drink alcohol while driving in Mississippi.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "It is illegal to drink alcohol while driving in Mississippi. Open container laws prohibit drivers and passengers from consuming alcohol in a vehicle. Therefore, the statement is false.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 38, "total_tokens": 122}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 9.764e-06, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_3306", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Romanian belongs to the Romance language family, shared with French, Spanish, Portuguese and Italian. \n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Romanian is indeed a Romance language, derived from Latin, just like French, Spanish, Portuguese, and Italian. It is the most spoken Romance language in Eastern Europe. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 134}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0702999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_3325", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"Resident Evil 3\", how many inventory slots does Jill have at the start of the game?\n\nOptions: \nA. 10\nB. 8\nC. 6\nD. 12\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In the original 1999 version of \"Resident Evil 3: Nemesis,\" Jill Valentine begins the game with 10 inventory slots. This capacity remains the same throughout the game unless the player is playing the 2020 remake, which features a different inventory system.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 170}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:58:25.047627+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00012375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_3340", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: It is automatically considered entrapment in the United States if the police sell you illegal substances without revealing themselves.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "B. False\n\nSelling illegal substances without revealing themselves does not automatically constitute entrapment; entrapment involves inducing someone to commit a crime they would not have otherwise committed. Simply failing to disclose police identity during a sting does not meet the legal definition of entrapment. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 159}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3116e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_3365", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: There are 86400 seconds in a day.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "There are 24 hours in a day, 60 minutes in an hour, and 60 seconds in a minute.  \nSo, total seconds in a day = 24 \u00d7 60 \u00d7 60 = 86400.  \nThis confirms the statement is correct.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 156}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3077e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_3373", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If someone said \"you are olid\", what would they mean?\n\nOptions: \nA. Your appearance is repulsive.\nB. You are incomprehensible/an idiot.\nC. You are out of shape/weak.\nD. You smell extremely unpleasant.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The word \"olid\" is a rare or archaic term meaning foul-smelling. If someone said \"you are olid,\" they would most likely be referring to an unpleasant odor. \n\nThus, the correct answer is: \\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 166}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3265000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_3404", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Cucumbers are usually more than 90% water.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Cucumbers are known for their high water content, which typically exceeds 90%. This makes them very hydrating and low in calories. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 88, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 131}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0547999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_3461", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The sum of all the numbers on a roulette wheel is 666.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The numbers on a standard roulette wheel range from 1 to 36. The sum of these numbers is given by the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series: $ \\frac{n(n+1)}{2} = \\frac{36 \\times 37}{2} = 666 $. Therefore, the statement is correct.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 168}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4190000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_3470", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Spoon theory is a theory, utilizing \"Spoons\" as a metaphor for energy they can use in a day.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Spoon theory is indeed a metaphor used to describe the amount of energy a person, particularly someone with a chronic illness or disability, has for daily activities, with each \"spoon\" representing a unit of energy. The theory was popularized by Christine Miserandino in an essay where she used spoons to explain the limitations of living with lupus. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 182}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5387e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_35", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When was the Declaration of Independence approved by the Second Continental Congress?\n\nOptions: \nA. June 4, 1776\nB. July 2, 1776\nC. May 4, 1776\nD. July 4, 1776\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Declaration of Independence was adopted by the Second Continental Congress on July 4, 1776, which is now celebrated as Independence Day in the United States. Although Congress voted for independence on July 2, the formal approval of the document occurred on July 4. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 127, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 196}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5917e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_3568", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: On average, at least 1 person is killed by a drunk driver in the United States every hour.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is supported by statistics from organizations like the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration (NHTSA), which indicate that alcohol-impaired driving fatalities occur at a rate of roughly one per hour in the United States.\n\nThis averages to about 28 deaths per day, aligning with annual data showing over 10,000 drunk-driving-related deaths each year.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 175}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4744999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_3575", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who founded the Khan Academy?\n\nOptions: \nA. Kitt Khan\nB. Adel Khan\nC. Ben Khan\nD. Sal Khan\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Sal Khan founded the Khan Academy, a non-profit educational organization that provides free online lessons and practice exercises. The platform started as a way for him to tutor his younger cousins and grew into a global learning resource. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 142}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1503e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_358", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Albert Einstein had trouble with mathematics when he was in school.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Albert Einstein did not have trouble with mathematics; in fact, he was quite skilled in it from a young age. The myth that he struggled with math is a common misconception. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 86, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 128}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0306000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_3604", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Great Wall of China is visible from the moon.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The claim that the Great Wall of China is visible from the moon is a common myth. In reality, it is not visible to the naked eye from the moon, and even from low Earth orbit, it is difficult to see without aid. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 140}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1535e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_3627", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: De Eemhof, Port Zelande and Het Heijderbos are holiday villas owned by what company?\n\nOptions: \nA. Yelloh Village\nB. Center Parcs\nC. Keycamp\nD. Villa Plus\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "De Eemhof, Port Zelande, and Het Heijderbos are well-known holiday parks in the Netherlands that are part of a major European holiday park operator. These parks are specifically operated by Center Parcs, which specializes in forest-based vacation villages. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 173}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4023e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_3719", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A statue of Charles Darwin sits in what London museum?\n\nOptions: \nA. Science Museum\nB. Tate\nC. British Museum\nD. Natural History Museum\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statue of Charles Darwin is located in the Natural History Museum in London, honoring his contributions to evolutionary biology. This museum is known for its focus on natural history and scientific research, making it a fitting location for Darwin's statue. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 150}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2187e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_3727", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In flight systems, what does the initialism \"TCAS\" stand for?\n\nOptions: \nA. Traffic Collision Avoidance System\nB. Traffic Communication Alert System\nC. Traffic Call-sign Abbreviation System\nD. Traffic Configuration Alignment System\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "TCAS stands for Traffic Collision Avoidance System, which is an aviation safety system designed to prevent mid-air collisions by monitoring nearby aircraft and providing alerts or resolution advisories. It operates independently of air traffic control and helps pilots maintain safe separation.  \n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 169}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3593999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_3768", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The website \"Shut Up & Sit Down\" reviews which form of media?\n\nOptions: \nA. Films\nB. Video Games\nC. Board Games\nD. Television Shows\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The website \"Shut Up & Sit Down\" is primarily known for its focus on tabletop gaming. It features reviews, videos, and commentary centered around board games. Therefore, the correct answer is C.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 148}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1870999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_3821", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If you are caught \"Goldbricking\", what are you doing wrong?\n\nOptions: \nA. Stealing\nB. Smoking\nC. Slacking\nD. Cheating\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Being \"goldbricking\" refers to pretending to work while actually slacking off or avoiding real work. It is a form of workplace idleness or laziness, not theft or cheating. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 151}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.22e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_3900", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Furby was released in 1998.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Furby was indeed first released in 1998 by Tiger Electronics. It quickly became a popular toy during the holiday season of that year. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 38, "total_tokens": 123}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 9.835e-06, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_392", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to Fair Works Australia, how long do you have to work to get Long Service Leave?\n\nOptions: \nA. 6 months\nB. 8 years\nC. 2 years\nD. 7 years\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "According to Fair Work Australia, long service leave entitlements are typically determined by state or territory laws, but generally, employees become eligible after around 7 to 10 years of continuous service. In most Australian states, the standard qualifying period is 7 years. Therefore, the most accurate answer based on common legislation is 7 years.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 183}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5138999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_3925", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The pickled gherkin was first added to hamburgers because a US health law required all fast-food to include a source of Vitamin C.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The claim that pickled gherkins were added to hamburgers due to a U.S. health law requiring a source of Vitamin C is not supported by historical evidence. There was no such law mandating Vitamin C in fast food, and gherkins were added primarily for flavor and texture. Therefore, the statement is incorrect.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 175}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4513e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_3989", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What was the name given to Japanese military dictators who ruled the country through the 12th and 19th Century?\n\nOptions: \nA. Samurai\nB. Ninja\nC. Shogun\nD. Shinobi\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is C. Shogun. Shoguns were military leaders who held de facto power in Japan from the 12th century until the 19th century, ruling in the name of the emperor. Samurai were warriors, while ninja and shinobi refer to covert agents or mercenaries, not rulers.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 183}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5052e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_4019", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"Buffalo buffalo Buffalo buffalo buffalo buffalo Buffalo buffalo.\" is a grammatically correct sentence.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The sentence \"Buffalo buffalo Buffalo buffalo buffalo buffalo Buffalo buffalo.\" is grammatically correct, using the word \"buffalo\" in different ways (as a noun, verb, and proper noun referring to the city). It relies on homonyms and syntactic structure to form a valid sentence in English.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3131999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_402", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Rolex is a company that specializes in what type of product?\n\nOptions: \nA. Watches\nB. Sports equipment\nC. Cars\nD. Computers\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Rolex is a well-known Swiss company that designs and manufactures high-end timepieces. It has built a global reputation for precision, luxury, and craftsmanship in watchmaking. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 136}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0844999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_4020", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Stagecoach owned \"South West Trains\" before losing the rights to FirstGroup and MTR in March of 2017.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is true: Stagecoach did operate \"South West Trains\" as part of a joint venture with MTR Corporation, not solely own it, and the franchise was indeed lost to FirstGroup (in a joint venture with MTR) in August 2017, not March. However, the core idea that Stagecoach operated South West Trains before losing the franchise is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 188}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5842e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_433", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 2013 how much money was lost by Nigerian scams?\n\nOptions: \nA. $12.7 Billion\nB. $95 Million\nC. $956 Million\nD. $2.7 Billion\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "According to a 2013 report by the research firm Ultrascan AGI, the total global losses attributed to Nigerian 419 scams amounted to approximately $12.7 billion. This figure represents the estimated financial impact of these advance-fee fraud schemes during that year.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 174}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:58:18.507526+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00012475, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_451", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Video streaming website YouTube was purchased in it's entirety by Facebook for US$1.65 billion in stock.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is false because YouTube was acquired by Google, not Facebook, in 2006 for $1.65 billion in stock. Facebook has never owned YouTube.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 138}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0987e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_479", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which country, not including Japan, has the most people of japanese decent?\n\nOptions: \nA. United States of America\nB. Brazil\nC. South Korea\nD. China\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The country with the largest population of Japanese descent outside of Japan is Brazil, due to significant Japanese immigration beginning in the early 20th century. Brazilian cities like S\u00e3o Paulo have large communities of Japanese descendants, making it the top country in this category. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 159}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2971e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_482", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Terry Gilliam was an animator that worked with which British comedy group?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Penny Dreadfuls\nB. The League of Gentlemen\u200e\nC. The Goodies\u200e\nD. Monty Python\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Terry Gilliam was known for his distinctive animation style and was a key member of the British comedy group Monty Python. He collaborated with the group on their television series and films, contributing surreal and whimsical animated sequences. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 162}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3009999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_543", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A scientific study on peanuts in bars found traces of over 100 unique specimens of urine.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "There is no credible scientific evidence supporting that a study found over 100 unique specimens of urine in peanuts served at bars. Such a claim is highly implausible and likely stems from misinformation or satire. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 142}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1474e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_629", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Dihydrogen Monoxide is a dangerous chemical.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Dihydrogen monoxide is a scientific name for water (H\u2082O), which is essential for life but can be dangerous in extreme circumstances, such as drowning or overhydration. However, presenting it as a \"dangerous chemical\" is often used as a hoax to highlight scientific misunderstanding. The statement is misleading, so the most accurate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 162}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3735e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_688", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Haggis is traditionally ate on Burns Night.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Haggis is indeed traditionally eaten on Burns Night, which celebrates the life and poetry of Robert Burns. The meal is a central part of the Burns Supper, often accompanied by \"Address to a Haggis.\"  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 135}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1064e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_701", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the MMO RPG \"Realm of the Mad God\", what dungeon is widely considered to be the most difficult?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Tomb of the Acient's\nB. Snake Pit\nC. The Shatter's\nD. The Puppet Master's Theater\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. While difficulty can be subjective, \"The Shatters\" is historically and widely regarded by the community as the most challenging dungeon due to its complex mechanics and high lethality. The other options are significantly easier and are often considered mid-tier or early-game content.", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 117, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 179}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:58:18.205961+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00012225, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_74", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to the United States' CDC, one in how many Americans die annually due to smoking?\n\nOptions: \nA. Twenty\nB. One hundred\nC. Ten\nD. Five\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "According to the CDC, about one in every five deaths in the United States is linked to smoking. This means approximately 1 in 5 Americans die annually due to smoking-related causes. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 118, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 168}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3378e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_753", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following card games revolves around numbers and basic math?\n\nOptions: \nA. Twister\nB. Go Fish\nC. Munchkin\nD. Uno\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question asks which card game revolves around numbers and basic math. Twister is not a card game, Go Fish is a card game but focuses on matching rather than math, and Munchkin involves dice and combat, not primarily math. Uno involves matching numbers and colors, and often requires basic numerical strategy and counting.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 169}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4029e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_799", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: You are allowed to sell your soul on eBay.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Selling a soul is not a legally recognized transaction, and eBay prohibits the sale of intangible or illegal items, including things like human organs or fictional concepts such as souls. Therefore, you are not allowed to sell your soul on eBay.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 138}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1364e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_836", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Bulls are attracted to the color red.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Bulls are actually colorblind to red and do not see the color as humans do. They react to the movement of the cape, not its color. Therefore, the statement is incorrect.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 82, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 126}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0222e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_845", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which American-owned brewery led the country in sales by volume in 2015?\n\nOptions: \nA. Miller Coors\nB. Anheuser Busch\nC. D. G. Yuengling and Son, Inc\nD. Boston Beer Company\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In 2015, D. G. Yuengling and Son, Inc. was the largest American-owned brewery by volume, as Anheuser-Busch and MillerCoors were foreign-owned at that time. While Anheuser-Busch had higher total sales, it was owned by the Belgian-Brazilian company AB InBev. Therefore, Yuengling holds the distinction of being the largest brewery that remained under American ownership.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 98, "total_tokens": 213}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:58:21.021880+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00017575, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_851", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What did the Spanish autonomous community of Catalonia ban in 2010, that took effect in 2012?\n\nOptions: \nA. Flamenco\nB. Fiestas\nC. Bullfighting\nD. Mariachi\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Spanish autonomous community of Catalonia banned bullfighting in 2010, with the law taking effect in 2012. This made Catalonia the first region in mainland Spain to outlaw the practice. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 164}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3093999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_88", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"Battle Cats\", what is Moneko / MISS Moneko's critical percentage rate?\n\nOptions: \nA. 15%\nB. 20%\nC. 10%\nD. 25%\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Battle Cats wiki and unit data list Moneko/MISS Moneko\u2019s explicit ability as a 20 % Critical Hit chance on each attack. This value is consistent across both her regular and evolved forms and matches the in-game description shown on the unit screen. Among the supplied choices, only 20 % aligns with that documented rate.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 227, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 300}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00046625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_883", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which church's interior in Vatican City was designed in 1503 by renaissance architects including Bramante, Michelangelo and Bernini?\n\nOptions: \nA. St. Peter's Basilica\nB. Catania Cathedral\nC. The Duomo of Florence\nD. St. Mark\u2019s Basilica\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The church described, located in Vatican City and designed by Renaissance architects such as Bramante, Michelangelo, and Bernini starting in 1503, is St. Peter's Basilica. These architects contributed to its construction and interior design over several centuries. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 127, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 187}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5016999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_916", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The architect known as Le Corbusier was an important figure in what style of architecture?\n\nOptions: \nA. Neoclassical\nB. Baroque\nC. Modernism\nD. Gothic Revival\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Le Corbusier was a pioneering architect who championed functional design, open floor plans, and the use of modern materials like reinforced concrete. He was a central figure in the development of Modernism in architecture during the 20th century. His \"Five Points of Architecture\" and iconic works like Villa Savoye exemplify this style.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 182}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5097e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_980", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What geometric shape is generally used for stop signs?\n\nOptions: \nA. Hexagon\nB. Circle\nC. Triangle\nD. Octagon\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Stop signs are universally recognized by their distinctive eight-sided shape. This geometric shape is an octagon, which helps drivers identify the sign even from a distance or in poor visibility. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 136}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0874e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_981", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This field is sometimes known as \u201cThe Dismal Science.\u201d\n\nOptions: \nA. Physics\nB. Politics\nC. Economics\nD. Philosophy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The term \"The Dismal Science\" is a nickname historically applied to economics, coined in the 19th century, partly due to predictions of population growth outpacing resources. It reflects early concerns about scarcity and human behavior in allocating limited resources. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 154}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2645e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_General Knowledge_990", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The bikini is named after the \"Bikini Atoll\", an island where the United States conducted tests on atomic bombs.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The bikini is indeed named after the Bikini Atoll, as the designer, Louis R\u00e9ard, chose the name in 1946 to suggest an explosive cultural impact, shortly after the U.S. began atomic testing there. The timing of the swimsuit's debut was meant to capitalize on the widespread media attention surrounding the atoll. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 175}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4629e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1057", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Japanese district Akihabara is also known by what nickname?\n\nOptions: \nA. Otaku Central \nB. Electric Town\nC. Big Eyes\nD. Moon Walk River\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Akihabara is widely known as \"Electric Town\" due to its numerous electronics shops and its historical role as a hub for electronic commerce in Tokyo. Over time, it also became a center for anime, manga, and otaku culture, but its official nickname remains tied to its electronic roots. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 169}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3942e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1120", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The flag of South Africa features 7 colours.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The flag of South Africa features six colors, not seven: red, blue, green, yellow, black, and white. The design combines these colors in a unique Y-shaped pattern. Therefore, the statement is incorrect.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 134}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0963999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_113", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Where is Hadrian's Wall located?\n\nOptions: \nA. Alexandria, Egypt\nB. Rome, Italy\nC. Carlisle, England\nD. Dublin, Ireland\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Hadrian's Wall is located in northern England, stretching from the River Tyne near Newcastle to the Solway Firth. It was built by the Romans under Emperor Hadrian to mark the northern boundary of the Roman Empire. The correct answer is Carlisle, England, as it lies along the wall's route.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 168}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3928999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1131", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Tokyo is the capital of Japan.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Tokyo is indeed the capital city of Japan. It is the political, economic, and cultural center of the country. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 81, "output_tokens": 31, "total_tokens": 112}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 8.850999999999999e-06, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1143", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is not a megadiverse country - one that harbors a high number of the earth's endemic species?\n\nOptions: \nA. Peru\nB. Thailand\nC. South Africa\nD. Mexico\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "All the listed countries are megadiverse, but Thailand is not officially recognized as one of the 17 megadiverse countries by Conservation International, unlike Peru, South Africa, and Mexico. Megadiverse countries are selected based on having high levels of biodiversity, especially endemism, and Thailand, while biodiverse, does not meet the full criteria. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 187}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5538999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1149", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The World Health Organization headquarters is located in which European country?\n\nOptions: \nA. France\nB. Switzerland\nC. Belgium\nD. United Kingdom\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The World Health Organization (WHO) headquarters is located in Geneva, Switzerland. Switzerland is known for hosting numerous international organizations and agencies. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 33, "total_tokens": 128}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0045e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1221", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: On a London Underground map, what colour is the Circle Line?\n\nOptions: \nA. Blue\nB. Red\nC. Green\nD. Yellow\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Circle Line on the London Underground map is represented by the color yellow. This distinguishes it from other lines such as the Central Line (red) or the Jubilee Line (silver). \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 140}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1245e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1317", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: New Haven is the capital city of the state of Connecticut in the United States.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is false because the capital city of Connecticut is Hartford, not New Haven. New Haven is a major city in Connecticut but does not serve as the state capital.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 130}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.039e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1511", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The formerly East-Prussian city of K\u00f6nigsberg is known as which Russian City today?\n\nOptions: \nA. Kazan\nB. Krasnodar\nC. Kaliningrad\nD. Kursk\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The city of K\u00f6nigsberg, formerly in East Prussia, became part of Russia after World War II and was renamed Kaliningrad in 1946. It is now a Russian exclave situated between Poland and Lithuania. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 163}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3138999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1545", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: St. Louis is the capital of the US State Missouri.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "St. Louis is a major city in Missouri, but it is not the capital. The capital of Missouri is Jefferson City. Therefore, the statement is false.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 86, "output_tokens": 37, "total_tokens": 123}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 9.806e-06, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1548", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Israel is 7 hours ahead of New York.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Israel is typically 7 hours ahead of New York during certain times of the year, depending on daylight saving time adjustments in both regions. However, due to differing daylight saving schedules, the time difference can vary between 6 and 7 hours. Generally, when both are not observing daylight saving, the difference is 7 hours.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 156}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3164e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1608", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: All of the following are classified as Finno-Ugric languages EXCEPT:\n\nOptions: \nA. Hungarian\nB. Finnish\nC. Estonian\nD. Samoyedic\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Finno-Ugric language family includes Hungarian, Finnish, and Estonian. Samoyedic is not part of the Finno-Ugric group but is instead a separate branch of the larger Uralic language family. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 159}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2971e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1664", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Nova Scotia is on the east coast of Canada.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Nova Scotia is indeed located on the east coast of Canada, bordered by the Atlantic Ocean. It is one of the Maritime provinces and is situated on the southeastern coast of the country. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 127}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0263999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_171", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the name of one of the Neo-Aramaic languages spoken by the Jewish population from Northwestern Iraq?\n\nOptions: \nA. Lishan Didan\nB. Hulaul\u00e1\nC. Lishana Deni\nD. Chaldean Neo-Aramaic\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. Lishana Deni is the specific Neo-Aramaic dialect historically spoken by the Jewish communities of the Zakho and Dohuk regions in Northwestern Iraq. The other options refer to dialects spoken by Jewish communities in different regions (Lishan Didan in Azerbaijan/Iran and Hulaul\u00e1 in Iranian Kurdistan) or a Christian-associated dialect (Chaldean Neo-Aramaic).", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 117, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 205}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:08:10.676251+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00016125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1770", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Harvard University is located in which city?\n\nOptions: \nA. Providence\nB. Cambridge\nC. New York\nD. Washington D.C.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Harvard University is located in Cambridge, Massachusetts. This city is directly across the Charles River from Boston and is home to several prestigious academic institutions. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 36, "total_tokens": 129}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0202999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1942", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What was the African nation of Zimbabwe formerly known as?\n\nOptions: \nA. Mozambique\nB. Zambia\nC. Rhodesia\nD.  Bulawayo\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The African nation of Zimbabwe was formerly known as Rhodesia, named after British colonialist Cecil Rhodes. It was called Southern Rhodesia during the colonial period before gaining independence in 1980. The name was changed to Zimbabwe upon independence.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 153}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2457999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1953", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Where is the fast food chain \"Panda Express\" headquartered?\n\nOptions: \nA. Fresno, California\nB. Rosemead, California\nC. San Diego, California\nD. Sacramento, California\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Panda Express is headquartered in Rosemead, California. This is where the company was founded and continues to operate its main offices. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 33, "total_tokens": 139}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0826e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1954", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Southeast Asian island of Borneo is politically divided among 3 countries.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The island of Borneo is indeed divided among three countries: Indonesia, Malaysia, and Brunei. Indonesia controls the largest portion (Kalimantan), while the Malaysian states of Sabah and Sarawak occupy the northern part, and Brunei is a small sovereign nation on the island. Therefore, the statement is correct.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 161}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.349e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_1997", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Montreal is in which Canadian province?\n\nOptions: \nA. Quebec\nB. Nova Scotia\nC. Alberta\nD. Ontario\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Montreal is the largest city in the province of Quebec and is located in the southern part of the province along the Saint Lawrence River. It is known for its French-speaking population and rich cultural heritage. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 137}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.109e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_2056", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The two largest ethnic groups of Belgium are Flemish and Walloon. \n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The two largest ethnic groups in Belgium are indeed the Flemish, who are Dutch-speaking and live in the northern region of Flanders, and the Walloons, who are French-speaking and reside in the southern region of Wallonia. This linguistic and cultural division is a key aspect of Belgium's demographic and political landscape. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 89, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 160}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3419e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_2088", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Broome is a town in which state of Australia?\n\nOptions: \nA. Northern Territory\nB. Tasmania\nC. South Australia\nD. Western Australia\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Broome is a town located in the northern part of Western Australia, known for its pearling history and proximity to the Kimberley region. It is situated along the Indian Ocean coast, which aligns with Western Australia's geography. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 155}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2716e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_2099", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following language families is the most controversial amongst modern linguists?\n\nOptions: \nA. Indo-European\nB. Dravidian\nC. Altaic\nD. Sino-Tibetan\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Altaic language family is considered the most controversial among linguists due to ongoing debates about whether the similarities among its proposed members (such as Turkish, Mongolian, and Korean) are due to genetic relationship or are the result of language contact and borrowing. While Indo-European, Dravidian, and Sino-Tibetan are widely accepted as valid language families, Altaic lacks consensus. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 192}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6125999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_2150", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: There are no deserts in Europe.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. While Europe lacks vast, arid sand seas like the Sahara, it contains several semi-arid regions and recognized deserts, such as the Tabernas Desert in Spain and the Oltenian Sahara in Romania. Therefore, the statement that there are no deserts in Europe is false.", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 77, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 141}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:08:10.523468+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00011525, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_2220", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: There is an island in Japan called \u014ckunoshima, A.K.A. \"Rabbit Island\", so named because of it's huge population of rabbits.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The island of \u014ckunoshima in Japan is indeed commonly known as \"Rabbit Island\" due to the large number of wild rabbits that inhabit it. Tourists often visit the island to interact with the rabbits, which roam freely. This makes the statement accurate.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 169}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3768000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_2346", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the county seat of King County, Washington?\n\nOptions: \nA. Seattle\nB. Skykomish\nC. Bellevue\nD. Enumclaw\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The county seat of King County, Washington, is Seattle, which is the largest city in the state and the administrative center of the county. Although other cities like Bellevue and Enumclaw are located within King County, they are not the county seat. Skykomish is a smaller town in the county and not a governmental center.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 170}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4157999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_2364", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What national museum will you find in Cooperstown, New York?\n\nOptions: \nA. National Toy Hall of Fame\nB. National Baseball Hall of Fame\nC. Metropolitan Museum of Art\nD. Museum of Modern Art\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The National Baseball Hall of Fame is located in Cooperstown, New York, and is dedicated to preserving the history of baseball in the United States. The other options listed are not located in Cooperstown. The Metropolitan Museum of Art and the Museum of Modern Art are in New York City, and while the National Toy Hall of Fame is a real institution, it is located in Rochester, New York.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 194}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6238999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_2393", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following Arab countries does NOT have a flag containing only Pan-Arab colours?\n\nOptions: \nA. United Arab Emirates\nB. Jordan\nC. Qatar\nD. Kuwait\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Pan-Arab colors are black, white, green, and red. Qatar's flag contains maroon and white, with maroon not being one of the traditional Pan-Arab colors. Therefore, Qatar does not have a flag with only Pan-Arab colors.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 160}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3042e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_2466", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Gothenburg is the capital of Sweden.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Gothenburg is not the capital of Sweden; the capital is Stockholm. Gothenburg is Sweden's second-largest city.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 83, "output_tokens": 31, "total_tokens": 114}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 8.993e-06, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_2468", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many stations does the Central Line have on the London Underground?\n\nOptions: \nA. 43\nB. 49\nC. 47\nD. 51\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Central Line on the London Underground has 49 stations. This includes stations from West Ruislip and Ealing Broadway in the west to Epping and Hainault in the east. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 156}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2439e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_2480", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which English county will you find the University of East Anglia?\n\nOptions: \nA. Norfolk\nB. Suffolk\nC. Essex\nD. Cambridgeshire\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The University of East Anglia is located in Norwich, which is in the county of Norfolk. Therefore, the correct answer is A. Norfolk.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 35, "total_tokens": 133}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0457999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_2604", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In which English county is the city of Portsmouth?\n\nOptions: \nA. Hampshire\nB. Buckinghamshire\nC. Surrey\nD. Oxfordshire\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The city of Portsmouth is located on the south coast of England and is part of the ceremonial and historic county of Hampshire. Although it is a unitary authority, it remains within the traditional boundaries of Hampshire. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 142}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1474e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_2812", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Liechtenstein does not have an airport.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Liechtenstein is a small landlocked country without an airport due to its size and mountainous terrain. It relies on nearby airports in Switzerland and Austria for air travel. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 83, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 129}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0493000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_2880", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the official German name of the Swiss Federal Railways?\n\nOptions: \nA. Schweizerische Staatsbahnen\nB. Schweizerische Nationalbahnen\nC. Bundesbahnen der Schweiz\nD. Schweizerische Bundesbahnen\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The official German name of the Swiss Federal Railways is \"Schweizerische Bundesbahnen,\" which directly translates to \"Swiss Federal Railways.\" This name reflects its status as a federal enterprise in Switzerland. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 166}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3235999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_3028", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Llanfair\u00adpwllgwyngyll\u00adgogery\u00adchwyrn\u00addrobwll\u00adllan\u00adtysilio\u00adgogo\u00adgoch is located on which Welsh island?\n\nOptions: \nA. Anglesey\nB. Bardsey\nC. Barry\nD. Caldey\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Llanfairpwllgwyngyllgogerychwyrndrobwllllantysiliogogogoch is a village located on the island of Anglesey in Wales. It is famous for having the longest place name in Europe. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 127, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 185}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4817e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_3087", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The title of the 1969 film \"Krakatoa, East_of Java\" is incorrect, as Krakatoa is in fact west of Java.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The 1969 film \"Krakatoa, East of Java\" is indeed titled incorrectly because Krakatoa is located west of Java, not east. The volcano is situated in the Sunda Strait between Java and Sumatra, placing it to the west of Java. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 177}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4568e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_3155", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The capital of the US State Ohio is the city of Chillicothe.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is false because while Chillicothe was the original capital of Ohio, the current capital is Columbus. Columbus has been the capital since 1816. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 137}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.109e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_3207", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Frankenmuth, a US city nicknamed \"Little Bavaria\", is located in what state?\n\nOptions: \nA. Kentucky\nB. Virginia\nC. Michigan\nD. Pennsylvania\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Frankenmuth, known as \"Little Bavaria\" for its strong German heritage and architecture, is located in Michigan. It is a popular tourist destination famous for its Bavarian-themed festivals, food, and the world's largest Christmas store. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 157}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2771e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_3211", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What event led to Liechenstein adding a crown to its flag?\n\nOptions: \nA. The 1936 Olympics\nB. Signing of the 1862 Constitution of Liechtenstein\nC. Charles VI's decree in 1719\nD. Coronation of Prince Johann I Joseph in 1805\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The addition of the crown to Liechtenstein's flag was inspired by the country's participation in the 1936 Summer Olympics in Berlin, where Liechtenstein realized its flag was identical to Haiti's. To distinguish itself, Liechtenstein added a crown to its flag shortly after. This change was officially adopted in 1937.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 135, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 212}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.7285e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_3353", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: There are no roads in/out of Juneau, Alaska.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Juneau, Alaska, is not connected to the rest of the road system in the United States or Canada by car-accessible roads, meaning there are no roads leading in or out of the city. Travel to and from Juneau is primarily by air or sea. Therefore, the statement is essentially true in practical terms.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 86, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 156}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3106e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_3368", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What name was historically used for the Turkish city currently known as Istanbul?\n\nOptions: \nA. Adrianople\nB. Constantinople\nC. H\u00fcdavendigar\nD. S\u00f6\u011f\u00fct\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The city now known as Istanbul was historically called Constantinople, serving as the capital of the Byzantine Empire. After the Ottoman conquest in 1453, it remained widely known by that name until the official name change to Istanbul in the 20th century. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 166}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3583999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_3407", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What island in the Canary Islands was the scene of one of the worst air disasters in history with the collision of two jumbo jets?\n\nOptions: \nA. Gran Canaria\nB. Maui\nC. Tenerife\nD. Fuerteventura\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is C. Tenerife. The Tenerife airport disaster occurred on March 27, 1977, when two Boeing 747 jumbo jets collided on the runway at Los Rodeos Airport (now Tenerife North Airport), resulting in 583 fatalities, the deadliest accident in aviation history. Gran Canaria was the original destination, but flights were diverted to Tenerife due to a bomb threat.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 100, "total_tokens": 216}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.8235999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_3452", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The body of the Egyptian Sphinx was based on which animal?\n\nOptions: \nA. Bull\nB. Lion\nC. Horse\nD. Dog\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The body of the Egyptian Sphinx is traditionally depicted with the body of a lion and the head of a human, symbolizing strength and wisdom. This iconic structure, located at Giza, reflects the lion's association with power in ancient Egyptian culture. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 150}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2274000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_3559", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Space Needle is located in which city?\n\nOptions: \nA. Los Angles\nB. Vancouver\nC. Toronto\nD. Seattle\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Space Needle is a famous landmark located in Seattle, Washington. It was built for the 1962 World's Fair and remains one of the city's most iconic structures. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 137}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1003e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_3638", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The prefix Sino- (As in Sino-American) is used to refer to what nationality?\n\nOptions: \nA. Japanese\nB. Russian\nC. Chinese\nD. Indian\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The prefix \"Sino-\" is derived from the Latin word \"Sinae,\" which refers to China. It is commonly used in terms like \"Sino-American\" to denote relations between China and another country. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 157}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2742e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_3698", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Sonoran Desert is located in eastern Africa.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Sonoran Desert is not located in eastern Africa; it is primarily found in the southwestern United States and northern Mexico. Therefore, the statement is incorrect.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 37, "total_tokens": 121}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 9.664e-06, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_3780", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: You could walk from Norway to North Korea while only passing through Russia.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "To travel from Norway to North Korea, one must pass through Russia because Norway shares a border with Russia, and Russia shares a short border with North Korea. Therefore, it is geographically possible to complete this journey by only passing through Russian territory.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 138}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:08:10.553508+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000102, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_3837", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following languages does NOT use the Latin alphabet?\n\nOptions: \nA. Vietnamese\nB. Turkish\nC. Swahili\nD. Georgian\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Georgian language uses the unique Georgian script, not the Latin alphabet. Vietnamese, Turkish, and Swahili all use variations of the Latin alphabet. Therefore, the correct answer is D.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 140}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1215999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_3843", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Colchester Overpass, otherwise known as \"Bunny Man Bridge\", is located where?\n\nOptions: \nA. Fairfax County, Virginia\nB. Lemon Grove, California\nC. Braxton County, Virgina\nD. Medford, Oregon\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Colchester Overpass, famously known as the \"Bunny Man Bridge,\" is located in Fairfax County, Virginia. It is associated with a local urban legend about a man wearing a bunny costume who supposedly committed murders in the area. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 169}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3535999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_3880", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following Inuit languages was the FIRST to use a unique writing system not based on the Latin alphabet?\n\nOptions: \nA. Inuktitut\nB. Inupiat\nC. Greenlandic\nD. Inuinnaqtun\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Inuit language that first used a unique writing system not based on the Latin alphabet is Inuktitut, which adopted Canadian Aboriginal syllabics in the 19th century. This writing system was originally developed for Cree but was adapted for Inuktitut and is distinct from the Latin alphabet. The other options either use Latin-based scripts or later adopted writing systems.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 196}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6265e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_4025", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Where would you find the \"Spanish Steps\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. London, England\nB. Barcelona, Spain\nC. Rome, Italy\nD. Berlin, Germany\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The \"Spanish Steps\" are a famous landmark located in Rome, Italy, connecting the Piazza di Spagna with the Trinit\u00e0 dei Monti church. Despite the name, they are not in Spain or any other country listed. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 153}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2428999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_429", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What North American tourist attraction is served by the \"Maid of the Mist\" tour company?\n\nOptions: \nA. Yosemite National Park\nB. Niagara Falls\nC. Disney World\nD. Whistler, British Columbia\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The \"Maid of the Mist\" is a famous boat tour that takes visitors to the base of Niagara Falls. It has been operating for over a century and is specifically associated with Niagara Falls on the U.S.-Canada border. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 163}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.311e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_473", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Hunua Ranges is located in...\n\nOptions: \nA. China\nB. Nepal\nC. New Zealand\nD. Mexico\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Hunua Ranges is a geographical feature located in the North Island of New Zealand, southeast of Auckland. It is known for its native bush, walking trails, and reservoirs supplying water to Auckland. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 146}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1931999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_504", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In which English county is Stonehenge?\n\nOptions: \nA. Wiltshire\nB. Somerset\nC. Cumbria\nD. Herefordshire\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Stonehenge is located in the county of Wiltshire, in South West England. It is one of the most famous prehistoric monuments in the world and has been a protected site for many years. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 144}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1587e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_514", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these countries is located the FURTHEST away from the South China Sea?\n\nOptions: \nA. Malaysia\nB. Vietnam\nC. Bangladesh\nD. Philippines\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Bangladesh is located in South Asia, far from the South China Sea, while Malaysia, Vietnam, and the Philippines all have coastlines directly on the South China Sea. Therefore, Bangladesh is the furthest from the South China Sea among the listed countries.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 157}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2800000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_724", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Into which basin does the Jordan River flow into?\n\nOptions: \nA. Aral Sea\nB. Salton Sea\nC. Dead Sea\nD. Caspian Sea\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Jordan River flows into the Dead Sea, which is a saltwater lake bordered by Jordan to the east and Israel and the Palestinian territories to the west. It is one of the saltiest bodies of water in the world and lies at the lowest elevation on Earth's surface. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 162}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3300000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_776", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If soccer is called football in England, what is American football called in England?\n\nOptions: \nA. Touchdown\nB. Combball\nC. American football\nD. Handball\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In England, American football is commonly referred to as \"American football\" to distinguish it from the sport known as football (soccer) in the U.S. The other options\u2014Touchdown, Combball, and Handball\u2014are not correct names for the sport.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 162}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3242e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_792", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these countries is \"doubly landlocked\" (surrounded entirely by one or more landlocked countries)?\n\nOptions: \nA. Uzbekistan\nB. Switzerland\nC. Bolivia\nD. Ethiopia\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A doubly landlocked country is one that is landlocked and also surrounded only by other landlocked countries. Among the options, only Uzbekistan meets this criterion, as it is surrounded by other landlocked countries in Central Asia. The other countries either have access to the sea or are bordered by non-landlocked nations.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 177}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4597e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_870", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following countries banned the use of personal genetic ancestry tests?\n\nOptions: \nA. Austria\nB. Germany\nC. Canada\nD. Sweden\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Germany has strict regulations on genetic testing, and personal genetic ancestry tests are effectively banned due to laws protecting genetic privacy under the Genetic Diagnostics Act. These laws restrict direct-to-consumer genetic testing without medical oversight. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 145}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1716e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Geography_878", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following European languages is classified as a \"language isolate?\"\n\nOptions: \nA. Maltese\nB. Galician\nC. Hungarian\nD. Basque\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is D. Basque is considered a language isolate because it has no known genetic relationship to any other language, especially not to the Indo-European family. Unlike Maltese, Galician, and Hungarian\u2014each of which belongs to a larger language family\u2014Basque stands alone in its linguistic lineage.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 168}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.39e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_1054", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which Louis was known as 'The Sun King of France'?\n\nOptions: \nA. Louis XIII\nB. Louis XV\nC. Louis XVI\nD. Louis XIV\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Louis XIV was known as 'The Sun King of France' due to his centralized rule and the grandeur of his reign, symbolized by the sun. He ruled for 72 years, the longest of any European monarch, and epitomized absolute monarchy. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 159}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3029e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_1092", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When did L. L. Zamenhof first publish \"Unua Libro\", the first publication describing his international language Esperanto?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1887\nB. 1915\nC. 1897\nD. 1905\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "L. L. Zamenhof first published \"Unua Libro\" in 1887, introducing the constructed language Esperanto to the public. This book was published under the pseudonym \"Doktoro Esperanto\" and marked the official beginning of the Esperanto movement. The correct answer is therefore:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 125, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 196}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5975000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_1162", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The \"Trail of Tears\" was a result of which United States President's Indian Removal Policy?\n\nOptions: \nA. John Quincy Adams\nB. Andrew Jackson\nC. Harry S. Truman\nD. Martin Van Buren\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The \"Trail of Tears\" was a direct result of the Indian Removal Act of 1830, which was championed by President Andrew Jackson. This policy led to the forced relocation of thousands of Native Americans, particularly the Cherokee, from their ancestral lands in the southeastern United States to territories west of the Mississippi River. The suffering and deaths during this journey gave it the name \"Trail of Tears.\"\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 197}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6510000000000003e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_1183", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: After his loss at the Battle of Waterloo, Napoleon Bonaparte was exiled to which island?\n\nOptions: \nA. Elba\nB. St. Helena\nC. Canary\nD. Corsica\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "After his defeat at the Battle of Waterloo in 1815, Napoleon Bonaparte was exiled to the remote island of St. Helena in the South Atlantic Ocean. This was his second and final exile, as he had previously been exiled to Elba in 1814 before escaping and returning to power. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 179}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4826e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_1436", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The son of which pope supposedly held a lecherous f\u00eate involving 50 courtesans in the papal palace?\n\nOptions: \nA. Pius III\nB. Urban II\nC. Innocent V\nD. Alexander VI\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is D. Alexander VI, who was a controversial pope during the Renaissance, known for the scandalous behavior of his family, particularly his son Cesare Borgia. There are historical accounts, though sometimes disputed, of a lavish and immoral banquet hosted by Cesare Borgia in the Vatican involving courtesans. This event is often associated with the perceived corruption of the papal court under Alexander VI.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 202}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6923e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_1452", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Under which name was Rodrigo Borgia made Pope?\n\nOptions: \nA. John Paul II\nB. Rodrigo I\nC. Pius VII\nD. Alexander VI\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Rodrigo Borgia was elected Pope in 1492 and took the name Alexander VI. He is one of the most controversial popes in history, known for his involvement in political intrigue and nepotism. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 150}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2158e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_1483", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The ontological argument for the proof of God's existence is first attributed to whom?\n\nOptions: \nA. Aristotle\nB. Immanuel Kant\nC. Anselm of Canterbury\nD. Ren\u00e9 Descartes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The ontological argument for the existence of God was first formulated by Anselm of Canterbury in the 11th century. He argued that God, defined as \"that than which nothing greater can be conceived,\" must exist in reality because existence is greater than mere conception. This argument is presented in his work *Proslogion*.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 182}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5039e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_1532", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Pianist Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Chopin was a composer of which musical era?\n\nOptions: \nA. Baroque\nB. Romantic\nC. Renaissance\nD. Classic\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Chopin was a composer of the Romantic era, known for his expressive piano works and emphasis on emotion and individualism. The Romantic period spanned much of the 19th century, which aligns with Chopin's lifetime (1810\u20131849). His music exemplifies the stylistic traits of Romanticism, such as lyrical melodies and rich harmonies.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 186}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5728999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_1641", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What was the name of one of the surviving palaces of Henry VIII located near Richmond, London?\n\nOptions: \nA. St James's Palace\nB. Buckingham Palace\nC. Coughton Court\nD. Hampton Court\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "One of the surviving palaces of Henry VIII located near Richmond, London is Hampton Court Palace. It was expanded significantly by Henry VIII and remains a prominent historical site. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 39, "total_tokens": 149}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1710000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_170", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Spain was formed in 1469 with the marriage of Isabella I of Castile and Ferdinand II of what other Iberian kingdom?\n\nOptions: \nA. Navarre\nB. Aragon\nC. Galicia\nD. Le\u00f3n\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The marriage of Isabella I of Castile and Ferdinand II in 1469 united the two most powerful kingdoms on the Iberian Peninsula, laying the foundation for modern Spain. Ferdinand was the king of Aragon, making this union between Castile and Aragon pivotal in Spanish history. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 117, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 184}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5006999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_1815", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: During the Spanish Civil War (1936), Francisco Franco fought for which political faction?\n\nOptions: \nA. Popular Front\nB. Papal State\nC. Nationalist Spain\nD. Republican Spain\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Francisco Franco was a leading figure in the Nationalist faction during the Spanish Civil War, which opposed the Republican government. The Nationalists were composed of conservatives, monarchists, fascists, and the military, seeking to overthrow the left-leaning Popular Front government. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 171}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_1865", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In addition to his career as an astrologer and \"prophet\", Nostradamus published a 1555 treatise that included a section on what?\n\nOptions: \nA. Cheating at card games\nB. Making jams and jellies\nC. Teaching parrots to talk\nD. Digging graves\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Nostradamus was a 16th-century physician and author best known for his prophecies, but he also wrote on health and hygiene. His 1555 treatise, *Les Proph\u00e9ties*, was accompanied by a section on practical health advice, including methods for preventing disease, such as making and using preserves to combat the plague. This aligns most closely with the option related to food preservation.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 132, "output_tokens": 93, "total_tokens": 225}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.8672e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_2026", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which dictator killed the most people?\n\nOptions: \nA. Joseph Stalin\nB. Kim Il Sung\nC. Adolf Hitler\nD. Mao Zedong\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is D. Mao Zedong. Estimates of deaths under his leadership, particularly during the Great Leap Forward, range from 45 to 70 million due to famine and political campaigns. While Stalin and Hitler also caused massive loss of life, Mao's policies resulted in the highest number of fatalities.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 195}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6309999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_2033", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is NOT classified as a Semetic language?\n\nOptions: \nA. Sumerian\nB. Mandaic\nC. Akkadian\nD. Maltese\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Sumerian is not a Semitic language; it is a language isolate with no known linguistic relatives. Mandaic, Akkadian, and Maltese are all classified as Semitic languages. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 157}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2713000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_2093", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"I disapprove of what you say, but I will defend to the death your right to say it\" is a quote from French philosopher Voltaire.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quote \"I disapprove of what you say, but I will defend to the death your right to say it\" is often attributed to Voltaire, but he did not actually say it. It was written by Evelyn Beatrice Hall, an English writer, to summarize Voltaire's views on free speech. Therefore, the statement is not literally true.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 182}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5155e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_2185", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The coat of arms of the King of Spain contains the arms from the monarchs of Castille, Leon, Aragon and which other former Iberian kingdom?\n\nOptions: \nA. Catalonia\nB. Granada\nC. Galicia\nD. Navarre\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The coat of arms of the King of Spain includes the arms of the historic kingdoms that contributed to the formation of modern Spain. Alongside Castile, Le\u00f3n, and Aragon, the Kingdom of Navarre was a significant medieval kingdom whose arms are featured. Granada is also represented, but it was a Nasrid emirate rather than a former Christian kingdom like the others.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 119, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 202}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6749000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_2331", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: United States President Ronald Reagan was the first president to appoint a woman to the Supreme Court. \n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Ronald Reagan appointed Sandra Day O'Connor to the Supreme Court in 1981, making her the first woman to serve on the Court. This appointment fulfilled a campaign promise and marked a historic milestone. Therefore, the statement is true.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 148}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2102999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_236", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The fourth funnel of the RMS Titanic was fake designed to make the ship look more powerful and symmetrical.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The fourth funnel of the RMS Titanic was indeed non-functional for engine exhaust and was primarily added for aesthetic purposes, including ventilation and to make the ship appear more impressive. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 138}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:08:11.671627+00:00"}, "cost": 9.325e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_253", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Fallingwater House, located in Pennsylvania, was designed by which architect?\n\nOptions: \nA. Antoni Gaudi\nB. Frank Lloyd Wright\nC. Frank Gehry\nD. Le Corbusier\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Fallingwater House in Pennsylvania is one of the most famous works of Frank Lloyd Wright, designed in 1935 as a private residence. It exemplifies his philosophy of organic architecture, integrating buildings with their natural surroundings. The correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 123, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 194}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5833e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_2594", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following ancient Near Eastern peoples still exists as a modern ethnic group?\n\nOptions: \nA. Assyrians\nB. Elamites\nC. Hittites\nD. Babylonians\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Assyrians are the only ancient Near Eastern people listed who still exist today as a modern ethnic group, primarily living in parts of Iraq, Syria, Turkey, and Iran. They have maintained a distinct cultural and linguistic identity, particularly through the use of Eastern Aramaic languages and Christian religious traditions. The Elamites, Hittites, and Babylonians are all extinct as ethnic groups.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 189}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5884e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_2707", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What did the first vending machines in the early 1880's dispense?\n\nOptions: \nA. Sodas \nB. Cigarettes\nC. Alcohol\nD. Post cards\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The first vending machines in the early 1880s were installed in England and dispensed postcards, primarily used in post offices to sell postal cards and envelopes. These machines were invented by Percival Everitt and became popular for automating the sale of small postal items. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 169}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3855e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_2840", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Oxford University is older than the Aztec Empire. \n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Oxford University was founded in the late 12th century, around 1096, making it one of the oldest universities in the world. The Aztec Empire, on the other hand, was established in 1428, centuries after Oxford's founding. Therefore, Oxford University is indeed older than the Aztec Empire.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 161}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3634999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_2888", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who is the creator of the soft drink, Dr. Pepper?\n\nOptions: \nA. James Wellington\nB. Charles Alderton\nC. Boris Heviltik\nD. Johnson Hinsin\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The creator of Dr. Pepper is Charles Alderton, a pharmacist who developed the drink in Waco, Texas, in 1885. He worked at Morrison's Old Corner Drug Store and formulated the unique flavor that became Dr. Pepper. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 162}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3154999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_2949", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: King Henry VIII was the second monarch of which European royal house?\n\nOptions: \nA. Stuart\nB. York\nC. Tudor\nD. Lancaster\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "King Henry VIII was the second monarch of the Tudor dynasty, which came to power after the Wars of the Roses. His father, Henry VII, was the first Tudor monarch, making Henry VIII the second. The other houses listed\u2014Stuart, York, and Lancaster\u2014preceded or succeeded the Tudors.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 166}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3816e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3273", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In relation to the British Occupation in Ireland, what does the IRA stand for.\n\nOptions: \nA. Irish Reformation Army\nB. Irish-Royal Alliance\nC. Irish Republican Army\nD. Irish Rebel Alliance\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The IRA stands for Irish Republican Army, which was a paramilitary organization involved in various campaigns for Irish independence from British rule. The name reflects its republican ideals and historical role in resisting British occupation. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 154}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2268e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3283", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The pantheon in Rome was used to worship what god?\n\nOptions: \nA. Zeus\nB. Athena\nC. Any god they wanted\nD. Both Athena and Zeus\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Pantheon in Rome was originally built as a temple to honor all the gods of ancient Rome, not just one specific deity. Its name comes from the Greek words meaning \"temple of all the gods.\" Therefore, it was used to worship any god the Romans wished.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 161}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3199999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_332", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Battle of Trafalgar took place on October 23rd, 1805\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Battle of Trafalgar actually took place on October 21st, 1805, not October 23rd. Therefore, the statement is incorrect.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 139}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1116e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3348", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The ancient city of Chich\u00e9n Itz\u00e1 was built by which civilization?\n\nOptions: \nA. Toltecs\nB. Mayans\nC. Incas\nD. Aztecs\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The ancient city of Chich\u00e9n Itz\u00e1 was primarily built by the Maya civilization, although it shows influence from the Toltecs due to later cultural interactions. It is located in the Yucat\u00e1n Peninsula of Mexico, a region historically inhabited by the Maya. While the Toltecs had some influence on the site, the original builders and dominant culture were the Maya.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 183}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5312999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3423", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In what year was the video game company Electronic Arts founded?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1981\nB. 1999\nC. 2005\nD. 1982\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Electronic Arts was founded in 1982 by Trip Hawkins. The company was established with the goal of creating high-quality video games for personal computers. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 38, "total_tokens": 148}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1609999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3509", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The United States Department of Homeland Security was formed in response to the September 11th attacks.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The United States Department of Homeland Security was established in 2002 in direct response to the September 11, 2001, terrorist attacks. Its primary purpose is to protect the country from various threats, including terrorism. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 149}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2173999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3511", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which Las Vegas casino was originally constructed and operated by mobster Bugsy Siegel?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Flamingo\nB. The MGM Grand\nC. The Sahara\nD. The Sands\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Bugsy Siegel was instrumental in the development of the Flamingo Hotel and Casino in Las Vegas, which opened in 1946. It was one of the first luxury casinos on the Strip and was partially funded with mob money. The other options were developed later by different individuals.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 171}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4026e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3563", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If you grab the bladed end of a longsword in a specific way, you will not cut yourself.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "This technique is known as \"half-swording,\" where a fencer grips the blade with a gloved hand to gain better leverage and control for thrusting or close-quarters combat. Because the edges of a longsword are not typically razor-sharp near the hilt and the pressure is applied perpendicular to the edge, it is possible to hold the blade without injury.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 174}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:08:11.374230+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00014475, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3603", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sir Issac Newton served as a Member of Parliament, but the only recorded time he spoke was to complain about a draft in the chambers.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is widely cited as a humorous anecdote about Sir Isaac Newton, suggesting that during his time as a Member of Parliament, he only spoke once\u2014to complain about a draft. However, there is no reliable historical evidence that Newton ever spoke in Parliament, draft complaint or otherwise. Most historians consider the story apocryphal, and records indicate he was a largely silent MP.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 185}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5542e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3667", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Hagia Sophia was commissioned by which emperor of the Byzantine Empire?\n\nOptions: \nA. Theodosius the Great\nB. Justinian I\nC. Constantine IV\nD. Arcadius\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Hagia Sophia was commissioned by Emperor Justinian I in 532 AD after the previous church was destroyed during the Nika riots. It was constructed as a monumental cathedral in Constantinople and became a symbol of Byzantine architecture. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 161}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3026e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3712", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these 1900s tanks were designed and built BEFORE the others?\n\nOptions: \nA. M4 Sherman\nB. Cromwell \nC. Renault FT\nD.  Panzer IV\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Renault FT was designed and built during World War I, entering service in 1917, making it the earliest tank among the options. The other tanks\u2014Panzer IV, M4 Sherman, and Cromwell\u2014were developed during the late 1930s and early 1940s for use in World War II. Therefore, the Renault FT predates the others by over two decades.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 199}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6797000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3884", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who is attributed credit for recording the epic poem The Odyssey?\n\nOptions: \nA. Homer\nB. Socrates\nC. Aristotle\nD. Odysseus\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The epic poem *The Odyssey* is traditionally attributed to the ancient Greek poet Homer. While the historical existence of Homer is debated, ancient and modern scholarship widely credits him as the author. Socrates, Aristotle, and Odysseus were not poets of the work\u2014Socrates and Aristotle were philosophers, and Odysseus is the fictional hero of the poem.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 178}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4957999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3902", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is not in the Indo-European language family?\n\nOptions: \nA. Finnish\nB. Russian\nC. English\nD. Hindi\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Finnish is not part of the Indo-European language family; it belongs to the Uralic language family, specifically the Finno-Ugric group. Russian, English, and Hindi are all Indo-European languages, belonging to the Slavic, Germanic, and Indo-Iranian branches respectively. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 162}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3445000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3923", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The original Roman alphabet lacked the following letters EXCEPT:\n\nOptions: \nA. J\nB. X\nC. W\nD. U\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The original Roman alphabet did not include the letters J, W, or U, as these were later developments. The letter X, however, was part of the early Roman alphabet and used to represent the /ks/ sound. Therefore, the only letter among the options that was present originally is X.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 159}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3202999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3954", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The seed drill was invented by which British inventor?\n\nOptions: \nA. Jethro Tull\nB. Isaac Newton\nC. Charles Babbage\nD. J.J Thomson\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The seed drill was invented by Jethro Tull, an 18th-century British agriculturalist. This invention significantly improved the efficiency of planting crops by ensuring seeds were sown at the correct depth and spacing. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 152}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2271000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3970", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which English king was married to Eleanor of Aquitaine?\n\nOptions: \nA. Henry V\nB. Richard I\nC. Henry I\nD. Henry II\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "D. Henry II was married to Eleanor of Aquitaine, one of the most powerful and influential women in medieval Europe. Eleanor was first married to King Louis VII of France, but after their marriage was annulled, she married Henry, who later became King Henry II of England. Their marriage significantly expanded English territories and influence in France.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 172}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4358e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3972", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Abolitionist John Brown raided the arsenal in which Virginia Town?\n\nOptions: \nA. Harrisonburg\nB. Richmond\nC. Harper's Ferry\nD. Martinsburg\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "John Brown's raid occurred in 1859 when he attempted to seize weapons from the federal arsenal to spark a slave rebellion. The town where this arsenal was located is Harper's Ferry, which was then part of Virginia. This event significantly heightened tensions leading up to the American Civil War.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.36e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_3985", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: With which Greek philosopher would you associate the phrase, \"I know that I know nothing\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. Aristotle\nB. Pythagoras\nC. Socrates\nD. Plato\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The phrase \"I know that I know nothing\" is most commonly associated with Socrates, reflecting his Socratic irony and method of questioning to expose ignorance. Although the exact wording does not appear in ancient texts, it captures the essence of Socratic wisdom as described in Plato's dialogues. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 168}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3812999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_411", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In what year was the famous 45 foot tall Hollywood sign first erected?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1933\nB. 1923\nC. 1913\nD. 1903\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Hollywood sign was originally erected in 1923 as \"Hollywoodland\" to promote a real estate development. It was a temporary structure but became an iconic landmark over time. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 159}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2594e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_422", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The creator of the Enigma Cypher and Machine was of what nationality?\n\nOptions: \nA. German\nB. British\nC. American\nD. Polish\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Enigma machine was originally developed by a German engineer, Arthur Scherbius, in the early 1920s. Although the Poles later made significant breakthroughs in breaking the Enigma cipher, the machine itself was a German invention. Therefore, the creator's nationality was German.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 164}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3587e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_438", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: After the 1516 Battle of Marj Dabiq, the Ottoman Empire took control of Jerusalem from which sultanate?\n\nOptions: \nA. Mamluk\nB. Ummayyad\nC. Ayyubid\nD. Seljuq\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "After the Battle of Marj Dabiq in 1516, the Ottoman Empire defeated the Mamluk Sultanate, leading to the incorporation of territories including Jerusalem into Ottoman rule. The Mamluks had controlled Jerusalem since the 13th century, following the Ayyubids. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 122, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 199}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6361999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_453", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What was the aim of the \"Umbrella Revolution\" in Hong Kong in 2014?\n\nOptions: \nA. Lower taxes\nB. Go back under British Rule\nC. Genuine universal suffrage\nD. Gaining Independence\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The \"Umbrella Revolution\" in 2014 was a pro-democracy movement in Hong Kong that called for greater political freedom and a more democratic electoral system. Protesters demanded genuine universal suffrage for the selection of Hong Kong's Chief Executive, opposing Beijing's restrictions on candidate nominations. The movement did not seek independence or a return to British rule, but rather democratic reforms within the framework of \"One Country, Two Systems.\"\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 94, "total_tokens": 208}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.7494e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_46", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Tiananmen Square protests of 1989 were held in Hong Kong.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Tiananmen Square protests of 1989 took place in Beijing, not in Hong Kong. Therefore, the statement is factually incorrect. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 38, "total_tokens": 130}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0331999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_485", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What number does the Roman numeral \"D\" stand for?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1000\nB. 50\nC. 500\nD. 100\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Roman numeral \"D\" stands for 500. This is a standard value in the Roman numeral system, where D represents half of M (1000). \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 149}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1825999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_523", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The first televised presidential debate was between Jimmy Carter and Gerald Ford.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The first televised presidential debate actually occurred in 1960 between John F. Kennedy and Richard Nixon, not between Jimmy Carter and Gerald Ford. While Carter and Ford did debate in 1976, they were not the first. Therefore, the statement is incorrect.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 149}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2376999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_541", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In what dialogue did Socrates defend himself to the court of Athens? \n\nOptions: \nA. The Apology\nB. The Laws\nC. The Republic\nD. The Euthyphro\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Socrates defended himself in the dialogue known as The Apology, which recounts his speech during his trial in Athens. This work was written by Plato and is not an apology in the modern sense, but rather a defense of Socrates' actions and beliefs. The other options are dialogues on different topics and do not depict Socrates' trial.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 181}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5026e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_545", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The crown of the Empire State Building was originally built for what purpose?\n\nOptions: \nA. Antennae\nB. Flag Pole\nC. Lightning Rod\nD. Airship Dock\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The crown of the Empire State Building was originally designed as an airship docking station, intended for passenger airships to moor at the skyscraper's top. Although the idea was innovative, it proved impractical due to high winds and safety concerns, and was rarely used. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 164}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3442e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_64", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who invented the \"Flying Shuttle\" in 1738; one of the key developments in the industrialization of weaving?\n\nOptions: \nA. John Kay\nB. Richard Arkwright\nC. James Hargreaves\nD. John Deere\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The flying shuttle was invented by John Kay in 1733 (often cited around 1738), significantly advancing the weaving process during the early Industrial Revolution. Richard Arkwright and James Hargreaves were also key figures in textile manufacturing, but they developed later inventions (the water frame and spinning jenny, respectively). John Deere was an American inventor known for agricultural machinery, not weaving.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 117, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 206}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.7207e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_662", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 1967, a magazine published a story about extracting hallucinogenic chemicals from bananas to raise moral questions about banning drugs.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The story about extracting hallucinogenic chemicals from bananas was published in 1967 by the *Berkeley Barb*, a counterculture magazine, as a satirical piece to challenge drug prohibition policies. It claimed that banana peels contained psychoactive substances, prompting debates and even some attempts to replicate the results. The story was a hoax, but it made a serious point about the logic of drug laws.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 191}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6142e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_857", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Adolf Hitler was accepted into the Vienna Academy of Fine Arts.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Adolf Hitler applied to the Vienna Academy of Fine Arts but was rejected. He was, however, accepted into the school's architecture program, which he did not pursue. Therefore, the statement that he was accepted into the Academy of Fine Arts is false.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 86, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 143}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1806e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_924", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following African countries was most successful in resisting colonization?\n\nOptions: \nA. Namibia\nB. C\u00f4te d\u2019Ivoire\nC. Ethiopia\nD. Congo\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Ethiopia is the only African country that successfully resisted European colonization, maintaining its independence throughout the colonial period, notably after defeating Italian forces at the Battle of Adwa in 1896. While other nations faced colonization, Ethiopia preserved its sovereignty. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 160}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3042e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_940", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The minigun was designed in 1960 by which manufacturer.\n\nOptions: \nA. General Electric\nB. Colt Firearms\nC. Sig Sauer\nD. Heckler & Koch\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The minigun was designed in the 1960s by General Electric as part of a project to create a high-rate-of-fire rotary cannon for military aircraft and vehicles. It was developed from the earlier M61 Vulcan cannon and became widely known for its use in helicopters and ground vehicles during the Vietnam War. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 177}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4655e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_History_950", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The M41 Walker Bulldog remains in service in some countries to this day.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The M41 Walker Bulldog, a light tank developed by the United States in the 1950s, was widely exported and saw service in numerous countries. Although it has been retired by most modern militaries, some nations, particularly in South America and Asia, have kept upgraded versions in limited service. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 167}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4061e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_1006", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which psychological term refers to the stress of holding contrasting beliefs?\n\nOptions: \nA. Cognitive Dissonance\nB. Split-Brain\nC. Flip-Flop Syndrome\nD. Blind Sight\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The psychological term that refers to the stress or discomfort experienced when holding two conflicting beliefs or attitudes is cognitive dissonance. This concept was introduced by Leon Festinger and explains how people are motivated to reduce such discomfort. The other options are either not recognized psychological terms or refer to different phenomena.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 167}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3713e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_1062", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sound can travel through a vacuum.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Sound requires a medium, such as air, water, or solid material, to travel. In a vacuum, there are no particles to vibrate and transmit sound waves. Therefore, sound cannot travel through a vacuum.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 81, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 130}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0651e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_1175", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many degrees Fahrenheit is 100 degrees Celsius? \n\nOptions: \nA. 212\nB. 326\nC. 451\nD. 100\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "To convert Celsius to Fahrenheit, use the formula: \u00b0F = (\u00b0C \u00d7 9/5) + 32. Plugging in 100 for \u00b0C: (100 \u00d7 9/5) + 32 = 180 + 32 = 212. Therefore, 100 degrees Celsius is 212 degrees Fahrenheit.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 195}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6397e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_1234", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the name of the cognitive bias wherein a person with low ability in a particular skill mistake themselves as being superior?\n\nOptions: \nA. M\u00fcller-Lyer effect\nB. Freud-Hall effect\nC. Meyers-Briggs effect\nD. Dunning-Kruger effect\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Dunning-Kruger effect describes the cognitive bias where individuals with low ability in a skill overestimate their competence. This occurs because their lack of skill prevents them from recognizing their own deficiencies. The other options refer to unrelated psychological concepts.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 122, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 176}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4062e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_1362", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which planet did the \"Viking 1\" spacecraft send surface images of, starting in 1976?\n\nOptions: \nA. Saturn\nB. Jupiter\nC. Venus\nD. Mars\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The \"Viking 1\" spacecraft was the first successful mission to land on Mars and send back surface images, beginning in 1976. It was part of NASA's Viking program, which specifically targeted Mars for detailed study. The other planets listed\u2014Saturn, Jupiter, and Venus\u2014were not the destinations of the Viking 1 mission.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 184}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5326000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_1560", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The value of one Calorie is different than the value of one calorie.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is true because one Calorie (with a capital C) is equal to 1000 calories (with a lowercase c), commonly used to measure food energy. A calorie (lowercase c) is the amount of energy needed to raise the temperature of 1 gram of water by 1\u00b0C, while a Calorie (uppercase) is a kilocalorie.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 89, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 172}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4619e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_1973", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An average human can go two weeks without water.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "An average human cannot survive two weeks without water; most people can only last about 3 to 4 days without it. The statement is therefore incorrect.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 38, "total_tokens": 122}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 9.764e-06, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_2011", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Type 1 diabetes is a result of the liver working improperly.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Type 1 diabetes is caused by the autoimmune destruction of insulin-producing beta cells in the pancreas, not by the liver working improperly. The liver may play a role in glucose regulation, but it is not the underlying cause of Type 1 diabetes. Therefore, the statement is incorrect.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 149}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2376999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_2030", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Shrimp can swim backwards.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Shrimp are capable of swimming backwards by rapidly flexing their tails. This movement propels them through the water in a backward direction. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 80, "output_tokens": 34, "total_tokens": 114}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 9.08e-06, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_2194", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Where did the dog breed \"Chihuahua\" originate?\n\nOptions: \nA. Mexico\nB. France\nC. Russia\nD. Spain\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Chihuahua dog breed originated in Mexico, named after the Mexican state of Chihuahua. This small breed is believed to have descended from ancient toy dogs kept by the Toltec people. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 143}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1545e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_2281", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Celiac Disease is a disease that effects the heart, causing those effected to be unable to eat meat.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Celiac Disease is not a heart disease, nor does it require the avoidance of meat. It is an autoimmune disorder that affects the small intestine and is triggered by the ingestion of gluten, a protein found in wheat, barley, and rye. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 157}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2945e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_2764", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When the Falcon Heavy was launched on it's test flight, what was the only part of the operation that failed?\n\nOptions: \nA. Deployment of Starman\nB. Side Booster Landing\nC. Center Core Landing\nD. Ignition and Liftoff\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Falcon Heavy's test flight in February 2018 was largely successful, with the side boosters landing safely and Starman (the dummy payload) deployed into space. However, the center core booster failed to land on the drone ship and was lost at sea. This makes the center core landing the only major failure of the operation.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 117, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 192}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5807e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_2845", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Neanderthals were a direct ancestor of modern humans.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Neanderthals were not direct ancestors of modern humans, but rather a closely related sister species. Genetic evidence shows that Neanderthals interbred with modern humans, contributing to the DNA of some present-day populations, but they are not considered a direct lineage. Therefore, the statement is inaccurate.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 154}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2876999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_2853", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Centripedal force is an apparent force that acts outward on a body moving around a center, arising from the body's inertia.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement describes centrifugal force, not centripetal force. Centripetal force is a real force that acts inward toward the center of rotation, keeping an object in circular motion. Centrifugal force is the apparent outward force due to inertia, experienced in a rotating frame.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 163}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3370999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_2942", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Water always boils at 100\u00b0C, 212\u00b0F, 373.15K, no matter where you are.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Water only boils at 100\u00b0C, 212\u00b0F, or 373.15K at standard atmospheric pressure (1 atm), such as at sea level. At higher altitudes, where atmospheric pressure is lower, water boils at a lower temperature. Therefore, the statement is not universally true.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 177}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4655e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_3060", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"The Big Bang Theory\" was first theorized by a priest of what religious ideology?\n\nOptions: \nA. Jewish\nB. Islamic\nC. Christian\nD. Catholic\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Big Bang Theory was first proposed by Georges Lema\u00eetre, a Belgian physicist and priest. He was a member of the Catholic Church, making the correct answer D. While Christianity is a broader category, the most specific and accurate choice given is Catholic.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 157}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2800000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_3202", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A defibrillator is used to start up a heartbeat once a heart has stopped beating.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A defibrillator is not used to restart a stopped heart but rather to correct dangerous, abnormal heart rhythms like ventricular fibrillation by delivering an electric shock. It does not start a heart that has completely stopped (asystole). Therefore, the statement is false.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 181}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4968e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_3617", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: On which mission did the Space Shuttle Columbia break up upon re-entry?\n\nOptions: \nA. STS-109\nB. STS-61-C\nC. STS-107\nD. STS-51-L\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Space Shuttle Columbia broke up during re-entry on mission STS-107. This tragic event occurred on February 1, 2003, resulting in the loss of all seven crew members. The correct answer is therefore:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 171}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3735999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_3716", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is NOT a passive electrical component?\n\nOptions: \nA. Capacitor\nB. Inductor\nC. Transistor\nD. Resistor\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The transistor is an active electrical component because it can amplify signals and control current flow, unlike passive components which do not require external power and cannot amplify. Capacitors, inductors, and resistors are all passive components. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 155}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2687e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_419", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Axiom of Preventive Medicine states that people with ___ risk for a disease should be screened and we should treat ___ of those people.\n\nOptions: \nA. low, some\nB. high, some\nC. high, all\nD. low, all\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Axiom of Preventive Medicine suggests that screening and intervention are most effective when targeted at individuals at high risk for a disease, and treating all of those high-risk individuals can yield the best outcomes. This approach maximizes benefit and resource efficiency in preventive care. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 119, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 184}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4949e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_476", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A person can get sunburned on a cloudy day.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Sunburn is caused by ultraviolet (UV) radiation from the sun, which can penetrate cloud cover. Even on cloudy days, up to 80% of UV rays can reach the Earth's surface. Therefore, it is possible to get sunburned on a cloudy day.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 86, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 149}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2406000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_506", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Doppler effect applies to light.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Doppler effect applies to light, causing shifts in the observed wavelength depending on the relative motion between the source and the observer. This phenomenon is known as redshift when the source moves away and blueshift when it moves closer. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 82, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 135}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1122e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_589", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What physics principle relates the net electric flux out of a closed surface to the charge enclosed by that surface?\n\nOptions: \nA. Gauss's Law\nB. Biot-Savart Law\nC. Ampere's Law\nD. Faraday's Law\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Gauss's Law states that the net electric flux through a closed surface is proportional to the total charge enclosed by that surface. This principle directly relates electric flux and enclosed charge, which is exactly what the question describes. The other laws listed pertain to magnetic fields or electromagnetic induction, not this electric flux-charge relationship.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 185}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5135999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_656", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following liquids is least viscous? Assume temperature is 25\u00b0C.\n\nOptions: \nA. Mercury\nB. Benzene\nC. Water\nD. Acetone\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Acetone has the lowest viscosity among the listed liquids at 25\u00b0C, followed by benzene, water, and then mercury, which is denser but not necessarily more viscous\u2014however, in this case, acetone is the least viscous. Viscosity values at 25\u00b0C show acetone (~0.32 cP) is less viscous than water (~0.89 cP), benzene (~0.60 cP), and mercury (~1.55 cP). Therefore, the least viscous liquid is acetone.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 124, "total_tokens": 227}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.9713000000000003e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_710", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The most frequent subconscious activity repeated by the human body is blinking.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most frequent subconscious activity repeated by the human body is actually breathing, not blinking. While blinking is common and involuntary, breathing occurs more frequently and continuously.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 38, "total_tokens": 125}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 9.977e-06, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_772", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: It was once believed that injecting shark cartilage into people would prevent them from contracting cancer.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "It was once believed by some that shark cartilage could prevent or treat cancer, leading to its use as a dietary supplement. However, scientific studies have not found evidence to support this claim, and the idea is not accepted by the medical community. The statement reflects a belief that existed, even if it was incorrect.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 161}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3431999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_778", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In aeronautics, flaps and slats are used to control what on an aircraft?\n\nOptions: \nA. Weight \nB. Drag\nC. Lift\nD. Thrust\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Flaps and slats are high-lift devices deployed on the wings of an aircraft to increase lift during takeoff and landing. They achieve this by altering the wing's shape and increasing its surface area and camber. This enhanced lift allows the aircraft to fly at slower speeds safely.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 166}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3613e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science & Nature_808", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Where did the Great Storm of 1987 make landfall at, first?\n\nOptions: \nA. Wales\nB. Surrey\nC. Cornwall\nD. The Midlands\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Great Storm of 1987 first made landfall in southern England, specifically affecting coastal areas of the English Channel. Among the options, Cornwall is the most southerly and westernmost location, making it the first point of landfall. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 159}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2971e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_1015", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the name given to layer 4 of the Open Systems Interconnection (ISO) model?\n\nOptions: \nA. Transport\nB. Data link\nC. Session\nD. Network\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Layer 4 of the Open Systems Interconnection (OSI) model is responsible for end-to-end communication and ensures reliable data delivery. This layer is known as the Transport layer. It manages flow control, error correction, and data segmentation.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 157}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2713000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_1126", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Laserjet and inkjet printers are both examples of what type of printer?\n\nOptions: \nA. Impact printer\nB. Daisywheel printer\nC. Non-impact printer\nD. Dot matrix printer\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Laserjet and inkjet printers do not use physical impact to create printed images, distinguishing them from impact printers like dot matrix or daisywheel models. Instead, they use technologies such as toner fusion or ink spraying, which are characteristic of non-impact printing. Therefore, both are classified as non-impact printers.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 175}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4454999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_1145", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many bytes are in a single Kibibyte?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2400\nB. 1024\nC. 1240\nD. 1000\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A kibibyte (KiB) is a unit of digital information that equals 1024 bytes, based on binary prefixes. The prefix \"kibi-\" specifically denotes 2^10, which is 1024. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 174}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4210000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_1223", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: America Online (AOL) started out as which of these online service providers?\n\nOptions: \nA. GEnie\nB. Quantum Link\nC. Prodigy\nD. CompuServe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "America Online (AOL) originated from Quantum Link, an online service for Commodore 64 users, which was launched in 1985. In 1989, Quantum Link was rebranded as America Online after expanding its services beyond Commodore. The other options\u2014GEnie, Prodigy, and CompuServe\u2014were competing services but not the direct predecessor of AOL.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 90, "total_tokens": 195}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6454999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_1236", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: DHCP stands for Dynamic Host Configuration Port.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is incorrect because DHCP stands for Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol, not \"Port.\" The correct answer is therefore False. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 82, "output_tokens": 31, "total_tokens": 113}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 8.921999999999999e-06, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_1306", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: To bypass US Munitions Export Laws, the creator of the PGP published all the source code in book form. \n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The creator of PGP, Phil Zimmermann, published the source code in book form to argue that it was protected speech under the First Amendment, in response to U.S. export restrictions on cryptographic software. This act was intended to challenge the U.S. Munitions Export Laws, which classified strong encryption as a munition. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 175}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4658e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_1386", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these Cherry MX mechanical keyboard switches is both tactile and clicky?\n\nOptions: \nA. Cherry MX Brown\nB. Cherry MX Red\nC. Cherry MX Blue\nD. Cherry MX Black\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Cherry MX Blue switches are known for being both tactile and clicky, providing noticeable feedback and an audible click sound when pressed. Cherry MX Brown is tactile but not clicky, while Red and Black are linear with no tactile bump. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3454999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_1469", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In most programming languages, the operator ++ is equivalent to the statement \"+= 1\".\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The ++ operator in most programming languages increments a variable by 1, which is functionally equivalent to using += 1. However, ++ can also have prefix and postfix forms, affecting when the increment occurs in an expression. Despite these nuances, the net effect of adding 1 is the same, so the statement is generally true.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3832e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_1505", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This mobile OS held the largest market share in 2012.\n\nOptions: \nA. BlackBerry\nB. iOS\nC. Android\nD. Symbian\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In 2012, Android overtook other mobile operating systems to become the most widely used globally, driven by its adoption across numerous device manufacturers. While iOS was popular, especially in certain markets, Android's broader range of devices at various price points contributed to its larger market share. Symbian and BlackBerry were in decline by that time.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 175}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4629e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_1538", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to DeMorgan's Theorem, the Boolean expression (AB)' is equivalent to:\n\nOptions: \nA. A'B + B'A\nB. A' + B'\nC. A'B'\nD. AB' + AB\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "According to DeMorgan's Theorem, the complement of a product is the sum of the complements, meaning (AB)' = A' + B'.  \nThis directly matches option B.  \nThe other options do not correctly represent DeMorgan's equivalence.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 171}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3852e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_1540", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Windows 7 operating system has six main editions.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Windows 7 operating system indeed has six main editions: Starter, Home Basic, Home Premium, Professional, Enterprise, and Ultimate.\n\nThese editions were designed for different user needs and markets, ranging from basic functionality to advanced features.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 136}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1135e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_1556", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many Hz does the video standard PAL support?\n\nOptions: \nA. 50\nB. 59\nC. 25\nD. 60\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The PAL video standard operates at a frame rate of 25 frames per second, but the field rate is 50 Hz due to interlacing (each frame is split into two fields). Therefore, the correct answer is 50 Hz.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 157}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2800000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_156", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these is the name for the failed key escrow device introduced by the National Security Agency in 1993?\n\nOptions: \nA. Clipper Chip\nB. Nautilus\nC. Skipjack\nD. Enigma Machine\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Clipper Chip was a failed key escrow system proposed by the NSA in 1993, designed to allow government access to encrypted communications. Skipjack is the encryption algorithm used by the Clipper Chip, not the device itself. The correct answer is therefore:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 175}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4193999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_1574", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What was the first company to use the term \"Golden Master\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. Apple\nB. IBM\nC. Google\nD. Microsoft\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The term \"Golden Master\" (GM) is commonly associated with software development and refers to the final version of a product before mass production or release. Apple is widely recognized as the first company to popularly use the term \"Golden Master\" in the context of software, particularly for its operating systems and applications. While other companies later adopted the term, Apple's usage predates the others listed.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 180}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5244999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_1613", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"Hexadecimal\", what color would be displayed from the color code? \"#00FF00\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. Blue\nB. Yellow\nC. Green\nD. Red\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The color code \"#00FF00\" in hexadecimal represents green. In this format, the first two digits (00) are for red, the next two (FF) for green, and the last two (00) for blue. Since the green component is at maximum (FF) and red and blue are at zero, the resulting color is pure green.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 82, "total_tokens": 186}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5584e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_1694", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Unix Time is defined as the number of seconds that have elapsed since when?\n\nOptions: \nA. Midnight on the creator of Unix's birthday\nB. Midnight, January 1, 1970\nC. Midnight, July 4, 1980\nD. Midnight, July 4, 1976\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Unix Time is defined as the number of seconds that have elapsed since midnight, January 1, 1970, Coordinated Universal Time (UTC), excluding leap seconds. This date is known as the Unix epoch. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 134, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 192}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5314e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_1698", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The internet domain .fm is the country-code top-level domain for which Pacific Ocean island nation?\n\nOptions: \nA. Marshall Islands\nB. Fiji\nC. Micronesia\nD. Tuvalu\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The .fm domain is the country-code top-level domain for the Federated States of Micronesia, a nation in the Pacific Ocean. Despite \"FM\" commonly being associated with radio frequency, it officially represents Micronesia in the domain name system. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 163}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3255e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_17", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: On which day did the World Wide Web go online?\n\nOptions: \nA. November 24, 1995\nB. December 20, 1990\nC. December 17, 1996\nD. November 12, 1990\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The World Wide Web went online on December 20, 1990. This was when Tim Berners-Lee successfully demonstrated the first communication between an HTTP client and server via the internet.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 129, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 176}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3858999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_1726", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the correct term for the metal object in between the CPU and the CPU fan within a computer system?\n\nOptions: \nA. CPU Vent\nB. Temperature Decipator\nC. Heat Vent\nD. Heat Sink\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The metal object between the CPU and the CPU fan is designed to draw heat away from the processor. This component is known as a heat sink because it absorbs and dissipates heat. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 153}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.211e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_1786", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Pointers were not used in the original C programming language; they were added later on in C++.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is incorrect because pointers were part of the original C programming language, not added later in C++. C++ inherited pointers from C and expanded on them, but they were present in C from early on. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 150}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2244999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_1837", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In CSS, which of these values CANNOT be used with the \"position\" property?\n\nOptions: \nA. static\nB. center\nC. absolute\nD. relative\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The \"position\" property in CSS accepts values like static, relative, absolute, fixed, and sticky, but \"center\" is not a valid value. \"Center\" is unrelated to the position property and is typically used with text-align or flexbox properties. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.36e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_1863", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: All of the following programs are classified as raster graphics editors EXCEPT:\n\nOptions: \nA. Adobe Photoshop\nB. GIMP\nC. Inkscape\nD. Paint.NET\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Inkscape is a vector graphics editor, not a raster graphics editor, which makes it the correct exception among the listed programs. Raster graphics editors like Adobe Photoshop, GIMP, and Paint.NET work with pixel-based images, while Inkscape uses vector-based paths. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 118, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 190}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5578e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_1869", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many values can a single byte represent?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1024\nB. 8\nC. 256\nD. 1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A single byte consists of 8 bits, and each bit can be either 0 or 1. This allows for 2^8 = 256 possible combinations. Therefore, a byte can represent 256 different values.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 155}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.26e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_1872", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What does the \"MP\" stand for in MP3?\n\nOptions: \nA. Moving Picture\nB. Micro Point\nC. Multi Pass\nD. Music Player\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The \"MP\" in MP3 stands for \"Moving Picture,\" as it is derived from the Moving Picture Experts Group, the organization that developed the standard. MP3 is short for MPEG-1 Audio Layer 3, where MPEG refers to Moving Picture Experts Group. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2957999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_1977", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to the International System of Units, how many bytes are in a kilobyte of RAM?\n\nOptions: \nA. 500\nB. 1000\nC. 512\nD. 1024\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "According to the International System of Units (SI), the prefix \"kilo-\" denotes a factor of $10^3$, which equals 1000. While binary prefixes (kibibytes) use 1024, the SI standard strictly defines a kilobyte as 1000 bytes.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 186}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:58:27.497836+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00013775, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2029", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: MacOS is based on Linux.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "MacOS is not based on Linux; it is based on the Unix operating system, specifically derived from BSD (Berkeley Software Distribution). While both Linux and macOS are Unix-like, they have different kernels and development histories. Therefore, the statement is incorrect.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 80, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 136}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.128e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2095", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What does the 'S' in the RSA encryption algorithm stand for?\n\nOptions: \nA. Secure\nB. Schottky\nC. Shamir\nD. Stable\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The 'S' in RSA stands for Adi Shamir, one of the three inventors of the RSA algorithm. The algorithm is named after Ron Rivest, Adi Shamir, and Leonard Adleman. Therefore, the correct answer is C.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 157}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2829e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2133", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The logo for Snapchat is a Bell.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The logo for Snapchat is not a Bell; it is a ghost. The bell is commonly associated with notifications on social media platforms, but it is not Snapchat's logo. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 82, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 128}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0422000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2174", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: FLAC stands for \"Free Lossless Audio Condenser\"'\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "FLAC actually stands for \"Free Lossless Audio Codec,\" not \"Free Lossless Audio Condenser.\" The term \"Codec\" refers to encoding and decoding audio, which is accurate for FLAC's function. Therefore, the statement is incorrect.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 86, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 140}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1506e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2222", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In web design, what does CSS stand for?\n\nOptions: \nA. Corrective Style Sheet\nB. Cascading Style Sheet\nC. Counter Strike: Source\nD. Computer Style Sheet\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "CSS stands for Cascading Style Sheet, which is used to control the presentation of web pages, such as layout, colors, and fonts. It works alongside HTML to enhance the visual design of websites. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 150}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2013e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2239", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What was the first Android version specifically optimized for tablets?\n\nOptions: \nA. Eclair\nB. Froyo\nC. Marshmellow\nD. Honeycomb\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The first Android version specifically optimized for tablets was Honeycomb, which was released in 2011 as Android 3.0. It introduced a redesigned user interface tailored for larger screens, along with improved multitasking and notifications. Previous versions like Eclair and Froyo were primarily designed for smartphones.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 167}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3829000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2330", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who invented the \"Spanning Tree Protocol\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. Vint Cerf\nB. Paul Vixie\nC. Michael Roberts\nD. Radia Perlman\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Radia Perlman is credited with inventing the Spanning Tree Protocol (STP), which is fundamental in preventing loops in network bridges. Her work significantly advanced network reliability and is foundational in modern networking. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 149}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1971e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2361", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The numbering system with a radix of 16 is more commonly referred to as \n\nOptions: \nA. Octal\nB. Hexidecimal\nC. Binary\nD. Duodecimal\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The numbering system with a radix of 16 is known as hexadecimal. The prefix \"hexa-\" means six and \"deci-\" means ten, combining to represent 16. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 148}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1784e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2368", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In programming, the ternary operator is mostly defined with what symbol(s)?\n\nOptions: \nA. if then\nB. ?\nC. ?:\nD. ??\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The ternary operator in programming is commonly represented by the symbols `?:`, which together form a concise conditional expression. The `?` symbol alone is not sufficient, and `??` typically refers to a null-coalescing operator in some languages. The correct answer is therefore:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 159}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3087e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2380", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The acronym \"RIP\" stands for which of these?\n\nOptions: \nA. Routing Information Protocol\nB. Regular Interval Processes\nC. Routine Inspection Protocol\nD. Runtime Instance Processes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The acronym \"RIP\" commonly stands for \"Routing Information Protocol,\" which is a widely used network routing protocol. It is used by routers to share information and determine the best path for data transmission. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 149}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1942e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2422", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Python programming language gets its name from the British comedy group \"Monty Python.\"\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Python programming language was named by its creator, Guido van Rossum, who was a fan of the British comedy group \"Monty Python.\" This is why the language has various references to Monty Python in its documentation and examples. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 152}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2561e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2428", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which data structure does FILO apply to?\n\nOptions: \nA. Stack\nB. Heap\nC. Queue\nD. Tree\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "FILO stands for \"First In, Last Out,\" which describes the behavior of a stack data structure. In a stack, the first element added is the last one to be removed, similar to a stack of plates. This principle does not apply to heaps, queues (which follow FIFO), or trees.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3161e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2461", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If you were to code software in this language you'd only be able to type 0's and 1's.\n\nOptions: \nA. C++\nB. Binary\nC. Python\nD. JavaScript\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question describes a language where only 0's and 1's can be used, which directly refers to binary code, the most basic language understood by computers. While C++, Python, and JavaScript are high-level programming languages, binary is the low-level representation of machine code. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 175}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4425999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_251", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Time on Computers is measured via the EPOX System.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement \"Time on Computers is measured via the EPOX System\" is incorrect. Computer time is typically measured using Unix time (also known as POSIX time or Epoch time), which counts seconds since January 1, 1970, at 00:00:00 UTC. There is no widely recognized \"EPOX System\" in computing for time measurement.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 86, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 171}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4606e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2510", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which computer hardware device provides an interface for all other connected devices to communicate?\n\nOptions: \nA. Random Access Memory\nB. Central Processing Unit\nC. Motherboard\nD. Hard Disk Drive\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The motherboard serves as the main circuit board of a computer and connects all hardware components, allowing them to communicate with each other. It provides the electrical connections and pathways through which data travels between the CPU, RAM, storage devices, and other peripherals. Therefore, it acts as the central interface for all connected devices.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 172}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4184000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2524", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: On Twitter, what was the original character limit for a Tweet?\n\nOptions: \nA. 140\nB. 120\nC. 160\nD. 100\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The original character limit for a Tweet on Twitter was 140 characters. This limit was chosen to fit within the constraints of SMS messages, which max out at 160 characters, leaving 20 characters for usernames and commands. The limit was later increased to 280 in 2017.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 180}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4867999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2568", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In programming, what do you call functions with the same name but different implementations?\n\nOptions: \nA. Inheriting\nB. Abstracting\nC. Overriding\nD. Overloading\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Functions with the same name but different implementations, typically based on different parameters, are referred to as overloading. This is commonly used in languages like Java and C++. Overriding, on the other hand, refers to redefining a method in a subclass that was already defined in a parent class.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 169}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3913e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_271", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What was the name of the security vulnerability found in Bash in 2014?\n\nOptions: \nA. Stagefright\nB. Shellshock\nC. Bashbug\nD. Heartbleed\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The security vulnerability found in Bash in 2014 is commonly known as Shellshock. It allowed attackers to execute arbitrary commands by exploiting how Bash handled environment variables. This vulnerability is distinct from Heartbleed (which affected OpenSSL) and Stagefright (a mobile media processing flaw).\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 172}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4096999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2724", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Generally, which component of a computer draws the most power?\n\nOptions: \nA. Power Supply\nB. Hard Drive\nC. Video Card\nD. Processor\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The video card, or GPU, typically draws the most power in a computer, especially during demanding tasks like gaming or rendering. While the processor also consumes significant power, high-performance GPUs often exceed it. The power supply itself does not consume power but delivers it, and hard drives use relatively little.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 162}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3387e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2739", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Android versions are named in alphabetical order.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Android versions are indeed named in alphabetical order, starting from Android 1.5 (Cupcake), then Donut, Eclair, Froyo, Gingerbread, Ice Cream Sandwich, Jelly Bean, KitKat, Lollipop, Marshmallow, Nougat, Oreo, and Pie.\n\nThis naming convention followed the alphabet until Android 10, which broke the pattern by dropping the dessert names.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 82, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 171}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4721999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2771", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What internet protocol was documented in RFC 1459?\n\nOptions: \nA. HTTP\nB. IRC\nC. FTP\nD. HTTPS\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "RFC 1459 documents the Internet Relay Chat (IRC) protocol, which is used for real-time communication over the internet. The other options\u2014HTTP, FTP, and HTTPS\u2014are unrelated protocols documented in different RFCs. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 148}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2045e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2795", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Early RAM was directly seated onto the motherboard and could not be easily removed.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Early RAM, such as in older computers from the 1980s and early 1990s, was often soldered directly onto the motherboard, making it non-removable and non-upgradable. This contrasts with later designs that used RAM modules (like SIMMs or DIMMs) which could be easily replaced or upgraded. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 89, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 172}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4619e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2829", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which kind of algorithm is Ron Rivest not famous for creating?\n\nOptions: \nA. Stream cipher\nB. Hashing algorithm\nC. Asymmetric encryption\nD. Secret sharing scheme\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Ron Rivest is famous for his work on the RSA algorithm (asymmetric encryption), the MD series (hashing algorithms), and the RC series (stream and block ciphers). He is not primarily known for creating a secret sharing scheme, which is most famously associated with Adi Shamir.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 163}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:58:25.423216+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000122, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2844", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What amount of bits commonly equals one byte?\n\nOptions: \nA. 64\nB. 1\nC. 8\nD. 2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "One byte is commonly defined as 8 bits. This standard is widely used in computing and digital systems. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 28, "total_tokens": 124}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 9.615999999999999e-06, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2865", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What type of sound chip does the Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) have?\n\nOptions: \nA. ADPCM Sampler\nB. FM Synthesizer\nC. Programmable Sound Generator (PSG)\nD. PCM Sampler\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES) utilizes the Sony SPC700 sound chip, which is a sample-based synthesis engine. It functions by playing back compressed audio samples stored in its dedicated sound RAM.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 159}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:58:27.763144+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000101, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2895", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A Boolean value of \"0\" represents which of these words?\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A Boolean value of \"0\" typically represents \"False\" in most programming and logical contexts. In Boolean logic, 0 is associated with False, while 1 represents True. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 130}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0477e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2936", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When did the online streaming service \"Mixer\" launch?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2009\nB. 2013\nC. 2011\nD. 2016\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The online streaming service \"Mixer\" was originally launched as Beam in 2016 and later rebranded to Mixer in 2017. Therefore, the correct answer is the year it first launched under its original name. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 166}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.341e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2954", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What language does Node.js use?\n\nOptions: \nA. Java\nB. JavaScript\nC. Java Source\nD. Joomla Source Code\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Node.js uses JavaScript to run on the server side, allowing developers to build scalable network applications. It is not related to Java, despite the similar name. The correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 134}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0732e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2984", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which internet company began life as an online bookstore called 'Cadabra'?\n\nOptions: \nA. Overstock\nB. eBay\nC. Amazon\nD. Shopify\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The internet company that began as an online bookstore called 'Cadabra' is Amazon. The name was later changed to Amazon due to concerns about the pronunciation and association with the word \"cadaver.\" \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 144}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1558e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_2988", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The NVidia GTX 1080 gets its name because it can only render at a 1920x1080 screen resolution.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A. False\n\nThe name \"GTX 1080\" does not indicate a limitation to 1920x1080 resolution; instead, it is part of NVIDIA's naming convention for its GPU model series. The GTX 1080 is capable of rendering at resolutions higher than 1080p, including 1440p and 4K.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 195}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6425999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3013", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the most preferred image format used for logos in the Wikimedia database?\n\nOptions: \nA. .png\nB. .gif\nC. .jpeg\nD. .svg\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most preferred image format for logos in the Wikimedia database is .svg because it supports scalable vector graphics, ensuring clarity at any size. Vector formats like SVG are ideal for logos, which need to be displayed clearly at various resolutions. Other formats like .png, .gif, and .jpeg are raster-based and less suitable for scalability.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 174}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4471000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3075", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: .at is the top-level domain for what country?\n\nOptions: \nA. Argentina\nB. Australia\nC. Angola\nD. Austria\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The top-level domain \".at\" is the country code for Austria. This domain is used for websites associated with Austria. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 31, "total_tokens": 124}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 9.703e-06, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3102", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the programming language \"Python\", which of these statements would display the string \"Hello World\" correctly?\n\nOptions: \nA. echo \"Hello World\"\nB. console.log(\"Hello World\")\nC. print(\"Hello World\")\nD. printf(\"Hello World\")\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct statement in Python to display \"Hello World\" is `print(\"Hello World\")`.  \nOption A uses shell syntax, option B is JavaScript, and option D resembles C-style syntax.  \nThus, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 169}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3535999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3159", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which RAID array type is associated with data mirroring?\n\nOptions: \nA. RAID 5\nB. RAID 1\nC. RAID 0\nD. RAID 10\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "RAID 1 is specifically known for data mirroring, where data is written identically to two or more disks for redundancy. This provides high reliability and fault tolerance, as one drive can fail without data loss. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 152}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2241999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3164", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The teapot often seen in many 3D modeling applications is called what?\n\nOptions: \nA. Pixar Teapot\nB. Utah Teapot\nC. 3D Teapot\nD. Tennessee Teapot\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The teapot commonly featured in 3D modeling applications is known as the Utah Teapot, originally created at the University of Utah. It has become a standard reference object in computer graphics. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 153}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2168e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3171", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The last Windows operating system to be based on the Windows 9x kernel was Windows 98.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is false because the last Windows operating system based on the Windows 9x kernel was Windows Me (Millennium Edition), not Windows 98. Windows Me was released in 2000 and was the final version to use the 9x kernel before Microsoft transitioned to the NT kernel with Windows XP.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 168}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4045e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3175", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following languages is used as a scripting language in the Unity 3D game engine?\n\nOptions: \nA. C++\nB. Java\nC. Objective-C\nD. C#\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Unity 3D game engine primarily uses C# as its scripting language for game development. While Unity's underlying engine is written in C++, developers interact with the engine using C#. Other languages like Java and Objective-C are not supported for scripting in Unity.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 162}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3184000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3199", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In HTML, which non-standard tag used to be be used to make elements scroll across the viewport?\n\nOptions: \nA. <scroll></scroll>\nB. <move></move>\nC. <marquee></marquee>\nD. <slide></slide>\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. The `<marquee>` tag was a non-standard HTML element used to make text or elements scroll across the viewport, supported historically by some browsers like Internet Explorer. Although widely recognized, it is obsolete and not recommended for modern web development.", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 173}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3936e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3259", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"HTML\" stands for Hypertext Markup Language.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement \"HTML\" stands for Hypertext Markup Language is accurate. HTML is the standard markup language used to create web pages. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 39, "total_tokens": 123}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 9.864e-06, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3281", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: HTML is what type of language?\n\nOptions: \nA. Programming Language\nB. Macro Language\nC. Scripting Language\nD. Markup Language\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "HTML is used to structure content on the web, but it does not perform logic or computations like programming or scripting languages. It defines elements using tags and attributes, which is characteristic of a markup language. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 147}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1974000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3305", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: .rs is the top-level domain for what country?\n\nOptions: \nA. Serbia\nB. Russia\nC. Rwanda\nD. Romania\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The top-level domain .rs is assigned to Serbia. This domain was introduced in 2007 following Serbia's independence from the State Union of Serbia and Montenegro. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 141}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1403e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3395", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the number of keys on a standard Windows Keyboard?\n\nOptions: \nA. 64\nB. 104\nC. 76\nD. 94\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A standard Windows keyboard typically has 104 keys, including the alphanumeric keys, function keys, control keys, and the Windows-specific keys like the Windows key and menu key.\n\nThis count is common for full-sized US-layout keyboards designed for Windows.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 159}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2913e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3422", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Released in 2001, the first edition of Apple's Mac OS X operating system (version 10.0) was given what animal code name?\n\nOptions: \nA. Leopard\nB. Puma\nC. Tiger\nD. Cheetah\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The first edition of Apple's Mac OS X 10.0, released in 2001, was code-named \"Cheetah.\" This was followed by subsequent versions with big cat names in ascending order. Leopard, Puma, and Tiger came in later releases.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 119, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 182}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4749e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3447", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The open source program Redis is a relational database server.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "B. False\n\nRedis is an open-source in-memory data structure store, often used as a key-value database, cache, or message broker, not a relational database. It does not support SQL or enforce relational schema like traditional relational databases.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 139}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1434999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3458", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which company was established on April 1st, 1976 by Steve Jobs, Steve Wozniak and Ronald Wayne?\n\nOptions: \nA. Atari\nB. Commodore\nC. Apple\nD. Microsoft\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The company established on April 1st, 1976 by Steve Jobs, Steve Wozniak, and Ronald Wayne is Apple. This is confirmed by historical records of the founding of Apple Inc. Atari, Commodore, and Microsoft were founded by other individuals and at different times.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 177}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4480999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3497", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What does the International System of Quantities refer 1024 bytes as?\n\nOptions: \nA. Kelobyte\nB. Kylobyte\nC. Kibibyte\nD. Kilobyte\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The International System of Quantities uses binary prefixes to distinguish powers of 1024 from powers of 1000. 1024 bytes is specifically referred to as a \"kibibyte\" to avoid confusion with the decimal \"kilobyte,\" which is 1000 bytes. This distinction is standardized by the IEC (International Electrotechnical Commission).\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 195}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6368000000000003e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3504", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The computer OEM manufacturer Clevo, known for its Sager notebook line, is based in which country?\n\nOptions: \nA. Germany\nB. China (People's Republic of)\nC. United States\nD. Taiwan\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Clevo, which manufactures notebooks sold under the Sager brand, is a Taiwanese company known for producing high-performance laptops and barebone systems.\n\nThe company is headquartered in Taiwan and has been a major OEM in the laptop market for many years.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 164}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3239e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3536", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What port does HTTP run on?\n\nOptions: \nA. 443\nB. 23\nC. 53\nD. 80\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The HTTP protocol runs on port 80 by default. Port 443 is used for HTTPS, port 23 for Telnet, and port 53 for DNS.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 142}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1358e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_360", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which programming language shares its name with an island in Indonesia?\n\nOptions: \nA. Jakarta\nB. Java\nC. Python\nD. C\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The programming language named after an island in Indonesia is Java, which shares its name with the island of Java. This language was originally developed by Sun Microsystems and is widely used in web and enterprise applications. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 141}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1373999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3602", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who is the original author of the realtime physics engine called PhysX?\n\nOptions: \nA. AMD\nB. NovodeX\nC. Ageia\nD. Nvidia\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The original author of the PhysX physics engine is Ageia, which developed it before being acquired by Nvidia. After the acquisition, Nvidia continued its development and integration into their products. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 148}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1928999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3613", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: All program codes have to be compiled into an executable file in order to be run. This file can then be executed on any machine.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is false because not all programming languages require compilation into an executable. Interpreted languages, such as Python or JavaScript, are executed directly by an interpreter without prior compilation into a standalone executable. Additionally, compiled executables are often platform-specific and cannot run on any machine without compatibility considerations.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 166}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3671e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3626", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The first computer bug was formed by faulty wires.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The first computer \"bug\" was actually a literal moth found trapped in a relay of the Harvard Mark II computer in 1947, not caused by faulty wires. The term \"bug\" had already been used to describe technical glitches before this incident, but this event popularized the term in computing. Therefore, the statement is incorrect.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3364000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_366", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What does RAID stand for?\n\nOptions: \nA. Range of Applications with Identical Designs\nB. Randomized Abstract Identification Description\nC. Redundant Array of Independent Disks\nD. Rapid Access for Indexed Devices\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "RAID stands for Redundant Array of Independent Disks, which is a technology used to combine multiple hard drives for improved performance, reliability, or data redundancy. This term is commonly used in computer storage systems. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 159}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2739e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3666", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which computer language would you associate Django framework with?\n\nOptions: \nA. C++\nB. Python\nC. Java\nD. C#\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Django is a high-level web framework that is written in and designed for use with Python. It follows the model-view-controller (MVC) architectural pattern and is widely used for developing web applications in Python. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 177}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.451e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3756", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What does the acronym CDN stand for in terms of networking?\n\nOptions: \nA. Compressed Data Network\nB. Computational Data Network\nC. Content Distribution Network\nD. Content Delivery Network\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The acronym CDN stands for Content Delivery Network, which is a system of distributed servers that deliver web content to users based on their geographic location. This helps improve load times and reduce bandwidth costs. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 148}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1812999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3769", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What did the name of the Tor Anonymity Network orignially stand for?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Only Router\nB. The Ominous Router\nC. The Orange Router\nD. The Onion Router\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The name \"Tor\" originally stood for \"The Onion Router,\" reflecting its use of layered encryption to anonymize internet traffic. Each layer of encryption is peeled away at different points in the network, much like layers of an onion. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 162}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3039e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3792", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Lenovo acquired IBM's personal computer division, including the ThinkPad line of laptops and tablets, in what year?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1999\nB. 2005\nC. 2002\nD. 2008\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Lenovo acquired IBM's personal computer division, including the ThinkPad line, in 2005. This deal marked a significant shift in the global PC market, with Lenovo emerging as a major player. The correct answer is \\boxed{B}.", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 120, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 172}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3719999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3812", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: While Apple was formed in California, in which western state was Microsoft founded?\n\nOptions: \nA. Colorado\nB. Arizona\nC. Washington\nD. New Mexico\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Microsoft was founded in Albuquerque, New Mexico, in 1975, but it was soon relocated to Washington state, where it established its long-term headquarters. However, the question asks where Microsoft was founded, not where it is currently based. The correct founding location is New Mexico.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 161}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3257999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_387", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What does the Prt Sc button do?\n\nOptions: \nA. Captures what's on the screen and copies it to your clipboard\nB. Nothing\nC. Saves a .png file of what's on the screen in your screenshots folder in photos\nD. Closes all windows\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Prt Sc (Print Screen) button captures an image of the entire screen and copies it to the clipboard, allowing you to paste it into other applications. It does not automatically save a file unless combined with other keys (like Windows + Prt Sc). Therefore, the most accurate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 122, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 188}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5262e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3882", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How long is an IPv6 address?\n\nOptions: \nA. 128 bytes\nB. 128 bits\nC. 32 bits\nD. 64 bits\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "An IPv6 address is 128 bits long, which allows for a much larger address space than IPv4. This length is standardized to accommodate the growing number of devices connected to the internet. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 150}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1984e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3885", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Windows ME operating system was released in the year 2000.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Windows ME (Millennium Edition) operating system was indeed released in the year 2000, specifically on September 14, 2000. Therefore, the statement is accurate. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 140}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1390000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_389", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many bits make up the significand portion of a single precision floating point number?\n\nOptions: \nA. 23\nB. 53\nC. 8\nD. 15\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The significand portion of a single precision floating point number consists of 23 bits. This is defined by the IEEE 754 standard for floating point representation. The remaining bits are used for the exponent (8 bits) and the sign (1 bit).\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3425999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3966", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The programming language 'Swift' was created to replace what other programming language?\n\nOptions: \nA. C#\nB. Objective-C\nC. Ruby\nD. C++\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The programming language Swift was developed by Apple to replace Objective-C as the primary language for iOS and macOS development. It was introduced in 2014 with the goal of providing a more modern, safe, and efficient alternative to Objective-C. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 155}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2628999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_4044", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In any programming language, what is the most common way to iterate through an array?\n\nOptions: \nA. 'For' loops\nB. 'If' Statements\nC. 'While' loops\nD. 'Do-while' loops\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most common way to iterate through an array in programming languages is using a 'for' loop, as it provides a clear and concise syntax for accessing each element by index. While 'while' and 'do-while' loops can also iterate, 'for' loops are specifically designed for such tasks. 'If' statements are not used for iteration.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 189}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5623000000000003e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_4055", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these is not a key value of Agile software development?\n\nOptions: \nA. Comprehensive documentation\nB. Individuals and interactions\nC. Customer collaboration\nD. Responding to change\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The key values of Agile software development are outlined in the Agile Manifesto, which prioritizes individuals and interactions, customer collaboration, and responding to change over processes and tools, contract negotiation, and following a plan. Comprehensive documentation is not emphasized; instead, Agile values working software over comprehensive documentation. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 173}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4342e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_4063", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the programming language Java, which of these keywords would you put on a variable to make sure it doesn't get modified?\n\nOptions: \nA. Public\nB. Final\nC. Private\nD. Static\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The keyword `final` in Java is used to ensure that a variable cannot be modified after it is initialized. This applies to primitive types and object references, making them constant. The other options relate to access control (`public`, `private`) or class-level sharing (`static`), not immutability.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 174}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4297e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_424", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Dutch computer scientist Mark Overmars is known for creating which game development engine?\n\nOptions: \nA. Construct\nB. Game Maker\nC. Torque 2D\nD. Stencyl\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Mark Overmars is best known for creating Game Maker, a popular 2D game development engine initially developed in the early 2000s. He designed it to help students and beginners learn game development through an accessible interface. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2783999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_499", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the domain name for the country Tuvalu?\n\nOptions: \nA. .tv\nB. .tt\nC. .tu\nD. .tl\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The domain name for the country Tuvalu is .tv, which is commonly used for television and media-related websites due to its association with \"television.\" The other options correspond to different countries: .tt is Trinidad and Tobago, .tu is not a valid country code, and .tl is Timor-Leste.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 168}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3987e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_512", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The HTML5 standard was published in 2014.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The HTML5 standard was officially published as a W3C Recommendation in October 2014. This marked the completion of the standard after years of development and testing. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 135}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0977e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_524", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these programming languages is a low-level language?\n\nOptions: \nA. Python\nB. C#\nC. Pascal\nD. Assembly\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Assembly language is considered a low-level language because it is closely related to machine code and provides minimal abstraction from a computer's hardware architecture. In contrast, Python, C#, and Pascal are high-level programming languages that offer greater abstraction and are easier to read and write. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3103e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_533", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The series of the Intel HD graphics generation succeeding that of the 5000 and 6000 series (Broadwell) is called:\n\nOptions: \nA. HD Graphics 600\nB. HD Graphics 700 \nC. HD Graphics 7000\nD. HD Graphics 500\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Intel HD graphics generation that succeeded the 5000 and 6000 series (Broadwell) is part of the Skylake microarchitecture, which introduced the HD Graphics 500 series. This naming convention shifted with Skylake, where the new integrated graphics were branded as HD Graphics 5xx, including models like HD Graphics 510, 515, 520, etc. Therefore, the correct answer is the next named series in line, which is HD Graphics 500.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 134, "output_tokens": 116, "total_tokens": 250}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.1114e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_587", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The programming language \"Python\" is based off a modified version of \"JavaScript\".\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is incorrect because Python and JavaScript are two distinct programming languages with different syntax, design philosophies, and origins. Python was not based on JavaScript; it was created by Guido van Rossum and first released in 1991, while JavaScript was developed later by Brendan Eich in 1995. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 169}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4289999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_593", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The T-Mobile Sidekick smartphone is a re-branded version of the Danger Hiptop.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The T-Mobile Sidekick smartphone was developed by Danger, Inc. and marketed under the Hiptop name outside the U.S., while T-Mobile rebranded it as the Sidekick in the United States. Despite the different names, they are essentially the same device made by Danger. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 188}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5668e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_638", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these people was NOT a founder of Apple Inc?\n\nOptions: \nA. Ronald Wayne\nB. Steve Wozniak\nC. Steve Jobs\nD. Jonathan Ive\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Jonathan Ive was a prominent designer at Apple, known for his work on the iMac, iPod, and iPhone, but he was not a founder of the company. The founders of Apple Inc. were Ronald Wayne, Steve Wozniak, and Steve Jobs. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 181}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4794000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_667", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the server hosting industry IaaS stands for...\n\nOptions: \nA. Infrastructure as a Service\nB. Internet and a Server\nC. Infrastructure as a Server\nD. Internet as a Service\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "IaaS stands for \"Infrastructure as a Service,\" which is a cloud computing model providing virtualized computing resources over the internet. This term is widely used in the server hosting industry to describe services like virtual machines, storage, and networking. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2783999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_711", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Nvidia's headquarters are based in which Silicon Valley city?\n\nOptions: \nA. Palo Alto\nB. Cupertino\nC. Mountain View\nD. Santa Clara\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Nvidia's headquarters are located in Santa Clara, California, which is in the heart of Silicon Valley. This city is home to many major technology companies and is where Nvidia has its main campus. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 142}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1416e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_774", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who is the founder of Palantir?\n\nOptions: \nA. Peter Thiel\nB. Jack Dorsey\nC. Mark Zuckerberg\nD. Marc Benioff\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Peter Thiel is the co-founder of Palantir Technologies, a data analytics company established in 2003. He played a key role in its founding alongside others like Alex Karp, who became CEO. The other individuals listed founded different companies: Jack Dorsey (Twitter/Block), Mark Zuckerberg (Facebook), and Marc Benioff (Salesforce).\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 179}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5029e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_785", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many cores does the Intel i7-6950X have?\n\nOptions: \nA. 10\nB. 12\nC. 8\nD. 4\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Intel i7-6950X is a high-end processor from the Broadwell-E lineup, released in 2016. It features 10 cores and 20 threads, making it suitable for demanding multitasking and professional workloads. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3484e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_84", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these was the name of a bug found in April 2014 in the publicly available OpenSSL cryptography library?\n\nOptions: \nA. Corrupted Blood\nB. Shellshock\nC. Heartbleed\nD. Shellscript\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Heartbleed bug was a serious vulnerability in the OpenSSL cryptography library discovered in April 2014. It allowed attackers to read sensitive data from the memory of systems using vulnerable versions of OpenSSL. The correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 129, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 194}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5659e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_87", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How fast is USB 3.1 Gen 2 theoretically?\n\nOptions: \nA. 8 Gb/s\nB. 1 Gb/s\nC. 5 Gb/s\nD. 10 Gb/s\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "USB 3.1 Gen 2 has a theoretical maximum data transfer rate of 10 Gb/s. This is double the speed of USB 3.1 Gen 1, which is 5 Gb/s. The correct answer is therefore:\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 170}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3751999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_885", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Harvard architecture for micro-controllers added which additional bus?\n\nOptions: \nA. Control\nB. Data\nC. Address\nD. Instruction\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Harvard architecture uses separate buses for instruction and data to allow simultaneous access to both, improving performance. This means it includes an additional bus specifically for instructions, separate from the data bus. Therefore, the correct answer is the instruction bus.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 147}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1974000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_907", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Linus Torvalds created Linux and Git.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Linus Torvalds is indeed the creator of both the Linux kernel and the version control system Git. He developed Linux in 1991 and later created Git in 2005 to support the development of the Linux kernel. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 146}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2163999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_909", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the name of the process that sends one qubit of information using two bits of classical information?\n\nOptions: \nA. Quantum Entanglement\nB. Super Dense Coding\nC. Quantum Teleportation\nD. Quantum Programming\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The process that sends one qubit of information using two bits of classical information is known as super dense coding. In this protocol, two classical bits are used to transmit one qubit's worth of quantum information by leveraging a pre-shared entangled pair. This distinguishes it from quantum teleportation, which sends a qubit using two classical bits but requires an entangled pair.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 193}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6051999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_910", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following computer components can be built using only NAND gates?\n\nOptions: \nA. Register\nB. CPU\nC. RAM\nD. ALU\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "All of the listed components can theoretically be built using only NAND gates, as NAND gates are functionally complete. However, the most basic and direct digital logic component that forms part of a CPU and is commonly constructed from NAND gates is the ALU (Arithmetic Logic Unit). Thus, the most appropriate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 166}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3786999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_922", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Moore's law originally stated that the number of transistors on a microprocessor chip would double every...\n\nOptions: \nA. Two Years\nB. Eight Years\nC. Year\nD. Four Years\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Gordon Moore originally predicted in 1965 that the number of transistors on a chip would double every year. He later revised this projection in 1975 to a doubling period of approximately two years. Given the phrasing \"originally stated,\" the most accurate answer is one year.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:58:25.771199+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00012125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_947", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many kilobytes in one gigabyte (in decimal)?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1024\nB. 1000\nC. 1048576\nD. 1000000\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In the decimal system, 1 gigabyte (GB) is equal to 1,000 megabytes (MB), and 1 megabyte is equal to 1,000 kilobytes (KB). Therefore, 1 GB = 1,000 \u00d7 1,000 = 1,000,000 KB. This makes the correct answer:\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 117, "output_tokens": 90, "total_tokens": 207}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.7307e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_964", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: It's not possible to format a write-protected DVD-R Hard Disk.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is true because DVD-R media is \"write-once\" technology, meaning data can be burned onto it only once and cannot be erased or reformatted. Furthermore, the term \"DVD-R Hard Disk\" is technically inaccurate, as these are two distinct types of storage media.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 88, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 153}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:58:22.056251+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0001195, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_968", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the name of the default theme that is installed with Windows XP?\n\nOptions: \nA. Bliss\nB. Neptune\nC. Luna\nD. Whistler\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The default theme installed with Windows XP is called Luna, which features the characteristic blue taskbar and start menu. Although \"Bliss\" is the name of the default wallpaper, the theme itself is named Luna. Neptune and Whistler were codenames during development, not official theme names.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 163}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3428999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_971", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these is not a layer in the OSI model for data communications?\n\nOptions: \nA. Transport Layer\nB. Application Layer\nC. Physical Layer\nD. Connection Layer\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The OSI model consists of seven layers: Physical, Data Link, Network, Transport, Session, Presentation, and Application. \"Connection Layer\" is not one of the layers in the OSI model. The correct answer is therefore:\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 152}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2271000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_995", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When Gmail first launched, how much storage did it provide for your email?\n\nOptions: \nA. 5GB\nB. 1GB\nC. 512MB\nD. Unlimited\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "When Gmail first launched in 2004, it offered 1GB of storage, which was significantly more than competitors at the time. This generous amount of storage was a major selling point and helped popularize the service. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2754999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_1438", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Topology, the complement of an open set is a closed set.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In topology, a set is defined as closed if its complement is open. Therefore, if a set is open, its complement must be closed by definition. This makes the statement true.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 89, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 132}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0619e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_1530", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many zeptometres are inside one femtometre?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1,000,000,000\nB. 1,000,000\nC. 1000\nD. 10\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "To convert from femtometres (fm) to zeptometres (zm), recall that 1 femtometre = 10\u207b\u00b9\u2075 metres and 1 zeptometre = 10\u207b\u00b2\u00b9 metres. Therefore, 1 fm = 10\u207b\u00b9\u2075 / 10\u207b\u00b2\u00b9 = 10\u2076 zm, which is 1,000,000 zeptometres. So, the correct answer is B.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 124, "output_tokens": 110, "total_tokens": 234}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.9804e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_1682", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The notion of a \"set that contains all sets which do not contain themselves\" is a paradoxical idea attributed to which English philospher?\n\nOptions: \nA. Bertrand Russel\nB. Alfred North Whitehead\nC. John Locke\nD. Francis Bacon\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The paradox described is known as Russell's Paradox, which highlights a contradiction in naive set theory. It was formulated by the English philosopher and logician Bertrand Russell. This paradox led to significant developments in the foundations of mathematics and logic.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 119, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 173}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3849e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_1766", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many Millibars (mbar) to 1 Inch of Mercury (inHg)\n\nOptions: \nA. 27.4\nB. 30.0\nC. 33.9\nD. 10.6\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The standard conversion from inches of mercury (inHg) to millibars (mbar) is approximately 1 inHg = 33.86 mbar, which rounds to 33.9 mbar. This conversion is commonly used in meteorology and aviation. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 118, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 190}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5578e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_1870", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following mathematicians made major contributions to game theory?\n\nOptions: \nA. Stefan Banach\nB. Leonhard Euler\nC. John Von Neumann\nD. Carl Friedrich Gauss\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "John Von Neumann is widely regarded as one of the founders of game theory, having co-authored the seminal book \"Theory of Games and Economic Behavior\" with Oskar Morgenstern. His work laid the mathematical foundation for analyzing strategic interactions between rational decision-makers. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3484e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_2008", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The decimal number 31 in hexadecimal would be what?\n\nOptions: \nA. 3D\nB. 1F\nC. 1B\nD. 2E\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The decimal number 31 can be converted to hexadecimal by dividing by 16. 31 \u00f7 16 = 1 remainder 15, where 15 corresponds to F in hexadecimal, resulting in 1F. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3542e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_2054", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The set of all algebraic numbers is countable.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The set of all algebraic numbers consists of roots of polynomials with integer coefficients. Since there are only countably many such polynomials and each has finitely many roots, the set of algebraic numbers is countable. Therefore, the statement is true.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 144}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1934999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_2055", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the plane curve proposed by Descartes to challenge Fermat's extremum-finding techniques called?\n\nOptions: \nA. Elliptic Paraboloid of Descartes\nB. Descarte's Helicoid\nC. Cartesian Coordinates\nD. Folium of Descartes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The plane curve proposed by Descartes to challenge Fermat's methods for finding extrema is known as the Folium of Descartes. It is a cubic plane curve defined by the equation $ x^3 + y^3 = 3xy $. This curve was used historically to test techniques in calculus and algebraic geometry.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 124, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 196}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6003999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_2069", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What type of function is x\u00b2+2x+1?\n\nOptions: \nA. Linear\nB. Exponential\nC. Quadratic\nD. Rational\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The function $x^2 + 2x + 1$ is a polynomial of degree 2, which defines a quadratic function. Quadratic functions are of the form $ax^2 + bx + c$, where $a \\neq 0$. \n\nThus, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 164}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3587e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_2129", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An equilateral triangle always has every angle measuring 60\u00b0.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "An equilateral triangle has all three sides equal, and by the properties of triangles, all angles must also be equal. Since the sum of angles in any triangle is 180\u00b0, each angle in an equilateral triangle is 180\u00b0 \u00f7 3 = 60\u00b0. Therefore, the statement is correct.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 88, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 162}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3648e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_2154", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The sum of any two odd integers is odd.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The sum of two odd integers is always even, not odd. For example, 3 + 5 = 8, which is even. Therefore, the statement is false.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 126}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0164e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_23", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A universal set, or a set that contains all sets, exists.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A universal set that contains all sets cannot exist in standard set theory (such as Zermelo-Fraenkel set theory) because it leads to logical contradictions, like Russell's paradox. Therefore, the statement is false.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 88, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 139}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1347999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_2462", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the derivative of Acceleration with respect to time?\n\nOptions: \nA. Shift\nB. Bump\nC. Jerk\nD. Slide\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The derivative of acceleration with respect to time is known as \"jerk,\" which describes the rate of change of acceleration. This term is commonly used in physics and engineering to analyze motion smoothness. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 142}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1416e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_2492", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What prime number comes next after 19?\n\nOptions: \nA. 21\nB. 23\nC. 25\nD. 27\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The next prime number after 19 is 23, since 21, 25, and 27 are all divisible by numbers other than 1 and themselves (21 = 3\u00d77, 25 = 5\u00d75, 27 = 3\u00d79). A prime number has exactly two distinct positive divisors: 1 and itself.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 186}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.57e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_2536", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The French mathematician \u00c9variste Galois is primarily known for his work in which?\n\nOptions: \nA. Abelian Integration\nB. Galois Theory\nC. Galois' Continued Fractions\nD. Galois' Method for PDE's \n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\u00c9variste Galois is best known for developing what is now called Galois Theory, which connects field theory and group theory, particularly in the context of solving polynomial equations. His groundbreaking work laid the foundation for understanding the solvability of equations by radicals. The other options are not recognized as his primary contributions.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 185}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5135999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_2943", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If you could fold a piece of paper in half 50 times, its' thickness will be 3/4th the distance from the Earth to the Sun.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Each time you fold a piece of paper in half, its thickness doubles. After 50 folds, the thickness would be $ 2^{50} $ times the original thickness, which is an astronomically large number\u2014far exceeding the distance from Earth to the Sun. Therefore, the statement is actually **true** in a theoretical sense, despite being physically impossible.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 189}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5768e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_2959", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following famous mathematicians died in a duel at the age of 20?\n\nOptions: \nA. Euler\nB. Galois\nC. Gauss\nD. Abel\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The mathematician who died in a duel at the age of 20 was \u00c9variste Galois, known for his foundational work in group theory.\n\nEuler, Gauss, and Abel all died of natural causes or illness, not in duels.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 159}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2942e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_297", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Zero factorial is equal to zero. \n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Zero factorial (0!) is defined as 1, not 0. Therefore, the statement \"Zero factorial is equal to zero\" is incorrect. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 82, "output_tokens": 37, "total_tokens": 119}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 9.521999999999998e-06, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_3105", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: E = MC3\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The equation E = mc\u00b3 is incorrect; the correct equation from Einstein's theory of relativity is E = mc\u00b2, where E is energy, m is mass, and c is the speed of light.\n\nTherefore, the statement E = MC3 is false.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 79, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 138}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1509000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_331", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the complex plane, multiplying a given function by i rotates it anti-clockwise by how many degrees?\n\nOptions: \nA. 90\nB. 0\nC. 270\nD. 180\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Multiplying a complex number by $ i $ corresponds to a 90-degree counterclockwise rotation in the complex plane. This is because $ i $ has a magnitude of 1 and an argument of 90 degrees. Therefore, the function is rotated anti-clockwise by exactly 90 degrees.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 181}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4852000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_344", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The metric prefix \"atto-\" makes a measurement how much smaller than the base unit?\n\nOptions: \nA. One Quintillionth\nB. One Billionth\nC. One Septillionth\nD. One Quadrillionth\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The metric prefix \"atto-\" represents a factor of $10^{-18}$, which is one quintillionth of the base unit. This means it makes a measurement one quintillionth the size of the base unit. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 169}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3710000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_3480", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: L'H\u00f4pital was the mathematician who created the homonymous rule that uses derivatives to evaluate limits with indeterminations.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "L'H\u00f4pital's rule is named after Guillaume de l'H\u00f4pital, who published it in his 1696 textbook, but the rule was actually discovered by Johann Bernoulli. L'H\u00f4pital paid Bernoulli for his work and included the rule in his book, which is why it bears his name. Thus, while L'H\u00f4pital did not create the rule himself, he is credited with its publication.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 99, "total_tokens": 199}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.7e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_359", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The proof for the Chinese Remainder Theorem used in Number Theory was NOT developed by its first publisher, Sun Tzu.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Chinese Remainder Theorem was indeed discussed by the ancient Chinese mathematician Sun Tzu, but the formal proof and modern formulation were developed later by other mathematicians, such as Gauss. Therefore, the proof used in modern number theory was not developed by Sun Tzu.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 161}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3229e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_3774", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: 111,111,111 x 111,111,111 = 12,345,678,987,654,321\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given equation is:  \n111,111,111 \u00d7 111,111,111 = 12,345,678,987,654,321.\n\nThis is a known mathematical pattern: squaring a number made of repeating 1s (like 11, 111, etc.) produces a symmetric result. Specifically, 111,111,111\u00b2 does equal 12,345,678,987,654,321.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 124, "output_tokens": 136, "total_tokens": 260}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.2404e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_3783", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which mathematician refused the Fields Medal?\n\nOptions: \nA. Andrew Wiles\nB. Terence Tao\nC. Grigori Perelman\nD. Edward Witten\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Grigori Perelman declined the Fields Medal in 2006 for his work on the Poincar\u00e9 conjecture, despite being widely celebrated for his contributions to mathematics. He is the only person to have done so, citing disagreements with the mathematical community. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 161}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3199999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_3929", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which greek mathematician ran through the streets of Syracuse naked while shouting \"Eureka\" after discovering the principle of displacement?\n\nOptions: \nA. Homer\nB. Archimedes\nC. Euclid\nD. Eratosthenes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The story of a Greek mathematician running through the streets of Syracuse naked while shouting \"Eureka!\" is famously attributed to Archimedes, who made the discovery while working on a problem of determining the purity of gold in a crown. This moment marked his realization of the principle of buoyancy and displacement. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 182}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4894e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_3998", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the correct order of operations for solving equations?\n\nOptions: \nA. Parentheses, Exponents, Addition, Substraction, Multiplication, Division\nB. The order in which the operations are written.\nC. Addition, Multiplication, Division, Subtraction, Addition, Parentheses\nD. Parentheses, Exponents, Multiplication, Division, Addition, Subtraction\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct order of operations is commonly remembered by the acronym PEMDAS: Parentheses, Exponents, Multiplication and Division (from left to right), Addition and Subtraction (from left to right). Option D correctly lists this sequence. The other options either misorder the operations or present incorrect sequences.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 141, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 208}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6711e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_3999", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the area of a circle with a diameter of 20 inches if \u03c0= 3.1415?\n\nOptions: \nA. 314.15 Inches\nB. 3141.5 Inches\nC. 1256.6 Inches\nD. 380.1215 Inches\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The radius of the circle is half the diameter, so $ r = 10 $ inches.  \nThe area is calculated as $ A = \\pi r^2 = 3.1415 \\times 10^2 = 3.1415 \\times 100 = 314.15 $ square inches.  \nThus, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 138, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 227}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.8698e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_434", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The binary number \"101001101\" is equivalent to the Decimal number \"334\"\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The binary number \"101001101\" can be converted to decimal by calculating:  \n1\u00d72\u2078 + 0\u00d72\u2077 + 1\u00d72\u2076 + 0\u00d72\u2075 + 0\u00d72\u2074 + 1\u00d72\u00b3 + 1\u00d72\u00b2 + 0\u00d72\u00b9 + 1\u00d72\u2070 = 256 + 64 + 8 + 4 + 1 = 333.  \nSince 333 \u2260 334, the statement is false.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 128, "total_tokens": 227}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.9829e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_633", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What shape does sin(x) or cos(x) make on a graph?\n\nOptions: \nA. Zig-Zags\nB. A Parabola\nC. Waves\nD. A Straight Line\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The graph of sin(x) or cos(x) produces a repeating pattern of smooth, continuous oscillations. This shape is best described as waves, rising and falling periodically. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 145}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1484e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_742", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following dice is not a platonic solid?\n\nOptions: \nA. 10-sided die\nB. 20-sided die\nC. 12-sided die\nD. 8-sided die\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A Platonic solid is a regular, convex polyhedron with identical faces made of congruent regular polygons. The 10-sided die (a pentagonal trapezohedron) is not a Platonic solid because its faces are not regular polygons meeting at each vertex in the same configuration. The 20-sided, 12-sided, 8-sided, and 4-sided dice are Platonic solids, but the 10-sided die is not.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 102, "total_tokens": 211}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.7939e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_900", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these numbers is closest to the total number of possible states for an army standard Enigma Machine?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.58 x 10^22\nB. 1.58 x  10^18\nC. 1.58 x 10^20\nD. 1.58 x 10^24\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The total number of possible settings for a standard German Army Enigma machine (with 3 rotors selected from 5, ring settings, plugboard with 10 pairs, and initial rotor positions) is approximately 1.58 \u00d7 10^20. This accounts for the combinations of rotor selection and order, starting positions, ring settings, and plugboard configurations. \n\nThus, the closest value is:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 148, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 240}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.9708e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_1144", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Baseball, how many times does the ball have to be pitched outside of the strike zone before the batter is walked?\n\nOptions: \nA. 4\nB. 2\nC. 3\nD. 1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In baseball, a batter is awarded a walk when the pitcher throws four pitches outside the strike zone that the batter does not swing at. This is known as a \"base on balls\" or a \"walk.\" Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 164}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.321e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_1521", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: During Wimbledon, spectators in the grounds can buy the tennis balls that have been used in matches.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Spectators at Wimbledon cannot purchase the used tennis balls directly from the grounds during the tournament. The used balls are typically collected and repurposed or sold through official channels after the event. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 138}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1103e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_1550", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Soccer player Cristiano Ronaldo opened a museum dedicated to himself.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Cristiano Ronaldo opened a museum dedicated to his career and achievements, known as Museu CR7, in his hometown of Funchal, Madeira, in 2013. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 81, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 129}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:24.019224+00:00"}, "cost": 9.225e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_1919", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Skateboarding was included in the 2020 Summer Olympics in Tokyo.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Skateboarding made its Olympic debut at the 2020 Summer Olympics in Tokyo, which were held in 2021 due to the pandemic. This marked the first time the sport was included in the Olympic program. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 143}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1690000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_1998", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Why was The Green Monster at Fenway Park was originally built?\n\nOptions: \nA. To make getting home runs harder.\nB. To prevent viewing games from outside the park.\nC. To display advertisements.\nD. To provide extra seating.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Green Monster at Fenway Park was originally built to prevent people outside the park from watching games for free. It served as a barrier to stop spectators from viewing over the shorter original wall. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 138, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 194}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5398e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_2177", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A stimpmeter measures the speed of a ball over what surface?\n\nOptions: \nA.  Football Pitch\nB. Pinball Table\nC. Cricket Outfield\nD. Golf Putting Green\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A stimpmeter is a device used in golf to measure the speed of a putting green by determining how far a ball rolls on the grass surface. It is specifically designed for use on golf courses, particularly on putting greens, to assess green speed consistently. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 162}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3184000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_2249", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Peyton Manning retired after winning Super Bowl XLIX.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Peyton Manning retired after winning Super Bowl 50, not Super Bowl XLIX. Super Bowl XLIX was won by the Seattle Seahawks over the Denver Broncos. Therefore, the statement is incorrect.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 130}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0564e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_2289", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This Canadian television sportscaster is known for his \"Hockey Night in Canada\" role, a commentary show during hockey games.\n\nOptions: \nA. Don McKellar\nB. Donald Sutherland\nC. Don Taylor \nD. Don Cherry\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Don Cherry is the well-known Canadian sportscaster famous for his role on \"Hockey Night in Canada,\" particularly for his segment \"Coach's Corner.\" The other options are Canadian public figures but are not associated with hockey broadcasting. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 167}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3394000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_2603", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who was the British professional wrestler Shirley Crabtree better known as?\n\nOptions: \nA. Giant Haystacks\nB. Kendo Nagasaki\nC. Masambula\nD. Big Daddy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Shirley Crabtree was a British professional wrestler best known by his ring name Big Daddy. He became a prominent figure in British wrestling during the 1970s and 1980s, often teaming with or facing Giant Haystacks. His flamboyant persona and partnership with the promoter Max Crabtree helped popularize wrestling on UK television.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 120, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 207}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.7219999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_2629", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Formula 1, the Virtual Safety Car was introduced following the fatal crash of which driver?\n\nOptions: \nA. Gilles Villeneuve\nB. Ronald Ratzenberger\nC. Jules Bianchi\nD. Ayrton Senna\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Virtual Safety Car (VSC) was introduced in Formula 1 following the 2014 Japanese Grand Prix, where Jules Bianchi suffered a severe head injury after crashing into a recovery vehicle. His accident highlighted the need for improved safety procedures when track conditions required caution without deploying the physical Safety Car. The VSC system was implemented in 2015 to manage such situations more safely.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 201}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6794000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_2743", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many games did Arsenal FC go unbeaten during the 2003-2004 season of the English Premier League\n\nOptions: \nA. 38\nB. 51\nC. 22\nD. 49\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Arsenal FC went unbeaten in all 38 league games during the 2003-2004 English Premier League season, earning them the nickname \"The Invincibles.\" The question specifically asks about the number of games in that single season, not an extended unbeaten run across seasons. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 118, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 194}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5978000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_3275", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What tool lends it's name to a last-stone advantage in an end in Curling?\n\nOptions: \nA. Drill\nB. Hammer\nC. Screwdriver\nD. Wrench\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In curling, the \"hammer\" refers to the advantage of having the last stone in an end, which can be crucial for scoring. This term is commonly used in curling strategy and gameplay. The correct answer is the tool that lends its name to this advantage.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 163}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3313e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_335", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What cricketing term denotes a batsman being dismissed with a score of zero?\n\nOptions: \nA. Bye\nB. Beamer\nC. Carry\nD. Duck\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A batsman who is dismissed without scoring any runs is said to have scored a \"duck.\" This term is widely used in cricket to describe a zero score upon dismissal. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 139}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1029e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_3408", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: At which bridge does the annual Oxford and Cambridge boat race start?\n\nOptions: \nA. Hammersmith\nB. Putney\nC. Battersea\nD. Vauxhall \n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The annual Oxford and Cambridge Boat Race starts at Putney Bridge on the River Thames. This has been the traditional starting point for the race since 1845. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 159}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2564999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_3440", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which professional wrestler fell from the rafters to his death during a live Pay-Per-View event in 1999?\n\nOptions: \nA. Al Snow\nB. Chris Benoit\nC. Lex Luger\nD. Owen Hart\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is D. Owen Hart tragically fell from the rafters during a live pay-per-view event, Over the Edge, in 1999, while attempting to make his entrance as his \"Blue Blazer\" character.\n\nThe accident occurred due to a malfunction in the harness system meant to lower him safely into the ring. This remains one of the most devastating incidents in professional wrestling history.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 203}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6965e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_571", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In association football, or soccer, a corner kick is when the game restarts after someone scores a goal.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A corner kick is actually awarded when the defending team last touches the ball before it crosses their own goal line, not when a goal is scored. The game restarts with a corner kick from the corner arc nearest to where the ball went out. Therefore, the statement is incorrect.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3015999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_828", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many scoring zones are there on a conventional dart board?\n\nOptions: \nA. 62\nB. 42\nC. 102\nD. 82\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A conventional dartboard has 20 numbered sections, each with a single and double scoring zone, plus the bullseye (inner and outer), totaling 62 scoring zones. This includes 20 singles, 20 doubles, 20 trebles (though trebles are part of the same zones), and 2 bullseye sections, but the standard count of distinct scoring areas is 62. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 195}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6513000000000003e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_914", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Formula E is an auto racing series that uses hybrid electric race cars.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Formula E is an auto racing series that uses fully electric race cars, not hybrid electric ones. The cars in Formula E are powered entirely by electricity, with no internal combustion engine component. Therefore, the statement is incorrect.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 171}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4026e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Sports_976", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which boxer was banned for taking a bite out of Evander Holyfield's ear in 1997?\n\nOptions: \nA. Roy Jones Jr.\nB. Evander Holyfield\nC. Lennox Lewis\nD. Mike Tyson\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Mike Tyson was disqualified during a 1997 heavyweight championship fight against Evander Holyfield for biting a piece of Holyfield's ear. This infamous incident led to widespread media coverage and Tyson's temporary suspension from boxing. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 164}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3123000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_1069", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What was the name of the first front-wheel-drive car produced by Datsun (now Nissan)?\n\nOptions: \nA. Bluebird\nB. Sunny\nC. Cherry\nD. Skyline\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The first front-wheel-drive car produced by Datsun (now Nissan) was the Cherry. Introduced in the 1970s, the Datsun Cherry marked the company's shift toward front-wheel-drive technology. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 155}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2484e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_1173", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Bugatti was an Italian car manufacturer.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Bugatti was founded by Ettore Bugatti, an Italian-born engineer, but the company was established in Molsheim, Alsace, which was part of Germany at the time (now France). Therefore, Bugatti is generally considered a French manufacturer. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 162}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3358e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_120", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What kind of train was Stepney, a train on the Bluebell Railway notable for his appearance in \"The Railway Series\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. LB&SCR A1X\nB. LB&SCR J1\nC. LB&SCR E2\nD. LB&SCR D1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Stepney was an LB&SCR A1X class locomotive, a rebuilt version of the original A1 class, famously known for its appearances in \"The Railway Series\" by Rev. W. Awdry. It has been preserved and is operational on the Bluebell Railway. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 124, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 187}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5104e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_1232", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which car tire manufacturer is famous for its \"P Zero\" line?\n\nOptions: \nA. Michelin\nB. Goodyear\nC. Pirelli\nD. Bridgestone\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The \"P Zero\" line is a high-performance tire series produced by Pirelli, widely used in sports cars and luxury vehicles. This product line is one of Pirelli's most recognized and marketed tire models. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 154}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2413e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_1245", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following car models has been badge-engineered (rebadged) the most?\n\nOptions: \nA. Suzuki Swift\nB. Holden Monaro\nC. Isuzu Trooper\nD. Chevy Camaro\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Isuzu Trooper is widely recognized for being sold under a vast array of different brand names and badges globally, including Acura, Honda, Opel, Vauxhall, Holden, and Subaru. This extensive rebranding strategy across multiple international markets makes it the most badge-engineered vehicle among the provided options.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 168}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:06.270688+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000122, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_1293", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What car manufacturer gave away their patent for the seat-belt in the interest of saving lives?\n\nOptions: \nA. Ford\nB. Renault\nC. Volvo\nD. Ferrari\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Volvo developed the three-point seat belt and made it freely available to other manufacturers to improve global automotive safety. In 1959, they patented the design but chose not to restrict its use, prioritizing public safety over profit. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 155}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2571e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_132", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When BMW was established in 1916, it was producing automobiles.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "BMW was established in 1916, but initially it produced aircraft engines, not automobiles. The company began manufacturing automobiles much later, with its first car introduced in the 1920s. Therefore, the statement is false.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 145}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1890000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_1329", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The LS2 engine is how many cubic inches?\n\nOptions: \nA. 364\nB. 346\nC. 402\nD. 376\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The LS2 engine is a General Motors small-block V8 that has a displacement of 6.0 liters, which converts to approximately 364 cubic inches. This engine was introduced in the early 2000s and used in various Chevrolet and GMC vehicles. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 166}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3583999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_1419", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Complete the following analogy: Audi is to Volkswagen as Infiniti is to ?\n\nOptions: \nA. Subaru\nB. Nissan\nC. Hyundai\nD. Honda\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Audi is a luxury division of Volkswagen, just as Infiniti is a luxury division of Nissan. Therefore, the correct analogy is Infiniti is to Nissan as Audi is to Volkswagen. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 162}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2894e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_143", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Jaguar Cars was previously owned by which car manfacturer?\n\nOptions: \nA. Chrysler\nB. General Motors\nC. Fiat\nD. Ford\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Jaguar Cars was previously owned by Ford Motor Company, which acquired Jaguar in 1989 and later merged it into the Premier Automotive Group. Ford sold Jaguar to Tata Motors in 2008. The correct answer is therefore D.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 151}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2345e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_1566", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What year did the Chevrolet LUV mini truck make its debut?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1973\nB. 1972\nC. 1975\nD. 1982\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Chevrolet LUV mini truck made its debut in 1972. It was introduced as a compact pickup truck and quickly gained popularity in the U.S. market. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 152}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1981e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_1602", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following collision avoidance systems helps airplanes avoid colliding with each other?\n\nOptions: \nA. TCAS\nB. TAWS\nC. GPWS\nD. OCAS\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is A. TCAS (Traffic Alert and Collision Avoidance System) is specifically designed to detect nearby aircraft and provide resolution advisories to pilots to avoid mid-air collisions. TAWS and GPWS are terrain awareness systems, and OCAS is not a standard aviation system. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3542e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_1743", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following passenger jets is the longest?\n\nOptions: \nA. Boeing 787-10\nB. Airbus A330-200\nC. Airbus A350-1000\nD. Boeing 747-8\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Boeing 747-8 is the longest passenger jet among the options listed, with a length of approximately 76.4 meters. All other options are significantly shorter: the Boeing 787-10 is about 68.3 meters, the A330-200 is 59 meters, and the A350-1000 is 73.8 meters. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 117, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 195}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6107e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_1753", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The LS7 engine is how many cubic inches?\n\nOptions: \nA. 364\nB. 346\nC. 427\nD. 376\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The LS7 engine is a 7.0-liter V8 engine produced by General Motors, which translates to approximately 427 cubic inches. This engine was notably used in the Chevrolet Corvette Z06. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 152}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2241999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_1868", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The LS1 engine is how many cubic inches?\n\nOptions: \nA. 355\nB. 346\nC. 350\nD. 360\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The LS1 engine has a displacement of 346 cubic inches. Although it is often rounded to 5.7 liters, the exact conversion comes out to 346 cubic inches. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 150}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1984e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_1879", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which Audi does not use Haldex based all wheel drive system?\n\nOptions: \nA. Audi TT\nB. Audi S3\nC. Audi A3\nD. Audi A8\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Audi A8 uses a permanent all-wheel drive system based on a Torsen center differential, not the Haldex system used in transverse-engine platforms. In contrast, the Audi TT, S3, and A3 (in most configurations) utilize the Haldex-based quattro system. Therefore, the correct answer is the model that differs in drivetrain layout.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 184}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5413e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_2087", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: BMW M GmbH is a subsidiary of BMW AG that focuses on car performance.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "BMW M GmbH, originally known as BMW Motorsport GmbH, is indeed a subsidiary of BMW AG dedicated to developing high-performance variants of BMW vehicles. It is responsible for models such as the M3, M5, and X5 M, which are engineered for enhanced power, handling, and sporty aesthetics. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 89, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 164}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3819e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_2387", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which animal features on the logo for Abarth, the motorsport division of Fiat?\n\nOptions: \nA. Horse\nB. Scorpion\nC. Snake\nD. Bull\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Abarth logo features a scorpion, which is a symbol tied to the brand's Italian heritage and the zodiac sign of its founder, Carlo Abarth. The scorpion represents power, precision, and a sting in the tail\u2014qualities associated with the performance of Abarth vehicles. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 187}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5394e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_2389", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which car tire manufacturer is famous for its \"Eagle\" brand of tires, and is the official tire supplier of NASCAR?\n\nOptions: \nA. Michelin\nB. Goodyear\nC. Pirelli\nD. Bridgestone\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Goodyear is well known for its \"Eagle\" line of high-performance tires and has a long-standing association with NASCAR as the official tire supplier. The company has been the exclusive tire provider for NASCAR's top series for many years. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 168}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3494e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_2519", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which one is NOT the function of engine oil in car engines?\n\nOptions: \nA. Combustion\nB. Cooling\nC. Reduce corrosion\nD. Lubrication\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Engine oil serves several critical functions in a car engine, including lubrication to reduce friction, cooling by transferring heat away from components, and reducing corrosion by protecting metal surfaces. However, it does not play a role in combustion, which is the process of burning fuel to generate power. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 168}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.39e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_2541", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What UK Train does NOT go over 125MPH?\n\nOptions: \nA. Javelin\nB. Class 43\nC. Sprinter\nD. Pendolino\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Javelin (Class 395) can reach speeds up to 140 mph, the Class 43 (HST) can exceed 125 mph (up to 125 mph regularly, with some runs faster), and the Pendolino (Class 390) operates at up to 125 mph, often hitting that limit. However, the Sprinter family of trains (e.g., Class 150, 158, etc.) are diesel multiple units with a maximum speed typically around 75\u201390 mph, well under 125 mph. Therefore, the Sprinter does not go over 125 mph.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 152, "total_tokens": 256}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.2584e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_2548", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Volkswagen's legendary VR6 engine has cylinders positioned at what degree angle?\n\nOptions: \nA. 15 Degree\nB. 45 Degree\nC. 90 Degree\nD. 30 Degree\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Volkswagen VR6 engine features a narrow-angle V-configuration where the cylinders are positioned at a 15-degree angle, allowing for a compact design that fits in engines bays typically meant for inline-four engines. This unique layout combines the benefits of a V-engine with the space efficiency of a straight engine. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 176}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4468e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_2579", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which supercar company is from Sweden?\n\nOptions: \nA. McLaren\nB. Lamborghini\nC. Koenigsegg\nD. Bugatti\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is C. Koenigsegg. Koenigsegg is a Swedish manufacturer of high-performance supercars, founded in 1994 by Christian von Koenigsegg. The other options\u2014McLaren (UK), Lamborghini (Italy), and Bugatti (France)\u2014are from different countries.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 171}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4315999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_2597", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What are the cylinder-like parts that pump up and down within the engine?\n\nOptions: \nA. Leaf Springs\nB. Pistons\nC. ABS\nD. Radiators\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The cylinder-like parts that move up and down inside an engine are responsible for compressing fuel and air and converting combustion energy into motion. These components are known as pistons. Leaf springs, ABS, and radiators serve entirely different functions unrelated to this motion.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 156}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2729e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_2715", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following vehicles featured a full glass roof at base model?\n\nOptions: \nA. Mercedes-Benz A-Class\nB. Chevy Volt\nC. Renault Avantime\nD. Honda Odyssey\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Renault Avantime, a luxury minivan produced in the early 2000s, was notable for its distinctive full glass roof, even on base models. This feature set it apart from other vehicles in its class at the time. None of the other listed vehicles offered a full glass roof as standard in their base trims.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 123, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 203}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6732999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_2719", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following countries has officially banned the civilian use of dash cams in cars?\n\nOptions: \nA. Austria\nB. United States\nC. South Korea\nD. Czechia\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Austria has strict privacy laws that restrict the use of dash cams by civilians, as they can record people without consent in public spaces, which violates data protection regulations. While other countries may have restrictions, Austria is known for officially banning civilian dash cam use. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 159}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2942e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_279", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When was Cadillac founded?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1985\nB. 1898\nC. 1964\nD. 1902\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Cadillac was founded in 1902, making it one of the oldest American luxury automobile brands. It was established by Henry Leland and named after Antoine de la Mothe Cadillac, the founder of Detroit. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 153}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2312999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_291", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which Italian city is home of the car manufacturer 'Fiat'?\n\nOptions: \nA. Modena\nB. Rome\nC. Turin\nD. Maranello\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Italian car manufacturer Fiat was founded and is headquartered in Turin. While Modena and Maranello are known for other automotive brands like Ferrari and Lamborghini, Turin is specifically associated with Fiat. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 148}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.19e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_3076", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What country was the Trabant 601 manufactured in?\n\nOptions: \nA. Soviet Union\nB. Hungary\nC. East Germany\nD. France\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Trabant 601 was a compact car produced by VEB Sachsenring Automobilwerke in Zwickau, which was located in East Germany. It became an iconic vehicle of the former German Democratic Republic (GDR). \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 152}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2387e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_3158", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which country has the international vehicle registration letter 'A'?\n\nOptions: \nA. Australia\nB. Austria\nC. Armenia\nD. Afghanistan\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The international vehicle registration letter 'A' stands for Austria. This code is used on vehicle license plates to identify the country of registration internationally. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 34, "total_tokens": 128}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0074e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_3234", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which Variable Valve Timing technology is used by BMW?\n\nOptions: \nA. VANOS\nB. MultiAir\nC. VVT-iw\nD. VVEL\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "BMW uses VANOS as its Variable Valve Timing technology. VANOS adjusts the timing of the intake and exhaust valves to optimize engine performance and efficiency. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 35, "total_tokens": 133}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0457999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_3245", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The LS3 engine is how many cubic inches?\n\nOptions: \nA. 376\nB. 346\nC. 427\nD. 364\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The LS3 engine is a General Motors small-block V8 with a displacement of 6.2 liters, which converts to approximately 376 cubic inches. This engine is commonly found in vehicles like the Chevrolet Corvette and Camaro. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2783999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_3296", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The majority of Subaru vehicles are made in China.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}\n\nThe majority of Subaru vehicles are not made in China. Most Subaru vehicles are manufactured in Japan, with some production also taking place in the United States through Subaru of Indiana Automotive.", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 124}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 9.963999999999998e-06, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_3396", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 2014, over 6 million General Motors vehicles were recalled due to what critical flaw?\n\nOptions: \nA. Faulty brake pads\nB. Faulty ignition switch\nC. Breaking fuel lines\nD. Malfunctioning gas pedal\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is B. Faulty ignition switch. In 2014, General Motors recalled over 6 million vehicles due to a defect in the ignition switch that could unexpectedly turn off the engine, disabling critical safety systems like airbags. This flaw was linked to numerous accidents, injuries, and fatalities. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 186}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5236e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_3397", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The difference between the lengths of a Boeing 777-300ER and an Airbus A350-1000 is closest to:\n\nOptions: \nA. 10m \nB. 100m\nC. 1m\nD. 0.1m\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Boeing 777-300ER is approximately 73.9 meters long, while the Airbus A350-1000 is about 73.8 meters long. The difference in length is only about 0.1 meters. Therefore, the closest difference is 0.1m.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 128, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 202}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6488e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_3527", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Automobiles produced by Tesla Motors operate on which form of energy?\n\nOptions: \nA. Diesel\nB. Nuclear\nC. Gasoline\nD. Electricity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Tesla Motors produces electric vehicles that run entirely on electricity. These cars are powered by rechargeable battery packs, not by fossil fuels or nuclear energy. \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 36, "total_tokens": 132}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0415999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_3564", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these companies does NOT manufacture motorcycles?\n\nOptions: \nA. Honda\nB. Kawasaki\nC. Toyota\nD. Yamaha\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Toyota is primarily an automobile manufacturer and does not produce motorcycles, unlike Honda, Kawasaki, and Yamaha, which are well-known for both motorcycles and other vehicles or products. While Honda, Kawasaki, and Yamaha all have long-standing motorcycle divisions, Toyota has never entered the motorcycle market. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3161e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_3606", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How much horsepower is produced by the SD40-2 Locomotive?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2,190\nB. 2,578\nC. 3,000\nD. 3,200\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The SD40-2 locomotive is a widely used diesel-electric locomotive known for its 3,000 horsepower engine. This model, built by Electro-Motive Diesel (EMD), was introduced in the 1970s and became a standard in North American freight service. The correct answer is therefore:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 182}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5039e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_3616", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The term \"GTO\" was originated by Ferrari?\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The term \"GTO\" stands for \"Gran Turismo Omologato,\" which Ferrari used for homologating high-performance cars for racing, starting with the 250 GTO in the 1960s. While the term \"Gran Turismo\" existed before, Ferrari popularized the specific designation \"GTO\" in the automotive world. Therefore, the term \"GTO\" as used in this context was indeed originated by Ferrari.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 98, "total_tokens": 183}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5835e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_3704", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What nickname was given to Air Canada Flight 143 after it ran out of fuel and glided to safety in 1983?\n\nOptions: \nA. Gimli Glider\nB. Gimli Microlight\nC. Gimli Superb\nD. Gimli Chaser\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The nickname \"Gimli Glider\" was given to Air Canada Flight 143 after it ran out of fuel mid-flight and successfully glided to an emergency landing at a former airbase in Gimli, Manitoba. The incident occurred in 1983 and became famous for the skillful handling by the flight crew. The correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 125, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 203}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6675000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_3718", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What do the 4 Rings in Audi's Logo represent?\n\nOptions: \nA. Main cities vital to Audi\nB. States in which Audi makes the most sales\nC. Previously independent automobile manufacturers\nD. Countries in which Audi makes the most sales\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The four rings in Audi's logo represent four previously independent automobile manufacturers that merged to form Auto Union, the predecessor of Audi. These companies were Audi, DKW, Horch, and Wanderer. The logo symbolizes their unity and collaboration.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 170}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3664999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_3762", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which one of these chassis codes are used by BMW 3-series?\n\nOptions: \nA. F10\nB. E39\nC. E46\nD. E85\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The BMW 3-Series has used several chassis codes over the years, including E39 (fifth generation, 1995\u20132003) and E46 (fourth generation, 1998\u20132005). F10 is the chassis code for the 5-Series, and E85 is for the first-generation Z4 roadster. Therefore, both E39 and E46 are correct for the 3-Series, but since only one answer can be chosen and E46 is a direct 3-Series model, it is a valid choice.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 130, "total_tokens": 234}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.0384e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_3934", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Japanese Shinkansen beat the French TGV's speed record for fastest electric rail train.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The French TGV holds the world speed record for a conventional electric rail train, achieving 574.8 km/h (357 mph) in 2007. The Japanese Shinkansen, while extremely fast and efficient, has not surpassed this record. Therefore, the statement is false.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 162}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3503e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_4026", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Arriva is owned by the Deutsche Bahn.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Arriva is a multinational public transport company that was acquired by Deutsche Bahn in 2010. Therefore, it is correct that Arriva is owned by Deutsche Bahn. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 127}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0263999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_447", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which Japanese company is the world's largest manufacturer of motorcycles?\n\nOptions: \nA. Honda\nB. Suzuki\nC. Kawasaki\nD. Yamaha\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Honda is the world's largest manufacturer of motorcycles, consistently leading global sales and production for many years. It produces a wide range of motorcycles for various markets and has a strong presence in Asia, Europe, and the Americas. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 145}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1774000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_471", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The snowmobile was invented by Canadian Joseph-Armand Bombardier in 1937.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Joseph-Armand Bombardier received a patent for his first successful snow vehicle, the B7, in 1937. This invention laid the foundation for the modern snowmobile industry.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 134}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:03.983089+00:00"}, "cost": 8.85e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_509", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Ferrari has never made a V10 engine for any of its cars.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Ferrari has indeed produced V10 engines, most notably in the Ferrari F10 (2010 Formula 1 car) and the road-going Ferrari 458 Italia, which features a 4.5L V10 engine. Therefore, the statement that Ferrari has never made a V10 engine is incorrect.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 89, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 164}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3819e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_601", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The General Motors EV1 was the first street-legal production electric vehicle.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is false because the General Motors EV1 was the first mass-produced electric vehicle from a major automaker in the modern era, but not the first street-legal production electric vehicle in history. Electric vehicles were produced and sold commercially as early as the late 19th and early 20th centuries.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 155}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:04.943314+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00012625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_645", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What part of an automobile engine uses lobes to open and close intake and exhaust valves, and allows an air/fuel mixture into the engine?\n\nOptions: \nA. Drive shaft\nB. Piston\nC. Camshaft\nD. Crankshaft\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The camshaft uses lobes to open and close the intake and exhaust valves, allowing the air/fuel mixture into the engine and exhaust gases out. It is precisely timed with the crankshaft to ensure proper engine operation. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 167}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3335999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_673", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Chevrolet Corvette has always been made exclusively with V8 engines only.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is false because the Chevrolet Corvette has not always been made exclusively with V8 engines. Starting with the 2020 model year, Chevrolet introduced the C8 Corvette with an available turbocharged V6 engine in its E-Ray hybrid variant. Additionally, there were earlier experimental or special edition models that deviated from the traditional V8.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 88, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 163}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3748e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_694", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The full English name of the car manufacturer BMW is Bavarian Motor Works\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The full English name of the German company BMW (Bayerische Motoren Werke) is indeed translated as Bavarian Motor Works. Therefore, the statement provided is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 83, "output_tokens": 39, "total_tokens": 122}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:06.097301+00:00"}, "cost": 7.925e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_867", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the name of Nissan's most popular electric car?\n\nOptions: \nA. Deer\nB. Roots\nC. Leaf\nD. Tree\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Nissan Leaf is the most popular electric car produced by Nissan. It was one of the first mass-market electric vehicles and has been widely recognized for its reliability and efficiency. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 134}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0674e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_872", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What model was the sports car gifted to Yuri Gagarin by the French government in 1965?\n\nOptions: \nA. AC Cobra\nB. Porsche 911\nC. Matra Djet\nD. Alpine A110\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The sports car gifted to Yuri Gagarin by the French government in 1965 was the Matra Djet. Matra, a French company, produced the Djet as one of the earliest mid-engined production cars, and it was presented as a diplomatic gift. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 117, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 181}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4706999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_983", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When was Tesla founded?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2005\nB. 2003\nC. 2008\nD. 2007\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Tesla was founded in 2003 by a group of engineers and entrepreneurs, including Martin Eberhard and Marc Tarpenning. The company was established with the goal of accelerating the world's transition to sustainable energy through electric vehicles. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 157}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2713000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "OpenTDB_Vehicles_991", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 1993 Swedish car manufacturer Saab experimented with replacing the steering wheel with a joystick in a Saab 9000.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In 1993, Saab did experiment with alternative control systems, including a joystick, as part of its \"Saab Magic Eye\" concept in the Saab 9000. This was intended to improve ergonomics and safety, although it never reached production. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 117, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 189}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5507e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_0", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Programmed cell death (PCD) is the regulated death of cells within an organism. The lace plant (Aponogeton madagascariensis) produces perforations in its leaves through PCD. The leaves of the plant consist of a latticework of longitudinal and transverse veins enclosing areoles. PCD occurs in the cells at the center of these areoles and progresses outwards, stopping approximately five cells from the vasculature. The role of mitochondria during PCD has been recognized in animals; however, it has been less studied during PCD in plants.', 'The following paper elucidates the role of mitochondrial dynamics during developmentally regulated PCD in vivo in A. madagascariensis. A single areole within a window stage leaf (PCD is occurring) was divided into three areas based on the progression of PCD; cells that will not undergo PCD (NPCD), cells in early stages of PCD (EPCD), and cells in late stages of PCD (LPCD). Window stage leaves were stained with the mitochondrial dye MitoTracker Red CMXRos and examined. Mitochondrial dynamics were delineated into four categories (M1-M4) based on characteristics including distribution, motility, and membrane potential (\u0394\u03a8m). A TUNEL assay showed fragmented nDNA in a gradient over these mitochondrial stages. Chloroplasts and transvacuolar strands were also examined using live cell imaging. The possible importance of mitochondrial permeability transition pore (PTP) formation during PCD was indirectly examined via in vivo cyclosporine A (CsA) treatment. This treatment resulted in lace plant leaves with a significantly lower number of perforations compared to controls, and that displayed mitochondrial dynamics similar to that of non-PCD cells.']\n\nQuestion: Do mitochondria play a role in remodelling lace plant leaves during programmed cell death?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that mitochondrial dynamics change progressively during programmed cell death (PCD) in lace plant leaves, with distinct stages correlating with PCD progression. Inhibiting mitochondrial permeability transition pore (PTP) formation with cyclosporine A reduced PCD and perforation formation, indicating functional involvement. This evidence supports a regulatory role for mitochondria in leaf remodelling during PCD.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 463, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 550}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.1573e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_1", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Assessment of visual acuity depends on the optotypes used for measurement. The ability to recognize different optotypes differs even if their critical details appear under the same visual angle. Since optotypes are evaluated on individuals with good visual acuity and without eye disorders, differences in the lower visual acuity range cannot be excluded. In this study, visual acuity measured with the Snellen E was compared to the Landolt C acuity.', '100 patients (age 8 - 90 years, median 60.5 years) with various eye disorders, among them 39 with amblyopia due to strabismus, and 13 healthy volunteers were tested. Charts with the Snellen E and the Landolt C (Precision Vision) which mimic the ETDRS charts were used to assess visual acuity. Three out of 5 optotypes per line had to be correctly identified, while wrong answers were monitored. In the group of patients, the eyes with the lower visual acuity, and the right eyes of the healthy subjects, were evaluated.', 'Differences between Landolt C acuity (LR) and Snellen E acuity (SE) were small. The mean decimal values for LR and SE were 0.25 and 0.29 in the entire group and 0.14 and 0.16 for the eyes with strabismus amblyopia. The mean difference between LR and SE was 0.55 lines in the entire group and 0.55 lines for the eyes with strabismus amblyopia, with higher values of SE in both groups. The results of the other groups were similar with only small differences between LR and SE.']\n\nQuestion: Landolt C and snellen e acuity: differences in strabismus amblyopia?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found a small but measurable difference between Landolt C and Snellen E acuity in patients with strabismus amblyopia, with Snellen E yielding slightly higher acuity values by an average of 0.55 lines. Although the difference is small, it is consistent and quantifiable, indicating that the optotypes do not perform identically in this population. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 451, "output_tokens": 90, "total_tokens": 541}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.102099999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_10", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"The objective of the current study is to determine to what extent the reduction of Chile's traffic fatalities and injuries during 2000-2012 was related to the police traffic enforcement increment registered after the introduction of its 2005 traffic law reform.\", \"A unique dataset with assembled information from public institutions and analyses based on ordinary least square and robust random effects models was carried out. Dependent variables were traffic fatality and severe injury rates per population and vehicle fleet. Independent variables were: (1) presence of new national traffic law; (2) police officers per population; (3) number of traffic tickets per police officer; and (4) interaction effect of number of traffic tickets per police officer with traffic law reform. Oil prices, alcohol consumption, proportion of male population 15-24 years old, unemployment, road infrastructure investment, years' effects and regions' effects represented control variables.\", 'Empirical estimates from instrumental variables suggest that the enactment of the traffic law reform in interaction with number of traffic tickets per police officer is significantly associated with a decrease of 8% in traffic fatalities and 7% in severe injuries. Piecewise regression model results for the 2007-2012 period suggest that police traffic enforcement reduced traffic fatalities by 59% and severe injuries by 37%.']\n\nQuestion: Did Chile's traffic law reform push police enforcement?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study indicates that the traffic law reform interacted significantly with the number of traffic tickets per police officer, leading to notable reductions in fatalities and injuries. This suggests that the reform amplified the effect of police enforcement, implying a stronger enforcement effort post-reform. Therefore, the evidence supports that the reform did push police enforcement.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 360, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 429}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.246e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_100", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Female citizens of Sami (the indigenous people of Norway) municipalities in northern Norway have a low risk of breast cancer. The objective of this study was to describe the attendance rate and outcome of the Norwegian Breast Cancer Screening Program (NBCSP) in the Sami-speaking municipalities and a control group.', 'A retrospective registry-based study.', 'The 8 municipalities included in the administration area of the Sami language law (Sami) were matched with a control group of 11 municipalities (non-Sami). Population data were accessed from Statistics Norway. Data regarding invitations and outcome in the NBCSP during the period 2001-2010 was derived from the Cancer Registry of Norway (CRN). The NBCSP targets women aged 50-69 years. Rates and percentages were compared using chi-square test with a p-value<0.05 as statistical significant.', 'The attendance rate in the NBCSP was 78% in the Sami and 75% in the non-Sami population (p<0.01). The recall rates were 2.4 and 3.3% in the Sami and non-Sami population, respectively (p<0.01). The rate of invasive screen detected cancer was not significantly lower in the Sami group (p=0.14). The percentage of all breast cancers detected in the NBCSP among the Sami (67%) was lower compared with the non-Sami population (86%, p=0.06).']\n\nQuestion: Mammographic screening in Sami speaking municipalities and a control group. Are early outcome measures influenced by ethnicity?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The attendance rate and recall rate in the NBCSP were significantly different between the Sami and non-Sami populations, indicating variations in screening outcomes. Although the rate of invasive cancer detected was not significantly different, the lower percentage of breast cancers detected through screening in the Sami group suggests differences in early detection. These differences in key early outcome measures imply that ethnicity may influence screening outcomes.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 412, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 493}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.7352e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_101", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To explore whether electrochemiluminescence (ECL) assays can help improve prediction of time to type 1 diabetes in the TrialNet autoantibody-positive population.', 'TrialNet subjects who were positive for one or more autoantibodies (microinsulin autoantibody, GAD65 autoantibody [GADA], IA-2A, and ZnT8A) with available ECL-insulin autoantibody (IAA) and ECL-GADA data at their initial visit were analyzed; after a median follow-up of 24 months, 177 of these 1,287 subjects developed diabetes.', 'Univariate analyses showed that autoantibodies by radioimmunoassays (RIAs), ECL-IAA, ECL-GADA, age, sex, number of positive autoantibodies, presence of HLA DR3/4-DQ8 genotype, HbA1c, and oral glucose tolerance test (OGTT) measurements were all significantly associated with progression to diabetes. Subjects who were ECL positive had a risk of progression to diabetes within 6 years of 58% compared with 5% for the ECL-negative subjects (P<0.0001). Multivariate Cox proportional hazards models were compared, with the base model including age, sex, OGTT measurements, and number of positive autoantibodies by RIAs. The model with positivity for ECL-GADA and/or ECL-IAA was the best, and factors that remained significantly associated with time to diabetes were area under the curve (AUC) C-peptide, fasting C-peptide, AUC glucose, number of positive autoantibodies by RIAs, and ECL positivity. Adding ECL to the Diabetes Prevention Trial risk score (DPTRS) improved the receiver operating characteristic curves with AUC of 0.83 (P<0.0001).']\n\nQuestion: Do Electrochemiluminescence Assays Improve Prediction of Time to Type 1 Diabetes in Autoantibody-Positive TrialNet Subjects?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that ECL positivity for IAA and/or GADA significantly improves the prediction of progression to type 1 diabetes, with a much higher risk in ECL-positive individuals compared to ECL-negative ones. Adding ECL data to existing models, including the DPTRS, significantly improved predictive accuracy, as shown by the increased AUC and statistical significance. Therefore, electrochemiluminescence assays do improve prediction.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 510, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 601}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.531e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_102", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"Little is known about the validity and reliability of expert assessments of the quality of antimicrobial prescribing, despite their importance in antimicrobial stewardship. We investigated how infectious disease doctors' assessments compared with a reference standard (modal expert opinion) and with the assessments of their colleagues.\", 'Twenty-four doctors specialized in infectious diseases or clinical microbiology (16 specialists and 8 residents) from five hospitals were asked to assess the appropriateness of antimicrobial agents prescribed for a broad spectrum of indications in 56 paper cases. They were instructed how to handle guideline applicability and deviations. We created a reference standard of antimicrobial appropriateness using the modal assessment of 16 specialists. We calculated criterion validity and interrater and intrarater overall and specific agreement with an index expert (senior infectious disease physician) and analysed the influence of doctor characteristics on validity.', 'Specialists agreed with the reference standard in 80% of cases (range 75%-86%), with a sensitivity and specificity of 75% and 84%, respectively. This did not differ by clinical specialty, hospital or years of experience, and residents had similar results. Specialists agreed with the index expert in 76% of cases and the index expert agreed with his previous assessments in 71% of cases.']\n\nQuestion: Assessment of appropriate antimicrobial prescribing: do experts agree?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that specialists agreed with the reference standard (modal expert opinion) in 80% of cases, and residents performed similarly, indicating a reasonable level of agreement among experts. However, agreement was not perfect, with sensitivity at 75% and specificity at 84%, and intrarater agreement for the index expert was only 71%. Despite some variability, the overall results suggest that experts generally agree.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 354, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 446}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.4333999999999993e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_106", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"Breast cancer is the most common malignancy afflicting women, and the most common cancer overall in Jordan. A woman's decision to go for screening is influenced by her social support network. This study aims to explore Jordanian men's individual and contextual perspectives on women's breast cancer and their own role in the breast health of the females within their families.\", 'An explorative qualitative design was used to purposively recruit 24 married men aged 27 to 65\\xa0years (median 43\\xa0years) from four governorates in Jordan. Data in the form of interviews transcriptions was subjected to qualitative content analysis.', \"Three themes were identified: a) Supporting one's wife; b) Marital needs and obligations; c) Constrained by a culture of destiny and shame. The first theme was built on men's feelings of responsibility for the family's health and well-being, their experiences of encouraging their wives to seek health care and their providing counselling and instrumental support. The second theme emerged from men's views about other men's rejection of a wife inflicted by breast cancer, their own perceptions of diminished femininity due to mastectomy and their own concerns about protecting the family from the hereditary risk of breast cancer. The third theme was seen in men's perception of breast cancer as an inevitable act of God that is far away from one's own family, in associating breast cancer with improper behaviour and in their readiness to face the culture of Eib (shame).\"]\n\nQuestion: \"Would a man smell a rose then throw it away?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The provided study context discusses Jordanian men's supportive attitudes toward wives' breast health (including some rejection of cancer cases due to stigma or perceived femininity loss) but makes no reference whatsoever to roses, smelling flowers, or any analogous behavior. The question is therefore unanswerable from the given text, making a definitive yes/no impossible. This leaves \"maybe\" as the only reasonable selection among the options.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 492, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 575}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0008225, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_107", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"Research on stroke survivors' driving safety has typically used either self-reports or government records, but the extent to which the 2 may differ is not known. We compared government records and self-reports of motor vehicle collisions and driving convictions in a sample of stroke survivors.\", 'The 56 participants were originally recruited for a prospective study on driving and community re-integration post-stroke; the study population consisted of moderately impaired stroke survivors without severe communication disorders who had been referred for a driving assessment. The driving records of the 56 participants for the 5 years before study entry and the 1-year study period were acquired with written consent from the Ministry of Transportation of Ontario (MTO), Canada. Self-reports of collisions and convictions were acquired via a semistructured interview and then compared with the MTO records.', 'Forty-three participants completed the study. For 7 (13.5%) the MTO records did not match the self-reports regarding collision involvement, and for 9 (17.3%) the MTO records did not match self-reports regarding driving convictions. The kappa coefficient for the correlation between MTO records and self-reports was 0.52 for collisions and 0.47 for convictions (both in the moderate range of agreement). When both sources of data were consulted, up to 56 percent more accidents and up to 46 percent more convictions were identified in the study population in the 5 years before study entry compared to when either source was used alone.']\n\nQuestion: Department of Transportation vs self-reported data on motor vehicle collisions and driving convictions for stroke survivors: do they agree?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found discrepancies between self-reports and government records, with 13.5% of participants differing on collision involvement and 17.3% on convictions. The kappa coefficients (0.52 for collisions, 0.47 for convictions) indicate only moderate agreement, not full concordance. Therefore, the two data sources do not fully agree.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 411, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 492}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.7281e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_108", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Longer duration of neoadjuvant (NA) imatinib\\xa0(IM) used for locally advanced (LA) gastrointestinal stromal tumours (GIST) is not based on biology of the tumour reflected by kit mutation analysis.', 'LA or locally recurrent (LR) GIST treated with NA IM from May 2008 to March 2015 from a prospective database were included in\\xa0the analysis. Archived formalin-fixed paraffin-embedded tissues (FFPE) were used for testing KIT exons 9, 11, 13 and 17 by PCR.', 'One hundred twenty-five patients with LA or LR GIST were treated with NA IM. Forty-five patients (36\\xa0%) had undergone c-kit mutation testing. Exon 11 was seen in 25 patients (55.5\\xa0%), 3 with exon 9 (6.7\\xa0%) and 2 with exon 13 (4.4\\xa0%). Twelve were wild type (26.6\\xa0%) and \\xa03 (6.7 %) were declared uninterpretable. Response rate (RR) for the exon 11 mutants was higher than the non-exon 11 mutant group (84 vs. 40\\xa0%, p\\u2009=\\u20090.01). Disease stabilization rate (DSR) rates were also higher in the exon 11 subgroup than non-exon 11 group (92 vs. 75\\xa0%). Eighty-four per cent exon 11 and 75\\xa0% non-exon 11 mutants were surgical candidates. Patients undergoing surgery had significantly improved event free survival (EFS) (p\\u2009<\\u20090.001) compared to patients not undergoing surgery, with the same trend seen in OS (p\\u2009=\\u20090.021). Patients with a SD on response to NA IM had a lower EFS (p\\u2009=\\u20090.076) and OS compared to patients achieving CR/PR. There were no differences between the various exon variants in terms of outcomes and responses']\n\nQuestion: Neoadjuvant Imatinib in Locally Advanced Gastrointestinal stromal Tumours, Will Kit Mutation Analysis Be a Pathfinder?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data show that patients with exon 11 mutations had significantly higher response and disease stabilization rates compared to non-exon 11 mutants, indicating a biological impact on treatment response. However, the study concludes there were no differences in outcomes between various exon variants, and longer duration of neoadjuvant imatinib is not based on tumor biology from KIT mutations. Thus, KIT mutation analysis does not clearly guide treatment duration or serve as a definitive pathfinder.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 587, "output_tokens": 100, "total_tokens": 687}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 5.1677e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_110", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Although there is evidence for the influential role of transformational leadership on health outcomes, researchers have used either attitude outcomes (e.g. job satisfaction) or softer health measures, such as general well-being. Specific measures of well-being such as sleep quality have not been used, despite its association with working conditions.', 'A longitudinal design was used to collect data from Danish healthcare workers at time 1 in 2005 (n = 447) and 18 months later at time 2 in 2007 (n = 274). Structural equation modelling was used to investigate the relationships between transformational leadership, self-efficacy and sleep quality at both time points independently (cross-sectionally) and longitudinally.', \"For all constructs, time 2 measures were influenced by the baseline level. Direct relationships between transformational leadership and sleep quality were found. This relationship was negative cross-sectionally at both time points, but positive between baseline and follow-up. The relationship between leadership and employees' sleep quality was not mediated by employees' self-efficacy.\"]\n\nQuestion: Does self-efficacy mediate the relationship between transformational leadership behaviours and healthcare workers' sleep quality?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study explicitly states that \"the relationship between leadership and employees' sleep quality was not mediated by employees' self-efficacy.\" This directly answers the question about mediation. Therefore, self-efficacy does not serve as a mediator in this context.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 318, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 373}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.8077999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_112", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['From 2000 to 2007, 344 patients underwent pancreatoduodenectomy for PA. Fifty-three patients (elevated group) had preoperatively elevated serum CA 19-9 levels (>400 IU/ml) after resolution of obstructive jaundice. Of these, 27 patients had high levels (400-899 IU/ml (HL)) and 26 patients had very high levels>or=900 IU/ml (VHL). Fifty patients with normal preoperative serum CA 19-9 levels (<37 IU/ml) comprised the control group.', 'Median survival of the control group (n = 50) versus elevated group (n = 53) was 22 versus 15 months (p = 0.02) and overall 3-year survival was 32% versus 14% (p = 0.03). There was no statistical difference in the median and 3-year overall survival between patients with HL and VHL. Patients in the elevated group who normalized their CA 19-9 levels after surgery (n = 11) had a survival equivalent to patients in the control group.']\n\nQuestion: Very high serum CA 19-9 levels: a contraindication to pancreaticoduodenectomy?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data show that while elevated CA 19-9 levels are associated with worse survival, there was no significant difference in survival between the high level (400\u2013899 IU/ml) and very high level (\u2265900 IU/ml) groups. Additionally, patients with elevated levels who normalized after surgery had survival similar to the control group, suggesting surgery still provides benefit. Therefore, very high CA 19-9 levels alone should not preclude surgery.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 358, "output_tokens": 103, "total_tokens": 461}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.5718000000000006e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_113", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Demonstrate that the rabbit may be used in the training of surgery, in addition to present its perioperative care.', 'Thirty two animals, with age and weight, respectively, from 3 to 5.5 months old and 3000 to 4200 grams, were undergone different periods of pre-operative fasting, exclusive intramuscular anesthesia (ketamine+xylazine), laparotomy with total gastrectomy and total splenectomy. It was dosed the pre-operative (initial) and post-surgical (end) serum blood glucose, in addition to quantify the gastric content after the resection of the part.', 'The anesthetical-surgical procedure presented a mortality rate of 3.125% (1:32) and a morbidity rate of 6.25% (2:32). It was evidenced an initial mean blood glucose = 199.4 mg/dl and the end = 326.1 mg/dl. In spite of extended fasting (minimum of 2 hours for the absolute fasting and maximum of 8.5 hours for liquids, and 20.5 hours for solids) all animals presented at the end of the surgical procedure any gastric content and a blood glucose increase. Those with fasting for liquids and solids when compared to the quantity of solid gastric content, presented a moderate negative degree of correlation.']\n\nQuestion: Perioperative care in an animal model for training in abdominal surgery: is it necessary a preoperative fasting?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study indicates that despite extended periods of preoperative fasting, all animals still presented gastric content at the end of the surgical procedure. Therefore, the results suggest that preoperative fasting is not effective in ensuring an empty stomach in this rabbit model.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 376, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 428}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:10.370472+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000172, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_119", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Effective musical communication requires conveyance of the intended message in a manner perceptible to the receiver. Communication disorders that impair transmitting or decoding of structural features of music (e.g., pitch, timbre) and/or symbolic representation may result in atypical musical communication, which can have a negative impact on music therapy interventions.', 'This study compared recognition of symbolic representation of emotions or movements in music by two groups of children with different communicative characteristics: severe to profound hearing loss (using cochlear implants [CI]) and autism spectrum disorder (ASD). Their responses were compared to those of children with typical-development and normal hearing (TD-NH). Accuracy was examined as a function of communicative status, emotional or movement category, and individual characteristics.', 'Participants listened to recorded musical excerpts conveying emotions or movements and matched them with labels. Measures relevant to auditory and/or language function were also gathered.', 'There was no significant difference between the ASD and TD-NH groups in identification of musical emotions or movements. However, the CI group was significantly less accurate than the other two groups in identification of both emotions and movements. Mixed effects logistic regression revealed different patterns of accuracy for specific emotions as a function of group.']\n\nQuestion: Do communication disorders extend to musical messages?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context indicates that children with severe to profound hearing loss (using cochlear implants) were significantly less accurate in identifying musical emotions and movements, suggesting impaired musical communication. This implies that certain communication disorders, particularly those affecting auditory processing, can extend to the perception of musical messages. Therefore, the evidence supports that musical communication can be affected.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 325, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 398}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.0375e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_12", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Specific markers for differentiation of nonalcoholic (NASH) from alcoholic steatohepatitis (ASH) are lacking. We investigated the role of routine laboratory parameters in distinguishing NASH from ASH.', 'Liver biopsies performed at our hospital over a 10-year period were reviewed, 95 patients with steatohepatitis identified and their data prior to biopsy reevaluated. The diagnosis NASH or ASH was assigned (other liver diseases excluded) on the basis of the biopsy and history of alcohol consumption (<140 g/week). Logistic regression models were used for analysis.', 'NASH was diagnosed in 58 patients (61%; 30 f) and ASH in 37 (39%; 9 f). High-grade fibrosis (59% vs. 19%, P<0.0001) and an AST/ALT ratio>1 (54.1% vs 20.7%, P = 0.0008) were more common in ASH. The MCV was elevated in 53% of ASH patients and normal in all NASH patients (P<0.0001). Multivariate analysis identified the MCV (P = 0.0013), the AST/ALT ratio (P = 0.011) and sex (P = 0.0029) as relevant regressors (aROC = 0.92). The AST/ALT ratio (P<0.0001) and age (P = 0.00049) were independent predictors of high-grade fibrosis. Differences in MCV were more marked in high-grade fibrosis.']\n\nQuestion: Differentiation of nonalcoholic from alcoholic steatohepatitis: are routine laboratory markers useful?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that routine laboratory parameters such as MCV, AST/ALT ratio, and sex were significant predictors in differentiating NASH from ASH, with a high area under the ROC curve (aROC = 0.92), indicating strong diagnostic accuracy. Additionally, MCV was normal in all NASH patients but elevated in over half of ASH patients, highlighting its utility. Therefore, routine laboratory markers are useful in distinguishing between the two conditions.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 405, "output_tokens": 118, "total_tokens": 523}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.0555e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_120", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['It is postulated that some aspects of methotrexate toxicity may be related to its action as an anti-folate. Folic acid (FA) is often given as an adjunct to methotrexate therapy, but there is no conclusive proof that it decreases the toxicity of methotrexate and there is a theoretical risk that it may decrease the efficacy of methotrexate.', 'To look at the effect of stopping FA supplementation in UK rheumatoid arthritis (RA) patients established on methotrexate<20 mg weekly and FA 5 mg daily, to report all toxicity (including absolute changes in haematological and liver enzyme indices) and to report changes in the efficacy of methotrexate.', 'In a prospective, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled study, 75 patients who were established on methotrexate<20 mg weekly and FA 5 mg daily were asked to stop their FA and were randomized to one of two groups: placebo or FA 5 mg daily. Patients were evaluated for treatment toxicity and efficacy before entry and then at intervals of 3 months for 1 yr.', 'Overall, 25 (33%) patients concluded the study early, eight (21%) in the group remaining on FA and 17 (46%) in the placebo group (P = 0.02). Two patients in the placebo group discontinued because of neutropenia. At 9 months there was an increased incidence of nausea in the placebo group (45 vs. 7%, P = 0.001). The placebo group had significantly lower disease activity on a few of the variables measured, but these were probably not of clinical significance.']\n\nQuestion: Do patients with rheumatoid arthritis established on methotrexate and folic acid 5 mg daily need to continue folic acid supplements long term?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that patients who stopped folic acid supplementation had higher rates of study discontinuation, including due to neutropenia, and experienced more nausea, indicating increased toxicity. Although disease activity was slightly better in the placebo group, the differences were not clinically significant, while the increased toxicity was a concern. Therefore, continuing folic acid appears beneficial in reducing methotrexate-related toxicity.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 456, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 539}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.0676e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_124", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['DNA was collected for genotyping from 73 term newborns suffering from TTN and 55 healthy controls from a Caucasian cohort.', 'TTN infants were more likely to be male (70% vs. 49%; p<0.05), had a lower mean birthweight (3120 +/- 450 vs. 3396 +/- 504 g; p<0.001) and gestational age (GA) (38.4 +/- 1.2 vs. 39.4 +/- 1.3 weeks; p<0.001) and were more often delivered by caesarean section (CS) (71% vs. 26%; p<0.001). The beta1Ser49Gly polymorphism differed significantly between cases and controls. Multivariate analysis provided beta1Gly49 homozygotes with higher risk for TTN (OR 18.5; 95%CI 1.5-229; p = 0.023) than beta1Ser49 allele carrier. Further analysis showed significant association of T-47C, A46G, C79G and C491T (TACC) haplotype in ADRB2 gene with TTN (p = 0.048).']\n\nQuestion: Transient tachypnea of the newborn (TTN): a role for polymorphisms in the beta-adrenergic receptor (ADRB) encoding genes?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context indicates that the beta1Ser49Gly polymorphism and the TACC haplotype in the ADRB2 gene are significantly associated with TTN, with statistical support (p = 0.023 and p = 0.048, respectively). These findings suggest a genetic influence of ADRB gene polymorphisms on TTN risk. Therefore, the evidence supports a role for these polymorphisms in TTN.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 406, "output_tokens": 99, "total_tokens": 505}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.8726e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_125", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['There is increasing pressure on mental health providers to reduce the duration of treatments, while retaining level of quality and effectiveness. The risk is that the population is underserved and therefore needs new treatment episodes. The primary aim of this study was to investigate whether duration of treatment and return into mental health care were related.', \"This study examined Dutch patients with an initial treatment episode in 2009 or 2010 in specialized mental health settings for depressive disorder (N\\xa0=\\xa085,754). Follow-up data about treatment episodes were available up until 2013. The data set included demographic (age, gender), and clinical factors (comorbidity with other DSM-IV Axis; scores on the 'Global Assessment of Functioning'). Cox regression analyses were used to assess whether duration of treatment and relapse into mental health care were related.\", 'The majority of patients did not return into mental health care (86\\xa0%). Patients with a shorter duration of treatment (5-250\\xa0min; 251-500\\xa0min and 751-1000\\xa0min) were slightly more likely to return (reference group:>1000\\xa0min) (HR 1.19 95\\xa0% CI 1.13-1.26; HR 1.11 95\\xa0% CI 1.06-1.17; HR 1.18 95\\xa0% CI 1.11-1.25), adjusted for demographic and clinical variables.']\n\nQuestion: Is duration of psychological treatment for depression related to return into treatment?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that patients with shorter treatment durations were slightly more likely to return to mental health care, even after adjusting for demographic and clinical factors. This indicates a relationship between treatment duration and relapse into care. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 426, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 480}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.5646000000000004e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_128", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To determine under what conditions lay people and health professionals find it acceptable for a physician to breach confidentiality to protect the wife of a patient with a sexually transmitted disease (STD).', 'In a study in France, breaching confidentiality in 48 scenarios were accepted by 144 lay people, 10 psychologists and 7 physicians. The scenarios were all possible combinations of five factors: severity of the disease (severe, lethal); time taken to discuss this with (little time, much time); intent to inform the spouse about the disease (none, one of these days, immediately); intent to adopt protective behaviours (no intent, intent); and decision to consult an expert in STDs (yes, no), 2 x 2 x 3 x 2 x 2. The importance and interactions of each factor were determined, at the group level, by performing analyses of variance and constructing graphs.', 'The concept of breaching confidentiality to protect a wife from her husband\\'s STD was favoured much more by lay people and psychologists than by physicians (mean ratings 11.76, 9.28 and 2.90, respectively, on a scale of 0-22). The patient\\'s stated intentions to protect his wife and to inform her of the disease had the greatest impact on acceptability. A cluster analysis showed groups of lay participants who found breaching confidentiality \"always acceptable\" (n = 14), \"depending on the many circumstances\" (n = 87), requiring \"consultation with an expert\" (n = 30) and \"never acceptable (n = 13)\".']\n\nQuestion: Do French lay people and health professionals find it acceptable to breach confidentiality to protect a patient's wife from a sexually transmitted disease?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study indicates that while the level of acceptability varies significantly between groups and depends on specific circumstances, there is a general tendency to find it acceptable under certain conditions. Since the participants' ratings and cluster analysis show that most individuals do not categorically reject the practice, \"maybe\" is the most accurate reflection of the nuanced findings.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 433, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 503}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:29.045796+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00021325, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_134", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['This paper investigates the impact of geographic scale (census tract, zip code, and county) on the detection of disparities in breast cancer mortality among three ethnic groups in Texas (period 1995-2005). Racial disparities were quantified using both relative (RR) and absolute (RD) statistics that account for the population size and correct for unreliable rates typically observed for minority groups and smaller geographic units. Results were then correlated with socio-economic status measured by the percentage of habitants living below the poverty level.', 'African-American and Hispanic women generally experience higher mortality than White non-Hispanics, and these differences are especially significant in the southeast metropolitan areas and southwest border of Texas. The proportion and location of significant racial disparities however changed depending on the type of statistic (RR versus RD) and the geographic level. The largest proportion of significant results was observed for the RD statistic and census tract data. Geographic regions with significant racial disparities for African-Americans and Hispanics frequently had a poverty rate above 10.00%.']\n\nQuestion: Identification of racial disparities in breast cancer mortality: does scale matter?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study explicitly shows that the detection of racial disparities in breast cancer mortality varies by geographic scale, with different results observed at census tract, zip code, and county levels. It also notes that the largest proportion of significant disparities was found using census tract data and the absolute disparity measure (RD). This indicates that scale does influence the identification of disparities.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 301, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 376}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.8871e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_136", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Disorders of consciousness (DOC) diagnosis relies on the presence or absence of purposeful motor responsiveness, which characterizes the minimally conscious state (MCS) and the unresponsive wakefulness syndrome (UWS), respectively. Functional neuroimaging studies have raised the question of possible residual conscious awareness also in clinically-defined UWS patients. The aim of our study was to identify electrophysiological parameters, by means of a transcranial magnetic stimulation approach, which might potentially express the presence of residual networks sustaining fragmentary behavioral patterns, even when no conscious behavior can be observed.', 'We enrolled 25 severe DOC patients, following post-anoxic or traumatic brain injury and 20 healthy individuals (HC) as control group. Baseline electrophysiological evaluation evidenced, in comparison to HC, a partial preservation of cortical effective connectivity and excitability in clinically defined MCS, whereas these components were absent in clinically defined UWS. Then, we applied an anodal transcranial direct current stimulation (a-tDCS) protocol over the orbitofrontal cortex.', 'a-tDCS was able to boost cortical connectivity and excitability in all HC, MCS, and to unmask such excitability/connectivity in some UWS patients.']\n\nQuestion: Can transcranial direct current stimulation be useful in differentiating unresponsive wakefulness syndrome from minimally conscious state patients?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that anodal transcranial direct current stimulation (a-tDCS) enhanced cortical connectivity and excitability in both healthy controls and minimally conscious state (MCS) patients, and importantly, it unmasked such activity in some unresponsive wakefulness syndrome (UWS) patients. This differential response to a-tDCS\u2014where MCS patients show preserved and boostable cortical function while UWS patients generally do not, except in cases where residual function is unmasked\u2014suggests a potential utility in differentiation. Therefore, a-tDCS may help distinguish between UWS and MCS by revealing residual cortical excitability and connectivity not evident at baseline.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 352, "output_tokens": 137, "total_tokens": 489}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.8692e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_137", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Aromatase inhibitors (AIs) are an effective treatment for postmenopausal women with hormone receptor-positive breast cancer. However, patients receiving AIs report a higher incidence of musculoskeletal symptoms and bone fractures; the mechanism and risk factors for this correlation are not well studied. The aim of this study was to correlate these musculoskeletal symptoms and bone fractures in patients receiving AIs with bone mineral density (BMD), previous tamoxifen use, and administration of calcium/bisphosphonate (Ca/Bis).', 'We reviewed charts of 856 patients with hormone receptor-positive nonmetastatic breast cancer seen at our institution between January 1999 and October 2007. A total of 316 patients met the inclusion criteria of treatment with one of the AIs for>or = 3 months and availability of a dualenergy X-ray absorptiometry (DEXA) during this treatment. Arthralgia, generalized bone pain and/or myalgia, bone fracture after beginning AIs, any tamoxifen treatment, and Ca/Bis therapy were recorded.', 'Our study demonstrates a significant association between symptoms and DEXA-BMD results (P<.001). Similarly, the group receiving tamoxifen before AIs had fewer patients with arthralgia or generalized bone pain/myalgia or bone fracture (P<.001). Furthermore, the group receiving AIs plus Ca/Bis had more patients without musculoskeletal symptoms and had fewer fractures. Finally, the group receiving steroidal AIs compared with nonsteroidal AIs had more patients with arthralgia or generalized bone pain and/or myalgia, and bone fractures (P<.001).']\n\nQuestion: Aromatase inhibitor-related musculoskeletal symptoms: is preventing osteoporosis the key to eliminating these symptoms?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows a significant association between musculoskeletal symptoms and low bone mineral density (BMD), and that calcium/bisphosphonate use reduced both symptoms and fractures. However, the reduction in symptoms with Ca/Bis and prior tamoxifen use suggests that while bone health is important, it may not be the sole factor. Additionally, differences between steroidal and nonsteroidal AIs imply a direct drug effect on symptoms beyond just bone density.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 513, "output_tokens": 120, "total_tokens": 633}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.8422999999999994e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_139", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Nd:YAG laser-induced thermo therapy (LITT) of rat brains is associated with blood-brain barrier (BBB) permeability changes. We address the question of whether LITT-induced locoregional disruption of the BBB could possibly allow a locoregional passage of chemotherapeutic agents into brain tissue to treat malignant glioma.STUDY DESIGN/', 'CD Fischer rats were subject to LITT of the left forebrain. Disruption of the BBB was analyzed using Evans blue and immunohistochemistry (IH). Animals were perfused with paclitaxel, and high-pressure liquid chromatography (HPLC) was employed to analyze the content of paclitaxel in brain and plasma samples.', 'LITT induces an opening of the BBB as demonstrated by locoregional extravasation of Evans blue, C3C, fibrinogen, and IgM. HPLC proved the passage of paclitaxel across the disrupted BBB.']\n\nQuestion: Locoregional opening of the rodent blood-brain barrier for paclitaxel using Nd:YAG laser-induced thermo therapy: a new concept of adjuvant glioma therapy?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study demonstrates that Nd:YAG laser-induced thermo therapy (LITT) disrupts the blood-brain barrier (BBB), allowing paclitaxel to pass into brain tissue, as confirmed by Evans blue extravasation and HPLC analysis. This locoregional BBB opening suggests a potential method to deliver chemotherapeutic agents like paclitaxel to treat malignant glioma. Therefore, the findings support the concept of using LITT as an adjuvant therapy.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 317, "output_tokens": 105, "total_tokens": 422}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.3007e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_140", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Despite surgical refinements, perioperative use of tracheobronchoscopy (TBS) as part of surgical approach to esophageal atresia (EA) is still controversial. The purpose of this study was to evaluate the influence of preoperative TBS in newborns with EA in preventing complications and improving diagnosis and surgical treatment.', 'In the period ranging from 1997 to 2003, 62 patients with EA underwent preoperative TBS. The procedure was carried out with flexible bronchoscope maintaining spontaneous breathing. When a wide carinal fistula was found, this was mechanically occluded by Fogarty catheter and cannulated with rigid bronchoscopy. Type of EA, surgical procedure variations caused by TBS, and associated anomalies not easily detectable were recorded.', 'Before TBS, the Gross classification of the 62 patients was as follows: type A, 9 patients; type B, none; type C, 51 patients. At TBS, however, 3 of 9 type A patients had an unsuspected proximal fistula (type B). These 3 patients, plus the 2 with H-type fistula, were repaired through a cervical approach. In 4 patients, previously undetected malformations of the respiratory tree (2 aberrant right upper bronchus and 2 hypoplastic bronchi) were found at TBS. Carinal fistulas in 14 type C patients were occluded by Fogarty catheter to improve ventilation during repair. No complications were observed. Overall, TBS was clinically useful in 28 (45.2%) of 62 patients, including 15 (24.2%) of 62 infants in whom it was crucial in modifying the surgical approach.']\n\nQuestion: Preoperative tracheobronchoscopy in newborns with esophageal atresia: does it matter?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that preoperative tracheobronchoscopy (TBS) was clinically useful in 45.2% of patients and crucial in modifying the surgical approach in 24.2%. It led to the detection of previously undiagnosed anomalies and altered management, such as the use of a cervical approach or intraoperative ventilation strategies. Therefore, preoperative TBS significantly impacted diagnosis and treatment.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 469, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 558}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.2199e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_141", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To clarify whether horizontal canal ocular reflex is influenced by otolith organs input.', 'The subjects were seven healthy humans. The right ear was stimulated using ice-water. Each subject was kept in a left-ear-down position for 20 s and then repositioned to a prone position, a right-ear-down position and a supine position with 20 s intervals. Nystagmus was analysed using three-dimensional video-oculography.', 'Eye movements in the supine position and the prone position were not in a symmetric fashion. Nystagmus in the left-ear-down position and the right-ear-down position were not symmetric either. These phenomena indicate that the axis of the eyeball rotation was affected by the shift of the direction of gravity exerted on the head.']\n\nQuestion: Is horizontal semicircular canal ocular reflex influenced by otolith organs input?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The observed asymmetry in nystagmus across different head positions indicates that gravity\u2014detected by the otolith organs\u2014affects the horizontal semicircular canal ocular reflex. Since the axis of eye rotation changed with head orientation relative to gravity, otolith input must be influencing the reflex. Therefore, the evidence supports that the reflex is influenced by otolith organs.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 255, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 334}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.6004999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_143", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To determine whether the host immune response to gonorrhoea provides limited serovar specific protection from reinfection.', '508 episodes of gonorrhoea diagnosed at a city centre genitourinary medicine clinic including 22 patients with multiple infections over a 4 year period.', 'Patients with recurrent gonococcal infection were analysed with respect to the initial and subsequent serovars isolated.', 'No significant difference was seen in the prevalence of serovars isolated following a repeat infection compared with those without repeat infections. The site of the initial infection did not appear to influence the subsequent serovar isolated.']\n\nQuestion: Serovar specific immunity to Neisseria gonorrhoeae: does it exist?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant difference in the serovars isolated during repeat infections compared to first infections, and the site of initial infection did not influence the subsequent serovovar. This suggests that prior infection does not confer strong serovar-specific protection. Therefore, the evidence does not support the existence of serovar-specific immunity.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 221, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 294}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.2991e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_148", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['First, to establish whether a deprivation gradient in all-cause mortality exists for all ethnic groups within New Zealand; second, if such gradients do exist, whether their absolute slopes are the same; and third, if such gradients exist, what impact the unequal deprivation distributions of the different ethnic groups have on the observed ethnic inequalities in life expectancy at birth.', 'Abridged lifetables for the period 1999-2003 were constructed using standard demographic methods for each of four ethnic groups (Asian, Pacific, Maori and European) by NZDep2001 quintile and sex. Gradients were estimated by fitting generalised linear models to the quintile-specific life expectancy estimates for each ethnic group (by sex). The contribution of variation in deprivation distributions to inter-ethnic inequalities in life expectancy was estimated by re-weighting the quintile-specific mortality rates for each ethnic group using weights derived from the European deprivation distribution and recalculating the lifetable.', 'All four ethnic groups exhibit deprivation gradients in all-cause mortality (life expectancy). Maori show the steepest gradients, with slopes approximately 25% steeper than those of Europeans for both males and females. By contrast, gradients among Asian and Pacific peoples are shallower than those of their European counterparts.']\n\nQuestion: Do all ethnic groups in New Zealand exhibit socio-economic mortality gradients?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Yes, all ethnic groups in New Zealand exhibit socio-economic mortality gradients, as stated in the context: \"All four ethnic groups exhibit deprivation gradients in all-cause mortality (life expectancy).\" The gradients vary in steepness across groups, but they are present for each group.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 351, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 410}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.0820999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_149", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Unicompartmental replacement can be an alternative to tibial osteotomy in younger, active patients with unicompartmental knee disease. In unicompartmental replacement, the other compartments and knee ligaments are largely untouched. Therefore, it was hypothesized that the knee kinematics after unicompartmental replacement may also be unchanged. To test this hypothesis, knee kinematics and quadriceps tension were recorded before and after replacement with a unicompartmental design and then with a tricompartmental design.', 'Six human cadaver knees were tested before implantation, after implantation with a bicruciate-retaining unicompartmental knee prosthesis, and after implantation with a posterior cruciate-retaining tricompartmental knee prosthesis. The unicompartmental prosthesis was initially implanted, and it was then revised to a total condylar knee replacement. The knee kinematics were measured with use of an electromagnetic tracking device while the knee was put through dynamic simulated stair-climbing under peak flexion moments of approximately 40 N-m. Quadriceps tension was also measured for all three conditions.', 'No significant differences in tibial axial rotation were noted between the intact and unicompartmental conditions. However, tricompartmental replacement significantly affected tibial axial rotation (p = 0.001). Femoral rollback was not significantly affected by either unicompartmental or tricompartmental arthroplasty. Quadriceps tension was also similar among all three conditions.']\n\nQuestion: Can normal knee kinematics be restored with unicompartmental knee replacement?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant differences in tibial axial rotation between the intact and unicompartmental conditions, and femoral rollback was not significantly affected by unicompartmental arthroplasty. Additionally, quadriceps tension remained similar across all conditions, suggesting preserved function. These results indicate that unicompartmental knee replacement maintains normal knee kinematics.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 407, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 483}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.6497e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_15", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Breathlessness is one of the most distressing symptoms experienced by patients with advanced cancer and noncancer diagnoses alike. Often, severity of breathlessness increases quickly, calling for rapid symptom control. Oral, buccal, and parenteral routes of provider-controlled drug administration have been described. It is unclear whether patient-controlled therapy (PCT) systems would be an additional treatment option.', 'To investigate whether intravenous opioid PCT can be an effective therapeutic method to reduce breathlessness in patients with advanced disease. Secondary aims were to study the feasibility and acceptance of opioid PCT in patients with refractory breathlessness.', 'This was a pilot observational study with 18 inpatients with advanced disease and refractory breathlessness receiving opioid PCT. Breathlessness was measured on a self-reported numeric rating scale. Richmond Agitation Sedation Scale scores, Palliative Performance Scale scores, vital signs, and a self-developed patient satisfaction questionnaire were used for measuring secondary outcomes. Descriptive and interference analyses (Friedman test) and post hoc analyses (Wilcoxon tests and Bonferroni corrections) were performed.', 'Eighteen of 815 patients (advanced cancer; median age\\xa0=\\xa057.5\\xa0years [range 36-81]; 77.8% female) received breathlessness symptom control with opioid PCT; daily morphine equivalent dose at Day 1 was median\\xa0=\\xa020.3\\xa0mg (5.0-49.6\\xa0mg); Day 2: 13.0\\xa0mg (1.0-78.5\\xa0mg); Day 3: 16.0\\xa0mg (8.3-47.0\\xa0mg). Numeric rating scale of current breathlessness decreased (baseline: median\\xa0=\\xa05 [range 1-10]; Day 1: median\\xa0=\\xa04 [range 0-8], P\\xa0<\\xa00.01; Day 2: median\\xa0=\\xa04 [range 0-5], P\\xa0<\\xa00.01). Physiological parameters were stable over time. On Day 3, 12/12 patients confirmed that this mode of application provided relief of breathlessness.']\n\nQuestion: Patient-Controlled Therapy of Breathlessness in Palliative Care: A New Therapeutic Concept for Opioid Administration?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study demonstrates that patient-controlled intravenous opioids effectively reduced breathlessness in patients with advanced disease, with significant symptom relief and high patient acceptance. The results support the feasibility and potential of patient-controlled therapy (PCT) as a new therapeutic approach in palliative care. Therefore, the evidence aligns with the concept being viable and promising.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 582, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 654}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.8522e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_150", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['There are 71 previously untreated patients with cytological or histological evidence of primary lung cancer who were admitted to the oncology department between November 2013 and August 2014. Forty-five healthy individuals with age, sex and BMI matching the lung cancer patients, were recruited to take part in the study as a control group. Leptin levels were measured quantitatively by using a microELISA kit.', 'The serum leptin levels at diagnosis were significantly lower in lung cancer patients than those in control subjects (4.75\u00b14.91 ng/ml, 9.67\u00b18.02 ng/ml; p<0.001). We did not find any significant difference in leptin values related to clinicopathological parameters such as ECOG PS, weight loss, histological type, disease stage and TNM classification. Nevertheless, we demonstrated a significant correlation between serum leptin levels and BMI in lung cancer patients (correlation coefficient: 0.303; p>0.010). The analysis of serum leptin values did not show any association with the overall survival of the patients.']\n\nQuestion: Are serum leptin levels a prognostic factor in advanced lung cancer?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no association between serum leptin levels and overall survival in lung cancer patients, and no significant differences were observed with respect to clinicopathological parameters. This suggests that leptin levels do not serve as a prognostic factor in advanced lung cancer. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 331, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 389}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.9301e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_151", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To investigate if fetal gender (1) affects the risk of having an emergency department (ED) visit for asthma; and (2) is associated with adverse pregnancy outcomes among women who had at least one visit to the ED for asthma during pregnancy.', 'We linked two provincial administrative databases containing records on in-patient deliveries and ED visits. The study sample included women who delivered a live singleton baby between April 2003 and March 2004. Pregnant women who made at least one ED visit for asthma were counted as cases and the rest of the women as control subjects. We performed a multivariable analysis using logistic regression to model the risk of having an ED visit for asthma, with fetal gender being one of the predictors. In addition, a series of multivariable logistic regressions were also constructed separately for cases and controls for the following adverse delivery outcomes: low birth weight baby, preterm delivery, and delivery via Caesarian section.', 'Among 109,173 live singleton deliveries, 530 women had visited ED due to asthma during pregnancy. While having an ED visit for asthma was positively associated with teenage pregnancy, low income, and presence of pregnancy-induced hypertension, it was not associated with fetal gender (OR 1.01, 95% CI 0.85-1.19). Fetal gender was not a significant predictor of adverse pregnancy outcomes among women who had an asthma ED visit during pregnancy.']\n\nQuestion: Is fetal gender associated with emergency department visits for asthma during pregnancy?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant association between fetal gender and the risk of emergency department visits for asthma during pregnancy, with an odds ratio of 1.01 and a 95% confidence interval that includes 1 (0.85\u20131.19). This indicates that fetal gender does not meaningfully predict the likelihood of an asthma-related ED visit. Therefore, the evidence supports that there is no association.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 391, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 480}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.6661e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_152", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['This study sought to evaluate mutations in genes encoding the slow component of the cardiac delayed rectifier K+ current (I(Ks)) channel in familial atrial fibrillation (AF).', 'Although AF can have a genetic etiology, links between inherited gene defects and acquired factors such as atrial stretch have not been explored.', 'Mutation screening of the KCNQ1, KCNE1, KCNE2, and KCNE3 genes was performed in 50 families with AF. The effects of mutant protein on cardiac I(Ks) activation were evaluated using electrophysiological studies and human atrial action potential modeling.', 'One missense KCNQ1 mutation, R14C, was identified in 1 family with a high prevalence of hypertension. Atrial fibrillation was present only in older individuals who had developed atrial dilation and who were genotype positive. Patch-clamp studies of wild-type or R14C KCNQ1 expressed with KCNE1 in CHO cells showed no statistically significant differences between wild-type and mutant channel kinetics at baseline, or after activation of adenylate cyclase with forskolin. After exposure to hypotonic solution to elicit cell swelling/stretch, mutant channels showed a marked increase in current, a leftward shift in the voltage dependence of activation, altered channel kinetics, and shortening of the modeled atrial action potential duration.']\n\nQuestion: Stretch-sensitive KCNQ1 mutation A link between genetic and environmental factors in the pathogenesis of atrial fibrillation?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The R14C mutation in KCNQ1 showed altered channel behavior only under cell swelling conditions (mimicking atrial stretch), indicating that the genetic mutation interacts with mechanical stress to promote AF. This demonstrates a direct link between a genetic defect and an environmental factor (atrial stretch) in the development of atrial fibrillation. Therefore, the evidence supports a stretch-sensitive mechanism connecting genetic and acquired factors.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 380, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 468}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.578e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_154", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['We explored whether QT corrected dispersion (QTcD) can identify left ventricular hypertrophy (LVH) in hypertensives.', 'We enrolled 100 hypertensive patients (study group) and 30 normotensive subjects (control group). Echocardiography was performed to measure left ventricular mass and left ventricular mass index. Electrocardiogram was performed to measure QTcD.', \"LVH was present in 42 patients (42%) of the study group, none among controls. Hypertensive patients had significantly greater indices of LVH and QTcD compared with controls (p<0.001 for all). Similarly, among hypertensive patients, those with LVH had a significantly greater QTcD compared with those without (p<0.001). Pearson's correlation coefficient test demonstrated strongly positive correlations between QTcD and the indices of LVH (p<0.001 for all). Analysis of the receiver operating characteristic curves identified 60 ms as the optimal cut-off value of QTcD that best predicts LVH in hypertensives. Using this value, QTcD was able to predict LVH with a sensitivity of 92.9% and specificity 98.2%.\"]\n\nQuestion: Would corrected QT dispersion predict left ventricular hypertrophy in hypertensive patients?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found a strong positive correlation between corrected QT dispersion (QTcD) and left ventricular hypertrophy (LVH) in hypertensive patients, with high sensitivity and specificity at a cut-off of 60 ms. This indicates that QTcD is a reliable predictor of LVH in this population. Therefore, the evidence supports that QTc dispersion can predict LVH.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 355, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 438}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.3505e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_155", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Traumatic aortic injury (TAI) is a rare but life-threatening type of injury. We investigate whether the anatomy of the aortic arch influences the severity of aortic injury.', 'This is a retrospective study of twenty-two cases treated with TEVAR for TAI in our department from 2009 to 2014. Aortic injury was assessed in accordance with the recommendations of the Society of Vascular Surgery. We measured the aortic arch angle and the aortic arch index, based on the initial angio-CT scan, in each of the analyzed cases.', 'The mean aortic arch index and mean aortic arch angle were 6.8\\xa0cm and 58.3\u00b0, respectively, in the type I injury group; 4.4\\xa0cm and 45.9\u00b0 in the type III group; 3.3\\xa0cm and 37\u00b0 in the type IV group. There were substantial differences in both the aortic arch index and the aortic arch angle of the type III and IV groups. A multivariate analysis confirmed that the aortic arch angle was significantly associated with the occurrence of type III damage (OR 1.5; 95% CI 1.03-2.2).']\n\nQuestion: Traumatic aortic injury: does the anatomy of the aortic arch influence aortic trauma severity?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found substantial differences in aortic arch index and angle between injury types, with a multivariate analysis showing a significant association between aortic arch angle and type III injury. This indicates that anatomical variations in the aortic arch influence the severity of traumatic aortic injury. Therefore, the evidence supports a definitive influence.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 361, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 431}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.2631e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_161", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Earlier studies have demonstrated low peak oxygen uptake ((.)Vo(2)peak) in children with spina bifida. Low peak heart rate and low peak respiratory exchange ratio in these studies raised questions regarding the true maximal character of (.)Vo(2)peak values obtained with treadmill testing.', 'The aim of this study was to determine whether the Vo(2)peak measured during an incremental treadmill test is a true reflection of the maximum oxygen uptake ((.)Vo(2)max) in children who have spina bifida and are ambulatory.', 'A cross-sectional design was used for this study.', 'Twenty children who had spina bifida and were ambulatory participated. The (.)Vo(2)peak was measured during a graded treadmill exercise test. The validity of (.)Vo(2)peak measurements was evaluated by use of previously described guidelines for maximum exercise testing in children who are healthy, as well as differences between Vo(2)peak and (.)Vo(2) during a supramaximal protocol ((.)Vo(2)supramaximal).', 'The average values for (.)Vo(2)peak and normalized (.)Vo(2)peak were, respectively, 1.23 L/min (SD=0.6) and 34.1 mL/kg/min (SD=8.3). Fifteen children met at least 2 of the 3 previously described criteria; one child failed to meet any criteria. Although there were no significant differences between (.)Vo(2)peak and Vo(2)supramaximal, 5 children did show improvement during supramaximal testing.', 'These results apply to children who have spina bifida and are at least community ambulatory.']\n\nQuestion: Treadmill testing of children who have spina bifida and are ambulatory: does peak oxygen uptake reflect maximum oxygen uptake?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that although there were no significant differences between peak oxygen uptake and oxygen consumption during supramaximal testing, 5 out of 20 children showed improvement, suggesting that the peak values did not truly reflect maximum capacity in all cases. However, most children met standard criteria for maximal effort, indicating that peak oxygen uptake is generally a valid measure. Therefore, the best answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 458, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 542}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.091799999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_162", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To compare the probability of prenatal diagnosis (PND) and termination of pregnancy for fetal anomaly (TOPFA) between fetuses conceived by assisted reproductive techniques (ART) and spontaneously-conceived fetuses with congenital heart defects (CHD).', 'Population-based observational study.', 'Paris and surrounding suburbs.', 'Fetuses with CHD in the Paris registry of congenital malformations and cohort of children with CHD (Epicard).', 'Comparison of ART-conceived and spontaneously conceived fetuses taking into account potential confounders (maternal characteristics, multiplicity and year of birth or TOPFA).', 'Probability and gestational age at PND and TOPFA for ART-conceived versus spontaneously conceived fetuses.', 'The probability of PND (28.1% versus 34.6%, P = 0.077) and TOPFA (36.2% versus 39.2%, P = 0.677) were not statistically different between ART-conceived (n = 171) and spontaneously conceived (n = 4620) fetuses. Estimates were similar after adjustment for potential confounders. Gestational age at PND tended to be earlier for ART fetuses (23.1 versus 24.8 weeks, P = 0.05) but no statistical difference was found after adjustment for confounders. Gestational age at TOPFA was comparable between ART-conceived and spontaneously conceived fetuses.']\n\nQuestion: Is the probability of prenatal diagnosis or termination of pregnancy different for fetuses with congenital anomalies conceived following assisted reproductive techniques?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no statistically significant differences in the probability of prenatal diagnosis (PND) or termination of pregnancy for fetal anomaly (TOPFA) between fetuses conceived via assisted reproductive techniques (ART) and those conceived spontaneously. Although there was a trend toward earlier PND in ART-conceived fetuses, this difference was not significant after adjusting for confounders. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 410, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 494}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.751e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_163", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Ablation of persistent atrial fibrillation (AF) may require adjunctive methods of substrate modification. Both ablation-targeting complex fractionated atrial electrograms (CFAEs) recorded during AF and fractionated electrograms recorded during sinus rhythm (sinus rhythm fractionation [SRF]) have been described. However, the relationship of CFAEs with SRF is unclear.', 'Twenty patients (age 62 \u00b1 9 years, 13 males) with persistent AF and 9 control subjects without organic heart disease or AF (age 36 \u00b1 6 years, 4 males) underwent detailed CFAE and SRF left atrial electroanatomic maps. The overlap in left atrial regions with CFAEs and SRF was compared in the AF population, and the distribution of SRF was compared among patients with AF and normal controls. Propagation maps were analyzed to identify the activation patterns associated with SR fractionation.', 'SRF (338 \u00b1 150 points) and CFAE (418 \u00b1 135 points) regions comprised 29% \u00b1 14% and 25% \u00b1 15% of the left atrial surface area, respectively. There was no significant correlation between SRF and CFAE maps (r = .2; P = NS). On comparing patients with AF and controls, no significant difference was found in the distribution of SRF between groups (P = .74). Regions of SRF overlapped areas of wave-front collision 75% \u00b1 13% of the time.']\n\nQuestion: Is there a relationship between complex fractionated atrial electrograms recorded during atrial fibrillation and sinus rhythm fractionation?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant correlation between complex fractionated atrial electrograms (CFAEs) during atrial fibrillation and sinus rhythm fractionation (SRF), with a correlation coefficient of r = 0.2 and a non-significant P-value. Additionally, the distribution of SRF was similar in patients with AF and controls, further suggesting no strong relationship. Therefore, the evidence supports that there is no significant relationship between CFAEs and SRF.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 430, "output_tokens": 98, "total_tokens": 528}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.0329999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_166", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To compare the primary stability of miniscrews inserted into bone blocks of different bone mineral densities (BMDs) with and without cortical bone, and investigate whether some trabecular properties could influence primary stability.', 'Fifty-two bone blocks were extracted from fresh bovine pelvic bone. Four groups were created based on bone type (iliac or pubic region) and presence or absence of cortical bone. Specimens were micro-computed tomography imaged to evaluate trabecular thickness, trabecular number, trabecular separation, bone volume density (BV/TV), BMD, and cortical thickness. Miniscrews 1.4 mm in diameter and 6 mm long were inserted into the bone blocks, and primary stability was evaluated by insertion torque (IT), mini-implant mobility (PTV), and pull-out strength (PS).', 'Intergroup comparison showed lower levels of primary stability when the BMD of trabecular bone was lower and in the absence of cortical bone (P\u2264.05). The Pearson correlation test showed correlation between trabecular number, trabecular thickness, BV/TV, trabecular BMD, total BMD, and IT, PTV, and PS. There was correlation between cortical thickness and IT and PS (P\u2264.05).']\n\nQuestion: Is trabecular bone related to primary stability of miniscrews?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that trabecular properties such as trabecular number, thickness, bone volume density (BV/TV), and trabecular BMD were correlated with measures of primary stability (insertion torque, mobility, and pull-out strength). Lower primary stability was observed when trabecular bone mineral density was lower, indicating a clear relationship. Therefore, trabecular bone is related to the primary stability of miniscrews.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 361, "output_tokens": 93, "total_tokens": 454}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.4930999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_168", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Little is known about whether a routinely inserted endoscopic nasobiliary drainage (ENBD) tube improves the clinical course in patients with choledocholithiasis-induced acute cholangitis after clearance of choledocholithiasis.', 'The aim of this study was to investigate the need for ENBD on the clinical outcomes of patients with acute cholangitis undergoing endoscopic clearance of common bile duct (CBD) stones.', 'Prospective, randomized study.', 'Tertiary referral center.', 'A total of 104 patients with choledocholithiasis-induced acute cholangitis who underwent primary endoscopic treatment were compared according to insertion of an ENBD tube (51 in the ENBD group and 53 in the no-ENBD group).', 'Insertion of an ENBD tube after clearance of CBD stones.', 'Recurrence of cholangitis and length of hospital stay after clearance of CBD stones.', 'Baseline clinical characteristics were similar between both groups. There were no significant differences in the recurrence rate of cholangitis at 24 weeks (3.9% for the ENBD group vs 3.8% for the no-ENBD group at 24 weeks; P = .99) and length of hospital stay (7.9 days [standard error = 1.2] for the ENBD group vs 7.9 days [standard error = 0.7]for the no-ENBD group; P = .98). However, procedure time was longer (26.2 [SE = 1.8] minutes vs 22.7 [SE = 1.0]minutes, respectively; P = .01) and the discomfort score was higher (4.9 [SE = 0.4] vs 2.8 [SE = 0.3], respectively; P = .02) in the ENBD group than in the no-ENBD group.', 'Single-center study.']\n\nQuestion: Is it necessary to insert a nasobiliary drainage tube routinely after endoscopic clearance of the common bile duct in patients with choledocholithiasis-induced cholangitis?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant differences in recurrence of cholangitis or length of hospital stay between patients who received an ENBD tube and those who did not. However, the ENBD group experienced longer procedure times and higher discomfort scores. Therefore, routine insertion of an ENBD tube does not appear necessary.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 519, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 584}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.3348999999999994e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_169", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To assess quality of storage of vaccines in the community.', 'Questionnaire survey of general practices and child health clinics, and monitoring of storage temperatures of selected refrigerators.', 'Central Manchester and Bradford health districts.', '45 general practices and five child health clinics, of which 40 (80%) responded. Eight practices were selected for refrigeration monitoring.', 'Adherence to Department of Health guidelines for vaccine storage, temperature range to which vaccines were exposed over two weeks.', 'Of the 40 respondents, only 16 were aware of the appropriate storage conditions for the vaccines; eight had minimum and maximum thermometers but only one of these was monitored daily. In six of the eight practices selected for monitoring of refrigeration temperatures the vaccines were exposed to either subzero temperatures (three fridges) or temperatures up to 16 degrees C (three). Two of these were specialised drug storage refrigerators with an incorporated thermostat and external temperature gauges.']\n\nQuestion: Storage of vaccines in the community: weak link in the cold chain?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that most practices were unaware of proper vaccine storage conditions, and temperature monitoring was inadequate. Many vaccines were exposed to inappropriate temperatures, including subzero levels and temperatures as high as 16\u00b0C. This indicates a significant failure in maintaining the cold chain.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 284, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 343}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.6064e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_17", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To examine patterns of knowledge and attitudes among adults aged>65 years unvaccinated for influenza.', 'Surveyed Medicare beneficiaries in 5 areas; clustered unvaccinated seniors by their immunization related knowledge and attitudes.', 'Identified 4 clusters: Potentials (45%) would receive influenza vaccine to prevent disease; Fearful Uninformeds (9%) were unsure if influenza vaccine causes illness; Doubters (27%) were unsure if vaccine is efficacious; Misinformeds (19%) believed influenza vaccine causes illness. More Potentials (75%) and Misinformeds (70%) ever received influenza vaccine than did Fearful Uninformeds (18%) and Doubters (29%).']\n\nQuestion: Do patterns of knowledge and attitudes exist among unvaccinated seniors?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context clearly describes the identification of four distinct clusters of unvaccinated seniors based on their knowledge and attitudes toward influenza vaccination. These clusters\u2014Potentials, Fearful Uninformeds, Doubters, and Misinformeds\u2014demonstrate varying beliefs and behaviors, confirming the existence of patterns. Therefore, the evidence supports that such patterns do exist.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 239, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 315}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.4568999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_171", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The prevalence of retinal haemorrhages after convulsions is not well established. As these haemorrhages are considered characteristic of child abuse, we investigated their occurrence after convulsive episodes to see whether the finding of haemorrhage should prompt further investigation.', 'Prospective study of 153 children (aged 2 months to 2 years), seen in the emergency department after a convulsive episode. After a thorough history and physical examination, a retinal examination was performed by an ophthalmologist. If findings were positive, further investigation was undertaken to rule out systemic disorder or child abuse.', 'One child was found with unilateral retinal haemorrhages following an episode of a simple febrile convulsion. A thorough investigation uncovered no other reason for this finding.']\n\nQuestion: Convulsions and retinal haemorrhage: should we look further?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found only one case of retinal haemorrhage out of 153 children after convulsions, and no cause other than the convulsion was identified. However, since retinal haemorrhages are often associated with child abuse, the presence of this finding warrants further investigation to rule out serious underlying causes. Therefore, the most appropriate response is to look further when retinal haemorrhage is detected.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 253, "output_tokens": 93, "total_tokens": 346}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.7263e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_172", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"Community-based medical education is growing to meet the increased demand for quality clinical education in expanded settings, and its sustainability relies on patient participation. This study investigated patients' views on being used as an educational resource for teaching medical students.\", 'Questionnaire-based survey.', 'Patients attending six rural and 11 regional general practices in New South Wales over 18 teaching sessions in November 2008, who consented to student involvement in their consultation.', 'Patient perceptions, expectations and acceptance of medical student involvement in consultations, assessed by surveys before and after their consultations.', '118 of 122 patients consented to medical student involvement; of these, 117 (99%) completed a survey before the consultation, and 100 (85%) after the consultation. Patients were overwhelmingly positive about their doctor and practice being involved in student teaching and felt they themselves played an important role. Pre-consultation, patients expressed reluctance to allow students to conduct some or all aspects of the consultation independently. However, after the consultation, they reported they would have accepted higher levels of involvement than actually occurred.']\n\nQuestion: Are patients willing participants in the new wave of community-based medical education in regional and rural Australia?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that 99% of patients consented to student involvement and were overwhelmingly positive about their role in medical education. Although initially hesitant about student autonomy, patients retrospectively expressed willingness to accept even greater student involvement. This indicates strong support for community-based medical education.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 324, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 384}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.9004e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_173", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['This study aims to study femoral tunnel lengths drilled with a flexible reamer and the distance to important lateral structures obtained by flexing the knee at various angles and by drilling the guide pins arthroscopically to resemble clinical practice. The purpose of this cadaveric study was twofold: 1. to determine whether femoral tunnel lengths of greater than 20 mm can be created with a flexible reamer system at 90 \u00b0 of knee flexion and 2. to determine whether the lateral structures of the knee are safe with this technique.', 'Ten fresh cadaveric knees were utilized. The intra-osseous length can be measured with a specially de - signed flexible guide pin. Flexible pins were inserted with the knee at 70\u00b0, 90\u00b0, and 120\u00b0 of flexion. The intra-osseous length was measured with the measuring device. Each speci - men was dissected around the lateral aspect of the knee to identify the critical structures, the common peroneal nerve, and the LCL. The distance from the guide pins to the com - mon peroneal nerve and femoral attachment of the LCL were measured with a standard flexible paper ruler to the nearest millimeter.', 'There is a trend for progressively increasing mean intra-osseous length associated with increased flexion of the knee. The mean intra-osseous length for 70\u00b0 flexion was 25.2 mm (20 mm to 32 mm), which was statistically significant when compared to mean intra-osseous lengths of 32.1 mm (22 mm to 45 mm) and 38.0 mm (34 mm to 45 mm) in the 90\u00b0 and 120\u00b0 flexion groups, respectively (p<0.05). There were no significant differences among the groups with respect to distance to the LCL. There is a trend toward longer distances to the common peroneal nerve with increased flexion. There was a statistically significant dif - ference when comparing 120\u00b0 versus 70\u00b0 (p<0.05).']\n\nQuestion: Can Flexible Instruments Create Adequate Femoral Tunnel Lengths at 90\u00b0 of Knee Flexion in Anterior Cruciate Ligament Reconstruction?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that the mean intra-osseous length at 90\u00b0 of knee flexion was 32.1 mm, which is well above the 20 mm threshold considered adequate for femoral tunnel length. This indicates that flexible instruments can indeed create sufficiently long femoral tunnels at 90\u00b0 flexion. Additionally, the technique was found to be safe with respect to lateral knee structures.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 552, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 640}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.799199999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_175", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The levels of bone formation and resorption can be assessed at the tissue level by bone histomorphometry on transiliac bone biopsies. Systemic biochemical markers of bone turnover reflect the overall bone formation and resorption at the level of the entire skeleton but cannot discriminate the different skeletal compartments.', 'Our aim was to investigate the correlations between the serum biochemical markers of formation and resorption with histomorphometric parameters.', 'We performed post hoc analysis of a previous clinical study.', 'Patients were selected from the general population.', 'A total of 371 untreated postmenopausal osteoporotic women aged 50 to 84 years with a lumbar T-score \u2264 -2.5 SD or \u2264 -1 SD with at least one osteoporotic fracture.', 'Transiliac bone biopsies were obtained after a double tetracycline labeling, and blood samples were collected.', 'The static and dynamic parameters of formation and bone resorption were measured by histomorphometry. Serum biochemical markers of formation (bone alkaline phosphatase [ALP]; procollagen type I N-terminal propeptide [PINP]) and resorption (C-terminal crosslinking telopeptide of collagen type 1 [sCTX]) were assessed.', \"The mean values of biochemical markers were: bone ALP, 15.0 \u00b1 5.2 ng/mL; PINP, 56.2 \u00b1 21.9 \u03bcg/mL; and sCTX, 0.58 \u00b1 0.26 ng/mL. Bone ALP and PINP were significantly correlated with both the static and dynamic parameters of formation (0.21 \u2264 r' \u2264 0.36; 0.01 \u2265 P \u2265 .0001). sCTX was significantly correlated with all resorption parameters (0.18 \u2264 r' \u2264 0.24; 0.02 \u2265 P \u2265 .0001).\"]\n\nQuestion: Are Biochemical Markers of Bone Turnover Representative of Bone Histomorphometry in 370 Postmenopausal Women?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found significant correlations between serum biochemical markers (bone ALP, PINP, sCTX) and histomorphometric parameters of bone formation and resorption, indicating that these markers reflect bone turnover as measured by histomorphometry. Although correlations were statistically significant, they were moderate in strength, suggesting that while biochemical markers are representative, they are not perfect substitutes. Therefore, the evidence supports that biochemical markers are reasonably representative of histomorphometric findings in this population.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 510, "output_tokens": 100, "total_tokens": 610}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.620999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_177", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"To explore the impact of delivery mode on women's postpartum quality of life in rural China and probe factors influencing postnatal quality of life.\", \"Childbirth significantly affects puerpera's physical, psychological and social domains of quality of life. Under the circumstance of increasing high caesarean section rate in rural China, the impact of delivery mode on postnatal quality of life remains unclear.\", 'Cross-sectional study design.', \"Women residing in rural areas and in their 0-12 months after childbirth from 30 rural townships participated in a household survey. A structured questionnaire was used to evaluate women's socio-demographic characteristics, previous pregnant experiences, foetal characteristics and use of maternal health services. The scale for rural postnatal quality of life was adopted to assess postnatal quality of life from six dimensions: physical complaints and pain, sleep and energy, sex satisfaction, interpersonal communication, self-evaluated living stress and perceived life satisfaction.\", 'The overall caeserean section rate was 70\u00b70% (962/1375), and most of them (59\u00b77%) were selected by maternal request. None of six dimensions and total score of quality of life displayed significant difference between women with normal delivery and cesaerean section. It was found that postnatal home visit related to good postnatal quality of life and lower husband education level, male gender of infant were associated with poor quality of life.']\n\nQuestion: Does delivery mode affect women's postpartum quality of life in rural China?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant differences in any of the six dimensions of quality of life or the total score between women who had normal delivery and those who had cesarean section. Despite a high cesarean section rate, delivery mode was not associated with postnatal quality of life. Therefore, the evidence suggests that delivery mode does not affect postpartum quality of life in this population.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 388, "output_tokens": 82, "total_tokens": 470}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.5748e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_178", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Irregular bleeding affects many users of combined menopausal hormone therapy (HT) and commonly leads to invasive and expensive investigations to exclude underlying malignancy. In most cases no abnormality is found.', 'The main objective of this study was to explore the role of uterine natural killer (uNK) cells and their regulatory cytokine IL-15 in irregular bleeding in HT users.', 'This was a prospective observational study conducted between 2002 and 2004.', 'The study was conducted in a tertiary referral menopause clinic at King Edward Memorial Hospital, Western Australia.', 'Patients included 117 postmenopausal women taking combined HT.', 'Outpatient endometrial biopsies were taken during and outside bleeding episodes.', 'The relationship between endometrial uNK cells (CD56+) and bleeding patterns was measured. We also addressed the impact of HT exposure on uNK cell populations, the relationship between endometrial IL-15 expression and uNK cell populations, and killer Ig like receptor genotype in subjects with irregular bleeding.', 'Endometrial CD56+ uNK cells were significantly increased in biopsies obtained during bleeding episodes (P<0.001), compared with HT users with no bleeding. The highest level of IL-15 expression was also seen in biopsies taken during bleeding. No clear relationship between killer Ig like receptor genotype and bleeding on HT was observed.']\n\nQuestion: Menopausal hormone therapy and irregular endometrial bleeding: a potential role for uterine natural killer cells?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that endometrial CD56+ uterine natural killer (uNK) cells were significantly increased during bleeding episodes in women on menopausal hormone therapy, and IL-15 expression was also highest during these episodes. This suggests a potential association between uNK cells and irregular bleeding. Therefore, the results support a possible role for uterine natural killer cells in this condition.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 393, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 480}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.6603e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_179", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['We evaluated the differences between percutaneous ethanol injection with and without aspiration of ethanol-mixed fluid for treatment of benign cystic thyroid nodules.', 'We examined 60 patients with benign cystic thyroid nodules confirmed by fine-needle aspiration biopsy and divided them into 2 groups according to nonaspiration (group A, n = 30) or aspiration (group B, n = 30) of ethanol-mixed fluid after intracystic ethanol injection. We evaluated in both groups the complete disappearance of the cystic portion of the thyroid nodule on follow-up ultrasonography (first follow-up ultrasonography; mean, 4.6 months in group A; mean, 4.4 months in group B) (chi-square test), side effects or complications during and after the procedure (chi-square test), and the total procedure time (Student t test).', 'Most patients showed complete disappearance of the cystic portion of the thyroid nodule (group A, n = 29; group B, n = 28), and they revealed no recurrence on follow-up ultrasonography. There was no statistical difference in the success rates between group A and group B (P>.05). Pain, the most common side effect, and other mild side effects or complications occurred in small numbers of patients in each group, but there was no significant difference in side effects or complications between the 2 groups (P>.05), except for intracystic hemorrhage (P<.05) and the complaint of all group B patients due to a double puncture (P<.001). The total procedure time was nearly double in group B than in group A because of the additional procedures, such as complete evacuation of the ethanol-mixed fluid and the 10-minute compression.']\n\nQuestion: Percutaneous ethanol injection for benign cystic thyroid nodules: is aspiration of ethanol-mixed fluid advantageous?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant difference in success rates or most side effects between the aspiration and nonaspiration groups. Although aspiration was associated with higher rates of intracystic hemorrhage and required nearly double the procedure time, it did not improve outcomes. Therefore, aspiration of ethanol-mixed fluid does not appear to be advantageous.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 471, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 541}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.0440999999999994e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_18", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Although the retroperitoneal approach has been the preferred choice for open urological procedures, retroperitoneoscopy is not the preferred approach for laparoscopy. This study aims to develop a training model for retroperitoneoscopy and to establish an experimental learning curve.', 'Fifteen piglets were operated on to develop a standard retroperitoneoscopic nephrectomy (RPN) training model. All procedures were performed with three ports. Intraoperative data (side, operative time, blood loss, peritoneal opening) were recorded. Animals were divided into groups A, the first eight, and B, the last seven cases. Data were statistically analyzed.', 'We performed fifteen RPNs. The operative time varied from 15 to 50 minutes (median 30 minutes). Blood loss varied from 5 to 100 mL (median 20 mL). We experienced five peritoneal openings; we had two surgical vascular complications managed laparoscopically. There was statistical difference between groups A and B for peritoneal opening (p = 0.025), operative time (p = 0.0037), and blood loss (p = 0.026).', 'RPN in a porcine model could simulate the whole procedure, from creating the space to nephrectomy completion. Experimental learning curve was eight cases, after statistical data analysis.']\n\nQuestion: Is there a model to teach and practice retroperitoneoscopic nephrectomy?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study describes the development of a training model for retroperitoneoscopic nephrectomy using piglets and outlines a standardized procedure with measurable outcomes. It also establishes an experimental learning curve based on statistical analysis of the surgical performance. Therefore, a model to teach and practice retroperitoneoscopic nephrectomy was successfully developed.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 387, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 457}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.4476999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_181", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Prior literature identified the use of Performance Measurement Systems (PMS) as crucial in addressing improved processes of care. Moreover, a strategic use of PMS has been found to enhance quality, compared to non-strategic use, although a clear understanding of this linkage is still to be achieved. This paper deals with the test of direct and indirect models related to the link between the strategic use of PMS and the level of improved processes in health care organizations. Indirect models were mediated by the degree of perceived managerial discretion.', 'A PLS analysis on a survey of 97 Italian managers working for health care organizations in the Lombardy region was conducted. The response rate was 77.6%.', 'The strategic use of PMS in health care organizations directly and significantly (p\\u2009<\\u20090.001) enhances performance in terms of improved processes. Perceived managerial discretion is positively and significantly (p\\u2009<\\u20090.001) affected by the strategic use of PMS, whereas the mediation effect is non-significant.']\n\nQuestion: Are performance measurement systems useful?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on the context, the study found that the strategic use of Performance Measurement Systems (PMS) directly and significantly enhances improved processes in healthcare organizations (p < 0.001). This indicates a clear positive impact of PMS when used strategically. Therefore, PMS are indeed useful.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 313, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 378}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.8723e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_185", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Reliable longitudinal data of patients with functional somatic symptoms in general practice are lacking.', 'To identify distinctive features in patients with chronic functional somatic symptoms, and to determine whether these symptoms support the hypothesis of the existence of specific somatic syndromes.', 'Observational study, with a comparison control group.', 'Four primary care practices affiliated with the University of Nijmegen in the Netherlands.', 'One hundred and eighty-two patients diagnosed between 1998 and 2002 as having chronic functional somatic symptoms and 182 controls matched by age, sex, socioeconomic status, and practice were included. Data on comorbidity, referrals, diagnostic tests, and hospital admissions over a period of 10 years prior to the diagnosis were collected. Medication use and number of visits to the general practitioner (GP) were extracted from the moment computerised registration was started.', 'In the 10 years before the diagnosis of chronic functional somatic symptoms, significantly more patients than controls presented functional somatic symptoms in at least two body systems, and used more somatic and psychotropic drugs. They visited the GP twice as much, statistically had significantly more psychiatric morbidity, and were referred more often to mental health workers and somatic specialists. The number of patients undergoing diagnostic tests was higher for patients with chronic functional somatic symptoms than for controls, but hospital admissions rates were equal.']\n\nQuestion: Chronic functional somatic symptoms: a single syndrome?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study identifies that patients with chronic functional somatic symptoms exhibited symptoms across multiple body systems, higher healthcare use, and greater psychiatric comorbidity, suggesting overlapping features rather than distinct, separate syndromes. However, the presence of diverse symptoms and high variability in presentation supports the idea that these may not constitute a single, unified syndrome. Therefore, the findings lean toward heterogeneity, implying the symptoms do not form one single syndrome.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 371, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 462}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.5440999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_19", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Elevated resting heart rate (RHR) is a neglected marker in cardiovascular risk factor studies of sub-Saharan African populations. This study aimed to determine the prevalence of elevated RHR and other risk factors for cardiovascular disease (CVD) and to investigate any associations between RHR and these risk factors in a rural population in Ghana.', 'Cross-sectional analysis.', 'A total of 574 adults aged between 18-65 years were randomly sampled from a population register. Data collected included those on sociodemographic variables and anthropometric, blood pressure (BP), and RHR measurements. Within-person variability in RHR was calculated using data from repeat measurements taken 2 weeks apart.', 'Of study participants, 36% were male. Prevalence of casual high BP was 19%. In the population, 10% were current cigarette smokers and habitual alcohol use was high at 56%. As measured by body mass index, 2% were obese and 14% had abdominal obesity. RHR was elevated (>90 bpm) in 19%. Overall, 79% of study participants were found to have at least one CVD risk factor. RHR was significantly associated with age, waist circumference, and BP. Individuals with an elevated RHR had a higher risk (OR 1.94, 95% CI 1.15-3.26%, p = 0.013) of casual high BP compared with participants with normal RHR independently of several established CVD risk factors. The regression dilution ratio of RHR was 0.75 (95% CI 0.62-0.89).']\n\nQuestion: Cardiovascular risk in a rural adult West African population: is resting heart rate also relevant?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that 19% of participants had an elevated resting heart rate (RHR), which was significantly associated with age, waist circumference, and blood pressure. Elevated RHR was independently linked to a higher risk of casual high blood pressure (OR 1.94, 95% CI 1.15\u20133.26), indicating its relevance as a cardiovascular risk factor. Therefore, resting heart rate is indeed relevant in assessing cardiovascular risk in this population.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 445, "output_tokens": 103, "total_tokens": 548}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.1895e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_190", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Mechanically ventilated patients experience profound stress. Interventions are needed to ameliorate stress that does not cause adverse effects. The purpose of this study was to explore the influence of music on stress in a sample of patients over the duration of ventilatory support.RESEARCH METHODOLOGY/', 'Randomised controlled trial; randomised patients (56.8+16.9 years, 61% male, APACHE III 57.2+18.3) receiving ventilatory support to: (1) patient-directed music (PDM) where patients self-initiated music listening whenever desired from a preferred collection, (2) headphones only to block ICU noise, or (3) usual ICU care. Twenty-four hour urinary cortisol samples were collected from a sub-set of subjects with intact renal function and not receiving medications known to influence cortisol levels (n=65).', '12 ICUs in the Midwestern United States.', 'Urinary free cortisol (UFC), an integrative biomarker of stress.', 'Controlling for illness severity, gender, and baseline UFC (29-45 mg/day), mixed models analysis revealed no significant differences among groups in UFC over the course of ventilatory support.']\n\nQuestion: Does music influence stress in mechanically ventilated patients?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant differences in urinary free cortisol (UFC), a biomarker of stress, among patients exposed to music, headphones only, or usual care, after controlling for key variables. This suggests that music did not have a measurable effect on physiological stress in mechanically ventilated patients. Therefore, the most accurate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 340, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 411}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.124e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_191", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Spasticity and loss of function in an affected arm are common after stroke. Although botulinum toxin is used to reduce spasticity, its functional benefits are less easily demonstrated. This paper reports an exploratory meta-analysis to investigate the relationship between reduced arm spasticity and improved arm function.', 'Individual data from stroke patients in two randomised controlled trials of intra-muscular botulinum toxin were pooled. The Modified Ashworth Scale (elbow, wrist, fingers) was used to calculate a \"Composite Spasticity Index\". Data from the arm section of the Barthel Activities of Daily Living Index (dressing, grooming, and feeding) and three subjective measures (putting arm through sleeve, cleaning palm, cutting fingernails) were summed to give a \"Composite Functional Index\". Change scores and the time of maximum change were also calculated.', 'Maximum changes in both composite measures occurred concurrently in 47 patients. In 26 patients the improvement in spasticity preceded the improvement in function with 18 showing the reverse. There was a definite relationship between the maximum change in spasticity and the maximum change in arm function, independent of treatment (rho = -0.2822, p = 0.0008, n = 137). There was a clear relationship between the changes in spasticity and in arm function in patients treated with botulinum toxin (Dysport) at 500 or 1000 units (rho = -0.5679, p = 0.0090, n = 22; rho = -0.4430, p = 0.0018, n = 47), but not in those treated with placebo or 1500 units.']\n\nQuestion: Does reducing spasticity translate into functional benefit?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found a statistically significant relationship between reduced spasticity and improved arm function, particularly in patients treated with botulinum toxin at 500 or 1000 units. Although the relationship was not seen in all treatment groups (e.g., placebo or 1500 units), the overall correlation was significant. Therefore, the evidence supports that reducing spasticity can translate into functional benefit.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 487, "output_tokens": 109, "total_tokens": 596}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.5477e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_194", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To investigate the effect of bracket-ligature combination on the amount of orthodontic space closure over three months.', 'Randomized clinical trial with three parallel groups.', 'A hospital orthodontic department (Chesterfield Royal Hospital, UK).', 'Forty-five patients requiring upper first premolar extractions.', 'Informed consent was obtained and participants were randomly allocated into one of three groups: (1) conventional pre-adjusted edgewise brackets and elastomeric ligatures; (2) conventional pre-adjusted edgewise brackets and Super Slick(\u00ae) low friction elastomeric ligatures; (3) Damon 3MX(\u00ae) passive self-ligating brackets. Space closure was undertaken on 0\u00b7019\u00d70\u00b7025-inch stainless steel archwires with nickel-titanium coil springs. Participants were recalled at four weekly intervals. Upper alginate impressions were taken at each visit (maximum three). The primary outcome measure was the mean amount of space closure in a 3-month period.', 'A one-way ANOVA was undertaken [dependent variable: mean space closure (mm); independent variable: group allocation]. The amount of space closure was very similar between the three groups (1 mm per 28 days); however, there was a wide variation in the rate of space closure between individuals. The differences in the amount of space closure over three months between the three groups was very small and non-significant (P\\u200a=\\u200a0\u00b7718).']\n\nQuestion: Does the bracket-ligature combination affect the amount of orthodontic space closure over three months?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that the differences in space closure between the three bracket-ligature groups were very small and statistically non-significant (P = 0.718). This indicates no meaningful effect of bracket-ligature combination on the amount of space closure over three months. Therefore, the evidence does not support a significant effect.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 412, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 485}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.6552e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_195", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"There has never been a nationally representative survey of medical students' personal health-related practices, although they are inherently of interest and may affect patient-counseling practices. This study evaluated the health practices and the vaccination status of first year residents working at the academic hospital H\u00f4tel-Dieu de France.\", 'The medical files of all medicine and surgery residents in their first year of specialization between the years 2005 and 2008 were reviewed. These residents were required to go through a preventive medical visit at the University Center of Family and Community Health.', 'One hundred and nine residents (109) were included in the study; 68 (6239%) were male and 41 (37.61%) were female with a mean age of 26 years. Only 6 residents (5.50%) practiced physical activity according to international guidelines (more than three times a week for more than 30 minutes each time). Most residents (n = 76 ; 69.73%) used to skip one or two meals especially breakfast and as a consequence 30 male (44.11%) and 4 female (9.75%) students were overweight, with a statistical difference between the two sexes (Fisher test, p-value = 0.001). Twenty-eight residents (25.69%) were smokers with a male predominance. Fourteen residents of both genders (12.84%) drank alcohol regularly (>3 times a week) and 71 (65.14%) had a drink occasionally (once a month or less). Only 25 residents (23%) of the cohort had a complete and up-to-date immunization status. The immunization gap was basically against measles, mumps, rubella (MMR) and diphtheria, tetanus, poliomyelitis (dT Polio). Ninety-nine residents (90.83%) had full immunization against hepatitis B with an adequate response in 78 residents (71.56%).']\n\nQuestion: Health habits and vaccination status of Lebanese residents: are future doctors applying the rules of prevention?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study reveals that a majority of residents do not follow recommended health practices: only 5.5% met physical activity guidelines, nearly 70% skipped meals, over 25% smoked, and 65% had poor or incomplete vaccination status, especially for MMR and dT Polio. Despite high hepatitis B vaccination rates, overall preventive health behaviors were inadequate. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 526, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 610}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.574599999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_196", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Vaginal intraepithelial neoplasia is a little known disease which could be related to risk factors different from simple HPV infections.', 'To ascertain wheter vaginal lesions have a natural history similar to cervical lesions.MATERIALS &', 'A retrospective study to identify patients with vaginal lesions and synchronous cervical lesions through biopsy. The rate of mild cervical lesions (koilocytosis, warts, CIN I with and without koilocytosis) was compared with the rate of severe cervical lesions (CIN II and III, cervical carcinoma) in patients with mild vaginal lesions (warts and koilocytosis, and low-grade VAIN) and in patients with severe vaginal lesions (high-grade VAIN). Using koilocytosis as a marker, the rate of \"active\" cervical lesions was compared with the rate of \"non active\" cervical lesions in patients with \"active\" versus \"non active\" vaginal lesions. Finally, the rates of mild and severe cervical lesions were compared among each group of VAIN (low-grade, high-grade, with or without koilocytosis).', 'In patients with mild vaginal lesions, mild cervical lesions were significantly more frequent than severe cervical lesions. In patients with \"active\" vaginal lesions the rate of \"active\" cervical lesions was significantly higher than \"non active\" cervical lesions. The differences in rates of mild cervical lesions and severe cervical lesions among patients with high-grade VAIN and low-grade VAIN (with and without koilocytosis) were not significant.']\n\nQuestion: Does vaginal intraepithelial neoplasia have the same evolution as cervical intraepithelial neoplasia?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that in patients with mild or \"active\" vaginal lesions, there was a higher frequency of mild or \"active\" cervical lesions, suggesting some similarity in behavior. However, no significant differences were found in cervical lesion rates between high-grade and low-grade VAIN groups, indicating divergent patterns. This implies that vaginal intraepithelial neoplasia does not have the same evolution as cervical intraepithelial neoplasia.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 486, "output_tokens": 117, "total_tokens": 603}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.6206000000000005e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_198", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The brain-dead donor supply has become one of the criteria limiting the performance of heart transplantation. Conventional screening criteria are too limiting and exclude suitable heart donors. Echocardiography is now widely available and is a reliable tool to assess left ventricular dysfunction in brain-dead donors. Yet few data are available on the degree of left ventricular dysfunction where a transplantation is possible.', 'Fifty-five potential brain-dead heart donors (age 38 +/- 11 years) were prospectively evaluated by transesophageal echocardiography (TEE) before harvesting. Fractional area change (FAC) was used to assess left ventricular function in potential brain-dead donors. Transplanted hearts were evaluated on the fifth postoperative day. The transplantation was considered a success if the recipient was alive, not retransplanted, without an assistance device or an epinephrine infusion of more than 1 mg/h and showed an ejection fraction above 40%.', 'Of the 55 potential heart donors, 20 exhibited an FAC of less than 50%. Forty hearts were harvested, 36 of which were successfully transplanted. Nine patients had an FAC below 50% (group H2) and 27 had an FAC over 50% (group H1). Four patients died: 2 from hemorrhage (FAC>50% in donors); 1 from right and one from left ventricular dysfunction (FAC<50% in donors). The FAC increased significantly from 51 +/- 15% to 57 +/- 11% in 18 hearts that underwent TEE in donors and afterwards in recipients. Overall actuarial survival was 86.2% versus 64.6% at 1 and 2 years in group H1 and group H2, respectively (p = NS).']\n\nQuestion: Transesophageal echocardiographic assessment of left ventricular function in brain-dead patients: are marginally acceptable hearts suitable for transplantation?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that hearts with reduced left ventricular function (FAC <50%) were successfully transplanted, with recipients achieving an ejection fraction above 40% and acceptable survival rates, despite slightly lower 2-year survival compared to those with better donor function. Although there were complications in some cases with lower FAC, the overall outcomes support the use of these marginally acceptable hearts. Therefore, the evidence suggests that such hearts can be suitable for transplantation.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 528, "output_tokens": 132, "total_tokens": 660}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 5.0688e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_199", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Twenty-eight female Sprague Dawley rats were allocated randomly to 4 groups. The sham group (group 1) was only subjected to catheter insertion, not to pneumoperitoneum. Group 2 received a 1 mg/kg dose of 0.9% sodium chloride by the intraperitoneal route for 10 min before pneumoperitoneum. Groups 3 and 4 received 6 and 12 mg/kg edaravone, respectively, by the intraperitoneal route for 10 min before pneumoperitoneum. After 60 min of pneumoperitoneum, the gas was deflated. Immediately after the reperfusion period, both ovaries were excised for histological scoring, caspase-3 immunohistochemistry and biochemical evaluation including glutathione (GSH) and malondialdehyde (MDA) levels. Also, total antioxidant capacity (TAC) was measured in plasma samples to evaluate the antioxidant effect of edaravone.', 'Ovarian sections in the saline group revealed higher scores for follicular degeneration and edema (p<0.0001) when compared with the sham group. Administration of different doses of edaravone in rats significantly prevented degenerative changes in the ovary (p<0.0001). Caspase-3 expression was only detected in the ovarian surface epithelium in all groups, and there was a significant difference between the treatment groups and the saline group (p<0.0001). Treatment of rats with edaravone reduced caspase-3 expression in a dose-dependent manner. Moreover, biochemical measurements of oxidative stress markers (MDA, GSH and TAC) revealed that prophylactic edaravone treatment attenuated oxidative stress induced by I/R injury.']\n\nQuestion: Attenuation of ischemia/reperfusion-induced ovarian damage in rats: does edaravone offer protection?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study demonstrates that edaravone significantly reduced follicular degeneration, edema, and caspase-3 expression, while also improving oxidative stress markers (MDA, GSH, TAC) in a dose-dependent manner. These findings indicate a protective effect against ischemia/reperfusion-induced ovarian damage. Therefore, edaravone offers protection.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 478, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 557}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.1837999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_2", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Apparent life-threatening events in infants are a difficult and frequent problem in pediatric practice. The prognosis is uncertain because of risk of sudden infant death syndrome.', 'Eight infants aged 2 to 15 months were admitted during a period of 6 years; they suffered from similar maladies in the bath: on immersion, they became pale, hypotonic, still and unreactive; recovery took a few seconds after withdrawal from the bath and stimulation. Two diagnoses were initially considered: seizure or gastroesophageal reflux but this was doubtful. The hypothesis of an equivalent of aquagenic urticaria was then considered; as for patients with this disease, each infant\\'s family contained members suffering from dermographism, maladies or eruption after exposure to water or sun. All six infants had dermographism. We found an increase in blood histamine levels after a trial bath in the two infants tested. The evolution of these \"aquagenic maladies\" was favourable after a few weeks without baths. After a 2-7 year follow-up, three out of seven infants continue to suffer from troubles associated with sun or water.']\n\nQuestion: Syncope during bathing in infants, a pediatric form of water-induced urticaria?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The described episodes of pallor, hypotonia, and unresponsiveness during bathing, along with dermographism, family history of water- or sun-induced reactions, and elevated histamine levels, strongly suggest a histamine-mediated response to water exposure. These features align with aquagenic urticaria or a related condition, even if classic skin lesions are not emphasized. Therefore, the evidence supports classifying these events as a pediatric form of water-induced urticaria.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 326, "output_tokens": 101, "total_tokens": 427}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.324599999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_20", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"The incidence of large-scale urban attacks on civilian populations has significantly increased across the globe over the past decade. These incidents often result in Hospital Multiple Casualty Incidents (HMCI), which are very challenging to hospital teams. 15 years ago the Emergency and Disaster Medicine Division in the Israeli Ministry of Health defined a key of 20 percent of each hospital's bed capacity as its readiness for multiple casualties. Half of those casualties are expected to require immediate medical treatment. This study was performed to evaluate the efficacy of the current readiness guidelines based on the epidemiology of encountered HMCIs.\", 'A retrospective study of HMCIs was recorded in the Israeli Defense Force (IDF) home front command and the Israeli National Trauma Registry (ITR) between November 2000 and June 2003. An HMCI is defined by the Emergency and Disaster Medicine Division in the Israeli Ministry of Health as>or=10 casualties or>or=4 suffering from injuries with an ISS>or=16 arriving to a single hospital.', 'The study includes a total of 32 attacks, resulting in 62 HMCIs and 1292 casualties. The mean number of arriving casualties to a single hospital was 20.8+/-13.3 (range 4-56, median 16.5). In 95% of the HMCIs the casualty load was<or=52. Based on severity scores and ED discharges 1022 (79.2%) casualties did not necessitate immediate medical treatment.']\n\nQuestion: Israeli hospital preparedness for terrorism-related multiple casualty incidents: can the surge capacity and injury severity distribution be better predicted?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data from the study show that 95% of HMCIs involved 52 or fewer casualties, and 79.2% of casualties did not require immediate treatment, suggesting a predictable pattern in both surge capacity needs and injury severity. This indicates that current readiness guidelines (based on 20% bed capacity) may be evaluated and potentially refined using actual epidemiological data. Therefore, the surge capacity and injury severity distribution can likely be better predicted.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 427, "output_tokens": 99, "total_tokens": 526}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.0217e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_204", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The number of new diagnoses of HIV infection is rising in the northwestern hemisphere and it is becoming increasingly important to understand the mechanisms behind this trend.', 'To evaluate whether reported unsafe sexual behaviour among HIV- infected individuals is changing over time.', 'Participants in the Swiss HIV Cohort Study were asked about their sexual practices every 6 months for 3 years during regular follow-up of the cohort beginning on 1 April 2000.', ': Logistic regression models were fit using generalized estimating equations assuming a constant correlation between responses from the same individual.', 'At least one sexual behaviour questionnaire was obtained for 6545 HIV-infected individuals and the median number of questionnaires completed per individual was five. There was no evidence of an increase in reported unsafe sex over time in this population [odds ratio (OR), 1.0; 95% confidence interval (CI), 0.96-1.05]. Females (OR, 1.38; 95% CI, 1.19-1.60), 15-30 year olds (OR, 1.26; 95% CI, 1.09-1.47), those with HIV-positive partners (OR, 12.58; 95% CI, 10.84-14.07) and those with occasional partners (OR, 3.25; 95% CI, 2.87-3.67) were more likely to report unsafe sex. There was no evidence of a response bias over time, but individuals were less willing to leave questions about their sexual behaviour unanswered or ambiguous (OR, 0.93; 95% CI, 0.90-0.97).']\n\nQuestion: Is unsafe sexual behaviour increasing among HIV-infected individuals?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no evidence of an increase in reported unsafe sex over time among HIV-infected individuals, with an odds ratio of 1.0 and a 95% confidence interval that includes 1.0 (0.96\u20131.05), indicating no significant change. Therefore, the data do not support a rising trend in unsafe sexual behaviour.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 465, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 545}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.1015e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_205", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Cholestasis occurs frequently in patients with small bowel atresia (SBA) and is often attributed to prolonged parental nutrition. When severe or prolonged, patients may undergo unnecessary intensive or invasive investigation. We characterized cholestasis and analyzed the pertinence of investigating this patient population.', 'With Research Ethics Board approval, patients with SBA between 1996 and 2005 were retrospectively reviewed. Demographics, location of atresia, operative findings, complications, investigations, resumption of feeding, duration of prolonged parental nutrition, and follow-up information were examined. Cholestasis was evaluated for incidence, severity, and evolution.', 'Fifty-five patients (29 male, 26 female), with a median gestational age and birth weight of 36 weeks and 2025 g, respectively, were reviewed. Care was withdrawn for 2 patients before repair. For the remaining 53 patients, SBA were duodenal atresia in 18, jejunoileal atresia in 32, and multiple atresia in 3. Of 53, 24 (45%) patients developed cholestasis postoperatively (direct/total bilirubin>20%). All patients with short bowel (4) and 60% (6/10) of patients with a delay of enteral feeding more than 14 days postoperatively had cholestasis. Ten patients (36%) proceeded with in-depth evaluations for cholestasis, with 8 (28%) undergoing liver biopsy. No patient had biliary atresia. No deaths were related to isolated cholestasis/cirrhosis. Cholestasis resolved spontaneously in all the survivors.']\n\nQuestion: Cholestasis associated with small bowel atresia: do we always need to investigate?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that cholestasis occurred in 45% of patients with small bowel atresia but resolved spontaneously in all survivors, with no cases of biliary atresia or deaths related to cholestasis. Despite 36% of patients undergoing in-depth evaluations, including liver biopsies, no significant underlying liver disease was found. Therefore, routine invasive investigation for cholestasis in this population may not be necessary.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 457, "output_tokens": 94, "total_tokens": 551}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.1846999999999994e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_206", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To investigate the cost-effectiveness of up to \u00a3400 worth of financial incentives for smoking cessation in pregnancy as an adjunct to routine health care.', 'Cost-effectiveness analysis based on a Phase II randomized controlled trial (RCT) and a cost-utility analysis using a life-time Markov model.', 'The RCT was undertaken in Glasgow, Scotland. The economic analysis was undertaken from the UK National Health Service (NHS) perspective.', 'A total of 612 pregnant women randomized to receive usual cessation support plus or minus financial incentives of up to \u00a3400 vouchers (US $609), contingent upon smoking cessation.', 'Comparison of usual support and incentive interventions in terms of cotinine-validated quitters, quality-adjusted life years (QALYs) and direct costs to the NHS.', \"The incremental cost per quitter at 34-38 weeks pregnant was \u00a31127 ($1716).This is similar to the standard look-up value derived from Stapleton&West's published ICER tables, \u00a31390 per quitter, by looking up the Cessation in Pregnancy Incentives Trial (CIPT) incremental cost (\u00a3157) and incremental 6-month quit outcome (0.14). The life-time model resulted in an incremental cost of \u00a317 [95% confidence interval (CI)\\u2009=\\u2009-\u00a393, \u00a3107] and a gain of 0.04 QALYs (95% CI\\u2009=\\u2009-0.058, 0.145), giving an ICER of \u00a3482/QALY ($734/QALY). Probabilistic sensitivity analysis indicates uncertainty in these results, particularly regarding relapse after birth. The expected value of perfect information was \u00a330 million (at a willingness to pay of \u00a330\\u2009000/QALY), so given current uncertainty, additional research is potentially worthwhile.\"]\n\nQuestion: Are financial incentives cost-effective to support smoking cessation during pregnancy?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The incremental cost-effectiveness ratio (ICER) of \u00a3482 per QALY gained is well below typical willingness-to-pay thresholds (e.g., \u00a320,000\u2013\u00a330,000 per QALY), suggesting cost-effectiveness. However, there is considerable uncertainty, particularly due to potential relapse after birth, and the probabilistic sensitivity analysis shows wide confidence intervals. Despite the uncertainty, the low ICER and positive QALY gain support a likely \"yes.\"\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 518, "output_tokens": 109, "total_tokens": 627}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.7678e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_208", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"The aim of this study was to assess the reproducibility of different measurement methods and define the most workable technique for measuring head and neck paragangliomas, to determine the best method for evaluating tumour growth. The evaluation of tumour growth is vital for a 'wait-and-scan' policy, a management strategy that became increasingly important.\", 'Method comparison study.', 'Thirty tumours, including carotid body, vagal body, jugulotympanic tumours and conglomerates of multiple tumours, were measured in duplicate, using linear dimensions, manual area tracing and an automated segmentation method.', 'Reproducibility was assessed using the Bland-Altman method.', 'The smallest detectable difference using the linear dimension method was 11% for carotid body and 27% for vagal body tumours, compared with 17% and 20% for the manual area tracing method. Due to the irregular shape of paragangliomas in the temporal bone and conglomerates, the manual area tracing method showed better results in these tumours (26% and 8% versus 54% and 47%). The linear dimension method was significantly faster (median 4.27 versus 18.46 minutes, P<0.001). The automatic segmentation method yielded smallest detectable differences between 39% and 75%, and although fast (2.19 \u00b1 1.49 minutes), it failed technically.']\n\nQuestion: Measurement of head and neck paragangliomas: is volumetric analysis worth the effort?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that while volumetric methods like manual area tracing showed better reproducibility for irregularly shaped tumours, they were significantly more time-consuming than linear measurements. The automated segmentation method, though fast, had high smallest detectable differences and frequent technical failures. Given the trade-off between accuracy and efficiency, the added effort of volumetric analysis may not be justified in routine practice.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 441, "output_tokens": 119, "total_tokens": 560}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.3211e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_209", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The use of three-dimensional (3D) ultrasound may help to determine the exact position of the needle during breast biopsy, thereby reducing the number of core samples that are needed to achieve a reliable histological diagnosis. The aim of this study was to demonstrate the efficacy of 3D ultrasound-validated large-core needle biopsy (LCNB) of the breast.', 'A total of 360 core needle biopsies was obtained from 169 breast lesions in 146 patients. Additional open breast biopsy was performed in 111 women (127/169 breast lesions); the remaining 42 lesions were followed up for at least 24 months. 3D ultrasound visualization of the needle in the postfiring position was used to classify the biopsy as central, marginal or outside the lesion. Based on this classification it was decided whether another sample had to be obtained.', 'A median of two core samples per lesion provided for all the lesions a sensitivity for malignancy of 96.9%, specificity of 100%, false-positive rate of 0% and false-negative rate of 3.1%, and for the excised lesions a sensitivity of 96.5%, specificity of 100%, false-positive rate of 0%, false-negative rate of 3.5% and an underestimation rate of 3.4%.']\n\nQuestion: Three-dimensional ultrasound-validated large-core needle biopsy: is it a reliable method for the histological assessment of breast lesions?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study reports high sensitivity (96.9%), specificity (100%), and low false-negative and underestimation rates, indicating strong diagnostic accuracy. These results suggest that 3D ultrasound-validated LCNB is effective in correctly identifying both benign and malignant breast lesions. Therefore, the evidence supports its reliability for histological assessment.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 386, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 460}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.4806e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_210", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The proper angle of miniscrew insertion is important for cortical anchorage, patient safety, and biomechanical control. The purposes of this study are to report the alveolar process thickness and inter-radicular space in the posterior region of the mandible, to assess the impact of different miniscrew insertion angle protocols, and to identify differences between the genders or types of malocclusion.', 'In this retrospective study, 100 individuals were selected for orthodontic treatment at a radiology clinic. Cone-beam computed tomography data were imported into 3-dimensional software. The predictor variable was the location in the mandible and insertion angle. The demographic variables collected included age, gender, and malocclusion (Angle Classes I and II). The primary outcome variables were bone thickness and inter-radicular space. The inter-radicular spaces were evaluated 5 mm from the cement-enamel junction. The bone thicknesses were taken at 45\u00b0, 60\u00b0, and 90\u00b0 in relation to the alveolar ridge, simulating a miniscrew insertion. These factors were evaluated for sexual dimorphism and malocclusion (Angle Classes I and II). Sexual dimorphism and malocclusion were evaluated with t tests. To compare the inter-radicular space and the thickness of bone between areas, an analysis of variance for repeated measures was used.', 'The sample was composed of 100 patients with a mean age of 17.4 \u00b1 6.74 years. There were 61 female and 39 male patients and 60 Class I and 40 Class II molar relationships. The inter-radicular space ranged from 2.46 to 3.31 mm, and alveolar bone thickness ranged from 8.01 to 13.77 mm. The thickness tended to decrease with the increase in insertion angle from 45\u00b0 to 90\u00b0. No significant differences between the genders or types of malocclusion were found.']\n\nQuestion: Can bone thickness and inter-radicular space affect miniscrew placement in posterior mandibular sites?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Yes, bone thickness and inter-radicular space are critical factors for successful miniscrew placement, as they determine the available space for safe and stable insertion without damaging adjacent structures. The study measured these variables at different angles and locations to assess feasibility, indicating their direct relevance to placement decisions. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 512, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 582}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.3351999999999994e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_213", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To examine age-related differences in the relationship between personality and coping strategies in an Australian population of psychiatric inpatients.', 'Consenting eligible adults (N=238) from 18-100 years of age consecutively admitted to inpatient psychiatry units were assessed using the SCID I and II, the Coping Orientations to Problems Experienced Scale (COPE), the Brief Psychiatric Rating Scale (BPRS), the Global Assessment of Functioning Scale (GAF), the Social and Occupational Functioning Assessment Scale (SOFAS), the 12 Item Short-Form Heath Survey (SF12), the Sarason Social Support Questionnaire, and the NEO Five Factor Inventory (NEO-FFI) (cognitively impaired, and non-English speaking patients were excluded).', 'Older adults reported less symptomatology than younger patients and younger patients described more personality dysfunction than older patients. As assessed by the COPE, older adults reported lower levels of dysfunctional coping strategies than younger adults. Personality traits, social supports, gender, and age predicted coping strategies, while Axis I diagnosis, education, personality disorder, and symptom severity were not significant predictors of coping strategies.']\n\nQuestion: Does age moderate the effect of personality disorder on coping style in psychiatric inpatients?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context indicates that personality disorder was not a significant predictor of coping strategies, and there is no mention of an interaction effect between age and personality disorder on coping style. Therefore, there is no evidence that age moderates the effect of personality disorder on coping style.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 335, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 393}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.9585e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_214", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Advanced glycation end products (AGEs), formed by non-enzymatic glycation and oxidation (glycoxidation) reactions, have been implicated in the pathogenesis of several diseases, including normoglycemic uremia. AGE research in uremia has focused on the accumulation of carbohydrate-derived adducts generated by the Maillard reaction. Recent studies, however, have demonstrated that one AGE, the glycoxidation product carboxymethyllysine (CML), could be derived not only from carbohydrates but also from oxidation of polyunsaturated fatty acids in vitro, raising the possibility that both carbohydrate and lipid autoxidation might be increased in uremia.', 'To address this hypothesis, we applied gas chromatography-mass spectrometry and high performance liquid chromatography to measure protein adducts formed in uremic plasma by reactions between carbonyl compounds and protein amino groups: pentosidine derived from carbohydrate-derived carbonyls, malondialdehyde (MDA)-lysine derived from lipid-derived carbonyls, and CML originating possibly from both sources.', 'All three adducts were elevated in uremic plasma. Plasma CML levels were mainly (>95%) albumin bound. Their levels were not correlated with fructoselysine levels and were similar in diabetic and non-diabetic patients on hemodialysis, indicating that their increase was not driven by glucose. Pentosidine and MDA-lysine were also increased in plasma to the same extent in diabetic and non-diabetic hemodialysis patients. Statistical analysis indicated that plasma levels of CML correlated weakly (P<0.05) with those of pentosidine and MDA-lysine, but that pentosidine and MDA-lysine varied independently (P>0.5).']\n\nQuestion: Autoxidation products of both carbohydrates and lipids are increased in uremic plasma: is there oxidative stress in uremia?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The elevated levels of pentosidine (from carbohydrate autoxidation), MDA-lysine (from lipid autoxidation), and CML (from both) in uremic plasma indicate increased oxidative modification of proteins. The fact that these adducts are elevated independently of glucose levels and in both diabetic and non-diabetic hemodialysis patients supports the presence of systemic oxidative stress in uremia. Therefore, the evidence strongly suggests that oxidative stress is present.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 471, "output_tokens": 100, "total_tokens": 571}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.344099999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_215", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Using polymerase chain reaction techniques, we evaluated the presence of HPV infection in human breast milk collected from 21 HPV-positive and 11 HPV-negative mothers.', \"Of the 32 studied human milk specimens, no 'high-risk' HPV 16, 18, 31, 33, 35, 39, 45, 51, 52, 56, 58 or 58 DNA was detected.\"]\n\nQuestion: Can 'high-risk' human papillomaviruses (HPVs) be detected in human breast milk?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study analyzed 32 human milk samples using polymerase chain reaction and found no detectable DNA from high-risk HPV types, including HPV 16, 18, and others. This suggests that high-risk HPVs were not present in the breast milk specimens tested. Therefore, based on this evidence, the most accurate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 202, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 277}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.1842e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_22", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Secondhand smoke exposure (SHSe) threatens fragile infants discharged from a neonatal intensive care unit (NICU). Smoking practices were examined in families with a high respiratory risk infant (born at very low birth weight; ventilated>12 hr) in a Houston, Texas, NICU. Socioeconomic status, race, and mental health status were hypothesized to be related to SHSe and household smoking bans.', \"Data were collected as part of The Baby's Breath Project, a hospital-based SHSe intervention trial targeting parents with a high-risk infant in the NICU who reported a smoker in the household (N = 99). Measures of sociodemographics, smoking, home and car smoking bans, and depression were collected.\", 'Overall, 26% of all families with a high-risk infant in the NICU reported a household smoker. Almost half of the families with a smoker reported an annual income of less than $25,000. 46.2% of families reported having a total smoking ban in place in both their homes and cars. Only 27.8% families earning less than $25,000 reported having a total smoking ban in place relative to almost 60% of families earning more (p<.01). African American and Caucasian families were less likely to have a smoking ban compared with Hispanics (p<.05). Mothers who reported no smoking ban were more depressed than those who had a household smoking ban (p<.02).']\n\nQuestion: Secondhand smoke risk in infants discharged from an NICU: potential for significant health disparities?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data show clear disparities in secondhand smoke exposure based on income, race, and mental health, with lower-income, African American, and Caucasian families less likely to have smoking bans. Additionally, mothers without smoking bans were more depressed, indicating a link between socioeconomic stressors and SHSe. These patterns suggest a significant potential for health disparities.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 405, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 478}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.6055e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_220", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Midurethral sling (MUS) can improve overactive bladder (OAB) symptoms. It is unclear if anterior/apical prolapse (AA) repair provides additional benefit. We hypothesized that women with mixed urinary incontinence (MUI) experience greater improvement in the OAB component of their symptoms after concomitant MUS and AA repair compared with MUS alone.', 'This is a retrospective cohort study of women with bothersome MUI (defined by objective stress test and validated questionnaire) undergoing MUS alone (\"MUS-only\") or concomitant MUS and AA repair (\"MUS + AA\"). Our primary outcome was the Overactive Bladder Questionnaire Symptom Severity (OAB-q SS) change score 6\\xa0weeks after surgery.', 'Of 151 women, 67 (44\\xa0%) underwent MUS-only and 84 (56\\xa0%) underwent MUS + AA. The MUS-only cohort was younger and had less severe baseline prolapse (p\\u2009<\\u20090.05 for both). Postoperative complications (predominantly UTI) occurred in 35 (23\\xa0%) patients and were similar between cohorts. For all subjects mean OAB-q SS scores significantly improved postoperatively (p\\u2009<\\u20090.05). Our primary outcome, OAB-q SS change score, showed no significant differences between cohorts (30\\u2009\u00b1\\u200926 MUS-only vs 25\\u2009\u00b1\\u200925 MUS + AA, p\\u2009=\\u20090.20), indicating similar improvements in OAB symptoms. Multivariate linear regression analysis revealed no difference in OAB-q SS change score between cohorts; however, OAB-q SS change scores were lower for women with a postoperative complication (\u03b2\\u2009=\\u2009-19, 95\\xa0% CI -31 to -6; p\\u2009<\\u20090.01).']\n\nQuestion: Does concomitant anterior/apical repair during midurethral sling improve the overactive bladder component of mixed incontinence?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant difference in OAB symptom improvement between women who underwent MUS alone and those who had concomitant MUS and AA repair, as measured by the OAB-q SS change score (p = 0.20). Both groups showed significant postoperative improvement in OAB symptoms, but adding anterior/apical repair did not provide additional benefit. Therefore, the evidence does not support a beneficial effect of concomitant repair on OAB symptoms.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 562, "output_tokens": 100, "total_tokens": 662}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.990199999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_225", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"To evaluate the relationship between knee extensor strength, postural stability, functional ambulation, and disease severity in Parkinson's disease (PD).\", 'A cohort study.', 'University research laboratory.', 'Patients (N=44) with idiopathic PD.', 'Not applicable.', \"Participants were evaluated on their isokinetic knee extensor strength. Additionally, participants completed an assessment of their postural stability (Functional Reach Test for static stability and a dynamic postural stability assessment as measured by the center of pressure-center of mass moment arm during gait initiation). Participants also underwent an evaluation of their functional ambulation as measured by a 6-minute walk test. Lastly, participants were evaluated by a neurologist specially trained in movement disorders to assess neurologic status and disease severity using the Unified Parkinson's Disease Rating Scale and the Hoehn and Yahr disability score.\", 'Knee extensor strength positively correlated with dynamic postural stability and negatively correlated with disease severity. Further, dynamic postural stability was negatively correlated to disease severity and positively correlated with functional ambulation in this cohort of patients with PD (P<.05). The results also suggest that the Functional Reach Test may be a valuable assessment tool to examine postural stability in PD.']\n\nQuestion: Knee extensor strength, dynamic stability, and functional ambulation: are they related in Parkinson's disease?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context indicates that knee extensor strength positively correlates with dynamic postural stability, which in turn is positively correlated with functional ambulation. These relationships were statistically significant (P<.05), indicating a clear association among the three factors in patients with Parkinson's disease. Therefore, the evidence supports a definite relationship.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 349, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 418}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.167899999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_227", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Several studies have suggested a protective effect of folic acid (FA) on congenital heart anomalies. Down syndrome (DS) infants are known to have a high frequency of heart anomalies. Not all children with DS suffer from heart anomalies, which raises the question whether maternal factors might affect the risk of these anomalies. Our objectives were to investigate whether first-trimester FA use protects against heart anomalies among DS children.', 'Women with liveborn DS children participating in the Slone Epidemiology Center Birth Defects Study between 1976 and 1997 were included. We performed case-control analyses using DS, with heart anomalies as cases and DS, without heart anomalies as controls. Subanalyses were performed for defects that have been associated with FA in non-DS populations (conotruncal, ventricular septal [VSD]) and for those that are associated with DS (ostium secundum type atrial septal defects [ASD]and endocardial cushion defects [ECD]). Exposure was defined as the use of any FA-containing product for an average of at least 4 days per week during the first 12 weeks of pregnancy, whereas no exposure was defined as no use of FA in these 12 weeks.', 'Of the 223 cases, 110 (49%) were exposed versus 84 (46%) of the 184 controls. After adjustment for possible confounders, no protective effect of FA was found on heart anomalies overall (OR 0.95, 95% CI: 0.61-1.47) nor separately for conotruncal defects, VSDs, ASDs, or ECDs.']\n\nQuestion: Can folic acid protect against congenital heart defects in Down syndrome?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant protective effect of folic acid on congenital heart anomalies in children with Down syndrome, either overall or in specific defect subtypes. Adjusted odds ratios did not show a statistically significant reduction in risk. Therefore, the evidence does not support a protective effect.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 446, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 508}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.7866e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_228", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Francophones may experience poorer health due to social status, cultural differences in lifestyle and attitudes, and language barriers to health care. Our study sought to compare mental health indicators between Francophones and non-Francophones living in the province of Manitoba.', 'Two populations were used: one from administrative datasets housed at the Manitoba Centre for Health Policy and the other from representative survey samples. The administrative datasets contained data from physician billings, hospitalizations, prescription drug use, education, and social services use, and surveys included indicators on language variables and on self-rated health.', 'Outside urban areas, Francophones had lower rates of diagnosed substance use disorder (rate ratio [RR] = 0.80; 95% CI 0.68 to 0.95) and of suicide and suicide attempts (RR = 0.59; 95% CI 0.43 to 0.79), compared with non-Francophones, but no differences were found between the groups across the province in rates of diagnosed mood disorders, anxiety disorders, dementia, or any mental disorders after adjusting for age, sex, and geographic area. When surveyed, Francophones were less likely than non-Francophones to report that their mental health was excellent, very good, or good (66.9%, compared with 74.2%).']\n\nQuestion: Are there mental health differences between francophone and non-francophone populations in manitoba?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data show that outside urban areas, Francophones had significantly lower rates of diagnosed substance use disorders and suicide/suicide attempts compared to non-Francophones, indicating differences in specific mental health outcomes. However, no differences were found in rates of mood disorders, anxiety, dementia, or any mental disorder overall after adjustment. Additionally, survey results indicate Francophones were less likely to report positive mental health, suggesting disparities in self-perceived mental health.\n\nThus, there are both statistical differences and similarities depending on the measure, but differences do exist in key areas.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 381, "output_tokens": 121, "total_tokens": 502}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.9151e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_230", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Primary eosinophilic esophagitis, a chronic inflammatory disorder of the esophagus, evokes recurrent dysphagia. Endoscopy is often unremarkable, and no consensus exists regarding management of resultant dysphagia. The response of a series of patients with primary eosinophilic esophagitis to dilation is reported together with a description of a possibly pathognomonic sign: fragile esophageal mucosa, for which the term \"cr\u00eape-paper\" mucosa is introduced.', 'Five men underwent endoscopy because of dysphagia confirmed (clinically, endoscopically, and histologically) to be caused by primary eosinophilic esophagitis and were treated by bouginage.', 'All patients had extremely fragile, inelastic, and delicate mucosa, which tore easily even with minor trauma. After the procedure, patients remained asymptomatic for 3 to 24 months.']\n\nQuestion: Fragility of the esophageal mucosa: a pathognomonic endoscopic sign of primary eosinophilic esophagitis?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The term \"cr\u00eape-paper\" mucosa is introduced in the context as a possibly pathognomonic sign of primary eosinophilic esophagitis, and all five patients exhibited this fragile mucosa. However, the use of \"possibly pathognomonic\" suggests it is not definitively established. Therefore, while highly suggestive, it cannot be confirmed as absolutely pathognomonic based on this limited series.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 301, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 392}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.0470999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_231", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The incidence of acetabular fractures in osteoporotic patients is increasing. Immediate total hip arthroplasty (THA) has potential advantages, but achieving acetabular component stability is challenging and, at early followup, reported revision rates for loosening are high.QUESTIONS/', 'This study measured acetabular component stability and the initial surface contact achieved between the acetabular component and unfractured region of the pelvis after THA using an oversized acetabular component and cup-cage reconstruction.', 'Between November 2011 and November 2013, we treated 40 acute acetabular fractures in patients older than 70 years of age. Of these, 12 (30%) underwent immediate THA using an oversized acetabular component with screws inserted only into the ilium and a cup-cage construct. Postoperatively all patients were mobilized without weightbearing restrictions. Indications for immediate THA after acetabular fractures were displaced articular comminution deemed unreducible. Eleven of the 12 were prospectively studied to evaluate the initial stability of the reconstructions using radiostereometric analysis. One of the patients died of a pulmonary embolism after surgery, and the remaining 10 (median age, 81 years; range, 72-86 years) were studied. Of these, five were analyzed at 1 year and five were analyzed at 2 years. Acetabular component migration was defined as acceptable if less than the limits for primary THA that predict later loosening (1.76 mm of proximal migration and 2.53\u00b0 of sagittal rotation). The contact surface between the acetabular component and ilium in direct continuity with the sacroiliac joint, and the ischium and pubis in direct continuity with the symphysis pubis, was measured on postoperative CT scans.', 'At 1 year the median proximal migration was 0.83 mm (range, 0.09-5.13 mm) and sagittal rotation was 1.3\u00b0 (range, 0.1\u00b0-7.4\u00b0). Three of the 10 components had migration above the suggested limits for primary THA at 1 year postoperatively. The contact surface achieved at surgery between the acetabular component and pelvis ranged from 11 to 17 cm(2) (15%-27% of each component).']\n\nQuestion: Does cup-cage reconstruction with oversized cups provide initial stability in THA for osteoporotic acetabular fractures?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The provided study reports median acetabular component migration values (0.83 mm proximal, 1.3\u00b0 rotation) that fall inside published limits for primary THA, yet three of ten reconstructions exceeded those same limits at one year. This mixed pattern, together with the modest host-bone contact achieved (15\u201327 %), indicates that initial stability is obtained in some but not all osteoporotic fractures. Consequently, the most accurate choice among the options is \u201cmaybe.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 677, "output_tokens": 98, "total_tokens": 775}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00109125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_233", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Xanthogranulomatous cholecystitis (XGC) is an uncommon variant of chronic cholecystitis, characterized by marked thickening of the gallbladder wall and dense local adhesions. It often mimics a gallbladder carcinoma (GBC), and may coexist with GBC, leading to a diagnostic dilemma. Furthermore, the premalignant nature of this entity is not known. This study was undertaken to assess the p53, PCNA and beta-catenin expression in XGC in comparison to GBC and chronic inflammation.', 'Sections from paraffin-embedded blocks of surgically resected specimens of GBC (69 cases), XGC (65), chronic cholecystitis (18) and control gallbladder (10) were stained with the monoclonal antibodies to p53 and PCNA, and a polyclonal antibody to beta-catenin. p53 expression was scored as the percentage of nuclei stained. PCNA expression was scored as the product of the percentage of nuclei stained and the intensity of the staining (1-3). A cut-off value of 80 for this score was taken as a positive result. Beta-catenin expression was scored as type of expression-membranous, cytoplasmic or nuclear staining.', 'p53 mutation was positive in 52% of GBC cases and 3% of XGC, but was not expressed in chronic cholecystitis and control gallbladders. p53 expression was lower in XGC than in GBC (P<0.0001). PCNA expression was seen in 65% of GBC cases and 11% of XGC, but not in chronic cholecystitis and control gallbladders. PCNA expression was higher in GBC than XGC (P=0.0001), but there was no significant difference between the XGC, chronic cholecystitis and control gallbladder groups. Beta-catenin expression was positive in the GBC, XGC, chronic cholecystitis and control gallbladder groups. But the expression pattern in XGC, chronic cholecystitis and control gallbladders was homogenously membranous, whereas in GBC the membranous expression pattern was altered to cytoplasmic and nuclear.']\n\nQuestion: Xanthogranulomatous cholecystitis: a premalignant condition?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that p53 and PCNA expression, markers often associated with malignancy, are significantly lower in xanthogranulomatous cholecystitis (XGC) compared to gallbladder carcinoma (GBC), and similar to chronic cholecystitis and control groups. Beta-catenin expression in XGC remains membranous, unlike the abnormal cytoplasmic/nuclear expression seen in GBC, suggesting a lack of malignant transformation. Therefore, the evidence does not support XGC being a premalignant condition.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 585, "output_tokens": 116, "total_tokens": 701}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 5.3135e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_236", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To examine the representativeness of a randomized controlled trial (RCT) sample versus one obtained by consecutive new case ascertainment, for subjects with child bipolar I disorder.', \"Subjects (N = 247) were outpatients who participated in either the National Institute of Mental Health-funded Phenomenology and Course of Pediatric Bipolar Disorders study or the Treatment of Early Age Mania (TEAM) study. Both studies required that subjects have current DSM-IV bipolar I disorder (manic or mixed phase) and a Children's Global Assessment Scale (CGAS) score<or=60. All subjects had elation and/or grandiosity. Subjects in the Phenomenology study were obtained from 1995 to 1998 by consecutive new case ascertainment from designated pediatric and psychiatric facilities. Subjects in the TEAM RCT were recruited from media and community sources between March 2003 and March 2005. Assessment instruments included the Washington University in St. Louis Kiddie Schedule for Affective Disorders and Schizophrenia, given separately to parents about their children and to children about themselves, and the CGAS. Logistic regression was used for comparisons.\", 'The TEAM and Phenomenology groups were similar in age (10.4 [SD = 2.3], 10.9 [SD = 2.3]years, respectively) and other demography. Both had long current episode duration (4.8 [SD = 2.4], 3.2 [SD = 2.3]years) and low lifetime use of any mood stabilizer (23.6%, 35.0%). Many mania symptoms and ultradian rapid cycling, psychosis, and suicidality were significantly more prevalent in the RCT sample.']\n\nQuestion: Diagnostic characteristics of child bipolar I disorder: does the \"Treatment of Early Age Mania (team)\" sample generalize?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The \"Treatment of Early Age Mania (TEAM)\" sample showed significantly higher prevalence of severe symptoms such as psychosis, suicidality, and ultradian rapid cycling compared to the consecutively ascertained Phenomenology sample, suggesting it is not fully representative of the general child bipolar I population. This indicates that findings from the RCT may not generalize well due to a more severe symptom profile in the TEAM sample. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 465, "output_tokens": 97, "total_tokens": 562}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.2715e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_237", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Measurement of basal metabolic rate (BMR) is suggested as a tool to estimate energy requirements. Therefore, BMR prediction equations have been developed in multiple populations because indirect calorimetry is not always feasible. However, there is a paucity of data on BMR measured in overweight and obese adults living in Asia and equations developed for this group of interest. The aim of this study was to develop a new BMR prediction equation for Chinese adults applicable for a large BMI range and compare it with commonly used prediction equations.', 'Subjects were 121 men and 111 women (age: 21-67 years, BMI: 16-41\\xa0kg/m(2)). Height, weight, and BMR were measured. Continuous open-circuit indirect calorimetry using a ventilated hood system for 30\\xa0min was used to measure BMR. A regression equation was derived using stepwise regression and accuracy was compared to 6 existing equations (Harris-Benedict, Henry, Liu, Yang, Owen and Mifflin). Additionally, the newly derived equation was cross-validated in a separate group of 70 Chinese subjects (26 men and 44 women, age: 21-69 years, BMI: 17-39\\xa0kg/m(2)).', 'The equation developed from our data was: BMR (kJ/d)\\u2009=\\u200952.6 x weight (kg)\\u2009+\\u2009828 x gender\\u2009+\\u20091960 (women\\u2009=\\u20090, men\\u2009=\\u20091; R(2)\\u2009=\\u20090.81). The accuracy rate (within 10\\xa0% accurate) was 78\\xa0% which compared well to Owen (70\\xa0%), Henry (67\\xa0%), Mifflin (67\\xa0%), Liu (58\\xa0%), Harris-Benedict (45\\xa0%) and Yang (37\\xa0%) for the whole range of BMI. For a BMI greater than 23, the Singapore equation reached an accuracy rate of 76\\xa0%. Cross-validation proved an accuracy rate of 80\\xa0%.']\n\nQuestion: Estimation of basal metabolic rate in Chinese: are the current prediction equations applicable?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that commonly used prediction equations had low accuracy rates (ranging from 37% to 70%) when applied to Chinese adults, especially those with higher BMI. The newly developed equation showed superior accuracy (78%) and performed well in cross-validation (80%), indicating that existing equations are not optimal. Therefore, the current prediction equations are not fully applicable for Chinese adults, particularly in a broader BMI range.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 601, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 693}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 5.1871000000000005e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_238", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To examine the attitudes of players and coaches to the use of protective headgear, particularly with respect to the prevention of concussion.', 'A questionnaire designed to assess attitudes to headgear was administered to 63 players from four different Canadian teams, each representing a different level of play (high school, university, community club, national). In addition, coaches from all four levels were questioned about team policies and their personal opinions about the use of headgear to prevent concussion.', 'Although the players tended to believe that the headgear could prevent concussion (62%), the coaches were less convinced (33%). Despite the players\\' belief that headgear offers protection against concussion, only a minority reported wearing headgear (27%) and few (24%) felt that its use should be made mandatory. Common reasons for not wearing headgear were \"its use is not mandatory\", \"it is uncomfortable\", and \"it costs too much\".']\n\nQuestion: Does rugby headgear prevent concussion?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context indicates that while 62% of players believe headgear can prevent concussion, only 33% of coaches share this belief, and the study does not provide scientific evidence confirming its effectiveness. Additionally, the passage highlights that many players do not wear headgear and do not support making it mandatory, citing comfort, cost, and lack of requirement. Therefore, based on the given information, the effectiveness of rugby headgear in preventing concussion is uncertain.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 271, "output_tokens": 98, "total_tokens": 369}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.9041000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_239", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['A case of spinal subdural hematoma (SSDH) following subarachnoid hemorrhage (SAH) because of a ruptured internal carotid aneurysm is described. Such a case has never been reported.', 'A 52-year-old woman underwent a craniotomy for a ruptured internal carotid aneurysm. A computed tomography scan showed that SAH existed predominantly in the posterior fossa and subdural hematoma beneath the cerebellar tentorium. Intrathecal administration of urokinase, IV administration of fasudil hydrochloride, and continuous cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) evacuation via cisternal drainage were performed as prophylactic treatments for vasospasm. On the sixth postoperative day, the patient complained of severe lower back and buttock pain. Magnetic resonance imaging showed a subdural hematoma in the lumbosacral region. Although the mass effect was extensive, the patient showed no neurologic symptoms other than the sciatica. She was treated conservatively. The hematoma dissolved gradually and had diminished completely 15 weeks later. Her pain gradually subsided, and she was discharged 7 weeks later without any neurologic deficit.']\n\nQuestion: Spinal subdural hematoma: a sequela of a ruptured intracranial aneurysm?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The case describes a spinal subdural hematoma (SSDH) that developed after a ruptured intracranial aneurysm and subsequent subarachnoid hemorrhage, suggesting a possible causal relationship. Although rare and previously unreported, the temporal association and clinical course support SSDH as a sequela in this instance. Therefore, the most appropriate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 388, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 483}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.7048e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_240", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Patients presenting with transient ischemic attack or stroke may have symptom-related lesions on acute computed tomography angiography (CTA) such as free-floating intraluminal thrombus (FFT). It is difficult to distinguish FFT from carotid plaque, but the distinction is critical as management differs. By contouring the shape of these vascular lesions (\"virtual endarterectomy\"), advanced morphometric analysis can be performed. The objective of our study is to determine whether quantitative shape analysis can accurately differentiate FFT from atherosclerotic plaque.', 'We collected 23 consecutive cases of suspected carotid FFT seen on CTA (13 men, 65 \u00b1 10 years; 10 women, 65.5 \u00b1 8.8 years). True-positive FFT cases (FFT+) were defined as filling defects resolving with anticoagulant therapy versus false-positives (FFT-), which remained unchanged. Lesion volumes were extracted from CTA images and quantitative shape descriptors were computed. The five most discriminative features were used to construct receiver operator characteristic (ROC) curves and to generate three machine-learning classifiers. Average classification accuracy was determined by cross-validation.', 'Follow-up imaging confirmed sixteen FFT+ and seven FFT- cases. Five shape descriptors delineated FFT+ from FFT- cases. The logistic regression model produced from combining all five shape features demonstrated a sensitivity of 87.5% and a specificity of 71.4% with an area under the ROC curve = 0.85 \u00b1 0.09. Average accuracy for each classifier ranged from 65.2%-76.4%.']\n\nQuestion: Can shape analysis differentiate free-floating internal carotid artery thrombus from atherosclerotic plaque in patients evaluated with CTA for stroke or transient ischemic attack?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that quantitative shape analysis using five discriminative features could differentiate free-floating thrombus (FFT+) from atherosclerotic plaque (FFT-) with a sensitivity of 87.5% and specificity of 71.4%, and an area under the ROC curve of 0.85. This indicates a statistically significant ability to distinguish between the two lesion types. Therefore, shape analysis shows promise in differentiating FFT from plaque on CTA.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 444, "output_tokens": 99, "total_tokens": 543}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.1424e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_241", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To determine the prevalence and nature of global cognitive dysfunction and language deficits in an unselected population based cohort of patients with motor neuron disease (MND).', 'A battery of neuropsychological and language tests was administered to patients presenting consecutively over a 3 year period to a regional neurology service with a new diagnosis of sporadic motor neuron disease.', 'The 18 patients could be divided on the basis of their performance into three groups: Three patients were demented and had impaired language function (group 1); two non-demented patients had an aphasic syndrome characterised by word finding difficulties and anomia (group 2). Major cognitive deficits were therefore found in five of the 18 patients (28%). The remaining 13 performed normally on the test battery apart from decreased verbal fluency (group 3).']\n\nQuestion: Dementia and aphasia in motor neuron disease: an underrecognised association?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that 28% of patients with motor neuron disease had major cognitive deficits, including dementia and aphasia, indicating that these conditions are present in a significant portion of MND patients. The presence of both dementia and aphasic syndromes, even in non-demented individuals, suggests an underrecognized association. Therefore, the evidence supports the idea that this association is indeed underrecognized.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 266, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 353}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.7586e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_243", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Our aim was to determine the value of echo-planar diffusion-weighted MR imaging (epiDWI) in differentiating various types of primary parotid gland tumors.', 'One hundred forty-nine consecutive patients with suspected tumors of the parotid gland were examined with an epiDWI sequence by using a 1.5T unit. Image analysis was performed by 2 radiologists independently, and the intraclass correlation coefficient was computed. Histologic diagnosis was obtained in every patient. For comparison of apparent diffusion coefficients (ADCs), a paired 2-tailed Student t test with a Bonferroni correction was used.', 'In 136 patients, a primary parotid gland tumor was confirmed by histology. Among the observers, a high correlation was calculated (0.98). ADC values of pleomorphic adenomas were significantly higher than those of all other entities, except for myoepithelial adenomas (P = .054). ADC values of Warthin tumors were different from those of myoepithelial adenomas, lipomas, and salivary duct carcinomas (P<.001, 0.013, and .037, respectively). Mucoepidermoid carcinomas, acinic cell carcinomas, and basal cell adenocarcinomas were not differentiable from Warthin tumors (P = .094, .396, and .604, respectively).']\n\nQuestion: Diffusion-weighted echo-planar MR imaging of primary parotid gland tumors: is a prediction of different histologic subtypes possible?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study demonstrates that while some tumor types (such as pleomorphic adenomas) show distinct ADC values, others overlap significantly, making a definitive prediction of all histologic subtypes difficult. Therefore, the findings suggest that while epiDWI provides useful diagnostic information, it does not allow for a complete or reliable prediction of all specific histologic subtypes.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 384, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 456}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:08.419971+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000204, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_247", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['As part of an MRC funded study into primary care oral anticoagulation management, INR measurements obtained in general practice were validated against values on the same samples obtained in hospital laboratories. A prospective comparative trial was undertaken between three hospital laboratories and nine general practices. All patients attending general practice based anticoagulant clinics had parallel INR estimations performed in general practice and in a hospital laboratory.', '405 tests were performed. Comparison between results obtained in the practices and those in the reference hospital laboratory (gold standard), which used the same method of testing for INR, showed a correlation coefficient of 0.96. Correlation coefficients comparing the results with the various standard laboratory techniques ranged from 0.86 to 0.92. It was estimated that up to 53% of tests would have resulted in clinically significant differences (change in warfarin dose) depending upon the site and method of testing. The practice derived results showed a positive bias ranging from 0.28 to 1.55, depending upon the site and method of testing.']\n\nQuestion: Is the international normalised ratio (INR) reliable?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The high correlation coefficient of 0.96 with the reference hospital laboratory suggests strong agreement, but the presence of clinically significant differences in up to 53% of tests and a positive bias indicate potential reliability issues in practice. While the INR is generally reliable, variability due to testing site and method raises concerns about consistency. Therefore, the most accurate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 311, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 391}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.0081e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_250", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Adoption and implementation of evidence-based measures for catheter care leads to reductions in central line-associated bloodstream infection (CLABSI) rates in the NICU. The purpose of this study is to evaluate whether this rate reduction is sustainable for at least 1 year and to identify key determinants of this sustainability at the NICU of the Floating Hospital for Children at Tufts Medical Center.', 'We reviewed the incidence of CLABSIs in the NICU temporally to the implementation of new practice policies and procedures, from July 2008 to December 2013.', 'Adoption of standardized care practices, including bundles and checklists, was associated with a significant reduction of the CLABSI rate to zero for>370 consecutive days in our NICU in 2012. Overall, our CLABSI rates decreased from 4.1 per 1000 line days in 2009 (13 infections; 3163 line days) to 0.94 in 2013 (2 infections; 2115 line days), which represents a 77% reduction over a 5-year period. In the first quarter of 2013, there was a brief increase in CLABSI rate to 3.3 per 1000 line days; after a series of interventions, the CLABSI rate was maintained at zero for>600 days. Ongoing training, surveillance, and vigilance with catheter insertion and maintenance practices and improved documentation were identified as key drivers for success.']\n\nQuestion: Is zero central line-associated bloodstream infection rate sustainable?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that the NICU achieved a zero CLABSI rate for over 370 consecutive days in 2012 and later maintained it for over 600 days after interventions, indicating sustainability over an extended period. Ongoing training, surveillance, and improved practices were identified as key factors enabling this sustained reduction. Therefore, the evidence supports that a zero CLABSI rate is achievable and sustainable with continued effort.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 414, "output_tokens": 94, "total_tokens": 508}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.8793999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_255", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The last 20 years has seen a marked improvement in skin cancer awareness campaigns. We sought to establish whether this has affected the presenting Breslow thickness of malignant melanoma in the South West.', 'This is a retrospective study looking at the first presentation of melanomas from 2003 to 2011. Data was accessed using the local online melanoma database.', 'A total of 2001 new melanomas presented from 2003 to 2012 (Male:Female = 1:1.062). The average yearly number of melanomas was 200.1 (range = 138-312). The mean age was 62.5 years (range 12-99). Data was analysed using a Chi\u00b2 test. For 0-1 mm melanomas, there is a significant difference in the observed versus expected values over the 10 years (p = 0.0018). There is an increasing proportion of 0-1 mm (thin) melanomas presenting year on year, with a positive linear trend. This is very statistically significant (p<0.0001). The 1-2 mm melanomas are decreasing in proportion with a negative linear trend (p = 0.0013). The 2-4 mm are also decreasing in proportion (p = 0.0253). There is no significant change in the thick>4 mm melanomas (p = 0.1456).']\n\nQuestion: Are we seeing the effects of public awareness campaigns?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data shows a statistically significant increase in the proportion of thin (0\u20131 mm) melanomas and a decrease in intermediate thickness melanomas over time, suggesting earlier detection. This trend aligns with improved public awareness leading to earlier presentation of skin cancers. Therefore, the evidence supports that public awareness campaigns are having a positive effect.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 412, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 483}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.6351999999999993e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_257", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['This study was planned to evaluate whether increased nuchal translucency (NT) thickness in the first trimester of gestation can be related to onset of gestational diabetes mellitus (GDM) during pregnancy.', \"From January 2006 to August 2008, a group of 678 singleton pregnancies who had developed GDM has been selected as a study group among a total of 3966 pregnant women who had undergone first trimester screening for aneuploidies at 11-14 weeks of gestation. A group of 420 single pregnant women with physiological pregnancy were enrolled as control group. Both fetal structural and karyotype's anomalies were excluded in the two groups. NT was mesured by a Fetal Medicine Foundation certificated operator; GDM was diagnosed at 24-28 weeks of gestation following Carpenter and Coustan criteria. In the analyses of continuos variables, study and control group were compared by Student's t-test and Anova test.\", 'There was no significative difference (p = 0.585) between NT values in the study (mean = 1.56) and control group (mean = 1.54).']\n\nQuestion: Does nuchal translucency thickness in the first trimester predict GDM onset during pregnancy?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant difference in nuchal translucency (NT) thickness between pregnancies that developed gestational diabetes mellitus (GDM) and those that did not (p = 0.585). This indicates that increased NT thickness in the first trimester is not associated with an increased risk of developing GDM. Therefore, NT thickness does not predict GDM onset.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 355, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 440}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.3705e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_258", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"To examine family-based transmission of the number of 5' flanking arginine vasopressin V1a receptor (AVPR1A) microsatellites, which include [(GATA)(14)] and complex [(CT)(4)-TT-(CT)(8)-(GT)(24)]repeats, in probands with a prepubertal and early adolescent bipolar disorder phenotype (PEA-BP). Preferential transmission of the number of AVPR1A microsatellite repeats to hypersexual and uninhibited people-seeking probands was hypothesized, based on reports from preclinical work in the literature.\", 'Probands were 83 participants in an ongoing controlled study of PEA-BP. The PEA-BP phenotype was defined by DSM-IV mania with at least one of the cardinal symptoms of mania (elation and/or grandiosity) to avoid diagnosing mania only by symptoms that overlapped with those for attention-deficit hyperactivity disorder (ADHD). Comprehensive assessment of the probands included separate Washington University in St. Louis Kiddie Schedule for Affective Disorders and Schizophrenia (WASH-U-KSADS) interviews of parents about their children and of children about themselves. Hypersexuality and uninhibited people-seeking were assessed from the corresponding WASH-U-KSADS items. Microsatellite genotyping of the AVPR1A repeats was conducted using fluorescently labeled primers and detected by laser-induced fluorescence. Alleles were determined with the assistance of semi-automated allele-calling software. There were 32 complete, biological trios (28 informative families) for the GATA repeat and 34 complete, biological trios (30 informative families) for the complex repeat. Data were analyzed using case-control and family-based association methods.', 'Preferential transmission of AVPR1A GATA or complex repeats was not significant for hypersexuality or uninhibited people-seeking, using the transmission disequilibrium test. Similarly, case-control analyses found no significant associations between hypersexuality or uninhibited people-seeking and the number of AVPR1A GATA or complex repeats. For p<0.05, there was about 80% power to detect odds ratios of 5.0 and 4.0 (in the family-based analyses) and 3.5 and 2.6 (in the case-control analyses), for allele frequencies of 0.1 and 0.5, respectively.']\n\nQuestion: Are the arginine vasopressin V1a receptor microsatellites related to hypersexuality in children with a prepubertal and early adolescent bipolar disorder phenotype?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant preferential transmission of AVPR1A GATA or complex repeats to children with hypersexuality or uninhibited people-seeking behaviors, based on both family-based and case-control analyses. Despite sufficient statistical power to detect moderate to large effects, no significant associations were observed. Therefore, the evidence does not support a relationship between these microsatellites and hypersexuality in this population.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 616, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 702}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 5.2336e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_259", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['We review our results on surgical treatment of patients with stage I non-small cell lung carcinoma and we attempted to clarify the prognostic significance of some surgical--pathologic variables.', 'From 1993 to 1999, 667 patients received curative lung resection and complete hilar and mediastinal lymphadenectomy for non-small cell lung cancer. Of these, there were 436 Stage I disease (65%), of whom 144 T1N0 and 292 T2N0. No patients had pre- or postoperative radio- or chemotherapy. Prognostic significance of the following independent variables was tested using univariate (log-rank) and multivariate (Cox proportional-hazards) analysis: type of resection (sublobar vs lobectomy vs pneumonectomy), histology (squamous cell vs adenocarcinoma), tumour size (<or=3cm vs>3cm), histologic vascular invasion, visceral pleura involvement, positive bronchial resection margin, general T status.', 'Overall 5-year survival was 63%. In both univariate and multivariate survival analysis, significant prognostic factors were histology (adenocarcinoma 65% vs squamous cell carcinoma 51%), tumour size (<or=3cm 67% vs>3cm 46%), and the presence of negative resection margin. Five-year survival by general T status was 66% in T1N0 vs 55% in T2N0 disease (P=0.19).']\n\nQuestion: Stage I non-small cell lung carcinoma: really an early stage?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The 5-year survival rate for Stage I non-small cell lung carcinoma in this study is 63%, with further stratification showing better outcomes for smaller tumors and certain histologies, indicating variability in prognosis even within Stage I. Despite being classified as early-stage, the presence of significant prognostic factors like tumor size, histology, and resection margin status suggests that not all Stage I cases behave indolently. Therefore, Stage I may not always represent a uniformly \"early\" or benign disease.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 427, "output_tokens": 108, "total_tokens": 535}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.1117e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_26", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Social and cultural factors combined with little information may prevent the diffusion of epidural analgesia for pain relief during childbirth. The present study was launched contemporarily to the implementation of analgesia for labor in our Department in order to perform a 2 years audit on its use. The goal is to evaluate the epidural acceptance and penetration into hospital practice by women and care givers and safety and efficacy during childbirth.', 'This audit cycle measured epidural analgesia performance against 4 standards: (1) Implementation of epidural analgesia for labor to all patients; (2) Acceptance and good satisfaction level reported by patients and caregivers. (3) Effectiveness of labor analgesia; (4) No maternal or fetal side effects.', 'During the audit period epidural analgesia increased from 15.5% of all labors in the first trimester of the study to 51% in the last trimester (p<0.005). Satisfaction levels reported by patients and care givers were good. A hierarchical clustering analysis identified two clusters based on VAS (Visual Analogue Scale) time course: in 226 patients (cluster 1) VAS decreased from 8.5\u00b11.4 before to 4.1\u00b11.3 after epidural analgesia; in 1002 patients (cluster 2) VAS decreased from 8.12\u00b11.7 before (NS vs cluster 1), to 0.76\u00b10.79 after (p<0.001 vs before and vs cluster 2 after). No other differences between clusters were observed.']\n\nQuestion: Implementation of epidural analgesia for labor: is the standard of effective analgesia reachable in all women?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study results show that while pain scores decreased significantly for all patients, the hierarchical clustering analysis identified two distinct groups with different levels of residual pain (VAS 4.1 vs. 0.76). Because the effectiveness of the analgesia varied between these clusters, it indicates that the same level of \"effective analgesia\" was not reached for every woman. Therefore, the standard is not uniformly reachable for all patients.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 423, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 514}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:30.473611+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00024225, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_261", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Studies examining predictors of survival among the oldest-old have primarily focused on objective measures, such as physical function and health status. Only a few studies have examined the effect of personality traits on survival, such as optimism. The aim of this study was to examine whether an optimistic outlook predicts survival among the oldest-old.', 'The Danish 1905 Cohort Survey is a nationwide, longitudinal survey comprising all individuals born in Denmark in 1905. At baseline in 1998, a total of 2,262 persons aged 92 or 93 agreed to participate in the intake survey. The baseline in-person interview consisted of a comprehensive questionnaire including physical functioning and health, and a question about whether the respondent had an optimistic, neutral or pessimistic outlook on his or her own future.', 'During the follow-up period of 12 years (1998-2010) there were 2,239 deaths (99 %) in the 1905 Cohort Survey. Univariable analyses revealed that optimistic women and men were at lower risk of death compared to their neutral counterparts [HR 0.82, 95 % CI (0.73-0.93) and 0.81, 95 % CI (0.66-0.99), respectively]. When confounding factors such as baseline physical and cognitive functioning and disease were taken into account the association between optimism and survival weakened in both sexes, but the general pattern persisted. Optimistic women were still at lower risk of death compared to neutral women [HR 0.85, 95 % CI (0.74-0.97)]. The risk of death was also decreased for optimistic men compared to their neutral counterparts, but the effect was non-significant [HR 0.91, 95 % CI (0.73-1.13)].']\n\nQuestion: Optimism and survival: does an optimistic outlook predict better survival at advanced ages?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that optimistic individuals, particularly women, had a significantly lower risk of death compared to those with a neutral outlook, even after adjusting for physical and cognitive health. Although the effect was not statistically significant for men, the trend still favored optimism. Overall, the evidence supports a positive association between optimism and survival in the oldest-old.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 495, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 568}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.244499999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_262", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Swedish hospital mergers seem to stem from a conviction among policy makers that bigger hospitals lead to lower average costs and improved clinical outcomes. The effects of mergers in the form of multisited hospitals have not been systematically evaluated. The purpose of this article is to contribute to this area of knowledge by exploring responses to the merger of Blekinge Hospital.', 'The evaluation was guided by the philosophy of triangulation. A questionnaire was sent to 597 randomly selected employees, that is 24% of the health care staff. Four hundred ninety-eight employees answered the questionnaire, giving a response rate of 83%. Furthermore, interviews of different groups of stakeholders were conducted.', 'A moderate increase of quality was assessed, which, a low proportion of the employees perceived had decisively or largely to do with the merger. The majority perceives economical incentives as the drivers of change, but, at the same time, only 10% of this group believes this target was reached completely or to a large extent.']\n\nQuestion: Is it better to be big?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context suggests that while policy makers believe bigger hospitals lead to lower costs and better outcomes, employee perceptions indicate only a moderate quality increase and widespread skepticism about achieving economic goals. Most employees saw economic incentives as the main driver but doubted these targets were met. Therefore, the evidence does not strongly support the idea that bigger is better.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 289, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 359}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.7519e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_263", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Orthodontic patients show high prevalence of tooth-size discrepancy. This study investigates the possible association between arch form, clinically significant tooth-size discrepancy, and sagittal molar relationship.', 'Pretreatment orthodontic casts of 230 Saudi patients were classified into one of three arch form types (tapered, ovoid, and square) using digitally scanned images of the mandibular arches. Bolton ratio was calculated, sagittal molar relationship was defined according to Angle classification, and correlations were analyzed using ANOVA, chi-square, and t-tests.', 'No single arch form was significantly more common than the others. Furthermore, no association was observed between the presence of significant Bolton discrepancy and the sagittal molar relationship or arch form. Overall Bolton discrepancy is significantly more prevalent in males.']\n\nQuestion: Is arch form influenced by sagittal molar relationship or Bolton tooth-size discrepancy?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant association between arch form and either sagittal molar relationship or Bolton tooth-size discrepancy. Statistical analyses (ANOVA, chi-square, and t-tests) showed no correlation among these variables. Therefore, arch form does not appear to be influenced by sagittal molar relationship or tooth-size discrepancy.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 256, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 324}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.4976e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_264", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To prospectively evaluate the amount of tissue removed at loop electrosurgical excision procedure (LEEP) vs. cold knife conization.', \"Forty consecutive LEEP or cold knife conization specimens were prospectively measured and weighed by a single pathology technician. Diameter, length and weight of the specimens were compared using Student's t test.\", 'Mean diameter of cold knife cone specimens was 2.6 vs. 2.2 cm for LEEP (P = .07). Mean length of cold knife cone specimens was 1.5 vs. 1.0 cm for LEEP (P = .001). Mean weight for cold knife cone specimens was 4.4 vs. 2.0 g for LEEP (P = .001).']\n\nQuestion: Cold knife conization vs. LEEP. Are they the same procedure?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context shows that cold knife conization and LEEP differ significantly in specimen length and weight, with cold knife conization removing more tissue. These differences indicate that the two procedures are not the same. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 250, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 303}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.305e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_265", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The hypothesis was tested that pectin content and methylation degree participate in regulation of cell wall mechanical properties and in this way may affect tissue growth and freezing resistance over the course of plant cold acclimation and de-acclimation.', 'Experiments were carried on the leaves of two double-haploid lines of winter oil-seed rape (Brassica napus subsp. oleifera), differing in winter survival and resistance to blackleg fungus (Leptosphaeria maculans).', 'Plant acclimation in the cold (2 degrees C) brought about retardation of leaf expansion, concomitant with development of freezing resistance. These effects were associated with the increases in leaf tensile stiffness, cell wall and pectin contents, pectin methylesterase (EC 3.1.1.11) activity and the low-methylated pectin content, independently of the genotype studied. However, the cold-induced modifications in the cell wall properties were more pronounced in the leaves of the more pathogen-resistant genotype. De-acclimation promoted leaf expansion and reversed most of the cold-induced effects, with the exception of pectin methylesterase activity.']\n\nQuestion: Are pectins involved in cold acclimation and de-acclimation of winter oil-seed rape plants?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The passage indicates that pectin content, methylation degree, and pectin methylesterase activity change during cold acclimation and de-acclimation, affecting cell wall properties and freezing resistance. These changes were observed in both genotypes of winter oil-seed rape, with more pronounced effects in the pathogen-resistant line. This evidence clearly supports the involvement of pectins in both acclimation and de-acclimation processes.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 345, "output_tokens": 96, "total_tokens": 441}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.4095e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_266", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Interference from irrelevant negative material might be a key mechanism underlying intrusive ruminative thoughts in depression. Considering commonalities between depression and social anxiety and the presence of similar intrusive thoughts in social anxiety, the current study was designed to assess whether interference from irrelevant material in working memory is specific to depression or is also present in social anxiety disorder.', 'To examine the effects of irrelevant emotional material on working memory performance, participants memorized two lists of words on each trial and were subsequently instructed to ignore one of the lists. Participants were then asked to indicate whether a probe word belonged to the relevant list or not.', 'Compared to control and social anxiety groups, the depression groups (both pure and comorbid with social anxiety disorder) exhibited greater difficulties removing irrelevant emotional material from working memory (i.e., greater intrusion effects). Greater intrusion effects were also associated with increased rumination.', 'Although we included three clinical groups (depression, social anxiety, and the comorbid groups), the results are based on a relatively small number of participants.']\n\nQuestion: Updating emotional content in working memory: a depression-specific deficit?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that individuals with depression, both pure and comorbid with social anxiety, had greater difficulty removing irrelevant emotional material from working memory compared to those with social anxiety alone and controls. This suggests a specific deficit in updating emotional content in working memory associated with depression. Although the sample size was small, the results point toward depression-specific interference effects.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 418, "output_tokens": 116, "total_tokens": 534}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.1278e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_27", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To evaluate the impact of HER2 immunoreactivity on clinical outcome in locally advanced urothelial carcinoma patients who received surgery alone, or methotrexate, vinblastine, epirubicin, and cisplatin (M-VEC) as adjuvant chemotherapy.', \"We studied 114 formalin-fixed paraffin-embedded specimens obtained from locally advanced urothelial carcinoma patients receiving surgery alone or adjuvant M-VEC. The authors evaluated HER2 immunoreactivity using immunohistochemical staining and explored the influence of pathological parameters and HER2 immunoreactivity on progression-free survival (PFS) and disease-specific overall survival (OS) using univariate and multivariate Cox's analyses.\", 'Urothelial carcinoma of the bladder had a significantly higher frequency of HER2 immunoreactivity than that of the upper urinary tract (60.7 vs. 20.7%, p<0.0001). Overall, nodal status was a strong and independent prognostic indicator for clinical outcome. The HER2 immunoreactivity was significantly associated with PFS (p = 0.02) and disease-specific OS (p = 0.005) in advanced urothelial carcinoma patients. As for patients with adjuvant M-VEC, HER2 immunoreactivity was a significant prognostic factor for PFS (p = 0.03) and disease-specific OS (p = 0.02) using univariate analysis, but not multivariate analysis, and not for patients receiving watchful waiting.']\n\nQuestion: Does HER2 immunoreactivity provide prognostic information in locally advanced urothelial carcinoma patients receiving adjuvant M-VEC chemotherapy?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study indicates that HER2 immunoreactivity was a significant prognostic factor for both progression-free survival and disease-specific overall survival in patients receiving adjuvant M-VEC according to univariate analysis. Although it was not significant in the multivariate analysis, it is identified as providing prognostic information in the context of the study's findings.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 396, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 467}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:38.301037+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0002055, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_270", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['It is now widely accepted that AMP-activated protein kinase (AMPK) is a critical regulator of energy homeostasis. Recently, it has been shown to regulate circadian clocks. In seasonal breeding species such as sheep, the circadian clock controls the secretion of an endogenous rhythm of melatonin and, as a consequence, is probably involved in the generation of seasonal rhythms of reproduction. Considering this, we identified the presence of the subunits of AMPK in different hypothalamic nuclei involved in the pre- and post-pineal pathways that control seasonality of reproduction in the ewe and we investigated if the intracerebroventricular (i.c.v.) injection of two activators of AMPK, metformin and AICAR, affected the circadian rhythm of melatonin in ewes that were housed in constant darkness. In parallel the secretion of insulin was monitored as a peripheral metabolic marker. We also investigated the effects of i.c.v. AICAR on the phosphorylation of AMPK and acetyl-CoA carboxylase (ACC), a downstream target of AMPK, in brain structures along the photoneuroendocrine pathway to the pineal gland.', 'All the subunits of AMPK that we studied were identified in all brain areas that were dissected but with some differences in their level of expression among structures. Metformin and AICAR both reduced (p<0.001 and p<0.01 respectively) the amplitude of the circadian rhythm of melatonin secretion independently of insulin secretion. The i.c.v. injection of AICAR only tended (p = 0.1) to increase the levels of phosphorylated AMPK in the paraventricular nucleus but significantly increased the levels of phosphorylated ACC in the paraventricular nucleus (p<0.001) and in the pineal gland (p<0.05).']\n\nQuestion: The effect of an intracerebroventricular injection of metformin or AICAR on the plasma concentrations of melatonin in the ewe: potential involvement of AMPK?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The intracerebroventricular injection of metformin and AICAR reduced the amplitude of the circadian rhythm of melatonin secretion, and AICAR increased phosphorylation of ACC, a downstream target of AMPK, in key brain regions. This suggests that AMPK activation in the brain influences melatonin secretion. Therefore, the effect on melatonin is likely mediated by AMPK.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 505, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 590}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.4355e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_271", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Cerebral hemispherectomy, a surgical procedure undergone to control intractable seizures, is becoming a standard procedure with more cases identified and treated early in life [33]. While the effect of the dominant hemisphere resection on spoken language has been extensively researched, little is known about reading abilities in individuals after left-sided resection. Left-lateralized phonological abilities are the key components of reading, i.e., grapheme-phoneme conversion skills [1]. These skills are critical for the acquisition of word-specific orthographic knowledge and have been shown to predict reading levels in average readers as well as in readers with mild cognitive disability [26]. Furthermore, impaired phonological processing has been implicated as the cognitive basis in struggling readers. Here, we explored the reading skills in participants who have undergone left cerebral hemispherectomy.', 'Seven individuals who have undergone left cerebral hemispherectomy to control intractable seizures associated with perinatal infarct have been recruited for this study. We examined if components of phonological processing that are shown to reliably separate average readers from struggling readers, i.e., phonological awareness, verbal memory, speed of retrieval, and size of vocabulary, show the same relationship to reading levels when they are mediated by the right hemisphere [2].', 'We found that about 60% of our group developed both word reading and paragraph reading in the average range. Phonological processing measured by both phonological awareness and nonword reading was unexpectedly spared in the majority of participants. Phonological awareness levels strongly correlated with word reading. Verbal memory, a component of phonological processing skills, together with receptive vocabulary size, positively correlated with reading levels similar to those reported in average readers. Receptive vocabulary, a bilateral function, was preserved to a certain degree similar to that of strongly left-lateralized phonological skills [3]. Later seizure onset was associated with better reading levels.']\n\nQuestion: Literacy after cerebral hemispherectomy: Can the isolated right hemisphere read?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that about 60% of individuals who underwent left cerebral hemispherectomy developed average reading skills, and phonological processing\u2014critical for reading\u2014was largely preserved. Phonological awareness and verbal memory correlated with reading levels similarly to typical readers, indicating functional reading abilities mediated by the right hemisphere. Therefore, the isolated right hemisphere can support reading.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 642, "output_tokens": 114, "total_tokens": 756}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 5.698199999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_276", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Preventive home visits are offered to community dwelling older people in Denmark aimed at maintaining their functional ability for as long as possible, but only two thirds of older people accept the offer from the municipalities. The purpose of this study is to investigate 1) whether socioeconomic status was associated with acceptance of preventive home visits among older people and 2) whether municipality invitational procedures for the preventive home visits modified the association.', 'The study population included 1,023 community dwelling 80-year-old individuals from the Danish intervention study on preventive home visits. Information on preventive home visit acceptance rates was obtained from questionnaires. Socioeconomic status was measured by financial assets obtained from national registry data, and invitational procedures were identified through the municipalities. Logistic regression analyses were used, adjusted by gender.', 'Older persons with high financial assets accepted preventive home visits more frequently than persons with low assets (adjusted OR = 1.5 (CI95%: 1.1-2.0)). However, the association was attenuated when adjusted by the invitational procedures. The odds ratio for accepting preventive home visits was larger among persons with low financial assets invited by a letter with a proposed date than among persons with high financial assets invited by other procedures, though these estimates had wide confidence intervals.']\n\nQuestion: Are acceptance rates of a national preventive home visit programme for older people socially imbalanced?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that older individuals with higher financial assets were more likely to accept preventive home visits than those with lower assets, indicating a socioeconomic disparity in acceptance rates. Although this association was influenced by municipal invitational procedures, the initial imbalance suggests a social gradient in uptake. Therefore, the evidence supports the presence of social imbalance.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 356, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 425}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.217599999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_277", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Some studies suggest that open access articles are more often cited than non-open access articles. However, the relationship between open access and citations count in a discipline such as intensive care medicine has not been studied to date. The present article analyzes the effect of open access publishing of scientific articles in intensive care medicine journals in terms of citations count.', 'We evaluated a total of 161 articles (76% being non-open access articles) published in Intensive Care Medicine in the year 2008. Citation data were compared between the two groups up until April 30, 2011. Potentially confounding variables for citation counts were adjusted for in a linear multiple regression model.', 'The median number (interquartile range) of citations of non-open access articles was 8 (4-12) versus 9 (6-18) in the case of open access articles (p=0.084). In the highest citation range (>8), the citation count was 13 (10-16) and 18 (13-21) (p=0.008), respectively. The mean follow-up was 37.5 \u00b1 3 months in both groups. In the 30-35 months after publication, the average number (mean \u00b1 standard deviation) of citations per article per month of non-open access articles was 0.28 \u00b1 0.6 versus 0.38 \u00b1 0.7 in the case of open access articles (p=0.043). Independent factors for citation advantage were the Hirsch index of the first signing author (\u03b2=0.207; p=0.015) and open access status (\u03b2=3.618; p=0.006).']\n\nQuestion: Does open access publishing increase the impact of scientific articles?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that open access articles had significantly higher citation counts in the higher citation range and over time, with open access status being an independent predictor of citation advantage. Although the overall median citation difference was not statistically significant, the results in key analyses support a positive impact of open access. Therefore, the evidence suggests that open access publishing does increase the impact of scientific articles.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 467, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 547}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.1157e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_278", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Infantile hypertrophic pyloric stenosis (IHPS) is a common condition which presents in infants at 2-12 weeks of postnatal life, and whose cause remains obscure. Multiple associated abnormalities have been recognized within the external hypertrophied pyloric muscle layer, but the internal component of the pyloric mucosa has received scant attention in the literature to date. Our purpose in this study was to show that pyloric mucosal redundancy is a constant finding in infants with IHPS, to discuss its possible cause, and to explore the hypothesis of a relationship between pyloric mucosal redundancy and the development of IHPS.', 'We identified 102 consecutive infants with surgically confirmed IHPS and determined the thickness of the pyloric mucosa compared with the thickness of the surrounding hypertrophied muscle. Fifty-one infants who did not have pyloric stenosis served as controls.', 'Mean mucosal thickness in patients with IHPS approximated mean muscle thickness, with a ratio of 0.89. In infants with IHPS, the pyloric mucosa constitutes approximately one third of the cross-sectional diameter of the pyloric mass and fills and obstructs the pyloric canal.']\n\nQuestion: In vivo visualization of pyloric mucosal hypertrophy in infants with hypertrophic pyloric stenosis: is there an etiologic role?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study demonstrates that pyloric mucosal redundancy is a constant finding in infants with IHPS, with the mucosa occupying a significant portion of the pyloric canal and contributing to obstruction. The mucosal thickness was nearly proportional to the hypertrophied muscle, suggesting a potential role in the pathophysiology. Therefore, the evidence supports a possible etiologic role of mucosal hypertrophy.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 416, "output_tokens": 107, "total_tokens": 523}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.0236e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_282", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['This study aims to evaluate the efficacy of closed reduction and the effects of timing and fracture types on patient satisfaction.', 'Only patients with isolated nasal fractures were included in the study. Patients with additional maxillofacial fractures and patients whose application time to our clinic was more than 10 days after the trauma were excluded. Patients were classified into 5 types according to their fracture. All patients underwent closed reduction and external fixation under local anesthesia. Patients were asked about their satisfaction in a survey at 28th day and sixth month after the surgery. Patients were divided into groups according to fracture type and intervention time, and the results of the survey were evaluated.', 'Of the 43 patients included in the study, 38 were male, 5 were female, and the average age was 24.9. The average intervention time of the patients was 5.44 days. Twenty-eight (65%) of 43 patients were satisfied with the result, whereas 15 (35%) patients were not happy with their operation. In a comparison of patient satisfaction rates according to fracture type, the mild fracture group had a higher satisfaction rate compared to the severe fracture group.']\n\nQuestion: Nasal fractures:  is closed reduction satisfying?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that 65% of patients were satisfied with the results of closed reduction, indicating a majority experienced satisfaction. Although satisfaction was higher in mild fracture cases, overall, the procedure led to a positive outcome for most patients. Therefore, the most appropriate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 330, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 390}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.9429999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_285", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Celiac disease (CD) is believed to be a permanent intolerance to gluten. A number of patients, however, discontinue the gluten-free diet (GFD) without developing symptoms or signs. The aim of our study was to investigate whether CD patients are capable of developing tolerance to gluten.', 'All 77 adult patients from our hospital known to have biopsy-proven CD for more than 10 years were invited to participate. We investigated symptoms, gluten consumption, antibodies for CD and other autoimmunity, human leukocyte antigen (HLA)-typing, bone mineral density, and performed small bowel biopsies. Tolerance was defined as no immunological or histological signs of CD while consuming gluten.', 'Sixty-six patients accepted participation, but after review of the diagnostic biopsies 53 were found to have true CD. Twenty-three percent of patients had a gluten-containing diet, 15% admitted gluten transgression and 62% followed the GFD. Patients on a GFD had significantly more osteoporosis. Normal small bowel mucosa was found in four of eight on gluten-containing diet and in four of four with gluten transgression. Two patients were considered to have developed tolerance to gluten. One of them was HLA-DQ2/DQ8 negative.']\n\nQuestion: Gluten tolerance in adult patients with celiac disease 20 years after diagnosis?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that out of 53 patients with confirmed celiac disease, two were considered to have developed tolerance to gluten, as they showed no immunological or histological signs of disease while consuming gluten. One of these patients was even negative for the typical HLA-DQ2/DQ8 genetic markers, suggesting true tolerance. Therefore, while rare, gluten tolerance is possible in some adult patients with celiac disease after long-term follow-up.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 355, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 450}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.4705e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_286", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The US Preventive Services Task Force recommends against spirometry in the absence of symptoms. However, as much as 50% of COPD cases in the United States remain undiagnosed.', 'Report of symptoms, smoking history, and spirometric data were collected from subjects screened for a work-related medical evaluation (N = 3,955). Prevalence of airflow obstruction and respiratory symptoms were assessed. Sensitivity, specificity, positive and negative predictive values, and relative risks of predicting symptoms and smoking history for COPD were calculated.', 'Forty-four percent of smokers in our sample had airways obstruction (AO). Of these, 36% reported a diagnosis of or treatment for COPD. Odds ratio (95% CI) for AO with smoking (>or = 20 pack-years) was 3.73 (3.12- 4.45), 1.98 (1.73-2.27) for cough, 1.79 (1.55-2.08) for dyspnea, 1.95 (1.70-2.34) for sputum, and 2.59 (2.26-2.97) for wheeze. Respiratory symptoms were reported by 92% of smokers with AO, 86% smokers with restriction, 76% smokers with normal spirometry, and 73% of nonsmokers. Sensitivity (92% vs 90%), specificity (19% vs 22%), positive (47% vs 40%) and negative (75% vs 80%) predictive values for the presence of one or more symptoms were similar between smokers and all subjects.']\n\nQuestion: Do symptoms predict COPD in smokers?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The high sensitivity (92%) of symptoms for airflow obstruction (AO) in smokers suggests that most smokers with AO have symptoms, meaning symptoms are common in those with COPD. However, the low specificity (19%) and positive predictive value (47%) indicate that many smokers without COPD also have symptoms, so symptoms alone are not reliable for predicting COPD. Therefore, while symptoms are prevalent, they do not accurately discriminate COPD in smokers.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 459, "output_tokens": 97, "total_tokens": 556}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.2289e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_287", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"Web search engines are an important tool in communication and diffusion of knowledge. Among these, Google appears to be the most popular one: in August 2008, it accounted for 87% of all web searches in the UK, compared with Yahoo's 3.3%. Google's value as a diagnostic guide in general medicine was recently reported. The aim of this comparative cross-sectional study was to evaluate whether searching Google with disease-related terms was effective in the identification and diagnosis of complex immunological and allergic cases.\", 'Forty-five case reports were randomly selected by an independent observer from peer-reviewed medical journals. Clinical data were presented separately to three investigators, blinded to the final diagnoses. Investigator A was a Consultant with an expert knowledge in Internal Medicine and Allergy (IM&A) and basic computing skills. Investigator B was a Registrar in IM&A. Investigator C was a Research Nurse. Both Investigators B and C were familiar with computers and search engines. For every clinical case presented, each investigator independently carried out an Internet search using Google to provide a final diagnosis. Their results were then compared with the published diagnoses.', 'Correct diagnoses were provided in 30/45 (66%) cases, 39/45 (86%) cases, and in 29/45 (64%) cases by investigator A, B, and C, respectively. All of the three investigators achieved the correct diagnosis in 19 cases (42%), and all of them failed in two cases.']\n\nQuestion: Search engine as a diagnostic tool in difficult immunological and allergologic cases: is Google useful?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that Google was able to help clinicians and a nurse reach the correct diagnosis in a majority of complex immunological and allergic cases, with the expert clinician achieving the correct diagnosis in 66% of cases and the registrar in 86%. Even though accuracy varied among the investigators, the overall performance suggests Google can be a helpful diagnostic aid. Therefore, the evidence supports that Google is useful as a diagnostic tool in these cases.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 405, "output_tokens": 94, "total_tokens": 499}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.8155e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_288", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Various factors contribute to the effective implementation of evidence-based treatments (EBTs). In this study, cognitive processing therapy (CPT) was administered in a Veterans Affairs (VA) posttraumatic stress disorder (PTSD) specialty clinic in which training and supervision were provided following VA implementation guidelines. The aim was to (a) estimate the proportion of variability in outcome attributable to therapists and (b) identify characteristics of those therapists who produced better outcomes.', 'We used an archival database of veterans (n = 192) who completed 12 sessions of CPT by therapists (n = 25) who were trained by 2 nationally recognized trainers, 1 of whom also provided weekly group supervision. Multilevel modeling was used to estimate therapist effects, with therapists treated as a random factor. The supervisor was asked to retrospectively rate each therapist in terms of perceived effectiveness based on supervision interactions. Using single case study design, the supervisor was interviewed to determine what criteria she used to rate the therapists and emerging themes were coded.', 'When initial level of severity on the PTSD Checklist (PCL; McDonald&Calhoun, 2010; Weathers, Litz, Herman, Huska,&Keane, 1993) was taken into account, approximately 12% of the variability in the PCL at the end of treatment was due to therapists. The trainer, blind to the results, identified the following characteristics and actions of effective therapists: effectively addressing patient avoidance, language used in supervision, flexible interpersonal style, and ability to develop a strong therapeutic alliance.']\n\nQuestion: Uniformity of evidence-based treatments in practice?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context indicates that despite using a standardized evidence-based treatment (CPT), approximately 12% of the variability in patient outcomes was attributable to differences among therapists. This suggests that therapist characteristics and behaviors influenced treatment outcomes, indicating a lack of uniformity in practice. Therefore, the implementation of the evidence-based treatment was not fully uniform.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 409, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 482}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.6339e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_29", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Measurement of visceral adipose tissue (VAT) needs to be accurate and sensitive to change for risk monitoring. The purpose of this study is to determine the CT slice location where VAT area can best reflect changes in VAT volume and body weight.', '60 plain abdominal CT images from 30 males\\xa0[mean age (range) 51 (41-68) years, mean body weight (range) 71.1 (101.9-50.9) kg] who underwent workplace screenings twice within a 1-year interval were evaluated. Automatically calculated and manually corrected areas of the VAT of various scan levels using \"freeform curve\" region of interest on CT were recorded and compared with body weight changes.', 'The strongest correlations of VAT area with VAT volume and body weight changes were shown in a slice 3 cm above the lower margin of L3 with r values of 0.853 and 0.902, respectively.']\n\nQuestion: Visceral adipose tissue area measurement at a single level: can it represent visceral adipose tissue volume?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found strong correlations between visceral adipose tissue (VAT) area at a specific slice (3 cm above the lower margin of L3) and both VAT volume and body weight changes, with r values of 0.853 and 0.902, respectively. This high correlation suggests that a single-level measurement can reliably reflect changes in overall VAT volume. Therefore, the answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 301, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 389}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.0171e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_291", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Although dose-volume parameters in image-guided brachytherapy have become a standard, the use of posterior-inferior border of the pubic symphysis (PIBS) points has been recently proposed in the reporting of vaginal doses. The aim was to evaluate their pertinence.', 'Nineteen patients who received image-guided brachytherapy after concurrent radiochemotherapy were included. Per treatment, CT scans were performed at Days 2 and 3, with reporting of the initial dwell positions and times. Doses delivered to the PIBS points were evaluated on each plan, considering that they were representative of one-third of the treatment. The movements of the applicator according to the PIBS point were analysed.', 'Mean prescribed doses at PIBS -2, PIBS, PIBS +2 were, respectively, 2.23 \u00b1 1.4, 6.39 \u00b1 6.6, and 31.85 \u00b1 36.06 Gy. Significant differences were observed between the 5 patients with vaginal involvement and the remaining 14 at the level of PIBS +2 and PIBS: +47.60 Gy and +7.46 Gy, respectively (p = 0.023 and 0.03). The variations between delivered and prescribed doses at PIBS points were not significant. However, at International commission on radiation units and measurements rectovaginal point, the delivered dose was decreased by 1.43 \u00b1 2.49 Gy from the planned dose (p = 0.019). The delivered doses at the four points were strongly correlated with the prescribed doses with R(2) ranging from 0.93 to 0.95. The movements of the applicator in regard of the PIBS point assessed with the Digital Imaging and Communications in Medicine coordinates were insignificant.']\n\nQuestion: Vaginal dose assessment in image-guided brachytherapy for cervical cancer: Can we really rely on dose-point evaluation?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows strong correlation between prescribed and delivered doses at PIBS points (R\u00b2: 0.93\u20130.95) and insignificant applicator movement relative to PIBS, supporting their reliability. Although some dose differences were observed in patients with vaginal involvement, the overall dose-point evaluation remained consistent. Therefore, the evidence suggests that dose-point evaluation can be relied upon in this context.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 515, "output_tokens": 112, "total_tokens": 627}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.7765e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_292", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Stock et al. (Eur Respir J 25:47-53, 2005) recently estimated asthma prevalence in Germany using claims data on prescriptions and hospital diagnoses and found high prevalence peaks in infants. Our objective was to critically assess and discuss various aspects of identifying children with asthma using prescription data.', 'We replicated the selection procedure of Stock et al. using data on 290,919 children aged 0-17 years insured in the Gm\u00fcnder ErsatzKasse (GEK) in 2005. Asthma prevalence was also estimated in a sample of 17,641 children aged 0-17 years participating in the German Health Interview and Examination Survey for Children and Adolescents (KiGGS) from 2003 to 2006.', 'In children aged 0-4 years insured in the GEK, prevalences were found to range from 11.7 to 17.7% for boys and from 7.2 to 11.1% for girls when the criteria of Stock et al. were applied. A steady decline in prevalences was observed in older age groups. Asthma prevalence estimated in the KiGGS data showed a quite different distribution. In the age group 0-4 years, prevalences were found to range from 0 to 2.6% in boys and from 0 to 1.0% in girls; in children>4 years, prevalences were found to increase with increasing age.']\n\nQuestion: Prescriptions as a proxy for asthma in children: a good choice?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows a significant discrepancy between asthma prevalence estimated from prescription data (very high in infants) and that from a population-based health survey (low in infants, increasing with age), suggesting prescriptions overestimate asthma in young children. This likely reflects the use of asthma medications for other conditions like viral wheezing, not confirmed asthma. Therefore, prescriptions alone are not a reliable proxy for asthma diagnosis in children.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 414, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 500}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.7994e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_293", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Parental drinking has been shown to be associated with offspring drinking. However, the relationship appears to be more complex than often assumed and few studies have tracked it over longer time periods.', 'To explore the long-term (10-year) transmission of familial drinking during adolescence to offspring drinking patterns in young adulthood.', 'Swedish longitudinal study, assessing the relationship between familial drinking in 2000 and offspring drinking in 2010 using simultaneous quantile regression analysis (n=744).DATA: Data on familial drinking was gathered from the Swedish level-of-living surveys (LNU) and from partner LNU in 2000 while data on offspring drinking in young adulthood was gathered from LNU 2010. Drinking among offspring, parents and potential stepparents was measured through identical quantity-frequency indices referring to the past 12 months in 2010 and 2000 respectively.', 'Young adults whose families were abstainers in 2000 drank substantially less across quintiles in 2010 than offspring of non-abstaining families. The difference, however, was not statistically significant between quintiles of the conditional distribution. Actual drinking levels in drinking families were not at all or weakly associated with drinking in offspring. Supplementary analyses confirmed these patterns.']\n\nQuestion: Does the familial transmission of drinking patterns persist into young adulthood?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that while offspring of abstinent families drank less in young adulthood, the differences were not statistically significant across the distribution, and actual drinking levels in families were not consistently associated with offspring drinking. This suggests that familial drinking patterns during adolescence do not strongly predict drinking behavior in young adulthood. Therefore, the evidence does not support a persistent transmission.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 358, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 433}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.2918e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_294", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To investigate the effect of fenofibrate on sleep apnoea indices.', 'Proof-of-concept study comprising a placebo run-in period (1 week, 5 weeks if fibrate washout was required) and a 4-week randomized, double-blind treatment period. Thirty-four subjects (mean age 55 years, body mass index 34 kg/m 2 , fasting triglycerides 3.5 mmol/L) with diagnosed sleep apnoea syndrome not treated with continuous positive airways pressure were enrolled and randomized to once daily treatment with fenofibrate (145 mg NanoCrystal(R) tablet) or placebo. Overnight polysomnography, computerized attention/vigilance tests and blood sampling for measurement of lipids, insulin, fasting plasma glucose and fibrinogen were performed at the end of each study period.', 'NCT00816829.', 'As this was an exploratory study, a range of sleep variables were evaluated. The apnoea/hypopnoea index (AHI) and percentage of time spent with arterial oxygen saturation (SpO(2))<90% were relevant as they have been evaluated in other clinical trials. Other variables included total apnoeas, hypopnoeas and oxygen desaturations, and non-cortical micro-awakenings related to respiratory events per hour.', 'Fenofibrate treatment significantly reduced the percentage of time with SpO(2)<90% (from 9.0% to 3.5% vs. 10.0% to 11.5% with placebo, p = 0.007), although there was no significant change in the AHI (reduction vs. control 14% (95%CI -47 to 40%, p = 0.533). Treatment reduced obstructive apnoeas (by 44%, from 18.5 at baseline to 15.0 at end of treatment vs. 29.0 to 30.5 on placebo, p = 0.048), and non-cortical micro-awakenings per hour (from 23.5 to 18.0 vs. 24.0 to 25.0 with placebo, p = 0.004). Other sleep variables were not significantly influenced by fenofibrate.', 'Exploratory study in patients with mild to moderate sleep apnoea, limited treatment duration; concomitant hypnotic treatment (35%); lack of correction for multiplicity of testing.']\n\nQuestion: Proof of concept study: does fenofibrate have a role in sleep apnoea syndrome?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that fenofibrate significantly reduced the percentage of time with SpO\u2082 <90% and obstructive apnoeas, along with non-cortical micro-awakenings, suggesting a beneficial effect on some sleep apnoea-related parameters. However, the lack of significant change in the apnoea/hypopnoea index (AHI), the primary marker for sleep apnoea severity, and the study\u2019s limitations (short duration, no multiplicity correction) prevent definitive conclusions. Therefore, while results are promising, they are not conclusive.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 641, "output_tokens": 121, "total_tokens": 762}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 5.7610999999999994e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_295", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To determine the potential prognostic value of using functional magnetic resonance imaging (fMRI) to identify patients with disorders of consciousness, who show potential for recovery.', 'Observational study.', 'Unit for acute rehabilitation care.', 'Patients (N=22) in a vegetative state (VS; n=10) and minimally conscious state (MCS; n=12) during the first 200 days after the initial incident.', 'Not applicable.', 'Further course on the Coma Recovery Scale-Revised.', 'Participants performed a mental imagery fMRI paradigm. They were asked to alternately imagine playing tennis and navigating through their home. In 14 of the 22 examined patients (VS, n=5; MCS, n=9), a significant activation of the regions of interest (ROIs) of the mental imagery paradigm could be found. All 5 patients with activation of a significant blood oxygen level dependent signal, who were in a VS at the time of the fMRI examination, reached at least an MCS at the end of the observation period. In contrast, 5 participants in a VS who failed to show activation in ROIs, did not (sensitivity 100%, specificity 100%). Six of 9 patients in an MCS with activation in ROIs emerged from an MCS. Of 3 patients in an MCS who did not show activation, 2 patients stayed in an MCS and 1 patient emerged from the MCS (sensitivity 85%, specificity 40%).']\n\nQuestion: Can mental imagery functional magnetic resonance imaging predict recovery in patients with disorders of consciousness?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The fMRI mental imagery paradigm showed a strong association with recovery outcomes: all patients in a vegetative state who exhibited brain activation reached at least a minimally conscious state, while those without activation did not improve. This indicates high sensitivity and specificity in predicting recovery for VS patients. Although results were less specific for MCS patients, the overall evidence supports predictive value.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 406, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 482}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.642599999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_30", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The accepted treatment protocol for necrotizing fasciitis (NF) consists of extensive surgery and wide spectrum antibiotics. Hyperbaric oxygenation (HBO) has been recommended as adjuvant therapy for NF, improving patient mortality and outcome. However, the beneficial effect of HBO for NF remains controversial.', 'A retrospective evaluation of treatment outcome in 37 patients treated for NF between 1984 and 1993 was carried out. The mortality rate, morbidity criteria, and risk factors for grave prognosis were compared between a group of 25 patients who received HBO as part of their treatment protocol and a group of the remaining 12 patients treated by surgical excision and antibiotics alone.', \"The two groups were found to be similar with regard to age, gender, the incidence of individual risk factors for ominous prognosis, and the Acute Physiology and Chronic Health Evaluation (APACHE) II score for disease's severity on presentation. The mortality rate among the HBO-treated patients was 36%, as opposed to 25% in the non-HBO group. The mean number of surgical d\u00e9bridements required per patient was significantly higher in the HBO group: 3.3 compared with 1.5 in the non-HBO-treated patients. Although the average length of hospitalization for survivors was shorter for the HBO group, the difference between the groups did not reach statistical significance.\"]\n\nQuestion: Necrotizing fasciitis: an indication for hyperbaric oxygenation therapy?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found a higher mortality rate (36% vs. 25%) and a significantly greater number of surgical debridements in the HBO group compared to the non-HBO group, despite similar baseline characteristics. These results do not support a beneficial effect of hyperbaric oxygen therapy in necrotizing fasciitis. Therefore, the evidence from this study does not justify a definitive \"yes\" or even a strong \"maybe\" for HBO use.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 378, "output_tokens": 98, "total_tokens": 476}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.6638e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_301", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To illustrate how maternal mortality audit identifies different causes of and contributing factors to maternal deaths in different settings in low- and high-income countries and how this can lead to local solutions in reducing maternal deaths.', 'Descriptive study of maternal mortality from different settings and review of data on the history of reducing maternal mortality in what are now high-income countries.', 'Kalabo district in Zambia, Farafenni division in The Gambia, Onandjokwe district in Namibia, and the Netherlands.', 'Population of rural areas in Zambia and The Gambia, peri-urban population in Namibia and nationwide data from The Netherlands.', 'Data from facility-based maternal mortality audits from three African hospitals and data from the latest confidential enquiry in The Netherlands.', 'Maternal mortality ratio (MMR), causes (direct and indirect) and characteristics.', 'MMR ranged from 10 per 100,000 (the Netherlands) to 1540 per 100,000 (The Gambia). Differences in causes of deaths were characterized by HIV/AIDS in Namibia, sepsis and HIV/AIDS in Zambia, (pre-)eclampsia in the Netherlands and obstructed labour in The Gambia.']\n\nQuestion: The use of audit to identify maternal mortality in different settings: is it just a difference between the rich and the poor?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}\n\nNo, the differences in maternal mortality causes are not just about wealth but also reflect varying health system challenges, disease prevalence, and access to care. Audits reveal context-specific factors like HIV/AIDS in Namibia or obstructed labor in The Gambia, which require tailored solutions. While income level plays a role, the root causes and contributing factors differ significantly across settings.", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 351, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 429}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.2721e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_302", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The effect of neoadjuvant chemotherapy (NACT) on topographical distribution patterns of lymph node metastasis in cervical cancer was unknown.', 'Patients with FIGO stage IB1-IIB who underwent radical surgery with or without NACT were enrolled (3527 patients). A matched-case comparison design was used to compare the effects of NACT on lymph node metastasis.', 'We analyzed groups of 167 and 140 patients who were diagnosed with lymph node metastasis in the matched primary surgery group and NACT group, respectively, and no significant difference was observed (p = 0.081). The incidence of lymph node metastasis was significantly decreased in the NACT-responsive group compared to the non-responsive group (18.4% vs. 38.6%, P<0.001). The metastatic rates for every lymph node group also declined in the NACT-responsive group except for the deep inguinal and the para-aortic lymph node groups. Clinical response, deep stromal, parametrial and lymph vascular invasions were independent risk factors for lymph node metastasis in the NACT group. Furthermore, deep stromal invasion and lymph vascular invasion, but not the response to NACT, were independently associated with upper LNM. The number of lymph nodes involved, response to NACT, tumor histology and a positive vaginal margin were independent prognostic factors affecting DFS or OS rates in node-positive patients treated with NACT plus radical surgery.']\n\nQuestion: Could the extent of lymphadenectomy be modified by neoadjuvant chemotherapy in cervical cancer?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant difference in overall lymph node metastasis between the primary surgery and NACT groups, but the NACT-responsive group had significantly lower metastasis rates, except in deep inguinal and para-aortic nodes. This suggests that NACT may alter the pattern and burden of metastasis, potentially allowing for a modified extent of lymphadenectomy in responders. Therefore, the extent of lymphadenectomy could be influenced by NACT response.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 404, "output_tokens": 96, "total_tokens": 500}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.8284e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_303", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Blood stream infection (BSI) and the subsequent development of sepsis are among the most common infection complications occurring in severe burn patients. This study was designed to evaluate the relationship between the burn wound flora and BSI pathogens.', 'Documentation of all bacterial and fungal wound and blood isolates from severe burn patients hospitalized in the burn unit and intensive care unit was obtained from medical records retrieved retrospectively from a computerized, hospital-wide database over a 13-year period. All data were recorded in relation to the Ryan score.', 'Of 195 severe burn patients, 88 had at least 1 BSI episode. Transmission of the same pathogen from wound to blood was documented in 30% of the patients, with a rising BSI frequency as the Ryan score increased. There were a total of 263 bacteremic episodes in 88 study patients, 44% of blood isolates were documented previously in wound cultures, and transmission of the same pathogen from wound to blood was noted in 65% of bacteremic patients.']\n\nQuestion: Do Wound Cultures Give Information About the Microbiology of Blood Cultures in Severe Burn Patients?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that 44% of blood isolates were previously documented in wound cultures, and 65% of bacteremic patients had evidence of the same pathogen transmitted from wound to blood. This indicates a significant overlap between wound and blood pathogens, suggesting wound cultures can provide useful information about potential bloodstream infections. Therefore, wound cultures do give information about the microbiology of blood cultures in severe burn patients.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 317, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 406}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.1407e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_304", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Longitudinal cohort studies in sub-Saharan Africa are urgently needed to understand cardiovascular disease development. We, therefore, explored health behaviours and conventional risk factors of African individuals with optimal blood pressure (BP) (\u2264 120/80 mm Hg), and their 5-year prediction for the development of hypertension.', 'The Prospective Urban Rural Epidemiology study in the North West Province, South Africa, started in 2005 and included African volunteers (n = 1994; aged>30 years) from a sample of 6000 randomly selected households in rural and urban areas.', 'At baseline, 48% of the participants were hypertensive (\u2265 140/90 mmHg). Those with optimal BP (n = 478) were followed at a success rate of 70% for 5 years (213 normotensive, 68 hypertensive, 57 deceased). Africans that became hypertensive smoked more than the normotensive individuals (68.2% vs 49.8%), and they also had a greater waist circumference [ratio of geometric means of 0.94 cm (95% CI: 0.86-0.99)] and greater amount of \u03b3-glutamyltransferase [0.74 U/l (95% CI: 0.62-0.88)]at baseline. The 5-year change in BP was independently explained by baseline \u03b3-glutamyltransferase [R(2) = 0.23, \u03b2 = 0.13 U/l (95% CI: 0.01-0.19)]. Alcohol intake also predicted central systolic BP and carotid cross-sectional wall area (CSWA) at follow-up. Waist circumference was another predictor of BP changes [\u03b2 = 0.18 cm (95% CI: 0.05-0.24)]and CSWA. HIV infection was inversely associated with increased BP.']\n\nQuestion: Are behavioural risk factors to be blamed for the conversion from optimal blood pressure to hypertensive status in Black South Africans?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data show that individuals who developed hypertension were more likely to smoke, have higher alcohol intake, and greater waist circumference\u2014behavioral risk factors linked to blood pressure changes. Additionally, alcohol and waist circumference independently predicted increases in blood pressure and vascular changes over 5 years. Therefore, behavioral risk factors appear to play a significant role in the conversion from optimal blood pressure to hypertension.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 530, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 611}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.573e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_305", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The gap between evidence-based treatments and routine care has been well established. Findings from the Sequenced Treatments Alternatives to Relieve Depression (STAR*D) emphasized the importance of measurement-based care for the treatment of depression as a key ingredient for achieving response and remission; yet measurement-based care approaches are not commonly used in clinical practice.', 'The Nine-Item Patient Health Questionnaire (PHQ-9) for monitoring depression severity was introduced in 19 diverse psychiatric practices. During the one-year course of the project the helpfulness and feasibility of implementation of PHQ-9 in these psychiatric practices were studied. The project was modeled after the Institute for Healthcare Improvement Breakthrough Series. Two of the 19 practices dropped out during the course of the project.', 'By the conclusion of the study, all remaining 17 practices had adopted PHQ-9 as a routine part of depression care in their practice. On the basis of responses from 17 psychiatrists from those practices, PHQ-9 scores influenced clinical decision making for 93% of 6,096 patient contacts. With the additional information gained from the PHQ-9 score, one or more treatment changes occurred during 40% of these clinical contacts. Changing the dosage of antidepressant medication and adding another medication were the most common treatment changes recorded by psychiatrists, followed by starting or increasing psychotherapy and by switching or initiating antidepressants. In 3% of the patient contacts, using the PHQ-9 led to additional suicide risk assessment.']\n\nQuestion: Systematic use of patient-rated depression severity monitoring: is it helpful and feasible in clinical psychiatry?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context indicates that 17 out of 19 psychiatric practices successfully adopted the PHQ-9 as a routine part of depression care, and the majority of clinicians reported that PHQ-9 scores influenced clinical decisions in 93% of patient contacts. Treatment changes were made in 40% of contacts based on the PHQ-9, demonstrating both feasibility and clinical impact. Therefore, the systematic use of patient-rated depression monitoring is both helpful and feasible.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 410, "output_tokens": 100, "total_tokens": 510}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.9109999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_307", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To study the relationship between lunar position and the day of delivery; to investigate the synodic distribution of spontaneous deliveries, especially in relation to the presence of a full moon.', 'Retrospective analysis of 1248 spontaneous full-term deliveries in three-year period (36 lunar months), setted at Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology, Civil Hospital, Fano (Marche, Italy), using circular statistics techniques.', 'A connection between the distribution of spontaneous full-term deliveries and the lunar month was found. The effect of the phases of the moon seems to be particularly relevant in multiparae and plurigravidae; in these cases, the mean day of delivery corresponds to the first or second day after the full moon.']\n\nQuestion: Does lunar position influence the time of delivery?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found a connection between the distribution of spontaneous full-term deliveries and the lunar month, particularly noting that deliveries in multiparae and plurigravidae tended to occur on the first or second day after the full moon. This suggests a statistically relevant relationship between lunar position and timing of delivery. Therefore, the evidence supports a positive association.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 238, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 312}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.4298e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_31", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To assess if the Hawkins sign can predict whether or not astragalus fractures of the neck will develop avascular necrosis. It is also assessed whether the occurrence of this complication is related to the displacement of the fracture, soft tissue injury, or delay in the reduction or surgery. The results were compared with those found in the literature.', 'A retrospective study was conducted on 23 talar neck fractures recorded over a a period of thirteen years. The following variables were analysed: displacement of the fracture, soft tissue injury, delay and type of treatment, complications, observation of the Hawkins sign, and functional outcome.', 'There were 7 type I Hawkins fractures, 11 type II, and 4 type III and 1 type IV. Four cases developed avascular necrosis (2 Hawkins type II and 2 type III). Hawkins sign was observed in 12 cases, of which none developed necrosis. Four cases with negative Hawkins sign developed necrosis. No statistically significant differences were found when comparing the development of avascular necrosis with the displacement of the fracture, soft tissue injury, or delay in treatment. Differences were found when comparing the development of avascular necrosis with the Hawkins sign (P=.03).']\n\nQuestion: Is the Hawkins sign able to predict necrosis in fractures of the neck of the astragalus?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Hawkins sign was associated with a lower risk of avascular necrosis, as none of the 12 cases with a positive sign developed necrosis, while all four cases with necrosis had a negative sign. A statistically significant difference was found between the presence of the Hawkins sign and the development of necrosis (P = .03). Therefore, the Hawkins sign can predict the absence of necrosis.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 346, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 434}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.3366e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_311", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Controlled ovarian stimulation (COS) with intrauterine insemination (IUI) is a common treatment in couples with unexplained non-conception. Induction of multifollicular growth is considered to improve pregnancy outcome, but it contains an increased risk of multiple pregnancies and ovarian hyperstimulation syndrome. In this study the impact of the number of follicles (>14 mm) on the ongoing pregnancy rate (PR) and multiple PR was evaluated in the first four treatment cycles.', 'A retrospective cohort study was performed in all couples with unexplained non-conception undergoing COS-IUI in the Academic Hospital of Maastricht. The main outcome measure was ongoing PR. Secondary outcomes were ongoing multiple PR, number of follicles of>or=14 mm, and order of treatment cycle.', 'Three hundred couples were included. No significant difference was found in ongoing PR between women with one, two, three or four follicles respectively (P=0.54), but in women with two or more follicles 12/73 pregnancies were multiples. Ongoing PR was highest in the first treatment cycle and declined significantly with increasing cycle order (P=0.006), while multiple PR did not change.']\n\nQuestion: Is controlled ovarian stimulation in intrauterine insemination an acceptable therapy in couples with unexplained non-conception in the perspective of multiple pregnancies?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The provided study context shows no significant gain in ongoing pregnancy rate from multifollicular growth (\u22652 follicles >14 mm), yet 12 of 73 such pregnancies were multiples. This directly indicates that the elevated multiple-pregnancy risk is not offset by any therapeutic benefit, rendering COS-IUI unacceptable on that basis alone. Therefore the answer is no.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 451, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 527}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00075375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_313", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Digital tomosynthesis (DT) is a new X-ray-based imaging technique that allows image enhancement with minimal increase in radiation exposure. The purpose of this study was to compare DT with noncontrast computed tomography (NCCT) and to evaluate its potential role for the follow-up of patients with nephrolithiasis in a nonemergent setting.', 'A retrospective review of patients with nephrolithiasis at our institution that underwent NCCT and DT from July 2012 to September 2013 was performed. Renal units (RUs) that did not undergo treatment or stone passage were randomly assigned to two blinded readers, who recorded stone count, size area (mm(2)), maximum stone length (mm), and location, for both DT and NCCT. Mean differences per RU were compared. Potential variables affecting stone detection rate, including stone size and body mass index (BMI), were evaluated. Interobserver agreement was determined using the intraclass correlation coefficient to measure the consistency of measurements made by the readers.', 'DT and NCCT demonstrated similar stone detection rates in terms of stone counts and stone area mm(2). Of the 79 RUs assessed, 41 RUs showed exact stone counts on DT and NCCT. The mean difference in stone area was 16.5\\u2009mm(2) (-4.6 to 38.5), p\\u2009=\\u20090.121. The mean size of the largest stone on NCCT and DT was 9.27 and 8.87\\u2009mm, respectively. Stone size and BMI did not cause a significant difference in stone detection rates. Interobserver agreement showed a strong correlation between readers and adequate reproducibility.']\n\nQuestion: Digital Tomosynthesis: A Viable Alternative to Noncontrast Computed Tomography for the Follow-Up of Nephrolithiasis?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on the study results, digital tomosynthesis (DT) showed similar stone detection rates compared to noncontrast computed tomography (NCCT), with no significant differences in stone count, area, or largest stone size. The high interobserver agreement and lack of significant impact from variables like stone size and BMI support its reliability. Therefore, DT appears to be a viable alternative for follow-up imaging in nephrolithiasis.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 474, "output_tokens": 90, "total_tokens": 564}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.2653999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_314", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Since insulin therapy might have an atherogenic effect, we studied the relationship between cumulative insulin dose and atherosclerosis in type 1 diabetes. We have focused on patients with type 1 diabetes instead of type 2 diabetes to minimise the effect of insulin resistance as a potential confounder.', 'An observational study was performed in 215 subjects with type 1 diabetes treated with multiple insulin injection therapy. Atherosclerosis was assessed by measurement of carotid intima-media thickness (CIMT).', 'The cumulative dose of regular insulin showed a positive and significant relation with CIMT: increase of 21 microm in CIMT per S.D. of insulin use (95% CI: 8-35 adjusted for gender and age), which remained unchanged after adjustment for duration of diabetes, HbA1c, BMI, pulse pressure, physical activity and carotid lumen diameter. A similar relation was found for intermediate-acting insulin: 15.5 microm per S.D. (2-29), which was no longer present after further adjustment.']\n\nQuestion: High cumulative insulin exposure: a risk factor of atherosclerosis in type 1 diabetes?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found a significant positive association between cumulative dose of regular insulin and carotid intima-media thickness (CIMT), a marker of atherosclerosis, which persisted after adjusting for multiple confounders. Although the association for intermediate-acting insulin was no longer significant after full adjustment, the consistent trend supports a potential risk. Therefore, the evidence suggests that high cumulative insulin exposure is associated with increased atherosclerosis in type 1 diabetes.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 318, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 413}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.2078e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_317", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The aim of this study was to prospectively compare the diagnostic performance of magnetic resonance imaging (MRI), multidetector computed tomography (MDCT) and endoscopic ultrasonography (EUS) in the preoperative locoregional staging of gastric cancer.', 'This study had Institutional Review Board approval, and informed consent was obtained from all patients. Fifty-two patients with biopsy-proven gastric cancer underwent preoperative 1.5-T MRI, 64-channel MDCT and EUS. All images were analysed blind, and the results were compared with histopathological findings according to the seventh edition of the TNM classification. After the population had been divided on the basis of the local invasion (T1-3 vs T4a-b) and nodal involvement (N0 vs N+), sensitivity, specificity, positive and negative predictive value, and accuracy were calculated and diagnostic performance measures were assessed using the McNemar test.', 'For T staging, EUS showed higher sensitivity (94%) than MDCT and MRI (65 and 76%; p = 0.02 and p = 0.08). MDCT and MRI had significantly higher specificity (91 and 89%) than EUS (60%) (p = 0.0009 and p = 0.003). Adding MRI to MDCT or EUS did not result in significant differences for sensitivity. For N staging, EUS showed higher sensitivity (92%) than MRI and MDCT (69 and 73%; p = 0.01 and p = 0.02). MDCT showed better specificity (81%) than EUS and MRI (58 and 73%; p = 0.03 and p = 0.15).']\n\nQuestion: Preoperative locoregional staging of gastric cancer: is there a place for magnetic resonance imaging?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on the study results, MRI showed moderate sensitivity and high specificity for T staging, but adding MRI to MDCT or EUS did not significantly improve sensitivity. While MRI performs reasonably well, it does not outperform EUS or MDCT and adds no significant diagnostic benefit when combined. Therefore, the evidence suggests a limited independent role for MRI in routine preoperative staging.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 470, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 549}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.1269999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_318", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The present study investigated factors that explain when and why different groups of teammates are more likely to request and accept backup from one another when needed in an environment characterized by extreme time pressure and severe consequences of error: commercial air traffic control (ATC).', 'Transactive memory theory states that teammates develop consensus regarding the distribution of their relative expertise as well as confidence in that expertise over time and that this facilitates coordination processes. The present study investigated whether this theory could help to explain between-team differences in requesting and accepting backup when needed.', 'The present study used cross-sectional data collected from 51 commercial ATC teams. Hypotheses were tested using multiple regression analysis.', 'Teammates with greater experience working together requested and accepted backup from one another more than those with lesser experience working together. Teammate knowledge consensus and perceived team efficacy appear to have mediated this relationship.']\n\nQuestion: Do familiar teammates request and accept more backup?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Familiar teammates, defined as those with greater experience working together, were found to request and accept backup more often. This effect was mediated by teammate knowledge consensus and perceived team efficacy. Therefore, the evidence supports that familiar teammates do request and accept more backup.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 260, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 316}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.406e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_319", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"To assess the results of transsphenoidal pituitary surgery in patients with Cushing's disease over a period of 18 years, and to determine if there are factors which will predict the outcome.\", 'Sixty-nine sequential patients treated surgically by a single surgeon in Newcastle upon Tyne between 1980 and 1997 were identified and data from 61 of these have been analysed.', 'Retrospective analysis of outcome measures.', \"Patients were divided into three groups (remission, failure and relapse) depending on the late outcome of their treatment as determined at the time of analysis, i.e. 88 months (median) years after surgery. Remission is defined as biochemical reversal of hypercortisolism with re-emergence of diurnal circadian rhythm, resolution of clinical features and adequate suppression on low-dose dexamethasone testing. Failure is defined as the absence of any of these features. Relapse is defined as the re-emergence of Cushing's disease more than one year after operation. Clinical features such as weight, sex, hypertension, associated endocrine disorders and smoking, biochemical studies including preoperative and postoperative serum cortisol, urine free cortisol, serum ACTH, radiological, histological and surgical findings were assessed in relation to these three groups to determine whether any factors could reliably predict failure or relapse after treatment.\", 'Of the 61 patients included in this study, 48 (78.7%) achieved initial remission and 13 (21.3%) failed treatment. Seven patients suffered subsequent relapse (range 22-158 months) in their condition after apparent remission, leaving a final group of 41 patients (67.2%) in the remission group. Tumour was identified at surgery in 52 patients, of whom 38 achieved remission. In comparison, only 3 of 9 patients in whom no tumour was identified achieved remission. This difference was significant (P = 0.048). When both radiological and histological findings were positive, the likelihood of achieving remission was significantly higher than if both modalities were negative (P = 0.038). There were significant differences between remission and failure groups when 2- and 6-week postoperative serum cortisol levels (P = 0.002 and 0.001, respectively) and 6-week postoperative urine free cortisol levels (P = 0.026) were compared. This allowed identification of patients who failed surgical treatment in the early postoperative period. Complications of surgery included transitory DI in 13, transitory CSF leak in 8 and transitory nasal discharge and cacosmia in 3. Twelve of 41 patients required some form of hormonal replacement therapy despite achieving long-term remission. Thirteen patients underwent a second operation, of whom 5 achieved remission.']\n\nQuestion: Transsphenoidal pituitary surgery in Cushing's disease: can we predict outcome?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study identifies several factors that significantly predict surgical outcomes, such as the intraoperative identification of a tumor, concordant positive radiological and histological findings, and early postoperative cortisol and urine free cortisol levels. These factors were statistically associated with remission, failure, or relapse, allowing for early prediction of treatment failure. Therefore, outcome can be predicted to a meaningful extent based on these variables.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 711, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 797}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 5.9081e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_322", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Ambulatory 24-h dual-channel pharyngeal and oesophageal pH monitoring is the standard test for measuring gastro-oesophageal and gastropharyngeal reflux. Artefacts caused by the intake of food may result in falsely positive gastropharyngeal reflux, which necessitates a manual review of 24-h pH data. The purpose of the study was to investigate the influence of meals and whether leaving out meals affected the reliability of the test.', 'Patients referred for otolaryngological complaints, suspected to have been caused by gastro-oesophageal reflux, underwent 24-h dual-channel pH monitoring. The raw unprocessed pH data were corrected by visual inspection of the 24-h tracings (corrected data), by leaving out meals or meals plus a 2-h postprandrial period.', 'The raw pH data were substantially influenced by artefacts of food intake and pseudoreflux. Data obtained by leaving out meals agreed best with manually corrected data. Many of the falsely positive reflux episodes could be removed, thereby inducing a 9%-18% chance of undetected reflux. When examining the fraction of time supine, manually corrected data and data leaving out meals were fully concordant and detected 79% of patients with gastropharyngeal reflux. However, leaving out meals plus a 2-h postprandrial period resulted in 21%-50% falsely negative tests.']\n\nQuestion: Artefacts in 24-h pharyngeal and oesophageal pH monitoring: is simplification of pH data analysis feasible?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that removing meal periods from the pH data analysis significantly reduced artefacts caused by food intake and closely agreed with manually corrected data, especially when assessing gastropharyngeal reflux in the supine position. Although some reflux episodes were missed (9%-18%), the method remained largely reliable, whereas extending exclusions to include a 2-hour postprandial period led to unacceptably high false-negative rates. Therefore, simplification by excluding meals alone is feasible.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 403, "output_tokens": 102, "total_tokens": 505}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.8812999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_323", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The aim of this study was to analyze the properties of the immune cell microenvironment of regional lymph nodes (LNs) positive for lung cancer.', 'Twenty-four patients operated on for stages T1 and T2 of the NSCLC, were enrolled in the study. Peripheral blood and LN tissue were obtained from different lymph node sites and levels. As a control, LN tissue was taken from patients diagnosed with emphysema or pneumothorax. The cells from randomly chosen LN were tested by multi-color flow cytometry. Separate portions of LN were snap-frozen and examined for the presence of cytokeratin positive cells (CK). Propensity for apoptosis, level of TCR zeta chain expression of T cells and the number and maturation status of dendritic cells were confronted with the presence of CK-positive cells.', 'The presence of metastases correlated with the downregulation of TCR zeta, especially CD8(+) T cells. The most striking feature was the reduction in the number of myeloid CD11c(+) dendritic cells in the LN of patients with LN metastases. This could be a reflection of the immunodeficient state observed in lung cancer patients. Even in the absence of metastases in the regional LN, the same type of changes in the LN microenvironment were observed in those LN located nearer the primary tumor.']\n\nQuestion: Can the condition of the cell microenvironment of mediastinal lymph nodes help predict the risk of metastases in non-small cell lung cancer?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that changes in the lymph node microenvironment, such as reduced TCR zeta expression and fewer myeloid dendritic cells, were present even in non-metastatic lymph nodes near the tumor. These alterations suggest an immunosuppressive environment that correlates with the presence of metastases. Therefore, the condition of the cell microenvironment may serve as an early indicator of metastatic risk.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 380, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 467}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.568e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_324", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The authors examined equivalence of wandering and physically nonaggressive agitation (PNA) as concepts.', 'A cross-sectional correlational design was used.', 'Participants were recruited from 22 nursing homes and 6 assisted living facilities in two states.', 'Ambulatory residents meeting DSM-IV criteria for dementia (N = 181) were studied.', 'Video-tapes for up to twelve 20-minute observations per participant were coded for wandering using an empirically derived taxonomy of ambulation patterns. Separate raters coded the same tapes for six PNA behaviors on the agitation behavior mapping instrument.', 'Most participants (73.5%) wandered; all showed PNA behaviors. Factor analyses yielded an one-factor solution for wandering (explained variance = 43.66%) and a two-factor solution for PNA (explained variance = 53.45%). Overall wandering correlated significantly with PNA Factor 1 (df =179, r = 0.68, p<0.001) and Factor 2, but at a lower value (df = 179, r = 0.26, p<0.01).']\n\nQuestion: Are wandering and physically nonaggressive agitation equivalent?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The factor analyses revealed different underlying structures for wandering (one factor) and physically nonaggressive agitation (two factors), suggesting they are not the same construct. Although wandering correlated significantly with both PNA factors, the moderate correlation (r = 0.68) and distinct factor structures indicate they are related but not equivalent. Therefore, the evidence does not support equivalence.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 330, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 410}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.1429999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_327", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"The 'law of spatiotemporal concentrations of events' introduced major preventative shifts in policing communities. 'Hotspots' are at the forefront of these developments yet somewhat understudied in emergency medicine. Furthermore, little is known about interagency 'data-crossover', despite some developments through the Cardiff Model. Can police-ED interagency data-sharing be used to reduce community-violence using a hotspots methodology?\", \"12-month (2012) descriptive study and analysis of spatiotemporal clusters of police and emergency calls for service using hotspots methodology and assessing the degree of incident overlap. 3775 violent crime incidents and 775 assault incidents analysed using spatiotemporal clustering with k-means++ algorithm and Spearman's rho.\", \"Spatiotemporal location of calls for services to the police and the ambulance service are equally highly concentrated in a small number of geographical areas, primarily within intra-agency hotspots (33% and 53%, respectively) but across agencies' hotspots as well (25% and 15%, respectively). Datasets are statistically correlated with one another at the 0.57 and 0.34 levels, with 50% overlap when adjusted for the number of hotspots. At least one in every two police hotspots does not have an ambulance hotspot overlapping with it, suggesting half of assault spatiotemporal concentrations are unknown to the police. Data further suggest that more severely injured patients, as estimated by transfer to hospital, tend to be injured in the places with the highest number of police-recorded crimes.\"]\n\nQuestion: Can routinely collected ambulance data about assaults contribute to reduction in community violence?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data show a significant spatiotemporal overlap between ambulance and police records, with ambulance data revealing assault concentrations not captured by police, indicating added value in identifying hidden hotspots. The correlation between datasets and the finding that severely injured patients are often in high-crime areas suggest ambulance data can inform targeted interventions. Therefore, routinely collected ambulance data can contribute to reducing community violence.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 423, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 504}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.8132999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_328", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To estimate changes in uterine myoma volume during pregnancy.', 'Review of departmental electronic perinatal database and medical records. Canadian Task Force Classification II-3.', 'Obstetrical ultrasound unit in an academic tertiary care center.', 'One hundred-seven patients diagnosed with uterine myomas during pregnancy and who had two or more obstetrical ultrasounds in different periods of pregnancy.', 'We analyzed the change in volume of uterine myomas between the first half of pregnancy (up until 19 weeks), third quarter (20-30 weeks), and last quarter (31 weeks to term). The volume of largest uterine myoma was calculated using the formula Volume (mm3)=Pi/6x(length mm)x(width mm)x(height mm).', 'The mean age of the population was 31+/-6 years. Between the first and the second study periods, the percentage of uterine myomas that decreased in size was 55.1% (95% CI: 43-66), with a mean decrease in volume of 35%+/-4%; while the percentage of uterine myomas that enlarged was 44.9% (95% CI: 34-56), with a mean increase in volume of 69%+/-11%. Between the second and the third study periods, 75% (95% CI: 56-87) became smaller, with a mean decrease in volume of 30%+/-3%; while 25% (95% CI: 13-43) enlarged, with a mean increase in volume of 102%+/-62%.']\n\nQuestion: Volume change of uterine myomas during pregnancy: do myomas really grow?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data show that while some myomas grew (44.9% in the first half, 25% in the second half), a greater percentage decreased in size (55.1% initially, 75% later), with notable mean volume reductions. Although growth occurred in a subset, the overall trend indicates that myomas are more likely to decrease in size during pregnancy, especially in the third trimester. Therefore, the answer is: \\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 425, "output_tokens": 101, "total_tokens": 526}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.0274999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_332", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To report three cases illustrating that it is not unusual for a primary eyelid tumour to metastasise to the parotid gland and vice versa.', 'Two patients with malignant parotid tumours underwent radical parotidectomy and presented subsequently with eyelid lesions. Biopsy showed that both eyelid lesions were histologically similar to the primary parotid tumour. A third patient was noted to have ipsilateral upper eyelid and parotid gland tumours. Histology and immunocytochemistry were used to differentiate the primary tumour and the metastasis.']\n\nQuestion: Eyelid-parotid metastasis: do we screen for coexisting masses?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context describes cases where tumors metastasized between the eyelid and parotid gland, indicating a clinical link. This suggests that when a tumor is found in one location, there is a risk of metastasis to or from the other site. Therefore, screening for coexisting masses is warranted.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 211, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 277}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.1581e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_334", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['A growing body of research emphasizes the importance of contextual factors on health outcomes. Using postcode sector data for Scotland (UK), this study tests the hypothesis of spatial heterogeneity in the relationship between area-level deprivation and mortality to determine if contextual differences in the West vs. the rest of Scotland influence this relationship. Research into health inequalities frequently fails to recognise spatial heterogeneity in the deprivation-health relationship, assuming that global relationships apply uniformly across geographical areas. In this study, exploratory spatial data analysis methods are used to assess local patterns in deprivation and mortality. Spatial regression models are then implemented to examine the relationship between deprivation and mortality more formally.', 'The initial exploratory spatial data analysis reveals concentrations of high standardized mortality ratios (SMR) and deprivation (hotspots) in the West of Scotland and concentrations of low values (coldspots) for both variables in the rest of the country. The main spatial regression result is that deprivation is the only variable that is highly significantly correlated with all-cause mortality in all models. However, in contrast to the expected spatial heterogeneity in the deprivation-mortality relationship, this relation does not vary between regions in any of the models. This result is robust to a number of specifications, including weighting for population size, controlling for spatial autocorrelation and heteroskedasticity, assuming a non-linear relationship between mortality and socio-economic deprivation, separating the dependent variable into male and female SMRs, and distinguishing between West, North and Southeast regions. The rejection of the hypothesis of spatial heterogeneity in the relationship between socio-economic deprivation and mortality complements prior research on the stability of the deprivation-mortality relationship over time.']\n\nQuestion: Does context matter for the relationship between deprivation and all-cause mortality?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study finds that while there are spatial concentrations of deprivation and mortality, the relationship between deprivation and all-cause mortality does not vary significantly across regions, including the West of Scotland versus the rest. This suggests that the effect of deprivation on mortality is consistent regardless of regional context. Therefore, context does not significantly alter the relationship.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 418, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 488}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.6678e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_335", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"That alcohol consumption is strongly influenced by the drinking behavior of social company has been demonstrated in observational research. However, not everyone is equally vulnerable to other people's drinking, and it is important to unravel which factors underlie these individual differences. This study focuses on the role of psychosocial stress in attempting to explain individual differences in the propensity to imitate alcohol consumption.\", \"With a 2 (confederate's drinking condition: alcohol vs. soda) \u00d7 2 (participant's stress condition: stress vs. no stress) experimental design, we tested whether the tendency to imitate other people's drinking was related to participants' induced stress levels. The young male adults (N = 106) were randomly assigned to each of the conditions. In each session, directly after the stress or no-stress period, confederates and participants entered a bar laboratory where we observed their drinking behavior. Prior to entering the session, confederates were instructed to drink alcohol or soda.\", 'Participants in both stress and no-stress conditions consumed substantially more alcohol when confederates drank alcohol than when they drank soda. There was no difference in alcohol consumed between stress and no-stress conditions. No moderating effect of stress on the tendency to drink along with peers was found.']\n\nQuestion: Does stress increase imitation of drinking behavior?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that participants drank more alcohol when confederates drank alcohol, regardless of whether they were under stress or not. There was no significant difference in alcohol consumption between the stress and no-stress conditions, indicating stress did not influence the imitation of drinking behavior. Therefore, stress does not increase imitation of drinking behavior.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 342, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 412}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.1281999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_336", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"Schools can play an important role in the prevention of obesity, e.g. by providing an environment that stimulates healthy eating habits and by developing a food policy to provide such an environment. The effectiveness of a school food policy is affected by the content of the policy, its implementation and its support by parents, teachers and principals. The aim of this study is to detect opportunities to improve the school food policy and/or implementation at Dutch primary schools. Therefore, this study explores the school food policy and investigates schools' (teachers and principals) and parents' opinion on the school food policy.\", \"Data on the schools' perspective of the food policy was collected from principals and teachers by means of semi-structured interviews. In total 74 principals and 72 teachers from 83 Dutch primary schools were interviewed. Data on parental perceptions about the school food policy were based on a cross-sectional survey among 1,429 parents from the same schools.\", \"Most principals (87.1%) reported that their school had a written food policy; however in most cases the rules were not clearly defined. Most of the principals (87.8%) believed that their school paid sufficient attention to nutrition and health. Teachers and principals felt that parents were primarily responsible to encourage healthy eating habits among children, while 49.8% of the parents believed that it is also a responsibility of the school to foster healthy eating habits among children. Most parents reported that they appreciated the school food policy and comply with the food rules. Parents' opinion on the enforcement of the school food policy varied: 28.1% believed that the school should enforce the policy more strongly, 32.1% was satisfied, and 39.8% had no opinion on this topic.\"]\n\nQuestion: School food policy at Dutch primary schools: room for improvement?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data indicate that while most schools have a written food policy, the rules are often not clearly defined, and there is a disconnect between the responsibilities perceived by parents and school staff. Additionally, nearly 28% of parents believe the policy should be enforced more strongly, signaling room for improvement. These findings suggest that despite existing policies, there are clear opportunities to enhance both the content and implementation of school food policies.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 448, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 536}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.0607999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_337", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The atopy patch test (APT), namely the patch test with aeroallergens, is regarded as specific for patients with atopic dermatitis (AD), but small numbers of positive APT were reported in the past also in atopic subjects without dermatitis and in healthy persons.', 'The aim of this study was to evaluate the response to the APT with house dust mites (HDM) in subjects nonaffected by AD and to compare the outcomes observed in these cases with those pointed out in AD patients, evaluating also the differences between two allergen extracts manufactured at different purifications and concentrations.', 'Forty-seven atopic subjects without eczema (AWE), 33 nonatopic (NA) subjects and 77 adult AD patients were patch tested with an extract of purified bodies of HDM at 20% and with another extract of whole bodies of HDM at 30%, the latter corresponding to 300 microg/g of Der p 1. The reproducibility of APT was also tested in 8 AD patients, in 37 AWE subjects and in 19 NA subjects.', 'Positive responses with extract at 20% were observed in 29 (37.7%) AD, in 5 (10.6%) AWE and in 4 (12.1%) NA subjects. The APT with HDM at 30% was positive in 32 (41.6%) AD, 9 (19.1%) AWE and 4 (12.1%) NA persons. The rates of positivity and the intensity scores of responses were significantly different between AD and non-AD subjects (p<0.01). The reproducibility of the APT in the three groups was satisfactory.']\n\nQuestion: Is the atopy patch test with house dust mites specific for atopic dermatitis?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The atopy patch test (APT) with house dust mites produced positive results in atopic and nonatopic subjects without atopic dermatitis, although at lower rates than in AD patients. Since positivity was observed in individuals not affected by AD, the test cannot be considered fully specific for the condition. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 468, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 542}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.062799999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_338", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The primary physis is responsible for longitudinal bone growth. Similarly, epiphysial growth relies on endochondral ossification from the circumferential secondary physeal [corrected]. injury can result in disruption of normal ossification. The cause of juvenile osteochondritis dissecans (OCD) remains elusive. We hypothesized that juvenile OCD results from an insult affecting endochondral ossification from the secondary physis. The purpose of our study was to evaluate the MRI appearance of the distal femoral epiphysis-particularly the secondary physis-of children with juvenile OCD and to compare these findings with the MRI findings of unaffected children.', 'Knee MRI examinations of 30 children (age range, 8 years 8 months to 13 years 4 months) with OCD and 30 matched control patients were evaluated for skeletal maturity; location of the OCD lesion, if present; secondary physeal [corrected] continuity; overlying chondroepiphysial integrity, contour, and width; signal intensity of subchondral bone; and secondary physeal [corrected]conspicuity. Variables were compared using chi-square tests.', 'All children were skeletally immature. Condylar lesions were medial in 24 knees and lateral in six knees. All were in the middle one third, posterior one third, or middle and posterior thirds in the sagittal plane. The majority of lesions spanned the intercondylar and middle one third of the femoral condyle in the coronal plane (73%). There was a significant difference between secondary physeal [corrected] disruption in juvenile OCD condyles compared with unaffected condyles (p<0.001) and control condyles (p<0.001). Compared with unaffected and control condyles, the OCD group showed chondroepiphysial widening (p<0.001) and subchondral bone edema (p<0.001) on MRI. Neither chondroepiphysial integrity nor chondroepiphysial contour was significantly different between groups (p = 0.21, p = 0.31, respectively).']\n\nQuestion: Juvenile osteochondritis dissecans: is it a growth disturbance of the secondary physis of the epiphysis?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found a significant association between juvenile osteochondritis dissecans (OCD) and disruption of the secondary physis, along with chondroepiphysial widening and subchondral bone edema on MRI. These findings support the hypothesis that juvenile OCD involves a disturbance in endochondral ossification from the secondary physis. Therefore, the evidence suggests that juvenile OCD is indeed a growth disturbance of the secondary physis.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 598, "output_tokens": 116, "total_tokens": 714}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 5.4058e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_341", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"In this study, an expert panel assessed causality of adverse reports by using the WHO global introspection (GI) method. The same reports were independently assessed using 15 published algorithms. The causality assessment level 'possible' was considered the lower limit for a report to be considered to be drug related. For a given algorithm, sensitivity was determined by the proportion of reports simultaneously classified as drug related by the algorithm and the GI method. Specificity was measured as the proportion of reports simultaneously considered non-drug related. The analysis was performed for the total sample and within serious or unexpected events.\", 'Five hundred adverse reports were studied. Algorithms presented high rates of sensitivity (average of 93%, positive predictive value of 89%) and low rates of specificity (average of 7%, negative predictive value of 31%).']\n\nQuestion: Can decisional algorithms replace global introspection in the individual causality assessment of spontaneously reported ADRs?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The algorithms show high sensitivity but very low specificity, meaning they correctly identify most true drug-related cases but misclassify many non-drug-related cases as related. This poor specificity limits their reliability in ruling out drug causality, making them inadequate for replacing the more balanced global introspection method. Therefore, they cannot reliably replace global introspection for individual causality assessment.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 266, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 343}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.6586e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_345", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Outcome feedback is the process of learning patient outcomes after their care within the emergency department. We conducted a national survey of Canadian Royal College emergency medicine (EM) residents and program directors to determine the extent to which active outcome feedback and follow-up occurred. We also compared the perceived educational value of outcome feedback between residents and program directors.', \"We distributed surveys to all Royal College-accredited adult and pediatric EM training programs using a modified Dillman method. We analyzed the data using student's t-test for continuous variables and Fisher's exact test for categorical variables.\", 'We received 210 completed surveys from 260 eligible residents (80.8%) and 21 of 24 program directors (87.5%) (overall 81.3%). Mandatory active outcome feedback was not present in any EM training program for admitted or discharged patients (0/21). Follow-up was performed electively by 89.4% of residents for patients admitted to the hospital, and by 44.2% of residents for patients discharged home. A majority of residents (76.9%) believed that patient follow-up should be mandatory compared to 42.9% of program directors (p=0.002). The perceived educational value of outcome feedback was 5.8/7 for residents and 5.1/7 for program directors (difference 0.7; p=0.002) based on a seven-point Likert scale (1=not important; 7=very important).']\n\nQuestion: Outcome Feedback within Emergency Medicine Training Programs: An Opportunity to Apply the Theory of Deliberate Practice?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study reveals that while residents highly value outcome feedback and believe it should be mandatory, none of the programs have mandatory active outcome feedback systems in place. This gap represents an opportunity to incorporate structured, deliberate practice\u2014characterized by systematic feedback and reflection\u2014into emergency medicine training. Therefore, the findings support the application of deliberate practice theory in this context.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 472, "output_tokens": 117, "total_tokens": 589}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.5212e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_349", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Most older drivers continue to drive as they age. To maintain safe and independent transport, mobility is important for all individuals, but especially for older drivers.', 'The objective of this study was to investigate whether automatic transmission, compared with manual transmission, may improve the driving behavior of older drivers.', 'In total, 31 older drivers (mean age 75.2 years) and 32 younger drivers - used as a control group (mean age 39.2 years) - were assessed twice on the same fixed route; once in a car with manual transmission and once in a car with automatic transmission. The cars were otherwise identical. The driving behavior was assessed with the Ryd On-Road Assessment driving protocol. Time to completion of left turns (right-hand side driving) and the impact of a distraction task were measured.', \"The older group had more driving errors than the younger group, in both the manual and the automatic transmission car. However, and contrary to the younger drivers, automatic transmission improved the older participants' driving behavior as demonstrated by safer speed adjustment in urban areas, greater maneuvering skills, safer lane position and driving in accordance with the speed regulations.\"]\n\nQuestion: Does automatic transmission improve driving behavior in older drivers?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that automatic transmission improved older drivers' behavior by enhancing speed adjustment, maneuvering skills, lane position, and adherence to speed regulations. Although older drivers made more errors overall compared to younger drivers, the use of automatic transmission led to measurable improvements in their performance. Therefore, the evidence supports a positive effect of automatic transmission on older drivers' driving behavior.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 324, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 401}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.0703999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_35", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Recent evaluations of IT innovations in primary care have highlighted variations between centres and practices in uptake and use. We evaluated whether structural characteristics of a general practice were associated with variations in use of a web-based clinical information system underpinning a Managed Clinical Network in diabetes, between the years 2001 and 2003.', 'Using a computerised audit trail, we calculated the numbers of web-based operations that occurred in each practice, stratified by staff type and year, and adjusted for the numbers of registered diabetic patients. In regression analyses, we determined whether total use was associated with structural characteristics of the practice (total list size, training status, numbers of GPs (general practitioners), mean age of the GPs, numbers of female GPs, level of deprivation of the population and whether staff had received advanced training in diabetes care).', 'Initially there were a few practices which made very frequent use of the information system, with relatively high numbers of practices using the facility infrequently. However, overall use gradually became more evenly spread. This effect was particularly evident among nurse users. Frequent use by GPs was evident in only a small number of practices, with mean GP use decreasing over the three years. In linear regression analyses, none of the general practice variables were associated with online use, either overall or stratified by staff type, except for the numbers of diabetes-educated staff. This was consistently associated with increased use by nurses and GPs.']\n\nQuestion: Do general practice characteristics influence uptake of an information technology (IT) innovation in primary care?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context indicates that most general practice characteristics (e.g., list size, GP numbers, deprivation level) were not associated with IT system use. However, the number of staff with advanced diabetes training was consistently linked to higher system use by both nurses and GPs. Therefore, while most characteristics did not influence uptake, one specific factor did, making the overall answer \"yes.\"\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 519, "output_tokens": 106, "total_tokens": 625}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.7449e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_350", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['In this study we investigated whether the association between measures of fetal growth restriction and intellectual performance was mediated by socioeconomic or familial factors.', 'This was a population-based cohort study of 357,768 Swedish males born as singletons without congenital malformations between 1973 and 1981. The main outcome measure was intellectual performance at military conscription.', 'Compared with men born with appropriate birth weight for gestational age, men born light for gestational age suffered an increased risk of low intellectual performance after adjustment for maternal and socioeconomic factors. The increase in risk of low intellectual performance related to a decrease in birth weight for gestational age was similar between families and within families. Men born short or with a small head circumference for gestational age were also at increased risk of low intellectual performance, both when adjusting for maternal and socioeconomic factors and within families.']\n\nQuestion: Birth characteristics and risk of low intellectual performance in early adulthood: are the associations confounded by socioeconomic factors in adolescence or familial effects?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that the association between fetal growth restriction (e.g., low birth weight, short length, small head circumference) and low intellectual performance persisted even after adjusting for maternal and socioeconomic factors and when comparing within families. This indicates that the associations were not fully explained by socioeconomic or familial confounding factors. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 283, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 357}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.7493000000000003e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_356", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To assess pain-related attentional biases among individuals with episodic migraine.', 'Prior studies have examined whether chronic pain patients selectively attend to pain-related stimuli in the environment, but these studies have produced largely mixed findings and focused primarily on patients with chronic musculoskeletal pain. Limited research has implicated attentional biases among chronic headache patients, but no studies have been conducted among episodic migraineurs, who comprise the overwhelming majority of the migraine population.', 'This was a case-control, experimental study. Three hundred and eight participants (mean age\\u2009=\\u200919.2 years [standard deviation\\u2009=\\u20093.3]; 69.5% female; 36.4% minority), consisting of 84 episodic migraineurs, diagnosed in accordance with International Classification of Headache Disorders (2(nd) edition) criteria using a structured diagnostic interview, and 224 non-migraine controls completed a computerized dot probe task to assess attentional bias toward headache-related pictorial stimuli. The task consisted of 192 trials and utilized 2 emotional-neutral stimulus pairing conditions (headache-neutral and happy-neutral).', 'No within-group differences for reaction time latencies to headache vs happy conditions were found among those with episodic migraine or among the non-migraine controls. Migraine status was unrelated to attentional bias indices for both headache (F [1,306]\\u2009=\\u20090.56, P\\u2009=\\u2009.45) and happy facial stimuli (F [1,306]\\u2009=\\u20090.37, P\\u2009=\\u2009.54), indicating a lack of between-group differences. Lack of within- and between-group differences was confirmed with repeated measures analysis of variance.']\n\nQuestion: Do episodic migraineurs selectively attend to headache-related visual stimuli?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no within-group or between-group differences in attentional bias toward headache-related stimuli among episodic migraineurs compared to controls. Statistical analyses showed no significant effects of migraine status on attentional bias indices for headache-related pictorial stimuli. Therefore, there is no evidence that episodic migraineurs selectively attend to headache-related visual stimuli.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 492, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 564}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.2131999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_357", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['This was a study to compare the results of mitral valve (MV) repair and MV replacement for the treatment of functional mitral regurgitation (MR) in advanced dilated and ischemic cardiomyopathy (DCM).', 'One-hundred and thirty-two patients with severe functional MR and systolic dysfunction (mean ejection fraction 0.32 \u00b1 0.078) underwent mitral surgery in the same time frame. The decision to replace rather than repair the MV was taken when 1 or more echocardiographic predictors of repair failure were identified at the preoperative echocardiogram. Eighty-five patients (64.4%) received MV repair and 47 patients (35.6%) received MV replacement. Preoperative characteristics were comparable between the 2 groups. Only ejection fraction was significantly lower in the MV repair group (0.308 \u00b1 0.077 vs 0.336 \u00b1 0.076, p = 0.04).', 'Hospital mortality was 2.3% for MV repair and 12.5% for MV replacement (p = 0.03). Actuarial survival at 2.5 years was 92 \u00b1 3.2% for MV repair and 73 \u00b1 7.9% for MV replacement (p = 0.02). At a mean follow-up of 2.3 years (median, 1.6 years), in the MV repair group LVEF significantly increased (from 0.308 \u00b1 0.077 to 0.382 \u00b1 0.095, p<0.0001) and LV dimensions significantly decreased (p = 0.0001). On the other hand, in the MV replacement group LVEF did not significantly change (from 0.336 \u00b1 0.076 to 0.31 \u00b1 0.11, p = 0.56) and the reduction of LV dimensions was not significant. Mitral valve replacement was identified as the only predictor of hospital (odds ratio, 6; 95% confidence interval, 1.1 to 31; p = 0.03) and overall mortality (hazard ratio, 3.1; 95% confidence interval, 1.1 to 8.9; p = 0.02).']\n\nQuestion: Mitral replacement or repair for functional mitral regurgitation in dilated and ischemic cardiomyopathy: is it really the same?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows significantly better outcomes with mitral valve repair compared to replacement, including lower hospital mortality, higher actuarial survival, and improved left ventricular function and dimensions. Mitral valve replacement was identified as an independent predictor of higher mortality. Therefore, the two procedures are not the same in this patient population.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 626, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 695}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 5.1346e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_358", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To study whether nontriploid partial hydatidiform moles truly exist.', 'We conducted a reevaluation of pathology and ploidy in 19 putative nontriploid partial hydatidiform moles using standardized histologic diagnostic criteria and repeat flow cytometric testing by the Hedley technique.', 'On review of the 19 moles, 53% (10/19) were diploid nonpartial moles (initially pathologically misclassified), and 37% (7/19) were triploid partial moles (initial ploidy misclassifications). One additional case (5%) was a diploid early complete mole (initially pathologically misclassified).']\n\nQuestion: Do nontriploid partial hydatidiform moles exist?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study reevaluated 19 putative nontriploid partial moles and found that all were misclassified: either as diploid nonpartial moles, triploid partial moles, or an early complete mole. No confirmed cases of nontriploid partial moles were identified upon reanalysis. This suggests that nontriploid partial hydatidiform moles do not truly exist.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 237, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 321}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.5226999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_362", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['There is controversy surrounding the optimal management of the testicular remnant associated with the vanishing testes syndrome. Some urologists advocate the need for surgical exploration, whereas others believe this is unnecessary. These differing opinions are based on the variable reports of viable germ cell elements found within the testicular remnants. To better understand the pathology associated with this syndrome and the need for surgical management, we reviewed our experience regarding the incidence of viable germ cell elements within the testicular remnant.', 'An institutional review board-approved, retrospective review was performed of all consecutive patients undergoing exploration for a nonpalpable testis at Eastern Virginia Medical School and Geisinger Medical Center between 1994 and 2006. Patients who were found to have spermatic vessels and a vas deferens exiting a closed internal inguinal ring were included in this analysis.', 'Fifty-six patients underwent removal of the testicular remnant. Patient age ranged from 11 to 216 months. In 8 of the specimens (14%), we identified viable germ cell elements. In an additional 4 patients (7%), we identified seminiferous tubules without germ cell elements.']\n\nQuestion: Histologic evaluation of the testicular remnant associated with the vanishing testes syndrome: is surgical management necessary?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The histologic evaluation found viable germ cell elements in 14% of testicular remnants, with an additional 7% showing seminiferous tubules without germ cells. This suggests that in a notable proportion of cases, there may be potentially functional tissue, supporting consideration for surgical exploration and management. Therefore, the presence of viable elements in over 10% of cases leans toward a recommendation for surgical evaluation.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 342, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 431}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.3181999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_369", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Cutaneous melanoma in nonwhite persons has a manifestation and a prognosis that are different than those of cutaneous melanoma in white persons.', 'Case series.', 'Tertiary care university-affiliated community medical center located in a multiethnic state in which white persons are a minority of the population.', 'Consecutive series of 357 patients with melanoma seen between January 1994 and August 2003.', 'Ethnicity, age, sex, primary site, tumor thickness, nodal status, stage at diagnosis, and survival.', 'There were 208 men and 149 women who ranged in age from 15 to 93 years (mean, 58 years). Twenty-two patients initially had unknown primary sites. Of these 357 patients, 67 (18.7%) were nonwhite. There was no statistically significant difference in the age (P =.10) or sex (P =.57) distribution of these 2 populations. Nonwhite patients at initial diagnosis had thicker tumors (P =.002), more frequently had ulcerated primary tumors (P<.001), more frequently had positive nodes (P =.004), and were at a more advanced stage (P =.002) than their white counterparts. The anatomic distribution between the 2 populations was significantly different (P<.001), with a high incidence of melanoma on the sole and subungual locations and a substantially less frequent occurrence on the head and neck, trunk, and extremities in the nonwhite population when compared with the white population. The overall survival rate of the nonwhite patients was significantly worse than that of the white patients, but when stratified by stage at initial diagnosis, there was no difference in outcome.']\n\nQuestion: Cutaneous melanoma in a multiethnic population: is this a different disease?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data show that cutaneous melanoma in nonwhite individuals presents with thicker, more ulcerated tumors, higher nodal involvement, and advanced stage at diagnosis, with distinct anatomic distribution compared to white individuals. However, survival differences disappear when adjusted for stage, suggesting the disease behaves similarly once diagnosed at comparable stages. Thus, while presentation and outcomes differ, it is not a fundamentally different disease.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 470, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 555}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.187e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_370", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Men appear to benefit more from being married than women with respect to mortality in middle age. However, there is some uncertainty about gender differences in mortality risks in older individuals, widowed, divorced and single individuals and about the impact of living arrangements.', 'Longitudinal data with 1990 census records being linked to mortality data up to 2005 were used (Swiss National Cohort). The sample comprised all residents over age 44 years in Switzerland (n=2,440,242). All-cause mortality HRs for marital status and living arrangements were estimated by Cox regression for men and women and different age groups with adjustment for education and socio-professional category.', 'The benefit of being married was stronger for men than for women; however, mortality patterns were similar, with higher mortality in divorced and single individuals compared with widowed individuals (<80 years). After adjustment for living arrangements, the gender difference by marital status disappeared. Stratification by living arrangement revealed that mortality risks were highest for 45-64-year-old divorced (HR 1.72 (95% CI 1.67 to 1.76)) and single men (HR 1.67 (95% CI 1.63 to 1.71)) who lived alone. In women of the same age, the highest mortality risk was observed for those who were single and living with a partner (HR 1.70 (95% CI 1.58 to 1.82)). In older age groups, the impact of marital status decreased.']\n\nQuestion: Marital status, living arrangement and mortality: does the association vary by gender?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study indicates that while the benefit of being married is initially stronger for men, the gender difference disappears after adjusting for living arrangements. Furthermore, the specific mortality risks associated with marital status and living arrangements differ significantly between men and women (e.g., divorced/single men living alone vs. single women living with a partner). Therefore, the association between these factors and mortality does vary by gender.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 421, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 506}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:13.726621+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00023275, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_371", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Neuromedin U (NmU) is a neuropeptide with anorexigenic activity. Two receptor subtypes (NmUR1 and NmUR2) confer the effects of NmU on target cells. We have recently demonstrated that NmU reduces insulin secretion from isolated pancreatic islets. Aim of our current study is to investigate the role of somatostatin at mediating the effects of NmU on insulin secretion.', 'Expression of NmU in the pancreas was detected by immunohistochemistry. Insulin and somatostatin secretion from in situ perfused rat pancreas and isolated pancreatic islets was measured by radioimmunoassay. The paracrine effects of somatostatin within pancreatic islets were blocked by cyclosomatostatin, a somatostatin receptor antagonist.', 'Receptor subtype NmUR1, but not NmUR2, was expressed in the endocrine pancreas, predominantly in the periphery. Neuromedin U reduced insulin secretion from in situ perfused rat pancreas and stimulated somatostatin secretion from isolated pancreatic islets. Neuromedin U stimulated somatostatin secretion at both physiological and supraphysiological glucose concentrations. Cyclosomatostatin increased insulin secretion and reduced NmU-induced inhibition of insulin secretion.']\n\nQuestion: Does somatostatin confer insulinostatic effects of neuromedin u in the rat pancreas?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that neuromedin U (NmU) stimulates somatostatin secretion and that NmU's inhibition of insulin secretion is reduced when somatostatin signaling is blocked by cyclosomatostatin. This indicates that somatostatin plays a key role in mediating NmU's insulinostatic effects. Therefore, the evidence supports that somatostatin confers the insulinostatic effects of NmU.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 369, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 464}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.5699e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_372", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Kell haemolytic disease in pregnancies has been suggested to be associated with decreased fetal platelet counts. The aim of this study was to evaluate the incidence and clinical significance of fetal thrombocytopenia in pregnancies complicated by Kell alloimmunization.', 'In this retrospective cohort study, fetal platelet counts were performed in 42 pregnancies with severe Kell alloimmunization prior to the first intrauterine blood transfusion. Platelet counts from 318 first intrauterine transfusions in RhD alloimmunized pregnancies were used as controls.', 'Fetal thrombocytopenia (platelet count<150 x 10(9)/l) was found in 4/42 (10%) in the Kell group and in 84/318 (26%) in the RhD group. None of the fetuses in the Kell alloimmunized pregnancies, including 15 with severe hydrops, had a clinically significant thrombocytopenia defined as a platelet count<50 x 10(9)/l. In the RhD alloimmunized pregnancies, 2/230 (1%) of the non-hydropic fetuses and 7/30 (23%) of the severely hydropic fetuses had a clinically significant thrombocytopenia.']\n\nQuestion: Kell alloimmunization in pregnancy: associated with fetal thrombocytopenia?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that fetal thrombocytopenia (platelet count <150 x 10\u2079/L) occurred in 10% of Kell alloimmunized pregnancies, but none had severe thrombocytopenia (<50 x 10\u2079/L), even in cases of severe hydrops. In contrast, RhD alloimmunization was associated with higher rates of both mild and severe thrombocytopenia. Therefore, Kell alloimmunization is not strongly associated with clinically significant fetal thrombocytopenia.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 372, "output_tokens": 114, "total_tokens": 486}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.7811999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_373", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The identification of the most suspect enhancing part of a lesion is regarded as a major diagnostic criterion in dynamic magnetic resonance mammography. Computer-aided diagnosis (CAD) software allows the semi-automatic analysis of the kinetic characteristics of complete enhancing lesions, providing additional information about lesion vasculature. The diagnostic value of this information has not yet been quantified.', 'Consecutive patients from routine diagnostic studies (1.5 T, 0.1 mmol gadopentetate dimeglumine, dynamic gradient-echo sequences at 1-minute intervals) were analyzed prospectively using CAD. Dynamic sequences were processed and reduced to a parametric map. Curve types were classified by initial signal increase (not significant, intermediate, and strong) and the delayed time course of signal intensity (continuous, plateau, and washout). Lesion enhancement was measured using CAD. The most suspect curve, the curve-type distribution percentage, and combined dynamic data were compared. Statistical analysis included logistic regression analysis and receiver-operating characteristic analysis.', 'Fifty-one patients with 46 malignant and 44 benign lesions were enrolled. On receiver-operating characteristic analysis, the most suspect curve showed diagnostic accuracy of 76.7 +/- 5%. In comparison, the curve-type distribution percentage demonstrated accuracy of 80.2 +/- 4.9%. Combined dynamic data had the highest diagnostic accuracy (84.3 +/- 4.2%). These differences did not achieve statistical significance. With appropriate cutoff values, sensitivity and specificity, respectively, were found to be 80.4% and 72.7% for the most suspect curve, 76.1% and 83.6% for the curve-type distribution percentage, and 78.3% and 84.5% for both parameters.']\n\nQuestion: Application of computer-aided diagnosis (CAD) in MR-mammography (MRM): do we really need whole lesion time curve distribution analysis?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that while combined dynamic data (including whole lesion distribution) yielded the highest diagnostic accuracy, the differences between the methods did not achieve statistical significance. Therefore, the results suggest that whole lesion analysis is not strictly necessary to achieve comparable diagnostic performance.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 467, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 523}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:27.813419+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00020075, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_374", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The aim of the study was to evaluate, if elderly persons are sufficiently protected against infectious diseases by vaccination.', '300 elderly (>60 years) and 300 young (<35 years) persons from five Austrian cities were recruited according to the criteria of a field study. Antibody concentrations against tetanus, diphtheria, tickborne encephalitis and influenza were assessed by ELISA or by haemagglutination inhibition test. Disease and vaccination histories were recorded.', 'The results of the study demonstrate that protection against infectious diseases was frequently insufficient in the elderly. This was partly due to the fact that old persons were not vaccinated according to recommended strategies. However, low antibody concentration and a short duration of protective humoral immunity were also observed in many elderly persons in spite of regular vaccination. This was not only the case in frail, but also in healthy elderlies.']\n\nQuestion: Vaccine protection in the elderly: are Austrian seniors adequately protected by vaccinations?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that protection against infectious diseases was frequently insufficient in the elderly, even among those who were regularly vaccinated. It noted low antibody concentrations and short duration of immunity, not only in frail but also in healthy elderly individuals. Therefore, Austrian seniors are not adequately protected by vaccinations.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 273, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 334}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.5483e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_375", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Epidemiological data show significant associations of vitamin D deficiency and autoimmune diseases. Vitamin D may prevent autoimmunity by stimulating naturally occurring regulatory T cells.', 'To elucidate whether vitamin D supplementation increases Tregs frequency (%Tregs) within circulating CD4+ T cells.', 'We performed an uncontrolled vitamin D supplementation trial among 50 apparently healthy subjects including supplementation of 140,000 IU at baseline and after 4 weeks (visit 1). The final follow-up visit was performed 8 weeks after the baseline examination (visit 2). Blood was drawn at each study visit to determine 25-hydroxyvitamin D levels and %Tregs. Tregs were characterized as CD4+CD25++ T cells with expression of the transcription factor forkhead box P3 and low or absent expression of CD127.', 'Forty-six study participants (65% females, mean age +/- SD 31 +/- 8 years) completed the trial. 25(OH)D levels increased from 23.9 +/- 12.9 ng/ml at baseline to 45.9 +/- 14.0 ng/ml at visit 1 and 58.0 +/- 15.1 ng/ml at visit 2. %Tregs at baseline were 4.8 +/- 1.4. Compared to baseline levels we noticed a significant increase of %Tregs at study visit 1 (5.9 +/- 1.7, P<0.001) and 2 (5.6 +/- 1.6, P<0.001).']\n\nQuestion: Vitamin D supplementation and regulatory T cells in apparently healthy subjects: vitamin D treatment for autoimmune diseases?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study demonstrates that vitamin D supplementation significantly increases the frequency of regulatory T cells in healthy subjects, which supports the hypothesis that it could be a potential therapeutic strategy for autoimmune diseases. Therefore, the findings align with the possibility suggested in the title.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 428, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 482}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:22.311756+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000188, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_378", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To determine the ability of early sonogram to predict the presentation of twin A at birth.', 'A retrospective cohort study was conducted on all twin pregnancies evaluated at our Fetal Evaluation Unit from 2007 to 2009. Sonogram records were reviewed for the presentation of twin A at seven gestational age intervals and inpatient medical records were reviewed for the presentation of twin A at delivery. The positive predictive value, sensitivity, and specificity of presentation as determined by ultrasound, at each gestational age interval, for the same presentation at delivery were calculated.', 'Two hundred and thirty-eight twin pregnancies met inclusion criteria. A total of 896 ultrasounds were reviewed. The positive predictive value of cephalic presentation of twin A as determined by ultrasound for the persistence of cephalic presentation at delivery reached 95% after 28 weeks gestation. The positive predictive value for noncephalic presentation as established by sonogram for noncephalic at delivery was>90% after 32 weeks gestation.']\n\nQuestion: Can third trimester ultrasound predict the presentation of the first twin at delivery?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that the positive predictive value of ultrasound for both cephalic and noncephalic presentations of twin A reaches high levels (\u226590%) in the third trimester, specifically after 28 and 32 weeks gestation. This indicates that ultrasound in the third trimester is highly predictive of the presentation at delivery. Therefore, the evidence supports that third trimester ultrasound can predict the presentation of the first twin at delivery.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 304, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 399}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.1084e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_38", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Accurate and updated information on airborne pollen in specific areas can help allergic patients. Current monitoring systems are based on a morphologic identification approach, a time-consuming method that may represent a limiting factor for sampling network enhancement.', 'To verify the feasibility of developing a real-time polymerase chain reaction (PCR) approach, an alternative to optical analysis, as a rapid, accurate, and automated tool for the detection and quantification of airborne allergenic pollen taxa.', 'The traditional cetyl trimethyl ammonium bromide-based method was modified for DNA isolation from pollen. Taxon-specific DNA sequences were identified via bioinformatics or literature searches and were PCR amplified from the matching allergenic taxa; based on the sequences of PCR products, complementary or degenerate TaqMan probes were developed. The accuracy of the quantitative real-time PCR assay was tested on 3 plant species.', 'The setup of a modified DNA extraction protocol allowed us to achieve good-quality pollen DNA. Taxon-specific nuclear gene fragments were identified and sequenced. Designed primer pairs and probes identified selected pollen taxa, mostly at the required classification level. Pollen was properly identified even when collected on routine aerobiological tape. Preliminary quantification assays on pollen grains were successfully performed on test species and in mixes.']\n\nQuestion: Biomolecular identification of allergenic pollen: a new perspective for aerobiological monitoring?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The passage describes the successful development and testing of a quantitative real-time PCR method for identifying and quantifying allergenic pollen, offering a faster, more accurate alternative to traditional morphological analysis. It highlights the feasibility of this biomolecular approach, including successful DNA extraction, taxon-specific identification, and application to routine aerobiological samples. This supports the idea that biomolecular identification presents a new and viable perspective for aerobiological monitoring.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 346, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 437}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.3666e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_381", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To evaluate the effects of insulin 30/70 twice daily or bedtime isophane (NPH) insulin plus continued sulfonylurea and metformin in patients with type 2 diabetes in primary care.', 'Open-label, randomized trial.', 'Persons younger than 76 years with type 2 diabetes whose disease had not been controlled with oral hypoglycemic agents alone. A total of 64 insulin-naive patients treated with maximal feasible dosages of sulfonylurea and metformin (baseline glycosylated hemoglobin [HbA1c]=8.5%) were randomly assigned to insulin monotherapy (IM group; n=31) or insulin in addition to unchanged oral hypoglycemic medication (IC group; n=33) for 12 months. Insulin doses were adjusted to obtain fasting glucose<7.0 mmol/L and postprandial glucose<10.0 mmol/L.', 'Outcome measures included HbA1c, treatment failure, weight, hypoglycemic events and symptoms, satisfaction with treatment, general well-being, and fear of injecting insulin and testing.', 'HbA1c improved from 8.3% to 7.6% in the IC group, and from 8.8% to 7.6% in the IM group (P=NS). The IC group had 24% treatment failures, compared with 2% in the IM group (P=.09). Patients in the IC group had less weight gain than those in the IM group (1.3 vs 4.2 kg; P=.01), and they reported fewer hypoglycemic events (2.7 vs 4.3; P=.02). Increased satisfaction with treatment was equal in the 2 groups, and general well-being improved by 3.0 points more in the IC group (P=.05). Fear of self-injecting and self-testing did not differ.']\n\nQuestion: Starting insulin in type 2 diabetes: continue oral hypoglycemic agents?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that continuing oral hypoglycemic agents with insulin (IC group) led to similar HbA1c reduction compared to insulin monotherapy (IM group), but with less weight gain, fewer hypoglycemic events, and greater improvement in general well-being. Although treatment failure was higher in the IC group, the overall benefits support continuing oral agents when initiating insulin. Therefore, the most appropriate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 512, "output_tokens": 93, "total_tokens": 605}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.5652e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_382", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Adhesive capsulitis is often difficult to diagnose in its early stage and to differentiate from other common shoulder disorders.', 'The aim of this study was to validate any or all of the 8 clinical identifiers of early-stage primary/idiopathic adhesive capsulitis established in an earlier Delphi study.', 'This was a cross-sectional study.', 'Sixty-four patients diagnosed with early-stage adhesive capsulitis by a physical therapist or medical practitioner were included in the study. Eight active and 8 passive shoulder movements and visual analog scale pain scores for each movement were recorded prior to and immediately following an intra-articular injection of corticosteroid and local anesthetic. Using the local anesthetic as the reference standard, pain relief of \u226570% for passive external rotation was deemed a positive anesthetic response (PAR).', 'Sixteen participants (25%) demonstrated a PAR. Univariate logistic regression identified that of the proposed identifiers, global loss of passive range of movement (odds ratio [OR]=0.26, P=.03), pain at the end of range of all measured active movements (OR=0.06, P=.02), and global loss of passive glenohumeral movements (OR=0.23, P=.02) were associated with a PAR. Following stepwise removal of the variables, pain at the end of range of all measured active movements remained the only identifier but was associated with reduced odds of a PAR.', 'The lack of a recognized reference standard for diagnosing early-stage adhesive capsulitis remains problematic in all related research.']\n\nQuestion: Clinical identifiers for early-stage primary/idiopathic adhesive capsulitis: are we seeing the real picture?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that only a few clinical identifiers were statistically associated with a positive anesthetic response, and even then, the strongest predictor (pain at end of range in active movements) was linked to reduced odds of a positive response. This suggests that current proposed clinical identifiers may not reliably diagnose early-stage adhesive capsulitis. Given the lack of a recognized reference standard and weak associations, the evidence indicates we may not yet be seeing the real picture.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 422, "output_tokens": 94, "total_tokens": 516}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.9361999999999993e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_384", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['There is no standard protocol for the evaluation of antiseptics used for skin and mucous membranes in the presence of interfering substances. Our objective was to suggest trial conditions adapted from the NF EN 13727 standard, for the evaluation of antiseptics used in gynecology and dermatology.', 'Three antiseptic solutions were tested in vitro: a chlorhexidine-benzalkonium (CB) combination, a hexamidine-chlorhexidine-chlorocresol (HCC) combination, and povidone iodine (P). The adaptation of trial conditions to the standard involved choosing dilutions, solvent, and interfering substances. The activity of solutions was assessed on the recommended strains at concentrations of 97% (pure solution), 50%, and 10% (diluted solution), and 1%. A logarithmic reduction \u2265 5 was expected after 60seconds of contact, to meet requirements of bactericidal activity.', 'HCC did not present any bactericidal activity except on P. aeruginosa at a concentration of 97%. P was not bactericidal on E. hirae at any concentration and on S. aureus at 97%. CB had the most homogeneous bactericidal activity with a reduction>5 log on the 4 bacterial strains at concentrations of 97%, 50% and 10%.']\n\nQuestion: Bactericidal activity of 3 cutaneous/mucosal antiseptic solutions in the presence of interfering substances: Improvement of the NF EN 13727 European Standard?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study aimed to adapt and improve the NF EN 13727 standard for evaluating antiseptics used in gynecology and dermatology by testing three solutions under modified conditions. Among the tested antiseptics, only the chlorhexidine-benzalkonium (CB) combination showed consistent bactericidal activity across multiple strains and concentrations. The proposed adaptations suggest an improvement to the standard, making the answer:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 406, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 498}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.8026e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_385", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Current guidelines for the treatment of uncomplicated urinary tract infection (UTI) in women recommend empiric therapy with antibiotics for which local resistance rates do not exceed 10-20%. We hypothesized that resistance rates of Escherichia coli to fluoroquinolones may have surpassed this level in older women in the Israeli community setting.', 'To identify age groups of women in which fluoroquinolones may no longer be appropriate for empiric treatment of UTI.', 'Resistance rates for ofloxacin were calculated for all cases of uncomplicated UTI diagnosed during the first 5 months of 2005 in a managed care organization (MCO) in Israel, in community-dwelling women aged 41-75 years. The women were without risk factors for fluoroquinolone resistance. Uncomplicated UTI was diagnosed with a urine culture positive for E. coli. The data set was stratified for age, using 5 year intervals, and stratum-specific resistance rates (% and 95% CI) were calculated. These data were analyzed to identify age groups in which resistance rates have surpassed 10%.', 'The data from 1291 urine cultures were included. The crude resistance rate to ofloxacin was 8.7% (95% CI 7.4 to 10.2). Resistance was lowest among the youngest (aged 41-50 y) women (3.2%; 95% CI 1.11 to 5.18), approached 10% in women aged 51-55 years (7.1%; 95% CI 3.4 to 10.9), and reached 19.86% (95% CI 13.2 to 26.5) among the oldest women (aged 56-75 y).']\n\nQuestion: Empiric treatment of uncomplicated urinary tract infection with fluoroquinolones in older women in Israel: another lost treatment option?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that fluoroquinolone resistance in E. coli among women aged 56\u201375 years in Israel was 19.86%, exceeding the recommended 10\u201320% resistance threshold for empiric use. This suggests fluoroquinolones are no longer appropriate for empiric treatment in older women. Therefore, the answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 500, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 581}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.36e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_389", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Utilization of the Recovery Knowledge Inventory (RKI) and Recovery Attitudes Questionnaire (RAQ) in southeastern Australia raised questions about the RAQ, including links between attitudes, faith, and culture in supporting the recovery journey. These questions are particularly important when considered in the context of people with mental illness who live in secular multicultural societies.']\n\nQuestion: Recovery Outcome Measures: Is There a Place for Culture, Attitudes, and Faith?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context highlights the importance of examining how culture, attitudes, and faith influence recovery, especially in secular multicultural societies. It suggests that tools like the RAQ raise valid questions about the role of these factors in recovery outcomes. Therefore, the most appropriate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 163, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 221}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.7372999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_391", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To determine survival among patients with epithelial ovarian carcinoma (EOC) who underwent a second-look laparotomy (SLL) and those refusing the procedure. Also to analyze factor(s) influencing the survival of the patients.', 'Medical records were reviewed of patients with advanced EOC who were clinically free of disease after primary surgery and platinum-based chemotherapy between January 1, 1992, and December 31, 1998. All of them were offered SLL. Measurement outcomes include patient survival and disease-free survival.', \"There were 50 patients with clinically complete remission after chemotherapy. Sixteen patients underwent SLL, and thirty-four patients refused the procedure (NSLL). Seven patients (43.8%) were reported to have positive SLL. After the median follow-up time of 35 months, 12 patients had died, and 5 patients were lost to follow-up. The median survival time for patients with SLL was about 60 months. Five-year survival rates of patients in the SLL, and NSLL groups were 37 per cent (95%CI = 7%-69%), and 88 per cent (95%CI = 65%-96%) respectively (P<0.001). The median time to relapse was about 25 months for patients with negative SLL. Five-year disease-free survival rates of patients in the negative SLL, and NSLL groups were 28 per cent (95%CI = 4%-59%), and 54 per cent (95%CI = 34%-70%) respectively (P=0.251). By Cox regression analysis, tumor grade was the only significant prognostic factor influencing patients' survival (HR = 6, 95%CI of HR = 1.2-34.2).\"]\n\nQuestion: Advanced epithelial ovarian carcinoma in Thai women: should we continue to offer second-look laparotomy?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that patients who refused second-look laparotomy (NSLL) had a significantly higher 5-year survival rate (88%) compared to those who underwent the procedure (37%), with a statistically significant difference (P<0.001). Although tumor grade was the only significant prognostic factor in Cox regression, the markedly better survival in the NSLL group suggests that SLL did not provide a survival benefit and may even be associated with worse outcomes. Therefore, based on these findings, continuing to offer second-look laparotomy is not supported.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 493, "output_tokens": 123, "total_tokens": 616}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.7303e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_392", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['There is a positive association between chronic inflammation and the risk of cardiovascular disease, but whether there is an association between C-reactive protein (CRP) and carotid atherosclerosis is controversial. We investigated the relationship between high-sensitivity CRP (hsCRP) levels and carotid intima-media thickness (IMT) in healthy Koreans.', 'We measured hsCRP levels, the carotid IMT, and conventional cardiovascular risk factors including obesity parameters, blood pressure, lipid profiles, insulin resistance, and smoking habits in 820 volunteers (35-79 years old) in a cross-sectional study.', 'Higher hsCRP quartile groups had higher mean IMTs, as compared with the lowest quartile (P<0.001 for the trend across quartiles). However, after adjustment for age, the relationship between hsCRP level and IMT was substantially weaker (P = 0.018). After additional adjustments for conventional cardiovascular risk factors, no significant association was observed (P = 0.548). The unadjusted risk for a high carotid IMT value (>or = 1.0 mm) was also positively related to hsCRP quartile, but this relationship was not significant after adjustment for age and other cardiovascular risk factors.']\n\nQuestion: Is high-sensitivity C-reactive protein associated with carotid atherosclerosis in healthy Koreans?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that while higher hsCRP levels were initially associated with increased carotid IMT, this association became non-significant after adjusting for age and conventional cardiovascular risk factors. This suggests that the observed relationship was largely explained by these confounding factors. Therefore, there is no independent association between hsCRP and carotid atherosclerosis in healthy Koreans.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 416, "output_tokens": 109, "total_tokens": 525}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.0436e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_393", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['A new edition of the TNM was recently released that includes modifications for the staging system of kidney cancers. Specifically, T2 cancers were subclassified into T2a and T2b (<or =10 cm vs>10 cm), tumors with renal vein involvement or perinephric fat involvement were classified as T3a cancers, and those with adrenal involvement were classified as T4 cancers.', 'Our aim was to validate the recently released edition of the TNM staging system for primary tumor classification in kidney cancer.', 'Our multicenter retrospective study consisted of 5339 patients treated in 16 academic Italian centers.', 'Patients underwent either radical or partial nephrectomy.', 'Univariable and multivariable Cox regression models addressed cancer-specific survival (CSS) after surgery.', 'In the study, 1897 patients (35.5%) were classified as pT1a, 1453 (27%) as pT1b, 437 (8%) as pT2a, 153 (3%) as pT2b, 1059 (20%) as pT3a, 117 (2%) as pT3b, 26 (0.5%) as pT3c, and 197 (4%) as pT4. At a median follow-up of 42 mo, 786 (15%) had died of disease. In univariable analysis, patients with pT2b and pT3a tumors had similar CSS, as did patients with pT3c and pT4 tumors. Moreover, both pT3a and pT3b stages included patients with heterogeneous outcomes. In multivariable analysis, the novel classification of the primary tumor was a powerful independent predictor of CSS (p for trend<0.0001). However, the substratification of pT1 tumors did not retain an independent predictive role. The major limitations of the study are retrospective design, lack of central pathologic review, and the small number of patients included in some substages.']\n\nQuestion: Validation of the 2009 TNM version in a large multi-institutional cohort of patients treated for renal cell carcinoma: are further improvements needed?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that while the 2009 TNM classification was a powerful independent predictor of cancer-specific survival, it revealed issues such as similar outcomes between pT2b and pT3a tumors and heterogeneous outcomes within pT3a and pT3b stages. Additionally, the substratification of pT1 tumors did not retain independent predictive value. These findings suggest that despite improvements, further refinements to the staging system may be necessary.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 550, "output_tokens": 98, "total_tokens": 648}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.8849999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_398", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The high prevalence of obesity in African American (AA) women may result, in part, from a lower resting metabolic rate (RMR) than non-AA women. If true, AA women should require fewer calories than non-AA women to maintain weight. Our objective was to determine in the setting of a controlled feeding study, if AA women required fewer calories than non-AA women to maintain weight.', 'This analysis includes 206 women (73% AA), aged 22-75 years, who participated in the Dietary Approaches to Stop Hypertension (DASH) trial-a multicenter, randomized, controlled, feeding study comparing the effects of 3 dietary patterns on blood pressure in individuals with prehypertension or stage 1 hypertension. After a 3-week run-in, participants were randomized to 1 of 3 dietary patterns for 8 weeks. Calorie intake was adjusted during feeding to maintain stable weight. The primary outcome of this analysis was average daily calorie (kcal) intake during feeding.', 'AA women had higher baseline weight and body mass index than non-AA women (78.4 vs 72.4 kg, P<.01; 29.0 vs 27.6 kg/m(2), P<.05, respectively). During intervention feeding, mean (SD) kcal was 2168 (293) in AA women and 2073 (284) in non-AA women. Mean intake was 94.7 kcal higher in AA women than in non-AA women (P<.05). After adjustment for potential confounders, there was no difference in caloric intake between AA and non-AA women (\u0394 = -2.8 kcal, P = .95).']\n\nQuestion: Do African American women require fewer calories to maintain weight?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data show that African American (AA) women had a higher average daily caloric intake during the study compared to non-AA women, and after adjusting for confounders, there was no significant difference in caloric needs between the groups. This indicates that AA women do not require fewer calories to maintain weight. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 455, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 523}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.9105000000000006e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_399", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['There are few data concerning emergency double-balloon enteroscopy (DBE) and its usefulness in the management of severe acute obscure gastrointestinal bleeding (OGIB). The aim of this retrospective study was to evaluate emergency DBE and capsule endoscopy (CE) in patients with overt OGIB, analyzing the feasibility of this combined approach.', 'Emergency DBE in patients with overt OGIB was defined as performance within 24\\u2009h of symptom onset. We reported 27 patients (16 men, mean age: 64.6\\u2009\u00b1\\u200917.9 years) with overt severe bleeding who underwent 29 emergency DBE (22 anterograde, 7 retrograde). Of 27 patients, 16 (59.3%) underwent CE with real time (RT) viewing.', \"Patients were diagnosed with the following: Dieulafoy's lesion (DL; n\\u2009=\\u200911, 40.7%), angioectasia (n\\u2009=\\u20097, 25.9%), tumors (n\\u2009=\\u20094, 14.8%), diverticulum (n\\u2009=\\u20093, 11.1%), ulcers (n\\u2009=\\u20092, 7.4%). We diagnosed 23 lesions amenable to endoscopic hemostasis and successfully treated 21 of them (77.8%). DL detection rate was statistically higher in the emergency DBE group than in OGIB patients with DBE done 24\\u2009h after symptom onset (40.7% vs 0.9%, respectively, P\\u2009<\\u20090.001). Combined approach with RT viewing by CE correctly modified DBE management in four patients (25%).\"]\n\nQuestion: Emergency double-balloon enteroscopy combined with real-time viewing of capsule endoscopy: a feasible combined approach in acute overt-obscure gastrointestinal bleeding?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that emergency double-balloon enteroscopy (DBE) combined with real-time (RT) viewing of capsule endoscopy (CE) was performed in patients with acute overt obscure gastrointestinal bleeding (OGIB), and this combined approach correctly modified DBE management in 25% of cases. The high diagnostic yield and successful treatment of lesions, especially the increased detection of Dieulafoy's lesions, support the feasibility of this approach. Therefore, the evidence from the study indicates that the combined approach is feasible.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 534, "output_tokens": 111, "total_tokens": 645}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.9013999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_40", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To describe the biomechanical and wound healing characteristics of corneas after excimer laser keratorefractive surgery.', \"Histologic, ultrastructural, and cohesive tensile strength evaluations were performed on 25 normal human corneal specimens, 206 uncomplicated LASIK specimens, 17 uncomplicated sub-Bowman's keratomileusis (SBK) specimens, 4 uncomplicated photorefractive keratectomy (PRK) specimens, 2 uncomplicated advanced surface ablation (ASA) specimens, 5 keratoconus specimens, 12 postoperative LASIK ectasia specimens, and 1 postoperative PRK ectasia specimen and compared to previously published studies.\", \"Histologic and ultrastructural studies of normal corneas showed significant differences in the direction of collagen fibrils and/or the degree of lamellar interweaving in Bowman's layer, the anterior third of the corneal stroma, the posterior two-thirds of the corneal stroma, and Descemet's membrane. Cohesive tensile strength testing directly supported these morphologic findings as the stronger, more rigid regions of the cornea were located anteriorly and peripherally. This suggests that PRK and ASA, and secondarily SBK, should be biomechanically safer than conventional LASIK with regard to risk for causing keratectasia after surgery. Because adult human corneal stromal wounds heal slowly and incompletely, all excimer laser keratorefractive surgical techniques still have some distinct disadvantages due to inadequate reparative wound healing. Despite reducing some of the risk for corneal haze compared to conventional PRK, ASA cases still can develop corneal haze or breakthrough haze from the hypercellular fibrotic stromal scarring. In contrast, similar to conventional LASIK, SBK still has the short- and long-term potential for interface wound complications from the hypocellular primitive stromal scar.\"]\n\nQuestion: Biomechanical and wound healing characteristics of corneas after excimer laser keratorefractive surgery: is there a difference between advanced surface ablation and sub-Bowman's keratomileusis?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Yes, there is a difference between advanced surface ablation (ASA) and sub-Bowman's keratomileusis (SBK) in terms of biomechanical and wound healing characteristics. The text indicates that ASA and PRK are biomechanically safer than LASIK (and by extension SBK) regarding keratectasia risk due to preservation of anterior corneal structure, while SBK carries potential interface complications from a hypocellular scar. Additionally, ASA can still develop corneal haze due to fibrotic scarring, whereas SBK avoids haze but compromises structural integrity.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 518, "output_tokens": 126, "total_tokens": 644}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.9378e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_401", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Although body dysmorphic disorder (BDD) is classified in DSM-III-R as a nonpsychotic somatoform disorder, controversy exists as to whether BDD can present with psychotic features. If it can, this raises the possibility that its DSM-III-R psychotic counterpart-delusional disorder, somatic type--may not be a separate disorder. The purpose of this study was to determine whether patients with nonpsychotic BDD (defined according to DSM-III-R criteria, i.e., with maintenance of some insight) were different from patients with psychotic BDD (those whose preoccupation was without insight and of delusional intensity).', 'Fifty consecutive patients meeting DSM-III-R criteria A and C for BDD were assessed with a semistructured interview and the Structured Clinical Interview for DSM-III-R (SCID). Family histories of psychiatric disorders were blindly assessed. The 24 patients with nonpsychotic BDD were compared with the 26 patients with psychotic BDD with respect to demographics, phenomenology, course of illness, associated features, comorbid psychiatric disorders, family history, and treatment response.', 'Patients with psychotic BDD displayed a significantly higher rate of lifetime DSM-III-R psychotic disorder diagnoses than patients with nonpsychotic BDD. However, the two groups did not differ significantly on most other variables examined. For instance, both psychotic and nonpsychotic patients displayed significant morbidity; high comorbidity with mood, anxiety, and psychoactive substance use disorders; and apparent preferential response to serotonin reuptake inhibitors rather than to non-serotonin reuptake blocking antidepressants or antipsychotics.']\n\nQuestion: Body dysmorphic disorder: does it have a psychotic subtype?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study distinguishes between nonpsychotic and psychotic forms of body dysmorphic disorder (BDD), with psychotic BDD defined by delusional intensity and lack of insight. Despite some differences, such as higher rates of comorbid psychotic disorders in the psychotic BDD group, both subtypes showed similar clinical features and treatment responses. This supports the existence of a psychotic subtype of BDD.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 427, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 513}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.8916999999999993e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_403", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To ascertain the perspectives of Trainee Ophthalmologist Diplomats (TOD) on the Ophthalmic Diploma Training (ODT) in West Africa with a view to improving the programme.', 'A survey of set 2005 TOD on ODT was carried out in Ghana, 2006.', \"The trainees included 10 (83.35%) males and two (16.7%) females whose ages ranged between thirty-two and fifty-one years. The sponsors of the trainees included Sight Savers International, five (41.7%); Christian Blind Mission International, three (25.0%); Eye Foundation, Lagos, Nigeria two (16.7%); Ministry of Defence Nigeria, one (8.3%); and Health Authority Ghana, one (8.3%). Nine trainees (75.0%) felt the programme was well structured, training allowances were adequate eight (66.7%) and inadequate four (33.3%). Eleven (91.7%) trainees would work wherever they were posted; ten (83.3%) trainees had sense of fulfillment and three (25%) would like to proceed for residency training. All trainees were at least good in chalazion surgery and treatment of common medical eye conditions. Majority were at least good in eye surgery like cataract, eleven (91.7%); trabeculectomy nine (75.0%); pterygium 10 (83.3%); eyelid, eight (66.7%); destructive 11 (91.6%) and refraction 9 (75.0%). Some trainees' perceived problems included inadequate sponsorship (33.3%), short duration of the course four (33.3%) and poor accommodation facility two (16.7%). However, trainees' suggested increase in training posts, four (33.3); training allowance three (25.0%); and incentives for trainers/training hospitals two (16.7%).\"]\n\nQuestion: Fulfilling human resources development goal in West Africa: can the training of ophthalmologist diplomates be improved?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The survey results indicate that while many trainees found the program well-structured and reported good clinical competence, several issues such as inadequate sponsorship, short course duration, and poor accommodation were identified. Additionally, trainees provided constructive suggestions for improvement, including increased training posts and allowances, indicating room for enhancement. \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 531, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 597}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.4300999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_404", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The potential effects of binge drinking during pregnancy on child motor function have only been assessed in a few, small studies. We aimed to examine the effects of binge alcohol consumption during early pregnancy, including number of binge episodes and timing of binge drinking, on child motor function at age 5.', \"We performed a prospective follow-up study of 678 women and their children sampled from the Danish National Birth Cohort based on maternal alcohol consumption during pregnancy. At 5 years of age, the children were tested with the Movement Assessment Battery for Children. Parental education, maternal IQ, prenatal maternal smoking, the child's age at testing, sex of child, and tester were considered core confounders, while the full model also controlled for prenatal maternal average alcohol intake, maternal age and prepregnancy body mass index, parity, home environment, postnatal parental smoking, health status, participation in organized sport, and indicators for hearing and vision impairment.\", 'There were no systematic or significant differences in motor function between children of mothers reporting isolated episodes of binge drinking and children of mothers with no binge episodes. No association was observed with respect to the number of binge episodes (maximum of 12) and timing of binge drinking.']\n\nQuestion: Does binge drinking during early pregnancy increase the risk of psychomotor deficits?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no systematic or significant differences in motor function between children of mothers who binge drank during early pregnancy and those who did not. It also found no association based on the number or timing of binge episodes. Therefore, the results suggest that isolated binge drinking during early pregnancy does not increase the risk of psychomotor deficits.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 337, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 408}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.1027e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_405", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Desmopressin releases tissue-type plasminogen activator, which augments cardiopulmonary bypass--associated hyperfibrinolysis, causing excessive bleeding. Combined use of desmopressin with prior administration of the antifibrinolytic drug tranexamic acid may decrease fibrinolytic activity and might improve postoperative hemostasis.', 'This prospective randomized study was carried out with 100 patients undergoing coronary artery bypass operations between April 1999 and November 2000 in G\u00fclhane Military Medical Academy. Patients were divided into 2 groups. Desmopressin (0.3 microg/kg) was administrated just after cardiopulmonary bypass and after protamine infusion in group 1 (n = 50). Both desmopressin and tranexamic acid (before the skin incision at a loading dose of 10 mg/kg over 30 minutes and followed by 12 hours of 1 mg.kg(-1).h(-1)) were administrated in group 2 (n = 50).', 'Significantly less drainage was noted in group 2 (1010 +/- 49.9 mL vs 623 +/- 41.3 mL, P =.0001). Packed red blood cells were transfused at 2.1 +/- 0.5 units per patient in group 1 versus 0.9 +/- 0.3 units in group 2 (P =.0001). Fresh frozen plasma was transfused at 1.84 +/- 0.17 units per patient in group 1 versus 0.76 +/- 0.14 units in group 2 (P =.0001). Only 24% of patients in group 2 required donor blood or blood products compared with 74% of those in the isolated desmopressin group (group 1, P =.00001). Group 1 and group 2 findings were as follows: postoperative fibrinogen, 113 +/- 56.3 mg/dL versus 167 +/- 45.8 mg/dL (P =.0001); fibrin split product, 21.2 +/- 2.3 ng/mL versus 13.5 +/- 3.4 ng/mL (P =.0001); and postoperative hemoglobin level, 7.6 plus minus 1.2 g/dL versus 9.1 plus minus 1.2 g/dL (P =.0001).']\n\nQuestion: Does tranexamic acid reduce desmopressin-induced hyperfibrinolysis?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that patients receiving both desmopressin and tranexamic acid (group 2) had significantly lower fibrin split products (13.5 vs 21.2 ng/mL) and less bleeding compared to those receiving desmopressin alone, indicating reduced fibrinolytic activity. This suggests that tranexamic acid effectively counteracts desmopressin-induced hyperfibrinolysis. Therefore, the evidence supports that tranexamic acid reduces desmopressin-induced hyperfibrinolysis.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 656, "output_tokens": 117, "total_tokens": 773}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 5.8275999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_406", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The aim of this study was to investigate the influence of the pharmacokinetics of s.c. anti-TNF agents on the grade of US-detected synovitis in RA patients.', 'Fifty RA patients were prospectively recruited from the Biologic Therapy Unit of our hospital. Inclusion criteria were being in treatment with s.c. anti-TNF agents and having had neither changes in therapy nor local corticosteroid injections in the previous 3 months. Patients underwent clinical, laboratory [28-joint DAS (DAS28) and Simplified Disease Activity Index (SDAI)]and US assessment at two time points, i.e. at peak plasma drug concentration and at trough plasma drug concentration. US assessments were performed blindly to the anti-TNF agent, the administration time and the clinical and laboratory data. Twenty-eight joints were investigated for the presence and grade (0-3) of B-mode synovitis and synovial power Doppler signal. Global indices for B-mode synovitis (BSI) and Doppler synovitis (DSI) were calculated for 12 joints and for wrist-hand-ankle-foot joints. B-mode US remission was defined as a BSI<1 and Doppler US remission as a DSI<1.', 'There were no significant differences between the clinical, laboratory and B-mode and Doppler US parameters at peak time and trough time (P = 0.132-0.986). There were no significant differences between the proportion of patients with active disease and those in remission according to DAS28, SDAI, B-mode US and Doppler US at peak time and trough time assessments (P = 0.070-1).']\n\nQuestion: Does ultrasound-scored synovitis depend on the pharmacokinetics of subcutaneous anti-TNF agents in patients with rheumatoid arthritis?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant differences in ultrasound scores for synovitis between peak and trough plasma concentrations of subcutaneous anti-TNF agents. This indicates that the pharmacokinetic fluctuations do not meaningfully affect ultrasound-detected synovitis. Therefore, the evidence suggests that ultrasound-scored synovitis does not depend on the pharmacokinetics of these agents.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 463, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 540}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.0573e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_408", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The Pathway represents a longitudinal program for medical students, consisting of both domestic and international experiences with poor populations. A previous study reported no significant attitudinal changes toward the medically indigent between Pathway and non-Pathway students.', 'The purpose of this study was to investigate and differentiate the skills and attitudes of Pathway and non-Pathway students in working with culturally diverse populations by conducting quantitative and qualitative analyses.', 'Selected items from a cultural assessment were analyzed using independent t-tests and a proportional analysis using approximation of the binomial distribution. In addition, a qualitative assessment of non-Pathway and Pathway students was conducted.', 'A statistically significant difference was found at the end of Years 2, 3, and 4 regarding student confidence ratings, and qualitative results had similar findings.']\n\nQuestion: Global Longitudinal Pathway: has medical education curriculum influenced medical students' skills and attitudes toward culturally diverse populations?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found statistically significant differences in student confidence ratings at the end of Years 2, 3, and 4, and qualitative results supported these findings. This indicates that the Pathway curriculum had a measurable impact on students' skills and attitudes. Therefore, the evidence supports that the curriculum influenced medical students' skills and attitudes toward culturally diverse populations.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 262, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 337}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.6102e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_409", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The data analysis was conducted to describe the rate of unsuccessful copper T380A intrauterine device (IUD) insertions among women using the IUD for emergency contraception (EC) at community family planning clinics in Utah.', 'These data were obtained from a prospective observational trial of women choosing the copper T380A IUD for EC. Insertions were performed by nurse practitioners at two family planning clinics in order to generalize findings to the type of service setting most likely to employ this intervention. Adjuvant measures to facilitate difficult IUD insertions (cervical anesthesia, dilation, pain medication, and use of ultrasound guidance) were not utilized. The effect of parity on IUD insertion success was determined using exact logistic regression models adjusted for individual practitioner failure rates.', 'Six providers performed 197 IUD insertion attempts. These providers had a mean of 14.1 years of experience (range 1-27, S.D. \u00b112.5). Among nulliparous women, 27 of 138 (19.6%) IUD insertions were unsuccessful. In parous women, 8 of 59 IUD insertions were unsuccessful (13.6%). The adjusted odds ratio (aOR) showed that IUD insertion failure was more likely in nulliparous women compared to parous women (aOR=2.31, 95% CI 0.90-6.52, p=.09).']\n\nQuestion: Failed IUD insertions in community practice: an under-recognized problem?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The high failure rate of 19.6% in nulliparous women and 13.6% in parous women, despite providers having substantial experience, suggests that failed IUD insertions are relatively common, especially in women without a history of childbirth. The adjusted odds ratio indicates a trend toward higher failure in nulliparous women, though it was not statistically significant (p = .09). Given the notable failure rates in a real-world clinical setting, this issue may indeed be under-recognized.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 403, "output_tokens": 111, "total_tokens": 514}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.971299999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_410", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The range of injury severity that can be seen within the category of type II supracondylar humerus fractures (SCHFs) raises the question whether some could be treated nonoperatively. However, the clinical difficulty in using this approach lies in determining which type II SCHFs can be managed successfully without a surgical intervention.', 'We reviewed clinical and radiographic information on 259 pediatric type II SCHFs that were enrolled in a prospective registry of elbow fractures. The characteristics of the patients who were treated without surgery were compared with those of patients who were treated surgically. Treatment outcomes, as assessed by the final clinical and radiographic alignment, range of motion of the elbow, and complications, were compared between the groups to define clinical and radiographic features that related to success or failure of nonoperative management.', 'During the course of treatment, 39 fractures were found to have unsatisfactory alignment with nonoperative management and were taken for surgery. Ultimately, 150 fractures (57.9%) were treated nonoperatively, and 109 fractures (42.1%) were treated surgically. At final follow-up, outcome measures of change in carrying angle, range of motion, and complications did not show clinically significant differences between treatment groups. Fractures without rotational deformity or coronal angulation and with a shaft-condylar angle of>15 degrees were more likely to be associated with successful nonsurgical treatment. A scoring system was developed using these features to stratify the severity of the injury. Patients with isolated extension deformity, but none of the other features, were more likely to complete successful nonoperative management.']\n\nQuestion: Type II supracondylar humerus fractures: can some be treated nonoperatively?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}\n\nYes, some type II supracondylar humerus fractures can be treated nonoperatively. The study found that 57.9% of the fractures were successfully managed without surgery, particularly when there was no rotational deformity, no coronal angulation, and a shaft-condylar angle greater than 15 degrees. Outcomes between nonoperative and surgical groups were similar, supporting nonoperative management in selected cases.", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 431, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 523}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.9800999999999994e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_412", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['We examined whether invasive lung-specimen collection-to-treatment times for intensive care unit patients with suspected ventilator-associated pneumonia (VAP) differ with to the work shift during which specimens were collected. We compared weekday day shifts and off-hours (from 6:30 p.m. to 8:29 a.m. the next day for night shifts, from Saturday 1:00 p.m. to Monday 8:29 a.m. for weekends, and from 8:30 a.m. to 8:29 a.m. the following morning for public holidays).', 'Single-center, observational study in the intensive care unit in an academic teaching hospital.', '101 patients who developed 152 episodes of bacteriologically confirmed VAP.', 'Of the 152 VAP episodes 66 were diagnosed during off-hours. Neither more bronchoscopy complications nor more inappropriate initial antimicrobial treatments for patients were observed between day and off-hour shifts. Indeed, the overall time from brochoalveolar lavage to antibiotic administration was shorter for off-hours than day-shifts due to shorter specimen collection-to-antibiotic prescription times, but antibiotic prescription-to-administration times were the same.']\n\nQuestion: Does invasive diagnosis of nosocomial pneumonia during off-hours delay treatment?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that the time from bronchoalveolar lavage to antibiotic administration was shorter during off-hours compared to day shifts, primarily due to faster specimen collection-to-prescription times. There was no delay in treatment during off-hours, and no increase in complications or inappropriate treatments. Therefore, invasive diagnosis during off-hours does not delay treatment.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 344, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 418}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.1824e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_415", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Family medicine has aspired to train residents and conduct research in settings that closely resemble community practice. The purpose of this study was to compare the patient characteristics of the ambulatory teaching centers of a consortium of seven community-based university-affiliated family practice residency programs in northeast Ohio with the National Ambulatory Medical Care Survey (NAMCS) results for family physicians (FPs) and general practitioners (GPs).', 'Ninety-eight faculty and resident physicians at the residency training site of the Northeastern Ohio Universities College of Medicine collected data on all ambulatory patient visits (N = 1498) for one randomly chosen week between July 1, 1991, and June 30, 1992. We compared these data with patient visits reported in the 1990 NAMCS for FPs and GPs.', 'The residency training sites saw slightly more children, women, blacks, and Medicare and Medicaid patients. The most common reason for an office visit in both populations was an undifferentiated symptom. Fifteen of the top 20 \"reason for visit\" codes were identical, as were 14 of the top 20 diagnoses. More preventive and therapeutic services were offered or performed at our residency training sites but fewer diagnostic services were performed. There were fewer consultations requested at our residency training sites but similar hospitalization rates for patients. The mean duration of visit differed by only 1 minute.']\n\nQuestion: Does family practice at residency teaching sites reflect community practice?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data show strong similarities between residency teaching sites and community practice, including nearly identical top reasons for visits and diagnoses, similar hospitalization rates, and only a 1-minute difference in visit duration. Although there are some differences in patient demographics and service types, the overall pattern closely mirrors community practice. Therefore, the best answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 383, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 454}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.4293e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_416", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"Rising health care costs and the need to consolidate expertise in tertiary services have led to the centralisation of services. In the UK, the result has been that many rural maternity units have become midwife-led. A key consideration is that midwives have the skills to competently and confidently provide maternity services in rural areas, which may be geographically isolated and where the midwife may only see a small number of pregnant women each year. Our objective was to compare the views of midwives in rural and urban settings, regarding their competence and confidence with respect to 'competencies' identified as being those which all professionals should have in order to provide effective and safe care for low-risk women.\", 'This was a comparative questionnaire survey involving a stratified sample of remote and rural maternity units and an ad hoc comparison group of three urban maternity units in Scotland. Questionnaires were sent to 82 midwives working in remote and rural areas and 107 midwives working in urban hospitals with midwife-led units.', 'The response rate from midwives in rural settings was considerably higher (85%) than from midwives in the urban areas (60%). Although the proportion of midwives who reported that they were competent was broadly similar in the two groups, there were some significant differences regarding specific competencies. Midwives in the rural group were more likely to report competence for breech delivery (p = 0.001), while more urban midwives reported competence in skills such as intravenous fluid replacement (p<0.001) and initial and discharge examination of the newborn (p<0.001). Both groups reported facing barriers to continuing professional development; however, more of the rural group had attended an educational event within the last month (p<0.001). Lack of time was a greater barrier for urban midwives (p = 0.02), whereas distance to training was greater for rural midwives (p = 0.009). Lack of motivation or interest was significantly higher in urban units (p = 0.006).']\n\nQuestion: Midwives' competence: is it affected by working in a rural location?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found significant differences in specific competencies between rural and urban midwives, with rural midwives more likely to report competence in breech delivery and urban midwives in other skills like intravenous fluid replacement. This indicates that working location influences the development of certain competencies. Therefore, midwives' competence is affected by working in a rural location.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 517, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 593}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.4306999999999994e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_424", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Recently, there has been increasing interest in the role of \"treatment as prevention\" (TasP). Some of the questions regarding TasP strategies arise from the perceived difficulties in achieving and maintaining viral load (VL) suppression over time and the risk of emergence of viral resistance that could compromise future treatment options. This study was conducted to assess these questions in a resource-limited setting.', 'We performed a retrospective observational study of HIV-infected patients diagnosed in the pre-HAART era on follow-up at a private center from Buenos Aires, Argentina. Socio-demographic, clinical, and laboratory data were extracted from clinical charts. Analyses were performed to test for potential associations of selected variables with current virologic failure or use of third-line drugs.', 'Of 619 patients on follow-up, 82 (13.2%) were diagnosed in the pre-HAART era. At the time of our study, 79 (96.3%) patients were on HAART, with a median duration of 14 years (IQR 12-15) of therapy, and exposure to mono or dual nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors regimens in 47.8% of cases.\\xa0Sixty-nine patients (87.3%) had undetectable VL, 37 (46.8%) never presented virologic failure, and 19 (24.1%) experienced only one failure. Thirteen patients (16.5%) were receiving third-line ART regimens, with an average of 2.7-fold more virologic failures than those on first- or second-line regimens (p = 0.007).']\n\nQuestion: Treatment as prevention in resource-limited settings: is it feasible to maintain HIV viral load suppression over time?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that 87.3% of HIV patients, including those from the pre-HAART era, achieved undetectable viral loads after a median of 14 years on therapy, indicating sustained viral suppression is possible even in a resource-limited setting. Despite prior use of less effective regimens, most patients did well on modern HAART, supporting the feasibility of treatment as prevention. Therefore, the evidence suggests a positive outlook for long-term viral suppression.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 449, "output_tokens": 100, "total_tokens": 549}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.1879e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_429", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To describe clinical characteristics of oral mucoceles/ranulas, with a focus on human immunodeficiency virus (HIV)-related salivary gland diseases.', 'A descriptive and clinical study, with review of patient data.', 'We reviewed 113 referred cases of oral mucocele. The following anatomical sites were identified: lip, tongue, and floor of the mouth (simple ranulas), as well as plunging ranulas. The age and gender data of the patients with oral mucoceles were recorded. The HIV status of the patients and other information were reviewed.', 'There were 30 (26.5%) males and 83 (73.5%) females. Most patients were below 30 years of age, with the peak frequency in the first and second decade. Ranula (simple and plunging) represented 84.1% of the mucocele locations. Mucocele on the lips represented 10.6%. Seventy-two (63.7%) patients were HIV positive; and 97.2% of them had ranulas. Thirty-eight (33.6%) patients presented with plunging ranulas; and 92.1% of them were HIV positive, compared with two patients presenting with plunging ranulas in the HIV-negative group. These results strongly suggest that an HIV-positive patient is statistically (P<0.001) more at risk of presenting with not only a simple, but also a plunging ranula type.']\n\nQuestion: Oral mucocele/ranula: Another human immunodeficiency virus-related salivary gland disease?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that 72 out of 113 patients (63.7%) with oral mucoceles were HIV positive, and 97.2% of those had ranulas. Additionally, 92.1% of patients with plunging ranulas were HIV positive, showing a statistically significant association (P<0.001). These findings strongly support that oral mucocele/ranula is associated with HIV, suggesting it as another HIV-related salivary gland disease.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 414, "output_tokens": 111, "total_tokens": 525}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.0494e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_433", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To examine the relationship between exposure to pro-smoking messages in media and susceptibility to smoking adoption among middle school students. The hypothesis that parental restriction of R-rated movie viewing is associated with lower adolescent smoking susceptibility was tested.', 'A sample of 1687 6th-, 7th-, and 8th-grade students from four Wisconsin middle schools were surveyed about their use of cigarettes, exposure to smoking in media, their views of smoking, and peer smoking behaviors.', 'An index of smoking susceptibility was created using measures of cigarette use and future intention to smoke. A zero-order correlation for parental restriction of R-rated movie viewing and smoking susceptibility showed a strong association (r = -.36, p<.001). A hierarchical logistic regression yielded odds ratios (ORs) for being susceptible to or having tried smoking for three levels of parental R-rated movie restriction. Results show that compared to full restriction, respondents with partial or no restriction were more likely to be susceptible to smoking (partial restriction: OR = 2.1, 95% CI = 1.5-2.8; no restriction: OR = 3.3, 95% CI = 2.3-4.6), when controlling for demographic factors, and family and friend smoking. Analyses using a measure of smoking prevalence as the dependent variable yielded similar results (partial restriction: OR = 1.5, 95% CI = 1.0-2.2; no restriction: OR = 2.5, 95% CI = 1.7-3.7).']\n\nQuestion: Cigarettes and cinema: does parental restriction of R-rated movie viewing reduce adolescent smoking susceptibility?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found a significant inverse relationship between parental restriction of R-rated movie viewing and adolescent smoking susceptibility, with lower restriction associated with higher susceptibility. The odds ratios indicate that partial or no restriction increases the likelihood of smoking susceptibility, even after controlling for other factors. Therefore, the evidence supports that parental restriction is associated with reduced smoking susceptibility.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 424, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 496}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.7303999999999994e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_435", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To determine whether betamethasone (BM) reduces the cochlear toxicity of otic gentamicin (GM) if given together.', 'Controlled animal study.', 'Thirty-four mice were assigned at random to receive intratympanic injections of either 0.1 % BM (11 mice), 0.3% GM (13 mice), or a combination of both (GM/BM) with benzalkonium chloride (10 mice) in the left ear (treated) and saline on the right (untreated). Six injections were given on alternate days. Auditory brainstem response thresholds were assessed at 1 month, 2 months, and>2 months.', 'There was a significantly greater degree of hearing loss in the BM-treated ears compared to the untreated ears (6.48 dB hearing loss, P = .007) and in the GM-treated ears compared to untreated ears (6.59 dB hearing loss, P = .010,). However, otic GM/BM and benzalkonium chloride did not cause significant additional hearing loss compared with the untreated ears (3.56 dB hearing loss, P = .242).']\n\nQuestion: Steroids in aminoglycoside-containing ear drops: do they reduce cochlear toxicity?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that while both betamethasone and gentamicin individually caused significant hearing loss, the combination of the two did not result in significant additional hearing loss compared to untreated ears. This suggests that the presence of the steroid in the combination treatment mitigated the toxicity observed with the individual agents. Therefore, the most likely answer is yes.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 331, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 401}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:25.085950+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00018775, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_437", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['This study investigated associations between the performance of dental students in each of the three components of the selection procedure [academic average, Undergraduate Medicine and Health Sciences Admission Test (UMAT) and structured interview], socio-demographic characteristics and their academic success in an undergraduate dental surgery programme.', 'Longitudinal review of admissions data relating to students entering dental education at the University of Otago, New Zealand, between 2004 and 2009 was compared with academic performance throughout the dental programme.', 'After controlling for variables, pre-admission academic average, UMAT scores and interview performance did not predict performance as a dental student. Class place in second year, however, was a strong predictor of class place in final year. Multivariate analysis demonstrated that the best predictors of higher class placement in the final year were New Zealand European ethnicity and domestic (rather than international) student status. Other socio-demographic characteristics were not associated with performance. These interim findings provide a sound base for the ongoing study.']\n\nQuestion: Does performance in selection processes predict performance as a dental student?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that after controlling for variables, pre-admission academic average, UMAT scores, and interview performance did not predict academic performance in the dental program. Instead, class placement in the second year was a strong predictor of final-year performance. Therefore, the selection process components were not predictive of later success.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 292, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 359}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.7431999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_44", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Studies have shown that schizophrenia patients have motion perception deficit, which was thought to cause eye-tracking abnormality in schizophrenia. However, eye movement closely interacts with motion perception. The known eye-tracking difficulties in schizophrenia patients may interact with their motion perception.', 'Two speed discrimination experiments were conducted in a within-subject design. In experiment 1, the stimulus duration was 150 msec to minimize the chance of eye-tracking occurrence. In experiment 2, the duration was increased to 300 msec, increasing the possibility of eye movement intrusion. Regular eye-tracking performance was evaluated in a third experiment.', 'At 150 msec, speed discrimination thresholds did not differ between schizophrenia patients (n = 38) and control subjects (n = 33). At 300 msec, patients had significantly higher thresholds than control subjects (p = .03). Furthermore, frequencies of eye tracking during the 300 msec stimulus were significantly correlated with speed discrimination in control subjects (p = .01) but not in patients, suggesting that eye-tracking initiation may benefit control subjects but not patients. The frequency of eye tracking during speed discrimination was not significantly related to regular eye-tracking performance.']\n\nQuestion: Is motion perception deficit in schizophrenia a consequence of eye-tracking abnormality?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The results show that at 150 msec (minimizing eye movement), there was no difference in speed discrimination between patients and controls, suggesting intact motion perception without eye-tracking interference. However, at 300 msec (with more eye movement), patients performed worse, and their eye-tracking frequency did not correlate with improved discrimination, unlike controls. This implies that motion perception deficits emerge with eye movement, but are not solely caused by eye-tracking abnormalities, as the two are not directly linked in patients.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 334, "output_tokens": 108, "total_tokens": 442}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.4513999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_441", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The objectives were to identify prognostic factors for the survival of children with cerebellar astrocytoma, and to evaluate the reproducibility and prognostic value of histological sub-classification and grading.', 'Children aged 0-14 years treated in Denmark for a cerebellar astrocytoma in the period 1960-1984 were included and followed until January 2001 or until their death. The histological specimens from each patient were reviewed for revised grading and classification according to three different classification schemes: the WHO, the Kernohan and the Daumas-Duport grading systems.', 'The overall survival rate was 81% after a follow-up time of 15-40 years. The significant positive prognostic factors for survival were \"surgically gross-total removal\" of the tumour at surgery and location of the tumour in the cerebellum proper as opposed to location in the fourth ventricle. No difference in survival time was demonstrated when we compared pilocytic astrocytoma and fibrillary astrocytoma. Moreover, we found that the Kernohan and the WHO classification systems had no predictive value and that the Daumas-Duport system is unsuitable as a prognostic tool for low-grade posterior fossa astrocytomas.']\n\nQuestion: Sub-classification of low-grade cerebellar astrocytoma: is it clinically meaningful?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that histological sub-classification and grading systems (WHO, Kernohan, and Daumas-Duport) had no significant prognostic value for survival in children with low-grade cerebellar astrocytoma. There was no difference in survival between pilocytic and fibrillary astrocytomas, and the classification systems were deemed unsuitable as prognostic tools. Therefore, sub-classification does not appear to be clinically meaningful.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 370, "output_tokens": 97, "total_tokens": 467}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.5969999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_442", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The CLASS Act, which was part of the Affordable Care Act of 2010, established a voluntary personal assistance services (PAS) insurance program. However, concerns about enrollment and adverse selection led to repeal of the CLASS Act in\\xa02013.', 'To estimate the number of middle-aged adults interested in purchasing PAS insurance, the sociodemographic, socioeconomic and disability attributes of this population, and the maximum monthly premium they would be willing to pay for such coverage.', 'A total of 13,384 adults aged 40-65 answered questions about their interest in PAS insurance in the 2011 Sample Adult National Health Interview Survey. We applied survey weights for the U.S. population and conducted logistic regression analyses to identify personal factors associated with interest in paying for the CLASS program.', 'An estimated 25.8 million adults aged 40-65 (26.7%) said they would be interested in paying for a public insurance program to cover PAS benefits. However, interest in PAS insurance varied by age, race, ethnicity, region, income, disability status, and family experience with ADL assistance. Only 1.6 million adults aged 40-65 (1.8%) said they would be willing to pay $100 per month or more for coverage.']\n\nQuestion: After CLASS--Is a voluntary public insurance program a realistic way to meet the long-term support and service needs of adults with disabilities?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The low willingness to pay a substantial monthly premium\u2014only 1.8% of middle-aged adults were willing to pay $100 or more\u2014suggests limited public support for a voluntary public insurance program like the CLASS Act. Combined with prior concerns about adverse selection and sustainability, this indicates such a model may not adequately meet long-term needs. Therefore, a voluntary program appears unrealistic as a comprehensive solution.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 378, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 465}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.5538e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_445", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To test if secular growth acceleration occurs during fetal life.', \"ANOVA Kruskal-Wallis and Mann-Whitney U-test have been used for the biometric characteristics comparison of nowadays fetal population with those three decades ago and to test the hypothesis about the existence of secular growth acceleration during fetal life. For this purpose, we first calculated mean values of particular biometric parameters for the whole pregnancy. During the period 2002-2009 biparietal diameter, fetal length and abdominal circumference measurements in singleton uncomplicated pregnancies between 22 and 41 gestational weeks were obtained. Gestational age was estimated according to Naegele's rule and confirmed with an early ultrasound examination. Pregnancies with fetal cromosomopathies and malformations were excluded as well as those resulting in perinatal death.\", 'There were no statistically significant differences of the examined fetal biometric parameters measured by ultrasound between contemporary fetal population and those from 35 years ago.']\n\nQuestion: The secular growth acceleration: does it appear during fetal life?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study compared fetal biometric parameters from the period 2002\u20132009 with those from 35 years earlier and found no statistically significant differences. This indicates that there is no evidence of secular growth acceleration during fetal life. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 291, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 353}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.6860999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_446", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"To investigate whether the presence of hippocampal atrophy (HCA) on MRI in Alzheimer's disease (AD) leads to a more rapid decline in cognitive function. To investigate whether cognitively unimpaired controls and depressed subjects with HCA are at higher risk than those without HCA of developing dementia.\", 'A prospective follow-up of subjects from a previously reported MRI study.', 'Melbourne, Australia.', 'Five controls with HCA and five age-matched controls without HCA, seven depressed subjects with HCA and seven without HCA, and 12 subjects with clinically diagnosed probable AD with HCA and 12 without HCA were studied. They were followed up at approximately 2 years with repeat cognitive testing, blind to initial diagnosis and MRI result.', 'HCA was rated by two radiologists blind to cognitive test score results. Cognitive assessment was by the Cambridge Cognitive Examination (CAMCOG).', 'No significant differences in rate of cognitive decline, mortality or progression to dementia were found between subjects with or without HCA.']\n\nQuestion: Does hippocampal atrophy on MRI predict cognitive decline?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant differences in the rate of cognitive decline between subjects with or without hippocampal atrophy (HCA). This was observed across controls, depressed individuals, and those with Alzheimer's disease. Therefore, based on this study, HCA does not predict cognitive decline.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 301, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 363}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.7570999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_447", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The present study aims to evaluate benefit of adding surgery to chemoradiotherapy alone in management of carcinoma esophagus.', 'We retrospectively analyzed 45 eligible patients of squamous cell esophageal carcinoma which were enrolled from February 2008 to April 2009. All patients were treated with chemoradiotherapy (50.40 Gy with 40 mg/m(2) of weekly cisplatin). Tumor response was assessed after 6 weeks of treatment. Patients with resectable disease were subjected to surgical resection (arm A) and remaining was kept on regular clinical follow-up (arm B). Overall survival (OS) was selected as the primary endpoint. The secondary end points were disease-free survival (DFS) and clinical toxicities.', 'Median follow-up was 13.6 months. Pathological complete response was seen in 60.9 % patients in arm A. In arm B, 77.3 % patients attained radiological complete response (p\\u2009=\\u20090.194). The median OS was 16.4 and 19.1 months (p\\u2009=\\u20090.388) and median DFS was 5.8 and 4.1 months (p\\u2009=\\u20090.347) in arm A and B, respectively. The 2-year survival probability was 39.1 and 36.4 % (p\\u2009=\\u20090.387) in arm A and B, respectively. The recurrence probability was 56.5 % (SE\\u2009=\\u20095.6 %) and 45.5 % (SE\\u2009=\\u20094.2 %) (p\\u2009=\\u20090.328) in arm A and B, respectively. The probability of loco regional recurrence was more in arm B than in arm A (p\\u2009=\\u20090.002).']\n\nQuestion: Chemoradiotherapy in the management of locally advanced squamous cell carcinoma esophagus: is surgical resection required?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no statistically significant difference in overall survival or disease-free survival between patients who underwent surgical resection and those who did not. While loco-regional recurrence was lower in the surgery group, the overall outcomes suggest that surgery may not be strictly required for all patients. Therefore, the most likely answer based on the provided data is that it is not definitively required.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 554, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 633}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:31.741041+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000257, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_448", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['We compared left ventricular regional wall motion, the global left ventricular ejection fraction, and the New York Heart Association functional class pre- and postoperatively.', 'Endomyocardial fibrosis is characterized by fibrous tissue deposition in the endomyocardium of the apex and/or inflow tract of one or both ventricles. Although left ventricular global systolic function is preserved, patients exhibit wall motion abnormalities in the apical and inferoapical regions. Fibrous tissue resection in New York Heart Association FC III and IV endomyocardial fibrosis patients has been shown to decrease morbidity and mortality.', 'We prospectively studied 30 patients (20 female, 30+/-10 years) before and 5+/-8 months after surgery. The left ventricular ejection fraction was determined using the area-length method. Regional left ventricular motion was measured by the centerline method. Five left ventricular segments were analyzed pre- and postoperatively. Abnormality was expressed in units of standard deviation from the mean motion in a normal reference population.', 'Left ventricular wall motion in the five regions did not differ between pre- and postoperative measurements. Additionally, the left ventricular ejection fraction did not change after surgery (0.45+/-0.13% x 0.43+/-0.12% pre- and postoperatively, respectively). The New York Heart Association functional class improved to class I in 40% and class II in 43% of patients postoperatively (p<0.05).']\n\nQuestion: Does quantitative left ventricular regional wall motion change after fibrous tissue resection in endomyocardial fibrosis?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The passage states that \"Left ventricular wall motion in the five regions did not differ between pre- and postoperative measurements,\" indicating no change in regional wall motion after surgery. This is further supported by the lack of significant change in ejection fraction. Therefore, the quantitative left ventricular regional wall motion does not change after fibrous tissue resection.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 489, "output_tokens": 102, "total_tokens": 591}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.4918999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_45", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['We have previously reported the feasibility of diagnostic and therapeutic peritoneoscopy including liver biopsy, gastrojejunostomy, and tubal ligation by an oral transgastric approach. We present results of per-oral transgastric splenectomy in a porcine model. The goal of this study was to determine the technical feasibility of per-oral transgastric splenectomy using a flexible endoscope.', 'We performed acute experiments on 50-kg pigs. All animals were fed liquids for 3 days prior to procedure. The procedures were performed under general anesthesia with endotracheal intubation. The flexible endoscope was passed per orally into the stomach and puncture of the gastric wall was performed with a needle knife. The puncture was extended to create a 1.5-cm incision using a pull-type sphincterotome, and a double-channel endoscope was advanced into the peritoneal cavity. The peritoneal cavity was insufflated with air through the endoscope. The spleen was visualized. The splenic vessels were ligated with endoscopic loops and clips, and then mesentery was dissected using electrocautery.', 'Endoscopic splenectomy was performed on six pigs. There were no complications during gastric incision and entrance into the peritoneal cavity. Visualization of the spleen and other intraperitoneal organs was very good. Ligation of the splenic vessels and mobilization of the spleen were achieved using commercially available devices and endoscopic accessories.']\n\nQuestion: Transgastric endoscopic splenectomy: is it possible?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study successfully performed transgastric endoscopic splenectomy in six pigs using a flexible endoscope, with no complications during access and successful ligation of splenic vessels. The procedure demonstrated good visualization and technical feasibility in a porcine model. Therefore, based on the provided context, the answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 407, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 476}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.5796999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_450", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To determine the effect of occupational exposure in a nuclear power plant in Griefswald, Germany on male and female fecundity.', 'The frequency of men and women exposed to ionizing radiation through work in a nuclear power plant among 270 infertile couples was retrospectively compared to a control fertile population using a pair-matched analysis. The total cumulative equivalent radiation dose was determined. In addition, the spermiograms of the male partners in both groups were compared and correlated to the degree of exposure.', 'No differences were noted in the frequency of nuclear power plant exposure between sterile and fertile groups. There was a higher rate of anomalous spermiograms in nuclear power plant workers. However, abnormalities were temporary. No correlation was found between the cumulative equivalent radiation dose and abnormal spermiograms.']\n\nQuestion: Does occupational nuclear power plant radiation affect conception and pregnancy?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no difference in the frequency of nuclear power plant exposure between infertile and fertile groups, and no correlation between cumulative radiation dose and abnormal spermiograms. Although there was a higher rate of temporary sperm abnormalities, these did not translate into reduced fertility. Therefore, the evidence suggests occupational radiation exposure in this context does not significantly affect conception and pregnancy.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 327, "output_tokens": 117, "total_tokens": 444}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.4917000000000005e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_451", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"Lower limb compartment syndrome has been reported to occur after colorectal, urological, and gynecological procedures during which the patient's lower limbs are elevated for prolonged periods of time.\", 'We investigated lower limb perfusion in a group of patients undergoing prolonged pelvic surgery both during and immediately after surgery, using intra-arterial blood pressure monitoring, laser doppler flowmetry, and pulse oximetry.', 'Use of the modified lithotomy position was not associated with any demonstrable decrease in lower limb perfusion. The addition of 15 degrees head-down tilt, however, during pelvic dissection, led to an immediate and significant drop in lower limb perfusion (P<0.05; Mann-Whitney U test). The subgroup of patients analyzed postoperatively showed a ten-fold increase (P<0.01) in perfusion that was confined to the muscle compartment with no demonstrable increase in skin perfusion or intra-arterial pedal blood pressure.']\n\nQuestion: Lloyd-Davies position with Trendelenburg--a disaster waiting to happen?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context indicates that the addition of a 15-degree head-down tilt (Trendelenburg) during pelvic surgery caused a significant drop in lower limb perfusion, increasing the risk of compartment syndrome. Although the modified lithotomy position (similar to Lloyd-Davies) alone did not reduce perfusion, the combination with Trendelenburg had adverse effects. Therefore, the combination poses a notable risk, suggesting a potential disaster.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 292, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 383}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.9832e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_454", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['This study investigated whether the time from emergency room registration to appendectomy (ETA) would affect the incidence of perforation and postoperative complications in patients with acute appendicitis.', 'Patients who underwent an appendectomy at the Ren-Ai branch of Taipei City Hospital between January 2010 and October 2012 were retrospectively reviewed. Their demographics, white blood cell count, C-reactive protein, body temperature, computed tomography scan usage, operation method, pathology report, postoperative complication, length of hospital stay, and ETA were abstracted. Multivariate analysis was performed to search the predictors, including ETA, of outcomes for the perforation and postoperative complication rates.', 'A total of 236 patients were included in the study. Perforation occurred in 12.7% (30/236) and postoperative complications developed in 24.1% (57/236) of these patients. There were 121 patients with ETA<8 hours, 88 patients with ETA of 8-24 hours, and 27 patients with ETA>24 hours; patients with ETA>24 hours had significantly longer hospital stay. Univariate analysis showed that perforated patients were significantly older, and had higher C-reactive protein level, longer hospital stay, and higher complication rate. Patients who developed postoperative complications were significantly older, and had higher neutrophil count, less use of computed tomography, and higher open appendectomy rate. After multivariate analysis, age \u226555 years was the only predictor for perforation [odds ratio (OR) = 3.65; 95% confidence interval (CI), 1.54-8.68]; for postoperative complications, age \u226555 years (OR = 1.65; 95% CI, 1.84-3.25), perforated appendicitis (OR = 3.17; 95% CI, 1.28-7.85), and open appendectomy (OR = 3.21; 95% CI, 1.36-7.58) were associated. ETA was not a significant predictor in both analyses.']\n\nQuestion: Appendectomy timing: Will delayed surgery increase the complications?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that time from emergency room registration to appendectomy (ETA) was not a significant predictor of perforation or postoperative complications after multivariate analysis. Although delayed surgery (ETA >24 hours) was associated with longer hospital stay, it did not independently increase complication rates. Therefore, based on the study's results, delayed surgery does not appear to increase complications.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 561, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 642}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.7931e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_455", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Vitamin D deficiency/insufficiency (VDDI) is common in CKD patients and may be associated with abnormal mineral metabolism. It is not clear whether the K/DOQI recommended doses of ergocalciferol are adequate for correction of VDDI and hyperparathyroidism.', 'Retrospective study of 88 patients with CKD Stages 1 - 5 and baseline 25-hydroxyvitamin D level<30 ng/ml (<75 nmol/l). Patients treated with ergocalciferol as recommended by K/DOQI guidelines. Only 53 patients had elevated baseline PTH level for the CKD stage. Patients were excluded if they received vitamin D preparations other than ergocalciferol or phosphate binders. 25-hydroxyvitamin D level, intact PTH level (iPTH), and other parameters of mineral metabolism were measured at baseline and after completion of ergocalciferol course.', '88 patients with CKD were treated with ergocalciferol. Mean age 56.8 +/- 9.5 years and 41% were males. The mean (+/- SD) GFR was 28.3 +/- 16.6 ml/min. At the end of the 6-month period of ergocalciferol treatment, the mean 25-hydroxyvitamin D level increased from 15.1 +/- 5.8 to 23.3 +/- 11.8 ng/ml (37.75 +/- 14.5 to 58.25 +/- 29.5 nmol/l) (p<0.001). Treatment led to>or = 5 ng/ml (12.5 nmol/l) increases in 25-hydroxyvitamin D level in 54% of treated patients, and only 25% achieved levels>or = 30 ng/ml (75 nmol/l). Mean iPTH level decreased from 157.9 +/- 125.9 to 150.7 +/- 127.5 pg/ml (p = 0.5). Only 26% of patients had>or = 30% decrease in their iPTH level after treatment with ergocalciferol.']\n\nQuestion: Treatment of vitamin D deficiency in CKD patients with ergocalciferol: are current K/DOQI treatment guidelines adequate?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that only 25% of patients achieved sufficient 25-hydroxyvitamin D levels (\u226530 ng/ml) and only 26% had a significant reduction in iPTH levels despite treatment with ergocalciferol per K/DOQI guidelines. This suggests the recommended doses are insufficient for effectively correcting vitamin D deficiency and hyperparathyroidism in most CKD patients. Therefore, the current guidelines are likely inadequate.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 596, "output_tokens": 99, "total_tokens": 695}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 5.2215999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_456", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['As with some procedures, trauma fellowship training and greater surgeon experience may result in better outcomes following intramedullary nailing (IMN) of diaphyseal femur fractures. However, surgeons with such training and experience may not always be available to all patients. The purpose of this study is to determine whether trauma training affects the post-operative difference in femoral version (DFV) following IMN.', 'Between 2000 and 2009, 417 consecutive patients with diaphyseal femur fractures (AO/OTA 32A-C) were treated via IMN. Inclusion criteria for this study included complete baseline and demographic documentation as well as pre-operative films for fracture classification and post-operative CT scanogram (per institutional protocol) for version and length measurement of both the nailed and uninjured femurs. Exclusion criteria included bilateral injuries, multiple ipsilateral lower extremity fractures, previous injury, and previous deformity. Of the initial 417 subjects, 355 patients met our inclusion criteria. Other data included in our analysis were age, sex, injury mechanism, open vs. closed fracture, daytime vs. nighttime surgery, mechanism of injury, and AO and Winquist classifications. Post-operative femoral version of both lower extremities was measured on CT scanogram by an orthopaedic trauma fellowship trained surgeon. Standard univariate and multivariate analyses were performed to determine statistically significant risk factors for malrotation between the two cohorts.', 'Overall, 80.3% (288/355) of all fractures were fixed by trauma-trained surgeons. The mean post-operative DFV was 8.7\u00b0 in these patients, compared to 10.7\u00b0 in those treated by surgeons of other subspecialties. This difference was not statistically significant when accounting for other factors in a multivariate model (p>0.05). The same statistical trend was true when analyzing outcomes of only the more severe Winquist type III and IV fractures. Additionally, surgeon experience was not significantly predictive of post-operative version for either trauma or non-trauma surgeons (p>0.05 for both).']\n\nQuestion: Comparing femoral version after intramedullary nailing performed by trauma-trained and non-trauma trained surgeons: is there a difference?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that while trauma-trained surgeons had a lower mean post-operative difference in femoral version (8.7\u00b0 vs. 10.7\u00b0), this difference was not statistically significant after adjusting for other variables in a multivariate model. Additionally, surgeon experience and trauma training did not significantly predict outcomes, even in more severe fracture types. Therefore, there is no statistically significant difference.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 548, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 633}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.7408e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_457", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Multiple viruses are often detected in children with respiratory infection but the significance of co-infection in pathogenesis, severity and outcome is unclear.', 'To correlate the presence of viral co-infection with clinical phenotype in children admitted with acute respiratory infections (ARI).', 'We collected detailed clinical information on severity for children admitted with ARI as part of a Spanish prospective multicenter study (GENDRES network) between 2011-2013. A nested polymerase chain reaction (PCR) approach was used to detect respiratory viruses in respiratory secretions. Findings were compared to an independent cohort collected in the UK.', '204 children were recruited in the main cohort and 97 in the replication cohort. The number of detected viruses did not correlate with any markers of severity. However, bacterial superinfection was associated with increased severity (OR: 4.356; P-value = 0.005), PICU admission (OR: 3.342; P-value = 0.006), higher clinical score (1.988; P-value = 0.002) respiratory support requirement (OR: 7.484; P-value<0.001) and longer hospital length of stay (OR: 1.468; P-value<0.001). In addition, pneumococcal vaccination was found to be a protective factor in terms of degree of respiratory distress (OR: 2.917; P-value = 0.035), PICU admission (OR: 0.301; P-value = 0.011), lower clinical score (-1.499; P-value = 0.021) respiratory support requirement (OR: 0.324; P-value = 0.016) and oxygen necessity (OR: 0.328; P-value = 0.001). All these findings were replicated in the UK cohort.']\n\nQuestion: Does Viral Co-Infection Influence the Severity of Acute Respiratory Infection in Children?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that the number of detected viruses did not correlate with any markers of severity in children with acute respiratory infections. Instead, bacterial superinfection and lack of pneumococcal vaccination were associated with increased severity, not viral co-infection. Therefore, the evidence suggests viral co-infection does not influence severity.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 519, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 589}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.3849e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_459", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The role of early revascularization among patients with acute myocardial infarction complicated by cardiogenic shock remains controversial. Angioplasty registries, while suggesting a benefit, are subject to selection bias, and clinical trials have been underpowered to detect early benefits. If an invasive strategy is beneficial in this population, patients admitted to hospitals with onsite coronary revascularization might be expected to have a better prognosis. We sought to determine whether access to cardiovascular resources at the admitting hospital influenced the prognosis of patients with acute myocardial infarction complicated by cardiogenic shock.', 'By use of the Cooperative Cardiovascular Project database (a retrospective medical record review of Medicare patients discharged with acute myocardial infarction), we identified patients aged>or =65 years whose myocardial infarction was complicated by cardiogenic shock.', 'Of the 601 patients with cardiogenic shock, 287 (47.8%) were admitted to hospitals without revascularization services and 314 (52.2%) were admitted to hospitals with coronary angioplasty and coronary artery bypass surgery facilities. Clinical characteristics were similar across the subgroups. Patients admitted to hospitals with revascularization services were more likely to undergo coronary revascularization during the index hospitalization and during the first month after acute myocardial infarction. After adjustment for demographic, clinical, hospital, and treatment strategies, the presence of onsite revascularization services was not associated with a significantly lower 30-day (odds ratio 0.83, 95% CI 0.47, 1.45) or 1-year mortality (odds ratio 0.91, 95% CI 0.49, 1.72).']\n\nQuestion: Cardiogenic shock complicating acute myocardial infarction in elderly patients: does admission to a tertiary center improve survival?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that although patients admitted to hospitals with revascularization services were more likely to undergo revascularization, there was no significant difference in 30-day or 1-year mortality after adjusting for various factors. The odds ratios for mortality were close to 1 and the confidence intervals included 1, indicating no statistically significant benefit. Therefore, admission to a tertiary center with onsite revascularization services did not significantly improve survival.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 463, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 555}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.2073e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_46", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"Fournier's gangrene is known to have an impact in the morbidity and despite antibiotics and aggressive debridement, the mortality rate remains high.\", \"To assess the morbidity and mortality in the treatment of Fournier's gangrene in our experience.\", 'The medical records of 14 patients with Fournier\\'s gangrene who presented at the University Hospital Center \"Mother Teresa\" from January 1997 to December 2006 were reviewed retrospectively to analyze the outcome and identify the risk factor and prognostic indicators of mortality.', 'Of the 14 patients, 5 died and 9 survived. Mean age was 54 years (range from 41-61): it was 53 years in the group of survivors and 62 years in deceased group. There was a significant difference in leukocyte count between patients who survived (range 4900-17000/mm) and those died (range 20.300-31000/mm3). Mean hospital stay was about 19 days (range 2-57 days).']\n\nQuestion: It's Fournier's gangrene still dangerous?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context indicates that despite treatment with antibiotics and aggressive debridement, the mortality rate for Fournier's gangrene remains high, with 5 out of 14 patients dying in the reviewed cases. Elevated leukocyte count and older age were associated with higher mortality, showing its severity. Therefore, Fournier's gangrene is still dangerous.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 325, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 402}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.0774999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_460", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"Little is known about how information needs change over time in the early postpartum period or about how these needs might differ given socioeconomic circumstances. This study's aim was to examine women's concerns at the time of hospital discharge and unmet learning needs as self-identified at 4 weeks after discharge.\", 'Data were collected as part of a cross-sectional survey of postpartum health outcomes, service use, and costs of care in the first 4 weeks after postpartum hospital discharge. Recruitment of 250 women was conducted from each of 5 hospitals in Ontario, Canada (n = 1,250). Women who had given vaginal birth to a single live infant, and who were being discharged at the same time as their infant, assuming care of their infant, competent to give consent, and able to communicate in one of the study languages were eligible. Participants completed a self-report questionnaire in hospital; 890 (71.2%) took part in a structured telephone interview 4 weeks after hospital discharge.', 'Approximately 17 percent of participants were of low socioeconomic status. Breastfeeding and signs of infant illness were the most frequently identified concerns by women, regardless of their socioeconomic status. Signs of infant illness and infant care/behavior were the main unmet learning needs. Although few differences in identified concerns were evident, women of low socioeconomic status were significantly more likely to report unmet learning needs related to 9 of 10 topics compared with women of higher socioeconomic status. For most topics, significantly more women of both groups identified learning needs 4 weeks after discharge compared with the number who identified corresponding concerns while in hospital.']\n\nQuestion: Learning needs of postpartum women: does socioeconomic status matter?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that women of low socioeconomic status were significantly more likely to report unmet learning needs across most topics compared to those of higher socioeconomic status. Although concerns like breastfeeding and infant illness were common across groups, disparities in unmet needs were clear. This indicates that socioeconomic status does influence postpartum learning needs.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 539, "output_tokens": 102, "total_tokens": 641}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.8469e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_461", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Evaluate the capability of different Computed Tomography scanners to determine urinary stone compositions based on CT attenuation values and to evaluate potential differences between each model.', '241 human urinary stones were obtained and their biochemical composition determined. Four different CT scanners (Siemens, Philips, GEMS and Toshiba) were evaluated. Mean CT-attenuation values and the standard deviation were recorded separately and compared with a t-paired test.', 'For all tested CT scanners, when the classification of the various types of stones was arranged according to the mean CT-attenuation values and to the confidence interval, large overlappings between stone types were highlighted. The t-paired test showed that most stone types could not be identified. Some types of stones presented mean CT attenuation values significantly different from one CT scanner to another. At 80kV, the mean CT attenuation values obtained with the Toshiba Aquilion were significantly different from those obtained with the Siemens Sensation. On the other hand, mean values obtained with the Philips Brilliance were all significantly equal to those obtained with the Siemens Sensation and with the Toshiba Aquilion. At 120kV mean CT attenuation values of uric acid, cystine and struvite stones obtained with the Philips model are significantly different from those obtained with the Siemens and the Toshiba but equal to those obtained with the GE 64.']\n\nQuestion: Pitfalls in urinary stone identification using CT attenuation values: are we getting the same information on different scanner models?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found significant overlaps in CT attenuation values between different stone types and variations in measurements across scanner models, indicating inconsistency in stone identification. For example, at different kV settings, attenuation values for the same stone types varied significantly between manufacturers like Siemens, Toshiba, and Philips. This suggests that different scanners do not provide the same information.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 487, "output_tokens": 113, "total_tokens": 600}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.5876999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_463", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['A prerequisite for a hormonal influence on anal continence in women is the presence of hormone receptors in the tissues of the anal canal. Using immunohistochemical techniques, we demonstrated and localized estrogen and progesterone receptors (ER, PR) in tissue sections of the anal canal.', 'Thirty-five specimens of the anorectal region from 21 patients (14 women, seven men) were examined histologically for smooth muscle (present in specimens from ten females and in seven males), striated muscle (present in three females and five males), and perimuscular connective tissue (present in 12 females and seven males). Immunostaining for ER and PR was then performed by incubating with primary anti-ER and anti-PR antibody and visualization of specific antibody binding by the ABC technique with DAB as chromogen.', 'Positive staining for ER and PR was seen exclusively over cell nuclei. Estrogen receptors were found in the smooth muscle cells of the internal sphincter of all females (10/10) and in four of the seven males. Staining for ER was detected in the perimuscular connective tissue of all females (12/12) and in four of the seven males. No specific staining for ER or PR was found in the nuclei of striated muscle cells of the external sphincter in males or females (n = 8). In females, about 50% of the ER-positive tissues were also found to be positive for PR. Amongst the male patients, only one exhibited staining for PR, and this was confined to the smooth muscle.']\n\nQuestion: Immunohistochemical assessment of steroid hormone receptors in tissues of the anal canal. Implications for anal incontinence?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study demonstrates the presence of estrogen and progesterone receptors in the smooth muscle and connective tissue of the anal canal, particularly in women, suggesting a hormonal influence on anal continence. This implies that hormonal changes could affect tissue function and contribute to anal incontinence. Therefore, the immunohistochemical findings support a potential role for hormones in anal incontinence.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 427, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 508}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.8416999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_465", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To determine whether anginal episodes might be related to extremes of hypotension in patients with ischaemic heart disease taking drugs to treat angina and heart failure.', 'Observational study of patients with ischaemic heart disease attending an urban tertiary referral cardiology centre.', 'A selected patient population was enrolled, having: angina on one or more hypotensive cardiovascular medications; hypotension on clinic or ambulatory measurement; and a resting ECG suitable for ambulatory monitoring. Patients had echocardiography, ambulatory blood pressure monitoring, and Holter monitoring. Hypotension induced ischaemic (HII) events were defined as episodes of ST segment ischaemia occurring at least one minute after an ambulatory blood pressure measurement (systolic/diastolic) below 100/65 mm Hg during the day, or 90/50 mm Hg at night.', '25 suitable patients were enrolled, and 107 hypotensive events were documented. 40 ST events occurred in 14 patients, of which a quarter were symptomatic. Fourteen HII events occurred in eight patients, with 13 of the 14 preceded by a fall in diastolic pressure (median diastolic pressure 57.5 mm Hg, interquartile range 11, maximum 72 mm Hg, minimum 45 mm Hg), and six preceded by a fall in systolic pressure (chi(2) = 11.9, p<0.001). ST events were significantly associated with preceding hypotensive events (chi(2) = 40.2, p<0.0001). Patients with HII events were more frequently taking multiple hypotensive drug regimens (8/8 v 9/17, chi(2) = 5.54, p = 0.022).']\n\nQuestion: Hypotension in patients with coronary disease: can profound hypotensive events cause myocardial ischaemic events?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found a significant association between hypotensive events and subsequent ST segment ischaemia, with 14 hypotension-induced ischaemic (HII) events occurring after low blood pressure measurements. Most HII events were preceded by a drop in diastolic pressure, and patients on multiple hypotensive drugs were more likely to experience these events. This evidence supports a causal relationship in this population.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 504, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 593}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.4683999999999994e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_470", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Hypertension is one of the important contributing factors linked with both causation and development of kidney disease. It is a multifactorial, polygenic, and complex disorder due to interaction of several risk genes with environmental factors. The present study was aimed to explore genetic polymorphism in ACE-1 gene as a risk factor for CKD among hypertensive patients.', 'Three hundred patients were enrolled in the study. Ninety were hypertensive patients with CKD taken as cases, whereas 210 hypertensive patients without CKD were taken as controls. Demographic data including age, sex, Body mass index (BMI), and other risk factors were also recorded. DNA was extracted from blood by salting out method. Genotyping of ACE gene was done by PCR technique. All the statistical analysis was done by using Epi Info and SPSS version 16 software (SPSS Inc., Chicago, IL).', 'Mean age was higher in the control group (p\\u2009<\\u20090.05). Variables among two groups were compared out of which age, BMI, hemoglobin (Hb) was found to be statistically significant whereas other variables like systolic blood pressure, triglyceride and low-density lipoprotein were not. Blood urea and serum creatinine levels were statistically significant in the two genotypes (p\\u2009<\\u20090.05). Total and HDL cholesterol were statistically significant for DD genotype of ACE gene (OR\\u2009=\\u20091.42, 95% CI\\u2009=\\u20090.72-2.81). Similarly, the risk for CKD among hypertensive patients was also associated with D allele of ACE gene (OR\\u2009=\\u20091.25, 95% CI\\u2009=\\u20090.86-1.79).']\n\nQuestion: Does angiotensin-converting enzyme-1 (ACE-1) gene polymorphism lead to chronic kidney disease among hypertensive patients?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study suggests a potential association between the D allele of the ACE-1 gene and increased risk of CKD in hypertensive patients, with an odds ratio of 1.25, though the 95% confidence interval includes 1, indicating the result is not statistically significant. While there is a trend, the data does not provide conclusive evidence of a causal relationship. Therefore, the most accurate answer is that the evidence points to a possible link, but it is not definitive.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 522, "output_tokens": 103, "total_tokens": 625}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.736199999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_473", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['In recent years, biofeedback has become increasingly popular for its proven success in peak performance training - the psychophysiological preparation of athletes for high-stakes sport competitions, such as the Olympic games. The aim of this research was to test whether an 8-week period of exposure to biofeedback training could improve the psychophysiological control over competitive anxiety and enhance athletic performance in participating subjects.', 'Participants of this study were highly competent athletes, each training in different sport disciplines. The experimental group consisted of 18 athletes (4 women, 14 men), whereas the Control group had 21 athletes (4 women, 17 men). All athletes were between 16 and 34 years old. The biofeedback device, Nexus 10, was used to detect and measure the psychophysiological responses of athletes. Athletes from both groups (control and experimental) were subjected to stress tests at the beginning of the study and once again at its conclusion. In between, the experimental group received training in biofeedback techniques. We then calculated the overall percentage of athletes in the experimental group compared with those in the control group who were able to control respiration, skin conductance, heart rate, blood flow amplitude, heart rate variability, and heart respiration coherence. One year following completion of the initial study, we questioned athletes from the experimental group, to determine whether they continued to use these skills and if they could detect any subsequent enhancement in their athletic performance.', 'We demonstrated that a greater number of participants in the experimental group were able to successfully control their psychophysiological parameters, in comparison to their peers in the control group. Significant results (p<0.05) were noted in regulation of GSR following short stress test conditions (p = 0.037), in regulation of HR after exposure to STROOP stressor (p = 0.037), in regulation of GSR following the Math and GSR stressors (p = 0.033, p = 0.409) and in achieving HR - breathing coherence following the math stressor (p = 0.042).']\n\nQuestion: Can biofeedback training of psychophysiological responses enhance athletes' sport performance?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that athletes in the experimental group who received biofeedback training showed significantly better control over key psychophysiological parameters like heart rate and skin conductance under stress, compared to the control group. These improvements in physiological regulation are linked to better management of competitive anxiety, a known factor affecting athletic performance. Although direct performance metrics aren't detailed, the sustained use of skills and reported performance enhancements one year later support a positive effect.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 531, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 622}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.6800999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_475", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Alcohol-associated cues elicit craving in human addicts but little is known about craving mechanisms. Current animal models focus on relapse and this may confound the effect of environmental cues. OBJECTIVES. To develop a model to study the effects of environmental cues on alcohol consumption in animals not experiencing withdrawal or relapse.', 'Rats were trained to orally self-administer an alcohol (5% w/v)/saccharin (0.2%) solution 30 min a day for 20 days. After stable responding on a free choice between alcohol/saccharin and water, rats were exposed to 5, 10 or 15 min of alcohol-associated cues or 5 min of non-alcohol associated cues. The effect of a 5-min cue was measured after a 10-day break from training or pre-treatment with 0.03, 0.1 or 1 mg/kg naltrexone.', 'Rats given 5 min of alcohol-associated cues responded significantly more on the active lever (26% increase) and consumed more alcohol as verified by increased blood alcohol levels (8.9 mM versus control 7.5 mM). Ten or 15 min of cues did not change alcohol consumption and 5 min in a novel environment decreased response by 66%. After a 10-day break in training, 5 min of alcohol-associated cues still increased alcohol consumption (29% increase) and the cue effect could be dose-dependently blocked by naltrexone (143% decrease at 0.03 mg/kg).']\n\nQuestion: Cue-induced behavioural activation: a novel model of alcohol craving?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study demonstrates that alcohol-associated cues increase lever responding and alcohol consumption, even after a break, and this effect is modulated by naltrexone, suggesting cue-induced activation reflects craving. These findings support the development of a novel model specifically for studying craving, independent of withdrawal or relapse. Therefore, the answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 415, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 485}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.6465e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_476", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Influenza vaccination remains below the federally targeted levels outlined in Healthy People 2020. Compared to non-Hispanic whites, racial and ethnic minorities are less likely to be vaccinated for influenza, despite being at increased risk for influenza-related complications and death. Also, vaccinated minorities are more likely to receive influenza vaccinations in office-based settings and less likely to use non-medical vaccination locations compared to non-Hispanic white vaccine users.', 'To assess the number of \"missed opportunities\" for influenza vaccination in office-based settings by race and ethnicity and the magnitude of potential vaccine uptake and reductions in racial and ethnic disparities in influenza vaccination if these \"missed opportunities\" were eliminated.', 'National cross-sectional Internet survey administered between March 4 and March 14, 2010 in the United States.', 'Non-Hispanic black, Hispanic and non-Hispanic white adults living in the United States (N\\u2009=\\u20093,418).', 'We collected data on influenza vaccination, frequency and timing of healthcare visits, and self-reported compliance with a potential provider recommendation for vaccination during the 2009-2010 influenza season. \"Missed opportunities\" for seasonal influenza vaccination in office-based settings were defined as the number of unvaccinated respondents who reported at least one healthcare visit in the Fall and Winter of 2009-2010 and indicated their willingness to get vaccinated if a healthcare provider strongly recommended it. \"Potential vaccine uptake\" was defined as the sum of actual vaccine uptake and \"missed opportunities.\"', 'The frequency of \"missed opportunities\" for influenza vaccination in office-based settings was significantly higher among racial and ethnic minorities than non-Hispanic whites. Eliminating these \"missed opportunities\" could have cut racial and ethnic disparities in influenza vaccination by roughly one half.']\n\nQuestion: Can routine offering of influenza vaccination in office-based settings reduce racial and ethnic disparities in adult influenza vaccination?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data show that racial and ethnic minorities had significantly more \"missed opportunities\" for influenza vaccination in office-based settings compared to non-Hispanic whites, and eliminating these could reduce disparities by about half. This suggests that routinely offering vaccination during office visits would increase uptake among minorities and narrow the gap. Therefore, routine offering in these settings can reduce disparities.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 480, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 557}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.178e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_479", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The aim of this study was to determine whether postictal psychotic episodes (PIPE) are predictive of the development of interictal psychotic episodes (IPE).', 'This was a retrospective study of 18 consecutive adults with a partial seizure disorder and PIPE (study group) and 36 patients with a partial seizure disorder but without PIPE (control group). These two groups were compared with respect to the likelihood of developing IPE over an 8-year follow-up period and the variables operant in the development of IPE. Statistical analyses consisted of logistic regression models to identify the variables predictive of the development of IPE. Predictors included: number and location of ictal foci, seizure type, etiology, age at seizure onset, duration of seizure disorder, MRI abnormalities, and psychiatric history prior to the index video/EEG monitoring (other than PIPE).', 'Seven patients with PIPE and one control patient went on to develop an IPE. Predictors of IPE in univariate logistic regression analyses included a history of PIPE (P=0.006), male gender (P=0.028), and having bilateral ictal foci (P=0.048). Significance disappeared for all of these variables when they were entered into a multivariate analysis.']\n\nQuestion: Long-term significance of postictal psychotic episodes II. Are they predictive of interictal psychotic episodes?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The univariate analysis suggested that postictal psychotic episodes (PIPE) were associated with interictal psychotic episodes (IPE), but this significance disappeared in the multivariate analysis. This indicates that PIPE alone is not an independent predictor of IPE when other variables are considered. Therefore, the most accurate answer is that PIPE are not definitively predictive of IPE in the long term.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 364, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 447}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.4144e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_48", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"To determine the impact of Florida's Medicaid Demonstration 4 years post-implementation on per member per month (PMPM) Medicaid expenditures and whether receiving care through HMOs versus provider service networks (PSNs) in the Demonstration was associated with PMPM expenditures.DATA: Florida Medicaid claims from two fiscal years prior to implementation of the Demonstration (FY0405, FY0506) and the first four fiscal years after implementation (FY0607-FY0910) from two urban Demonstration counties and two urban non-Demonstration counties.\", 'A difference-in-difference approach was used to compare changes in enrollee expenditures before and after implementation of the Demonstration overall and specifically for HMOs and PSNs.', 'Claims data were extracted for enrollees in the Demonstration and non-Demonstration counties and collapsed into monthly amounts (N = 26,819,987 person-months).', 'Among SSI enrollees, the Demonstration resulted in lower increases in PMPM expenditures over time ($40) compared with the non-Demonstration counties ($186), with Demonstration PSNs lowering PMPM expenditures by $7 more than HMOs. Savings were also seen among TANF enrollees but to a lesser extent.']\n\nQuestion: Do provider service networks result in lower expenditures compared with HMOs or primary care case management in Florida's Medicaid program?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on the context, provider service networks (PSNs) in Florida's Medicaid Demonstration were associated with lower per member per month (PMPM) expenditures compared to HMOs, with PSNs reducing expenditures by $7 more than HMOs among SSI enrollees. This indicates a cost advantage for PSNs over HMOs in this setting. Therefore, the evidence supports that PSNs result in lower expenditures compared to HMOs.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 375, "output_tokens": 98, "total_tokens": 473}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.6425e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_481", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Physical examination to detect abdominal injuries has been considered unreliable in alcohol-intoxicated trauma patients. Computed tomography (CT) plays the primary role in these abdominal evaluations.', 'We reviewed medical records of all blunt trauma patients admitted to our trauma service from January 1, 1992, to March 31, 1998. Study patients had a blood alcohol level>or =80 mg/dL, Glasgow Coma Scale (GCS) score of 15, and unremarkable abdominal examination.', 'Of 324 patients studied, 317 (98%) had CT scans negative for abdominal injury. Abdominal injuries were identified in 7 patients (2%), with only 2 (0.6%) requiring abdominal exploration. A significant association was found between major chest injury and abdominal injury.']\n\nQuestion: Blunt trauma in intoxicated patients: is computed tomography of the abdomen always necessary?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that 98% of intoxicated blunt trauma patients with normal abdominal exams and a GCS of 15 had negative CT scans, and only 0.6% required abdominal exploration. This suggests that CT may not be necessary in all such patients, especially those without additional risk factors like major chest injury. Therefore, CT is not always necessary.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 268, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 347}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.6927999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_482", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To investigate the role of human T-lymphotrophic virus type I (HTLV-I) infection in four patients who developed slowly progressive myelopathy with abnormal MRI lesions in the cervical cord levels.', 'Clinical and neuroradiologic examinations were performed, and the odds that an HTLV-I-infected individual of specified genotype, age, and provirus load had HTLV-I-associated myelopathy (HAM)/tropical spastic paraparesis (TSP) were calculated.', 'Anti-HTLV-I antibodies were positive in both the serum and the CSF in all of the patients. Biopsied sample from spinal cord lesions showed inflammatory changes in Patient 1. Patient 2 had a demyelinating type of sensorimotor polyneuropathy. Two of the three patients examined showed high risk of developing HAM/TSP in virologic and immunologic aspects.']\n\nQuestion: Chronic progressive cervical myelopathy with HTLV-I infection: Variant form of HAM/TSP?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The presence of chronic progressive cervical myelopathy, positive anti-HTLV-I antibodies in serum and CSF, inflammatory changes in spinal cord biopsy, and high risk for HAM/TSP in virologic and immunologic assessments strongly suggest a variant form of HAM/TSP. Although some atypical features like polyneuropathy are present, the core clinical and laboratory findings align with HTLV-I-associated neurological disease. Therefore, the most likely answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 279, "output_tokens": 98, "total_tokens": 377}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.9608999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_483", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['It remains controversial whether there is a gender difference in survival of patients with resected non-small cell lung cancer.', 'We retrospectively analyzed 2770 patients (1689 men and 1081 women) with non-small cell lung cancer who underwent pulmonary resection between 1995 and 2005 at the National Cancer Center Hospital, Tokyo. A gender difference in survival was studied in all patients, in those divided according to histology or pathologic stage, and in propensity-matched gender pairs.', 'There were no differences in background, such as preoperative pulmonary function, operation procedures, or operative mortality. The proportions of adenocarcinoma and pathologic stage I in women were greater than those in men (93.6% vs 61.7% and 71.4% vs 58.6%, respectively) (P<.001). Overall 5-year survival of women was better than that of men (81% vs 70%, P<.001). In adenocarcinoma, the overall 5-year survival for women was better than that for men in pathologic stage I (95% vs 87%, P<.001) and in pathologic stage II or higher (58% vs 51%, P = .017). In non-adenocarcinoma, there was no significant gender difference in survival in pathologic stage I (P = .313) or pathologic stage II or higher (P = .770). The variables such as age, smoking status, histology, and pathologic stage were used for propensity score matching, and survival analysis of propensity score-matched gender pairs did not show a significant difference (P = .69).']\n\nQuestion: Gender difference in survival of resected non-small cell lung cancer: histology-related phenomenon?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that women had better survival than men in adenocarcinoma but not in non-adenocarcinoma, indicating that the survival difference is dependent on histology. This suggests the gender difference in survival is related to tumor histology. Therefore, the answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 474, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 538}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.005399999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_484", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Postoperative CSF fistulas were described in 16 of 198 patients (8%) who underwent spine surgery between 2009 and 2010. The choice of the therapeutic strategy was based on the clinical condition of the patients, taking into account the possibility to maintain the prone position continuously and the risk of morbidity due to prolonged bed rest. Six patients were treated conservatively (position prone for three weeks), ten patients were treated by positioning an external CSF lumbar drainage for ten days. The mean follow-up period was ten months.', 'All patients healed their wound properly and no adverse events were recorded. Patients treated conservatively were cured in a mean period of 30 days, while patients treated with CSF drainage were cured in a mean period of 10 days.']\n\nQuestion: Is lumbar drainage of postoperative cerebrospinal fluid fistula after spine surgery effective?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data show that patients treated with lumbar drainage healed in a mean of 10 days, compared to 30 days for conservative treatment, with no adverse events reported. This indicates a faster recovery time with lumbar drainage, suggesting it is effective. Therefore, the evidence supports its effectiveness.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 262, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 327}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.5101999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_487", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Surgical excision of ovarian endometriomas in patients desiring pregnancy has recently been criticized because of the risk of damage to healthy ovarian tissue and consequent reduction of ovarian reserve. A correct diagnosis in cases not scheduled for surgery is therefore mandatory in order to avoid unexpected ovarian cancer misdiagnosis. Endometriosis is often associated with high levels of CA125. This marker is therefore not useful for discriminating ovarian endometrioma from ovarian malignancy. The aim of this study was to establish if the serum marker CA72-4 could be helpful in the differential diagnosis between ovarian endometriosis and epithelial ovarian cancer.', 'Serums CA125 and CA72-4 were measured in 72 patients with ovarian endometriomas and 55 patients with ovarian cancer.', 'High CA125 concentrations were observed in patients with ovarian endometriosis and in those with ovarian cancer. A marked difference in CA72-4 values was observed between women with ovarian cancer (71.0%) and patients with endometriosis (13.8%) (P<0.0001).']\n\nQuestion: Is CA72-4 a useful biomarker in differential diagnosis between ovarian endometrioma and epithelial ovarian cancer?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found a significant difference in CA72-4 levels between patients with ovarian cancer (71.0% had high levels) and those with endometriosis (13.8% had high levels), with a p-value of less than 0.0001, indicating strong statistical significance. This suggests that CA72-4 can effectively differentiate between the two conditions. Therefore, CA72-4 is a useful biomarker in this context.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 339, "output_tokens": 102, "total_tokens": 441}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.4269e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_488", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Reconstruction of the joint line is crucial in total knee arthroplasty (TKA). A routine height of tibial cut to maintain the natural joint line may compromise the preservation of the PCL. Since the PCL footprint is not accessible prior to tibial osteotomy, it seems beneficial to identify a reliable extraarticular anatomic landmark for predicting the PCL footprint and being visible within standard TKA approach. The fibula head predicts reliably the location of PCL footprint; however, it is not accessible during TKA. The aim of this study now was to analyze whether the tibial tuberosity can serve as a reliable referencing landmark to estimate the PCL footprint height prior to tibial cut.', 'The first consecutive case series included 216 CR TKA. Standing postoperative lateral view radiographs were utilized to measure the vertical distance between tibial tuberosity and tibial osteotomy plane. In the second case series, 223 knee MRIs were consecutively analyzed to measure the vertical distance between tibial tuberosity and PCL footprint. The probability of partial or total PCL removal was calculated for different vertical distances between tibial tuberosity and tibial cutting surface.', 'The vertical distance between the tibial tuberosity and tibial cut averaged 24.7 \u00b1 4 mm. The average vertical distance from tibial tuberosity to proximal and to distal PCL footprint was found to be 22 \u00b1 4.4 and 16 \u00b1 4.4 mm, respectively. Five knees were considered at 50% risk of an entire PCL removal after CR TKA.']\n\nQuestion: Preservation of the PCL when performing cruciate-retaining TKA: Is the tibial tuberosity a reliable predictor of the PCL footprint location?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study concludes that the tibial tuberosity serves as a reliable referencing landmark to estimate the PCL footprint height, as evidenced by the consistent measurements obtained in both the radiographic and MRI analyses. Therefore, it is considered a reliable predictor for preserving the PCL during TKA.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 425, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 486}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:32.312703+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00019775, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_489", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To determine the effect of the 2008 English public antibiotic campaigns.', 'English and Scottish (acting as controls) adults aged>or = 15 years were questioned face to face about their attitudes to and use of antibiotics, in January 2008 (1888) before and in January 2009 (1830) after the antibiotic campaigns.', 'Among English respondents, there was a small increase in recollection of campaign posters (2009 23.7% versus 2008 19.2%; P = 0.03), but this increase was only 2.3% higher in England than in Scotland. We did not detect any improvement in either England or Scotland, or any differences between England and Scotland in the understanding of the lack of benefit of antibiotics for coughs and colds, and we found no improvement in antibiotic use. We detected a significant increase in respondents retaining leftover antibiotics. Over 20% reported discussing antibiotics with their general practitioner (GP) or nurse in the year to January 2009. The offer of a delayed antibiotic prescription was reported significantly more often by English respondents (19% versus 8% Scottish in 2009; P = 0.01), and English respondents were advised to use other remedies for coughs and colds significantly more often in the year to January 2009 (12.7% in 2009 versus 7.4% in 2008; P<0.001).']\n\nQuestion: The English antibiotic awareness campaigns: did they change the public's knowledge of and attitudes to antibiotic use?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context indicates that there was no improvement in the understanding of the lack of benefit of antibiotics for coughs and colds, and no change in antibiotic use in England after the campaigns. Although there was a small increase in campaign poster recall and discussions with GPs, overall knowledge and attitudes did not significantly improve. Therefore, the campaigns did not substantially change public knowledge or attitudes.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 427, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 508}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.8416999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_491", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Tacrolimus is a potent immunosuppressive drug used in organ transplantation. Because of its substantial toxic effects, narrow therapeutic index, and interindividual pharmacokinetic variability, therapeutic drug monitoring of whole-blood tacrolimus concentrations has been recommended. We investigated the comparability of the results of 2 immunoassay systems, affinity column-mediated immunoassay (ACMIA) and microparticle enzyme immunoassay (MEIA), comparing differences in the tacrolimus concentrations measured by the 2 methods in relation to the hematologic and biochemical values of hepatic and renal functions.', 'A total of 154 samples from kidney or liver transplant recipients were subjected to Dimension RxL HM with a tacrolimus Flex reagent cartilage for the ACMIA method and IMx tacrolimus II for the MEIA method.', 'Tacrolimus concentrations measured by the ACMIA method (n = 154) closely correlated with those measured by the MEIA method (r = 0.84). The Bland-Altman plot using concentration differences between the 2 methods and the average of the 2 methods showed no specific trends. The tacrolimus levels determined by both the MEIA method and the ACMIA method were not influenced by hematocrit levels, but the difference between the 2 methods (ACMIA - MEIA) tended to be larger in low hematocrit samples (P<.001).']\n\nQuestion: Is the affinity column-mediated immunoassay method suitable as an alternative to the microparticle enzyme immunoassay method as a blood tacrolimus assay?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The affinity column-mediated immunoassay (ACMIA) method shows a strong correlation with the microparticle enzyme immunoassay (MEIA) method (r = 0.84), and the Bland-Altman plot reveals no specific bias, indicating good agreement between the two methods. Although the difference between the methods increases slightly at low hematocrit levels, this does not broadly undermine the overall comparability. Therefore, ACMIA is suitable as an alternative to MEIA for tacrolimus monitoring.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 408, "output_tokens": 111, "total_tokens": 519}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.0067999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_497", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To explore the extent to which parent-adolescent emotional closeness, family conflict, and parental permissiveness moderate the association of puberty and alcohol use in adolescents (aged 10-14).', 'Cross-sectional survey of 7631 adolescents from 231 Australian schools. Measures included pubertal status, recent (30day) alcohol use, parent-adolescent emotional closeness, family conflict, parental permissiveness of alcohol use and peer alcohol use. The analysis was based on a two-level (individuals nested within schools) logistic regression model, with main effects entered first, and interaction terms added second.', 'The interaction of family factors and pubertal stage did not improve the fit of the model, so a main effect model of family factors and pubertal stage was adopted. There were significant main effects for pubertal stage with boys in middle puberty at increased odds of alcohol use, and girls in advanced puberty at increased odds of alcohol use.']\n\nQuestion: The association of puberty and young adolescent alcohol use: do parents have a moderating role?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that the interaction of family factors (emotional closeness, conflict, permissiveness) with pubertal stage did not improve the model fit, indicating no moderating effect. Instead, only main effects of puberty and family factors were observed, meaning parents did not significantly alter the association between puberty and alcohol use. Therefore, the evidence suggests parents do not have a moderating role.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 299, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 384}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.9729e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_499", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To investigate the importance of loss of consciousness (LOC) in predicting neuropsychological test performance in a large sample of patients with head injury.', 'Retrospective comparison of neuropsychological test results for patients who suffered traumatic LOC, no LOC, or uncertain LOC.', 'Allegheny General Hospital, Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania.', 'The total number of patients included in this study was 383.', 'Neuropsychological test measures, including the visual reproduction, digit span, and logical memory subtests of the Wechsler memory scale (revised), the Trail Making test, Wisconsin Card Sorting test, Hopkins Verbal Learning test, Controlled Oral Word Association, and the Galveston Orientation and Amnesia test (GOAT).', 'No significant differences were found between the LOC, no LOC, or uncertain LOC groups for any of the neuropsychological measures used. Patients who had experienced traumatic LOC did not perform more poorly on neuropsychological testing than those with no LOC or uncertain LOC. All three groups demonstrated mildly decreased performance on formal tests of speed of information processing, attentional process, and memory.']\n\nQuestion: Does loss of consciousness predict neuropsychological decrements after concussion?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant differences in neuropsychological test performance between patients with traumatic loss of consciousness (LOC), no LOC, or uncertain LOC. All groups showed similar, mild decrements in cognitive functioning, suggesting that LOC does not uniquely predict worse outcomes. Therefore, loss of consciousness does not appear to be a strong predictor of neuropsychological decrements after concussion.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 314, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 393}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.0193999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_500", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"The long-term survival of patients with gastric cancer is governed by various factors, such as the clinical stage of the cancer, the patient's nutritional state, and the treatment and may be governed by the volume of intraperitoneal adipose tissue. The aim of this study is to clarify the relationship between the degree of the patients' body mass index and their long-term survival.\", \"Gastric cancer patients who had undergone a gastrectomy with D2-lymphadenectomy and with resection A and B according to the criteria of the Japanese Research Society for Gastric Cancer Rules were subgrouped into those patients with a body mass index<0.185 (the lower body mass index group) and those patients with a body mass index>0.210 (the higher body mass index group). The patient's morbidity and long-term survival rate was retrospectively compared between the 2 groups.\", 'A significantly longer mean survival rate was observed for the lower body mass index group in stage 2 (1667 vs. 1322 days, P = 0.0240). Also, a significantly longer mean survival rate was observed for the higher BMI group in stage 3a (1431 vs. 943, P = 0.0071).']\n\nQuestion: Does body mass index (BMI) influence morbidity and long-term survival in gastric cancer patients after gastrectomy?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows a significant difference in long-term survival between patients with lower and higher BMI across different cancer stages, indicating that BMI influences survival outcomes. Although the relationship varies by stage (favoring lower BMI in stage 2 and higher BMI in stage 3a), the results demonstrate a clear impact of BMI on survival. Therefore, the evidence supports that BMI does influence long-term survival.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 372, "output_tokens": 82, "total_tokens": 454}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.4612e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_505", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To compare the myoelectric onset of muscle fatigue in physically active trained young skiers with respect to elderly skiers and to test whether continuous training can counteract the selective loss of type II muscle fibers usually observed with aging.', 'An observational, cross-sectional study of the myoelectric onset of muscle fatigue in the left tibialis anterior muscles.', 'Surface electromyography recorded with portable devices at a downhill ski rescue lodge in the Italian Alps.', 'Fifty-four physically trained, active skiers (43 men, 11 women; age range, 24-85y).', 'Questionnaire on physical activity and 2 sustained isometric voluntary contractions at 20% and 2 at 80% of the maximal voluntary contraction level.', 'Isometric contractions and mean and median spectral frequencies calculated to monitor the myoelectric manifestations of muscle fatigue.', 'Fatigue indices did not differ significantly between younger and older subjects and, thus, did not show a correlation between myoelectric manifestations of muscle fatigue and age in physically active subjects.']\n\nQuestion: Can continuous physical training counteract aging effect on myoelectric fatigue?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant difference in fatigue indices between younger and older skiers, suggesting that continuous training may help maintain muscle fatigue resistance regardless of age. This implies that the myoelectric manifestations of muscle fatigue are not negatively affected by aging in physically active individuals. Therefore, continuous physical training appears to counteract the aging effect on myoelectric fatigue.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 309, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 385}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.9539e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_506", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Ischemic preconditioning (IP) is initiated through one or several short bouts of ischemia and reperfusion which precede a prolonged ischemia. To test whether a reperfusion must precede the prolonged index ischemia, a series without reperfusion (intraischemic preconditioning: IIP) and a series with gradual onset of ischemia, i.e. ramp ischemia (RI), which is possibly related to the development of hibernation, was compared to conventional IP (CIP).', 'Experiments were performed an 27 blood-perfused rabbit hearts (Langendorff apparatus) that were randomized into one of four series: (1) control (n = 7): 60 min normal flow - 60 min low flow (10%) ischemia - 60 min reperfusion. (2) CIP (n = 7): 4 times 5 min zero flow with 10 min reperfusion each - 60 min low flow (10%) - ischemia 60 min reperfusion. (3) IIP (n = 7): 50 min normal flow - 10 min no flow - 60min low flow (10%) ischemia -4 60min reperfusion. (4) RI (n=6): gradual reduction to 10% flow during 60min - 60min low flow (10%) ischemia - 60min reperfusion. At the end of each protocol, the infarcted area was assessed.', 'The infarct area in control hearts was 6.7+/-1.4% (means+/-SEM) of LV total area, in CIP hearts 2.6+/-0.8%, in IIP hearts 3.1+/-0.5%, and in RI hearts 3.0+/-0.3% (all p<0.05 vs. control). The differences between the three protection protocols were statistically not significant, and no protective protocol reduced post-ischemic myocardial dysfunction.']\n\nQuestion: Does ischemic preconditioning require reperfusion before index ischemia?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data show that both conventional ischemic preconditioning (CIP) with reperfusion and intraischemic preconditioning (IIP) without reperfusion significantly reduced infarct size compared to control, with no significant difference between the two. This indicates that reperfusion is not strictly necessary for preconditioning to be effective. Therefore, ischemic preconditioning does not require reperfusion before index ischemia.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 533, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 624}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.6943e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_509", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Polymorphisms in the oestrogen receptor 1 (ESR1) and oestrogen receptor 2 (ESR2) genes are associated with intermediate or endpoint markers of cardiovascular disease and with the efficacy of postmenopausal hormone therapy (HT). Contradictory findings have been described in the past and the role of these genetics variants remains unclear.', 'A cross-sectional study was carried out with 266 postmenopausal women, of whom 115 received oral HT (HT+) and 151 did not receive any HT (HT-). We analysed three single-nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) in ESR1 (rs1801132, rs7757956 and rs2813544) and two in ESR2 (rs3020450 and rs7154455) and derived haplotypes with three additional polymorphisms that had been previously investigated by our group (ESR1 rs2234693 and ESR2 rs1256049 and rs4986938).', 'The ESR1 rs2813544 polymorphism was associated with low-density lipoprotein cholesterol (LDL-C) in HT+ postmenopausal women (p\\u2009=\\u20090.044; pC\\u2009=\\u20090.388), while one ESR2 gene haplotype was associated with total cholesterol (T-chol) (p\\u2009=\\u20090.015; pC\\u2009=\\u20090.090) and LDL-C in HT+ postmenopausal women (p\\u2009=\\u20090.021; pC\\u2009=\\u20090.126).']\n\nQuestion: Are polymorphisms in oestrogen receptors genes associated with lipid levels in response to hormone therapy?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that specific polymorphisms in ESR1 and ESR2 were associated with LDL-C and total cholesterol levels in postmenopausal women undergoing hormone therapy. These associations, although not all statistically significant after correction, suggest a potential link between genetic variants and lipid response to HT. Therefore, the evidence supports a likely association.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 523, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 597}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.4532999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_51", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To determine the relationship between injury severity surrogates and other patient factors with the development and severity of heterotopic ossification (HO) following open reduction internal fixation of acetabular fractures treated with a posterior approach.', 'Retrospective review.', 'Academic level 1 trauma center.', 'Two hundred forty-one patients who were treated through a posterior approach with a minimum of 6-month radiographic follow-up were identified from an acetabular fracture database.', 'None.', 'The occurrence and severity (Brooker Grade III/IV) of HO 6 months postsurgery.', 'Length of stay (LOS) in the intensive care unit (ICU), non-ICU LOS>10 days, and HO prophylaxis with external radiation beam therapy (XRT) were significantly associated with the development of HO in a multivariate model [', '1-2 days, odds ratio (OR) = 4.33, 95% confidence interval (CI): 1.03-18.25; 3-6 days, OR = 4.1, 95% CI, 1.27-13.27;>6 days, OR = 11.7, 95% CI, 3.24-42.22; non-ICU LOS>10 days (vs. 0-6 days): OR = 7.6, 95% CI, 2.6-22.25; XRT HO prophylaxis: OR = 0.29, 95% CI, 0.10-0.85]. Other variables evaluated in multivariate modeling not significantly associated with development and severity of HO included age, gender, mechanism of injury, injury severity score, presence of neurologic injury, Letournel fracture type, occurrence of hip dislocation, interval from injury to surgery, operative time, and estimated blood loss.']\n\nQuestion: Do Surrogates of Injury Severity Influence the Occurrence of Heterotopic Ossification in Fractures of the Acetabulum?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that specific surrogates of injury severity, such as length of stay in the ICU and non-ICU length of stay, were significantly associated with the development of heterotopic ossification. Therefore, these factors do influence the occurrence of the condition.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 496, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 554}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:15.212333+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000211, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_510", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Sternal instability with mediastinitis is a very serious complication after median sternotomy. Biomechanical studies have suggested superiority of rigid plate fixation over wire cerclage for sternal fixation. This study tests the hypothesis that sternal closure stability can be improved by adding plate fixation in a human cadaver model.', 'Midline sternotomy was performed in 18 human cadavers. Four sternal closure techniques were tested: (1) approximation with six interrupted steel wires; (2) approximation with six interrupted cables; (3) closure 1 (wires) or 2 (cables) reinforced with a transverse sternal plate at the sixth rib; (4) Closure using 4 sternal plates alone. Intrathoracic pressure was increased in all techniques while sternal separation was measured by three pairs of sonomicrometry crystals fixed at the upper, middle and lower parts of the sternum until 2.0 mm separation was detected. Differences in displacement pressures were analyzed using repeated measures ANOVA and Regression Coefficients.', 'Intrathoracic pressure required to cause 2.0 mm separation increased significantly from 183.3 +/- 123.9 to 301.4 +/- 204.5 in wires/cables alone vs. wires/cables plus one plate respectively, and to 355.0 +/- 210.4 in the 4 plates group (p<0.05). Regression Coefficients (95% CI) were 120 (47-194) and 142 (66-219) respectively for the plate groups.']\n\nQuestion: Sternal plating for primary and secondary sternal closure; can it improve sternal stability?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study demonstrates that sternal plating significantly increases the intrathoracic pressure required to cause sternal separation compared to wire or cable closure alone. Both the group with wires/cables plus a plate and the group with four plates alone showed higher resistance to separation (p<0.05), indicating improved stability. Therefore, sternal plating enhances sternal stability in both primary and secondary closure.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 443, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 530}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.0153e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_512", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\": The histidine triad nucleotide-binding protein 1, HINT1, hydrolyzes adenosine 5'-monophosphoramidate substrates such as AMP-morpholidate. The human HINT1 gene is located on chromosome 5q31.2, a region implicated in linkage studies of schizophrenia. HINT1 had been shown to have different expression in postmortem brains between schizophrenia patients and unaffected controls. It was also found to be associated with the dysregulation of postsynaptic dopamine transmission, thus suggesting a potential role in several neuropsychiatric diseases.\", ': In this work, we studied 8 SNPs around the HINT1 gene region using the Irish study of high density schizophrenia families (ISHDSF, 1350 subjects and 273 pedigrees) and the Irish case control study of schizophrenia (ICCSS, 655 affected subjects and 626 controls). The expression level of HINT1 was compared between the postmortem brain cDNAs from schizophrenic patients and unaffected controls provided by the Stanley Medical Research Institute.', ': We found nominally significant differences in allele frequencies in several SNPs for both ISHDSF and ICCSS samples in sex-stratified analyses. However, the sex effect differed between the two samples. In expression studies, no significant difference in expression was observed between patients and controls. However, significant interactions amongst sex, diagnosis and rs3864283 genotypes were observed.']\n\nQuestion: Is the histidine triad nucleotide-binding protein 1 (HINT1) gene a candidate for schizophrenia?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The evidence suggests that HINT1 is located in a genomic region linked to schizophrenia and shows genetic associations in sex-stratified analyses, along with complex interactions involving sex, diagnosis, and genotype in expression studies. Although no significant expression difference was found between patients and controls, the genetic and interactive effects support its candidacy. Therefore, the most appropriate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 407, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 483}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.6497e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_513", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Neutrophil infiltration of the lung is characteristic of early posttraumatic acute respiratory distress syndrome (ARDS). This study examines the ability of neutrophils isolated (over the first 24 hrs) from the peripheral blood of patients admitted after major trauma to migrate in response to interleukin-8. Interleukin-8 is elevated in the lung within 2 hrs of major trauma in patients who later develop ARDS, and thus it plays a central role in the recruitment of neutrophils to the lung and their subsequent activation. We hypothesized that enhanced interleukin-8-mediated neutrophil migratory activity in the early postinjury phase, before the development of ARDS, may be a crucial factor in the etiology of ARDS.', 'Prospective observational study.', 'University Hospital Wales, the Royal Gwent Hospital, and East Glamorgan General Hospital. Laboratory work was conducted at the Institute of Nephrology.', 'Adult blunt trauma victims with Injury Severity Score>or = 18.', \"Neutrophils were isolated from citrated blood from 17 adult blunt major trauma patients at admission (0 hrs) and 8 and 24 hrs later. Identical samples were obtained from normal laboratory volunteers (n = 9). The neutrophil count in each specimen was measured, and the number of neutrophils migrating across porous tissue culture inserts in response to defined concentrations of interleukin-8 (0, 10, 30, and 100 ng/mL) was quantitated by peroxidase assay. Neutrophil counts in the whole blood specimens obtained from those later developing ARDS were elevated significantly at admission and declined rapidly throughout the next 24 hrs. Significantly greater numbers of trauma patients' neutrophils migrated to concentrations of interleukin-8 (30 and 100 ng/mL) at each time point when compared with normal volunteers (Mann-Whitney U test, p<.05). Neutrophils isolated from major trauma patients exhibited an enhanced migratory response to high concentrations of interleukin-8 throughout the first 24 hrs of admission, in contrast to the normal physiologic attenuation of migration seen in neutrophils isolated from normal laboratory volunteers.\"]\n\nQuestion: Increased neutrophil migratory activity after major trauma: a factor in the etiology of acute respiratory distress syndrome?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that neutrophils from major trauma patients exhibited significantly enhanced migratory responses to interleukin-8 compared to those from healthy volunteers, persisting over the first 24 hours post-injury. This heightened migration is implicated in neutrophil accumulation in the lungs, a key feature of ARDS development. Therefore, increased neutrophil migratory activity after major trauma is likely a contributing factor in the etiology of ARDS.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 568, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 663}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.9828e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_514", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Quantitative real-time PCR has become the predominant molecular technique to monitor BCRABL levels in response to treatment in Ph(+) leukemia patients. However, without some form of standardized methodology between laboratories, the correlation of results is difficult.', 'Using TaqMan-based assays, parallel quantitative real-time PCR analysis was performed on 70 clinical specimens at Vanderbilt University Medical Center and Virginia Commonwealth University. While the same positive control cell line (K562) and quality control gene (BCR) were used, the RNA isolation technique, cDNA synthesis, BCR control cell line, and PCR primer and probe sequences were different.', 'The detection of BCRABL-positive results spanned a dynamic range from 10(0) to 10(5)/100,000 cells. Forty-three samples were negative at both facilities. A Spearman rank correlation analysis was performed for the 22 BCRABL-positive paired results. The correlation coefficient, r(s), was 0.9435 (p<0.00001), suggesting a strong correlation of the results. One discordant result was obtained for consecutive samples from one patient with a low BCRABL copy number as a result of a minimal RNA yield at one laboratory.']\n\nQuestion: BCRABL transcript detection by quantitative real-time PCR : are correlated results possible from homebrew assays?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows a strong correlation (Spearman r = 0.9435, p < 0.00001) in BCRABL transcript detection between two laboratories using different homebrew assays, despite variations in methodologies. Although one discordant result occurred, likely due to low RNA yield, the overall results indicate high concordance. Therefore, correlated results are possible even with homebrew assays.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 356, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 448}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.4476e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_517", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['This paper uses a life-course approach to explore whether the timing and/or duration of urban (vs rural) exposure was associated with risk factors for NCDs.', 'A cross-sectional survey was conducted among health care workers in two hospitals in Thailand. Two measures of urbanicity were considered: early-life urban exposure and the proportion of urban life years. We explored four behavioral NCD risk factors, two physiological risk factors and four biological risk factors.', 'Both measures of urbanicity were each independently associated with increases in all behavioral and physiological risk factors. For some biological risk factors, people spending their early life in an urban area may be more susceptible to the effect of increasing proportion of urban life years than those growing up in rural areas.']\n\nQuestion: Living in an urban environment and non-communicable disease risk in Thailand: Does timing matter?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context indicates that both early-life urban exposure and the proportion of urban life years are independently associated with increased risk factors for non-communicable diseases (NCDs). It also suggests that the timing of urban exposure (e.g., during early life) may influence susceptibility to these risk factors. Therefore, timing does matter in the relationship between urban living and NCD risk.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 317, "output_tokens": 106, "total_tokens": 423}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.3107e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_518", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To evaluate renal damage and impairment of renal function 1 yr after laparoscopic partial nephrectomy (LPN) with warm ischemia>30 min.', 'From July 2004 to June 2005, 18 patients underwent LPN with warm ischemia time>30 min. Kidney damage markers (daily proteinuria and tubular enzymes) and renal function (serum creatinine, cystatin C, and creatinine clearances) were assessed on postoperative days 1 and 5 and at 12 mo. Glomerular filtration rate (GFR) was evaluated before surgery and at 3 mo. Renal scintigraphy was performed before the procedure, at 5 d and at 3 and 12 mo postoperatively. Statistical analysis was performed using the Student t test and logistic regression analysis.', 'In terms of kidney damage and renal function markers, the statistical analysis demonstrated that at 1 yr there was complete return to the normal range and no statistical difference between the values at the various time points. The GFR was not significantly different before and 3 mo after surgery. In terms of scintigraphy of the operated kidney, the values were 48.35+/-3.82% (40-50%) before the procedure, 36.88+/-8.42 (16-50%) on postoperative day 5 (p=0.0001), 40.56+/-8.96 (20-50%) at 3 mo (p=0.003), and 42.8+/-7.2% (20-50%) 1 yr after surgery (p=0.001).']\n\nQuestion: Is renal warm ischemia over 30 minutes during laparoscopic partial nephrectomy possible?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that despite warm ischemia times over 30 minutes during laparoscopic partial nephrectomy, renal function markers returned to normal within 1 year, and there was no significant long-term impairment. Although there was a temporary decline in renal function and scintigraphy values postoperatively, recovery was evident by 12 months. Therefore, warm ischemia over 30 minutes is feasible without causing permanent severe damage.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 469, "output_tokens": 94, "total_tokens": 563}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.2699e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_519", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['A variable effect of inflammation on alloimmunization to transfused red blood cells (RBCs) in mice has been recently reported. We investigated whether RBC alloimmunization in humans was affected by transfusion of blood products in temporal proximity to experiencing a febrile transfusion reaction (FTR) to platelets (PLTs), an event predominantly mediated by inflammatory cytokines.', 'Blood bank databases were used to identify patients who experienced an FTR or possible FTR to PLTs from August 2000 to March 2008 (FTR group). The control group of patients received a PLT transfusion on randomly selected dates without experiencing an FTR. The \"event\" was defined as the PLT transfusion that caused the FTR in the FTR group or the index PLT transfusion in the control group. The number of transfused blood products and their proximity to the event were recorded along with other recipient data. The primary endpoint was the rate of RBC alloimmunization between the two groups.', 'There were 190 recipients in the FTR group and 245 in the control group. Overall, the recipients in the control group were younger and received more blood products on the day of their event and over the subsequent 10 days. The alloimmunization rate among recipients in the FTR group was higher than in the control group (8% vs. 3%, respectively; p = 0.026).']\n\nQuestion: Does a febrile reaction to platelets predispose recipients to red blood cell alloimmunization?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that the alloimmunization rate was significantly higher in the FTR group (8%) compared to the control group (3%), with a p-value of 0.026, indicating statistical significance. This suggests that experiencing a febrile transfusion reaction to platelets is associated with an increased risk of red blood cell alloimmunization. Therefore, the evidence supports a positive association.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 404, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 492}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.7483999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_520", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Pregnancy induces adaptations in maternal metabolism to meet the increased need for nutrients by the placenta and fetus. Creatine is an important intracellular metabolite obtained from the diet and also synthesised endogenously. Experimental evidence suggests that the fetus relies on a maternal supply of creatine for much of gestation. However, the impact of pregnancy on maternal creatine homeostasis is unclear. We hypothesise that alteration of maternal creatine homeostasis occurs during pregnancy to ensure adequate levels of this essential substrate are available for maternal tissues, the placenta and fetus. This study aimed to describe maternal creatine homeostasis from mid to late gestation in the precocial spiny mouse.', 'Plasma creatine concentration and urinary excretion were measured from mid to late gestation in pregnant (n = 8) and age-matched virgin female spiny mice (n = 6). At term, body composition and organ weights were assessed and tissue total creatine content determined. mRNA expression of the creatine synthesising enzymes arginine:glycine amidinotransferase (AGAT) and guanidinoacetate methyltransferase (GAMT), and the creatine transporter (CrT1) were assessed by RT-qPCR. Protein expression of AGAT and GAMT was also assessed by western blot analysis.', 'Plasma creatine and renal creatine excretion decreased significantly from mid to late gestation (P<0.001, P<0.05, respectively). Pregnancy resulted in increased lean tissue (P<0.01), kidney (P<0.01), liver (P<0.01) and heart (P<0.05) mass at term. CrT1 expression was increased in the heart (P<0.05) and skeletal muscle (P<0.05) at term compared to non-pregnant tissues, and creatine content of the heart (P<0.05) and kidney (P<0.001) were also increased at this time. CrT1 mRNA expression was down-regulated in the liver (<0.01) and brain (<0.01) of pregnant spiny mice at term. Renal AGAT mRNA (P<0.01) and protein (P<0.05) expression were both significantly up-regulated at term, with decreased expression of AGAT mRNA (<0.01) and GAMT protein (<0.05) observed in the term pregnant heart. Brain AGAT (<0.01) and GAMT (<0.001) mRNA expression were also decreased at term.']\n\nQuestion: Maternal creatine homeostasis is altered during gestation in the spiny mouse: is this a metabolic adaptation to pregnancy?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows significant changes in plasma creatine, renal excretion, tissue creatine content, and expression of creatine-related enzymes and transporters during pregnancy, indicating a regulated shift in creatine homeostasis. These alterations suggest a physiological adaptation to prioritize creatine availability for the fetus and maternal tissues. Therefore, the evidence supports that these changes are metabolic adaptations to pregnancy.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 662, "output_tokens": 116, "total_tokens": 778}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 5.8602e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_521", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Rapid prescreening (RPS) is one of the quality assurance (QA) methods used in gynecologic cytology. The efficacy of RPS has been previously studied but mostly with respect to squamous lesions; in fact, there has been no study so far specifically looking at the sensitivity of RPS for detecting glandular cell abnormalities.', 'A total of 80,565 Papanicolaou (Pap) smears underwent RPS during a 25-month period. A sample was designated as \"review for abnormality\" (R) if any abnormal cells (at the threshold of atypical squamous cells of undetermined significance/atypical glandular cells [AGC]) were thought to be present or was designated as negative (N) if none were detected. Each sample then underwent full screening (FS) and was designated as either R or N and also given a cytologic interpretation.', 'The final cytologic interpretation was a glandular cell abnormality (\u2265AGC) in 107 samples (0.13%); 39 of these (36.4%) were flagged as R on RPS. Twenty-four patients (33.8%) out of 71 who had histologic follow-up were found to harbor a high-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion or carcinoma; 13 of those 24 Pap smears (54.2%) had been flagged as R on RPS. Notably, 11 AGC cases were picked up by RPS only and not by FS and represented false-negative cases; 2 of these showed endometrial adenocarcinoma on histologic follow-up.']\n\nQuestion: Pap smears with glandular cell abnormalities: Are they detected by rapid prescreening?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that 39 out of 107 Pap smears with glandular cell abnormalities (\u2265AGC) were flagged during rapid prescreening (RPS), meaning some were detected. However, RPS missed many cases, and notably, 11 AGC cases were only detected by RPS and not by full screening, indicating it did contribute to detection. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 446, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 538}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.0866e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_523", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Knowing the collaterals is essential for a spleen-preserving distal pancreatectomy with resection of the splenic vessels.', 'To ascertain the sources of the blood supply to the spleen after a spleen-preserving distal pancreatectomy with resection of the splenic vessels.', 'Perfusion of the cadaveric left gastric and right gastroepiploic arteries with methylene blue after occlusion of all the arteries except the short gastric arteries (n=10). Intraoperative color Doppler ultrasound was used for the evaluation of the hilar arterial blood flow at distal pancreatectomy (n=23) after 1) clamping of the splenic artery alone, 2) clamping of the splenic and left gastroepiploic arteries and 3) clamping of the splenic and short gastric arteries. CT angiography of the gastric and splenic vessels before and after a spleen-preserving distal pancreatectomy (n=10).', 'Perfusion of the cadaveric arteries revealed no effective direct or indirect (through the submucous gastric arterial network) communication between the left gastric and the branches of the short gastric arteries. In no case did intraoperative color Doppler ultrasound detect any hilar arterial blood flow after the clamping of the splenic and left gastroepiploic arteries. The clamping of the short gastric arteries did not change the flow parameters. In none of the cases did a post-spleen-preserving distal pancreatectomy with resection of the splenic vessels CT angiography delineate the short gastric vessels supplying the spleen. In all cases, the gastroepiploic arcade was the main arterial pathway feeding the spleen.']\n\nQuestion: Spleen-preserving distal pancreatectomy with resection of the splenic vessels. Should one rely on the short gastric arteries?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data shows no effective perfusion or arterial blood flow to the spleen via the short gastric arteries after resection of the splenic vessels. Intraoperative ultrasound and CT angiography consistently failed to detect hilar blood flow when the splenic and left gastroepiploic arteries were clamped, and the short gastric arteries did not compensate. Therefore, one should not rely on the short gastric arteries for splenic perfusion.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 466, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 558}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.2286e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_524", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The aim of this study was to evaluate poststapedectomy-delayed facial palsy etiopathogenesis, risk factors, evolution, and prevention.', 'Seven hundred six stapedectomies performed in 580 patients were reviewed. In all patients who developed delayed facial palsy, the dates of onset and subside of facial palsy, the anatomic and pathologic predisposing factors, and a possible history for recurrent labial herpetic lesions were considered. The House-Brackmann (H-B) grading system was used to evaluate the facial function. Virus-specific immunoglobulin (Ig) G and IgM antibodies against herpes simplex virus type 1 (HSV-1) were determined by enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA) 3 weeks after the onset of the paralysis. The results were compared with a control group without a history of recurrent herpes labialis.', 'Poststapedectomy facial palsy developed in 7 out of 706 procedures. All 7 patients referred a history of recurrent labial herpetic lesions. One patient showed a facial palsy H-B grade II, 2 a grade III, and 3 a grade IV. After acyclovir therapy, 6 subjects recovered completely, whereas 1 maintained an H-B grade II. An increased IgG antibody titer was found in 6 of the patients with delayed facial palsy and in 1 out of 7 controls. Mean IgG titer was 1:14,050 in the subjects with delayed facial palsy and 1:2,300 in controls (P<.001).']\n\nQuestion: Delayed peripheral facial palsy in the stapes surgery: can it be prevented?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study suggests that delayed facial palsy after stapedectomy is strongly associated with a history of recurrent labial herpes and elevated IgG antibodies against HSV-1, implicating herpes virus reactivation. Since antiviral therapy with acyclovir led to complete recovery in most patients, prophylactic antiviral treatment in at-risk patients (those with herpes labialis history) could potentially prevent the complication. Therefore, prevention appears possible in high-risk individuals.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 434, "output_tokens": 98, "total_tokens": 532}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.0613999999999994e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_525", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To evaluate retrospectively whether technical factors of hepatic arterial embolization affect the prognosis of patients with hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC).', 'Inclusion criteria of this study were the following: (1) patients received embolization as the initial treatment during 2003-2004, (2) Child A or B liver profile, (3) five or fewer HCCs with maximum diameter of 7 cm or smaller, and (4) no extrahepatic metastasis. Patient data were gathered from 43 centers. Prognostic factors were evaluated using univariate and multivariate analyses.', 'Eight hundred fifteen patients were enrolled. The 1-, 3-, 5-, and 7-year overall survival rates were 92.0 % (95 % CI 90.1-93.9), 62.9 % (95 % CI 59.3-66.6), 39.0 % (95 % CI 35.1-43.0), and 26.7 % (95 % CI 22.6-30.8) in all patients. Univariate analysis showed a Child-Pugh class-A, alpha-fetoprotein level lower than 100 ng/ml, tumor size of 3 cm or smaller, tumor number of 3 or fewer, one-lobe tumor distribution, nodular tumor type, within the Milan criteria, stage I or II, no portal venous invasion, use of iodized oil, and selective embolization were significantly better prognostic factors. In the multivariate Cox model, the benefit to survival of selective embolization remained significant (hazard ratio 0.68; 95 % CI 0.48-0.97; p = 0.033).']\n\nQuestion: Hepatic arterial embolization for unresectable hepatocellular carcinomas: do technical factors affect prognosis?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that selective embolization was a significant independent prognostic factor for better survival in patients with hepatocellular carcinoma, even after adjusting for other variables in multivariate analysis. This indicates that technical aspects of the procedure, such as the selectivity of embolization, do influence patient outcomes. Therefore, technical factors do affect prognosis.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 491, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 567}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.2461e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_527", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Staging laparoscopy (SL) is not regularly performed for patients with hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC). It may change treatment strategy, preventing unnecessary open exploration. An additional advantage of SL is possible biopsy of the nontumorous liver to assess fibrosis/cirrhosis. This study aimed to determine whether SL for patients with HCC still is useful.', 'Patients with HCC who underwent SL between January 1999 and December 2011 were analyzed. Their demographics, preoperative imaging studies, surgical findings, and histology were assessed.', 'The 56 patients (34 men and 22 women; mean age, 60 \u00b1 14 years) in this study underwent SL for assessment of extensive disease or metastases. For two patients, SL was unsuccessful because of intraabdominal adhesions. For four patients (7.1 %), SL showed unresectability because of metastases (n = 1), tumor progression (n = 1), or severe cirrhosis in the contralateral lobe (n = 2). An additional five patients did not undergo laparotomy due to disease progression detected on imaging after SL. Exploratory laparotomy for the remaining 47 patients showed 6 (13 %) additional unresectable tumors due to advanced tumor (n = 5) or nodal metastases (n = 1). Consequently, the yield of SL was 7 % (95 % confidence interval (CI), 3-17 %), and the accuracy was 27 % (95 % CI, 11-52 %). A biopsy of the contralateral liver was performed for 45 patients who underwent SL, leading to changes in management for 4 patients (17 %) with cirrhosis.']\n\nQuestion: Staging laparoscopy in patients with hepatocellular carcinoma: is it useful?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that staging laparoscopy (SL) changed management in some patients by identifying unresectable disease or cirrhosis, with a 7% yield for detecting unresectability and influencing management in 17% of biopsied cases. Although the overall accuracy was low (27%), the ability to prevent unnecessary laparotomies and guide treatment supports its utility in select cases. Therefore, the evidence suggests it can be useful.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 475, "output_tokens": 99, "total_tokens": 574}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.362499999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_53", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"To assess the extent to which the title and font of participant information sheets (PISs) can influence pregnant women's and trainee midwives' perceptions of an antenatal intervention.\", 'Pregnant women (n=35) and trainee midwives (n=36) were randomly presented with one of four PISs where the title and font of the PIS had been manipulated to create four experimental conditions (i.e., Double Fluent; Double Awkward; Fluent Title-Awkward Font; Awkward Title-Fluent Font). After reading the PIS, participants rated their perceptions of the intervention (i.e., Attractiveness, Complexity, Expected Risk, Required Effort) using five-point Likert scales.', 'A 4\u00d72 factorial multivariate analysis of variance revealed that pregnant women rated the Double Awkward condition as significantly more complex than the Double Fluent (p=.024) and Awkward Title-Fluent Font (p=.021) conditions.']\n\nQuestion: Processing fluency effects: can the content and presentation of participant information sheets influence recruitment and participation for an antenatal intervention?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that the manipulation of title and font (i.e., fluency) significantly affected how complex the intervention was perceived by pregnant women, with the Double Awkward condition rated as more complex than others. This indicates that the presentation of participant information sheets influences perceptions of the intervention, which could in turn affect recruitment and participation. Therefore, processing fluency effects are evident, suggesting that content and presentation do matter.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 311, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 400}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.0981e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_530", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To evaluate whether robotically assisted laparoscopic prostatectomy (RALP) is less invasive than radical retropubic prostatectomy (RRP), as experimental studies suggest that the acute phase reaction is proportional to surgery-induced tissue damage.', \"Between May and November 2006, all patients undergoing RRP or RALP in our department were prospectively assessed. Blood samples were collected 24 h before (T0), during surgery (T1), at the end of anaesthesia (T2), and 12 (T3) and 24 h after surgery (T4), and assayed for interleukin(IL)-6 and IL-1 alpha, C-reactive protein (CRP), and lactate. The Mann-Whitney U-, Student's t- and Friedman tests were used to compare continuous variables, and the Pearson chi-square and Fisher test for categorical variables, with a two-sided P<0.05 considered to indicate significance.\", 'In all, 35 and 26 patients were assessed for RALP and RRP, respectively; the median (interquartile range) age was 62 (56-68) and 68.5 (59.2-71.2) years, respectively (P<0.009). Baseline levels (T0) of IL-1, IL-6, CRP and lactate were comparable in both arms. IL-6, CRP and lactates levels increased during both kinds of surgery. The mean IL-6 and CPR values were higher for RRP at T1 (P = 0.01 and 0.001), T2 (P = 0.001 and<0.001), T3 (P = 0.002 and<0.001) and T4 (P<0.001 and 0.02), respectively. Lactate was higher for RRP at T2 (P = 0.001), T3 (P = 0.001) and T4 (P = 0.004), although remaining within the normal ranges. IL-1 alpha did not change at the different sample times.']\n\nQuestion: Is robotically assisted laparoscopic radical prostatectomy less invasive than retropubic radical prostatectomy?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that levels of IL-6, CRP, and lactate\u2014markers of tissue damage and inflammatory response\u2014were significantly lower in the robotically assisted laparoscopic prostatectomy (RALP) group compared to the radical retropubic prostatectomy (RRP) group at multiple time points. These findings indicate less surgical trauma and a reduced acute phase reaction with RALP. Therefore, the evidence supports that RALP is less invasive than RRP.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 575, "output_tokens": 102, "total_tokens": 677}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 5.1025e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_531", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Nasal Polyposis (NP) is defined as a chronic inflammatory disease of sinonasal mucosa leading to diffuse formation of benign polyps. Although family histories are frequently suggested in medical literature, no specific study focused on this point has been reported. The purpose of this study is to determine whether a hereditary factor could be implied for NP in a family where several members were affected. We included 99 members of this family.', 'All patients were assessed for conditions known to be associated with the development or presence of NP. Concerning NP, patients were screened with a validated questionnaire and selected patients had a medical examination by an Ear, Nose and Throat practitioner.', \"Thirteen patients had a personal history of NP without asthma, aspirin intolerance, Churg Strauss syndrome, cystic fibrosis, Young's syndrome, bare lymphocyte syndrome, or primary ciliary dyskinesia. Within this family, 19.7% of those older than 17 years were affected by NP, as compared with the national French prevalence of 2.1%.\"]\n\nQuestion: Nasal polyposis: is there an inheritance pattern?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that 19.7% of family members over 17 years old had nasal polyposis, significantly higher than the general population prevalence of 2.1%, and multiple family members were affected without other known associated conditions. This clustering of cases within a family suggests a possible hereditary component. Therefore, the most likely answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 308, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 386}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.9667999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_532", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['This study was conducted to investigate the expression and functional impact of the proto-oncogene c-kit in uveal melanoma.', 'Based on immunohistochemical (IHC) study of paraffin-embedded specimens from 134 uveal melanomas and Western blot analysis on eight fresh-frozen samples the expression of c-kit in uveal melanoma was studied. Furthermore, the phosphorylation of c-kit and the impact of the tyrosine kinase inhibitor STI571 was examined in the three uveal melanoma cell lines OCM-1, OCM-3, and 92-1.', 'Eighty-four of 134 paraffin-embedded samples and six of eight fresh-frozen samples expressed c-kit. c-Kit was strongly expressed and tyrosine phosphorylated in cultured uveal melanoma cells compared with cutaneous melanoma cells. Moreover, in contrast to cutaneous melanoma cell lines c-kit maintained a high phosphorylation level in serum-depleted uveal melanoma cells. No activation-related mutations in exon 11 of the KIT gene were found. On the contrary, expression of the stem cell growth factor (c-kit ligand) was detected in all three uveal melanoma cell lines, suggesting the presence of autocrine (paracrine) stimulation pathways. Treatment of uveal melanoma cell lines with STI571, which blocks c-kit autophosphorylation, resulted in cell death. The IC(50) of the inhibitory effects on c-kit phosphorylation and cell proliferation was of equal size and less than 2.5 microM.']\n\nQuestion: c-Kit-dependent growth of uveal melanoma cells: a potential therapeutic target?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that c-kit is highly expressed and phosphorylated in uveal melanoma cells, and its inhibition by STI571 leads to cell death, indicating functional importance. The presence of autocrine stimulation via stem cell growth factor and the sensitivity to tyrosine kinase inhibition suggest c-kit plays a key role in cell survival. Therefore, c-kit-dependent growth appears to be a viable therapeutic target.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 428, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 515}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.9088e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_533", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['We sought to determine the target populations and drug efficacy, toxicity, cost, and initiation age thresholds under which a pharmacologic regimen for knee osteoarthritis (OA) prevention could be cost-effective.', 'We used the Osteoarthritis Policy (OAPol) Model, a validated state-transition simulation model of knee OA, to evaluate the cost-effectiveness of using disease-modifying OA drugs (DMOADs) as prophylaxis for the disease. We assessed four cohorts at varying risk for developing OA: (1) no risk factors, (2) obese, (3) history of knee injury, and (4) high-risk (obese with history of knee injury). The base case DMOAD was initiated at age 50 with 40% efficacy in the first year, 5% failure per subsequent year, 0.22% major toxicity, and annual cost of $1,000. Outcomes included costs, quality-adjusted life expectancy (QALE), and incremental cost-effectiveness ratios (ICERs). Key parameters were varied in sensitivity analyses.', 'For the high-risk cohort, base case prophylaxis increased quality-adjusted life-years (QALYs) by 0.04 and lifetime costs by $4,600, and produced an ICER of $118,000 per QALY gained. ICERs>$150,000/QALY were observed when comparing the base case DMOAD to the standard of care in the knee injury only cohort; for the obese only and no risk factors cohorts, the base case DMOAD was less cost-effective than the standard of care. Regimens priced at $3,000 per year and higher demonstrated ICERs above cost-effectiveness thresholds consistent with current US standards.']\n\nQuestion: Pharmacologic regimens for knee osteoarthritis prevention: can they be cost-effective?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study indicates that for the high-risk cohort, the pharmacologic regimen produced an ICER of $118,000 per QALY, which is generally considered within the range of cost-effectiveness for many US standards. While the intervention was not cost-effective for lower-risk groups or at higher price points, the results demonstrate that it can be cost-effective under specific conditions. Therefore, the most accurate answer is that it is possible.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 462, "output_tokens": 99, "total_tokens": 561}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:26.168144+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000264, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_535", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Obesity is associated with an increased risk for cardiovascular disease. Although it is known that white adipose tissue (WAT) produces numerous proinflammatory and proatherogenic cytokines and chemokines, it is unclear whether adipose-derived chemotactic signals affect the chronic inflammation in atherosclerosis.', 'Histological examination showed that perivascular WAT (pWAT) is in close proximity to vascular walls, particularly at sites that have a tendency to develop atherosclerosis. In rodents, the amount of pWAT is markedly increased by a high-fat diet. At a functional level, supernatant from subcutaneous and pWAT strongly induced the chemotaxis of peripheral blood leukocytes. The migration of granulocytes and monocytes was mostly mediated by interleukin-8 and monocyte chemoattractant protein-1, respectively, whereas both chemokines contributed to the migration of activated T cells. Moreover, pWAT produces these chemokines, as shown by immunohistochemistry and by explant culture. The accumulation of macrophages and T cells at the interface between pWAT and the adventitia of human atherosclerotic aortas may reflect this prochemotactic activity of pWAT.']\n\nQuestion: Production of chemokines by perivascular adipose tissue: a role in the pathogenesis of atherosclerosis?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context indicates that perivascular white adipose tissue (pWAT) produces chemokines like interleukin-8 and monocyte chemoattractant protein-1, which induce leukocyte chemotaxis. These immune cells accumulate at the pWAT-adventitia interface in human atherosclerotic aortas, suggesting a direct role in vascular inflammation. This evidence supports a role for pWAT-derived chemokines in the development of atherosclerosis.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 359, "output_tokens": 104, "total_tokens": 463}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.5888999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_537", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Fruit and vegetables are protective of a number of chronic diseases; however, their intakes have been shown to vary by socioeconomic position (SEP). Household and food shopping environmental factors are thought to contribute to these differences. To determine whether household and food shopping environmental factors are associated with fruit and vegetable (FV) intakes, and contribute to socioeconomic inequalities in FV consumption.', 'Cross-sectional data were obtained by a postal questionnaire among 4333 adults (23-85 years) living in 168 neighbourhoods in the south-eastern Netherlands. Participants agreed/disagreed with a number of statements about the characteristics of their household and food shopping environments, including access, prices and quality. Education was used to characterise socioeconomic position (SEP). Main outcome measures were whether or not participants consumed fruit or vegetables on a daily basis. Multilevel logistic regression models examined between-area variance in FV consumption and associations between characteristics of the household and food shopping environments and FV consumption.', 'Only a few household and food shopping environmental factors were significantly associated with fruit and vegetable consumption, and their prevalence was low. Participants who perceived FV to be expensive were more likely to consume them. There were significant socioeconomic inequalities in fruit and vegetable consumption (ORs of not consuming fruit and vegetables were 4.26 and 5.47 among the lowest-educated groups for fruit and vegetables, respectively); however, these were not explained by any household or food shopping environmental factors.']\n\nQuestion: Household and food shopping environments: do they play a role in socioeconomic inequalities in fruit and vegetable consumption?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found significant socioeconomic inequalities in fruit and vegetable consumption, but these inequalities were not explained by household or food shopping environmental factors such as access, price, or quality. Although a few environmental factors were associated with consumption, their impact was minimal and did not account for the observed disparities.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 397, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 459}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.4387e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_539", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To investigate the association between primary systemic vasculitis (PSV) and environmental risk factors.', \"Seventy-five PSV cases and 273 controls (220 nonvasculitis, 19 secondary vasculitis, and 34 asthma controls) were interviewed using a structured questionnaire. Factors investigated were social class, occupational and residential history, smoking, pets, allergies, vaccinations, medications, hepatitis, tuberculosis, and farm exposure in the year before symptom onset (index year). The Standard Occupational Classification 2000 and job-exposure matrices were used to assess occupational silica, solvent, and metal exposure. Stepwise multiple logistic regression was used to calculate the odds ratio (OR) and 95% confidence interval (95% CI) adjusted for potential confounders. Total PSV, subgroups (47 Wegener's granulomatosis [WG], 12 microscopic polyangiitis, 16 Churg-Strauss syndrome [CSS]), and antineutrophil cytoplasmic antibody (ANCA)-positive cases were compared with control groups.\", 'Farming in the index year was significantly associated with PSV (OR 2.3 [95% CI 1.2-4.6]), with WG (2.7 [1.2-5.8]), with MPA (6.3 [1.9-21.6]), and with perinuclear ANCA (pANCA) (4.3 [1.5-12.7]). Farming during working lifetime was associated with PSV (2.2 [1.2-3.8]) and with WG (2.7 [1.3-5.7]). Significant associations were found for high occupational silica exposure in the index year (with PSV 3.0 [1.0-8.4], with CSS 5.6 [1.3-23.5], and with ANCA 4.9 [1.3-18.6]), high occupational solvent exposure in the index year (with PSV 3.4 [0.9-12.5], with WG 4.8 [1.2-19.8], and with classic ANCA [cANCA] 3.9 [1.6-9.5]), high occupational solvent exposure during working lifetime (with PSV 2.7 [1.1-6.6], with WG 3.4 [1.3-8.9], and with cANCA 3.3 [1.0-10.8]), drug allergy (with PSV 3.6 [1.8-7.0], with WG 4.0 [1.8-8.7], and with cANCA 4.7 [1.9-11.7]), and allergy overall (with PSV 2.2 [1.2-3.9], with WG 2.7 [1.4-5.7]). No other significant associations were found.']\n\nQuestion: Are environmental factors important in primary systemic vasculitis?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found significant associations between primary systemic vasculitis (PSV) and environmental factors such as farming, occupational silica and solvent exposure, and allergies. These associations were observed across PSV overall and specific subtypes like Wegener\u2019s granulomatosis and Churg-Strauss syndrome. Therefore, the evidence supports that environmental factors play an important role.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 727, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 805}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 5.9417000000000004e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_54", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Sternal fractures in childhood are rare. The aim of the study was to investigate the accident mechanism, the detection of radiological and sonographical criteria and consideration of associated injuries.', 'In the period from January 2010 to December 2012 all inpatients and outpatients with sternal fractures were recorded according to the documentation.', 'A total of 4 children aged 5-14\\xa0years with a sternal fracture were treated in 2\\xa0years, 2\\xa0children were hospitalized for pain management and 2 remained in outpatient care.']\n\nQuestion: Sternal fracture in growing children : A rare and often overlooked fracture?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context states that sternal fractures in childhood are rare and mentions only 4 cases over a 2-year period, supporting the idea that such fractures are uncommon. Additionally, the study aims to investigate detection methods and associated injuries, implying these fractures may be overlooked. Therefore, the evidence supports that sternal fractures in growing children are indeed rare and often overlooked.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 210, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 288}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.271e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_542", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To examine the clinical effect (efficacy and tolerability) of high doses of zonisamide (ZNS) (>500 mg/d) in adult patients with pharmacoresistant epilepsy.', 'Between 2006 and 2013, all epileptic outpatients treated with high doses of ZNS were selected. Safety and efficacy were assessed based on patient and caregiver reports. Serum levels of ZNS and other concomitant antiepileptic drugs were evaluated if available.', 'Nine patients (5 female): 8 focal/1 generalized pharmacoresistant epilepsy. Mean age: 34 years. Most frequent seizure type: complex partial seizures; other seizure types: generalized tonic-clonic, tonic, myoclonia. Zonisamide in polytherapy in all (100%), administered in tritherapy in 3 (33%) of 9 patients; mean dose: 633 (600-700) mg/d; efficacy (>50% seizure reduction) was observed in 5 (55%) of 9 patients. Five of 9 patients are still taking high doses of ZNS (more than 1 year). Adverse events were observed in 3 (37%) of 8 patients. Good tolerance to high doses of other antiepileptic drugs had been observed in 6 (66%) of 9 patients. Plasma levels of ZNS were only available in 2 patients; both were in the therapeutic range (34.95, 30.91) (10-40 mg/L).']\n\nQuestion: Could Adult European Pharmacoresistant Epilepsy Patients Be Treated With Higher Doses of Zonisamide?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study reports that high doses of zonisamide (>500 mg/day) were effective (>50% seizure reduction) in 55% of adult patients with pharmacoresistant epilepsy and were well-tolerated in most cases, with adverse events in only 37% of patients. Plasma levels remained within the therapeutic range, and five patients continued treatment for over a year, indicating feasibility and tolerability. These findings support the potential use of higher zonisamide doses in this population.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 429, "output_tokens": 106, "total_tokens": 535}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.1058999999999994e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_544", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The authors sought to determine whether the manic/mixed episode distinction in patients with bipolar disorder runs true over time.', 'Over an 11-year period, the observed distribution of manic and mixed episodes (N=1,224) for patients with three or more entries in the management information system of a community mental health center (N=241) was compared to the expected distribution determined by averaging 1,000 randomly generated simulations.', 'Episodes were consistent (all manic or all mixed) in significantly more patients than would be expected by chance.']\n\nQuestion: Does the manic/mixed episode distinction in bipolar disorder patients run true over time?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that patients were significantly more likely to have consistent episodes (all manic or all mixed) over time than would be expected by chance. This suggests that the manic/mixed episode distinction is stable and reliable for many individuals. Therefore, the evidence supports that the distinction runs true over time.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 209, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 274}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.1339e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_545", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['This retrospective study was carried out in the Ear Nose Throat (ENT) Unit of Giannina Gaslini Institute, Genoa, Italy on children operated for adenotonsillectomy (AT) or tonsillectomy (T) between January 2003 and February 2008. We considered in the study all the post-tonsillectomy late haemorrhages irrespective of their severity and for each case we evaluated whether they recurred in the day-time (B) (between 9.00 a.m. and 9.00 p.m.) or in the night-time (A) (between 9.00 p.m. and 9.00 a.m.). Finally we considered the number of haemorrhages per hour in the whole day.', 'Out of 3306 patients undergoing elective adenotonsillectomy or tonsillectomy, post-operative late haemorrhage occurred in 59 (1.78%). We noted that 42 episodes (71.2%) occurred in the night-time and 17 (28.8%) in the day-time. The average time from the operation was 8.4 days. A statistically significant difference (p=0.002) was found when comparing the frequencies of night-time and day-time haemorrhages. We did not observe any significant difference in the distribution per hour of the haemorrhages.']\n\nQuestion: Post-tonsillectomy late haemorrhage: is it a preferably night-time event?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that 71.2% of late haemorrhages occurred during the night-time (between 9.00 p.m. and 9.00 a.m.), compared to 28.8% during the day-time, and this difference was statistically significant (p=0.002). This indicates a clear preference for haemorrhages to occur at night. Therefore, the evidence supports that post-tonsillectomy late haemorrhage is a preferably night-time event.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 401, "output_tokens": 112, "total_tokens": 513}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.9671e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_546", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Acute hepatitis C virus infection in the era of universal screening of blood products has not disappeared, and is thought to be transmitted primarily via injecting drug use. A growing body of evidence supports iatrogenic transmission as an important mode of transmission. The aim of this study was to examine transmission routes and clinical characteristics in a group of patients with acute hepatitis C in Israel.', 'A retrospective chart review was conducted in three different liver clinics in Israel, of all new hepatitis C patients. Patients identified as possible acute hepatitis C were re-interviewed and all other sources such as blood bank records and pre-employment check-ups reviewed in order to establish the diagnosis of acute hepatitis C infection and to identify the transmission route.', 'Twenty-nine patients were found to have acute hepatitis C, representing 0.75% of all new referrals for hepatitis C. The most frequent (65%) mode of transmission was iatrogenic involving several, often minimal, procedures and clinical settings. The group in which iatrogenic transmission was suspected was older and the patients more often in monogamous relationship compared with other transmission routes groups. Injecting drug use was the second most common route of infection. Spontaneous seroconversion has occurred in approximately one third of the patients.']\n\nQuestion: Acute hepatitis C in Israel: a predominantly iatrogenic disease?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that 65% of acute hepatitis C cases were due to iatrogenic transmission, making it the most frequent mode of transmission. This majority suggests that iatrogenic transmission is the predominant route in this population. Therefore, the evidence supports the conclusion that acute hepatitis C in Israel is predominantly iatrogenic.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 347, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 421}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.2037e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_547", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"To evaluate the effect of an antismoking advertisement on young people's perceptions of smoking in movies and their intention to smoke.SUBJECTS/\", '3091 cinema patrons aged 12-24 years in three Australian states; 18.6% of the sample (n = 575) were current smokers.DESIGN/', 'Quasi-experimental study of patrons, surveyed after having viewed a movie. The control group was surveyed in week 1, and the intervention group in weeks 2 and 3. Before seeing the movie in weeks 2 and 3, a 30 s antismoking advertisement was shown, shot in the style of a movie trailer that warned patrons not to be sucked in by the smoking in the movie they were about to see.', 'Attitude of current smokers and non-smokers to smoking in the movies; intention of current smokers and non-smokers to smoke in 12 months.', 'Among non-smokers, 47.8% of the intervention subjects thought that the smoking in the viewed movie was not OK compared with 43.8% of the control subjects (p = 0.04). However, there was no significant difference among smokers in the intervention (16.5%) and control (14.5%) groups (p = 0.4). A higher percentage of smokers in the intervention group indicated that they were likely to be smoking in 12 months time (38.6%) than smokers in the control group (25.6%; p<0.001). For non-smokers, there was no significant difference in smoking intentions between groups, with 1.2% of intervention subjects and 1.6% of controls saying that they would probably be smoking in 12 months time (p = 0.54).']\n\nQuestion: Out of the smokescreen II: will an advertisement targeting the tobacco industry affect young people's perception of smoking in movies and their intention to smoke?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that while the advertisement slightly changed the perceptions of non-smokers, it did not significantly change the perceptions of smokers and actually correlated with an increased intention to smoke among the smoker intervention group. Therefore, the advertisement did not achieve the intended positive effect on smoking intentions.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 495, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 558}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:21.767074+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00021825, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_549", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The aim of the study was to evaluate the outcomes and patterns of failure in patients with metastatic carcinoma to cervical lymph nodes from an unknown head and neck primary origin, who were treated curatively with radiotherapy, with or without neck dissection.', 'The study included 61 patients referred to the McGill University Hospital Centers from 1987 to 2002. The median age was 57 years, with male to female ratio of 4:1. Distribution of patients by N status was as follows: N1, 16 patients (26%); N2a, 18 (30%); N2b, 13 (22%); N2c, 7 (11%); and N3, 7 (11%). Twenty patients underwent neck dissection (11 radical, 9 functional) and 41 patients had biopsy (9 fine-needle aspiration and 32 excisional biopsy). All patients received radiotherapy. The median dose to the involved node(s) was 64 Gy, and 60 Gy to the rest of the neck. Treatment of the neck was bilateral in 50 patients (82%) and ipsilateral in 11 (18%). The minimum duration of the follow-up was 12 months, with the median of 32 months.', 'The 5- and 8-year overall survival for the whole population was 79% and 67%, respectively. There was no statistically significant difference in the 8-year actuarial overall survival (64.8% and 67.6%, respectively, p = .64) and local relapse-free survival (75% vs 74.5%, respectively, p = .57), among patients who had biopsy versus those who had neck dissection.']\n\nQuestion: Metastatic carcinoma to the cervical nodes from an unknown head and neck primary site: Is there a need for neck dissection?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no statistically significant difference in overall survival or local relapse-free survival between patients who underwent neck dissection and those who had only biopsy. This suggests that neck dissection does not provide additional benefit in terms of survival outcomes when radiotherapy is used. Therefore, the evidence supports that neck dissection may not be necessary.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 488, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 559}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.1748e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_55", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['For women, the correlation between circulating androgens and sexual desire is inconclusive. Substitution with androgens at physiological levels improves sexual function in women who experience decreased sexual desire and androgen deficiency from surgical menopause, pituitary disease, and age-related decline in androgen production in the ovaries. Measuring bioactive testosterone is difficult and new methods have been proposed, including measuring the primary androgen metabolite androsterone glucuronide (ADT-G).AIM: The aim of this study was to investigate a possible correlation between serum levels of androgens and sexual desire in women and whether the level of ADT-G is better correlated than the level of circulating androgens with sexual desire.', 'This was a cross-sectional study including 560 healthy women aged 19-65 years divided into three age groups. Correlations were considered to be statistically significant at P<0.05.', 'Sexual desire was determined as the total score of the sexual desire domain of the Female Sexual Function Index. Total testosterone (TT), calculated free testosterone (FT), androstenedione, dehydroepiandrosterone sulfate (DHEAS), and ADT-G were analyzed using mass spectrometry.', 'Sexual desire correlated overall with FT and androstenedione in the total cohort of women. In a subgroup of women aged 25-44 years with no use of systemic hormonal contraception, sexual desire correlated with TT, FT, androstenedione, and DHEAS. In women aged 45-65 years, androstenedione correlated with sexual desire. No correlations between ADT-G and sexual desire were identified.']\n\nQuestion: Is there a correlation between androgens and sexual desire in women?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that sexual desire correlated with various androgens such as free testosterone, androstenedione, total testosterone, and DHEAS in specific groups of women, particularly in those aged 25\u201344 years not using hormonal contraception. Although no correlation was found with ADT-G, the observed associations between certain androgens and sexual desire indicate a relationship. Therefore, the evidence supports a positive correlation in specific subgroups.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 435, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 530}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.0385e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_551", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['It has been demonstrated that hiatal hernia repair (HHR) during laparoscopic adjustable gastric banding (LAGB) decreases the rate of reoperation. However, the technical aspects (location and number of sutures) are not standardized. It is unknown whether such technical details are associated with differing rates of reoperation for band-related problems.', 'A retrospective analysis was performed from a single institution, including 2,301 patients undergoing LAGB with HHR from July 1, 2007 to December 31, 2011. Independent variables were number and location of sutures. Data collected included demographics, operating room (OR) time, length of stay (LOS), follow-up time, postoperative BMI/%EWL, and rates of readmission/reoperation. Statistical analyses included ANOVA and Chi squared tests. Kaplan-Meier, log-rank, and Cox regression tests were used for follow-up data and reoperation rates, in order to account for differential length of follow-up and confounding variables.', 'There was no difference in length of follow-up among all groups. The majority of patients had one suture (range 1-6; 55 %). Patients with fewer sutures had shorter OR time (1 suture 45 min vs. 4+ sutures 56 min, p<0.0001). LOS, 30-day readmission, band-related reoperation, and postop BMI/%EWL were not statistically significant. Anterior suture placement (vs. posterior vs. both) was most common (61 %). OR time was shorter in those with anterior suture (41 min vs. posterior 56 min vs. both 59 min, p<0.0001). Patients with posterior suture had a longer LOS (84 % 1 day vs. anterior 74 % 1 day vs. both 74 % 1 day, p<0.0001). There was no difference in 30-day readmission, band-related reoperation, and postoperative BMI/%EWL.']\n\nQuestion: Location and number of sutures placed for hiatal hernia repair during laparoscopic adjustable gastric banding: does it matter?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant differences in reoperation rates, readmission, or weight loss outcomes based on the number or location of sutures used in hiatal hernia repair during LAGB. Although operative time and length of stay varied slightly, these differences did not translate into meaningful clinical outcomes. Therefore, the technical aspects of suture placement do not appear to significantly affect key postoperative results.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 547, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 632}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.7337e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_552", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Children with recurrent protracted bacterial bronchitis (PBB) and bronchiectasis share common features, and PBB is likely a forerunner to bronchiectasis. Both diseases are associated with neutrophilic inflammation and frequent isolation of potentially pathogenic microorganisms, including nontypeable Haemophilus influenzae (NTHi), from the lower airway. Defective alveolar macrophage phagocytosis of apoptotic bronchial epithelial cells (efferocytosis), as found in other chronic lung diseases, may also contribute to tissue damage and neutrophil persistence. Thus, in children with bronchiectasis or PBB and in control subjects, we quantified the phagocytosis of airway apoptotic cells and NTHi by alveolar macrophages and related the phagocytic capacity to clinical and airway inflammation.', 'Children with bronchiectasis (n = 55) or PBB (n = 13) and control subjects (n = 13) were recruited. Alveolar macrophage phagocytosis, efferocytosis, and expression of phagocytic scavenger receptors were assessed by flow cytometry. Bronchoalveolar lavage fluid interleukin (IL) 1\u03b2 was measured by enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay.', 'For children with PBB or bronchiectasis, macrophage phagocytic capacity was significantly lower than for control subjects (P = .003 and P<.001 for efferocytosis and P = .041 and P = .004 for phagocytosis of NTHi; PBB and bronchiectasis, respectively); median phagocytosis of NTHi for the groups was as follows: bronchiectasis, 13.7% (interquartile range [IQR], 11%-16%); PBB, 16% (IQR, 11%-16%); control subjects, 19.0% (IQR, 13%-21%); and median efferocytosis for the groups was as follows: bronchiectasis, 14.1% (IQR, 10%-16%); PBB, 16.2% (IQR, 14%-17%); control subjects, 18.1% (IQR, 16%-21%). Mannose receptor expression was significantly reduced in the bronchiectasis group (P = .019), and IL-1\u03b2 increased in both bronchiectasis and PBB groups vs control subjects.']\n\nQuestion: Is Alveolar Macrophage Phagocytic Dysfunction in Children With Protracted Bacterial Bronchitis a Forerunner to Bronchiectasis?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that both children with protracted bacterial bronchitis (PBB) and bronchiectasis have significantly reduced alveolar macrophage phagocytic function compared to controls, with the most severe impairment in bronchiectasis. Given that PBB and bronchiectasis share similar defects in macrophage function and airway inflammation, the findings support the idea that PBB may precede bronchiectasis. Therefore, phagocytic dysfunction in PBB could represent an early stage in the development of bronchiectasis.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 684, "output_tokens": 119, "total_tokens": 803}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 6.046399999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_554", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Little is known about the nutritional adequacy and feasibility of breastmilk replacement options recommended by WHO/UNAIDS/UNICEF. The study aim was to explore suitability of the 2001 feeding recommendations for infants of HIV-infected mothers for a rural region in KwaZulu Natal, South Africa specifically with respect to adequacy of micronutrients and essential fatty acids, cost, and preparation times of replacement milks.', 'Nutritional adequacy, cost, and preparation time of home-prepared replacement milks containing powdered full cream milk (PM) and fresh full cream milk (FM) and different micronutrient supplements (2 g UNICEF micronutrient sachet, government supplement routinely available in district public health clinics, and best available liquid paediatric supplement found in local pharmacies) were compared. Costs of locally available ingredients for replacement milk were used to calculate monthly costs for infants aged one, three, and six months. Total monthly costs of ingredients of commercial and home-prepared replacement milks were compared with each other and the average monthly income of domestic or shop workers. Time needed to prepare one feed of replacement milk was simulated.', 'When mixed with water, sugar, and each micronutrient supplement, PM and FM provided<50% of estimated required amounts for vitamins E and C, folic acid, iodine, and selenium and<75% for zinc and pantothenic acid. PM and FM made with UNICEF micronutrient sachets provided 30% adequate intake for niacin. FM prepared with any micronutrient supplement provided no more than 32% vitamin D. All PMs provided more than adequate amounts of vitamin D. Compared with the commercial formula, PM and FM provided 8-60% of vitamins A, E, and C, folic acid, manganese, zinc, and iodine. Preparations of PM and FM provided 11% minimum recommended linoleic acid and 67% minimum recommended alpha-linolenic acid per 450 ml mixture. It took 21-25 minutes to optimally prepare 120 ml of replacement feed from PM or commercial infant formula and 30-35 minutes for the fresh milk preparation. PM or FM cost approximately 20% of monthly income averaged over the first six months of life; commercial formula cost approximately 32%.']\n\nQuestion: Are WHO/UNAIDS/UNICEF-recommended replacement milks for infants of HIV-infected mothers appropriate in the South African context?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that home-prepared replacement milks, even with micronutrient supplements, were deficient in several essential vitamins and fatty acids, and their preparation was time-consuming and costly relative to local incomes. Commercial formula was even less affordable, costing about 32% of a worker\u2019s monthly income. These factors suggest that the recommended replacement milks are not nutritionally or economically feasible in this setting.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 678, "output_tokens": 118, "total_tokens": 796}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 5.9938e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_556", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Bias against operating on patients with prosthetic valve endocarditis (PVE) who have multiple prostheses may preclude the use of life-saving valve replacement. We investigated the accuracy of the preoperative diagnosis of PVE in patients with both mitral and aortic prosthesis and the safety of single-valve replacement when only one valve seemed infected.', 'Patients with a diagnosis of active PVE who had mitral and aortic prosthesis in place were assessed. We looked at the methods for diagnosis, causative agents, indication for valve replacement, operative findings and outcome.', 'Twenty patients, who had both mitral and aortic prostheses and a diagnosis of PVE, were assessed. Streptococci and staphylococci caused 70% of cases. By means of echocardiography, the valves involved were: mitral (11 patients), aortic (six patients), and in three cases both prosthetic valves seemed infected. Surgery was undertaken in 17 patients (85%). The positive predictive value of transesophageal echocardiogram (TEE) for the preoperative diagnosis of the site of infection was 100%. In 13 patients, only the prosthetic valve that seemed infected was replaced. Four of these patients died within a week after the procedure. Nine patients survived the surgical procedure, completed a course of antimicrobial therapy and were followed up for 15.78 months (95% CI: 12.83-18.72). All were considered cured and relapses were not observed.']\n\nQuestion: Surgical treatment of prosthetic valve endocarditis in patients with double prostheses: is single-valve replacement safe?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that in 13 patients who underwent single-valve replacement based on preoperative TEE findings, 9 survived, completed treatment, and showed no relapses during follow-up, indicating successful outcomes. The positive predictive value of TEE for identifying the infected valve was 100%, supporting the accuracy of the preoperative diagnosis. This evidence suggests that single-valve replacement is safe when only one valve appears infected.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 431, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 523}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.9800999999999994e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_557", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To study the risks of haemodynamic instability, and the possible occurrence of spinal haematoma, meningitis and epidural abscess when epidural analgesia is performed for cytoreductive surgery and hyperthermic intraperitoneal chemotherapy (HIPEC).', 'We retrospectively analyzed the data of 35 patients treated by HIPEC with oxaliplatin or cisplatin. An epidural catheter was inserted before induction of general anaesthesia. Postoperatively, a continuous epidural infusion of ropivacain, then a patient-controlled epidural analgesia were started.', 'The epidural catheter was used peroperatively before HIPEC in 12 subjects (34%), and after HIPEC in 23 subjects (66%). The median dose of ropivacain given peroperatively in the epidural catheter was 40 mg (30-75). Norepinephrin was used in two subjects (6%) peroperatively (median infusion rate 0.325 \u03bcg/kg per minute [0.32-0.33]), and in four subjects (11%) in the postoperative 24 hours. No spinal haematoma, meningitis or epidural abscess were noted. Five subjects (14%) had a thrombopenia or a prothrombin time less than 60% before catheter removal. Two subjects (6%) had a leukopenia before catheter removal. No thrombopenia or blood coagulation disorders were recorded the day of catheter removal.']\n\nQuestion: Epidural analgesia for surgical treatment of peritoneal carcinomatosis: a risky technique?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study reviewed 35 patients undergoing cytoreductive surgery and HIPEC with epidural analgesia and found no cases of spinal hematoma, meningitis, or epidural abscess. Despite some patients having transient coagulopathy or leukopenia before catheter removal, no complications were recorded at the time of removal. Therefore, the results suggest that epidural analgesia was not associated with major complications in this cohort.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 425, "output_tokens": 93, "total_tokens": 518}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.9475e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_56", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Immediate breast reconstruction (IBR) provides psychological benefit to many early breast cancer patients however concerns persist regarding its potential impact on chemotherapy delivery. We investigated the association between IBR, complications and adjuvant chemotherapy delivery.', 'Retrospective analysis of patients in an academic breast service, who underwent mastectomy, with or without reconstruction, and received adjuvant chemotherapy.', 'Comparisons were made between 107 patients who received IBR and 113 who received mastectomy alone. Those receiving IBR were on average younger, with lower body mass index (BMI) and better prognoses. Overall complication rates were comparable (mastectomy alone: 45.1% versus IBR: 35.5%, p = 0.2). There was more return to surgery in the IBR group with 11.5% of tissue expanders requiring removal, whilst more seromas occurred in the mastectomy group. There was no significant difference in the median time to chemotherapy.']\n\nQuestion: Does immediate breast reconstruction compromise the delivery of adjuvant chemotherapy?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant difference in the median time to chemotherapy between patients who underwent immediate breast reconstruction (IBR) and those who had mastectomy alone. Although the IBR group had higher rates of return to surgery, overall complication rates were comparable and did not delay chemotherapy initiation. Therefore, IBR does not appear to compromise the delivery of adjuvant chemotherapy.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 354, "output_tokens": 108, "total_tokens": 462}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.5934e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_561", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"Academic medical researchers are judged by how often their publications are cited in the literature. When serving as journal reviewers, they may be more favorably disposed to manuscripts that cite their work. We investigate whether manuscripts that contain a citation to the reviewer's work receive higher evaluations than those that do not and\\xa0whether peer reviewers encourage authors to cite that reviewer's work.\", \"We analyzed all research manuscripts submitted in 2012 to Annals of Emergency Medicine to determine whether they contained citations to each reviewer's work. To determine whether citation affected reviewer scores, we obtained each reviewer's score of the manuscript's overall desirability (1=worst to 5=best) and used descriptive statistics and regression modeling to compare scores of cited and noncited reviewers. We also enumerated how often reviewers suggested that authors add citations to the reviewer's work or other work.\", \"There were 395 manuscripts and 999 corresponding reviews with an manuscript desirability score. The 83 reviews by cited reviewers (8.3%) had a mean score of 2.8 (SD 1.4); the 916 reviews by noncited reviewers (91.7%), 2.5 (1.2; \u0394=0.3; 95% confidence interval [CI] 0 to 0.6). The mean score in the 117 reviews of the noncited reviewers of\\xa0the\\xa057\\xa0manuscripts that had both cited and noncited reviewers was 2.9 (SD 1.2) compared with 2.9 (SD 1.1) for the 68 reviews by cited reviewers (\u0394=0; 95% CI -0.3 to 0.4). In the final ordinal regression model, the unadjusted OR for\\xa0the manuscript desirability score was 1.6 (95% CI 1.0 to 2.7); when adjusting for the manuscripts' mean desirability score, it was 1.4 (95% CI 0.8 to\\xa02.2), demonstrating that manuscript quality was a confounder. Authors were asked to\\xa0add a citation to the reviewer's work in 28 reviews (3%) but to others' work in 98 (10%).\"]\n\nQuestion: Are Reviewers' Scores Influenced by Citations to Their Own Work?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data show a small unadjusted difference in scores (OR 1.6) for manuscripts citing a reviewer\u2019s work, but this effect diminishes and becomes nonsignificant after adjusting for manuscript quality (OR 1.4, 95% CI 0.8 to 2.2), indicating that the initial association is largely explained by confounding. In the matched analysis of the same manuscripts, there was no difference in scores between cited and noncited reviewers. Therefore, the most accurate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 579, "output_tokens": 111, "total_tokens": 690}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 5.2208999999999994e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_563", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"Alzheimer's disease (AD) is a primary degenerative disease that progressively affects all brain functions, with devastating consequences for the patient, the patient's family and society. Rest regional cerebral blood flow (rCBF) could have a strategic role in differentiating between AD patients and normal controls, but its use for this purpose has a low discriminatory capacity. The purpose of this study was to evaluate whether the diagnostic sensitivity of rCBF single-photon emission computed tomography (SPECT) could be increased by using an episodic memory task provocation, i.e. memory-provoked rCBF-SPECT (MP-SPECT).\", 'Eighteen persons (73.2+/-4.8 years) with mild AD and 18 healthy elderly (69.4+/-3.9 years) were included in the study. The subjects were injected with (99m)Tc-hexamethylpropylene amine oxime (HMPAO) during memory provocation with faces and names, followed by an rCBF-SPECT study. The rCBF (99m)Tc-HMPAO SPECT images were analysed using statistical parametric mapping (SPM2). Peaks with a false discovery rate corrected value of 0.05 were considered significant.', 'On MP-SPECT, the AD group showed a significant rCBF reduction in the left parietal cortex in comparison with healthy elderly. At rest, no significant group differences were seen.']\n\nQuestion: Memory-provoked rCBF-SPECT as a diagnostic tool in Alzheimer's disease?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that memory-provoked rCBF-SPECT (MP-SPECT) revealed significant cerebral blood flow reductions in the left parietal cortex in Alzheimer's patients compared to controls, whereas rest SPECT did not. This suggests that MP-SPECT improves diagnostic sensitivity by detecting abnormalities not visible at rest. Therefore, MP-SPECT shows potential as a diagnostic tool in Alzheimer's disease.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 399, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 484}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.6828999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_571", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Adults with a mild intellectual disability (ID) often show poor decoding and reading comprehension skills. The goal of this study was to investigate the effects of teaching text comprehension strategies to these adults. Specific research goals were to determine (1) the effects of two instruction conditions, i.e. strategy instruction to individuals and strategy instruction in small groups in a reciprocal teaching context; (2) intervention programme effects on specific strategy tests (so-called direct effects), and possible differences between strategies; (3) (long-term) transfer effects of the programme on general reading comprehension ability; and (4) the regression of general text comprehension by the variables of technical reading, IQ, reading comprehension of sentences (RCS), and pretest and posttest scores on the strategies taught.', \"In total, 38 adults (age range 20-72 years; mean age of 36 years) with ID participated in the study. IQs ranged from 45 to 69 with a mean IQ of 58. The intervention programme involved 15 weekly lessons of 1 h each, taught during 3 months. Blocks of lessons included each of Brown and Palincsar's strategies of summarizing, questioning, clarifying and predicting, as participants read and studied narrative and expository texts.\", 'Results indicated no significant difference between group and individual instruction conditions. Second, direct programme effects - as determined by posttest-pretest contrasts for strategy tests - were substantial, except for the questioning strategy. Third, even more substantial was the transfer effect to general text comprehension. Moreover, the results on this test were well maintained at a follow-up test. Finally, the variance of general reading comprehension ability was best explained by the test of RCS, and only moderately by the strategies trained.']\n\nQuestion: Adults with mild intellectual disabilities: can their reading comprehension ability be improved?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found substantial direct effects on strategy tests and even more substantial transfer effects to general reading comprehension, which were maintained at follow-up. This indicates that reading comprehension ability in adults with mild intellectual disabilities improved as a result of the intervention. Therefore, the evidence supports a positive outcome.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 450, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 512}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.815e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_573", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['In this study, the authors discussed the feasibility and value of diffusion-weighted (DW) MR imaging in the detection of uterine endometrial cancer in addition to conventional nonenhanced MR images.', 'DW images of endometrial cancer in 23 patients were examined by using a 1.5-T MR scanner. This study investigated whether or not DW images offer additional incremental value to conventional nonenhanced MR imaging in comparison with histopathological results. Moreover, the apparent diffusion coefficient (ADC) values were measured in the regions of interest within the endometrial cancer and compared with those of normal endometrium and myometrium in 31 volunteers, leiomyoma in 14 patients and adenomyosis in 10 patients. The Wilcoxon rank sum test was used, with a p<0.05 considered statistically significant.', 'In 19 of 23 patients, endometrial cancers were detected only on T2-weighted images. In the remaining 4 patients, of whom two had coexisting leiomyoma, no cancer was detected on T2-weighted images. This corresponds to an 83% detection sensitivity for the carcinomas. When DW images and fused DW images/T2-weighted images were used in addition to the T2-weighted images, cancers were identified in 3 of the remaining 4 patients in addition to the 19 patients (overall detection sensitivity of 96%). The mean ADC value of endometrial cancer (n=22) was (0.97+/-0.19)x10(-3)mm(2)/s, which was significantly lower than those of the normal endometrium, myometrium, leiomyoma and adenomyosis (p<0.05).']\n\nQuestion: Body diffusion-weighted MR imaging of uterine endometrial cancer: is it helpful in the detection of cancer in nonenhanced MR imaging?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that adding diffusion-weighted (DW) imaging to conventional T2-weighted MRI increased the detection sensitivity for endometrial cancer from 83% to 96%. This indicates that DW imaging provides incremental value in detecting cancers that were not visible on T2-weighted images alone. Therefore, DW imaging is helpful in the detection of uterine endometrial cancer when used with nonenhanced MR imaging.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 476, "output_tokens": 93, "total_tokens": 569}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.3096e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_575", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['This study was undertaken to examine whether use of alcohol, cigarettes, marijuana, cocaine, and other illicit drugs is related to the likelihood of sexual behaviors that increase risk for human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) infection among youth.', 'The 1990 national Youth Risk Behavior Survey was used to collect self-reported information about a broad range of health risk behaviors from a representative sample of 11,631 high school students in the United States.', 'Students who reported no substance use were least likely to report having had sexual intercourse, having had four or more sex partners, and not having used a condom at last sexual intercourse. Adjusted for age, sex, and race/ethnicity, odds ratios for each of these sexual risk behaviors were greatest among students who had used marijuana, cocaine, or other illicit drugs. Students who had used only alcohol or cigarettes had smaller but still significant increases in the likelihood of having had sexual intercourse and of having had four or more sex partners.']\n\nQuestion: Substance use and HIV-related sexual behaviors among US high school students: are they related?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that substance use, particularly marijuana, cocaine, and other illicit drugs, was associated with higher odds of engaging in HIV-related sexual risk behaviors among high school students. Even use of alcohol or cigarettes was linked to increased likelihood of risky sexual behaviors, though to a lesser extent. Therefore, the evidence strongly supports a relationship between substance use and HIV-related sexual behaviors.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 294, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 374}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.8874e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_579", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"Paget's disease of bone has been described as a few case reports from India. The aim of the present study is to document the existence of Paget's disease (PD) in India.\", 'We describe demography, clinical manifestations, biochemical and radiological profile and the treatment outcome of 21 patients of PD.', \"Mean (+/-SD) age of these patients at presentation was 49.2 +/- 17.6 years and the male to female ratio was 2.5:1. Common clinical manifestations included backache, headache and bone pains. Others were fracture, joint pain, deafness, gait ataxia, visual impairment and difficulty in biting. Two patients presented with hydrocephalus and one had recurrent paraparesis. Fifteen (71.4%) patients had polyostotic and six (28.6%) had monoostotic Paget's disease. More commonly involved bones were skull and spine (61.9%) followed by pelvis (38.1%), femur (33.3%), tibia (9%) and ulna (9%). Mean (+/-SD) serum alkaline phosphatase at diagnosis was 1514 +/- 1168 IU/L and nine months after treatment with bisphosphonates decreased to 454 +/- 406 IU/ L(P<0.03).\"]\n\nQuestion: Does Paget's disease exist in India?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study explicitly aims to document the existence of Paget's disease in India and presents clinical data from 21 confirmed cases. The detailed demographic, biochemical, and radiological findings confirm the presence of the disease in the Indian population. Therefore, the evidence strongly supports that Paget's disease does exist in India.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 374, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 443}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.3454e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_58", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['PRISM is claimed to score disease severity which has attributed an impact on length of PICU stay (LOS).', \"To determine the impact of PRISM on LOS, and evaluate an Artificial Neural Network's (ANN) performance to estimate LOS from PRISM item patterns.\", \"Retrospectively we performed correlation and regression analyses on routinely scored PRISM data of all consecutive admissions to our level-III PICU from 1994 to 1999 (n>2000) with individual LOS. In addition, an ANN was trained on the chronologically first 75% of those data (inputs, PRISM items + age + sex; output, LOS). The ANN's performance was tested on the remaining most recent 25% of the data sets.\", \"The Spearman and Pearson coefficients of correlation between PRISM and LOS were 0.2 (p<0.001) and 0.08 (p = 0.0003), the latter being slightly higher when LOS was logarithmically transformed. Pearson's coefficient of correlation between ANN derived LOS estimate and actual LOS was 0.21 (p<0.001) (LOS logarithmically transformed: 0.34; p<0.001) in the independent validation sample.\"]\n\nQuestion: Can PRISM predict length of PICU stay?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correlation between PRISM and length of stay (LOS) is statistically significant but weak (Pearson r = 0.08\u20130.2), indicating limited predictive ability. While PRISM shows a significant association with LOS, the low correlation suggests it cannot accurately predict LOS on its own. Therefore, the most appropriate answer is that PRISM alone cannot reliably predict LOS.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 361, "output_tokens": 82, "total_tokens": 443}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.3830999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_581", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To assess the accuracy of vaginal pH measurement on wet mount microscopy slides compared with direct measurements on fresh vaginal fluid. We also tested whether differences in accuracy were dependent on the sampling devices used or on the diagnosis of the vaginal infections.', \"Using a cotton swab, cytobrush or wooden spatula a vaginal fluid specimen was collected from 84 consecutive women attending a vulvo-vaginitis clinic. A pH strip (pH range 4-7, Merck) was brought in contact with the vaginal fluid on the sampling device and on the glass slide after adding one droplet of saline and performing microscopy by two different people unaware of the microscopy results of the clinical exam. Values were compared by Fisher exact and Student's t-tests.\", 'pH measurement from microscopy slides after the addition of saline causes systematic increases of pH leading to false positive readings. This is true for all types of disturbance of the flora and infections studied, and was seen in the abnormal as well as in the normal or intermediate pH range.']\n\nQuestion: Can vaginal pH be measured from the wet mount slide?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that measuring vaginal pH from wet mount slides after adding saline leads to systematic increases in pH, resulting in false positive readings. This inaccuracy was consistent across all types of sampling devices and diagnoses. Therefore, vaginal pH should not be measured from the wet mount slide.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 366, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 449}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.4286000000000003e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_582", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Whether mutation status should be used to guide therapy is an important issue in many cancers. We correlated mutation profile in radioiodine-refractory (RAIR) metastatic thyroid cancers (TCs) with patient outcome and response to tyrosine kinase inhibitors (TKIs), and discussed the results with other published data.', 'Outcome in 82 consecutive patients with metastatic RAIR thyroid carcinoma prospectively tested for BRAF, RAS and PI3KCA mutations was retrospectively analyzed, including 55 patients treated with multikinase inhibitors.', 'Papillary thyroid carcinomas (PTCs) were the most frequent histological subtype (54.9 %), followed by poorly differentiated thyroid carcinoma [PDTC] (30.5 %) and follicular thyroid carcinoma [FTC](14.6 %). A genetic mutation was identified in 23 patients (28 %) and BRAF was the most frequently mutated gene (23 %). Median progression-free survival (PFS) on first-line TKI treatment was 14.6 months (95% CI 9.9-18.4). BRAF mutation positively influenced median PFS, both in the entire TKI-treated cohort (median PFS 34.7 months versus 11.6 months; hazard ratio [HR] 0.29; 95% CI 0.09-0.98; p\\u2009=\\u20090.03) and in the TKI-treated PTC cohort (n\\u2009=\\u200922) [log-rank p\\u2009=\\u20090.086; HR 2.95; 95 % CI 0.81-10.70). However, in TKI-treated patients, PDTC histologic subtype was the only independent prognostic factor for PFS identified in the multivariate analysis (HR 2.36; 95% CI 1.01-5.54; p\\u2009=\\u20090.048).']\n\nQuestion: Does Molecular Genotype Provide Useful Information in the Management of Radioiodine Refractory Thyroid Cancers?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study indicates that mutation status, specifically the BRAF mutation, correlates with progression-free survival in patients treated with tyrosine kinase inhibitors. While histological subtype was identified as an independent prognostic factor, the findings suggest that molecular profiling provides clinically relevant information for managing these cancers. Therefore, the most likely answer is yes.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 540, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 608}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:28.840088+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000237, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_583", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The International Association of the Diabetes and Pregnancy Study Groups (IADPSG) recently recommended new criteria for diagnosing gestational diabetes mellitus (GDM). This study was undertaken to determine whether adopting the IADPSG criteria would be cost-effective, compared with the current standard of care.', 'We developed a decision analysis model comparing the cost-utility of three strategies to identify GDM: 1) no screening, 2) current screening practice (1-h 50-g glucose challenge test between 24 and 28 weeks followed by 3-h 100-g glucose tolerance test when indicated), or 3) screening practice proposed by the IADPSG. Assumptions included that 1) women diagnosed with GDM received additional prenatal monitoring, mitigating the risks of preeclampsia, shoulder dystocia, and birth injury; and 2) GDM women had opportunity for intensive postdelivery counseling and behavior modification to reduce future diabetes risks. The primary outcome measure was the incremental cost-effectiveness ratio (ICER).', 'Our model demonstrates that the IADPSG recommendations are cost-effective only when postdelivery care reduces diabetes incidence. For every 100,000 women screened, 6,178 quality-adjusted life-years (QALYs) are gained, at a cost of $125,633,826. The ICER for the IADPSG strategy compared with the current standard was $20,336 per QALY gained. When postdelivery care was not accomplished, the IADPSG strategy was no longer cost-effective. These results were robust in sensitivity analyses.']\n\nQuestion: Screening for gestational diabetes mellitus: are the criteria proposed by the international association of the Diabetes and Pregnancy Study Groups cost-effective?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that the IADPSG criteria are cost-effective only if postdelivery care reduces future diabetes incidence, with an ICER of $20,336 per QALY gained, which is generally considered cost-effective. However, without effective postdelivery interventions, the strategy is not cost-effective. Given that the model supports cost-effectiveness under realistic assumptions, the best answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 507, "output_tokens": 104, "total_tokens": 611}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.6396999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_587", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['An association has been described between elevated serum angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) and an increased risk of severe hypoglycaemia (SH). To ascertain whether this reported association could be replicated in a different country, it was re-examined in 300 individuals with Type 1 diabetes.', 'People with Type 1 diabetes, none of whom was taking renin-angiotensin system blocking drugs, were recruited. Participants recorded the frequency with which they had experienced SH. Glycated haemoglobin (HbA(1c)) and serum ACE were measured. The difference in the incidence of SH between different quartiles of ACE activity and the relationship between serum ACE and SH were examined using non-parametric statistical tests and a negative binomial model.', \"Data were obtained from 300 patients [158 male; HbA(1c) median (range) 8.2% (5.2-12.8%), median age 36 years (16-88); duration of diabetes 14.5 years (2-49)]. The incidence of SH was 0.93 episodes per patient year. The mean incidence of SH in the top and bottom quartiles of ACE activity was 0.5 and 1.7 episodes per patient year, respectively, but this difference was not statistically significant (P = 0.075). Spearman's test showed a very weak, although statistically significant, association between serum ACE level and SH incidence (r = 0.115, P = 0.047). The binomial model also showed a statistically significant (P = 0.002), but clinically weak, relationship between serum ACE and SH.\"]\n\nQuestion: Serum angiotensin-converting enzyme and frequency of severe hypoglycaemia in Type 1 diabetes: does a relationship exist?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found a statistically significant but clinically weak relationship between serum ACE levels and severe hypoglycemia incidence, as shown by both Spearman's test (P = 0.047) and the negative binomial model (P = 0.002). Although the difference in SH incidence between the top and bottom ACE quartiles was not significant (P = 0.075), the overall statistical models support a weak association. Therefore, the evidence suggests a relationship exists, albeit a small one.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 469, "output_tokens": 112, "total_tokens": 581}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.4499e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_588", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Studies have identified clinical predictors to guide radiologic evaluation of the cervical spine in geriatric patients. We hypothesized that clinical predictors are not adequate in the identification of cervical spine fractures in geriatric blunt trauma patients with low-energy mechanism.', 'A retrospective case-control study was performed on geriatric blunt trauma patients sustaining low-energy trauma from January 2000 to January 2006. A data form including 8 clinical predictors was completed for each group.', 'There were 35 study and 64 control patients identified. Both groups were similar in age (study 83.6 vs control 81.2) and injury severity score (study 9.06 vs control 9.61). Only neck tenderness exceeded the expected occurrence in the presence of a cervical spine injury (chi(2) = 18.1, P = .001) in just 45.5% of the study group.']\n\nQuestion: Cervical spine fractures in geriatric blunt trauma patients with low-energy mechanism: are clinical predictors adequate?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that only neck tenderness was significantly associated with cervical spine fractures, but it was present in only 45.5% of patients with fractures, indicating poor sensitivity. This suggests that clinical predictors are not reliable for ruling out fractures in this population. Therefore, clinical predictors are not adequate.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 295, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 361}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.7544999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_592", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The present study asked whether the processing of affective prosody is modulated by spatial attention. Pseudo-words with a neutral, happy, threatening, and fearful prosody were presented at two spatial positions. Participants attended to one position in order to detect infrequent targets. Emotional prosody was task irrelevant. The electro-encephalogram (EEG) was recorded to assess processing differences as a function of spatial attention and emotional valence.', 'Event-related potentials (ERPs) differed as a function of emotional prosody both when attended and when unattended. While emotional prosody effects interacted with effects of spatial attention at early processing levels (<200 ms), these effects were additive at later processing stages (>200 ms).']\n\nQuestion: Is the processing of affective prosody influenced by spatial attention?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that event-related potentials (ERPs) related to emotional prosody interacted with spatial attention at early processing levels (<200 ms), indicating modulation by attention. Although the effects were additive at later stages, the presence of an interaction at early stages confirms that spatial attention influences affective prosody processing. Therefore, the answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 241, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 316}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.4611e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_594", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Recent reports indicate that the prevalence of bipolar disorder (BD) in patients with an acute major depressive episode might be higher than previously thought. We aimed to study systematically all patients who sought therapy for major depressive episode (MDE) within the BRIDGE study in Germany, reporting on an increased number (increased from 2 in the international BRIDGE report to 5) of different diagnostic algorithms.', \"A total of 252 patients with acute MDE (DSM-IV confirmed) were examined for the existence of BD (a) according to DSM-IV criteria, (b) according to modified DSM-IV criteria (without the exclusion criterion of 'mania not induced by substances/antidepressants'), (c) according to a Bipolarity Specifier Algorithm which expands the DSM-IV criteria, (d) according to HCL-32R (Hypomania-Checklist-32R), and (e) according to a criteria-free physician's diagnosis.\", \"The five different diagnostic approaches yielded immensely variable prevalences for BD: (a) 11.6; (b) 24.8%; (c) 40.6%; (d) 58.7; e) 18.4% with only partial overlap between diagnoses according to the physician's diagnosis or HCL-32R with diagnoses according to the three DSM-based algorithms.\"]\n\nQuestion: Are bipolar disorders underdiagnosed in patients with depressive episodes?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The varying prevalence rates of bipolar disorder (BD) across different diagnostic methods\u2014ranging from 11.6% to 58.7%\u2014suggest that standard criteria (like DSM-IV) may miss many cases. The higher detection rates with broader tools (e.g., HCL-32R and modified criteria) indicate that BD is likely underdiagnosed when relying solely on traditional methods. This supports the conclusion that bipolar disorders are underdiagnosed in patients with depressive episodes.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 377, "output_tokens": 107, "total_tokens": 484}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.7467e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_596", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The objective of this study was to determine the most effective content of pictorial health warning labels (HWLs) and whether educational attainment moderates these effects.', 'Field experiments were conducted with 529 adult smokers and 530 young adults (258 nonsmokers; 271 smokers). Participants reported responses to different pictorial HWLs printed on cigarette packages. One experiment involved manipulating textual form (testimonial narrative vs. didactic) and the other involved manipulating image type (diseased organs vs. human suffering).', 'Tests of mean ratings and rankings indicated that pictorial HWLs with didactic textual forms had equivalent or significantly higher credibility, relevance, and impact than pictorial HWLs with testimonial forms. Results from mixed-effects models confirmed these results. However, responses differed by participant educational attainment: didactic forms were consistently rated higher than testimonials among participants with higher education, whereas the difference between didactic and testimonial narrative forms was weaker or not statistically significant among participants with lower education. In the second experiment, with textual content held constant, greater credibility, relevance, and impact was found for graphic imagery of diseased organs than imagery of human suffering.']\n\nQuestion: Can pictorial warning labels on cigarette packages address smoking-related health disparities?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study indicates that the effectiveness of different types of pictorial warning labels varies based on a participant's educational attainment. Because these labels impact different demographic groups in distinct ways, they have the potential to address or influence smoking-related health disparities. Therefore, the most likely answer is yes.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 316, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 379}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:32.239640+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0001735, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_598", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Sources of reports about laparoscopic and percutaneous treatment of liver hydatid cysts are limited to just a few countries. To address the reason behind this, we carried out a survey of 30 surgeons in northern Jordan.', 'A questionnaire was distributed to collect data regarding the surgical technique preferred by each surgeon. Further information was collected from those not adopting minimal-access techniques to determine their reasons for not doing so.', 'Only 3 surgeons (10%) considered laparoscopy as the first line of treatment. Of the 27 surgeons who did not consider percutaneous or laparoscopic treatment, fear of anaphylaxis and/or dissemination was the main reason given by 21 surgeons (78%) for not using minimal access techniques.']\n\nQuestion: Is fear of anaphylactic shock discouraging surgeons from more widely adopting percutaneous and laparoscopic techniques in the treatment of liver hydatid cyst?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context states that 21 out of 27 surgeons who do not use minimal-access techniques cited fear of anaphylaxis and/or dissemination as the main reason. This indicates that fear of anaphylactic shock is a significant barrier to adopting these techniques. Therefore, the evidence supports that fear is indeed discouraging wider adoption.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 266, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 340}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.6286000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_60", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"Voluntary asphyxiation among children, preteens, and adolescents by hanging or other means of inducing hypoxia/anoxia to enhance sexual excitement is not uncommon and can lead to unintended death. This study addresses autoerotic asphyxiation (AEA) with the intent of increasing pediatricians' knowledge of the syndrome and awareness of its typical onset among young patients. AEA is characteristically a clandestine and elusive practice. Provided with relevant information, pediatricians can identify the syndrome, demonstrate a willingness to discuss concerns about it, ameliorate distress, and possibly prevent a tragedy.\", 'A retrospective study was undertaken of published cases both fatal and nonfatal and included personal communications, referenced citations, clinical experience, and theoretical formulations as to causation. Characteristic AEA manifestations, prevalence, age range, methods of inducing hypoxia/anoxia, and gender weighting are presented. All sources were used as a basis for additional considerations of etiology and possibilities for intervention.', 'AEA can be conceptualized as a personalized, ritualized, and symbolic biopsychosocial drama. It seems to be a reenactment of intense emotional feeling-states involving an identification and sadomasochistic relationship with a female figure. Inept AEA practitioners can miscalculate the peril of the situation that they have contrived and for numerous reasons lose their gamble with death.']\n\nQuestion: Autoerotic asphyxiation: secret pleasure--lethal outcome?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The passage describes autoerotic asphyxiation (AEA) as a secretive practice aimed at enhancing sexual excitement through hypoxia, often leading to accidental death, especially among young individuals. It emphasizes that AEA is clandestine, potentially fatal, and rooted in complex psychological dynamics. Given the evidence of both intentional pleasure-seeking and high risk of lethal outcomes, the most accurate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 471, "output_tokens": 110, "total_tokens": 581}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.4441e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_600", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['48 cases of SbCC were analysed immunohistochemically using monoclonal \u03b2-catenin antibody and the results correlated with tumour size, histopathological differentiation, orbital invasion and pagetoid spread.', 'Cytoplasmic overexpression of \u03b2-catenin was seen in 66% cases of SbCC which correlated positively with tumour size, orbital invasion and pagetoid spread. This correlation was found to be significant in tumour size>2 cm (p = 0.242). Nuclear staining was not observed in any of the cases.']\n\nQuestion: Does \u03b2-catenin have a role in pathogenesis of sebaceous cell carcinoma of the eyelid?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The cytoplasmic overexpression of \u03b2-catenin in 66% of sebaceous cell carcinoma (SbCC) cases, along with its significant correlation with aggressive features like larger tumor size, orbital invasion, and pagetoid spread, suggests involvement in tumor progression. Although nuclear staining (indicative of canonical Wnt pathway activation) was absent, cytoplasmic accumulation may still contribute to pathogenesis through alternative mechanisms. Therefore, \u03b2-catenin likely plays a role in the disease.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 220, "output_tokens": 109, "total_tokens": 329}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.652e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_603", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['This prospective case-control study consisted of 33 patients with pre-eclampsia and 32 normotensive pregnant patients as controls. All of the subjects underwent otoscopic examinations - pure tone audiometry (0.25-16\\u2009kHz) and transient evoked otoacoustic emission (1-4\\u2009kHz) tests - during their third trimester of pregnancy.', 'The mean ages of the patients with pre-eclampsia and the control subjects were 29.6\\u2009\u00b1\\u20095.7 and 28.6\\u2009\u00b1\\u20095.3 years, respectively. The baseline demographic characteristics, including age, gravidity, parity number, and gestational week, were similar between the two patient groups. Hearing thresholds in the right ear at 1, 4, 8, and 10\\u2009kHz and in the left ear at 8 and 10\\u2009kHz were significantly higher in the patients with pre-eclampsia compared to the control subjects. The degree of systolic blood pressure measured at the time of diagnosis had a deteriorating effect on hearing at 8, 10, and 12\\u2009kHz in the right ear and at 10\\u2009kHz in the left ear.']\n\nQuestion: Hearing loss: an unknown complication of pre-eclampsia?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found significantly higher hearing thresholds at multiple frequencies in patients with pre-eclampsia compared to controls, suggesting an association between pre-eclampsia and hearing loss. Additionally, higher systolic blood pressure was linked to worse hearing, supporting a potential causal relationship. These findings indicate that hearing loss may indeed be an unknown complication of pre-eclampsia.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 388, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 467}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.5448000000000003e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_604", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The purpose of this study was to investigate the efficacy of ultrasonography to confirm Schanz pin placement in a cadaveric model, and the interobserver repeatability of the ultrasound methodology.', 'This investigation is a repeated measures cadaveric study with multiple examiners.', 'Cadaveric preparation and observations were done by an orthopaedic traumatologist and resident, and two general surgery traumatologists.', 'A total of 16 Schanz pins were equally placed in bilateral femora and tibiae. Four examiners took measurements of pin protrusion beyond the distal cortices using first ultrasonography and then by direct measurement after gross dissection.MAIN OUTCOME MEASURE(S): Distal Schanz pin protrusion length measurements from both ultrasonography and direct measurement post dissection.', 'Schanz pin protrusion measurements are underestimated by ultrasonography (p<0.01) by an average of 10 percent over the range of 5 to 18 mm, and they display a proportional bias that increases the under reporting as the magnitude of pin protrusion increases. Ultrasound data demonstrate good linear correlation and closely represent actual protrusion values in the 5 to 12 mm range. Interobserver repeatability analysis demonstrated that all examiners were not statistically different in their measurements despite minimal familiarity with the ultrasound methodology (p>0.8).']\n\nQuestion: Is portable ultrasonography accurate in the evaluation of Schanz pin placement during extremity fracture fixation in austere environments?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study reports that ultrasonography underestimates actual Schanz pin protrusion by an average of 10% (with proportional bias that grows at larger values) yet shows good linear correlation and close agreement in the clinically relevant 5\u201312 mm range, plus strong inter-observer repeatability. These mixed quantitative findings indicate that ultrasonography is neither fully accurate nor wholly unreliable for austere-environment use. Consequently the most defensible choice among the given options is \u201cmaybe.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 466, "output_tokens": 93, "total_tokens": 559}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000815, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_606", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['In patients with Los Angeles (LA) grade C or D oesophagitis, a positive relationship has been established between the duration of intragastric acid suppression and healing.AIM: To determine whether there is an apparent optimal time of intragastric acid suppression for maximal healing of reflux oesophagitis.', 'Post hoc analysis of data from a proof-of-concept, double-blind, randomized study of 134 adult patients treated with esomeprazole (10 or 40 mg od for 4 weeks) for LA grade C or D oesophagitis. A curve was fitted to pooled 24-h intragastric pH (day 5) and endoscopically assessed healing (4 weeks) data using piecewise quadratic logistic regression.', 'Maximal reflux oesophagitis healing rates were achieved when intragastric pH>4 was achieved for approximately 50-70% (12-17 h) of the 24-h period. Acid suppression above this threshold did not yield further increases in healing rates.']\n\nQuestion: A model of healing of Los Angeles grades C and D reflux oesophagitis: is there an optimal time of acid suppression for maximal healing?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that maximal healing of LA grades C and D oesophagitis occurs when intragastric pH > 4 is maintained for 50\u201370% of the day (12\u201317 hours), with no additional benefit beyond this range. This indicates a clear threshold for optimal acid suppression, supporting the existence of an optimal time. Therefore, the evidence points to a definitive \"yes.\"\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 332, "output_tokens": 90, "total_tokens": 422}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.2572000000000006e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_607", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To evaluate the diagnostic accuracy of gadofosveset-enhanced magnetic resonance (MR) angiography in the assessment of carotid artery stenosis, with digital subtraction angiography (DSA) as the reference standard, and to determine the value of reading first-pass, steady-state, and \"combined\" (first-pass plus steady-state) MR angiograms.', 'This study was approved by the local ethics committee, and all subjects gave written informed consent. MR angiography and DSA were performed in 84 patients (56 men, 28 women; age range, 61-76 years) with carotid artery stenosis at Doppler ultrasonography. Three readers reviewed the first-pass, steady-state, and combined MR data sets, and one independent observer evaluated the DSA images to assess stenosis degree, plaque morphology and ulceration, stenosis length, and tandem lesions. Interobserver agreement regarding MR angiographic findings was analyzed by using intraclass correlation and Cohen kappa coefficients. Sensitivity, specificity, positive predictive value (PPV), and negative predictive value (NPV) were calculated by using the McNemar test to determine possible significant differences (P<.05).', 'Interobserver agreement regarding all MR angiogram readings was substantial. For grading stenosis, sensitivity, specificity, PPV, and NPV were, respectively, 90%, 92%, 91%, and 91% for first-pass imaging; 95% each for steady-state imaging; and 96%, 99%, 99%, and 97% for combined imaging. For evaluation of plaque morphology, respective values were 84%, 86%, 88%, and 82% for first-pass imaging; 98%, 97%, 98%, and 97% for steady-state imaging; and 98%, 100%, 100%, and 97% for combined imaging. Differences between the first-pass, steady-state, and combined image readings for assessment of stenosis degree and plaque morphology were significant (P<.001).']\n\nQuestion: Gadofosveset-enhanced MR angiography of carotid arteries: does steady-state imaging improve accuracy of first-pass imaging?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data show that steady-state imaging has higher sensitivity, specificity, positive predictive value, and negative predictive value than first-pass imaging for both stenosis grading and plaque morphology. The differences between first-pass, steady-state, and combined imaging were statistically significant (P<.001), indicating improved accuracy with steady-state imaging. Therefore, steady-state imaging does improve diagnostic accuracy compared to first-pass imaging alone.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 552, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 639}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.7891999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_608", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['This study aims to examine the accuracy of a new sternal skin conductance (SSC) device in measuring hot flashes and to assess the acceptability of the device by women.', 'Three small descriptive pilot studies were performed using two sequential prototypes of the SSC device developed by an engineering device company in the Midwest. The devices were worn either in a monitored setting for 24 hours or in an ambulatory setting for 5 weeks. During the study period, women recorded hot flashes in a prospective hot flash diary and answered questions about the acceptability of wearing the SSC device.', 'The first prototype was not able to collect any analyzable skin conductance data owing to various malfunction issues, including poor conductance and battery failure. However, 16 women wore the device for 5 weeks and reported that wearing the device was acceptable, although 31% stated that it interfered with daily activities. Hot flash data from the second prototype revealed a 24% concordance rate between self-reported and device-recorded hot flashes.']\n\nQuestion: Sternal skin conductance: a reasonable surrogate for hot flash measurement?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The second prototype of the SSC device showed only a 24% concordance rate between self-reported and device-recorded hot flashes, indicating poor agreement. Although the device was generally acceptable to wear, its accuracy in detecting hot flashes was low. Therefore, based on the data, sternal skin conductance does not appear to be a reliable surrogate for hot flash measurement.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 301, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 381}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.9370999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_609", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The elephant trunk technique for aortic dissection is useful for reducing false lumen pressure; however, a folded vascular prosthesis inside the aorta can cause haemolysis. The purpose of this study was to investigate whether an elephant trunk in a small-calibre lumen can cause haemolysis.', 'Inpatient and outpatient records were retrospectively reviewed.', 'Two cases of haemolytic anaemia after aortic surgery using the elephant trunk technique were identified from 2011 to 2013. A 64-year-old man, who underwent graft replacement of the ascending aorta for acute Stanford type A aortic dissection, presented with enlargement of the chronic dissection of the descending aorta and moderate aortic regurgitation. A two-stage surgery was scheduled. Total arch replacement with an elephant trunk in the true lumen and concomitant aortic valve replacement were performed. Postoperatively, he developed severe haemolytic anaemia because of the folded elephant trunk. The anaemia improved after the second surgery, including graft replacement of the descending aorta. Similarly, a 61-year-old man, who underwent total arch replacement for acute Stanford type A aortic dissection, presented with enlargement of the chronic dissection of the descending aorta. Graft replacement of the descending aorta with an elephant trunk inserted into the true lumen was performed. The patient postoperatively developed haemolytic anaemia because of the folded elephant trunk, which improved after additional stent grafting into the elephant trunk.']\n\nQuestion: Elephant trunk in a small-calibre true lumen for chronic aortic dissection: cause of haemolytic anaemia?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The described cases demonstrate that a folded elephant trunk placed in the true lumen can lead to mechanical hemolysis due to turbulent blood flow or shear stress. Both patients developed haemolytic anaemia postoperatively, which resolved after corrective procedures addressed the folded graft. This supports that the elephant trunk in a small-calibre lumen can indeed cause haemolytic anaemia.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 420, "output_tokens": 82, "total_tokens": 502}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.802e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_61", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Comorbid major depression (MD) and alcohol use disorder (AUD), particularly in adolescents, have been shown to be associated with poorer subsequent MD outcomes.', 'Longitudinal data were used to model associations between a four-level classification of MD/AUD during the period 15-18 years (neither; MD-only; AUD-only; comorbid MD/AUD) and MD over the period 18-35 years. These associations were then adjusted for confounding by a series of factors measured in childhood.', 'The three disorder groups had rates of adult MD during the period 18-35 years that were significantly (p<.05) higher than that of the group with no disorder. Furthermore, those in the comorbid MD/AUD group had significantly (p<.05) higher rates of adult MD than those in the AUD-only group, and marginally (p<.10) higher rates of adult MD than those in the MD-only group. After adjustment for confounding, the difference in rates of adult MD between the MD-only group and the MD/AUD group were no longer statistically significant. The factors that explained the associations were gender, childhood behavior problems, and exposure to physical and sexual abuse.', 'The data were obtained by self-report, and may have been subject to biases.']\n\nQuestion: Major depression and alcohol use disorder in adolescence: Does comorbidity lead to poorer outcomes of depression?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that comorbid MD/AUD in adolescence was initially associated with higher rates of adult MD compared to MD-only, but this difference became non-significant after adjusting for childhood confounders like behavior problems and abuse. This suggests that the poorer outcomes are not due to comorbidity itself, but rather to shared underlying risk factors. Therefore, the answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 370, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 451}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.437e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_610", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The optimum protocol for expander volume adjustment with respect to the timing and application of radiotherapy remains controversial.', 'Eighteen New Zealand rabbits were divided into three groups. Metallic port integrated anatomic breast expanders of 250 cc were implanted on the back of each animal and controlled expansion was performed. Group I underwent radiotherapy with full expanders while in Group II, expanders were partially deflated immediately prior to radiotherapy. Control group did not receive radiotherapy.The changes in blood flow at different volume adjustments were investigated in Group II by laser Doppler flowmetry. Variations in the histopathologic properties of the irradiated tissues including the skin, capsule and the pocket floor, were compared in the biopsy specimens taken from different locations in each group.', 'A significant increase in skin blood flow was detected in Group II with partial expander deflation. Overall, histopathologic exam revealed aggravated findings of chronic radiodermatitis (epidermal atrophy, dermal inflammation and fibrosis, neovascularisation and vascular changes as well as increased capsule thickness) especially around the lower expander pole, in Group II.']\n\nQuestion: Does partial expander deflation exacerbate the adverse effects of radiotherapy in two-stage breast reconstruction?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The histopathologic results show aggravated findings of chronic radiodermatitis, including increased capsule thickness and vascular changes, especially in Group II (partial deflation), despite improved blood flow. This suggests that partial deflation, while increasing perfusion, is associated with worse tissue damage from radiotherapy. Therefore, partial expander deflation does exacerbate the adverse effects of radiotherapy.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 325, "output_tokens": 82, "total_tokens": 407}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.1275e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_613", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Guidelines emphasize that irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) is not a diagnosis of exclusion and encourage clinicians to make a positive diagnosis using the Rome criteria alone. Yet many clinicians are concerned about overlooking alternative diagnoses. We measured beliefs about whether IBS is a diagnosis of exclusion, and measured testing proclivity between IBS experts and community providers.', 'We developed a survey to measure decision-making in two standardized patients with Rome III-positive IBS, including IBS with diarrhea (D-IBS) and IBS with constipation (C-IBS). The survey elicited provider knowledge and beliefs about IBS, including testing proclivity and beliefs regarding IBS as a diagnosis of exclusion. We surveyed nurse practitioners, primary care physicians, community gastroenterologists, and IBS experts.', 'Experts were less likely than nonexperts to endorse IBS as a diagnosis of exclusion (8 vs. 72%; P<0.0001). In the D-IBS vignette, experts were more likely to make a positive diagnosis of IBS (67 vs. 38%; P<0.001), to perform fewer tests (2.0 vs. 4.1; P<0.01), and to expend less money on testing (US$297 vs. $658; P<0.01). Providers who believed IBS is a diagnosis of exclusion ordered 1.6 more tests and consumed $364 more than others (P<0.0001). Experts only rated celiac sprue screening and complete blood count as appropriate in D-IBS; nonexperts rated most tests as appropriate. Parallel results were found in the C-IBS vignette.']\n\nQuestion: Is irritable bowel syndrome a diagnosis of exclusion?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context states that guidelines emphasize IBS is **not** a diagnosis of exclusion and that experts are less likely to view it as such. It also highlights that providers who believe it is a diagnosis of exclusion order more tests unnecessarily. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 447, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 506}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.7637e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_616", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"Because of the inflammatory nature of Crohn's disease, ileocolic resections are often difficult to perform, especially if an abscess, phlegmon, or recurrent disease at a previous ileocolic anastomosis is present. Our goal was to determine whether the above factors are contraindications to a successful laparoscopic-assisted ileocolic resection.\", \"Between 1992 and 1996, 46 laparoscopic-assisted ileocolic resections were attempted. Fourteen patients had an abscess or phlegmon treated with bowel rest before operation (group I), 10 patients had recurrent Crohn's disease at the previous ileocolic anastomosis (group II), and 22 patients had no previous operation and no phlegmon or abscess associated with their disease (group III). These groups were compared with each other and with 70 consecutive open ileocolic resections for Crohn's disease during the same time period (group IV).\", 'Operative blood loss and time were greater in group IV than in groups I, II, and III (245 versus 151, 131, and 195 ml, respectively, and 202 versus 152, 144, and 139 minutes, respectively). Conversion to open procedure occurred in 5 patients (group I, 1 [7%]; group II, 2 [20%]; group III, 2 [9%]). Morbidity was highest in group IV (21% versus 0%, 10%, and 10%, respectively). Only one patient died (group IV, 1%). Length of hospital stay was longest in group IV (7.9 versus 4.8, 3.9, and 4.5 days, respectively).']\n\nQuestion: Laparoscopic-assisted ileocolic resections in patients with Crohn's disease: are abscesses, phlegmons, or recurrent disease contraindications?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that laparoscopic-assisted ileocolic resections were successfully performed in patients with abscesses, phlegmons, or recurrent disease, with lower morbidity and shorter hospital stays compared to open surgery. Although conversion rates were slightly higher in some groups, the procedure was feasible and safe. Therefore, these factors are not absolute contraindications.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 502, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 581}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.3542e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_62", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To characterize the use and delivery of cough and cold medicines in children younger than 6 presenting to an inner-city pediatric emergency department (PED) following 2007 FDA warnings.', 'A cross-sectional observational study was performed using a convenience sampling of PED patients during the fall of 2010. Caregivers were presented with 6 commonly used cough medicine preparations and were asked to demonstrate if and how they would administer these to their children.', 'In all, 65 patients and their caregivers consented and participated in the study. During the demonstration, 82% (53/65) stated that they would treat with cough or cold medicines, and 72% (38/53) incorrectly dosed the medication they desired to give.']\n\nQuestion: Cold preparation use in young children after FDA warnings: do concerns still exist?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that 82% of caregivers still used cough and cold medicines in children under 6 despite FDA warnings, and 72% of those dosed the medication incorrectly. This indicates ongoing use and misuse of these medications after the warnings. Therefore, concerns about cold preparation use in young children still exist.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 251, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 320}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.4720999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_620", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The aim of the present study was to assess the effects of exercise training on heart rate, QT interval, and on the relation between ventricular repolarization and heart rate in men and women.', 'A 24 h Holter recording was obtained in 80 healthy subjects (40 males) who differed for the degree of physical activity. Trained individuals showed a lower heart rate and a higher heart rate variability than sedentary subjects, independent of the gender difference in basal heart rate. Mean 24 h QTc was similar in trained and non-trained men, while a significant difference was observed between trained and non-trained women. Exercise training reduced the QT/RR slope in both genders. This effect on the QT/RR relation was more marked in women; in fact, the gender difference in the ventricular repolarization duration at low heart rate observed in sedentary subjects was no longer present among trained individuals.']\n\nQuestion: Effects of exercise training on heart rate and QT interval in healthy young individuals: are there gender differences?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that while both genders experienced lower heart rates and reduced QT/RR slope with exercise training, there were notable gender differences: QTc duration differed significantly between trained and non-trained women but not men, and the gender difference in repolarization at low heart rates disappeared with training. This indicates that the effects of exercise training on ventricular repolarization and QT/RR dynamics are gender-specific.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 285, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 372}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.8935000000000003e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_622", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The aim of this study was to describe the evolution and epidemiologic characteristics of shigellosis patients over a 25 year period in a large city.', 'Shigellosis is a notifiable disease in Spain since 1988. Cases are analyzed in Barcelona residents included in the registry between 1988-2012. A descriptive analysis by sex, age, mode of transmission and Shigella species is presented. Trend analysis and time series were performed.', 'Of the 559 cases analyzed, 60.15% were males. A sustained increase was observed in the trend since 2008 in males (p<0,05), especially at the expense of males who had no history of food poisoning or travel to endemic areas. The increasing tendency was greater in males from 21 to 60 years, both for S. flexneri (since 2009), and for S. sonnei (since 2004). In 2012 it was noted that in the men with S. flexneri, the 63% were men who have sex with men.']\n\nQuestion: Analysis of the epidemiological pattern of Shigellosis in Barcelona between 1988 and 2012: Is it an emerging sexually transmitted infection?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data show a sustained increase in shigellosis among males, particularly men who have sex with men (MSM), with 63% of *S. flexneri* cases in 2012 linked to this group. The rise is not explained by foodborne illness or travel, suggesting sexual transmission as a key driver. This pattern supports shigellosis emerging as a sexually transmitted infection in this population.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 355, "output_tokens": 93, "total_tokens": 448}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.4504999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_625", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The neonatal infection by Streptococcus group B is one of the main causes of neonatal morbi-mortality rate. For this reason a screening is made to each pregnant woman in order to detect its presence, and if it was the case, to apply an antibiotic treatment during labour. The aim of this study was to know the prevalence of this Streptococcus in the pregnant women from Melilla, as well as the differences according to culture and age.', 'A descriptive cross-sectional study located in the Hospital Comarcal from Melilla.', 'The sample is taken from 280 women: 194 are from Muslim culture (69.3%), 68 are from Christian culture (24.3%) and 18 women from unknown cultures (6.4%). Also it is known that 78 of them are 25 years old or less (27.85%), 158 are between 26 and 34 years old (56.42%) and 44 are 35 years old or more (15.71%).']\n\nQuestion: PREVALENCE OF THE STREPTOCOCUS AGALACTIAE IN THE PREGNANT WOMAN FROM THE AUTONOMIC CITY OF MELILLA: IS CULTURE A DETERMINANT FACTOR?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The provided context describes a study on the prevalence of Streptococcus agalactiae (Group B Streptococcus) in pregnant women in Melilla, including breakdowns by culture and age, but it does not present the actual results or statistical analysis linking culture to prevalence. Without data showing a significant association between culture and infection rates, we cannot conclude that culture is a determinant factor. Therefore, based on the information given, the most appropriate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 354, "output_tokens": 99, "total_tokens": 453}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.5034e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_627", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Embolisation of atherosclerotic debris during abdominal aortic aneurysm (AAA) repair is responsible for significant peri-operative morbidity. Reports have suggested that preferential clamping of the distal vessel(s) before the proximal aorta may decrease the number of emboli passing distally and hence reduce complications.', 'Forty patients undergoing AAA repair were randomised to have either first clamping of the proximal aorta or the iliac vessels. Emboli passing through the Superficial Femoral Arteries were detected with a Transcranial Doppler ultrasound system.', 'There was no difference between the two groups in the number of emboli detected (p=0.49) and no significant correlation between number of emboli and dissection time (r=0.0008). However, there was a significantly higher number of emboli in the patient sub-group that were current smokers (p=0.034).']\n\nQuestion: Does the sequence of clamp application during open abdominal aortic aneurysm surgery influence distal embolisation?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant difference in the number of emboli detected between patients who had proximal aorta clamping versus iliac vessel clamping (p=0.49). This suggests that the sequence of clamp application does not influence distal embolisation. Therefore, the evidence does not support a beneficial effect of clamp sequence on reducing embolic events.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 297, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 376}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.8987000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_63", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Bystander resuscitation plays an important role in lifesaving cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR). A significant reduction in the \"no-flow-time\", quantitatively better chest compressions and an improved quality of ventilation can be demonstrated during CPR using supraglottic airway devices (SADs). Previous studies have demonstrated the ability of inexperienced persons to operate SADs after brief instruction. The aim of this pilot study was to determine whether an instruction manual consisting of four diagrams enables laypersons to operate a Laryngeal Mask Supreme\u00ae (LMAS) in the manikin.', 'An instruction manual of four illustrations with speech bubbles displaying the correct use of the LMAS was designed. Laypersons were handed a bag containing a LMAS, a bag mask valve device (BMV), a syringe prefilled with air and the instruction sheet, and were asked to perform and ventilate the manikin as displayed. Time to ventilation was recorded and degree of success evaluated.', 'A total of 150 laypersons took part. Overall 145 participants (96.7%) inserted the LMAS in the manikin in the right direction. The device was inserted inverted or twisted in 13 (8.7%) attempts. Eight (5.3%) individuals recognized this and corrected the position. Within the first 2 minutes 119 (79.3%) applicants were able to insert the LMAS and provide tidal volumes greater than 150 ml (estimated dead space). Time to insertion and first ventilation was 83.2 \u00b1 29 s. No significant difference related to previous BLS training (P = 0.85), technical education (P = 0.07) or gender could be demonstrated (P = 0.25).']\n\nQuestion: Does a 4 diagram manual enable laypersons to operate the Laryngeal Mask Supreme\u00ae?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that 96.7% of laypersons inserted the Laryngeal Mask Supreme\u00ae in the correct direction, and nearly 80% successfully ventilated the manikin within 2 minutes, indicating effective use of the device with the 4-diagram manual. There was no significant impact from prior training or background, suggesting the instructions were clear and easy to follow. Therefore, the evidence supports that the manual enables laypersons to operate the device.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 473, "output_tokens": 101, "total_tokens": 574}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.3683e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_630", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Tuberculosis continues to be a public health problem in emerging countries with a recent evidence of increased incidence of extrapulmonary localization in developed countries probably linked to HIV. To our knowledge the occurrence of cerebro-mediastinal tuberculosis in an immuno-competent child has not been previously described; moreover the child we describe has a probable Say-Barber-Miller syndrome. We discuss a putative causative link between this syndrome and the occurrence of tuberculosis.', 'A seven-year-old girl presented to our department with a history of infantile encephalopathy since birth characterized by a facial dysmorphy (evocative of a bird face), microcephaly, and mental retardation, and with recurrent infections. The child had complained of back pain for several months; the parents reported anorexia, loss of weight. Spinal and cerebral MRI showed a mediastinal mass involving the spine and cerebral lesions evocative of tuberculomas. The tuberculin interdermal reaction was positive. Culture of a vertebral biopsy was positive for Koch bacillus. Anti-tuberculosis treatment improved general and local status. An extensive immunological work-up was normal.']\n\nQuestion: Cerebromediastinal tuberculosis in a child with a probable Say-Barber-Miller syndrome: a causative link?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The case describes cerebro-mediastinal tuberculosis in a child with probable Say-Barber-Miller syndrome and normal immunological work-up, suggesting the syndrome might predispose to severe tuberculosis despite immune competence. However, the evidence for a causative link is circumstantial and based on a single case, so a definitive conclusion cannot be drawn. Therefore, the most appropriate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 340, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 421}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.2239999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_631", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Virtual planning and guided surgery with or without prebent or milled plates are becoming more and more common for mandibular reconstruction with fibular free flaps (FFFs). Although this excellent surgical option is being used more widely, the question of the additional cost of planning and cutting-guide production has to be discussed. In capped payment systems such additional costs have to be offset by other savings if there are no special provisions for extra funding. Our study was designed to determine whether using virtual planning and guided surgery resulted in time saved during surgery and whether this time gain resulted in self-funding of such planning through the time saved.', 'All consecutive cases of FFF surgery were evaluated during a 2-year period. Institutional data were used to determine the price of 1 minute of operative time. The time for fibula molding, plate adaptation, and insetting was recorded.', 'During the defined period, we performed 20 mandibular reconstructions using FFFs, 9 with virtual planning and guided surgery and 11 freehand cases. One minute of operative time was calculated to cost US $47.50. Multiplying this number by the time saved, we found that the additional cost of virtual planning was reduced from US $5,098 to US $1,231.50 with a prebent plate and from US $6,980 to US $3,113.50 for a milled plate.']\n\nQuestion: Are virtual planning and guided surgery for head and neck reconstruction economically viable?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The provided study shows that virtual planning yields meaningful operative time savings (valued at $47.50 per minute), thereby lowering the net added cost from several thousand dollars to a residual $1,231\u2013$3,113 depending on plate type. Because a positive incremental cost remains, full self-funding via time savings alone is not achieved in a capped-payment environment. Consequently, economic viability is not definitively established and hinges on case-specific factors such as willingness-to-pay thresholds or non-monetary benefits.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 488, "output_tokens": 103, "total_tokens": 591}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0008675, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_632", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To compare growth curves of body mass index from children to adolescents, and then to young adults, in Japanese girls and women in birth cohorts born from 1930 to 1999.', 'Retrospective repeated cross sectional annual nationwide surveys (national nutrition survey, Japan) carried out from 1948 to 2005.', 'Japan.', '76,635 females from 1 to 25 years of age.', 'Body mass index.', 'Generally, body mass index decreased in preschool children (2-5 years), increased in children (6-12 years) and adolescents (13-18 years), and slightly decreased in young adults (19-25 years) in these Japanese females. However, the curves differed among birth cohorts. More recent cohorts were more overweight as children but thinner as young women. The increments in body mass index in early childhood were larger in more recent cohorts than in older cohorts. However, the increments in body mass index in adolescents were smaller and the decrease in body mass index in young adults started earlier, with lower peak values in more recent cohorts than in older cohorts. The decrements in body mass index in young adults were similar in all birth cohorts.']\n\nQuestion: Do overweight children necessarily make overweight adults?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that more recent birth cohorts of Japanese females were more overweight as children but became thinner as young adults, with lower peak BMI values and earlier decreases in BMI. This indicates that being overweight in childhood does not necessarily lead to being overweight in adulthood. Therefore, the data suggest that overweight children do not necessarily become overweight adults.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 339, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 411}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.1269e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_634", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Unintended pregnancy has been significantly associated with subsequent female sterilization. Whether women who are sterilized after experiencing an unintended pregnancy are less likely to express desire for sterilization reversal is unknown.', 'This study used national, cross-sectional data collected by the 2006-2010 National Survey of Family Growth. The study sample included women ages 15-44 who were surgically sterile from a tubal sterilization at the time of interview. Multivariable logistic regression was used to examine the relationship between a history of unintended pregnancy and desire for sterilization reversal while controlling for potential confounders.', 'In this nationally representative sample of 1,418 women who were sterile from a tubal sterilization, 78% had a history of at least one unintended pregnancy and 28% expressed a desire to have their sterilization reversed. In unadjusted analysis, having a prior unintended pregnancy was associated with higher odds of expressing desire for sterilization reversal (odds ratio [OR]: 1.80; 95% confidence interval [CI]: 1.15-2.79). In adjusted analysis controlling for sociodemographic factors, unintended pregnancy was no longer significantly associated with desire for reversal (OR: 1.46; 95% CI: 0.91-2.34).']\n\nQuestion: Does a history of unintended pregnancy lessen the likelihood of desire for sterilization reversal?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data show that women with a history of unintended pregnancy were initially more likely to desire sterilization reversal (OR: 1.80), but this association became non-significant after adjusting for sociodemographic factors (OR: 1.46, 95% CI: 0.91\u20132.34). Therefore, a history of unintended pregnancy does not significantly lessen (and may even slightly increase) the likelihood of desiring reversal.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 374, "output_tokens": 101, "total_tokens": 475}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.6654e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_637", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Although the mechanism of muscle wasting in end-stage renal disease is not fully understood, there is increasing evidence that acidosis induces muscle protein degradation and could therefore contribute to the loss of muscle protein stores of patients on hemodialysis, a prototypical state of chronic metabolic acidosis (CMA). Because body protein mass is controlled by the balance between synthesis and degradation, protein loss can occur as result of either increased breakdown, impaired synthesis, or both. Correction of acidosis may therefore help to maintain muscle mass and improve the health of patients with CMA. We evaluated whether alkalizing patients on hemodialysis might have a positive effect on protein synthesis and on nutritional parameters.', 'Eight chronic hemodialysis patients were treated daily with oral sodium bicarbonate (NaHCO(3)) supplementation for 10-14 days, yielding a pre-dialytic plasma bicarbonate concentration of 28.6 +/-1.6 mmol/l. The fractional synthesis rates (FSR) of muscle protein and albumin were obtained by the L-[(2)H(5)ring]phenylalanine flooding technique.', 'Oral NaHCO(3 )supplementation induced a significant increase in serum bicarbonate (21.5 +/- 3.4 vs. 28.6 +/- 1.6 mmol/l; p = 0.018) and blood pH (7.41 vs. 7.46; p = 0.041). The FSR of muscle protein and the FSR of albumin did not change significantly (muscle protein: 2.1 +/- 0.2 vs. 2.0 +/- 0.5% per day, p = 0.39; albumin: 8.3 +/- 2.2 vs. 8.6 +/- 2.5% per day, p = 0.31). Plasma concentrations of insulin-like growth factor 1 decreased significantly (33.4 +/- 21.3 vs. 25.4 +/- 12.3 nmol/l; p = 0.028), whereas thyroid-stimulating hormone, free thyroxin and free triiodothyronine did not change significantly and nutritional parameters showed no improvement.']\n\nQuestion: Does increasing blood pH stimulate protein synthesis in dialysis patients?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that oral sodium bicarbonate supplementation increased blood pH and serum bicarbonate levels, but there was no significant change in the fractional synthesis rates of muscle protein or albumin. Additionally, nutritional parameters did not improve, indicating no measurable stimulation of protein synthesis. Therefore, increasing blood pH does not appear to stimulate protein synthesis in dialysis patients.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 560, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 634}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.7159999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_638", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The present studywas designed to investigate the possible role of T cells in spatial learning ability in mouse after toluene exposure.', 'Eight-week-old male wild-type (WT) and nude mice of BALB/c strain were exposed to toluene (0, 9 and 90 ppm) in a nose-only exposure chamber for 30 min per day for 3 consecutive days and then once per week for 4 weeks. Twenty-four hours after the completion of exposure, we examined the spatial learning ability in each mouse using the Morris water maze apparatus.', 'In the acquisition phase, a longer escape latency was observed in nude mice exposed to 90 ppm toluene on days 3 and 4 when compared with corresponding WT mice. However, the effect of toluene on the escape latency was not significant in nude mice. In the probe trial, WT mice exposed to 90 ppm toluene showed poor retention memory compared with the control group. In the reversal phase, we did not find any significant difference between groups.']\n\nQuestion: Can T-cell deficiency affect spatial learning ability following toluene exposure?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that nude mice (which lack functional T cells) exposed to 90 ppm toluene had longer escape latencies in the acquisition phase compared to wild-type mice, indicating impaired spatial learning. Additionally, while both groups were affected, the differences in performance suggest T-cell deficiency influences the response to toluene. Therefore, T-cell deficiency appears to affect spatial learning ability following toluene exposure.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 303, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 392}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.0413e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_639", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Pigmentary dilution is observed in patients with homocystinuria. Therefore, it is possible that an increase of local homocysteine (Hcy) interferes with normal melanogenesis and plays a role in the pathogenesis of vitiligo. Vitamin B12 and folic acid, levels of which are decreased in vitiligo, are important cofactors in the metabolism of Hcy. Consequently, a nutritional deficiency in either of these two vitamins will result in an increase in homocysteine in the circulation, a finding that we expect to find in vitiligo.', 'To determine the level of Hcy in the blood of patients with vitiligo as a first step in revealing if it has any relationship with the pathogenesis of vitiligo and consequently if this will have an impact on the treatment of vitiligo.', 'Twenty-six patients of both sexes with vitiligo (age range 20-50 years, mean 31.4 +/- 8.09) and 26 age-matched healthy controls were included in the study. After excluding factors that may affect serum Hcy levels, blood samples from patients and controls were obtained for homocysteine determination by enzyme immunoassay.', 'The mean serum level of Hcy was significantly higher in patients with vitiligo than in controls (21.61 +/- 13.28 vs. 13.1 +/- 4.88 micromol L(-1); P<0.001). The Hcy level was significantly higher in male patients than in female patients (28.67 +/- 15.95 vs. 15.56 +/- 6.2 micromol L(-1); P<0.001) and in male controls compared with female controls (15.07 +/- 4.61 vs. 12.05 +/- 4.82 micromol L(-1); P<0.001). The homocysteine level was related to the activity of vitiligo and was significantly higher in patients with progressive disease than in controls (25.4 +/- 14.99 vs. 13.1 +/- 4.88 micromol L(-1); P<0.001). No significant difference in Hcy levels was found between either untreated vitiligo patients (22.77 +/- 13.36 micromol L(-1)) or patients receiving ultraviolet therapy (20.45 +/- 13.73 micromol L(-1)) and the total patient group (21.62 +/- 13.28 micromol L(-1)).']\n\nQuestion: Is there a relationship between homocysteine and vitiligo?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found significantly higher levels of homocysteine in patients with vitiligo compared to healthy controls, particularly in those with progressive disease. This suggests a clear association between elevated homocysteine levels and vitiligo. Therefore, the evidence supports a relationship between homocysteine and vitiligo.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 671, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 742}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 5.4740999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_64", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The aim of this work is to assess a previously described slit-lamp biomicroscopy-based method (SLBM) for measuring pupil diameter and compare it to Colvard infrared pupillometry (CIP).', 'Two examiners performed three repeated measurements with each instrument in 40 healthy eyes. We determined the agreement of SLBM and CIP, intraobserver and interobserver repeatabilities, and interobserver concordance (kappa) and SLBM ability for detecting pupil sizes over 6.0\\xa0mm.', \"The mean (\u00b1standard deviation [SD]) pupil diameter was 5.81 \u00b1 0.70\\xa0mm with SLBM and 6.26 \u00b1 0.68\\xa0mm with CIP (p\\u2009=\\u20090.01) averaging both examiner's results. Mean differences between the SLBM and CIP were -0.60\\xa0mm and -0.30\\xa0mm for each examiner using the average of the three readings (p\\u2009=\\u20090.02), and they were very similar using the first reading. Intraobserver reproducibility: the width of the 95% LoA ranged from 1.79 to 2.30\\xa0mm. The ICCs were 0.97 and 0.92 for SLBM, and 0.96 and 0.90 for CIP. Interobserver reproducibility: the width of the LoA ranged from 1.82 to 2.09\\xa0mm. Kappa statistics were 0.39 and 0.49 for the first and mean SLBM readings, respectively, and 0.45 for both the first and mean CIP readings. Sensitivity and specificity of SLBM for detection of pupils larger than 6\\xa0mm ranged from 55.56% to 73.68% and from 76.19% to 95.45%, respectively. The best trade-off between sensitivity and specificity ranged from 5.4\\xa0mm to 6.2\\xa0mm.\"]\n\nQuestion: Can we measure mesopic pupil size with the cobalt blue light slit-lamp biomicroscopy method?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The provided context describes an SLBM approach that produces systematically smaller pupil measurements than CIP (by ~0.3\u20130.6 mm) together with only moderate inter-observer concordance. This difference is expected once visible illumination (here cobalt-blue slit-lamp light) is introduced, because any visible light drives pupil constriction and therefore precludes truly mesopic conditions. Consequently the method cannot be regarded as a valid means of measuring mesopic pupil size.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 625, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 717}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00101125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_643", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The intent of this study was to determine if the use of a single or combination of static foot posture measurements can be used to predict rearfoot, midfoot, and forefoot plantar surface area in individuals with pronated or normal foot types.', 'Twelve foot measurements were collected on 52 individuals (mean age 25.8 years) with the change in midfoot width used to place subjects in a pronated or normal foot mobility group. Dynamic plantar contact area was collected during walking with a pressure sensor platform. The 12 measures were entered into a stepwise regression analysis to determine the optimal set of measures associated with regional plantar surface area.', 'A two variable model was found to describe the relationship between the foot measurements and forefoot plantar contact area (r(2)=0.79, p<0.0001). A four variable model was found to describe the relationship between the foot measurements and midfoot plantar contact area (r(2)=0.85, p<0.0001) in those individuals with a 1.26cm or greater change in midfoot width.']\n\nQuestion: Can static foot posture measurements predict regional plantar surface area?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that static foot posture measurements were significantly associated with regional plantar surface area, particularly for the forefoot and midfoot, with high r\u00b2 values (0.79 and 0.85, respectively). These results indicate that static measurements can predict dynamic plantar contact areas in individuals with pronated or normal foot types. Therefore, the evidence supports a positive conclusion.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 325, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 409}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.1475e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_644", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To determine the ability of dentists to recognize digitally manipulated radiographs.', 'A poster was presented at the Annual Meeting of the German Society for Periodontology displaying the intra-oral radiographs of 12 different patients. Half of the radiographs were subjected to digital manipulation to add or remove specific features. Dentists were asked to identify these radiographs by means of a questionnaire.', 'Thirty-nine dentists submitted usable questionnaires. Statistical evaluation revealed a distribution of hits similar to the random distribution. None of the dentists detected all the six manipulated radiographs; three dentists had five correct, but there were five with only one. An authentic radiograph scored highest as a manipulation.']\n\nQuestion: Can dentists recognize manipulated digital radiographs?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that dentists' ability to detect manipulated radiographs was no better than random chance, with most performing poorly and even authentic images being incorrectly identified as manipulated. This indicates a general inability to reliably recognize digital alterations. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 224, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 276}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.1104e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_645", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Delayed gastric emptying (DGE) is the most frequent postoperative complication after pylorus-preserving pancreaticoduodenectomy (PPPD). This prospective, non-randomized study was undertaken to determine whether the incidence of DGE may be reduced by modifying the original reconstructive anatomy with a retrocolic duodenojejunostomy towards an antecolic duodenojejunostomy.', 'The study was comprised of 51 patients who underwent PPPD between August 1994 and November 1997. The operation was carried out as originally described but was modified by performing the duodenojejunostomy antecolically. Clinical data were recorded prospectively, with special regard to DGE.', 'After PPPD, the nasogastric tube could be removed at a median of 2 days (range 1-22 days) postoperatively; in two patients, the nasogastric tube was reinserted because of vomiting and nausea. A liquid diet was started at a median of 5 days (3-11 days); the patients were able to tolerate a full, regular diet at a median of 10 days (7-28 days). The overall incidence of DGE was 12% (n=6). No postoperative complications other than DGE were exhibited by 36 patients (71%). In this group, DGE was only seen in one patient (3%). In the second group, where postoperative complications other than DGE occurred (n=15), five patients (30%) exhibited DGE (P=0.002).']\n\nQuestion: Is delayed gastric emptying following pancreaticoduodenectomy related to pylorus preservation?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The provided study examines DGE rates specifically after PPPD (i.e., with pylorus preservation) and shows that incidence can be reduced to only 12% overall (and 3% without other complications) simply by altering the reconstructive route to antecolic duodenojejunostomy. This directly implies that DGE is driven by technical/anatomic factors in reconstruction rather than pylorus preservation itself. The answer is therefore no.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 516, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 607}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0008725, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_646", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Upper tract urinary carcinoma (UTUC) is a relatively uncommon but aggressive disease. The Ki-67 antigen is a classic marker of cellular proliferation, but there is still controversy regarding the significance and importance of Ki-67 in tumor progression.', 'In this study, we first detected Ki-67 expression in UTUC patients by immunohistochemistry (IHC). Subsequently, we quantitatively combined the results with those from the published literature in a meta-analysis after searching several databases.', 'IHC results demonstrated that patients with muscle-invasive tumors (T2-T4) had higher Ki-67 expression than those with non-muscle-invasive tumors (Tis-T1), suggesting that high Ki-67 expression may be associated with the aggressive form of UTUC. Kaplan-Meier curves showed that patients with high Ki-67 expression had significantly poorer cancer-specific survival (CSS) and disease-free survival (DFS). Furthermore, multivariate analysis suggested that Ki-67 expression was an independent prognostic factor for CSS (hazard ratio, HR=3.196) and DFS (HR=3.517) in UTUC patients. Then, a meta-analysis of the published literature investigating Ki-67 expression and its effects on UTUC prognosis was conducted. After searching the PubMed, Medline, Embase, Cochrane Library and Scopus databases, 12 articles met the eligibility criteria for this analysis. The eligible studies included a total of 1740 patients with a mean number of 82 patients per study (range, 38-475). The combined results showed that increased Ki-67 levels were associated with poor survival and disease progression, with a pooled HR estimate of 2.081 and 2.791, respectively. In subgroup analysis, the pooled HR was statistically significant for cancer-specific survival (HR=2.276), metastasis-free survival (HR=3.008) and disease-free survival (HR=6.336).']\n\nQuestion: Is Overexpression of Ki-67 a Prognostic Biomarker of Upper Tract Urinary Carcinoma?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study demonstrates that high Ki-67 expression is associated with more aggressive tumor features (e.g., muscle invasion) and poorer survival outcomes, including cancer-specific and disease-free survival. Multivariate analysis confirms Ki-67 as an independent prognostic factor, and the meta-analysis supports its association with poor prognosis across multiple studies. Therefore, the evidence strongly supports Ki-67 overexpression as a prognostic biomarker in upper tract urinary carcinoma.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 527, "output_tokens": 97, "total_tokens": 624}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.7116999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_649", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['This study provides the first large-volume (1000 implant) comparison of the deflation rates of Poly Implant Prosthesis prefilled textured saline breast implants versus a control group of Mentor Siltex textured saline implants.', \"A consecutive series of 500 Poly Implant Prosthesis prefilled textured saline breast implants was compared with a consecutive series of 500 Mentor Siltex breast implants. Each breast implant was evaluated for a 4-year period, and the annual deflation rate (number of deflations during a given year divided by the total number of implants) and cumulative deflation rate (cumulative total of deflations through a given year divided by the total number of implants) were recorded. Statistical significance was calculated using the Fisher's exact test at year 1 and the chi-square analysis at years 2 through 4.\", \"The cumulative deflation rates of the Poly Implant Prosthesis implants was as follows: year 1, 1.2 percent; year 2, 5.6 percent; year 3, 11.4 percent; and year 4, 15.4 percent. The cumulative deflation rates of the Mentor implants was: year 1, 0.2 percent; year 2, 0.6 percent; year 3, 1.6 percent; and year 4, 4.4 percent. At year 1, the difference between deflation rates was not statistically significant (Fisher's exact test, p>0.05). However, at year 2 (chi-square, 13.29; p<0.001), year 3 (chi-square, 37.91; p<0.001), and year 4 (chi-square, 32.69; p<0.001), the difference was statistically significant.\"]\n\nQuestion: A comparison of 500 prefilled textured saline breast implants versus 500 standard textured saline breast implants: is there a difference in deflation rates?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The cumulative deflation rates for Poly Implant Prosthesis implants were significantly higher than those for Mentor implants at years 2, 3, and 4, with p-values less than 0.001, indicating statistical significance. Although the difference was not significant at year 1, the later years show a clear and significant difference in deflation rates. Therefore, there is a statistically significant difference in deflation rates between the two types of implants.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 504, "output_tokens": 99, "total_tokens": 603}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.5684e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_650", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"Fixation of foreign bodies (FB), in the mucosa, can favor its migration, giving origin to the popular saying: 'FB walk to the heart'.AIM: Describe the mechanisms involved in FB migration and how to diagnose them.\", 'From a sample of 3,000 foreign bodies, during 40 years, we analyzed four which had extra-lumen migration. We analyzed clinical, radiologic, endoscopic and ultrasound data collected at the medical documentation service.', 'Three clinical histories are presented, describing two fish bones and one piece of fish cartilage. FB shifting was analyzed in all of them. Migration started in the esophagus in two, one going to the aorta and the other to the neck area. In the other two, migration started in the pharynx, and the FB moved towards the prevertebral fascia and the other externalized in the submandibular region. The mechanisms and the risks posed to the patient, by FB migration, and the way to diagnose them are hereby discussed.']\n\nQuestion: Do foreign bodies migrate through the body towards the heart?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The phrase \"FB walk to the heart\" is a popular saying, but the context indicates that while foreign bodies can migrate, they do not literally travel to the heart. Instead, migration occurs along tissue planes or fascial spaces, such as to the aorta or prevertebral fascia, due to inflammatory or mechanical processes. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 298, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 377}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.9058e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_654", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Coronary atherosclerotic burden is excessive in diabetic patients. Diabetes mellitus (DM) is an independent predictor for both death and myocardial infarction. It is not known whether the prevalence of complex coronary lesions, such as bifurcation and ostial lesions, is different in diabetics from nondiabetics.', 'The aim of present study was to investigate the prevalence of these lesions in patients with DM.', 'One thousand fourteen consecutive patients (mean age 61.3+/-10.7 years) were investigated. Coronary angiograms were examined for bifurcation and ostial lesions using a digital quantitative system. Patients were classified as diabetic (n=281) or nondiabetic (n=733).', 'Patient mean age, and rates of hypertension and hyperlipidemia were significantly higher in the diabetic group than in the nondiabetic group (P<0.0001), although smoking was significantly lower (P=0.001). Reasons for coronary angiography and treatment were comparable between the two groups. The prevalence of bifurcation lesions and ostial lesions was significantly greater in the diabetic group than in the nondiabetic group (9.8% versus 4.3% [P=0.001] and 38.4% versus 29.2% [P=0.003]in the diabetic group versus the nondiabetic group). The presence of DM and greater age were found to be independent predictors for bifurcation lesions (OR=2.27 [P=0.004] and OR=1.03 [P=0.01], for DM and age, respectively) and ostial lesions (OR=1.40 [P=0.027] and OR=1.02 [P=0.001], for DM and age, respectively) in multivariate analysis.']\n\nQuestion: Are complex coronary lesions more frequent in patients with diabetes mellitus?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that the prevalence of bifurcation and ostial lesions\u2014types of complex coronary lesions\u2014was significantly higher in diabetic patients compared to nondiabetic patients (9.8% vs. 4.3% and 38.4% vs. 29.2%, respectively; both P < 0.01). Multivariate analysis also identified diabetes mellitus as an independent predictor for these lesions. Therefore, complex coronary lesions are indeed more frequent in patients with diabetes mellitus.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 487, "output_tokens": 118, "total_tokens": 605}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.637699999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_656", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To ascertain whether level of intrauterine cocaine exposure (IUCE) is associated with early adolescent delinquent behavior, after accounting for prenatal exposures to other psychoactive substances and relevant psychosocial factors.', 'Ninety-three early adolescents (12.5-14.5 years old) participating since birth in a longitudinal study of IUCE reported delinquent acts via an audio computer-assisted self-interview. Level of IUCE and exposure to cigarettes, alcohol, and marijuana were determined by maternal report, maternal and infant urine assays, and infant meconium assays at birth. Participants reported their exposure to violence on the Violence Exposure Scale for Children-Revised at ages 8.5, 9.5, and 11 years and during early adolescence, and the strictness of supervision by their caregivers during early adolescence.', 'Of the 93 participants, 24 (26%) reported \u2265 3 delinquent behaviors during early adolescence. In the final multivariate model (including level of IUCE and cigarette exposure, childhood exposure to violence, and caregiver strictness/supervision) \u2265 3 delinquent behaviors were not significantly associated with level of IUCE but were significantly associated with intrauterine exposure to half a pack or more of cigarettes per day and higher levels of childhood exposure to violence, effects substantially unchanged after control for early adolescent violence exposure.']\n\nQuestion: Are there effects of intrauterine cocaine exposure on delinquency during early adolescence?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that after accounting for other factors such as cigarette exposure, violence exposure, and caregiver supervision, intrauterine cocaine exposure (IUCE) was not significantly associated with delinquent behaviors in early adolescence. Instead, delinquency was significantly linked to cigarette exposure and childhood exposure to violence. Therefore, the evidence suggests no significant effect of IUCE on delinquency.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 377, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 458}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.4867e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_662", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The study was performed to evaluate the clinical and technical efficacy of endovenous laser ablation (EVLA) of small saphenous varicosities, particularly in relation to the site of endovenous access.', 'Totally 59 patients with unilateral saphenopopliteal junction incompetence and small saphenous vein reflux underwent EVLA (810 nm, 14 W diode laser) with ambulatory phlebectomies. Small saphenous vein access was gained at the lowest site of truncal reflux. Patients were divided into 2 groups: access gained above mid-calf (AMC, n = 33) and below mid-calf (BMC, n = 26) levels. Outcomes included Venous Clinical Severity Scores (VCSS), Aberdeen Varicose Vein Questionnaire (AVVQ), patient satisfaction, complications, and recurrence rates.', 'Both groups demonstrated significant improvement in VCSS, AVVQ, generic quality of life Short Form 36, and EuroQol scores (P<.05) up to 1 year. No differences were seen between AMC and BMC groups for complications (phlebitis: 2 [6%] and 1 [3.8%], P>.05; paresthesia: 2 [6%] and 5 [19%], P = .223) and recurrence (3 [9%] and 1 [3.8%], P = .623), respectively.']\n\nQuestion: Endovenous laser ablation in the treatment of small saphenous varicose veins: does site of access influence early outcomes?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant differences between the two groups (above vs. below mid-calf access) in terms of complications, recurrence rates, or clinical outcomes. Both groups showed similar improvements in clinical scores and quality of life measures. Therefore, the site of access does not appear to influence early outcomes.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 427, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 493}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.691699999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_667", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The solitary kidney (SK) is currently debated in the literature, as living kidney donation is extensively used and the diagnosis of congenital SK is frequent. Tubulointerstitial lesions associated with adaptive phenomena may occur early within the SK.', 'Analysis of the significance of urinary biomarkers in the assessment of tubulointerstitial lesions of the SK.', 'A cross-sectional study of 37 patients with SK included 18 patients-acquired SK (mean age 56.44\\u2009\u00b1\\u200912.20 years, interval from nephrectomy 10.94\\u2009\u00b1\\u20099.37 years), 19 patients-congenital SK (mean age 41.52\\u2009\u00b1\\u200910.54 years). Urinary NAG, urinary alpha-1-microglobulin, albuminuria, eGFR (CKD-EPI equation) were measured.', 'In acquired SK, NAG increased in 60.66%, urinary alpha 1-microglobulin in 16.66%, albuminuria in 55.55% of patients. Inverse correlation with eGFR presented NAG (R(2\\u2009)=\\u20090.537, p\\u2009=\\u20090.022), urinary alpha 1-microglobulin (R(2\\u2009)=\\u20090.702, p\\u2009=\\u20090.001), albuminuria (R(2\\u2009)=\\u20090.655, p\\u2009=\\u20090.003). In congenital SK, NAG increased in 52.63%, urinary alpha 1-microglobulin in 5.26%, albuminuria in 47.36% of patients. In this group, urinary biomarkers correlated inversely with eGFR: NAG (R(2\\u2009)=\\u20090.743, p\\u2009<\\u20090.001), urinary alpha 1-microglobulin (R(2\\u2009)=\\u20090.701, p\\u2009=\\u20090.001), albuminuria (R(2\\u2009)=\\u20090.821, p\\u2009<\\u20090.001). Significant correlations were found between the urinary biomarkers in both groups.']\n\nQuestion: Is the urinary biomarkers assessment a non-invasive approach to tubular lesions of the solitary kidney?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study evaluates urinary biomarkers such as NAG, alpha-1-microglobulin, and albuminuria to assess tubulointerstitial lesions in patients with a solitary kidney, without mentioning invasive procedures for biomarker measurement. These markers are commonly collected through standard urine tests, which are non-invasive. Therefore, the assessment of urinary biomarkers represents a non-invasive approach.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 707, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 791}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 5.8596999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_67", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To investigate whether problems in instrumental activities of daily living (IADL) can add to conventionally used clinical measurements in helping to predict a diagnosis of dementia at 1- and 2-year follow-up.', 'Multicenter prospective cohort study.', 'Memory clinics in Europe.', 'Individuals aged 55 and older without dementia.', 'IADLs were measured using pooled activities from five informant-based questionnaires. Structural equation modeling (SEM) was used to investigate the relation between IADLs and dementia. Age, sex, education, depression, and cognitive measures (Mini-Mental State Examination and verbal memory) were included in the model.', 'Five hundred thirty-one participants had baseline and 1-year follow-up assessments; 69 (13.0%) of these had developed dementia at 1-year follow-up. At 2-year follow-up, 481 participants were seen, of whom 100 (20.8%) had developed dementia. Participants with IADL disabilities at baseline had a higher conversion rate (24.4%) than participants without IADL disabilities (16.7%) (chi-square\\xa0=\\xa04.28, degrees of freedom\\xa0=\\xa01, P\\xa0=\\xa0.04). SEM showed that IADL disability could help predict dementia in addition to the measured variables at 1-year follow-up (odds ratio (OR)\\xa0=\\xa02.20, 95% confidence interval (CI)\\xa0= 1.51-3.13) and 2-year follow-up (OR\\xa0=\\xa02.11, 95% CI\\xa0=\\xa01.33-3.33).']\n\nQuestion: Do instrumental activities of daily living predict dementia at 1- and 2-year follow-up?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that IADL disabilities at baseline were significantly associated with a higher risk of developing dementia at both 1- and 2-year follow-ups, even after adjusting for age, sex, education, depression, and cognitive measures. Structural equation modeling showed that IADLs added predictive value beyond standard clinical variables, with significant odds ratios at both time points. Therefore, instrumental activities of daily living do predict dementia.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 463, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 554}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.1973e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_670", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"To be able to adhere to discharge instructions after a visit to the emergency department (ED), patients should understand both the care that they received and their discharge instructions. The objective of this study is to assess, at discharge, patients' comprehension of their ED care and instructions and their awareness of deficiencies in their comprehension.\", \"We conducted structured interviews of 140 adult English-speaking patients or their primary caregivers after ED discharge in 2 health systems. Participants rated their subjective understanding of 4 domains: (1) diagnosis and cause; (2) ED care; (3) post-ED care, and (4) return instructions. We assessed patient comprehension as the degree of agreement (concordance) between patients' recall of each of these domains and information obtained from chart review. Two authors scored each case independently and discussed discrepancies before providing a final concordance rating (no concordance, minimal concordance, partial concordance, near concordance, complete concordance).\", \"Seventy-eight percent of patients demonstrated deficient comprehension (less than complete concordance) in at least 1 domain; 51% of patients, in 2 or more domains. Greater than a third of these deficiencies (34%) involved patients' understanding of post-ED care, whereas only 15% were for diagnosis and cause. The majority of patients with comprehension deficits failed to perceive them. Patients perceived difficulty with comprehension only 20% of the time when they demonstrated deficient comprehension.\"]\n\nQuestion: Patient comprehension of emergency department care and instructions: are patients aware of when they do not understand?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that 78% of patients had deficient comprehension in at least one domain, but patients perceived difficulty only 20% of the time when comprehension was actually deficient. This indicates a significant lack of awareness regarding their own misunderstandings. Therefore, patients are generally not aware when they do not understand.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 402, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 470}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.5342e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_671", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Multislice helical computed tomography (CT), which can provide detailed 2-D and 3-D reconstructed images, is useful in imaging diagnosis for dental implant treatment. Therefore, in this study, it was performed to clarify the mandibular depiction of double-oblique reconstructed images when changing their thickness.', 'A total of 38 sites in the mandibular molar region were examined using multislice helical CT. The thicknesses of the double-oblique images using multislice helical CT scans were reconstructed in 4 conditions: 0.3 mm, 0.9 mm, 1.6 mm, and 4.1 mm. In double-oblique images, mandibular depiction was evaluated by 5 oral radiologists using a subjective rating score.', 'In the alveolar crest and the whole of the mandibular canal, the highest value was obtained with 0.9 mm-thick images; however, there was no significant difference between 0.3 mm and 0.9 mm-thick images.']\n\nQuestion: Can mandibular depiction be improved by changing the thickness of double-oblique computed tomography images?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Yes, mandibular depiction can be improved by changing the thickness of double-oblique CT images, as the study found the highest depiction scores at 0.9 mm thickness. Although there was no significant difference between 0.3 mm and 0.9 mm, the variation in image quality across different thicknesses indicates that thickness affects depiction. Therefore, optimizing thickness improves diagnostic image quality.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 339, "output_tokens": 107, "total_tokens": 446}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.4769e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_672", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The criteria for administration of adjuvant radiation therapy after thymoma resection remains controversial, and it is unclear whether patients with Masaoka stage III thymoma benefit from adjuvant radiation. The goal of this report was to determine whether or not this group benefits from radiation therapy in disease-specific survival and disease-free survival.', 'Case records of the Massachusetts General Hospital were retrospectively reviewed from 1972 to 2004. One hundred and seventy-nine patients underwent resection for thymoma, of which 45 had stage III disease.', 'Forty-five stage III patients underwent resection and in 36 it was complete. Thirty-eight stage III patients received radiation therapy. Baseline prognostic factors between radiated and nonradiated groups were similar. The addition of adjuvant radiotherapy did not alter local or distant recurrence rates in patients with stage III thymoma. Disease-specific survival at 10 years in stage III patients who did not receive radiation was 75% (95% confidence interval, 32% to 100%) and in patients who did receive radiation therapy it was 79% (95% confidence interval, 64% to 94%) (p = 0.21). The most common site of relapse was the pleura.']\n\nQuestion: Adjuvant radiation of stage III thymoma: is it necessary?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that adjuvant radiotherapy did not significantly alter recurrence rates or disease-specific survival in patients with stage III thymoma. Given the lack of statistical benefit observed in this retrospective review, the findings suggest that adjuvant radiation is not necessary.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 349, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 402}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:29.583469+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00016675, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_673", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To define the concentrations of inhibin in serum and tissue of patients with hydatidiform mole and assess their value as a clinical marker of the condition.', 'Prospective study of new patients with hydatidiform mole, comparison of paired observations, and case-control analysis.', \"A university hospital, two large public hospitals, and a private women's clinic in Japan.\", 'Seven consecutive referred patients seen over four months with newly diagnosed complete hydatidiform mole, including one in whom the mole was accompanied by viable twin fetuses (case excluded from statistical analysis because of unique clinical features). All patients followed up for six months after evacuation of molar tissue.', 'Correlation of serum inhibin concentrations with trophoblastic disease.', 'Serum concentrations of inhibin, human chorionic gonadotrophin, and follicle stimulating hormone were compared before and seven to 10 days after evacuation of the mole. Before evacuation the serum inhibin concentrations (median 8.3 U/ml; 95% confidence interval 2.4 to 34.5) were significantly greater than in 21 normal women at the same stage of pregnancy (2.8 U/ml; 2.1 to 3.6), and inhibin in molar tissue was also present in high concentrations (578 U/ml cytosol; 158 to 1162). Seven to 10 days after evacuation inhibin concentrations in serum samples from the same patients declined significantly to values (0.4 U/ml; 0.1 to 1.4) similar to those seen in the follicular phase of normal menstrual cycles. None of the four patients whose serum inhibin concentrations were 0.4 U/ml or less after evacuation developed persistent trophoblastic disease. Though serum human chorionic gonadotrophin concentrations declined after evacuation (6.6 x 10(3) IU/l; 0.8 x 10(3) to 32.6 x 10(3], they remained far higher than in non-pregnant women. Serum follicle stimulating hormone concentrations remained suppressed.']\n\nQuestion: Inhibin: a new circulating marker of hydatidiform mole?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that serum inhibin concentrations are significantly elevated in patients with hydatidiform mole and decline sharply after evacuation, correlating with disease resolution. Notably, patients with low post-evacuation inhibin levels did not develop persistent trophoblastic disease, suggesting its potential as a clinical marker. These findings support inhibin as a promising new circulating marker for hydatidiform mole.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 533, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 619}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.6442999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_682", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The combined use of free and total prostate-specific antigen (PSA) in early detection of prostate cancer has been controversial. This article systematically evaluates the discriminating capacity of a large number of combination tests.', \"Free and total PSA were analyzed in stored serum samples taken prior to diagnosis in 429 cases and 1,640 controls from the Physicians' Health Study. We used a classification algorithm called logic regression to search for clinically useful tests combining total and percent free PSA and receiver operating characteristic analysis and compared these tests with those based on total and complexed PSA. Data were divided into training and test subsets. For robustness, we considered 35 test-train splits of the original data and computed receiver operating characteristic curves for each test data set.\", 'The average area under the receiver operating characteristic curve across test data sets was 0.74 for total PSA and 0.76 for the combination tests. Combination tests with higher sensitivity and specificity than PSA>4.0 ng/mL were identified 29 out of 35 times. All these tests extended the PSA reflex range to below 4.0 ng/mL. Receiver operating characteristic curve analysis indicated that the overall diagnostic performance as expressed by the area under the curve did not differ significantly for the different tests.']\n\nQuestion: Prostate-specific antigen and free prostate-specific antigen in the early detection of prostate cancer: do combination tests improve detection?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that combination tests of free and total PSA had slightly higher diagnostic performance (AUC of 0.76 vs. 0.74) and were more sensitive and specific than using total PSA alone in 29 out of 35 analyses. Although the improvement was not statistically significant, the consistent identification of better-performing combination tests suggests a potential benefit. Therefore, the most appropriate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 466, "output_tokens": 109, "total_tokens": 575}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.3985999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_683", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Embalming is the through disinfection and art of preserving bodies after death using chemical substances. It keeps a body life like in appearance during the time it lies in a state prior to funeral.', 'This study was undertaken to investigate the effectiveness of Raksi in sacrificed rats in arresting postmortem changes and establishing scientific fact whether Raksi can be an alternative to standard embalming constituent if it is not available.', '50 albino rats were systematically randomized into control and experiment groups. Raksi and distilled water were injected for embalming purpose intraventricularly in experiment and control groups of rats respectively and kept for 48 to 96 hours for observation for postmortem changes.', 'Observations made at 48 and 72 hours of embalming revealed that Raksi can arrest postmortem changes in the rats up to 72 hours (3rd day) successfully in the experimental group whereas moderate to severe postmortem changes were seen in the control group. The experimental group showed mild degree of putrefactive changes, liberation of gases and liquefaction of tissues only at 96 hours (4th day) of embalming.', 'The Raksi used in this experiment contained 34% of alcohol, which was determined by an alcohol hydrometer. Experiment clearly demonstrated from its result that raksi can be utilised temporarily for embalming since it contains alcohol and has preservative, bactericidal and disinfectant properties.']\n\nQuestion: Can homemade alcohol (Raksi) be useful for preserving dead bodies?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on the study described, Raksi, which contains 34% alcohol, effectively delayed postmortem changes in rats for up to 72 hours and showed preservative, bactericidal, and disinfectant properties. The experimental group exhibited significantly less decomposition compared to the control group, indicating Raksi's potential as a temporary embalming agent. Therefore, homemade alcohol (Raksi) can be useful for preserving dead bodies under certain conditions.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 393, "output_tokens": 97, "total_tokens": 490}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.7603e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_686", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['It is not known whether common carotid intima media thickness (CIMT) can serve as a surrogate marker of cardiovascular risk among black Africans. Therefore, we examined whether CIMT differed significantly among individuals with distinct cardiovascular phenotype and correlated significantly with traditional cardiovascular risk factors in a black African population.', \"CIMT was measured in 456 subjects with three distinct cardiovascular phenotypes - 175 consecutive Nigerian African stroke patients, 161 hypertensive patients without stroke and 120 normotensive non-smoking adults. For each pair of cardiovascular phenotypes, c-statistics were obtained for CIMT and traditional vascular risk factors (including age, gender, weight, waist circumference, smoking, alcohol, systolic and diastolic blood pressures, fasting plasma glucose, fasting total cholesterol). Pearson's correlation coefficients were calculated to quantify bivariate relationships.\", 'Bilaterally, CIMT was significantly different among the three cardiovascular phenotypes (right: p\\u2009<\\u20090.001, F\\u2009=\\u200933.8; left: p\\u2009<\\u20090.001, F\\u2009=\\u200948.6). CIMT had a higher c-statistic for differentiating stroke versus normotension (c\\u2009=\\u20090.78 right; 0.82 left, p\\u2009<\\u20090.001) and hypertension versus normotension (c\\u2009=\\u20090.65 right; 0.71 left, p\\u2009<\\u20090.001) than several traditional vascular risk factors. Bilaterally, combining all subjects, CIMT was the only factor that correlated significantly (right: 0.12\\u2009\u2264\\u2009r\\u2009\u2264\\u20090.41, 0.018\\u2009\u2264\\u2009p\\u2009<\\u20090.0001; left: 0.18\\u2009\u2264\\u2009r\\u2009\u2264\\u20090.41, 0.005\\u2009\u2264\\u2009p\\u2009<\\u20090.0001) to all the traditional cardiovascular risk factors assessed.']\n\nQuestion: Can common carotid intima media thickness serve as an indicator of both cardiovascular phenotype and risk among black Africans?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on the study findings, common carotid intima media thickness (CIMT) significantly differed among individuals with different cardiovascular phenotypes and showed strong correlations with traditional cardiovascular risk factors in a black African population. It also demonstrated a higher c-statistic than several traditional risk factors in distinguishing between stroke, hypertension, and normotension. Therefore, CIMT can serve as an indicator of both cardiovascular phenotype and risk in this population.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 666, "output_tokens": 93, "total_tokens": 759}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 5.6585999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_687", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Infants referred to our institution with a final diagnosis of ARM were retrospectively reviewed between 2001 and 2009. The first cohort consisted of patients that were referred between November 2001 and November 2006 with the diagnosis of an ARM that had been delayed for more than 48 h. The second cohort was those referred between December 2006 and May 2009 with whom the diagnosis of ARM had not been made within 24 h of birth.', 'Nineteen infants were referred with delayed diagnosis of an ARM over the 7.5 years of the study. Of 44 patients referred to our institution between December 2006 and May 2009, diagnosis of an ARM was delayed more than 24 h in 14 (32%). There was no difference in gender, birth weight, prematurity, type of malformation or presence of associated anomalies between those with timely and delayed diagnosis of their ARM. A significantly greater proportion of those with a delayed diagnosis presented with obstructive symptoms (86% vs. 27%, P<0.001), including abdominal distension (57%) and delayed passage of meconium or stool (29%). Despite undergoing neonatal examination, the diagnosis of ARM was missed in 12 patients overall.']\n\nQuestion: Delayed diagnosis of anorectal malformations: are current guidelines sufficient?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that 32% of anorectal malformations (ARM) were diagnosed more than 24 hours after birth, and the diagnosis was missed in 12 infants despite neonatal examination. A high proportion of those with delayed diagnosis presented with obstructive symptoms, suggesting that current screening practices failed to detect these cases promptly. This indicates that current guidelines may not be sufficient to ensure timely diagnosis.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 377, "output_tokens": 90, "total_tokens": 467}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.5767e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_690", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Lifestyle changes over the last 30 years are the most likely explanation for the increase in allergic disease over this period.AIM: This study tests the hypothesis that the consumption of fast food is related to the prevalence of asthma and allergy.', 'As part of the International Study of Asthma and Allergies in Childhood (ISAAC) a cross-sectional prevalence study of 1321 children (mean age = 11.4 years, range: 10.1-12.5) was conducted in Hastings, New Zealand. Using standard questions we collected data on the prevalence of asthma and asthma symptoms, as well as food frequency data. Skin prick tests were performed to common environmental allergens and exercise-induced bronchial hyperresponsiveness (BHR) was assessed according to a standard protocol. Body mass index (BMI) was calculated as weight/height2 (kg/m2) and classified into overweight and obese according to a standard international definition.', 'After adjusting for lifestyle factors, including other diet and BMI variables, compared with children who never ate hamburgers, we found an independent risk of hamburger consumption on having a history of wheeze [consumption less than once a week (OR = 1.44, 95% CI: 1.06-1.96) and 1+ times a week (OR = 1.65, 95% CI: 1.07-2.52)] and on current wheeze [consumption less than once a week (OR = 1.17, 95% CI: 0.80-1.70) and 1+ times a week (OR = 1.81, 95% CI: 1.10-2.98)]. Takeaway consumption 1+ times a week was marginally significantly related to BHR (OR = 2.41, 95% CI: 0.99-5.91). There was no effect on atopy.']\n\nQuestion: Fast foods - are they a risk factor for asthma?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that hamburger consumption was independently associated with an increased risk of both past and current wheeze, even after adjusting for other lifestyle and dietary factors. Additionally, frequent takeaway food consumption was marginally significantly linked to exercise-induced bronchial hyperresponsiveness, a feature of asthma. Although no effect was found on atopy (allergic predisposition), the association with respiratory symptoms supports a link between fast food and asthma risk.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 515, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 607}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.5765e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_692", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Beating-heart valve surgery appears to be a promising technique for protection of hypertrophied hearts. Normothermic normokalemic simultaneous antegrade/retrograde perfusion (NNSP) may improve myocardial perfusion. However, its effects on myocardial oxygenation and energy metabolism remain unclear. The present study was to determine whether NNSP improved myocardial oxygenation and energy metabolism of hypertrophied hearts relative to normothermic normokalemic antegrade perfusion (NNAP).', 'Twelve hypertrophied pig hearts underwent a protocol consisting of three 20-minute perfusion episodes (10 minutes NNAP and 10 minutes NNSP in a random order) with each conducted at a different blood flow in the left anterior descending coronary artery (LAD [100%, 50%, and 20% of its initial control]). Myocardial oxygenation was assessed using near-infrared spectroscopic imaging. Myocardial energy metabolism was monitored using localized phosphorus-31 magnetic resonance spectroscopy.', 'With 100% LAD flow, both NNAP and NNSP maintained myocardial oxygenation, adenosine triphosphate, phosphocreatine, and inorganic phosphate at normal levels. When LAD flow was reduced to 50% of its control level, NNSP resulted in a small but significant decrease in myocardial oxygenation and phosphocreatine, whereas those measurements did not change significantly during NNAP. With LAD flow further reduced to 20% of its control level, both NNAP and NNSP caused a substantial decrease in myocardial oxygenation, adenosine triphosphate, and phosphocreatine with an increase in inorganic phosphate. However, the changes were significantly greater during NNSP than during NNAP.']\n\nQuestion: Does normothermic normokalemic simultaneous antegrade/retrograde perfusion improve myocardial oxygenation and energy metabolism for hypertrophied hearts?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that NNSP does not improve myocardial oxygenation and energy metabolism compared to NNAP, especially under reduced blood flow conditions. At 50% and 20% LAD flow, NNSP resulted in greater decreases in oxygenation and high-energy phosphates than NNAP. Therefore, NNSP is not superior and may even be detrimental under low-flow conditions.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 544, "output_tokens": 93, "total_tokens": 637}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.792399999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_694", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['This quasi-experimental study was conducted using a crossover design among two groups of total 64 nursing students. Participants were asked to create concept maps (group A) or were evaluated with the traditional method of quiz (group B) for eight weeks and then take a cumulative test (no. 1). Consequently, subjects used the alternate method for another eight weeks and then take the second cumulative test (no. 2).', 'The results of this study showed that the mean scores for cumulative tests (both no. 1 and no. 2) was higher in the group that engaged in map construction compared to the group that only take the quizzes. In addition, there was a gradual increase in the mean scores of developed map during the eight sessions of intervention.']\n\nQuestion: Does concept mapping enhance learning outcome of nursing students?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study results show higher mean scores on cumulative tests for students who created concept maps compared to those who only took quizzes. There was also a gradual improvement in concept map quality over time, suggesting enhanced learning. This evidence supports that concept mapping positively impacts learning outcomes.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 242, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 300}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.2981999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_696", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Our previous work demonstrated that the Transmissible Liability Index (TLI), an instrument designed as an index of liability for substance use disorder (SUD), is associated with risk of substance use disorder. This longitudinal study assessed whether TLI measured in 10-12-year-olds (late childhood) predicts suicidal behavior from age 12-14 (preadolescence) to age 25 (young adulthood). We hypothesized that TLI would predict number and severity of suicide attempts.', 'Subjects were sons of men who had lifetime history of SUD (n\\u2009=\\u2009250), called the High Average Risk (HAR) group, and sons of men with no lifetime history of a SUD (n\\u2009=\\u2009250), called the Low Average Risk (LAR) group. The TLI was delineated at baseline (age 10-12), and age-specific versions were administered at 12-14, 16, 19, 22, and 25 years of age.', 'TLI was significantly associated with number and severity of lifetime suicide attempts.']\n\nQuestion: Does the Transmissible Liability Index (TLI) assessed in late childhood predict suicidal symptoms at young adulthood?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that the Transmissible Liability Index (TLI), measured in late childhood, was significantly associated with the number and severity of lifetime suicide attempts, extending into young adulthood. This association persisted across longitudinal assessments, supporting its predictive validity. Therefore, the evidence indicates that TLI in late childhood predicts suicidal symptoms in young adulthood.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 346, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 418}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.1766e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_699", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Cutaneous infections such as impetigo contagiosum (IC), molluscum contagiosum (MC) and herpes virus infection (HI) appear to be associated with atopic dermatitis (AD), but there are no reports of concrete epidemiological evidence.', 'We evaluated the association of childhood AD with these infections by conducting a population-based cross-sectional study.', \"Enrolled in this study were 1117 children aged 0-6 years old attending nursery schools in Ishigaki City, Okinawa Prefecture, Japan. Physical examination was performed by dermatologists, and a questionnaire was completed on each child's history of allergic diseases including AD, asthma, allergic rhinitis and egg allergy, and that of skin infections including IC, MC and HI, as well as familial history of AD.\", 'In 913 children (AD; 132), a history of IC, MC or HI was observed in 45.1%, 19.7%, and 2.5%, respectively. Multiple logistic regression analysis revealed that the odds of having a history of IC were 1.8 times higher in AD children than in non-AD children. Meanwhile, a history of MC was significantly correlated to the male gender, but not to a personal history of AD. As for HI, we found no correlated factors in this study.']\n\nQuestion: Are lifetime prevalence of impetigo, molluscum and herpes infection really increased in children having atopic dermatitis?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that only impetigo contagiosum (IC) showed a statistically significant association with atopic dermatitis, while molluscum contagiosum and herpes virus infection did not. Because the association was not consistent across all three infections, the answer is no.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 373, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 433}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:34.484188+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00018325, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_70", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['In a prospective study 218 preschool children were enrolled (stratified in 2 training programs, one specialized for phonologic awareness in order to prevent dyslexia, the other consisting in training of general perception) during the last year of kindergarten. After finishing the first grade 131 children were compared in their reading and writing abilities.', 'In the whole group only a slight difference was found between both training modalities concerning their writing abilities. However, children with a history of hearing loss, actual hearing loss or pathologic middle ear findings profited most from the specialized training program compared to the control in their reading abilities.']\n\nQuestion: Is a specialised training of phonological awareness indicated in every preschool child?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on the context, the specialized phonological awareness training showed significant benefits primarily for children with a history of hearing loss, actual hearing loss, or middle ear issues, but only slight differences in the whole group. This suggests that the training is particularly effective for at-risk children rather than universally beneficial for all preschoolers. Therefore, it is not indicated for every preschool child.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 220, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 299}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.352e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_701", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['If pancreas transplantation is a validated alternative for type 1 diabetic patients with end-stage renal disease, the management of patients who have lost their primary graft is poorly defined. This study aims at evaluating pancreas retransplantation outcome.', 'Between 1976 and 2008, 569 pancreas transplantations were performed in Lyon and Geneva, including 37 second transplantations. Second graft survival was compared with primary graft survival of the same patients and the whole population. Predictive factors of second graft survival were sought. Patient survival and impact on kidney graft function and survival were evaluated.', 'Second pancreas survival of the 17 patients transplanted from 1995 was close to primary graft survival of the whole population (71% vs. 79% at 1 year and 59% vs. 69% at 5 years; P=0.5075) and significantly better than their first pancreas survival (71% vs. 29% at 1 year and 59% vs. 7% at 5 years; P=0.0008) regardless of the cause of first pancreas loss. The same results were observed with all 37 retransplantations. Survival of second simultaneous pancreas and kidney transplantations was better than survival of second pancreas after kidney. Patient survival was excellent (89% at 5 years). Pancreas retransplantation had no impact on kidney graft function and survival (100% at 5 years).']\n\nQuestion: Pancreas retransplantation:  a second chance for diabetic patients?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that second pancreas graft survival is significantly better than first graft survival and comparable to primary graft survival in the general population, with excellent patient and kidney graft outcomes. Retransplantation did not negatively affect kidney function or survival, and results were consistent regardless of the cause of first graft loss. This supports pancreas retransplantation as a viable second chance.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 440, "output_tokens": 113, "total_tokens": 553}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.2539999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_702", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Nasopharyngeal carcinoma (NPC) with lung metastasis alone has been reported as a relatively favorable prognostic group, and combined modality treatment might be indicated for selected cases. However, the prognostic factors determining survival of this group and the indication of combined therapy have not been thoroughly studied.', 'We retrospectively reviewed 246 patients of NPC with lung metastasis(es) alone presented at diagnosis or as the first failure after primary treatment from 1993 to 2008 in an academic tertiary hospital. Univariate and multivariate survival analyses of post-metastasis survival (PMS) and overall survival (OS) were carried out to determine the prognostic factors.', 'The 3-year, 5-year, and 10-year of PMS and OS for the whole cohort were 34.3%, 17.0%, 8.6% and 67.8%, 45.4%, 18.5%, respectively. The median PMS (45.6 months vs. 23.7 months) and OS (73.7 months vs. 46.2 months) of patients treated with combined therapy was significantly longer than that of those treated with chemotherapy alone (P<0.001). Age, disease-free interval (DFI) and treatment modality were evaluated as independent prognostic factors of OS, while only age and treatment modality retain their independent significance in PMS analysis. In stratified survival analysis, compared to chemotherapy alone, combined therapy could benefit the patients with DFI>1 year, but not those with DFI \u2264 1 year.']\n\nQuestion: Factors determining the survival of nasopharyngeal carcinoma with lung metastasis alone: does combined modality treatment benefit?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that combined modality treatment significantly improves both post-metastasis survival and overall survival compared to chemotherapy alone, particularly in patients with a disease-free interval greater than 1 year. Age, DFI, and treatment modality were identified as independent prognostic factors, with combined therapy providing a clear survival benefit in specific subgroups. Therefore, combined modality treatment does benefit selected patients.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 448, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 534}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.0408e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_703", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To investigate the role of viral infection in benign paroxysmal positional vertigo (BPPV).', 'In this retrospective study, 483 patients with BPPV were included in the study group. The control group consisted of 461 healthy subjects. In both groups, serologic analysis of viral agents (HSV1, HSV2, Herpes zoster, EBV, CMV, adenovirus, influenza, and parainfluenza virus) was performed.', 'With the exception of influenza and parainfluenza, all viral serology values were higher in the BBPV group than the control group. We also observed seasonal variation. The BPPV group exhibited elevated values for HSV1 and adenovirus in March and May, for Herpes zoster, adenovirus, and influenza in April, for HSV1 in June, and for HSV1 and CMV in September, compared to the control group. In October, the BPPV group showed increased values for all of the viruses studied, compared to the control group.']\n\nQuestion: Do viral infections have a role in benign paroxysmal positional vertigo?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that most viral serology values were higher in the BPPV group compared to the control group, with notable seasonal patterns and elevated levels in specific months. This suggests a potential association between viral infections and BPPV. Therefore, the evidence supports a role for viral infections in BPPV.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 312, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 380}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.8951999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_708", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Bolus intravenous injection of epinephrine can decrease uterine blood flow. This study examined the effects of intravenous infusion of epinephrine on uterine blood flow in the gravid ewe.', 'Maternal and fetal vascular catheters and a maternal electromagnetic uterine artery flow probe were implanted in 10 near-term gravid ewes. After recovery, saline, 0.125% bupivacaine, 0.125% bupivacaine with 1:200,000 epinephrine, 0.125% bupivacaine with 1:400,000 epinephrine, and 0.125% bupivacaine with 1:800,000 epinephrine were infused into the maternal superior vena cava. Drugs were infused at 10 mL/h for 30 minutes and then at 20 mL/h for an additional 30 minutes. Animals also received an intravenous bolus of epinephrine 15 micrograms. Throughout all infusions, maternal heart rate, systemic and pulmonary blood pressures, uterine blood flow, cardiac output, and acid-base balance were measured, as well as fetal heart rate, blood pressure, and acid-base balance.', 'Epinephrine 15 micrograms decreased uterine blood flow to 68 +/- 14% of baseline (mean +/- SD). Infusion of all solutions had no effect on any measured hemodynamic variable.']\n\nQuestion: Does continuous intravenous infusion of low-concentration epinephrine impair uterine blood flow in pregnant ewes?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that a bolus of epinephrine decreased uterine blood flow, but intravenous infusions of epinephrine at various concentrations (even when combined with bupivacaine) had no effect on any measured hemodynamic variables, including uterine blood flow. This indicates that continuous infusion of low-concentration epinephrine does not impair uterine blood flow in pregnant ewes. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 432, "output_tokens": 98, "total_tokens": 530}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.0471999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_712", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Human immunodeficiency virus (HIV)-infected patients have generally been excluded from transplantation. Recent advances in the management and prognosis of these patients suggest that this policy should be reevaluated.', 'To explore the current views of U.S. transplant centers toward transplanting asymptomatic HIV-infected patients with end-stage renal disease, a written survey was mailed to the directors of transplantation at all 248 renal transplant centers in the United States.', 'All 148 responding centers said they require HIV testing of prospective kidney recipients, and 84% of these centers would not transplant an individual who refuses HIV testing. The vast majority of responding centers would not transplant a kidney from a cadaveric (88%) or a living donor (91%) into an asymptomatic HIV-infected patient who is otherwise a good candidate for transplantation. Among the few centers that would consider transplanting an HIV-infected patient, not a single center had performed such a transplant in the year prior to the survey. Most centers fear that transplantation in the face of HIV infection would be harmful to the individual, and some believe that it would be a waste of precious organs.']\n\nQuestion: Should all human immunodeficiency virus-infected patients with end-stage renal disease be excluded from transplantation?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context indicates that while most transplant centers currently exclude HIV-infected patients, there is recognition that advances in HIV management warrant reevaluation of this policy. Although the majority of centers refuse transplantation for asymptomatic HIV-positive patients, the question challenges the blanket exclusion, suggesting it may no longer be justified. Therefore, the most appropriate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 332, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 405}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.0872e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_716", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Epidermal growth factor receptor (EGFR) mutations as prognostic or predictive marker in patients with non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) have been used widely. However, it may be difficult to get tumor tissue for analyzing the status of EGFR mutation status in large proportion of patients with advanced disease.', 'We obtained pairs of tumor and serum samples from 57 patients with advanced NSCLC, between March 2006 and January 2009. EGFR mutation status from tumor samples was analyzed by genomic polymerase chain reaction and direct sequence and EGFR mutation status from serum samples was determined by the peptide nucleic acid locked nucleic acid polymerase chain reaction clamp.', 'EGFR mutations were detected in the serum samples of 11 patients and in the tumor samples of 12 patients. EGFR mutation status in the serum and tumor samples was consistent in 50 of the 57 pairs (87.7%). There was a high correlation between the mutations detected in serum sample and the mutations detected in the matched tumor sample (correlation index 0.62; P<0.001). Twenty-two of 57 patients (38.5%) received EGFR-tyrosine kinase inhibitors as any line therapy. The response for EGFR-tyrosine kinase inhibitors was significantly associated with EGFR mutations in both tumor samples and serum samples (P<0.05). There was no significant differences in overall survival according to the status of EGFR mutations in both serum and tumor samples (P>0.05).']\n\nQuestion: Can serum be used for analyzing the EGFR mutation status in patients with advanced non-small cell lung cancer?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found a high consistency (87.7%) and significant correlation (P<0.001) between EGFR mutation status in serum and tumor samples, and serum mutations were significantly associated with response to EGFR-tyrosine kinase inhibitors. This indicates that serum can reliably reflect the EGFR mutation status in advanced NSCLC patients. Therefore, serum can be used for analyzing EGFR mutation status.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 478, "output_tokens": 105, "total_tokens": 583}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.4438e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_720", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Paraffin-embedded tissues in Cukurova University Faculty of Medicine Department of Pathology between January 2002 and February 2006 were searched restrospectively to investigate this issue. We performed immunohistochemistry on biopsies of 125 patients with HBV infection, grouped as: mild, moderate and severe hepatitis, cirrhosis and HCC, 25 patients in each of them, using anti c-kit monoclonal antibody. The severity of parenchymal inflammation and of interface hepatitis was semiquantitatively graded on a haematoxylin and eosin stained paraffin sections. Additionally, 50 more HCC, formed on HBV basis, were studied to determine the prevalence of c-kit overexpression.', 'In cirrhotic liver, lower intensity of staining and rarely c-kit positivity were present. The greatest number of the c-kit positivity and higher intensity of staining was found in the livers of patients with severe hepatitis and HCC. In chronic hepatitis B infection, the staining intensity was parallel with the grade and stage of the disease. In the areas where fibrosis was seen, c-kit positivity was rare or absent. In the HCC specimens, c-kit positivity appeared both inside and around the cancerous nodes. C-kit expression was observed in 62 of 75 HCC tissue specimens (82%) (p<0.001).']\n\nQuestion: Expression of c-kit protooncogen in hepatitis B virus-induced chronic hepatitis, cirrhosis and hepatocellular carcinoma: has it a diagnostic role?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that c-kit expression is significantly higher in severe hepatitis and hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC), with 82% of HCC cases showing positivity, and correlates with disease severity. This suggests that c-kit expression could serve as a useful marker in distinguishing disease stages, particularly in identifying HCC. Therefore, c-kit has potential diagnostic value in the context of HBV-induced liver diseases.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 405, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 492}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.7455e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_721", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To consider whether the Barthel Index alone provides sufficient information about the long term outcome of stroke.', 'Cross sectional follow up study with a structured interview questionnaire and measures of impairment, disability, handicap, and general health. The scales used were the hospital anxiety and depression scale, mini mental state examination, Barthel index, modified Rankin scale, London handicap scale, Frenchay activities index, SF36, Nottingham health profile, life satisfaction index, and the caregiver strain index.', 'South east London.', 'People, and their identified carers, resident in south east London in 1989-90 when they had their first in a life-time stroke aged under 75 years.', 'Observational study.', 'Comparison and correlation of the individual Barthel index scores with the scores on other outcome measures.', 'One hundred and twenty three (42%) people were known to be alive, of whom 106 (86%) were interviewed. The median age was 71 years (range 34-79). The mean interval between the stroke and follow up was 4.9 years. The rank correlation coefficients between the Barthel and the different dimensions of the SF36 ranged from r = 0.217 (with the role emotional dimension) to r = 0.810 (with the physical functioning dimension); with the Nottingham health profile the range was r = -0.189 (with the sleep dimension, NS) to r = -0.840 (with the physical mobility dimension); with the hospital and anxiety scale depression component the coefficient was r = -0.563, with the life satisfaction index r = 0.361, with the London handicap scale r = 0.726 and with the Frenchay activities index r = 0.826.']\n\nQuestion: Longer term quality of life and outcome in stroke patients: is the Barthel index alone an adequate measure of outcome?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Barthel Index shows strong correlations with some physical aspects of recovery (e.g., physical functioning, r = 0.810), but weaker or negligible correlations with emotional, social, and broader quality of life domains (e.g., role emotional, r = 0.217; sleep, r = -0.189, NS). This indicates it does not fully capture the multidimensional nature of long-term stroke outcomes, particularly psychological and social well-being. Therefore, the Barthel Index alone is not an adequate measure.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 481, "output_tokens": 117, "total_tokens": 598}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.5851e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_722", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To assess gender differences among residents regarding their plans to have children during residency and determine the most influential reasons for these differences.', 'Using the Health Belief Model as a framework, the authors created an instrument to survey 424 residents from 11 residency programs at three academic medical institutions about their intentions to have children during residency. The authors developed a scale to assess the perceived career threats of having children during residency, evaluated its psychometric properties, and calculated the effect of the mediators.', 'The response rate was 77% (328/424). Forty-one percent of men versus 27% of women planned to have children during residency (P = .01). The instrument measured four career threats-extended training, loss of fellowship positions, pregnancy complications, and interference with career plans-on a five-point Likert scale. The scale had a Cronbach alpha of 0.84 and an eigenvalue of 2.2. Compared with men, women had higher scores for each item and a higher mean score (2.9 versus 2.1, P = .001), signifying greater belief in the potential of pregnancy to threaten careers. After adjusting for age, institution, postgraduate year, and knowledge of parental leave policies, women were less likely to plan to have children during residency (odds ratio 0.46 [95% confidence interval 0.25-0.84]). In mediation analysis, threats to career explained 67% of the gender variance.']\n\nQuestion: Do women residents delay childbearing due to perceived career threats?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data show that women residents perceive greater career threats from having children during residency, with higher scores on the career threat scale compared to men (2.9 vs. 2.1, P = .001). These perceived threats mediated 67% of the gender difference in childbearing plans, indicating a strong influence on their decisions. Therefore, the evidence supports that perceived career threats contribute significantly to women delaying childbearing.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 404, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 496}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.7884e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_724", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"The current study is aimed to assess the relationship between the 'economic/employment' and 'social/welfare' dimensions of social exclusion and suicide mortality in Europe.\", \"Suicide rates for 26 countries were obtained from the WHO. Data on social expenditure were obtained from the OECD database. Employment rates and GDP were obtained from the Total Economy Database. Questions about citizens' attitudes towards different aspects of social exclusion were taken from the European Social Survey. Structural equation modelling was applied to research the theoretical structure of the variables.\", \"All variables are statistically significant in male and female models except of the relationships between 'economic/employment' and 'social/welfare' dimensions and female suicides; and the relationship between 'employment rates' and 'economic/employment' dimension. Suicide mortality rates among both males and females are influenced negatively by 'economic/employment' and 'social/welfare' dimensions. Among females, the influence of 'social/welfare' dimension is stronger compared to the 'economic/employment' dimension. The remaining influence of GDP is positive in both models.\"]\n\nQuestion: Some aspects of social exclusion: do they influence suicide mortality?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study finds that both the 'economic/employment' and 'social/welfare' dimensions of social exclusion significantly influence suicide mortality, with statistically significant relationships in the models for both males and females. Although some specific paths are not significant, the overall impact of social exclusion dimensions on suicide rates is negative and meaningful. Therefore, aspects of social exclusion do influence suicide mortality.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 301, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 379}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.9171e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_726", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To ascertain whether a written information sheet is acceptable to patients and improves recall of the consent interview.', 'Prospective randomised controlled study using questionnaires, comparing a group of patients given information in a written sheet with appropriate explanation to a group given verbal information alone.', 'A specialist orthopaedic surgery unit.', 'The test group was 126 patients undergoing revision or primary total hip arthroplasty; 65 patients were given information verbally, 61 patients were given written information.', \"Patients' recall of information given, tested with a questionnaire completed on admission (mean of 18 days later).\", 'The patients receiving written information scored significantly higher (48% correct answers) than the patients receiving verbal information (38% correct answers).']\n\nQuestion: Informed consent for total hip arthroplasty: does a written information sheet improve recall by patients?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that patients who received written information in addition to verbal explanation scored significantly higher in recall (48% correct) compared to those who received only verbal information (38% correct). This indicates that the written information sheet improved patient recall. Therefore, the results support that a written information sheet does improve recall.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 324, "output_tokens": 99, "total_tokens": 423}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.2903999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_73", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Reconstructing the natural joint line in knee revision surgery improves clinical and functional outcome but may be challenging when both cartilage and bone were removed during previous operations. Assessing joint lines (JLs) by means of bony landmarks is inadvisable because of large variations in human anatomy. Because of the inherent symmetry of the human body, we hypothesised that JLs may be directly assessed by measuring the distances from the bony landmarks to the JL of the contralateral knee by means of radiographic images.', 'Using scaled weight-bearing radiographs in anteroposterior view of both knees, two independent observers measured the distances from the fibular head, the medial and lateral epicondyle, and the adductor tubercle to the JL. A two-sided p value of \u22640.05 was considered statistically significant.', 'Two hundred knees of 100 patients (50 men and 50 women) were examined. For the fibular head, the mean difference between the treated and the control knee was 0.0 mm with narrow confidence limits ranging from -1.1 to 1.1.']\n\nQuestion: Assessing joint line positions by means of the contralateral knee: a new approach for planning knee revision surgery?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study demonstrates that the distance from bony landmarks to the joint line is highly symmetric between knees, with a mean difference of 0.0 mm for the fibular head and narrow confidence limits. This symmetry supports using the contralateral knee as a reliable reference for joint line reconstruction in revision surgery. Therefore, assessing joint line positions by means of the contralateral knee is a valid new approach.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 384, "output_tokens": 111, "total_tokens": 495}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.8363999999999994e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_730", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The 58th World Health Assembly called for all health systems to move towards universal coverage where everyone has access to key promotive, preventive, curative and rehabilitative health interventions at an affordable cost. Universal coverage involves ensuring that health care benefits are distributed on the basis of need for care and not on ability to pay. The distribution of health care benefits is therefore an important policy question, which health systems should address. The aim of this study is to assess the distribution of health care benefits in the Kenyan health system, compare changes over two time periods and demonstrate the extent to which the distribution meets the principles of universal coverage.', 'Two nationally representative cross-sectional households surveys conducted in 2003 and 2007 were the main sources of data. A comprehensive analysis of the entire health system is conducted including the public sector, private-not-for-profit and private-for-profit sectors. Standard benefit incidence analysis techniques were applied and adopted to allow application to private sector services.', 'The three sectors recorded similar levels of pro-rich distribution in 2003, but in 2007, the private-not-for-profit sector was pro-poor, public sector benefits showed an equal distribution, while the private-for-profit sector remained pro-rich. Larger pro-rich disparities were recorded for inpatient compared to outpatient benefits at the hospital level, but primary health care services were pro-poor. Benefits were distributed on the basis of ability to pay and not on need for care.']\n\nQuestion: Does the distribution of health care benefits in Kenya meet the principles of universal coverage?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The distribution of health care benefits in Kenya does not meet the principles of universal coverage because benefits were distributed based on ability to pay rather than need for care, and significant pro-rich disparities persisted, especially in inpatient and private-for-profit services. Although some sectors showed improvement, overall equity in access was not achieved. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 390, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 458}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.449e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_731", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The study was carried on 2096 school children (1043 male, 1053 female) in Ankara. Their mean age was 9.03 years. Demographic properties of the study group and their families were determined and the serum lipid levels of the subjects were obtained. The relation between these demographic properties and lipid levels were investigated.', \"In 135 of the subjects' serum cholesterol level was>or=200 mg/dL and in 83 subjects serum LDL-cholesterol level was>or=130 mg/dL. Despite 64.4% of the subjects reported a family history of hyperlipidemia, no relations between family history and serum lipid levels were found.\"]\n\nQuestion: Cholesterol screening in school children: is family history reliable to choose the ones to screen?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that despite 64.4% of subjects reporting a family history of hyperlipidemia, there was no significant relationship between family history and elevated serum lipid levels. This suggests that using family history alone may not effectively identify children with high cholesterol. Therefore, family history does not appear to be a reliable criterion for selecting which children to screen.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 250, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 328}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.555e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_732", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The prevalence of combined humeral and glenoid defects varies between 79 and 84\\xa0% in case of chronic posttraumatic anterior shoulder instability. The main goal of this study was to evaluate the relationship between humeral and glenoid defects based on quantitative radiological criteria.', 'A retrospective study was performed between 2000 and 2011 including patients who underwent primary surgical shoulder stabilization for chronic posttraumatic anterior shoulder instability, with bone defects in both the glenoid and humerus and a healthy contralateral shoulder. The following measurements were taken: D/R ratio (Hill-Sachs lesion depth/humeral head radius) on an AP X-ray in internal rotation and the D1/D2 ratio [diameter of the involved glenoid articular surfaces (D1)/the healthy one (D2)] on a comparative Bernageau glenoid profile view. Measurements were taken by two observers. Correlations were determined by the Spearman correlation coefficients (r), Bland and Altman diagrams, and intra-class correlation coefficients (ICC). A sample size calculation was done.', 'Thirty patients were included, 25 men/5 women, mean age 29.8\\xa0\u00b1\\xa011.2\\xa0years. The mean D/R was 23\\xa0\u00b1\\xa012\\xa0% for observer 1 and 23\\xa0\u00b1\\xa010\\xa0% for observer 2. The mean D1/D2 was 95\\xa0\u00b1\\xa04\\xa0% for observer 1 and 94\\xa0\u00b1\\xa06\\xa0% for observer 2. No significant correlation was found between humeral and glenoid bone defects by observer 1 (r\\xa0=\\xa00.23, p\\xa0=\\xa00.22) or observer 2 (r\\xa0=\\xa00.05, p\\xa0=\\xa00.78). Agreement of the observers for the D/R ratio was excellent (ICC\\xa0=\\xa00.89\\xa0\u00b1\\xa00.04, p\\xa0<\\xa00.00001) and good for the D1/D2 ratio (ICC\\xa0=\\xa00.54\\xa0\u00b1\\xa00.14, p\\xa0=\\xa00.006).']\n\nQuestion: Bony defects in chronic anterior posttraumatic dislocation of the shoulder: Is there a correlation between humeral and glenoidal lesions?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant correlation between humeral and glenoid bone defects in patients with chronic anterior posttraumatic shoulder instability, as indicated by low Spearman correlation coefficients and non-significant p-values (p = 0.22 and p = 0.78 for the two observers). Although measurement reliability was good to excellent, the lack of correlation suggests the defects occur independently. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 615, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 701}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 5.2265e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_736", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To determine whether patients with high-risk metastatic breast cancer draw benefit from combination chemotherapy as first-line treatment.', \"A total of 260 women with measurable metastatic breast cancer fulfilling high-risk criteria, previously untreated with chemotherapy for their metastatic disease, were randomized to receive either mitoxantrone 12 mg/m(2) or the combination of fluorouracil 500 mg/m(2), epirubicin 50 mg/m(2) and cyclophosphamide 500 mg/m(2) (FEC) every 3 weeks. Treatment was continued until complete remission plus two cycles, or until disease progression. In the case of partial remission or stable disease, treatment was stopped after 12 cycles. Second-line treatment was vindesine, mitomycin and prednisolone. Gain from treatment was estimated using a modified Brunner's score composed of time to progression, patients' rating of the treatment benefit, alopecia, vomiting and performance status.\", \"After recruitment from 1992 to 1997 and observation from 1997 to 1999, the final evaluation showed that single-agent treatment with mitoxantrone does not differ significantly from combination treatment with FEC in terms of response, objective remission rate, remission duration, time to response, time to best response, time to progression or overall survival. There was, however, a significant difference in gain from treatment using a modified Brunner's score favoring the single-agent treatment arm. There was no evidence that any subgroup would fare better with combination treatment.\"]\n\nQuestion: Is first-line single-agent mitoxantrone in the treatment of high-risk metastatic breast cancer patients as effective as combination chemotherapy?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant difference between single-agent mitoxantrone and combination chemotherapy (FEC) in response rate, remission duration, time to progression, or overall survival. However, single-agent mitoxantrone was associated with a significantly better gain from treatment based on a modified Brunner's score, which included patient-reported outcomes and side effects. Therefore, single-agent mitoxantrone is at least as effective as combination therapy, with added benefits in treatment gain.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 505, "output_tokens": 132, "total_tokens": 637}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.9055e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_739", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Abdominal bloating is reported by a majority of irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) patients. Excess colonic fermentation may cause gaseous symptoms. Several foodstuffs contain oligosaccharides with an \u03b1-galactosidic linkage that is resistant to mammalian hydrolases. Assisted hydrolysis by exogenous \u03b1-galactosidase enzyme (AG) could offer a way of controlling IBS symptoms by reducing colonic fermentation and gas production. The aim of this study was to assess the effect of AG on symptom severity and quality of life in IBS patients with abdominal bloating or flatulence.', 'A total of 125 subjects with IBS received AG or placebo at meals for 12 weeks. IBS-Symptom Severity Score (IBS-SSS) and quality of life (QoL) were assessed at baseline, during the treatment and at 4-week follow-up.', 'AG showed a trend toward a more prominent decrease in IBS-SSS. The responder rate at week 16 was higher for the AG group. No difference was detected in QoL between AG and placebo groups. A total of 25 patients (18 in AG group and 7 in placebo group, p = 0.016) withdrew from the study. Abdominal pain and diarrhea were more often reported as reason for withdrawal in AG group.']\n\nQuestion: Does oral \u03b1-galactosidase relieve irritable bowel symptoms?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows a trend toward improved symptom severity scores and a higher responder rate with \u03b1-galactosidase (AG), suggesting some benefit. However, the lack of significant difference in quality of life and higher withdrawal rates due to abdominal pain and diarrhea in the AG group introduce uncertainty. Therefore, the evidence is not conclusive, supporting a cautious interpretation.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 386, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 462}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.5006e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_743", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The aim was to investigate the relationship between cognitive ability and frequency compressed speech recognition in listeners with normal hearing and normal cognition.', 'Speech-in-noise recognition was measured using Institute of Electrical and Electronic Engineers sentences presented over earphones at 65 dB SPL and a range of signal-to-noise ratios. There were three conditions: unprocessed, and at frequency compression ratios of 2:1 and 3:1 (cut-off frequency, 1.6 kHz). Working memory and cognitive ability were measured using the reading span test and the trail making test, respectively.', 'Participants were 15 young normally-hearing adults with normal cognition.', 'There was a statistically significant reduction in mean speech recognition from around 80% when unprocessed to 40% for 2:1 compression and 30% for 3:1 compression. There was a statistically significant relationship between speech recognition and cognition for the unprocessed condition but not for the frequency-compressed conditions.']\n\nQuestion: Does cognitive function predict frequency compressed speech recognition in listeners with normal hearing and normal cognition?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context states that there was a significant relationship between speech recognition and cognition for the unprocessed condition but not for the frequency-compressed conditions. This indicates that cognitive function does not predict speech recognition when frequency compression is applied. Therefore, cognitive function does not predict frequency compressed speech recognition.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 292, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 354}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.6932e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_744", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['79 adjacent proximal surfaces without restorations in permanent teeth were examined. Patients suspected to have carious lesions after a visual clinical and a bitewing examination participated in a CBCT examination (Kodak 9000 3D, 5 \u00d7 3.7 cm field of view, voxel size 0.07 mm). Ethical approval and informed consent were obtained according to the Helsinki Declaration. Radiographic assessment recording lesions with or without cavitation was performed by two observers in bitewings and CBCT sections. Orthodontic separators were placed interdentally between two lesion-suspected surfaces. The separator was removed after 3 days and the surfaces recorded as cavitated (yes/no), i.e. validated clinically. Differences between the two radiographic modalities (sensitivity, specificity and overall accuracy) were estimated by analyzing the binary data in a generalized linear model.', 'For both observers, sensitivity was significantly higher for CBCT than for bitewings (average difference 33%, p<0.001) while specificity was not significantly different between the methods (p = 0.19). The overall accuracy was also significantly higher for CBCT (p<0.001).']\n\nQuestion: Should cavitation in proximal surfaces be reported in cone beam computed tomography examination?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that CBCT had significantly higher sensitivity and overall accuracy compared to bitewing radiographs for detecting proximal carious lesions, with no significant difference in specificity. This indicates that CBCT is more effective at identifying lesions, including those with cavitation. Therefore, cavitation in proximal surfaces should be reported in CBCT examinations.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 346, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 419}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.1866e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_746", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"Affect-regulated exercise to feel 'good' can be used to control exercise intensity amongst both active and sedentary individuals and should support exercise adherence. It is not known, however, whether affect-regulated exercise training can lead to physical health gains. The aim of this study was to examine if affect-regulated exercise to feel 'good' leads to improved fitness over the course of an 8-week training programme.\", 'A repeated measures design (pretest-posttest) with independent groups (training and control).', \"20 sedentary females completed a submaximal graded exercise test and were then allocated to either a training group or control group. The training group completed two supervised sessions and one unsupervised session per week for 8 weeks. Exercise intensity was affect-regulated to feel 'good'. Following the 8 weeks of training, both groups completed a second submaximal graded exercise test.\", 'Repeated measures analyses of variance indicated a significant increase in the time to reach ventilatory threshold in the training group (318 \u00b1 23.7s) compared to control (248 \u00b1 16.9s). Overall compliance to training was high (>92%). Participants in the training group exercised at intensities that would be classified as being in the lower range of the recommended guidelines (\u2248 50% V\u02d9O(2) max) for cardiovascular health.']\n\nQuestion: Affect-regulated exercise intensity: does training at an intensity that feels 'good' improve physical health?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found a significant increase in the time to reach ventilatory threshold in the training group compared to the control group after 8 weeks of affect-regulated exercise. This improvement indicates enhanced cardiovascular fitness, a key component of physical health. Therefore, training at an intensity that feels 'good' does lead to measurable health gains.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 382, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 452}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.4122e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_75", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To determine whether there is a relationship between VEGF expression and renal vein and vena cava invasion in stage pT3 renal cell carcinoma and to evaluate the impact of VEGF expression on survival in pT3 renal cell carcinoma.', '78 patients with a pT3a or pT3b tumour without vena cava invasion or pT3b tumour with vena cava invasion were compared for age, gender, Fuhrman grade and immunohistochemical expression of VEGF. All these variables were submitted to univariate and multivariate analysis to establish their impact on survival.', 'Only tumour size appeared to be significantly different between the 3 groups. On univariate analysis, invasion of the perirenal fat, lymph node involvement, distant metastases and VEGF expression were significantly associated with survival (p<0.01). On multivariate analysis, lymph node involvement, distant metastases and VEGF expression (OR 6.07) were identified as independent predictive factors of survival.']\n\nQuestion: Is tumour expression of VEGF associated with venous invasion and survival in pT3 renal cell carcinoma?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The provided study context explicitly compared VEGF expression across invasion subgroups (pT3a/b with varying venous involvement) and found no significant differences; only tumor size varied. VEGF expression was, however, an independent predictor of survival on both univariate and multivariate analysis. Because the queried association requires both venous invasion and survival, and the former is absent, the answer is no.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 401, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 478}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00069375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_750", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Recently, orthostatic myoclonus (OM) has been suggested as a cause of gait impairment and unsteadiness in neurodegenerative diseases. The aim of this study was to investigate the frequency of orthostatic myoclonus, its clinical characteristics and the underlying associated neurological disorders.', 'A retrospective analysis of clinical data and electromyogram surface recordings from subjects with unexplained unsteadiness/gait impairment was performed. Diagnosis of OM was made when a pattern of non-rhythmic bursts was observed (duration range 20-100 ms; bursts per second \u226416).', \"Among 93 subjects studied, OM was the most frequent disorder (n = 16; 17.2%), followed by orthostatic tremor (13.9%) and low frequency tremors during orthostatism (12.9%). All patients with OM complained about unsteadiness during orthostatism and/or during gait. Leg jerking was only observed by visual inspection during orthostatism in four subjects and two also presented falls. Eleven out of 16 patients (68.7%) with OM had an associated neurodegenerative disease, such as multiple system atrophy (n = 3) Parkinson's disease (n = 2), Alzheimer's disease (n = 2), mild cognitive impairment (n = 2) and normal pressure hydrocephalus (n = 2). Although four subjects showed improvement of orthostatic myoclonus with antimyoclonic treatment, the follow-up was not systematic enough to evaluate their therapeutic effect on OM.\"]\n\nQuestion: Orthostatic myoclonus: an underrecognized cause of unsteadiness?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that orthostatic myoclonus (OM) was the most frequent disorder (17.2%) among subjects with unexplained unsteadiness or gait impairment, and most patients with OM had associated neurodegenerative diseases. Despite its frequency and clinical impact, OM may go unrecognized without specific electromyogram testing, suggesting it is underrecognized. Therefore, the evidence supports that OM is an underrecognized cause of unsteadiness.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 459, "output_tokens": 116, "total_tokens": 575}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.4189e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_751", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Mesial temporal sclerosis (MTS) is characterized by neuronal loss in the hippocampus. Studies on experimental models and patients with intractable epilepsy suggest that apoptosis may be involved in neuronal death induced by recurrent seizures.', 'We searched evidence for apoptotic cell death in temporal lobes resected from drug-resistant epilepsy patients with MTS by using the terminal deoxynucleotidyl transferase (TdT) and digoxigenin-11-dUTP (TUNEL) method and immunohistochemistry for Bcl-2, Bax, and caspase-cleaved actin fragment, fractin. The temporal lobe specimens were obtained from 15 patients (six women and nine men; mean age, 29 +/- 8 years).', 'Unlike that in normal adult brain, we observed Bcl-2 immunoreactivity in some of the remaining neurons dispersed throughout the hippocampus proper as well as in most of the reactive astroglia. Bax immunopositivity was increased in almost all neurons. Fractin immunostaining, an indicator of caspase activity, was detected in approximately 10% of these neurons. Despite increased Bax expression and activation of caspases, we could not find evidence for DNA fragmentation by TUNEL staining. We also could not detect typical apoptotic changes in nuclear morphology by Hoechst-33258 or hematoxylin counterstaining.']\n\nQuestion: Is the cell death in mesial temporal sclerosis apoptotic?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found evidence of caspase activation and increased Bax expression, but it explicitly failed to detect DNA fragmentation or typical apoptotic nuclear morphology. Therefore, the researchers concluded that the cell death observed did not meet the criteria for classical apoptosis.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 354, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 405}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:32.987384+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000165, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_752", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To investigate the diagnostic value of a half dose compared with a full dose of gadobenate dimeglumine in the assessment of synovitis or tenosynovitis in the wrist and finger joints in patients with early rheumatoid arthritis (RA) and a disease activity score greater than 3.2.', 'With institutional review board approval and informed consent, 57 patients with early RA underwent 3-T magnetic resonance (MR) imaging with two different doses of contrast media. The contrast enhancement was measured in inflamed synovial tissue at half dose (0.05 mmol per kilogram of body weight) and at full dose (0.1 mmol/kg) by using T1-weighted sequences with fat saturation. The differences and the correlation of signal intensities (SIs) at half- and full-dose sequences were compared by using the paired t test and Pearson correlations. Image quality, Rheumatoid Arthritis MRI Score (RAMRIS), and tenosynovitis score on half- and full-dose images were compared by two observers using the Wilcoxon test. Interrater agreement was assessed by using \u03ba statistics.', 'A significant difference in SI was found between half-dose and full-dose gadobenate dimeglumine-enhanced synovial tissue (mean: 914.35 \u00b1 251.1 vs 1022 \u00b1 244.5, P<.001). Because the SI showed high correlation between the ratio at half dose and full dose (r = 0.875), the formula, ratio of synovial enhancement to saline syringe at full dose = 0.337 + 1.070 \u00d7 ratio of synovial enhancement to saline syringe at half dose, can be used to convert the normalized value of half dose to full dose. However, no difference in RAMRIS (score 0 in 490 of 1026 joints; score 1 in 344; score 2 in 158; and score 3 in 34) or tenosynovitis scores in grading synovitis or tenosynovitis in image quality and in assessment of synovial enhancement was detected between half-dose and full-dose images (P = 1).']\n\nQuestion: Contrast-enhanced MR imaging of hand and finger joints in patients with early rheumatoid arthritis: do we really need a full dose of gadobenate dimeglumine for assessing synovial enhancement at 3 T?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant difference in image quality, RAMRIS, or tenosynovitis scores between half-dose and full-dose gadobenate dimeglumine, despite a statistically significant difference in signal intensity. The high correlation (r = 0.875) and conversion formula suggest that half-dose imaging provides comparable diagnostic information. Therefore, a full dose does not appear necessary for assessing synovial enhancement in early RA at 3 T.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 609, "output_tokens": 101, "total_tokens": 710}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 5.3339e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_754", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Reimbursement based on the total care of a patient during an acute episode of illness is believed to stimulate management and clinicians to reduce quality problems like waiting times and poor coordination of care delivery. Although many studies already show that this kind of case-mix based reimbursement leads to more efficiency, it remains unclear whether care coordination improved as well. This study aims to explore whether case-mix based reimbursement stimulates development of care coordination by the use of care programmes, and a process-oriented way of working.', 'Data for this study were gathered during the winter of 2007/2008 in a survey involving all Dutch hospitals. Descriptive and structural equation modelling (SEM) analyses were conducted.', \"SEM reveals that adoption of the case-mix reimbursement within hospitals' budgeting processes stimulates hospitals to establish care programmes by the use of process-oriented performance measures. However, the implementation of care programmes is not (yet) accompanied by a change in focus from function (the delivery of independent care activities) to process (the delivery of care activities as being connected to a chain of interdependent care activities).\"]\n\nQuestion: Does case-mix based reimbursement stimulate the development of process-oriented care delivery?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that case-mix based reimbursement stimulates the establishment of care programs using process-oriented performance measures, but it does not yet lead to a true shift from function-based to process-based care delivery. Although there is some movement toward process orientation, the focus remains on independent care activities rather than interconnected care processes. Therefore, the evidence suggests the answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 313, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 390}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.9922999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_755", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['This study examined the extent to which ADHD was associated with risky sexual behaviors (RSBs) in a sample of 92 undergraduates with (n = 44) and without (n = 48) ADHD. Mother-child relationship quality was examined as a potential moderator.', 'We conducted comprehensive assessments for ADHD and comorbid conditions and collected measures of RSB and mother-child relationship quality.', 'Female students with ADHD were least likely to use condoms than males overall and females without ADHD. An interaction between ADHD and mother-child relationship quality accounted for significant variance in the number of past-year sexual partners, such that a high-quality relationship was protective only for students with ADHD. No other significant associations were found between ADHD and RSB.']\n\nQuestion: Risky sexual behavior among college students With ADHD: is the mother-child relationship protective?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context indicates that a high-quality mother-child relationship was protective for students with ADHD in terms of the number of past-year sexual partners, as shown by a significant interaction effect. This suggests that the relationship quality moderates the link between ADHD and risky sexual behavior for those with ADHD. Therefore, the mother-child relationship is protective for students with ADHD.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 243, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 317}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.4653e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_758", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The purpose of this study was to clarify the prognostic factors for cervical spondylotic amyotrophy (CSA).', 'The authors retrospectively reviewed the medical records of 47 consecutive patients with CSA in whom the presence/absence of the pyramidal tract sign was noted. We analyzed whether the age, sex, presence of diabetes mellitus, medication (vitamin B12), type of the most atrophic and impaired muscle, the muscle strength at the presentation, the presence of the pyramidal tract sign, magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) findings, including the presence and number of T2 high signal intensity areas (T2 HIA) in the spinal cord and the conversion to surgery were associated with the recovery of muscle strength in the patients. In addition, we also investigated whether the duration of symptoms before surgery and the type of surgery were associated with the recovery of muscle strength in patients who required conversion to surgical treatment.', 'The presence of T2 HIA on MRI (P=0.002), the number of T2 HIA on MRI (P=0.002) and conversion to surgery (P=0.015) were found to be significantly associated with a poorer recovery at the observational final follow-up. Further, the presence of the pyramidal tract sign (P=0.043) was significantly associated with a poor recovery at the final follow-up after surgery.']\n\nQuestion: Prognostic factors for cervical spondylotic amyotrophy: are signs of spinal cord involvement associated with the neurological prognosis?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that the presence and number of T2 high signal intensity areas (T2 HIA) on MRI, which indicate spinal cord involvement, were significantly associated with poorer recovery in patients with cervical spondylotic amyotrophy. Additionally, the presence of pyramidal tract signs, another marker of spinal cord dysfunction, was also linked to worse outcomes. Therefore, signs of spinal cord involvement are indeed associated with neurological prognosis.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 399, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 491}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.7529e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_759", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['In this prospective, randomized, double-blind study, we compared the tibial and the peroneal evoked motor response with regard to efficacy of sciatic nerve block using the parasacral approach.', 'Twenty-six ASA I-III patients scheduled for elective lower limb surgery were randomized to receive a parasacral sciatic block, using a nerve stimulator technique seeking either a tibial (n = 14) or peroneal (n = 12) motor response. After the evoked motor response was obtained, a solution of 10 mL 2% lidocaine with epinephrine and 10 mL 0.75% ropivacaine (actual final concentration of epinephrine, 1/160,000) was slowly injected through the needle. Sensory and motor blocks were assessed every 5 min for 30 min by an anesthesiologist blinded to the elicited motor response. If the block was not complete 30 min after injection of the local anesthetics, it was considered as failed, and general anesthesia was supplemented.', 'Time to perform the block and level of minimal and maximal stimulation were not different between groups. The success rate of complete block was significantly higher in the tibial compared to the peroneal group (11 of 14 vs 2 of 12; P = 0.002).']\n\nQuestion: Parasacral sciatic nerve block: does the elicited motor response predict the success rate?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found a significantly higher success rate of complete block when a tibial motor response was elicited compared to a peroneal response (11 of 14 vs 2 of 12; P = 0.002). This indicates that the type of motor response is predictive of block success. Therefore, the elicited motor response does predict the success rate.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 405, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 491}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.7355e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_764", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Noise exposure in the neonatal intensive care unit is believed to be a risk factor for hearing loss in preterm neonates. Continuous positive airway pressure (CPAP) devices exceed recommended noise levels. High flow nasal cannulae (HFNC) are an increasingly popular alternative to CPAP for treating preterm infants, but there are no in vivo studies assessing noise production by HFNC.', 'To study whether HFNC are noisier than bubble CPAP (BCPAP) for preterm infants.', 'An observational study of preterm infants receiving HFNC or BCPAP. Noise levels within the external auditory meatus (EAM) were measured using a microphone probe tube connected to a calibrated digital dosimeter. Noise was measured across a range of frequencies and reported as decibels A-weighted (dBA).', 'A total of 21 HFNC and 13 BCPAP noise measurements were performed in 21 infants. HFNC gas flows were 2-5 L/min, and BCPAP gas flows were 6-10 L/min with set pressures of 5-7 cm of water. There was no evidence of a difference in average noise levels measured at the EAM: mean difference (95% CI) of -1.6 (-4.0 to 0.9) dBA for HFNC compared to BCPAP. At low frequency (500 Hz), HFNC was mean (95% CI) 3.0 (0.3 to 5.7) dBA quieter than BCPAP. Noise increased with increasing BCPAP gas flow (p=0.007), but not with increasing set pressure. There was a trend to noise increasing with increasing HFNC gas flows.']\n\nQuestion: Are high flow nasal cannulae noisier than bubble CPAP for preterm infants?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant difference in average noise levels between high flow nasal cannulae (HFNC) and bubble CPAP (BCPAP) at the external auditory meatus. HFNC was actually quieter at low frequencies, and while noise increased with higher gas flow in both systems, there was no overall evidence that HFNC was noisier. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 459, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 543}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.0989e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_765", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The gluten-free diet has traditionally been accepted as a healthy diet, but there are articles advocating that it may have some nutritional deficiencies. The current study assesses whether there was any change in the contributions of calories, essential elements, proportion of fatty acids, vitamins, minerals and fiber in children who were diagnosed with celiac diseases, comparing the diet with gluten prior one year after diagnosis with the diet without gluten to the year of diagnosis. The level of clinical or analytical impact that nutritional deficits could have was also assessed.', 'A prospective,descriptive, observational study in which information was collected from a dietary survey, anthropometric and analytical data at pre-diagnosis of celiac disease and following a gluten diet and one year after celiac disease diagnosis, under gluten-free diet.', 'A total of 37 patients meet the study criteria. A decrease in the intake of saturated fatty acids was found, with an increase of monounsaturated fatty acids and an increase in the intake of phosphorus in the diet without gluten. A deficient intake of vitamin D was found in both diets. Clinically, at year of gluten-free diet there was an improvement in weight and size. Analytically, there was an improvement in hemoglobin, ferritin, vitamin D, and parathyroid hormone in plasma.']\n\nQuestion: Nutritional assessment of gluten-free diet. Is gluten-free diet deficient in some nutrient?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found a deficient intake of vitamin D in both the gluten-containing and gluten-free diets, indicating a persistent deficiency even after switching to a gluten-free diet. Although some improvements were seen in nutrient levels and clinical markers after one year, the continued deficiency in vitamin D suggests the gluten-free diet may lack certain nutrients. Therefore, the gluten-free diet is deficient in at least one nutrient.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 353, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 436}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.3363e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_767", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Recent studies have shown that early antiretroviral therapy (ART) initiation results in significant HIV transmission reduction. This is the rationale behind the \"test and treat\" policy of the World Health Organization (WHO). Implementation of this policy will lead to an increased incidence of ART-related adverse effects, especially in sub-Saharan Africa (SSA). Is the region yet ready to cope with such a challenging issue?', 'The introduction and widespread use of ART have drastically changed the natural history of HIV/AIDS, but exposure to ART leads to serious medication-related adverse effects mainly explained by mitochondrial toxicities, and the situation will get worse in the near future. Indeed, ART is associated with an increased risk of developing cardiovascular disease, lipodystrophy, prediabetes and overt diabetes, insulin resistance and hyperlactatemia/lactic acidosis. The prevalence of these disorders is already high in SSA, and the situation will be exacerbated by the implementation of the new WHO recommendations. Most SSA countries are characterized by (extreme) poverty, very weak health systems, inadequate and low quality of health services, inaccessibility to existing health facilities, lack of (qualified) health personnel, lack of adequate equipment, inaccessibility and unaffordability of medicines, and heavy workload in a context of a double burden of disease. Additionally, there is dearth of data on the incidence and predictive factors of ART-related adverse effects in SSA, to anticipate on strategies that should be put in place to prevent the occurrence of these conditions or properly estimate the upcoming burden and prepare an adequate response plan. These are required if we are to anticipate and effectively prevent this upcoming burden.']\n\nQuestion: Antiretroviral therapy related adverse effects: Can sub-Saharan Africa cope with the new \"test and treat\" policy of the World Health Organization?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context highlights the significant challenges facing sub-Saharan Africa, including weak health systems, lack of resources, and limited data on adverse effects, which would hinder the region's ability to manage increased ART-related complications. The implementation of the \"test and treat\" policy is likely to exacerbate existing health burdens without adequate preparation. Therefore, the region is currently unprepared to cope effectively.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 438, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 518}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.9098e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_77", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To determine the duration of continuing pregnancy after antenatal corticosteroid (AC) administration and to evaluate the potential opportunity for rescue AC.', \"Retrospective analysis of women at 24-32 weeks' gestation who received AC at one institution.\", \"Six hundred ninety-two women received AC. Two hundred forty-seven (35.7%) delivered at>or = 34 weeks' gestation. Three hundred twenty-one (46.4%) delivered within 1 week of AC; 92 of those women (13.3%) delivered within 24 hours. Only 124 (17.9%) remained pregnant 1 week after AC and delivered at<34 weeks. The latter were compared to women delivering>2 week after AC but>or = 34 weeks. More likely to deliver at<34 weeks were those women who received AC for premature preterm rupture of membranes (OR 3.83, 95% CI 2.06-7.17), twins (OR 2.90, 95% CI 1.42-5.95) or before 28 weeks (OR 2.21, 95% CI 1.38-3.52).\"]\n\nQuestion: Continuation of pregnancy after antenatal corticosteroid administration: opportunity for rescue?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study indicates that a significant portion of women (17.9%) remained pregnant one week after receiving antenatal corticosteroids but delivered before 34 weeks, suggesting a potential clinical window for rescue therapy. Therefore, the findings support the existence of an opportunity for rescue corticosteroids in this specific patient population.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 357, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 423}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:09.729240+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00018825, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_771", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"Schizophrenia patients are typically found to have low IQ both pre- and post-onset, in comparison to the general population. However, a subgroup of patients displays above average IQ pre-onset. The nature of these patients' illness and its relationship to typical schizophrenia is not well understood. The current study sought to investigate the symptom profile of high-IQ schizophrenia patients.\", 'We identified 29 schizophrenia patients of exceptionally high pre-morbid intelligence (mean estimated pre-morbid intelligence quotient (IQ) of 120), of whom around half also showed minimal decline (less than 10 IQ points) from their estimated pre-morbid IQ. We compared their symptom scores (SAPS, SANS, OPCRIT, MADRS, GAF, SAI-E) with a comparison group of schizophrenia patients of typical IQ using multinomial logistic regression.', 'The patients with very high pre-morbid IQ had significantly lower scores on negative and disorganised symptoms than typical patients (RRR=0.019; 95% CI=0.001, 0.675, P=0.030), and showed better global functioning and insight (RRR=1.082; 95% CI=1.020, 1.148; P=0.009). Those with a minimal post-onset IQ decline also showed higher levels of manic symptoms (RRR=8.213; 95% CI=1.042, 64.750, P=0.046).']\n\nQuestion: Schizophrenia patients with high intelligence: A clinically distinct sub-type of schizophrenia?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that schizophrenia patients with high pre-morbid IQ exhibited significantly lower negative and disorganized symptoms, better functioning and insight, and distinct symptom patterns (e.g., higher manic symptoms in those with minimal IQ decline), suggesting a clinically distinct profile. These differences support the idea that high-IQ schizophrenia patients may represent a unique sub-type. Therefore, the evidence leans toward a clinically distinct sub-type.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 430, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 516}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.912999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_783", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To determine the incidence and severity of acute side effects from the use of polyvalent antivenin in victims of rattlesnake bites.', 'We retrospectively reviewed the records of all patients who presented with rattlesnake bites to a university teaching hospital during an 11-year period. From patient medical records, we extracted demographic data, clinical measurements, and outcomes during emergency department evaluation and subsequent hospitalization. Data regarding serum sickness were not collected.', 'Primary outcome variables were the occurrence of immediate hypersensitivity reaction to antivenin, the type of reaction, permanent disability at hospital discharge, and mortality.', 'We identified a total of 73 patients with rattlesnake bites during the study period. Bite envenomation was graded as nonenvenomated, 7 patients (10%); mild, 23 patients (32%); moderate, 32 patients (44%); and severe, 11 patients (15%). We identified 65 patients who received antivenin. Antivenin doses ranged from 1 to 30 vials per patient (mean, 12.0 +/- 6.0), for a total of 777 vials. In 43 patients (66%), 10 or more vials of antivenin were given. The mean number of vials of antivenin given to each snakebite grade were as follows: mild, 8.4 (+/-4.0); moderate, 11.8 (+/-5.7); and severe, 18.7 (+/-6.3). No deaths, amputations, or permanent disability from snakebite occurred in the patients receiving antivenin. Acute side effects of antivenin-occurring within the first 6 hours after administration-were seen in 12 patients (18%; 95% confidence interval, 10%-30%). Acute side effects consisted solely of urticaria in all but 1 patient (2%; 95% confidence interval, 0%-8%). This patient had a history of previous antivenin reaction and required a short course of intravenous epinephrine for blood pressure support. No other complications occurred.']\n\nQuestion: Does the aggressive use of polyvalent antivenin for rattlesnake bites result in serious acute side effects?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that acute side effects occurred in 12 patients (18%), but these were mostly mild (urticaria), with only one case requiring epinephrine and no permanent disability or death. This suggests that even with aggressive use (up to 30 vials), serious acute side effects are rare. Therefore, the evidence supports that serious acute side effects are not common.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 567, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 652}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.8757e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_784", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"This study sought to compare general surgery research residents' survey information regarding self-efficacy ratings to their observed performance during a simulated small bowel repair. Their observed performance ratings were based on their leadership skills in directing their assistant.\", \"Participants were given 15\\xa0min to perform a bowel repair using bovine intestines with standardized injuries. Operative assistants were assigned to help assist with the repair. Before the procedure, participants were asked to rate their expected skills decay, task difficulty, and confidence in addressing the small bowel injury. Interactions were coded to identify the number of instructions given by the participants to the assistant during the repair. Statistical analyses assessed the relationship between the number of directional instructions and participants' perceptions self-efficacy measures. Directional instructions were defined as any dialog by the participant who guided the assistant to perform an action.\", 'Thirty-six residents (58.3% female) participated in the study. Participants who rated lower levels of decay in their intraoperative decision-making and small bowel repair skills were noted to use their assistant more by giving more instructions. Similarly, a higher number of instructions correlated with lower perceived difficulty in selecting the correct suture, suture pattern, and completing the entire surgical task.']\n\nQuestion: Do resident's leadership skills relate to ratings of technical skill?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that residents who perceived lower skill decay and lower task difficulty provided more directional instructions to their assistants. Since these instructions were used as a proxy for leadership skills, the results indicate a correlation between these leadership behaviors and the residents' self-assessed technical proficiency. Therefore, the study suggests a relationship exists.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 329, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 398}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:10.774546+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00018575, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_786", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['CYP2D6 is an important cytochrome P450 enzyme. These enzymes catalyse the oxidative biotransformation of about 25% of clinically important drugs as well as the metabolism of numerous environmental chemical carcinogens. The most frequent null allele of CYP2D6 in European populations, CYP2D6*4, has been studied here in order to elucidate whether a relationship exists between this allele and the risk of developing breast cancer in a Spanish population.', 'Ninety-six breast cancer Spanish patients and one hundred healthy female volunteers were genotyped for the CYP2D6*4 allele using AmpliChip CYP450 Test technology.', 'Homozygous CYP2D6*4 frequency was significant lower in breast cancer patients than in the control group (OR=0.22, p=0.04). The heterozygous CYP2D6*4 group also displayed lower values in patients than in controls but the difference was not significant (OR=0.698, p=0.28). Therefore, the presence of the CYP2D6*4 allele seems to decrease susceptibility to breast carcinoma in the selected population.']\n\nQuestion: CYP2D6*4 allele and breast cancer risk: is there any association?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that the homozygous CYP2D6*4 genotype was significantly less frequent in breast cancer patients than in controls (OR=0.22, p=0.04), suggesting a protective effect. Although the heterozygous state was not statistically significant, the trend still indicated reduced risk. Therefore, there is evidence of an association between the CYP2D6*4 allele and reduced breast cancer risk.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 349, "output_tokens": 96, "total_tokens": 445}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.4379e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_787", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Base Deficit (BD) is a marker of tissue hypoxia in polytrauma patients. It guides resuscitative measures, and predicts outcomes, complications and mortality. The aim of this study was to examine the presence of BD in patients with isolated severe traumatic brain injury (TBI), and to assess if it correlates with the outcomes in these patients.', 'This was a retrospective observational study. All patients over the age of 16 years presenting to Aga Khan University Hospital from 2009 to 2013 with isolated TBI, were included. Data was extracted from 2009 to 2013. Glasgow Outcome Scale (GOS) of 4 and 5 at last follow up was categorized as favorable outcome. Data was analyzed using SPSS version 19 and receiver operative curve (ROC) was generated for BD as a predictor of mortality and unfavorable outcome.', 'One hundred and eight patients were analyzed. Ninety-eight (90.7%) were males. Mean age was 36.69 \u00b1 17.65. Eighty-eight (81.5%) patients had BD, while 20 (18.5%) patients had base excess. 62 (58.5%) of the patients had unfavorable outcomes. BD on admission had a statistically significant negative correlation with Glasgow Coma Scale (GCS) on presentation (r = -0.239, p = 0.025) and Revised Trauma Score (RTS) (r = -0.214, p = 0.046). However, there was no statistically significant difference in means of BD between survivors and non survivors. Area under receiver operator curve (ROC) for BD as a predictor of mortality statistically non-significant.']\n\nQuestion: Does base deficit predict mortality in patients with severe traumatic brain injury?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no statistically significant difference in base deficit (BD) between survivors and non-survivors, and the area under the ROC curve for BD as a predictor of mortality was statistically non-significant. Although BD correlated with GCS and RTS, it did not predict mortality. Therefore, the evidence from the study does not support BD as a predictor of mortality in severe TBI patients.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 478, "output_tokens": 104, "total_tokens": 582}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.4337999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_789", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['IVF singletons have poorer perinatal outcomes than singletons from spontaneous conceptions. This may be due to the influence of ovarian stimulation on the chromosomal constitution of the embryos which could be translated into localized chromosomal anomalies in the placenta. The aim of this study was to compare the incidence of confined placental mosaicism (CPM) in IVF/ICSI pregnancies and spontaneous conceptions.', 'We conducted a multi-centre retrospective analysis of karyotype results obtained by chorionic villus sampling (CVS), performed due to advanced maternal age (>or=36 years at 18 weeks of gestation), in the Netherlands between 1995 and 2005.', 'From a total of 322 246 pregnancies, 20 885 CVS results were analysed: 235 in the IVF/ICSI group and 20 650 in the control group. The mean age of women in both groups was 38.4 years (mean difference -0.08, 95% CI -0.35 to 0.18). Data relating to the fetal karyotype were missing in 143 cases in the control group. When taking into account missing data, the incidence of CPM was lower in the IVF-ICSI group than in the control group, 1.3% versus 2.2% (odds ratio 0.59, 95% CI 0.19-1.85), whereas the incidence of fetal chromosomal anomalies was increased 4.3% versus 2.4% (odds ratio 1.81, 95% CI 0.95-3.42). Neither differences were statistically significant.']\n\nQuestion: Does confined placental mosaicism account for adverse perinatal outcomes in IVF pregnancies?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that the incidence of confined placental mosaicism (CPM) was actually lower in IVF/ICSI pregnancies compared to spontaneous conceptions, though not statistically significant. Since CPM was not more common in IVF pregnancies, it is unlikely to be the primary explanation for their poorer perinatal outcomes. Therefore, the evidence does not support CPM as a contributing factor.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 474, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 560}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.2254e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_791", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Cancer of the buccal mucosa is an uncommon and aggressive neoplasm of the oral cavity. Less than 2% of patients treated for cancer of the oral cavity at Roswell Park Cancer Institute (RPCI) from 1971 to 1997 had primary buccal cancers. Because the majority of these patients did not undergo any adjuvant treatment, this group provided us with the opportunity to assess the relationship between margin status and local recurrence for both small (T1-T2) and large (T3-T4) tumors treated with surgery alone.', 'The RPCI tumor registry database reported 104 patients who were treated for buccal carcinoma. A retrospective chart review identified 27 patients who met our criteria for a buccal mucosal primary tumor (epicenter of the mass in the buccal mucosa). There were 13 men and 14 women, ranging in age from 34 to 94 years (mean, 75). Data were collected regarding patient demographics, presenting symptoms, stage, treatment received, and outcome.', 'All patients underwent surgical resection of their primary lesion; 21 (75%) had T1 or T2 tumors. The rate of local recurrence was 56% for the group as a whole. Patients with close or positive margins had a 66% local failure rate as compared with 52% when surgical margins were negative (greater than or equal to 5 mm from the resection margin after tissue fixation; P = ns). Among those in whom negative margins were achieved, patients with T1-T2 disease had a 40% local failure rate with surgical resection alone.']\n\nQuestion: Cancer of the buccal mucosa: are margins and T-stage accurate predictors of local control?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data show that while margin status and T-stage influence local recurrence rates, the differences are not statistically significant (P = ns), and even with negative margins, the local failure rate remains high, especially in early-stage tumors. This suggests that neither margin status nor T-stage alone can reliably predict local control. Therefore, the evidence does not support them as accurate predictors.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 450, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 528}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.975e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_792", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['In the Philippines, the current national control strategy for schistosomiasis is annual mass drug administration (MDA) with 40 mg/kg of praziquantel in all schistosomiasis-endemic villages with a prevalence \u226510%.', 'A cross-sectional survey of schistosomiasis was conducted in 2012 on 18 221 individuals residing in 22 schistosomiasis-endemic villages in the province of Northern Samar. The prevalence of schistosomiasis, intensity of Schistosoma infection, and morbidity of disease were assessed.', 'Despite an active schistosomiasis-control program in Northern Samar for>30 years, which included a MDA campaign in the last 5 years, the mean prevalence of schistosomiasis among 10 435 evaluated subjects was 27.1% (95% confidence interval [CI], 26.3%-28.0%), and the geometric mean intensity of infection among 2832 evaluated subjects was 17.2 eggs per gram of feces (95% CI, 16.4-18.1). Ultrasonography revealed high levels of schistosomiasis-induced morbidity in the schistosomiasis-endemic communities. Left lobe liver enlargement (\u226570 mm) was evident in 89.3% of subjects. Twenty-five percent of the study population had grade II/III liver parenchyma fibrosis, and 13.3% had splenomegaly (\u2265100 mm).']\n\nQuestion: Can mass drug administration lead to the sustainable control of schistosomiasis?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The high prevalence (27.1%) and significant morbidity (e.g., liver fibrosis, splenomegaly) despite over 30 years of control efforts, including 5 years of MDA, suggest that MDA alone has not achieved sustainable control in Northern Samar. Sustainable control would require reducing transmission and morbidity to very low levels, which has not occurred here. Therefore, the evidence points to MDA not being sufficient on its own for sustainable control.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 443, "output_tokens": 102, "total_tokens": 545}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.1652999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_796", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The so-called \"globulomaxillary cyst\", described as a fissural cyst, caused by entrapped epithelium between the nasal and maxillary process, is no longer considered for its own entity. Nevertheless, cystic lesions, which correspond to the previous image of globulomaxillary cysts, do still occur in daily practice. This raises the question to which entities pathological processes in this particular region actually belong to.', 'In a retrospective study, 17 cases (12 men and 5 women, 12-59\\xa0years old) of primarily diagnosed globulomaxillary cysts are analysed according to clinical, radiological and histological aspects, catamnestic processed and assigned to a new entity. The results are compared with the international literature and draws conclusions on the diagnostic and therapeutic procedure.', 'Seven lateral periodontal cysts, four radicular cysts, two keratocystic odontogenic tumours, one adenomatoid odontogenic tumour, one periapical granuloma, one residual cyst and one undefined jaw cyst were determined.']\n\nQuestion: Globulomaxillary cysts--do they really exist?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The term \"globulomaxillary cyst\" is no longer considered a valid distinct entity, as historical cases have been reclassified into other established cystic or tumoral lesions. Modern analysis shows these lesions are actually lateral periodontal cysts, radicular cysts, or other defined pathologies. Therefore, globulomaxillary cysts do not exist as a separate entity.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 317, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 401}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.0906999999999994e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_799", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['This study evaluated the effect of telmisartan on the livers of diabetic rats and also aimed to determine the hepatic distribution and role of transforming growth factor beta (TGF-beta) in diabetes-related hepatic degeneration while taking into account the possible protective effects of telmisartan.', 'Fifteen adult male rats were used and divided into three groups: the non-diabetic healthy group, alloxan-induced diabetic control group, and the alloxan-induced diabetic telmisartan group. The non-diabetic healthy group and the diabetic control group were exposed to saline for 30 days, while the group treated with diabetic drugs was orally administered telmisartan for 30 days (10 mg/kg/day). At the end of the experiment, the rats were sacrificed and the livers were dissected and transferred into the fixation solution. The livers were then evaluated using stereological and histopathological methods.', 'Our study of the numerical density of hepatocytes shows a significant difference between the diabetic control group and diabetic rats treated with telmisartan. Immunohistochemical staining for TGF-beta in liver sections of the diabetic rats treated with telmisartan showed no immunoreactivity. The diabetic control group was determined to be strongly immunoreactive to TGF-beta.']\n\nQuestion: Does telmisartan prevent hepatic fibrosis in rats with alloxan-induced diabetes?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that telmisartan-treated diabetic rats had no immunoreactivity for TGF-beta, a key mediator of fibrosis, while the untreated diabetic rats showed strong TGF-beta expression, which is associated with hepatic damage and fibrosis. Additionally, telmisartan improved hepatocyte density, suggesting a protective effect against liver degeneration. These findings indicate that telmisartan likely prevents hepatic fibrosis in alloxan-induced diabetic rats.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 433, "output_tokens": 121, "total_tokens": 554}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.2843e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_8", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Although observational data support an inverse relationship between high-density lipoprotein (HDL) cholesterol and coronary heart disease (CHD), genetic HDL deficiency states often do not correlate with premature CHD.', 'Carotid intima-media thickness (cIMT) measurements were obtained in cases comprising 10 different mutations in LCAT, ABCA1 and APOA1 to further evaluate the relationship between low HDL resulting from genetic variation and early atherosclerosis.', 'In a 1:2 case-control study of sex and age-related (+/-5 y) subjects (n=114), cIMT was nearly identical between cases (0.66+/-0.17 cm) and controls (0.65+/-0.18 cm) despite significantly lower HDL cholesterol (0.67 vs. 1.58 mmol/l) and apolipoprotein A-I levels (96.7 vs. 151.4 mg/dl) (P<0.05)']\n\nQuestion: Do mutations causing low HDL-C promote increased carotid intima-media thickness?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that despite significantly lower HDL cholesterol and apolipoprotein A-I levels in individuals with genetic mutations causing low HDL, carotid intima-media thickness (cIMT) was nearly identical between cases and controls. This suggests that genetically low HDL-C does not lead to increased cIMT, a marker of early atherosclerosis. Therefore, the data do not support a causal role for low HDL-C in promoting arterial thickening.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 309, "output_tokens": 99, "total_tokens": 408}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.1839e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_80", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['It is unclear whether traveling long distances to high-volume centers would compensate for travel burden among patients undergoing rectal cancer resection.', 'The purpose of this study was to determine whether operative volume outweighs the advantages of being treated locally by comparing the outcomes of patients with rectal cancer treated at local, low-volume centers versus far, high-volume centers.', 'This was a population-based study.', 'The National Cancer Database was queried for patients with rectal cancer.', 'Patients with stage II or III rectal cancer who underwent surgical resection between 2006 and 2012 were included.', 'The outcomes of interest were margins, lymph node yield, receipt of neoadjuvant chemoradiation, adjuvant chemotherapy, readmission within 30 days, 30-day and 90-day mortality, and 5-year overall survival.', 'A total of 18,605 patients met inclusion criteria; 2067 patients were in the long-distance/high-volume group and 1362 in the short-distance/low-volume group. The median travel distance was 62.6 miles for the long-distance/high-volume group and 2.3 miles for the short-distance/low-volume group. Patients who were younger, white, privately insured, and stage III were more likely to have traveled to a high-volume center. When controlled for patient factors, stage, and hospital factors, patients in the short-distance/low-volume group had lower odds of a lymph node yield \u226512 (OR = 0.51) and neoadjuvant chemoradiation (OR = 0.67) and higher 30-day (OR = 3.38) and 90-day mortality (OR = 2.07) compared with those in the long-distance/high-volume group. The short-distance/low-volume group had a 34% high risk of overall mortality at 5 years compared with the long-distance/high-volume group.', 'We lacked data regarding patient and physician decision making and surgeon-specific factors.']\n\nQuestion: Is the Distance Worth It?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that patients traveling longer distances to high-volume centers had significantly better outcomes, including higher lymph node yields, greater receipt of neoadjuvant chemoradiation, lower short-term mortality, and better 5-year survival, even after adjusting for confounding factors. Despite the travel burden, the clinical benefits at high-volume centers outweighed those at local low-volume centers. Therefore, the distance appears to be worth it.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 508, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 599}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.5168e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_800", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Skin diseases are the most frequently recognized occupational diseases in Denmark. The prognosis for occupational contact dermatitis is often poor.', 'To investigate the prognosis, assessed by eczema, job status and skin-related quality of life, among patients allergic to rubber chemicals and latex (ubiquitous allergens) and epoxy (nonubiquitous allergen), 2\\xa0years after recognition of occupational allergic contact dermatitis.', 'From a cohort of all patients recognized as having occupational dermatitis by the Danish National Board of Industrial Injuries in 2010, 199 patients with relevant rubber allergy (contact allergy to rubber chemicals or contact urticaria from latex) or epoxy allergy were identified. Follow-up consisted of a questionnaire covering current severity of eczema, employment, exposure and quality of life.', 'The response rate was 75%. Clearance of eczema was reported by 11% of patients and 67% reported improvement. Overall 22% of patients with allergy to a nonubiquitous allergen had total clearance of eczema compared with 10% of cases allergic to ubiquitous allergens and 0% of those with contact urticaria (P\\xa0=\\xa00\u00b7116). Improvement was significantly more frequent in those who had changed jobs compared with those who had not (P\\xa0=\\xa00\u00b701).']\n\nQuestion: Two-year follow-up survey of patients with allergic contact dermatitis from an occupational cohort: is the prognosis dependent on the omnipresence of the allergen?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data show that 22% of patients allergic to a nonubiquitous allergen (epoxy) had total clearance of eczema, compared to 10% with ubiquitous allergens (rubber chemicals/latex), and 0% with contact urticaria, suggesting a trend linked to allergen omnipresence. Although the difference was not statistically significant (P = 0.116), improvement was significantly more common in those who changed jobs, implying that reducing exposure helps prognosis. However, based on the evidence provided, the most accurate answer is that a clear dependence on omnipresence was not proven.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 393, "output_tokens": 135, "total_tokens": 528}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.1402999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_804", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The \"health workforce\" crisis has led to an increased interest in health professional education, including MPH programs. Recently, it was questioned whether training of mid- to higher level cadres in public health prepared graduates with competencies to strengthen health systems in low- and middle-income countries. Measuring educational impact has been notoriously difficult; therefore, innovative methods for measuring the outcome and impact of MPH programs were sought. Impact was conceptualized as \"impact on workplace\" and \"impact on society,\" which entailed studying how these competencies were enacted and to what effect within the context of the graduates\\' workplaces, as well as on societal health.', 'This is part of a larger six-country mixed method study; in this paper, the focus is on the qualitative findings of two English language programs, one a distance MPH program offered from South Africa, the other a residential program in the Netherlands. Both offer MPH training to students from a diversity of countries. In-depth interviews were conducted with 10 graduates (per program), working in low- and middle-income health systems, their peers, and their supervisors.', \"Impact on the workplace was reported as considerable by graduates and peers as well as supervisors and included changes in management and leadership: promotion to a leadership position as well as expanded or revitalized management roles were reported by many participants. The development of leadership capacity was highly valued amongst many graduates, and this capacity was cited by a number of supervisors and peers. Wider impact in the workplace took the form of introducing workplace innovations such as setting up an AIDS and addiction research center and research involvement; teaching and training, advocacy, and community engagement were other ways in which graduates' influence reached a wider target grouping. Beyond the workplace, an intersectoral approach, national reach through policy advisory roles to Ministries of Health, policy development, and capacity building, was reported. Work conditions and context influenced conduciveness for innovation and the extent to which graduates were able to have effect. Self-selection of graduates and their role in selecting peers and supervisors may have resulted in some bias, some graduates could not be traced, and social acceptability bias may have influenced findings.\"]\n\nQuestion: Impact of MPH programs: contributing to health system strengthening in low- and middle-income countries?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The qualitative findings indicate that MPH graduates contributed to health system strengthening through leadership roles, workplace innovations, policy development, and capacity building in low- and middle-income countries. Supervisors, peers, and graduates themselves reported considerable impact in both workplace and societal contexts. Although limitations like potential bias exist, the evidence supports a positive contribution.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 524, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 594}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.420399999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_805", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The objective was to evaluate the efficacy of diffusion-weighted imaging (DWI) in predicting the development of vascularization in hypovascular hepatocellular lesions (HHLs).', 'Forty-two HHLs that were diagnosed by computed tomographic (CT) arteriography were evaluated retrospectively. The lesion on DWI was classified as isointense, hypointense, or hyperintense. Follow-up studies that included intravenous dynamic CT or magnetic resonance imaging were performed.', 'The 730-day cumulative developments of vascularization in hypointense, isointense, and hyperintense lesions were 17%, 30%, and 40%, respectively. The differences among these developments were not statistically significant.']\n\nQuestion: Is diffusion-weighted imaging a significant indicator of the development of vascularization in hypovascular hepatocellular lesions?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The 730-day cumulative developments of vascularization were 17%, 30%, and 40% for hypointense, isointense, and hyperintense lesions on DWI, respectively. However, the differences among these rates were not statistically significant. Therefore, DWI does not serve as a significant indicator of vascularization development in hypovascular hepatocellular lesions.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 252, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 338}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.6491999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_81", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['It is commonly accepted that pathological gambling results from the interaction of multiple risk factors. Among these, dopamine replacement therapy (DRT) prescribed for Parkinson disease can be cited. Another dopamine agonist, aripiprazole, could be a new risk factor. We decided to explore this potential adverse drug reaction (ADR).', 'Based on a cohort of 166 pathological gamblers starting treatment in our department, data of each of the 8 patients treated by aripiprazole at inclusion were analyzed.', 'The patients involved were schizophrenic or bipolar, mostly young men with a history of addictive disorders and regular gambling prior to the prescription of aripiprazole. For each one of them, the causality of aripiprazole was considered, using an algorithm. The probability that pathological gambling is actually due to aripiprazole is \"possible\" in 7 cases out of 8, and \"doubtful\" in one.']\n\nQuestion: Aripiprazole: a new risk factor for pathological gambling?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study concludes that aripiprazole is a potential risk factor for pathological gambling, as the causality was assessed as \"possible\" in the majority of the analyzed cases. While the evidence is not definitive, the findings suggest a link that warrants further investigation. Therefore, \"maybe\" is the most accurate reflection of the study's exploratory nature.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 275, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 350}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:21.715049+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00018125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_814", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['ESC (Electronic Stability Control) is a crash avoidance technology that reduces the likelihood of collisions involving loss of control. Although past and emerging research indicates that ESC is effective in reducing collision rates and saving lives, and its inclusion in all vehicle platforms is encouraged, drivers may demonstrate behavioral adaptation or an overreliance on ESC that could offset or reduce its overall effectiveness. The main objective of the present study was to determine whether behavioral adaptation to ESC is likely to occur upon the widespread introduction of ESC into the Canadian vehicle fleet. Secondary objectives were to confirm the results of a previous ESC public survey and to generate a baseline measure for the future assessment of planned and ongoing ESC promotional activities in Canada.', \"Two separate telephone surveys evaluated drivers' perceptions and awareness of ESC. The first surveyed 500 randomly selected owners/drivers of passenger vehicles. The second surveyed 1017 owners/drivers of 2006-2008 ESC-equipped passenger vehicles from the provinces of Quebec and British Columbia, Canada.\", 'Though ESC drivers were much more likely than drivers of other vehicles to be aware of ESC (77% vs. 39%) and that their own vehicle was equipped with it (63% vs. 8%), 23 percent had never heard of it. Ninety percent of drivers who knew that their vehicle was equipped with ESC believed that ESC had made it safer to drive and reported being confident that ESC would work in an emergency. Twenty-three percent of ESC owners who knew their vehicle had ESC reported noticing long-lasting changes in their driving behavior since they began driving the vehicle.']\n\nQuestion: Could ESC (Electronic Stability Control) change the way we drive?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on the survey results, 23% of ESC owners who knew their vehicle had ESC reported noticing long-lasting changes in their driving behavior since acquiring the vehicle. This indicates that ESC has the potential to influence driving habits. Therefore, the evidence supports that ESC could change the way we drive.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 411, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 475}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.5581e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_815", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The insertion/deletion (ID) polymorphism of the angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) gene has been associated with increased coronary heart disease (CHD), although the mechanism of this association is not apparent. We tested the hypothesis that the deletion allele of the ACE gene is associated with insulin resistance.', 'We related ACE genotype to components of the insulin-resistance syndrome in 103 non-insulin-dependent diabetic (NIDDM) and 533 nondiabetic white subjects. NIDDM subjects with the DD genotype had significantly lower levels of specific insulin (DD 38.6, ID 57.1, and II 87.4 pmol.L-1 by ANOVA, P = .011). Non-insulin-treated subjects with the DD genotype had increased insulin sensitivity by HOMA % (DD 56.4%, II 29.4%, P = .027) and lower levels of des 31,32 proinsulin (DD 3.3, II 7.6 pmol.L-1, P = .012) compared with II subjects. There were no differences in prevalence of CHD or levels of blood pressure, serum lipids, or plasminogen activator inhibitor-1 (PAI-1) activity between the three ACE genotypes. In nondiabetic subjects there were no differences in insulin sensitivity, levels of insulin-like molecules, blood pressure, PAI-1, serum lipids, or CHD prevalence between the three ACE genotypes.']\n\nQuestion: The insertion allele of the ACE gene I/D polymorphism. A candidate gene for insulin resistance?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that in NIDDM subjects, the DD genotype (deletion/deletion) was associated with lower insulin levels and higher insulin sensitivity, suggesting the deletion allele\u2014not the insertion allele\u2014is linked to better insulin sensitivity. No significant associations were found in nondiabetic subjects, and the insertion allele (I) was not linked to insulin resistance. Therefore, the insertion allele is not supported as a candidate gene for insulin resistance.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 421, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 512}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.8991e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_819", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Poor bone quality and unstable fractures increase the cut-out rate in implants with gliding lag screws. The U-Blade (RC) lag screw for the Gamma3\u00aenail was introduced to provide monoaxial rotational stability of the femoral head and neck fragment. The purpose of this study was to evaluate whether the use of the U-Blade (RC) lag screw is associated with reduced cut-out in patients with OTA/AO 31A1-3 fractures.MATERIAL &', \"Between 2009 and 2014, 751 patients with OTA/AO 31A1-3 fractures were treated with a Gamma3\u00aenail at our institution. Out of this sample 199 patients were treated with U-blade (RC) lag screws. A total of 135 patients (117 female, 18 male) with standard lag screw (treatment group A) were matched equally regarding age (\u00b14 years) sex, fracture type and location to 135 patients with U-blade (RC) lag screw (treatment group B). Within a mean follow up of 9.2 months (range 6-18 months) we assessed the cut-out rate, the calTAD, lag screw migration, the Parker's mobility score and the Parker's ratio at postoperatively, six and 12 months following surgery. Furthermore we recorded all complications, ASA-Score, hospital stay and duration of surgery retrospectively.\", \"The most common fracture among group B with a cut-out of the lag screw were AO/OTA 2.3 and 3.2 fractures whereas in group A cut-out was most commonly seen in AO/OTA 2.1, 2.2 and 2.3 fractures, there was no significant reduction of the cut-out rate in group B 2.2% (n=3) compared to group A 3.7% (n=5). The duration of surgery was significantly shorter in group A (p<0.05). There was no significant difference in lag screw placement, the Parker's ratio and mobilization.\"]\n\nQuestion: Does an additional antirotation U-Blade (RC) lag screw improve treatment of AO/OTA 31 A1-3 fractures with gamma 3 nail?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant reduction in cut-out rate with the U-Blade (RC) lag screw (2.2% in group B vs. 3.7% in group A), and there were no significant differences in lag screw placement, Parker's ratio, or mobilization. Although the U-Blade aimed to improve rotational stability, the results do not support a clear benefit. Therefore, the additional antirotation feature does not appear to improve treatment outcomes.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 555, "output_tokens": 100, "total_tokens": 655}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.940499999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_82", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Using murine models, we have shown that the lysosomotropic amine, chloroquine, is effective in the prevention of graft-versus-host disease (GVHD) mediated by donor T cells reactive with recipient minor histocompatibility antigens (MiHCs). Because lysosomotropic amines can suppress major histocompatibility complex (MHC) class II antigen presentation, their mechanism of action is potentially different from current immune suppressant drugs used to control GVHD such as cyclosporine.', 'We investigated the use of cyclosporine and the lysosomotropic amines chloroquine and hydroxychloroquine in combination for additive or synergistic immunosuppression on T-cell responses in vitro to MiHC and MHC in mice.', 'We found that similar concentrations of chloroquine and hydroxychloroquine suppress the T-cell response to MiHC in mice (C57BL/6 anti-BALB.B) and that lysosomotropic amines in combination with cyclosporine result in synergistic suppression of a proliferative response to MiHC. Similar suppression and synergy appear to be present in an alloreactive response (C57BL/6 anti-BALB/c). Direct inhibition by chloroquine of T-cell proliferative responses induced by anti-CD3epsilon in the absence of antigen-presenting cells is present at higher concentrations than that required to suppress responses to MiHC or MHC. Chloroquine appears to induce decreased T-cell viability at high concentrations. This effect does not appear to be due to decreased T-cell production of interleukin-2 or interferon-gamma. At lower concentrations (<25 microg/ml), chloroquine can also decrease the ability of antigen-presenting cells to stimulate an a C57BL/6 anti-BALB/c T-cell response and can inhibit MHC class II expression after activation with lipopolysaccharide.']\n\nQuestion: Immune suppression by lysosomotropic amines and cyclosporine on T-cell responses to minor and major histocompatibility antigens: does synergy exist?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that lysosomotropic amines (chloroquine and hydroxychloroquine) in combination with cyclosporine result in synergistic suppression of T-cell proliferative responses to minor histocompatibility antigens (MiHC) and also show similar synergy in alloreactive responses to MHC. This synergy was observed in vitro in mouse models, indicating a combined effect greater than either agent alone. Therefore, the evidence supports the existence of synergy.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 513, "output_tokens": 101, "total_tokens": 614}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.6522999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_820", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Low intakes or blood levels of eicosapentaenoic and docosahexaenoic acids (EPA + DHA) are independently associated with increased risk of death from coronary heart disease (CHD). In randomized secondary prevention trials, fish or fish oil have been demonstrated to reduce total and CHD mortality at intakes of about 1 g/day. Red blood cell (RBC) fatty acid (FA) composition reflects long-term intake of EPA + DHA. We propose that the RBC EPA + DHA (hereafter called the Omega-3 Index) be considered a new risk factor for death from CHD.', 'We conducted clinical and laboratory experiments to generate data necessary for the validation of the Omega-3 Index as a CHD risk predictor. The relationship between this putative marker and risk for CHD death, especially sudden cardiac death (SCD), was then evaluated in several published primary and secondary prevention studies.', 'The Omega-3 Index was inversely associated with risk for CHD mortality. An Omega-3 Index of>or = 8% was associated with the greatest cardioprotection, whereas an index of<or = 4% was associated with the least.']\n\nQuestion: The Omega-3 Index: a new risk factor for death from coronary heart disease?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The passage explicitly proposes that the Omega-3 Index be considered a new risk factor for death from coronary heart disease (CHD) and provides evidence from studies showing its inverse association with CHD mortality. It identifies specific thresholds (\u22658% for greatest protection, \u22644% for least) that further support its role as a predictive risk marker. Therefore, the evidence strongly supports the Omega-3 Index as a new risk factor.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 380, "output_tokens": 115, "total_tokens": 495}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.848e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_825", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The purpose of this study was to search for evidence of an association between occupational arsenic exposure and diabetes mellitus, as implied by the relation of this disease to arsenic in drinking water in a recent study from Taiwan.', 'A case-referent analysis on death records of 5498 individuals in the art glass producing part of southeastern Sweden was performed. Out of all the enrolled subjects, 888 were glass workers. According to occupational title, glassblowers, foundry workers, and unspecified workers were regarded as potentially exposed to arsenic. Persons with a diagnosis of diabetes mellitus either as an underlying or contributing cause of death were considered cases. Referents were decedents without any indication of cancer, cardiovascular disease, or diabetes.', 'A slightly elevated risk [Mantel-Haenszel odds ratio (MH-OR) 1.2, 95% confidence interval (95% CI) 0.82-1.8] was found for diabetes mellitus among the glassworks employees, especially in combination with cardiovascular disease (MH-OR 1.4, 95% CI 0.81-2.3). For the glassblowers, other foundry workers and unspecified glassworkers probably exposed to arsenic, the M-H odds ratio was 1.4 (95% CI 0.92-2.2). Unspecified glass workers, who probably included persons with high exposure, carried the higher risk (MH-OR 1.8, 95% CI 1.1-2.8).']\n\nQuestion: Diabetes mellitus among Swedish art glass workers--an effect of arsenic exposure?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found a slightly elevated risk of diabetes mellitus among glass workers potentially exposed to arsenic, with the highest risk in unspecified glass workers (MH-OR 1.8, 95% CI 1.1\u20132.8), suggesting a possible association. However, the confidence intervals for some estimates include 1.0, indicating the results are not statistically significant in all groups. Therefore, while there is some evidence, it is not conclusive.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 420, "output_tokens": 100, "total_tokens": 520}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.9819999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_827", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To analyze the reliability of micro-computed tomography (micro-CT) to assess bone density and the microstructure of the maxillary bones at the alveolar process in human clinics by direct comparison with conventional stereologic-based histomorphometry.', 'Analysis of osseous microstructural variables including bone volumetric density (BV/TV) of 39 biopsies from the maxillary alveolar bone was performed by micro-CT. Conventional stereologic-based histomorphometry of 10 bone biopsies was performed by optic microscopy (OM) and low-vacuum surface electronic microscopy (SEM). Percentages of bone between micro-CT and conventional stereologic-based histomorphometry were compared.', 'Significant positive correlations were observed between BV/TV and the percentage of bone (%Bone) analyzed by SEM (r\\xa0=\\xa00.933, P\\xa0<\\xa00.001), by toluidine blue staining OM (r\\xa0=\\xa00.950, P\\xa0<\\xa00.001) and by dark field OM (r\\xa0=\\xa00.667, P\\xa0=\\xa00.05). The high positive correlation coefficient between BV/TV and trabecular thickness illustrates that a value of BV/TV upper than 50% squares with a bone presenting most of their trabecules thicker than 0.2\\xa0mm. The high negative correlation between BV/TV and trabecular separation shows that values of BV/TV upper than 50% squares with a bone presenting most of their trabecules separated less than 0.3\\xa0mm each other.']\n\nQuestion: Is micro-computed tomography reliable to determine the microstructure of the maxillary alveolar bone?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found significant positive correlations between micro-CT and conventional histomorphometry methods (SEM and OM) for assessing bone volume (BV/TV) and microstructural features like trabecular thickness and separation. High correlation coefficients (r = 0.933\u20130.950) indicate strong agreement, supporting the reliability of micro-CT. Therefore, micro-CT is a reliable method for evaluating maxillary alveolar bone microstructure.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 455, "output_tokens": 100, "total_tokens": 555}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.2305e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_828", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To determine whether the use of hydrophilic guidewires has increased the technical success rate of peripheral percutaneous transluminal angioplasty (PTA).MATERIAL/', 'We performed 125 procedures and analyzed the technical success rates of PTA using the conventional guidewire first and then if needed, the hydrophilic guidewire for iliac and SFA stenoses or occlusions. Angioplasty was performed on 25 stenosed, 25 occluded iliac arteries and 25 stenosed, 50 occluded femoral arteries. The result was defined as technical success when the lesion was crossed by a guidewire and balloon, then it was dilated with restoration of vessel lumen and less than 30% residual stenosis and the rise in ABI values was at least 0.15 after 24 hours.', 'The technical success rate after PTA of stenosed iliac arteries was achieved in 96% (24/25) using conventional wires and 100% using hydrophilic guidewire; in iliac occlusions, the rates were 60% (15/25) and 96%, respectively; in femoral stenosis - 84% (21/25) and 100%; in occlusions in the first group: lesions<10 cm -64% (16/25) and 96%, in the second group: lesions>10 cm -48% (12/25) and 88%. In the iliac group, there was no significant difference in the success of iliac stenosis PTA. However, there were significant changes in the success rates of PTA performed for SFA stenosis and iliac and SFA occlusions.']\n\nQuestion: Does use of hydrophilic guidewires significantly improve technical success rates of peripheral PTA?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data show that hydrophilic guidewires significantly improved success rates for iliac occlusions (60% to 96%), femoral stenosis (84% to 100%), and femoral occlusions (64% to 96% for <10 cm and 48% to 88% for >10 cm), with the text explicitly stating \"significant changes\" for these lesions. Although no significant difference was seen in iliac stenosis, overall improvement in key areas supports a significant impact. Therefore, the answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 483, "output_tokens": 125, "total_tokens": 608}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.6793e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_830", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['There has been a significant spike in fentanyl-related deaths from illicit fentanyl supplied via the heroin trade. Past fentanyl access was primarily oral or dermal via prescription fentanyl patch diversion. One factor potentially driving this increase in fatalities is the change in route of administration. Rapid intravenous (IV) fentanyl can produce chest wall rigidity. We evaluated post-mortem fentanyl and norfentanyl concentrations in a recent surge of lethal fentanyl intoxications.', \"Fentanyl related deaths from the Franklin County coroner's office from January to September 2015 were identified. Presumptive positive fentanyl results were confirmed by quantitative analysis using liquid chromatography tandem mass spectrometry (LC/MS/MS) and were able to quantify fentanyl, norfentanyl, alfentanyl, and sufentanyl.\", '48 fentanyl deaths were identified. Mean fentanyl concentrations were 12.5\\u2009ng/ml, (range 0.5\\u2009ng/ml to\\u2009>40\\u2009ng/ml). Mean norfentanyl concentrations were 1.9\\u2009ng/ml (range none detected to 8.3\\u2009ng/ml). No appreciable concentrations of norfentanyl could be detected in 20 of 48 cases (42%) and were less than 1\\u2009ng/ml in 25 cases (52%). Elevated fentanyl concentrations did not correlate with rises in norfentanyl levels. In several cases fentanyl concentrations were strikingly high (22\\u2009ng/ml and 20\\u2009ng/ml) with no norfentanyl detected.', 'The lack of any measurable norfentanyl in half of our cases suggests a very rapid death, consistent with acute chest rigidity. An alternate explanation could be a dose-related rapid onset of respiratory arrest. Deaths occurred with low levels of fentanyl in the therapeutic range (1-2\\u2009ng/ml) in apparent non-na\u00efve opiate abusers. Acute chest wall rigidity is a well-recognized complication in the medical community but unknown within the drug abuse community. The average abuser of illicit opioids may be unaware of the increasing fentanyl content of their illicit opioid purchase.']\n\nQuestion: Could chest wall rigidity be a factor in rapid death from illicit fentanyl abuse?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The passage indicates that the lack of measurable norfentanyl in half of the cases suggests very rapid death, which is consistent with acute chest wall rigidity. This condition is described as a well-recognized complication of rapid intravenous fentanyl administration, which can impair breathing and lead to death before significant metabolism occurs. Therefore, chest wall rigidity could indeed be a factor in rapid death from illicit fentanyl abuse.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 572, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 660}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.9411999999999994e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_832", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The aim of this study was to determine whether bone scans (BS) can be avoided if pelvis was included in CT thorax and abdomen to detect bony metastases from breast cancer.', 'Results of 77 pairs of CT (thorax, abdomen, and pelvis) and BS in newly diagnosed patients with metastatic breast cancer (MBC) were compared prospectively for 12 months. Both scans were blindly assessed by experienced radiologists and discussed at multidisciplinary team meetings regarding the diagnosis of bone metastases.', 'CT detected metastatic bone lesions in 43 (98%) of 44 patients with bone metastases. The remaining patient had a solitary, asymptomatic bony metastasis in shaft of femur. BS was positive in all patients with bone metastases. There were 11 cases of false positive findings on BS.']\n\nQuestion: Can computerised tomography replace bone scintigraphy in detecting bone metastases from breast cancer?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The provided study shows that CT (thorax/abdomen/pelvis) detected bone metastases in 98% of cases but missed a solitary lesion outside the scanned field (femur shaft). Whole-body BS detected all cases (though with multiple false positives). This indicates that CT cannot fully replace BS for comprehensive detection.\n\nThus, the correct choice is B.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 367, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 443}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00064875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_836", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Canine-assisted therapy has been receiving growing attention as a means of aiding children with autism spectrum disorder (ASD). Yet, only limited studies have been done and a great deal of literature related to this intervention is anecdotal. The present study aims at providing additional quantitative evidence on the potential of dogs to positively modulate the behavior of children with ASD.SETTINGS/', 'A 12-year-old boy diagnosed with ASD was exposed, at his usual treatment location (the Portuguese Association for Developmental Disorders and Autism at Vila Nova de Gaia, Portugal), to the following treatment conditions: (1) one-to-one structured activities with a therapist assisted by a certified therapy dog, and (2) one-to-one structured activities with the same therapist alone (as a control). To accurately assess differences in the behavior of the participant between these treatment conditions, the therapist followed a strict research protocol. The behavior of the participant was continuously video-recorded during both treatment conditions for further analysis and comparison. Treatment outcomes: In the presence of the dog, the participant exhibited more frequent and longer durations of positive behaviors (such as smiling and positive physical contacting) as well as less frequent and shorter durations of negative behaviors (such as aggressive manifestations).']\n\nQuestion: Can dogs prime autistic children for therapy?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that the presence of a therapy dog increased positive behaviors and decreased negative behaviors in a child with ASD during therapy sessions. This suggests that dogs may help create a more favorable emotional and behavioral state for engaging in therapy. Therefore, the evidence supports the idea that dogs can prime autistic children for therapy.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 331, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 398}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.0200999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_838", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Avascular necrosis of bone (AVN) is a well known complication in patients with systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE).', 'To investigate the role of antiphospholipid antibody status (IgM and IgG anticardiolipin antibodies and lupus anticoagulant) with adjustment for corticosteroid use as risk factors for the development of AVN.', 'A cohort of 265 patients receiving long term follow up in our SLE clinic from 1978 to 1998 was analysed. Patients with AVN complications were detected and then matched for age, sex, ethnicity, duration of disease, and organ disease with two other patients with SLE. A further 31 patients were chosen at random for the analysis.', 'Eleven patients had AVN, giving a point prevalence of 4%. There were no significant differences demonstrable in the presence of individual antiphospholipid antibodies (aPL) or their combination between the group with AVN or the two control groups.']\n\nQuestion: Risk factors for avascular necrosis of bone in patients with systemic lupus erythematosus: is there a role for antiphospholipid antibodies?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant differences in the presence of antiphospholipid antibodies (aPL) between SLE patients with avascular necrosis (AVN) and those without, even after adjusting for corticosteroid use. This suggests that antiphospholipid antibodies do not play a significant role in the development of AVN in SLE patients. Therefore, the evidence does not support a strong association.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 328, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 420}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.2488e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_839", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Using high-quality CT-on-rails imaging, the daily motion of the prostate bed clinical target volume (PB-CTV) based on consensus Radiation Therapy Oncology Group (RTOG) definitions (instead of surgical clips/fiducials) was studied. It was assessed whether PB motion in the superior portion of PB-CTV (SUP-CTV) differed from the inferior PB-CTV (INF-CTV).', 'Eight pT2-3bN0-1M0 patients underwent postprostatectomy intensity-modulated radiotherapy, totaling 300\\xa0fractions. INF-CTV and SUP-CTV were defined as PB-CTV located inferior and superior to the superior border of the pubic symphysis, respectively. Daily pretreatment CT-on-rails images were compared to the planning CT in the left-right (LR), superoinferior (SI), and anteroposterior (AP) directions. Two parameters were defined: \"total PB-CTV motion\" represented total shifts from skin tattoos to RTOG-defined anatomic areas; \"PB-CTV target motion\" (performed for both SUP-CTV and INF-CTV) represented shifts from bone to RTOG-defined anatomic areas (i.\\u2009e., subtracting shifts from skin tattoos to bone).', 'Mean (\u00b1 standard deviation, SD) total PB-CTV motion was -1.5\\xa0(\u00b1\\u202f6.0), 1.3\\xa0(\u00b1\\u202f4.5), and 3.7\\xa0(\u00b1\\u202f5.7)\\xa0mm in LR, SI, and AP directions, respectively. Mean (\u00b1\\u202fSD) PB-CTV target motion was 0.2\\xa0(\u00b11.4), 0.3\\xa0(\u00b12.4), and 0\\xa0(\u00b13.1)\\xa0mm in the LR, SI, and AP directions, respectively. Mean (\u00b1\\u202fSD) INF-CTV target motion was 0.1\\xa0(\u00b1\\u202f2.8), 0.5\\xa0(\u00b1\\u202f2.2), and 0.2 (\u00b1\\u202f2.5)\\xa0mm, and SUP-CTV target motion was 0.3\\xa0(\u00b1\\u202f1.8), 0.5\\xa0(\u00b1\\u202f2.3), and 0\\xa0(\u00b1\\u202f5.0)\\xa0mm in LR, SI, and AP directions, respectively. No statistically significant differences between INF-CTV and SUP-CTV motion were present in any direction.']\n\nQuestion: Prostate bed target interfractional motion using RTOG consensus definitions and daily CT on rails : Does target motion differ between superior and inferior portions of the clinical target volume?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study analyzed interfractional motion in the superior (SUP-CTV) and inferior (INF-CTV) portions of the prostate bed clinical target volume using RTOG definitions and daily CT-on-rails imaging. No statistically significant differences in motion were found between SUP-CTV and INF-CTV in any direction (LR, SI, AP). Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 718, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 804}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 5.9578e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_84", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Treatment of neonatal testicular torsion has two objectives: salvage of the involved testicle (which is rarely achieved) and preservation of the contralateral gonad. The second goal universally involves contralateral testicular scrotal fixation to prevent the future occurrence of contralateral torsion. However, there is controversy with regards to management of a synchronous contralateral hydrocele. It has been our policy not to address the contralateral hydrocele through an inguinal incision to minimize potential injury to the spermatic cord. Our objective in this study was to determine whether the decision to manage a contralateral hydrocele in cases of neonatal testicular torsion solely through a scrotal approach is safe and effective.', 'We reviewed all cases of neonatal testicular torsion occurring at our institution between the years 1999 and 2006. Age at presentation, physical examination, ultrasonographic and intraoperative findings were recorded. Patients were followed after initial surgical intervention to determine the likelihood of developing a subsequent hydrocele or hernia.', 'Thirty-seven patients were identified as presenting with neonatal torsion. Age of presentation averaged 3.5 days (range 1-14 days). Left-sided pathology was seen more commonly than the right, with a 25:12 distribution. All torsed testicles were nonviable. Twenty-two patients were noted to have a contralateral hydrocele at presentation. All hydroceles were opened through a scrotal approach at the time of contralateral scrotal fixation. No patient underwent an inguinal exploration to examine for a patent process vaginalis. None of the patients who presented with a hydrocele have developed a clinical hydrocele or hernia after an average 7.5 years (range 4.3-11.2) follow-up.']\n\nQuestion: Treatment of contralateral hydrocele in neonatal testicular torsion: Is less more?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that managing a contralateral hydrocele through a scrotal approach alone, without inguinal exploration, did not result in subsequent hydroceles or hernias during long-term follow-up. This suggests that a less invasive approach is both safe and effective. Therefore, in this context, \"less\" (avoiding inguinal exploration) is indeed more.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 477, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 558}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.1967e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_844", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Vancomycin is the primary treatment for infections caused by methicilin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus (MRSA). The association of vancomycin treatment failures with increased vancomycin minimum inhibitory concentration (MIC) is a well-recognized problem. A number of single-centre studies have identified progressive increases in glycopeptide MICs for S. aureus strains over recent years - a phenomenon known as vancomycin MIC creep. It is unknown if this is a worldwide phenomenon or if it is localized to specific centers.', 'The aim of this study was to evaluate the trend of vancomycin MIC for isolates of MRSA over a 3-year period in a tertiary university hospital in Portugal. MRSA isolates from samples of patients admitted from January 2007 to December 2009 were assessed. Etest method was used to determine the respective vancomycin MIC. Only one isolate per patient was included in the final analysis.', 'A total of 93 MRSA isolates were studied. The vancomycin MICs were 0.75, 1, 1.5 and 2 mg/L for 1 (1.1%), 19 (20.4%), 38 (40.9%), 35 (37.6%) isolates, respectively. During the 3 year period, we observed a significant fluctuation in the rate of MRSA with a vancomycin MIC\\u2009>\\u20091 mg/L (2007: 86.2%; 2008: 93.3%; 2009: 58.8%, p\\u2009=\\u20090.002). No MRSA isolate presented a MIC\\u2009>\\u20092 mg/L.']\n\nQuestion: Is vancomycin MIC creep a worldwide phenomenon?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The passage states that it is unknown whether vancomycin MIC creep is a worldwide phenomenon or limited to specific centers. While the study in Portugal observed fluctuations in vancomycin MICs, it does not provide enough evidence to confirm a global trend. Therefore, the most accurate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 479, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 542}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.0308999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_847", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Dickkopf-3 (DKK3) may act as a tumor suppressor as it is down-regulated in various types of cancer. This study assessed the DKK3 protein expression in gastric cancer and its potential value as a prognostic marker.', 'DKK3 expression was evaluated by immunohistochemistry in 158 gastric cancer samples from patients who underwent gastrectomy from 2002 to 2008. Clinicopathological parameters and survival data were analyzed.', 'Loss of DKK3 expression was found in 64 of 158 (40.5%) samples, and it was associated with advanced T stage (p<0.001), lymph node metastasis (p<0.001), UICC TNM stage (p<0.001), tumor location (p = 0.029), lymphovascular invasion (p = 0.035), and perineural invasion (p = 0.032). Patients without DKK3 expression in tumor cells had a significantly worse disease-free and overall survival than those with DKK3 expression (p<0.001, and p = 0.001, respectively). TNM stage (p = 0.028 and p<0.001, respectively) and residual tumor (p<0.001 and p = 0.003, respectively) were independent predictors of disease-free and overall survival. Based on the preoperative clinical stage assessed by computed tomography (CT), loss of DKK3 expression was predominantly associated with worse prognosis in patients with clinically node-negative advanced gastric cancer (AGC). The combination of DKK3 expression status and CT increased the accuracy of CT staging for predicting lymph node involvement from 71.5 to 80.0% in AGC patients.']\n\nQuestion: Aberrant loss of dickkopf-3 in gastric cancer: can it predict lymph node metastasis preoperatively?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that loss of DKK3 expression is significantly associated with lymph node metastasis (p<0.001) and that combining DKK3 status with CT imaging improves the accuracy of predicting lymph node involvement in advanced gastric cancer. This suggests DKK3 loss has predictive value when used alongside preoperative staging. Therefore, the answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 497, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 575}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.3087e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_85", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The purpose of this study is to measure the accuracy and reliability of normally sighted, visually impaired, and blind pedestrians at making street crossing decisions using visual and/or auditory information.', 'Using a 5-point rating scale, safety ratings for vehicular gaps of different durations were measured along a two-lane street of one-way traffic without a traffic signal. Safety ratings were collected from 12 normally sighted, 10 visually impaired, and 10 blind subjects for eight different gap times under three sensory conditions: (1) visual plus auditory information, (2) visual information only, and (3) auditory information only. Accuracy and reliability in street crossing decision-making were calculated for each subject under each sensory condition.', 'We found that normally sighted and visually impaired pedestrians were accurate and reliable in their street crossing decision-making ability when using either vision plus hearing or vision only (P>0.05). Under the hearing only condition, all subjects were reliable (P>0.05) but inaccurate with their street crossing decisions (P<0.05). Compared to either the normally sighted (P = 0.018) or visually impaired subjects (P = 0.019), blind subjects were the least accurate with their street crossing decisions under the hearing only condition.']\n\nQuestion: Are normally sighted, visually impaired, and blind pedestrians accurate and reliable at making street crossing decisions?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that normally sighted and visually impaired pedestrians are accurate and reliable when using vision (with or without hearing), but all groups, including blind subjects, are inaccurate when relying on hearing alone. Blind subjects were specifically found to be the least accurate under the hearing-only condition. Therefore, the overall answer is \"no\" because not all pedestrians are accurate across conditions.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 363, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 442}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.3672999999999994e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_850", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To determine the association between fetal biometry in the first or early second trimester and severe macrosomia at delivery.', \"This case-control study included 30 term severely macrosomic neonates; 90 appropriate-for-gestational age (AGA) neonates served as controls. All pregnancies underwent nuchal translucency (NT) screening at 11-14 weeks' gestation. Pregnancies were dated by accurate last menstrual period consistent with crown-rump length (CRL) measurements at the time of screening, early pregnancy CRL or date of fertilization. The association between birth weight and the difference between the measured and the expected CRL at the time of NT screening was analyzed.\", 'The difference between measured and expected CRL, expressed both in mm and in days of gestation, was statistically greater in the severely macrosomic neonates compared with controls (mean, 6.66 +/- 4.78 mm vs. 1.17 +/- 4.6 mm, P<0.0001 and 3 +/- 2.2 days vs. 0.5 +/- 2.3 days, P<0.0001, respectively). Furthermore, there were significant correlations between the extent of macrosomia and the discrepancy between expected and measured fetal size at the time of NT screening (r = 0.47, P<0.01 and r = 0.48, P<0.01, respectively).']\n\nQuestion: Is severe macrosomia manifested at 11-14 weeks of gestation?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that a larger-than-expected crown-rump length (CRL) at 11\u201314 weeks was significantly associated with severe macrosomia at birth, suggesting early fetal overgrowth is detectable. This indicates that signs of severe macrosomia can be observed as early as the first trimester. Therefore, the evidence supports that severe macrosomia is manifested at 11\u201314 weeks of gestation.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 406, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 501}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.832599999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_851", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To examine whether a history of cancer increased the likelihood of a fall in community-dwelling older adults, and if cancer type, stage, or time since diagnosis increased falls.', 'A longitudinal, retrospective, cohort study.', 'A home- and community-based waiver program in Michigan.', '862 older adults aged 65 years or older with cancer compared to 8,617 older adults without cancer using data from the Minimum Data Set-Home Care and Michigan cancer registry.', 'Reports of falls were examined for 90-180 days. Generalized estimating equations were used to compare differences between the groups.', 'Cancer, falls, patient characteristics, comorbidities, medications, pain, weight loss, vision, memory recall, and activities, as well as cancer type, stage, and time since diagnosis.', 'A fall occurred at a rate of 33% in older adults with cancer compared to 29% without cancer (p<0.00). Those with a history of cancer were more likely to fall than those without cancer (adjusted odds ratio 1.16; 95% confidence interval [1.02, 1.33]; p = 0.03). No differences in fall rates were determined by cancer type or stage, and the odds of a fall did not increase when adding time since cancer diagnosis.']\n\nQuestion: Do older adults with cancer fall more often?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that older adults with cancer had a higher fall rate (33%) compared to those without cancer (29%), and this difference was statistically significant (p = 0.03). The adjusted odds ratio of 1.16 indicates a higher likelihood of falling among those with cancer. Therefore, the evidence supports that older adults with cancer fall more often.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 369, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 450}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.4299e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_852", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To determine the advantages of scrotal incision in the treatment of undescended testis. Undescended testis is a common pediatric condition and is conventionally managed surgically by orchidopexy. A single scrotal incision orchidopexy has become accepted as a valid approach for patients with palpable undescended testicles. Because this approach also allows easy detection of atrophic testes or testicular remnants, it recently has also emerged as an alternative initial surgical approach to impalpable undescended testicles.', 'All orchidopexies performed between 2004 and 2008 at our university hospital were prospectively included in this study. A total of 194 scrotal orchidopexies were performed in 154 patients (mean age, 71 months; range, 4-229 months). In all cases a scrotal approach was chosen irrespective of the initial position or presence of an open processus vaginalis. Testicular position was examined at follow-up after a mean period of 10 months (3-22 months).', 'Overall, 36 of the 46 impalpable testicles (78%) could be diagnosed and treated accordingly, using only a scrotal incision. Conversion to laparoscopy was needed in 4 cases. A limited number of postoperative complications were seen. In all cases, the testes were palpable and remained in the scrotum on follow-up.']\n\nQuestion: Scrotal approach to both palpable and impalpable undescended testes: should it become our first choice?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study demonstrates that a scrotal approach successfully diagnosed and treated 78% of impalpable undescended testes without the need for conversion to laparoscopy, with all testes remaining in the scrotum postoperatively. It also reports minimal complications and supports the scrotal incision as effective for both palpable and selected impalpable cases. Given these outcomes, the scrotal approach appears reliable and justifiable as the initial surgical choice.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 422, "output_tokens": 104, "total_tokens": 526}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.0362e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_854", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The placement of the superficial cervical plexus block has been the subject of controversy. Although the investing cervical fascia has been considered as an impenetrable barrier, clinically, the placement of the block deep or superficial to the fascia provides the same effective anesthesia. The underlying mechanism is unclear. The aim of this study was to investigate the three-dimensional organization of connective tissues in the anterior region of the neck.', 'Using a combination of dissection, E12 sheet plastination, and confocal microscopy, fascial structures in the anterior cervical triangle were examined in 10 adult human cadavers.', 'In the upper cervical region, the fascia of strap muscles in the middle and the fasciae of the submandibular glands on both sides formed a dumbbell-like fascia sheet that had free lateral margins and did not continue with the sternocleidomastoid fascia. In the lower cervical region, no single connective tissue sheet extended directly between the sternocleidomastoid muscles. The fascial structure deep to platysma in the anterior cervical triangle comprised the strap fascia.']\n\nQuestion: Does the investing layer of the deep cervical fascia exist?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The passage describes detailed anatomical findings of fascial structures in the anterior neck, noting the presence of the platysma, strap muscle fascia, and other connective tissue sheets, but does not explicitly confirm the existence of the investing layer of the deep cervical fascia as a continuous, encircling structure. Instead, it reports that no single connective tissue sheet directly connects the sternocleidomastoid muscles in the lower neck and that the fascial organization is more segmented. Based on this evidence challenging traditional anatomical descriptions, the most accurate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 317, "output_tokens": 120, "total_tokens": 437}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.4507e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_855", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['More than 50,000 new HIV infections occur annually in the United States. Injection drug users represent twelve percent of incident HIV infections each year. Pharmacy sales of over-the-counter (OTC) syringes have helped prevent HIV transmission among injection drug users in many states throughout the United States. However, concerns exist among some law enforcement officials, policymakers, pharmacists, and community members about potential links between OTC syringe sales and crime.', 'We used a geographic information system and novel spatial and longitudinal analyses to determine whether implementation of pharmacy-based OTC syringe sales were associated with reported crime between January 2006 and December 2008 in Los Angeles Police Department Reporting Districts. We assessed reported crime pre- and post-OTC syringe sales initiation as well as longitudinal associations between crime and OTC syringe-selling pharmacies.', 'By December 2008, 9.3% (94/1010) of Los Angeles Police Department Reporting Districts had at least one OTC syringe-selling pharmacy. Overall reported crime counts and reported crime rates decreased between 2006 and 2008 in all 1010 Reporting Districts. Using generalized estimating equations and adjusting for potential confounders, reported crime rates were negatively associated with OTC syringe sales (adjusted rate ratio: 0.89; 95% confidence interval: 0.81, 0.99).']\n\nQuestion: Is crime associated with over-the-counter pharmacy syringe sales?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that reported crime rates were negatively associated with over-the-counter syringe sales, meaning that areas with these sales saw a decrease in crime. Therefore, there is an association between the two variables.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 377, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 425}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:09.654681+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00016625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_858", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Older adults typically perform worse on measures of working memory (WM) than do young adults; however, age-related differences in WM performance might be reduced if older adults use effective encoding strategies.', 'The purpose of the current experiment was to evaluate WM performance after training individuals to use effective encoding strategies.', 'Participants in the training group (older adults: n = 39; young adults: n = 41) were taught about various verbal encoding strategies and their differential effectiveness and were trained to use interactive imagery and sentence generation on a list-learning task. Participants in the control group (older: n = 37; young: n = 38) completed an equally engaging filler task. All participants completed a pre- and post-training reading span task, which included self-reported strategy use, as well as two transfer tasks that differed in the affordance to use the trained strategies - a paired-associate recall task and the self-ordered pointing task.', 'Both young and older adults were able to use the target strategies on the WM task and showed gains in WM performance after training. The age-related WM deficit was not greatly affected, however, and the training gains did not transfer to the other cognitive tasks. In fact, participants attempted to adapt the trained strategies for a paired-associate recall task, but the increased strategy use did not benefit their performance.']\n\nQuestion: Does strategy training reduce age-related deficits in working memory?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that while both young and older adults improved in working memory performance after strategy training, the age-related deficit in working memory was not greatly reduced. Although participants used the trained strategies, the gains did not eliminate the performance gap between age groups. Therefore, strategy training did not significantly reduce age-related deficits.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 361, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 428}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.2331e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_86", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Sulfasalazine is a widely used anti-inflammatory agent in the treatment of inflammatory bowel disease and several rheumatological disorders. Although as many as 20% of treated patients may experience reversible, dose-dependent side effects, less frequent but potentially severe, systemic reactions have also been reported.', 'A severe systemic reaction to sulfasalazine developed in a 21-year old female with rheumatoid arthritis characterized by eosinophilia, granulomatous enteritis and myelotoxicity, cholestatic hepatitis, and seizures. The clinical course and management of this patient are presented as well as a review of the incidence and outcome of severe systemic reactions to sulfasalazine.']\n\nQuestion: Is it Crohn's disease?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The patient described has granulomatous enteritis, which can resemble Crohn's disease histologically, but the context attributes the condition to a severe systemic reaction to sulfasalazine, not idiopathic inflammatory bowel disease. Therefore, the findings are drug-induced rather than definitive Crohn's disease. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 224, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 290}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.2503999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_861", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The purpose of this study was to identify the relationships between leg muscle power and sprinting speed with changes of direction.', 'the study was designed to describe relationships between physical qualities and a component of sports performance.', 'testing was conducted in an indoor sports hall and a biomechanics laboratory.', '15 male participants were required to be free of injury and have recent experience competing in sports involving sprints with changes of direction.', 'subjects were timed in 8 m sprints in a straight line and with various changes of direction. They were also tested for bilateral and unilateral leg extensor muscle concentric power output by an isokinetic squat and reactive strength by a drop jump.', 'The correlations between concentric power and straight sprinting speed were non-significant whereas the relationships between reactive strength and straight speed were statistically significant. Correlations between muscle power and speed while changing direction were generally low and non-significant for concentric leg power with some moderate and significant (p<0.05) coefficients found for reactive strength. The participants who turned faster to one side tended to have a reactive strength dominance in the leg responsible for the push-off action.']\n\nQuestion: Is muscle power related to running speed with changes of direction?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that correlations between concentric leg power and speed while changing direction were generally low and non-significant. While some moderate and significant relationships were found for reactive strength, the overall findings suggest that muscle power is not strongly or consistently related to speed with changes of direction in the context of this study.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 308, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 374}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:15.204497+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000176, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_865", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Bicompartmental knee arthroplasty features bone and ligament sparing as unicompartmental knee arthroplasty and is presumably better in the recovery of muscle strength and function compared to total knee arthroplasty (TKA) though not previously reported in the literature. The aim of the study was to compare isokinetic knee muscle strength and physical performance in patients who underwent either bicompartmental knee arthroplasty or TKA.', 'Each of 24 patients (31 knees) was prospectively examined preoperatively, at 6 and 12 months after each surgery. Isokinetic knee extensor and flexor strength as well as position sense were measured using the Biodex system. Timed up and go test, stair climbing test, and the 6-min walk test were used to assess physical performance. The results of each group were also compared with those from the corresponding healthy control, respectively.', 'Demography showed significant difference in the mean age between bicompartment (54.8 \u00b1 5.6 years) and TKA groups (65.7 \u00b1 6.7 years). Comparing between the two groups, knee extensor and flexor torque, hamstring/Quadriceps ratio, position sense, and physical performance were not significantly different preoperatively, at 6 and 12 months after surgery. In intra-group analysis, muscle strength and position sense at each time point were not different in both groups. In physical performance, both groups resulted in improvement in the 6-min walk test, and only TKA group showed enhancement in stair climbing test.']\n\nQuestion: Is bicompartmental knee arthroplasty more favourable to knee muscle strength and physical performance compared to total knee arthroplasty?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant differences in knee extensor and flexor torque, hamstring/Quadriceps ratio, position sense, or most physical performance measures between bicompartmental knee arthroplasty and TKA at 6 and 12 months post-surgery. Although both groups improved in the 6-minute walk test, only the TKA group showed improvement in stair climbing, and muscle strength did not favor one group over the other. Therefore, based on the results, bicompartmental knee arthroplasty is not more favorable than TKA regarding muscle strength and physical performance.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 437, "output_tokens": 126, "total_tokens": 563}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.3626999999999994e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_866", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Diabetes mellitus (DM) is undiagnosed in approximately half of the patients actually suffering from the disease. In addition, the prevalence of DM is more than twice as high as in patients with periodontitis when compared to periodontally healthy subjects. Thus, a high number of patients with periodontitis may have undiagnosed DM. The purpose of the present study was to evaluate whether blood oozing from a gingival crevice during routine periodontal examination can be used for determining glucose levels.', 'Observational cross-sectional studies were carried out in 75 patients (43 males and 32 females) with chronic periodontitis who were divided into two groups: Group I and Group II, respectively. Blood oozing from the gingival crevices of anterior teeth following periodontal probing was collected with the stick of glucose self-monitoring device, and the blood glucose levels were measured. At the same time, finger-prick blood was taken for glucometric analysis and subsequent readings were recorded.', \"The patient's blood glucose values ranged from 74 to 256 mg/dl. The comparison between gingival crevicular blood and finger-prick blood showed a very strong correlation, with a t value of 3.97 (at P value = 0.001).\"]\n\nQuestion: Can gingival crevicular blood be relied upon for assessment of blood glucose level?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found a very strong correlation between glucose levels in gingival crevicular blood and finger-prick blood, with a statistically significant p-value of 0.001. This indicates that gingival blood can reliably reflect systemic glucose levels in patients with chronic periodontitis. Therefore, the evidence supports its use for blood glucose assessment.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 369, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 444}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.3699e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_867", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"In this single-centre prospective study, triage nurses estimated the probability of admission using a 100\\u2005mm visual analogue scale (VAS), and GAPS was generated automatically from triage data. We compared calibration using rank sum tests, discrimination using area under receiver operating characteristic curves (AUC) and accuracy with McNemar's test.\", \"Of 1829 attendances, 745 (40.7%) were admitted, not significantly different from GAPS' prediction of 750 (41.0%, p=0.678). In contrast, the nurses' mean VAS predicted 865 admissions (47.3%), overestimating by 6.6% (p<0.0001). GAPS discriminated between admission and discharge as well as nurses, its AUC 0.876 compared with 0.875 for VAS (p=0.93). As a binary predictor, its accuracy was 80.6%, again comparable with VAS (79.0%), p=0.18. In the minority of attendances, when nurses felt at least 95% certain of the outcome, VAS' accuracy was excellent, at 92.4%. However, in the remaining majority, GAPS significantly outperformed VAS on calibration (+1.2% vs +9.2%, p<0.0001), discrimination (AUC 0.810 vs 0.759, p=0.001) and accuracy (75.1% vs 68.9%, p=0.0009). When we used GAPS, but 'over-ruled' it when clinical certainty was \u226595%, this significantly outperformed either method, with AUC 0.891 (0.877-0.907) and accuracy 82.5% (80.7%-84.2%).\"]\n\nQuestion: Predicting admission at triage: are nurses better than a simple objective score?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that GAPS, an objective score, performed comparably to triage nurses in overall discrimination and accuracy, and significantly better in calibration, especially when nurses were not highly certain. Only when nurses were at least 95% certain did their predictions outperform GAPS, but combining both methods yielded the best results. Therefore, nurses are not consistently better than the objective score.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 524, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 607}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.550399999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_868", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"To examine gout patients' knowledge of their condition, including the central role of achieving and maintaining the serum urate (SU) goal with the use of urate-lowering therapy (ULT).\", 'This study of 612 gout patients was conducted at a Veterans Affairs medical center. Gout patients were included based on administrative diagnostic codes and receipt of at least 1 allopurinol prescription over a 1-year period. Questionnaires were mailed to patients and linked to medical records data. The questionnaire included gout-specific knowledge questions, the Patient Activation Measure, and self-reported health outcomes. Knowledge was assessed descriptively. Multivariable logistic regression was used to determine predictors of SU goal knowledge. Associations of knowledge with health outcomes were examined in exploratory analyses.', 'The questionnaire had a 62% response rate. Only 14% of patients knew their SU goal, while the majority answered correctly for the other 5 gout-specific knowledge questions. In adjusted analyses, having a rheumatologist as initial prescriber (odds ratio [OR] 3.0 [95% confidence interval (95% CI) 1.4-6.2]) and knowing all of the other 5 gout-specific knowledge questions (OR 2.1 [95% CI 1.3-3.4]) were associated with greater odds of knowing the SU goal. SU goal knowledge was associated with self-reported global health status, but not with self-reported health-related quality of life or gout-specific health status.']\n\nQuestion: Target Serum Urate: Do Gout Patients Know Their Goal?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that only 14% of gout patients knew their serum urate (SU) goal, indicating a low level of awareness. Although some factors like seeing a rheumatologist increased the likelihood of knowing the goal, the majority of patients did not. Therefore, the evidence strongly suggests that most gout patients do not know their target serum urate.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 408, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 488}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.6967999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_87", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To determine the practices and knowledge of harmful effects regarding use of Chaalia and Pan Masala in three schools of Mahmoodabad and Chanesar Goth, Jamshed Town, Karachi, Pakistan.', 'To achieve the objective a cross-sectional design was used in three government schools of Mahmoodabad and Chanesar Goth, Jamshed Town, Karachi. Students of either gender drawn from these schools fulfilling the inclusion and exclusion criteria were interviewed using a pre-coded structured questionnaire. Along with demographic data, questions regarding frequency of Chaalia and Pan Masala use, practices of this habit in friends and family and place of procurement of these substances, were inquired. Knowledge was assessed about harmful effects and its source of information. In addition, practices in relation to that knowledge were assessed.', 'A total of 370 students were interviewed over a period of six weeks, of which 205 (55.4%) were boys. The ages of the students were between 10 and 15 years. Thirty one percent of the fathers and 62% of the mothers were uneducated. The frequency of use of any brand of Chaalia was found to be 94% and that of Pan Masala was 73.8%. Eighty five percent of them were regular users. A large majority (88%) procured the substances themselves from near their homes. Ninety five percent of the children had friends with the same habits. Eighty four percent were using the substances in full knowledge of their families. Chaalia was considered harmful for health by 96% and Pan Masala by 60%. Good taste was cited as a reason for continuing the habit by 88.5% of the children and use by friends by 57%. Knowledge about established harmful effects was variable. Knowledge about harmful effects was high in both \"daily\" and \"less than daily users\".']\n\nQuestion: Is Chaalia/Pan Masala harmful for health?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context states that 96% of children considered Chaalia harmful for health and 60% considered Pan Masala harmful. Additionally, the study assessed knowledge about the harmful effects, implying recognized health risks. Therefore, the evidence supports that Chaalia and Pan Masala are considered harmful.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 474, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 538}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.005399999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_870", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The aim of this study is to explore whether availability of sports facilities, parks, and neighbourhood social capital (NSC) and their interaction are associated with leisure time sports participation among Dutch adolescents.', 'Cross-sectional analyses were conducted on complete data from the last wave of the YouRAction evaluation trial. Adolescents (n\\u2009=\\u2009852) completed a questionnaire asking for sports participation, perceived NSC and demographics. Ecometric methods were used to aggregate perceived NSC to zip code level. Availability of sports facilities and parks was assessed by means of geographic information systems within the zip-code area and within a 1600 meter buffer. Multilevel logistic regression analyses, with neighborhood and individual as levels, were conducted to examine associations between physical and social environmental factors and leisure time sports participation. Simple slopes analysis was conducted to decompose interaction effects.', 'NSC was significantly associated with sports participation (OR: 3.51 (95%CI: 1.18;10.41)) after adjustment for potential confounders. Availability of sports facilities and availability of parks were not associated with sports participation. A significant interaction between NSC and density of parks within the neighbourhood area (OR: 1.22 (90%CI: 1.01;1.34)) was found. Decomposition of the interaction term showed that adolescents were most likely to engage in leisure time sports when both availability of parks and NSC were highest.']\n\nQuestion: Are neighbourhood social capital and availability of sports facilities related to sports participation among Dutch adolescents?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that neighbourhood social capital (NSC) was significantly associated with sports participation, while availability of sports facilities was not. Therefore, only NSC, not sports facilities, is related to sports participation.  \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 404, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 453}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.3583999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_871", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Polio eradication is now feasible after removal of Nigeria from the list of endemic countries and global reduction of cases of wild polio virus in 2015 by more than 80%. However, all countries must remain focused to achieve eradication. In August 2015, the Catholic bishops in Kenya called for boycott of a polio vaccination campaign citing safety concerns with the polio vaccine. We conducted a survey to establish if the coverage was affected by the boycott.', 'A cross sectional survey was conducted in all the 32 counties that participated in the campaign. A total of 90,157 children and 37,732 parents/guardians were sampled to determine the vaccination coverage and reasons for missed vaccination.', \"The national vaccination coverage was 93% compared to 94% in the November 2014 campaign. The proportion of parents/guardians that belonged to Catholic Church was 31% compared to 7% of the children who were missed. Reasons for missed vaccination included house not being visited (44%), children not being at home at time of visit (38%), refusal by parents (12%), children being as leep (1%), and various other reasons (5%). Compared to the November 2014 campaign, the proportion of children who were not vaccinated due to parent's refusal significantly increased from 6% to 12% in August 2015.\"]\n\nQuestion: Did the call for boycott by the Catholic bishops affect the polio vaccination coverage in Kenya in 2015?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The call for boycott by the Catholic bishops appears to have had a limited impact on overall vaccination coverage, as national coverage only slightly decreased from 94% to 93%. However, the proportion of unvaccinated children due to parental refusal doubled from 6% to 12%, indicating a notable increase in refusals despite the small change in overall coverage. This suggests the boycott influenced some parents, particularly within the Catholic community, but did not drastically alter the overall outcome.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 402, "output_tokens": 105, "total_tokens": 507}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.9042e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_872", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The purpose of this study was to determine whether there is an association between skewed X-inactivation and recurrent spontaneous abortion in a large, well-defined sample of women with recurrent loss.', 'X-chromosome inactivation patterns were compared in 5 groups of women. Group 1 (recurrent spontaneous abortion) consisted of 357 women with 2 or more spontaneous losses. In group 2 (infertility), there were 349 subjects from infertility practices recruited at the time of a positive serum beta-human chorionic gonadotropin. Group 3 (spontaneous abortion) women (n = 81) were recruited at the time of an ultrasound diagnosis of an embryonic demise or an anembryonic gestation. Groups 4 (primiparous) and 5 (multiparous) were healthy pregnant subjects previously enrolled in another study to determine the incidence and cause of pregnancy complications, such as preeclampsia and intrauterine growth restriction. The Primiparous group included 114 women in their first pregnancy, whereas the Multiparous group consisted of 79 women with 2 or more pregnancies but without pregnancy loss.', 'The rate of extreme skewing (90% or greater) in the recurrent spontaneous abortion population was 8.6%, and not statistically different from any of the other groups, except the Primiparous group (1.0%, P<.01). The incidence of X-inactivation skewing of 90% or greater was no different whether there had been at least 1 live birth (9.9%), or no previous live births and at least 3 losses (5.6%, P>.05). When age and skewing of 90% or greater are compared, subjects with extreme skewing have a mean age of 2 years older than those without extreme skewing (P<.05).']\n\nQuestion: Recurrent spontaneous abortion and skewed X-inactivation: is there an association?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that the rate of extreme X-inactivation skewing (90% or greater) in women with recurrent spontaneous abortion (8.6%) was not statistically different from most other groups, except the primiparous group. Although there was a significant association with age, no significant association was found between skewed X-inactivation and recurrent spontaneous abortion. Therefore, the evidence does not support a strong association.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 524, "output_tokens": 114, "total_tokens": 638}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.860399999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_875", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Associations between several psychopathological alterations and lowered beta-endorphin(beta E) plasma levels have already been stated in former studies. However, whereas single measures during static conditions generally failed in linking beta E levels with psychopathology, dynamic changes of beta E in particular have been shown to be associated with spells of anxiety and depression. During alcohol withdrawal, a decreased secretion of beta E with a delayed normalization has been reported, but up to now only few data became available regarding the interaction of plasma beta E and psychopathological parameters.', 'The aim of our study was to test the hypothesis whether beta E during acute alcohol withdrawal is associated with anxiety, depression, and craving.', 'We observed self-rated anxiety, depression, and craving during alcohol withdrawal and assessed beta E levels (RIA) in a consecutive sample of 60 alcoholics on day 1 and day 14 after onset of withdrawal, and in 30 healthy volunteers. To control for mutual interactions of beta E and the pituitary-adrenocortical hormone secretion, plasma corticotropin (ACTH) and cortisol were also determined.', 'In accordance with prior studies, beta E was significantly lowered on day 1 and day 14 of alcohol withdrawal relative to controls. Plasma levels of ACTH correlated significantly with beta E in alcoholics at both time points and in controls, without differing significantly between the groups. Self-rated anxiety, depression, and alcohol craving decreased significantly between day 1 and day 14. Levels of beta E were inversely correlated with anxiety day 1 (r=-0.58) and day 14 (r=-0.71). Partial correlation coefficients controlling for ACTH plasma levels revealed that this correlation was largely independent from ACTH. In addition, a significant inverse relationship was found between beta E and craving on day 14 (r=-0.28). No association appeared between beta E and depression.']\n\nQuestion: Is withdrawal-induced anxiety in alcoholism based on beta-endorphin deficiency?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found a significant inverse correlation between beta-endorphin (beta E) levels and anxiety during alcohol withdrawal, both on day 1 and day 14, even after controlling for ACTH levels. This suggests that lower beta E levels are associated with higher anxiety, supporting a link between beta-endorphin deficiency and withdrawal-induced anxiety. Therefore, the evidence points toward a \"yes.\"\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 485, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 569}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.283499999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_877", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To determine whether spectral Doppler measurements obtained from bilateral uterine, arcuate, radial, and spiral arteries in early gestation correlate with adverse pregnancy outcome.', \"One hundred five pregnant women underwent transvaginal Doppler sonographic examination of uteroplacental circulation at 6-12 weeks' gestation. Resistance index (RI) and pulsatility index (PI) of bilateral uterine, arcuate, radial, and spiral arteries were measured. Diameters of gestational sac (GS) and yolk sac, crown-rump length (CRL), GS-CRL difference, and GS/CRL ratio were also recorded. Correlation was made with pregnancy outcome.\", 'Sixteen women developed adverse pregnancy outcome. In these women, right uterine artery PI and RI were significantly higher than in women with normal obstetrical outcome. Spiral artery PI and RI values were also higher, but the difference was not statistically significant. GS-CRL difference, GS/CRL ratio, and yolk sac diameters were significantly lower in this group.']\n\nQuestion: Doppler examination of uteroplacental circulation in early pregnancy: can it predict adverse outcome?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that higher resistance index (RI) and pulsatility index (PI) in the right uterine artery were significantly associated with adverse pregnancy outcomes, indicating a predictive value. Additionally, other parameters like GS-CRL difference and yolk sac diameter were also significantly different in those with adverse outcomes. This suggests that early Doppler examination can provide useful predictive information.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 313, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 393}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.0223e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_878", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Complex regional pain syndrome type I is treated symptomatically. A protective effect of vitamin C (ascorbic acid) has been reported previously. A dose-response study was designed to evaluate its effect in patients with wrist fractures.', 'In a double-blind, prospective, multicenter trial, 416 patients with 427 wrist fractures were randomly allocated to treatment with placebo or treatment with 200, 500, or 1500 mg of vitamin C daily for fifty days. The effect of gender, age, fracture type, and cast-related complaints on the occurrence of complex regional pain syndrome was analyzed.', 'Three hundred and seventeen patients with 328 fractures were randomized to receive vitamin C, and ninety-nine patients with ninety-nine fractures were randomized to receive a placebo. The prevalence of complex regional pain syndrome was 2.4% (eight of 328) in the vitamin C group and 10.1% (ten of ninety-nine) in the placebo group (p=0.002); all of the affected patients were elderly women. Analysis of the different doses of vitamin C showed that the prevalence of complex regional pain syndrome was 4.2% (four of ninety-six) in the 200-mg group (relative risk, 0.41; 95% confidence interval, 0.13 to 1.27), 1.8% (two of 114) in the 500-mg group (relative risk, 0.17; 95% confidence interval, 0.04 to 0.77), and 1.7% (two of 118) in the 1500-mg group (relative risk, 0.17; 95% confidence interval, 0.04 to 0.75). Early cast-related complaints predicted the development of complex regional pain syndrome (relative risk, 5.35; 95% confidence interval, 2.13 to 13.42).']\n\nQuestion: Can vitamin C prevent complex regional pain syndrome in patients with wrist fractures?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows a significantly lower prevalence of complex regional pain syndrome (CRPS) in patients taking vitamin C (2.4%) compared to those on placebo (10.1%), with a statistically significant p-value of 0.002. The effect was most pronounced at doses of 500 mg and 1500 mg, where the relative risk of CRPS was reduced by about 83%. This evidence strongly supports a preventive effect of vitamin C.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 528, "output_tokens": 103, "total_tokens": 631}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.7788e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_880", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Rates of active travel vary by socio-economic position, with higher rates generally observed among less affluent populations. Aspects of both social and built environments have been shown to affect active travel, but little research has explored the influence of physical environmental characteristics, and less has examined whether physical environment affects socio-economic inequality in active travel. This study explored income-related differences in active travel in relation to multiple physical environmental characteristics including air pollution, climate and levels of green space, in urban areas across England. We hypothesised that any gradient in the relationship between income and active travel would be least pronounced in the least physically environmentally-deprived areas where higher income populations may be more likely to choose active transport as a means of travel.', 'Adults aged 16+ living in urban areas (n\\u2009=\\u200920,146) were selected from the 2002 and 2003 waves of the UK National Travel Survey. The mode of all short non-recreational trips undertaken by the sample was identified (n\\u2009=\\u2009205,673). Three-level binary logistic regression models were used to explore how associations between the trip being active (by bike/walking) and three income groups, varied by level of multiple physical environmental deprivation.', \"Likelihood of making an active trip among the lowest income group appeared unaffected by physical environmental deprivation; 15.4% of their non-recreational trips were active in both the least and most environmentally-deprived areas. The income-related gradient in making active trips remained steep in the least environmentally-deprived areas because those in the highest income groups were markedly less likely to choose active travel when physical environment was 'good', compared to those on the lowest incomes (OR\\u2009=\\u20090.44, 95% CI\\u2009=\\u20090.22 to 0.89).\"]\n\nQuestion: Are income-related differences in active travel associated with physical environmental characteristics?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that income-related differences in active travel vary depending on the level of physical environmental deprivation, with higher-income individuals being less likely to engage in active travel in areas with better physical environments. This suggests that physical environmental characteristics influence the income gradient in active travel. Therefore, income-related differences are associated with physical environmental characteristics.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 501, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 572}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.2671e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_885", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Platelet count is inversely related to prognosis in many cancers; however, its role in esophageal cancer is still controversial. The purpose of this study was to determine the prognostic value of preoperative platelet count in esophageal squamous cell carcinoma (ESCC).', 'From January 2006 to December 2008, a retrospective analysis of 425 consecutive patients with ESCC was conducted. A receiver operating characteristic (ROC) curve for survival prediction was plotted to verify the optimum cutoff point for preoperative platelet count. Univariate and multivariate analyses were performed to evaluate the prognostic parameters.', 'A ROC curve for survival prediction was plotted to verify the optimum cutoff point for platelet count, which was 205 (\u00d7 10(9)/L). Patients with platelet count \u2264 205 had a significantly better 5-year survival than patients with a platelet count>205 (60.7 vs. 31.6 %, P<0.001). The 5-year survival of patients either with platelet count \u2264 205 or>205 were similar (68.6 vs. 58.8 %, P = 0.085) when the nodes were negative. However, the 5-year survival of patients with platelet count \u2264 205 was better than that of patients with a platelet count>205 when the nodes were involved (32.0 vs. 12.7 %, P = 0.004). Multivariate analysis showed that platelet count (P = 0.013), T grade (P = 0.017), and N staging (P<0.001) were independent prognostic factors.']\n\nQuestion: Preoperative platelet count in esophageal squamous cell carcinoma: is it a prognostic factor?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that preoperative platelet count was significantly associated with 5-year survival in patients with esophageal squamous cell carcinoma, particularly in those with lymph node involvement. Multivariate analysis confirmed platelet count as an independent prognostic factor (P = 0.013). Therefore, the evidence supports that it is a prognostic factor.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 482, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 561}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.2121999999999994e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_886", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['In recent years the role of trace elements in lithogenesis has received steadily increasing attention.', 'This study was aimed to attempt to find the correlations between the chemical content of the stones and the concentration of chosen elements in the urine and hair of stone formers.', 'The proposal for the study was approved by the local ethics committee. Specimens were taken from 219 consecutive stone-formers. The content of the stone was evaluated using atomic absorption spectrometry, spectrophotometry, and colorimetric methods. An analysis of 29 elements in hair and 21 elements in urine was performed using inductively coupled plasma-atomic emission spectrometry.', 'Only a few correlations between the composition of stones and the distribution of elements in urine and in hair were found. All were considered incidental.']\n\nQuestion: Can we predict urinary stone composition based on an analysis of microelement concentration in the hair and urine?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found only a few correlations between stone composition and element concentrations in urine and hair, and these were considered incidental. This suggests there is no reliable predictive relationship. Therefore, we cannot predict urinary stone composition based on microelement analysis of hair and urine.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 327, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 410}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.1516999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_888", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['It has been shown in vitro that pretreatment of skin with fractional lasers enhances transdermal delivery of drugs. The aim of this study is to demonstrate in vivo firstly that laser enhances transdermal drug absorption and secondly that this can be manipulated by altering laser settings.STUDY DESIGN/', 'Four pigs were used in the IACUC approved animal study. On day 0, 5 g of 4% topical lidocaine was applied under occlusion for 60 minutes to a 400 cm(2) area on the abdomen. Blood was drawn at 0, 60, 90, 120, 180, and 240 minutes. On day 7, the Er:YAG laser was used at 500, 250, 50, and 25 \u00b5m ablative depth, respectively, over a 400 cm(2) area on the abdomen. Five grams of 4% topical lidocaine was applied immediately with occlusion for 60 minutes, and then removed. Blood was drawn at 0, 60, 90, 120, 180, and 240 minutes. The serum was extracted and analyzed for lidocaine and its metabolite monoethylglycinexylidide (MEGX).', 'Serum levels of lidocaine and MEGX were undetectable in untreated skin. Following laser treatment both lidocaine and MEGX were detectable. Peak levels of lidocaine were significantly higher (P = 0.0002) at 250 \u00b5m (0.62 mg/L), compared to 500 \u00b5m (0.45 mg/L), 50 \u00b5m (0.48 mg/L), and 25 \u00b5m (0.3 mg/L). Peak levels of MEGX were significantly higher (P \u2264 0.0001) at 250 \u00b5m (0.048 mg/L), compared to 500 \u00b5m (0.018 mg/L), 50 \u00b5m (0.036 mg/L), and 25 \u00b5m (0.0144 mg/L).']\n\nQuestion: Can fractional lasers enhance transdermal absorption of topical lidocaine in an in vivo animal model?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study demonstrates that after fractional laser treatment, serum levels of lidocaine and its metabolite MEGX became detectable, whereas they were undetectable in untreated skin. This indicates enhanced transdermal absorption of lidocaine following laser pretreatment. Additionally, the effect varied with laser settings, with peak absorption at 250 \u00b5m.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 578, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 655}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.8738e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_89", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The technique of induced sputum has allowed to subdivide asthma patients into inflammatory phenotypes according to their level of granulocyte airway infiltration. There are very few studies which looked at detailed sputum and blood cell counts in a large cohort of asthmatics divided into inflammatory phenotypes. The purpose of this study was to analyze sputum cell counts, blood leukocytes and systemic inflammatory markers in these phenotypes, and investigate how those groups compared with healthy subjects.', 'We conducted a retrospective cross-sectional study on 833 asthmatics recruited from the University Asthma Clinic of Liege and compared them with 194 healthy subjects. Asthmatics were classified into inflammatory phenotypes.', 'The total non-squamous cell count per gram of sputum was greater in mixed granulocytic and neutrophilic phenotypes as compared to eosinophilic, paucigranulocytic asthma and healthy subjects (p\\u2009<\\u20090.005). Sputum eosinophils (in absolute values and percentages) were increased in all asthma phenotypes including paucigranulocytic asthma, compared to healthy subjects (p\\u2009<\\u20090.005). Eosinophilic asthma showed higher absolute sputum neutrophil and lymphocyte counts than healthy subjects (p\\u2009<\\u20090.005), while neutrophilic asthmatics had a particularly low number of sputum macrophages and epithelial cells. All asthma phenotypes showed an increased blood leukocyte count compared to healthy subjects (p\\u2009<\\u20090.005), with paucigranulocytic asthmatics having also increased absolute blood eosinophils compared to healthy subjects (p\\u2009<\\u20090.005). Neutrophilic asthma had raised CRP and fibrinogen while eosinophilic asthma only showed raised fibrinogen compared to healthy subjects (p\\u2009<\\u20090.005).']\n\nQuestion: Detailed analysis of sputum and systemic inflammation in asthma phenotypes: are paucigranulocytic asthmatics really non-inflammatory?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that even paucigranulocytic asthmatics have increased sputum eosinophils and blood leukocytes compared to healthy subjects, indicating the presence of inflammation. Additionally, they exhibit elevated absolute blood eosinophils, which suggests systemic inflammatory activity. Therefore, paucigranulocytic asthma is not truly non-inflammatory.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 570, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 649}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.837e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_891", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['European Member States are facing a challenge to provide accessible and effective health care services for immigrants. It remains unclear how best to achieve this and what characterises good practice in increasingly multicultural societies across Europe. This study assessed the views and values of professionals working in different health care contexts and in different European countries as to what constitutes good practice in health care for immigrants.', 'A total of 134 experts in 16 EU Member States participated in a three-round Delphi process. The experts represented four different fields: academia, Non-Governmental Organisations, policy-making and health care practice. For each country, the process aimed to produce a national consensus list of the most important factors characterising good practice in health care for migrants.', 'The scoring procedures resulted in 10 to 16 factors being identified as the most important for each participating country. All 186 factors were aggregated into 9 themes: (1) easy and equal access to health care, (2) empowerment of migrants, (3) culturally sensitive health care services, (4) quality of care, (5) patient/health care provider communication, (6) respect towards migrants, (7) networking in and outside health services, (8) targeted outreach activities, and (9) availability of data about specificities in migrant health care and prevention. Although local political debate, level of immigration and the nature of local health care systems influenced the selection and rating of factors within each country, there was a broad European consensus on most factors. Yet, discordance remained both within countries, e.g. on the need for prioritising cultural differences, and between countries, e.g. on the need for more consistent governance of health care services for immigrants.']\n\nQuestion: Health care for immigrants in Europe: is there still consensus among country experts about principles of good practice?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context indicates that while there were differences within and between countries, there was a \"broad European consensus on most factors\" characterizing good practice in health care for immigrants. Despite some discordance on specific issues like cultural differences and governance, the overall agreement among experts across countries was evident. Therefore, the most accurate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 447, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 519}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.8937e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_893", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The ImmunoCAP ISAC 112 is a fluoro-immunoassay that allows detection of specific IgE to 112 molecular components from 51 allergenic sources. We studied the reliability of this technique intra- and inter- assay, as well as inter-batch- and inter-laboratory-assay.', \"Twenty samples were studied, nineteen sera from polysensitized allergic patients, and the technique calibrator provided by the manufacturer (CTR02). We measured the sIgE from CTR02 and three patients' sera ten times in the same and in different assays. Furthermore, all samples were tested in two laboratories and with two batches of ISAC kit. To evaluate the accuracy of ISAC 112, we contrasted the determinations of CTR02 calibrator with their expected values by T Student test. To analyse the precision, we calculated the coefficient of variation (CV) of the 15 allergens that generate the calibration curve, and to analyse the repeatability and the reproducibility, we calculated the intraclass coefficient correlation (ICC) to each allergen.\", 'The results obtained for CTR02 were similar to those expected in 7 of 15 allergens that generate the calibration curve, whereas in 8 allergens the results showed significant differences. The mean CV obtained in the CTR02 determinations was of 9.4%, and the variability of sera from patients was of 22.9%. The agreement in the intra- and inter-assay analysis was very good to 94 allergens and good to one. In the inter-batch analyse, we obtained a very good agreement to 82 allergens, good to 14, moderate to 5 allergens, poor to one, and bad to 1 allergen. In the inter-laboratory analyse, we obtained a very good agreement to 73 allergens, good to 22, moderate to 6 and poor to two allergens.']\n\nQuestion: Is the determination of specific IgE against components using ISAC 112 a reproducible technique?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows high repeatability and reproducibility for the majority of allergens tested, with very good to good agreement in intra- and inter-assay, inter-batch, and inter-laboratory analyses. Although some variability exists, particularly in inter-laboratory settings, the overall consistency supports reliable performance. Therefore, the determination of specific IgE using ISAC 112 is considered reproducible.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 514, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 603}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.5394e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_897", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The purpose of this study was to investigate whether knowledge of ultrasound-obtained estimated fetal weight (US-EFW) is a risk factor for cesarean delivery (CD).', 'Retrospective cohort from a single center in 2009-2010 of singleton, term live births. CD rates were compared for women with and without US-EFW within 1 month of delivery and adjusted for potential confounders.', 'Of the 2329 women in our cohort, 50.2% had US-EFW within 1 month of delivery. CD was significantly more common for women with US-EFW (15.7% vs 10.2%; P<.001); after we controlled for confounders, US-EFW remained an independent risk factor for CD (odds ratio, 1.44; 95% confidence interval, 1.1-1.9). The risk increased when US-EFW was>3500 g (odds ratio, 1.8; 95% confidence interval, 1.3-2.7).']\n\nQuestion: Estimated fetal weight by ultrasound: a modifiable risk factor for cesarean delivery?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that knowledge of ultrasound-estimated fetal weight (US-EFW) is associated with a higher likelihood of cesarean delivery, especially when the estimated weight exceeds 3500 g. This suggests that US-EFW may influence clinical decisions, making it a potentially modifiable risk factor. Therefore, the most appropriate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 305, "output_tokens": 90, "total_tokens": 395}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.0655e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_90", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To assess the impact of the comprehensive HIV/STD Control Program established in Jamaica since the late 1980s on the HIV/AIDS epidemic.', 'AIDS case reports, HIV testing of blood donors, antenatal clinic attenders (ANC), food service workers, sexually transmitted disease (STD) clinic attenders, female prostitutes, homosexuals and other groups were used to monitor the HIV/AIDS epidemic. Primary and secondary syphilis and cases of congenital syphilis were also monitored. National knowledge, attitude and practice (KAP) surveys were conducted in 1988, 1989, 1992, 1994 and 1996.', 'The annual AIDS incidence rate in Jamaica increased only marginally in the past three years from 18.5 per 100000 population to 21.4 in 1997. HIV prevalence in the general population groups tested has been about 1% or less. Among those at high risk, HIV prevalence rates have risen to 6.3% (95% confidence interval 5.0-8.0) in STD clinic attenders, around 10% and 21% in female prostitutes in Kingston and Montego Bay respectively and approximately 30% among homosexuals. Syphilis rates and congenital syphilis cases have declined. The proportion of men aged 15-49 years reporting sex with a non-regular partner declined from 35% in 1994 to 26% in 1996 (P<0.001). Women ever having used condoms increased from 51% in 1988 to 62.5% in 1992 and 73% in 1994 and 1996 (P<0.001), while condom use with a non-regular partner increased from 37% in 1992 to 73% in 1996 (P= 0.006). Condom use among men was high over the period: around 81% had ever used condoms and 77% used them with non-regular partners. Gay men, inner-city adults and adolescents aged 12-14 years all reported increases in condom use while condom sales and distribution increased from around 2 million in 1985 to 10 million in 1995.']\n\nQuestion: Is HIV/STD control in Jamaica making a difference?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data show declines in syphilis rates, increased condom use across multiple groups, and stable or low HIV prevalence in the general population despite high-risk groups showing higher rates. These trends suggest that the HIV/STD Control Program has had a positive impact on curbing the spread of HIV and STDs in Jamaica. Therefore, the evidence supports that the program is making a difference.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 609, "output_tokens": 82, "total_tokens": 691}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 5.1439e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_900", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The aim of this study was to assess the diagnostic value of articular sounds, standardized clinical examination, and standardized articular ultrasound in the detection of internal derangements of the temporomandibular joint.', 'Forty patients and 20 asymptomatic volunteers underwent a standardized interview, physical examination, and static and dynamic articular ultrasound. Sensitivity, specificity, and predictive values were calculated using magnetic resonance as the reference test.', 'A total of 120 temporomandibular joints were examined. Based on our findings, the presence of articular sounds and physical signs are often insufficient to detect disk displacement. Imaging by static and dynamic high-resolution ultrasound demonstrates considerably lower sensitivity when compared with magnetic resonance. Some of the technical difficulties resulted from a limited access because of the presence of surrounding bone structures.']\n\nQuestion: Internal derangement of the temporomandibular joint: is there still a place for ultrasound?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on the context, ultrasound demonstrated considerably lower sensitivity compared to MRI and faced technical limitations due to bone structures, making it less reliable for detecting internal derangements. While it may offer some utility, the evidence suggests it is insufficient as a primary diagnostic tool. Therefore, the most appropriate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 261, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 326}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.5030999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_901", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To assess whether it is possible for an experienced laparoscopic surgeon to perform efficient laparoscopic myomectomy regardless of the size, number, and location of the myomas.', 'Prospective observational study (Canadian Task Force classification II-1).', 'Tertiary endoscopy center.', 'A total of 505 healthy nonpregnant women with symptomatic myomas underwent laparoscopic myomectomy at our center. No exclusion criteria were based on the size, number, or location of myomas.', 'Laparoscopic myomectomy and modifications of the technique: enucleation of the myoma by morcellation while it is still attached to the uterus with and without earlier devascularization.', 'In all, 912 myomas were removed in these 505 patients laparoscopically. The mean number of myomas removed was 1.85 +/- 5.706 (95% CI 1.72-1.98). In all, 184 (36.4%) patients had multiple myomectomy. The mean size of the myomas removed was 5.86 +/- 3.300 cm in largest diameter (95% CI 5.56-6.16 cm). The mean weight of the myomas removed was 227.74 +/- 325.801 g (95% CI 198.03-257.45 g) and median was 100 g. The median operating time was 60 minutes (range 30-270 minutes). The median blood loss was 90 mL (range 40-2000 mL). Three comparisons were performed on the basis of size of the myomas (<10 cm and>or=10 cm in largest diameter), number of myomas removed (<or=4 and>or=5 myomas), and the technique (enucleation of the myomas by morcellation while the myoma is still attached to the uterus and the conventional technique). In all these comparisons, although the mean blood loss, duration of surgery, and hospital stay were greater in the groups in which larger myomas or more myomas were removed or the modified technique was performed as compared with their corresponding study group, the weight and size of removed myomas were also proportionately larger in these groups. Two patients were given the diagnosis of leiomyosarcoma in their histopathology and 1 patient developed a diaphragmatic parasitic myoma followed by a leiomyoma of the sigmoid colon. Six patients underwent laparoscopic hysterectomy 4 to 6 years after the surgery for recurrent myomas. One conversion to laparotomy occurred and 1 patient underwent open subtotal hysterectomy for dilutional coagulopathy.']\n\nQuestion: Laparoscopic myomectomy: do size, number, and location of the myomas form limiting factors for laparoscopic myomectomy?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study demonstrates that laparoscopic myomectomy was successfully performed regardless of the size, number, or location of myomas, with high efficiency and low conversion rates. Although larger or multiple myomas were associated with longer operating times and greater blood loss, these factors did not preclude the use of the laparoscopic approach. Therefore, the evidence suggests that these factors do not form absolute limiting factors.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 701, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 788}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 5.8470999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_905", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Implant-related infections represent one of the most severe complications in orthopaedics. A fast-resorbable, antibacterial-loaded hydrogel may reduce or prevent bacterial colonization and biofilm formation of implanted biomaterials.QUESTIONS/', 'We asked: (1) Is a fast-resorbable hydrogel able to deliver antibacterial compounds in vitro? (2) Can a hydrogel (alone or antibacterial-loaded) coating on implants reduce bacterial colonization? And (3) is intraoperative coating feasible and resistant to press-fit implant insertion?', 'We tested the ability of Disposable Antibacterial Coating (DAC) hydrogel (Novagenit Srl, Mezzolombardo, Italy) to deliver antibacterial agents using spectrophotometry and a microbiologic assay. Antibacterial and antibiofilm activity were determined by broth microdilution and a crystal violet assay, respectively. Coating resistance to press-fit insertion was tested in rabbit tibias and human femurs.', 'Complete release of all tested antibacterial compounds was observed in less than 96 hours. Bactericidal and antibiofilm effect of DAC hydrogel in combination with various antibacterials was shown in vitro. Approximately 80% of the hydrogel coating was retrieved on the implant after press-fit insertion.']\n\nQuestion: Does implant coating with antibacterial-loaded hydrogel reduce bacterial colonization and biofilm formation in vitro?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study demonstrated that the antibacterial-loaded hydrogel (DAC) showed bactericidal and antibiofilm effects in vitro. Both microbiologic assays and crystal violet assays confirmed reduction in bacterial colonization and biofilm formation. Therefore, the evidence supports a positive effect.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 358, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 416}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.1218e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_908", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['In familial adenomatous polyposis (FAP), correlations between site of mutation in the adenomatous polyposis coli (APC) gene and severity of colonic polyposis or extracolonic manifestations are well known. While mutation analysis is important for predictive diagnosis in persons at risk, its relevance for clinical management of individual patients is open to question.', 'We examined 680 unrelated FAP families for germline mutations in the APC gene. Clinical information was obtained from 1256 patients.', \"APC mutations were detected in 48% (327/680) of families. Age at diagnosis of FAP based on bowel symptoms and age at diagnosis of colorectal cancer in untreated patients were used as indicators of the severity of the natural course of the disease. A germline mutation was detected in 230 of 404 patients who were diagnosed after onset of bowel symptoms (rectal bleeding, abdominal pain, diarrhoea). When these patients were grouped according to the different sites of mutations, mean values for age at onset of disease differed significantly: patients carrying APC mutations at codon 1309 showed a disease onset 10 years earlier (mean age 20 years) compared with patients with mutations between codons 168 and 1580 (except codon 1309) (mean age 30 years), whereas patients with mutations at the 5' end of codon 168 or the 3' end of codon 1580 were diagnosed at a mean age of 52 years. Within each group of patients however large phenotypic variation was observed, even among patients with identical germline mutations. A higher incidence of desmoids was found in patients with mutations between codons 1445 and 1580 compared with mutations at other sites, while no correlation between site of mutation and presence of duodenal adenomas was observed.\"]\n\nQuestion: Can APC mutation analysis contribute to therapeutic decisions in familial adenomatous polyposis?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The text states that while mutation analysis is important for predictive diagnosis, its relevance for the clinical management of individual patients is \"open to question.\" Furthermore, the study highlights that large phenotypic variation exists even among patients with identical germline mutations, suggesting that the mutation site alone is not a definitive guide for therapeutic decisions. Therefore, the most likely answer is that it is not currently established as a primary tool for such decisions.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 483, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 572}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:34.996112+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00025425, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_91", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The morbidity and mortality associated with Panton-Valentine leucocidin (PVL)-positive Staphylococcus aureus suggest that this toxin is a key marker of disease severity. Nevertheless, the importance of PVL in the pathogenesis of primary bacteraemia caused by S. aureus is uncertain. We have determined the prevalence of PVL-encoding genes among isolates of S. aureus from bacteraemic patients.', 'Consecutive bacteraemia isolates of S. aureus (n=244) from patients hospitalized in 25 centres in the UK and Ireland during 2005 were screened for PVL and mecA genes. PVL-positive isolates were characterized by toxin gene profiling, PFGE, spa-typing and MIC determinations for a range of antimicrobials.', 'Four out of 244 isolates (1.6%) were PVL-positive and susceptible to oxacillin [methicillin-susceptible S. aureus (MSSA)]. Eighty-eight out of 244 (36%) were oxacillin-resistant (methicillin-resistant S. aureus), but none was PVL-positive. The four patients (two males: 30 and 33 years; two females: 62 and 80 years) had infection foci of: skin and soft tissue, unknown, indwelling line, and surgical site, and were located at one centre in Wales, one in England and two in Ireland. One of four PVL-positive isolates was resistant to penicillin and fusidic acid, the remainder were susceptible to all antibiotics tested. Genotypic analyses showed that the four isolates represented three distinct strains; the two isolates from Ireland were related.']\n\nQuestion: Is Panton-Valentine leucocidin associated with the pathogenesis of Staphylococcus aureus bacteraemia in the UK?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that only 1.6% of the 244 *S. aureus* bacteraemia isolates were PVL-positive, suggesting that PVL is not a common or primary factor in these cases. The context explicitly states that the importance of PVL in the pathogenesis of primary bacteraemia remains uncertain. Therefore, based on the low prevalence and the study's findings, the most likely answer is no.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 437, "output_tokens": 94, "total_tokens": 531}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:14.878602+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00025025, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_913", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To study whether exercise during pregnancy reduces the risk of postnatal depression.', 'Randomized controlled trial.', 'Trondheim and Stavanger University Hospitals, Norway.', 'Eight hundred and fifty-five pregnant women were randomized to intervention or control groups.', 'The intervention was a 12 week exercise program, including aerobic and strengthening exercises, conducted between week 20 and 36 of pregnancy. One weekly group session was led by physiotherapists, and home exercises were encouraged twice a week. Control women received regular antenatal care.', 'Edinburgh Postnatal Depression Scale (EPDS) completed three months after birth. Scores of 10 or more and 13 or more suggested probable minor and major depression, respectively.', 'Fourteen of 379 (3.7%) women in the intervention group and 17 of 340 (5.0%) in the control group had an EPDS score of \u226510 (p=0.46), and four of 379 (1.2%) women in the intervention group and eight of 340 (2.4%) in the control group had an EPDS score of \u226513 (p=0.25). Among women who did not exercise prior to pregnancy, two of 100 (2.0%) women in the intervention group and nine of 95 (9.5%) in the control group had an EPDS score of \u226510 (p=0.03).']\n\nQuestion: Does exercise during pregnancy prevent postnatal depression?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no statistically significant difference in postnatal depression rates between the intervention and control groups overall (p=0.46 and p=0.25). While a subgroup analysis showed a benefit for women who did not exercise prior to pregnancy, the primary results do not support a general conclusion that exercise prevents postnatal depression. Therefore, the most accurate answer based on the overall findings is no.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 389, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 474}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:24.470063+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00022475, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_914", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Endometrial polyp is a common cause of abnormal uterine bleeding, but the etiology and pathogenesis remain unclear. Vascular endothelial growth factor (VEGF) is angiogenic, related to thick walled vessels and transforming growth factor-beta1 (TGF-\u03b21) is related to fibrotic tissue, which are characteristics of endometrial polyps. The primary objective of this study was to find out if endometrial polyp formation is associated with increased expression of VEGF or TGF-\u03b21, or both. A secondary objective is to determine if the changes are related to steroid receptor expression.', 'This prospective study compared VEGF and TGF-\u03b21 expression of endometrial polyps and adjacent endometrial tissue in 70 premenopausal women. The comparison of results was separately made for endometrium specimens obtained in the proliferative and secretory phases. The results were correlated with the steroid receptors (estrogen receptor and progesterone receptor) expression.', \"The score of VEGF in glandular cells of endometrial polyps was significantly higher than the score in adjacent endometrium, both in the proliferative phase (P<0.001) and the secretory phase (P=0.03); the score of VEGF in stromal cells of endometrial polyps was significantly higher than the score in adjacent endometrium only in proliferative phase (P=0.006). The score of TGF-\u03b21 in glandular cells of endometrial polyps was significantly higher than the score in adjacent endometrium in proliferative phase (P=0.02); whereas the score of TGF-\u03b21 in stromal cells of endometrial polyps was significantly higher than the score in adjacent endometrium, both in the proliferative phase (P=0.006) and the secretory phase (P=0.008). There was a significant correlation between the expression of steroid receptors and VEGF and TGF-\u03b21 (Spearman's correlation P<0.001 and P<0.05, respectively).\"]\n\nQuestion: Is endometrial polyp formation associated with increased expression of vascular endothelial growth factor and transforming growth factor-beta1?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found significantly higher expression of both VEGF and TGF-\u03b21 in endometrial polyps compared to adjacent endometrial tissue, particularly in glandular and stromal cells during the proliferative phase. A significant correlation was also observed between steroid receptor expression and the levels of VEGF and TGF-\u03b21. These findings support that endometrial polyp formation is associated with increased expression of both growth factors.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 555, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 650}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.8904999999999993e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_915", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Recent studies have implicated the human cytomegalovirus (HCMV) as a possible pathogen for causing hypertension. We aimed to study the association between HCMV infection and hypertension in the United States National Health and Nutrition Examination Survey (NHANES).', 'We analyzed data on 2979 men and 3324 women in the NHANES 1999-2002. We included participants aged 16-49 years who had valid data on HCMV infection and hypertension.', 'Of the participants, 54.7% had serologic evidence of HCMV infection and 17.5% had hypertension. There were ethnic differences in the prevalence of HCMV infection (P<0.001) and hypertension (P<0.001). The prevalence of both increased with age (P<0.001). Before adjustment, HCMV seropositivity was significantly associated with hypertension in women (OR=1.63, 95% CI=1.25-2.13, P=0.001) but not in men. After adjustment for race/ethnicity, the association between HCMV seropositivity and hypertension in women remained significant (OR=1.55, 95% CI=1.20-2.02, P=0.002). Further adjustment for body mass index, diabetes status and hypercholesterolemia attenuated the association (OR=1.44, 95% CI=1.10-1.90, P=0.010). However, after adjusting for age, the association was no longer significant (OR=1.24, 95% CI=0.91-1.67, P=0.162).']\n\nQuestion: Is human cytomegalovirus infection associated with hypertension?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The association between HCMV infection and hypertension in women was significant before and after adjusting for race/ethnicity and certain health factors, but it became non-significant after adjusting for age. This suggests that age may be a key confounding factor explaining the observed association. Therefore, after full adjustment, there is no significant independent association.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 486, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 559}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.1806e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_916", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Treatment of HBeAg-negative chronic hepatitis B (CHB) with nucleos(t)ide analogues (NA) is usually indefinite, since the loss of HBsAg, as a criterion for its discontinuation, is a rare event. Recent evidence suggests that discontinuing NA therapy may be feasible in selected patients.', 'To analyze the rate of virological relapse in patients with HBeAg-negative CHB who discontinued treatment with NAs.', 'We performed a single-center observational study that included 140 patients with HBsAg-negative CHB. Twenty-two patients, who received only NAs, discontinued treatment for different reasons and were subsequently monitored. All had normal ALT and AST, undetectable DNA and absence of cirrhosis or significant comorbidities before stopping treatment.', 'Twelve patients showed virologic relapse (54.54%). The mean interval between discontinuation and relapse was 6.38 months (\u00b1 1.9) (75% relapsed during the first 12 months after discontinuation). Five received adefovir, 1 lamivudine and adefovir, 1 tenofovir and 5 lamivudine alone. The mean treatment duration in this group was 38.5 months (\u00b1 4.5). The sustained response group had a higher mean age and longer treatment duration than patients with virologic relapse but these differences were not statistically significant.']\n\nQuestion: Is it possible to stop treatment with nucleos(t)ide analogs in patients with e-antigen negative chronic hepatitis B?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study suggests that discontinuation of nucleos(t)ide analogues in selected patients with HBeAg-negative chronic hepatitis B may be feasible, although virological relapse occurs in a significant proportion (54.54% in this cohort). However, relapse typically occurred within the first year, and successful\u505c\u836f was observed in some patients, indicating it is possible under certain conditions.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 406, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 491}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.7325999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_921", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Serum pancreatic lipase may improve the diagnosis of pancreatitis compared to serum amylase. Both enzymes have been measured simultaneously at our hospital allowing for a comparison of their diagnostic accuracy.', \"Seventeen thousand five hundred and thirty-one measurements of either serum amylase and or serum pancreatic lipase were made on 10 931 patients treated at a metropolitan teaching hospital between January 2001 and May 2003. Of these, 8937 were initially treated in the Emergency Department. These results were collected in a database, which was linked by the patients' medical record number to the radiology and medical records. Patients with either an elevated lipase value or a discharge diagnosis of acute pancreatitis had their radiological diagnosis reviewed along with their biochemistry and histology record. The diagnosis of acute pancreatitis was made if there was radiological evidence of peripancreatic inflammation.\", 'One thousand eight hundred and twenty-five patients had either elevated serum amylase and or serum pancreatic lipase. The medical records coded for pancreatitis in a further 55 whose enzymes were not elevated. Three hundred and twenty of these had radiological evidence of acute pancreatitis. Receiver operator characteristic analysis of the initial sample from patients received in the Emergency Department showed improved diagnostic accuracy for serum pancreatic lipase (area under the curve (AUC) 0.948) compared with serum amylase (AUC, 0.906, P<0.05). A clinically useful cut-off point would be at the diagnostic threshold; 208 U/L (normal<190 U/L) for serum pancreatic lipase and 114 U/L (normal 27-100 U/L) for serum amylase where the sensitivity was 90.3 cf., 76.8% and the specificity was 93 cf., 92.6%. 18.8% of the acute pancreatitis patients did not have elevated serum amylase while only 2.9% did not have elevated serum pancreatic lipase on the first emergency department measurement.']\n\nQuestion: Should serum pancreatic lipase replace serum amylase as a biomarker of acute pancreatitis?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that serum pancreatic lipase has higher diagnostic accuracy (AUC 0.948 vs. 0.906), better sensitivity (90.3% vs. 76.8%), and comparable specificity compared to serum amylase. Additionally, only 2.9% of acute pancreatitis patients had normal lipase levels versus 18.8% with normal amylase, indicating superior detection. Therefore, serum pancreatic lipase should replace serum amylase as the preferred biomarker.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 537, "output_tokens": 115, "total_tokens": 652}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.9627e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_923", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To evaluate the outcome of a new modification of percutaneous needle suspension, using a bone anchor system for fixing the suture at the public bone, and to compare the results with those published previously.', \"From March 1996, 37 patients with stress urinary incontinence (>2 years) were treated using a bone anchor system. On each side the suture was attached to the pubocervical fascia and the vaginal wall via a broad 'Z'-stitch. A urodynamic investigation performed preoperatively in all patients confirmed stress incontinence and excluded detrusor instability. The outcome was assessed by either by a clinical follow-up investigation or using a standardized questionnaire, over a mean follow-up of 11 months (range 6-18).\", 'In the 37 patients, the procedure was successful in 25 (68%), with 16 (43%) of the patients completely dry and nine (24%) significantly improved. Removal of the bone anchor and suture was necessary in two patients, because of unilateral bacterial infection in one and a bilateral soft tissue granuloma in the other. One bone anchor became dislocated in a third patient. In two cases where the treatment failed, new detrusor instability was documented urodynamically. Minor complications were prolonged wound pain in 10 (26%) and transient urinary retention or residual urine in 12 patients (32%).']\n\nQuestion: Does bone anchor fixation improve the outcome of percutaneous bladder neck suspension in female stress urinary incontinence?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The provided context describes a study of bone-anchor percutaneous suspension with a 68% success rate (43% dry) but does not report any comparative data versus prior non-anchor techniques. It does, however, document anchor-specific complications (infection, granuloma, dislocation) and notes new detrusor instability, implying no net improvement. Consequently the most likely answer among the given choices is \u201cno.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 483, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 566}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00081125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_925", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Family caregivers of dementia patients are at increased risk of developing depression or anxiety. A multi-component program designed to mobilize support of family networks demonstrated effectiveness in decreasing depressive symptoms in caregivers. However, the impact of an intervention consisting solely of family meetings on depression and anxiety has not yet been evaluated. This study examines the preventive effects of family meetings for primary caregivers of community-dwelling dementia patients.', 'A randomized multicenter trial was conducted among 192 primary caregivers of community dwelling dementia patients. Caregivers did not meet the diagnostic criteria for depressive or anxiety disorder at baseline. Participants were randomized to the family meetings intervention (n\\u200a=\\u200a96) or usual care (n\\u200a=\\u200a96) condition. The intervention consisted of two individual sessions and four family meetings which occurred once every 2 to 3 months for a year. Outcome measures after 12 months were the incidence of a clinical depressive or anxiety disorder and change in depressive and anxiety symptoms (primary outcomes), caregiver burden and quality of life (secondary outcomes). Intention-to-treat as well as per protocol analyses were performed.', 'A substantial number of caregivers (72/192) developed a depressive or anxiety disorder within 12 months. The intervention was not superior to usual care either in reducing the risk of disorder onset (adjusted IRR 0.98; 95% CI 0.69 to 1.38) or in reducing depressive (randomization-by-time interaction coefficient\\u200a=\\u200a-1.40; 95% CI -3.91 to 1.10) or anxiety symptoms (randomization-by-time interaction coefficient\\u200a=\\u200a-0.55; 95% CI -1.59 to 0.49). The intervention did not reduce caregiver burden or their health related quality of life.']\n\nQuestion: Does a family meetings intervention prevent depression and anxiety in family caregivers of dementia patients?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that the family meetings intervention was not superior to usual care in preventing the onset of depressive or anxiety disorders, nor in reducing symptoms of depression or anxiety. There were no significant improvements in caregiver burden or quality of life. Therefore, the intervention did not demonstrate preventive effects.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 505, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 567}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.2055e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_926", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To investigate the association between age-related macular degeneration (AMD) and the polymorphisms of HIF1A, a major vascular epithelial growth factor regulator under hypoxic conditions. The associations of AMD and polymorphisms of genes CFH, SKIV2L and MYRIP were also studied.', 'Prospective study.', 'Eighty-seven AMD patients and 80 healthy subjects admitted to the Department of Ophthalmology at Pamukkale University Hospital, Denizli, Turkey, were included: 45 (52%) had wet type AMD, and 42 (48%) had dry type AMD.', 'Polymorphisms rs1061170 (CFH), rs429608 (SKIV2L), rs2679798 (MYRIP) and both rs11549465 and rs11549467 (HIF1A) were investigated in DNA isolated from peripheral blood samples of the cases and controls by dye-termination DNA sequencing.', 'Genotype distribution of rs1061170 (CFH), rs429608 (SKIV2L), rs2679798 (MYRIP) and both rs11549465 and rs11549467 (HIF1A) in AMD cases and healthy controls; association between genotypes and AMD subtypes.', 'Given the significant difference between the mean age of case and control groups (72.13\\u2009\u00b1\\u20095.77 vs. 62.80\\u2009\u00b1\\u20095.22, respectively) (P\\u2009=\\u2009.000), subsequent analyses were adjusted for age. We found that having at least one C allele for polymorphism rs1061170 increases AMD risk independent of age (OR\\u2009=\\u20092.42, 95% confidence interval [CI], 1.22-4.81). The ancestral T allele for polymorphism rs1061170 has a protective effect for AMD (OR\\u2009=\\u20090.53, 95% CI, 0.34-0.83). No statistically significant difference for distributions of other single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) emerged between patients and healthy subjects.']\n\nQuestion: HIF1A as a major vascular endothelial growth factor regulator: do its polymorphisms have an association with age-related macular degeneration?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study investigated polymorphisms in HIF1A (rs11549465 and rs11549467) but found no statistically significant difference in their distribution between AMD patients and healthy controls. Although HIF1A is a key regulator of vascular endothelial growth factor under hypoxia, the data did not support an association between these specific HIF1A polymorphisms and AMD. Therefore, the most accurate answer based on the provided results is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 648, "output_tokens": 106, "total_tokens": 754}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 5.6608e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_928", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['This study represents a subset of a complete data set, considering only those children aged admitted to the Pediatric Surgery and Pediatric Nephrology Clinics during the period January 2011 to July 2012.', 'In this study, we have determined that the QT interval changes significantly depending on the use of oxybutynin. The QT changes increased cardiac arrhythmia in children.']\n\nQuestion: Does oxybutynin hydrochloride cause arrhythmia in children with bladder dysfunction?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context states that oxybutynin use is associated with significant QT interval changes, which in turn increased cardiac arrhythmia in children. This suggests a direct link between oxybutynin and arrhythmia risk. Therefore, the evidence supports that oxybutynin hydrochloride can cause arrhythmia in children.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 177, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 247}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.9567e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_931", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The aims of the study were to report the rates of recurrent and residual cholesteatoma following primary CAT surgery and to report the rate of conversion to a modified radical mastoidectomy.', 'This was a retrospective review of a single surgeon series between 2006 and 2012.', 'In total 132 second-look operations were undertaken, with a mean interval between primary surgery and second-look procedures of 6 months. The rate of cholesteatoma at second-look surgery was 19.7%, which was split into residual disease (10.6%) and recurrent disease (9.09%). New tympanic membrane defects with cholesteatoma were considered as recurrent disease. Residual disease was defined as cholesteatoma present behind an intact tympanic membrane. The majority of recurrent and residual disease was easily removed at second look (73.1%). Only four cases were converted to a modified radical mastoidectomy (3%) and three cases required a third-look procedure.']\n\nQuestion: Can early second-look tympanoplasty reduce the rate of conversion to modified radical mastoidectomy?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that only 3% of cases required conversion to a modified radical mastoidectomy, and the majority of residual or recurrent cholesteatoma was easily managed at second look. This low conversion rate suggests that early second-look surgery may help avoid more extensive procedures. Therefore, the evidence supports that early second-look tympanoplasty can reduce the need for radical surgery.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 313, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 398}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.0723e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_938", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Hyperleptinemia and oxidative stress play a major role in the development of cardiovascular diseases in obesity. This study aimed to investigate whether there is a relationship between plasma levels of leptin and phagocytic nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate (NADPH) oxidase activity, and its potential relevance in the vascular remodeling in obese patients.', 'The study was performed in 164 obese and 94 normal-weight individuals (controls). NADPH oxidase activity was evaluated by luminescence in phagocytic cells. Levels of leptin were quantified by ELISA in plasma samples. Carotid intima-media thickness (cIMT) was measured by ultrasonography. In addition, we performed in-vitro experiments in human peripheral blood mononuclear cells and murine macrophages.', 'Phagocytic NADPH oxidase activity and leptin levels were enhanced (P<0.05) in obese patients compared with controls. NADPH oxidase activity positively correlated with leptin in obese patients. This association remained significant in a multivariate analysis. cIMT was higher (P<0.05) in obese patients compared with controls. In addition, cIMT also correlated positively with leptin and NADPH oxidase activity in obese patients. In-vitro studies showed that leptin induced NADPH oxidase activation. Inhibition of the leptin-induced NADPH oxidase activity by wortmannin and bisindolyl maleimide suggested a direct involvement of the phosphatidylinositol 3-kinase and protein kinase C pathways, respectively. Finally, leptin-induced NADPH oxidase activation promoted macrophage proliferation.']\n\nQuestion: Is leptin involved in phagocytic NADPH oxidase overactivity in obesity?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows that leptin levels are elevated in obese patients and positively correlate with phagocytic NADPH oxidase activity. In vitro experiments further demonstrate that leptin directly induces NADPH oxidase activation, which is linked to macrophage proliferation and vascular remodeling. This evidence strongly supports a direct role of leptin in NADPH oxidase overactivity in obesity.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 500, "output_tokens": 103, "total_tokens": 603}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.5799999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_939", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"An increasingly significant public health issue in Canada, and elsewhere throughout the developed world, pertains to the provision of adequate palliative/end-of-life (P/EOL) care. Informal caregivers who take on the responsibility of providing P/EOL care often experience negative physical, mental, emotional, social and economic consequences. In this article, we specifically examine how Canada's Compassionate Care Benefit (CCB)--a contributory benefits social program aimed at informal P/EOL caregivers--operates as a public health response in sustaining informal caregivers providing P/EOL care, and whether or not it adequately addresses known aspects of caregiver burden that are addressed within the population health promotion (PHP) model.\", \"As part of a national evaluation of Canada's Compassionate Care Benefit, 57 telephone interviews were conducted with Canadian informal P/EOL caregivers in 5 different provinces, pertaining to the strengths and weaknesses of the CCB and the general caregiving experience. Interview data was coded with Nvivo software and emerging themes were identified by the research team, with such findings published elsewhere. The purpose of the present analysis was identified after comparing the findings to the literature specific to caregiver burden and public health, after which data was analyzed using the PHP model as a guiding framework.\", 'Informal caregivers spoke to several of the determinants of health outlined in the PHP model that are implicated in their burden experience: gender, income and social status, working conditions, health and social services, social support network, and personal health practises and coping strategies. They recognized the need for improving the CCB to better address these determinants.']\n\nQuestion: Canada's Compassionate Care Benefit: is it an adequate public health response to addressing the issue of caregiver burden in end-of-life care?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}\n\nThe article indicates that informal caregivers experience significant burdens related to multiple determinants of health, such as income, social support, and working conditions, which are not adequately addressed by the Compassionate Care Benefit (CCB). Caregivers themselves recognized the need for improvements to the CCB, suggesting it falls short as a comprehensive public health response.", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 426, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 500}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.7646e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_94", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['One of the problems with manual resuscitators is the difficulty in achieving accurate volume delivery. The volume delivered to the patient varies by the physical characteristics of the person and method. This study was designed to compare tidal volumes delivered by the squeezing method, physical characteristics and education and practice levels.', '114 individuals trained in basic life support and bag-valve-mask ventilation participated in this study. Individual characteristics were obtained by the observer and the education and practice level were described by the subjects. Ventilation was delivered with a manual resuscitator connected to a microspirometer and volumes were measured. Subjects completed three procedures: one-handed, two-handed and two-handed half-compression.', 'The mean (standard deviation) volumes for the one-handed method were 592.84 ml (SD 117.39), two-handed 644.24 ml (SD 144.7) and two-handed half-compression 458.31 ml (SD 120.91) (p<0.01). Tidal volume delivered by two hands was significantly greater than that delivered by one hand (r = 0.398, p<0.01). The physical aspects including hand size, volume and grip power had no correlation with the volume delivered. There were slight increases in tidal volume with education and practice, but correlation was weak (r = 0.213, r = 0.281, r = 0.131, p<0.01).']\n\nQuestion: Can you deliver accurate tidal volume by manual resuscitator?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows significant variability in tidal volumes delivered by manual resuscitators, with volumes differing based on technique and individual performance, and physical characteristics or training having only weak correlations with accuracy. This indicates consistent and accurate volume delivery is difficult to achieve manually. Therefore, accurate tidal volume cannot be reliably delivered using a manual resuscitator.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 414, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 488}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.6793999999999994e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_940", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"To determine whether fibromyalgia (FM) is more common in patients with primary Sj\u00f6gren's syndrome (pSS) who complain of fatigue. The association and prevalence of fatigue and FM was recorded in a group of patients with pSS and a control group of lupus patients, a subset of whom had secondary Sj\u00f6gren's syndrome (sSS).\", '74 patients with pSS and 216 patients with lupus were assessed with a questionnaire to identify the presence of fatigue and generalised pain. From the lupus group, in a subset of 117 lupus patients (from the Bloomsbury unit) those with sSS were identified. All patients were studied for the presence of FM.', '50 of 74 patients with pSS (68%) reported fatigue-a prevalence significantly higher than in the lupus group (108/216 (50%); p<0.0087). Fatigue was present in 7/13 (54%) patients with SLE/sSS. FM was present in 9/74 patients with pSS (12%), compared with 11/216 lupus patients (5%), and in none of the patients with SLE/sSS. None of these values corresponds with previously reported figures of the incidence of FM in pSS.']\n\nQuestion: Fatigue in primary Sj\u00f6gren's syndrome: is there a link with the fibromyalgia syndrome?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that fatigue was significantly more common in patients with primary Sj\u00f6gren's syndrome (68%) compared to lupus patients (50%), and fibromyalgia (FM) was more prevalent in pSS (12%) than in lupus (5%). However, the presence of FM in only 9 out of 50 fatigued pSS patients suggests that while both fatigue and FM are more common in pSS, they do not strongly co-occur. Therefore, the data do not establish a clear link between fatigue in pSS and fibromyalgia.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 383, "output_tokens": 128, "total_tokens": 511}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.9992999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_943", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The apparent favorable effect of alcohol on the risk of acute myocardial infarction (MI) may be related to its hypoinsulinemic effect when consumed with meals. We studied how the timing of alcohol consumption in relation to meals might affect the risk of MI in a population with relatively high regular alcohol consumption.', 'We conducted a case-control study between 1995 and 1999 in Milan, Italy. Cases were 507 subjects with a first episode of nonfatal acute MI, and controls were 478 patients admitted to hospitals for other acute diseases. Odds ratios (ORs) and 95% confidence intervals (CIs) were calculated by multiple logistic regression models.', 'Compared with nondrinkers, an inverse trend in risk was observed when alcohol was consumed during meals only (for>or =3 drinks per day: OR = 0.50; 95% CI = 0.30-0.82). In contrast, no consistent trend in risk was found for subjects drinking outside of meals (for>or =3 drinks per day: 0.98; 0.49-1.96). The pattern of risk was similar when we considered people who drank only wine.']\n\nQuestion: Alcohol consumption and acute myocardial infarction: a benefit of alcohol consumed with meals?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found an inverse trend in the risk of acute myocardial infarction (MI) when alcohol was consumed during meals, with a significantly lower odds ratio (OR = 0.50) for those consuming three or more drinks per day with meals. In contrast, no such protective effect was observed when alcohol was consumed outside of meals. This suggests that the timing of alcohol consumption matters, and there is a benefit when alcohol is consumed with meals.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 355, "output_tokens": 97, "total_tokens": 452}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.4905e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_944", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Mossy fibers are the sole excitatory projection from dentate gyrus granule cells to the hippocampus, forming part of the trisynaptic hippocampal circuit. They undergo significant plasticity during epileptogenesis and have been implicated in seizure generation. Mossy fibers are a highly unusual projection in the mammalian brain; in addition to glutamate, they release adenosine, dynorphin, zinc, and possibly other peptides. Mossy fiber terminals also show intense immunoreactivity for the inhibitory neurotransmitter gamma-aminobutyric acid (GABA), and immunoreactivity for GAD67. The purpose of this review is to present physiologic evidence of GABA release by mossy fibers and its modulation by epileptic activity.', 'We used hippocampal slices from 3- to 5-week-old guinea pigs and made whole-cell voltage clamp recordings from CA3 pyramidal cells. We placed stimulating electrodes in stratum granulosum and adjusted their position in order to recruit mossy fiber to CA3 projections.', 'We have shown that electrical stimuli that recruit dentate granule cells elicit monosynaptic GABAA receptor-mediated synaptic signals in CA3 pyramidal neurons. These inhibitory signals satisfy the criteria that distinguish mossy fiber-CA3 synapses: high sensitivity to metabotropic glutamate-receptor agonists, facilitation during repetitive stimulation, and N-methyl-D-aspartate (NMDA) receptor-independent long-term potentiation.']\n\nQuestion: Do mossy fibers release GABA?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The provided context states that mossy fiber terminals show intense immunoreactivity for GABA and GAD67, and that electrical stimulation of dentate granule cells elicits GABAA receptor-mediated synaptic signals in CA3 pyramidal neurons. These findings provide physiologic evidence that mossy fibers release GABA. Therefore, the most likely correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 392, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 471}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.5731999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_945", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Some patients with suspected common bile duct (CBD) stones are found to have sludge and no stones. Although sludge in the gallbladder is a precursor of gallbladder stones, the significance of bile duct sludge (BDS) is poorly defined. This study aimed to compare BDS with bile duct stones in terms of frequency, associated risk factors, and clinical outcome after endoscopic therapy.', 'The study enrolled 228 patients who underwent therapeutic endoscopic retrograde cholangiopancreatography (ERCP) for suspected choledocholithiasis. The patients were divided into two groups: patients with BDS but no stones on ERCP and patients with CBD stones. The presence of risk factors for bile duct stones (age, periampullary diverticulum, ductal dilation or angulation, previous open cholecystectomy) were assessed at ERCP. Follow-up data (36 +/- 19 months) were obtained from medical records and by patient questioning.', 'Bile duct sludge occurred in 14% (31/228) of patients and was more common in females. After endoscopic clearance, CBD stones recurred in 17% (33/197) of the patients with CBD stones, and in 16% (5/31) of the patients with BDS (p = 0.99). Common bile duct dilation was less common in the sludge group. The other known risk factors for recurrent CBD stones (age, previous open cholecystectomy, bile duct angulation, and the presence of a peripampullary diverticulum) were not statistically different between the two groups.']\n\nQuestion: The clinical significance of bile duct sludge: is it different from bile duct stones?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that bile duct sludge (BDS) and bile duct stones had similar recurrence rates after endoscopic clearance (16% vs. 17%, p = 0.99), and most risk factors were not significantly different between groups. Although CBD dilation was less common in the sludge group, the overall clinical outcomes were comparable. Therefore, the clinical significance of bile duct sludge does not appear to be meaningfully different from that of bile duct stones.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 440, "output_tokens": 103, "total_tokens": 543}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.154e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_946", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"Manual resuscitation devices for infants and newborns must be able to provide adequate ventilation in a safe and consistent manner across a wide range of patient sizes (0.5-10\\u2005kg) and differing clinical states. There are little comparative data assessing biomechanical performance of common infant manual resuscitation devices across the manufacturers' recommended operating weight ranges. We aimed to compare performance of the Ambu self-inflating bag (SIB) with the Neopuff T-piece resuscitator in three resuscitation models.\", 'Five experienced clinicians delivered targeted ventilation to three lung models differing in compliance, delivery pressures and inflation rates; Preterm (0.5\\u2005mL/cmH2O, 25/5 cmH2O, 60 per minute), Term (3\\u2005mL/cmH2O, 30/5 cmH2O, 40 per minute) and Infant (9\\u2005mL/cmH2O, 35/5 cmH2O, 30 per minute). The Neopuff was examined with three gas inflow rates (5 litres per minute (LPM), 10 LPM and 15 LPM) and the Ambu with no gas inflow.', '3309 inflations were collected and analysed with analysis of variance for repeated measures. The Neopuff was unable to reach set peak inflation pressures and exhibited seriously elevated positive end expiratory pressure (PEEP) with all inflow gas rates (p<0.001) in this infant model. The Ambu SIB accurately delivered targeted pressures in all three models.']\n\nQuestion: Can Ambu self-inflating bag and Neopuff infant resuscitator provide adequate and safe manual inflations for infants up to 10\u2005kg weight?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that the Ambu self-inflating bag accurately delivered targeted ventilation pressures across all three infant lung models, while the Neopuff failed to reach set pressures and caused elevated PEEP, indicating potential safety risks. Therefore, only the Ambu SIB performed adequately and safely within the tested parameters. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 466, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 535}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.9986e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_947", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['All VLBW infants from January 2008 to December 2012 with positive blood culture beyond 72 hours of life were enrolled in a retrospective cohort study. Newborns born after June 2010 were treated with IgM-eIVIG, 250 mg/kg/day iv for three days in addition to standard antibiotic regimen and compared to an historical cohort born before June 2010, receiving antimicrobial regimen alone. Short-term mortality (i.e. death within 7 and 21 days from treatment) was the primary outcome. Secondary outcomes were: total mortality, intraventricular hemorrhage, necrotizing enterocolitis, periventricular leukomalacia, bronchopulmonary dysplasia at discharge.', '79 neonates (40 cases) were enrolled. No difference in birth weight, gestational age or SNAP II score (disease severity score) were found. Significantly reduced short-term mortality was found in treated infants (22% vs 46%; p = 0.005) considering all microbial aetiologies and the subgroup affected by Candida spp. Secondary outcomes were not different between groups.']\n\nQuestion: Are IgM-enriched immunoglobulins an effective adjuvant in septic VLBW infants?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study shows a significant reduction in short-term mortality (22% vs 46%, p = 0.005) in VLBW infants treated with IgM-enriched immunoglobulins (IgM-eIVIG) compared to those receiving antibiotics alone. This benefit was observed across all microbial causes, including Candida spp., suggesting a clinically meaningful effect. Although secondary outcomes were not different, the primary outcome strongly supports efficacy.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 348, "output_tokens": 98, "total_tokens": 446}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.4507999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_95", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"To explain China's cigarette pricing mechanism and the role of the Chinese State Tobacco Monopoly Administration (STMA) on cigarette pricing and taxation.\", 'Published government tobacco tax documentation and statistics published by the Chinese STMA are used to analyse the interrelations among industry profits, taxes and retail price of cigarettes in China.', 'The 2009 excise tax increase on cigarettes in China has not translated into higher retail prices because the Chinese STMA used its policy authority to ensure that retail cigarette prices did not change. The government tax increase is being collected at both the producer and wholesale levels. As a result, the 2009 excise tax increase in China has resulted in higher tax revenue for the government and lower profits for the tobacco industry, with no increase in the retail price of cigarettes for consumers.']\n\nQuestion: Can increases in the cigarette tax rate be linked to cigarette retail prices?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on the context, the 2009 excise tax increase did not lead to higher retail prices because the Chinese STMA controlled pricing, absorbing the tax increase at the producer and wholesale levels. This indicates that tax increases are not necessarily passed on to consumers. Therefore, increases in the cigarette tax rate cannot be directly linked to retail prices in this case.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 255, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 333}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.5904999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_953", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Acupuncture has been successfully used in myofascial pain syndromes. However, the number of needles used, that is, the dose of acupuncture stimulation, to obtain the best antinociceptive efficacy is still a matter of debate. The question was addressed comparing the clinical efficacy of two different therapeutic schemes, characterized by a different number of needles used on 36 patients between 29-60 years of age with by a painful cervical myofascial syndrome.', 'Patients were divided into two groups; the first group of 18 patients were treated with 5 needles and the second group of 18 patients were treated with 11 needles, the time of needle stimulation was the same in both groups: 100 seconds. Each group underwent six cycles of somatic acupuncture. Pain intensity was evaluated before, immediately after and 1 and 3 months after the treatment by means of both the Mc Gill Pain Questionnaire and the Visual Analogue Scale (VAS). In both groups, the needles were fixed superficially excluding the two most painful trigger points where they were deeply inserted.', 'Both groups, independently from the number of needles used, obtained a good therapeutic effect without clinically relevant differences.']\n\nQuestion: Neck pain treatment with acupuncture: does the number of needles matter?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study compared two groups receiving acupuncture with different numbers of needles (5 vs. 11) and found no clinically relevant differences in pain relief outcomes. Both groups showed similar improvements in pain intensity as measured by standardized scales. Therefore, the number of needles does not appear to matter for therapeutic effect in this context.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 338, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 407}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.0897999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_955", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To compare the results between a sliding compression hip screw and an intramedullary nail in the treatment of pertrochanteric fractures.', 'Prospective computer-generated randomization of 206 patients into two study groups: those treated by sliding compression hip screw (Group 1; n = 106) and those treated by intramedullary nailing (Group 2; n = 100).', 'University Level I trauma center.', 'All patients over the age of fifty-five years presenting with fractures of the trochanteric region caused by a low-energy injury, classified as AO/OTA Type 31-A1 and A2.', 'Treatment with a sliding compression hip screw (Dynamic Hip Screw; Synthes-Stratec, Oberdorf, Switzerland) or an intramedullary nail (Proximal Femoral Nail; Synthes-Stratec, Oberdorf, Switzerland).', 'Intraoperative: operative and fluoroscopy times, the difficulty of the operation, intraoperative complications, and blood loss. Radiologic: fracture healing and failure of fixation. Clinical: pain, social functioning score, and mobility score.', 'The minimum follow-up was one year. We did not find any statistically significant difference, intraoperatively, radiologically, or clinically, between the two groups of patients.']\n\nQuestion: Pertrochanteric fractures: is there an advantage to an intramedullary nail?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no statistically significant differences between the sliding compression hip screw and intramedullary nail in terms of intraoperative, radiologic, or clinical outcomes. Therefore, there is no demonstrated advantage to using an intramedullary nail over a sliding hip screw for pertrochanteric fractures in this patient population. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 370, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 441}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.337e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_956", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"The differential diagnosis between essential tremor (ET) and Parkinson's disease (PD) may be, in some cases, very difficult on clinical grounds alone. In addition, it is accepted that a small percentage of ET patients presenting symptoms and signs of possible PD may progress finally to a typical pattern of parkinsonism. Ioflupane, N-u-fluoropropyl-2a-carbomethoxy-3a-(4-iodophenyl) nortropane, also called FP-CIT, labelled with (123)I (commercially known as DaTSCAN) has been proven to be useful in the differential diagnosis between PD and ET and to confirm dopaminergic degeneration in patients with parkinsonism. The aim of this study is to identify dopaminergic degeneration in patients with PD and distinguish them from others with ET using semi-quantitative SPECT (123)I-Ioflupane (DaTSCAN) data in comparison with normal volunteers (NV), in addition with the respective ones of patients referred as suffering from ET, as well as, of patients with a PD diagnosis at an initial stage with a unilateral presentation of motor signs.\", 'Twenty-eight patients suffering from ET (10 males plus 18 females) and 28 NV (12 males and 16 females) were enroled in this study. In addition, 33 patients (11 males and 22 females) with an established diagnosis of PD with unilateral limb involvement (12 left hemi-body and 21 right hemi-body) were included for comparison with ET. We used DaTSCAN to obtain SPECT images and measure the radiopharmaceutical uptake in the striatum (S), as well as the caudate nucleus (CN) and putamen (P) in all individuals.', 'Qualitative (Visual) interpretation of the SPECT data did not find any difference in the uptake of the radiopharmaceutical at the level of the S, CN and P between NV and ET patients. Reduced accumulation of the radiopharmaceutical uptake was found in the P of all PD patients. Semiquantitative analysis revealed significant differences between NV and ET patients in the striatum, reduced in the latter. There was also a significant reduction in the tracer accumulation in the left putamen of patients with right hemi-parkinsonism compared to ET and NV. Patients with left hemi-parkinsonism, demonstrated reduced radioligand uptake in the right putamen in comparison with ET and NV. Clinical follow-up of 20 patients with ET at (so many months afterwards) revealed no significant change in clinical presentation, particularly no signs of PD. Follow-up DaTSCAN performed in 10 of them (so many months afterwards) was negative in all but one. This one had an equivocal baseline study which deteriorated 12\\xa0months later.']\n\nQuestion: SPECT study with I-123-Ioflupane (DaTSCAN) in patients with essential tremor. Is there any correlation with Parkinson's disease?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant reduction in radiopharmaceutical uptake in the putamen of patients with essential tremor (ET), which is a key marker of dopaminergic degeneration seen in Parkinson's disease (PD). Only one out of ten follow-up DaTSCAN scans in ET patients showed deterioration, and this was preceded by an equivocal baseline. Therefore, there is no strong correlation between ET and Parkinson's disease on DaTSCAN imaging.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 713, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 808}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 6.0123e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_96", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['We observed an endoscopic abnormally in a group of children with histological esophagitis. We termed this finding \"vertical lines in esophageal mucosa\" (VLEM). We examined the relationship between the presence of VLEM and significant histologic changes in esophageal mucosal biopsies.', 'Between January 1, 1992, and August 31, 1994, the senior author (JFF) performed 255 esophageal biopsies. The procedure reports, available endoscopic photographs, and histology reports were reviewed to establish the endoscopic and histologic appearance of the esophageal mucosa. Intraepithelial cells were counted in a blind review of 42 randomly selected biopsies.', 'The esophageal mucosa had a normal appearance on 160 endoscopic studies (Group 1) and VLEM were the only mucosal abnormalities in 41 endoscopies (Group 2). Histology was normal in 92 of 160 biopsies (57.5%) from Group 1, and 1 of 41 biopsies (2.4%) from Group 2. Most patients in Group 2 had eosinophilic esophagitis (34 of 41, 83%, specificity 0.85, sensitivity 0.5, p>0.001) which was of moderate to severe intensity (31 of 34, 91.2%, specificity 0.88, sensitivity 0.73, p<0.001).']\n\nQuestion: Vertical lines in distal esophageal mucosa (VLEM): a true endoscopic manifestation of esophagitis in children?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The presence of vertical lines in esophageal mucosa (VLEM) was strongly associated with histologic esophagitis, particularly eosinophilic esophagitis, in the studied pediatric population. Only 2.4% of Group 2 (with VLEM) had normal histology, compared to 57.5% in Group 1 (normal endoscopy), and the differences were statistically significant (p<0.001). This suggests VLEM is a reliable endoscopic sign of esophagitis in children.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 448, "output_tokens": 118, "total_tokens": 566}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.3608e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_960", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Traditional resectional techniques and chordal transfer are difficult to apply in video-assisted mitral valve repair. Using artificial chords appears easier in this setting. The purpose of this study was to review the effectiveness and reproducibility of neochordal repair as a routine approach to minimally invasive mitral repair, and to assess the stability of neochord implantation using the figure-of-eight suture without pledgets in this setting.', 'This is a retrospective review of all patients who underwent minimally invasive video-assisted mitral valve repair from 2008 to 2013. The primary endpoints were recurrent mitral regurgitation and reoperation.', 'A total of 426 consecutive patients were included during the study period, with a mean age of 55 \u00b1 18 years. Neochords were used in all patients, and in association with leaflet resection in 47 patients. One patient was not repairable and underwent valve replacement (repair rate, 99.8%). Fifteen patients had Grade I (3.5%) regurgitation, whereas the remainder had none. Patients were fast-tracked, with 25% extubated in the operation theatre and the remainder within 6 h. There were 5 deaths within 30 days (1.2%). Follow-up ranged 3-60 months, during which all of the patients remained with no or trace mitral regurgitation. No de-insertion or rupture of any neochords was found, and no patients required a reoperation.']\n\nQuestion: Is minimally invasive mitral valve repair with artificial chords reproducible and applicable in routine surgery?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study demonstrates that neochordal repair was successfully used in 426 patients with a 99.8% repair rate and no instances of neochord de-insertion or rupture during follow-up. All patients remained with no or trace mitral regurgitation, and no reoperations were required, indicating high effectiveness and stability. These outcomes support the reproducibility and routine applicability of the technique.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 418, "output_tokens": 90, "total_tokens": 508}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.8678e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_962", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The cytomorphology of liquid-based preparations in urine cytology is different than classic slide preparations.', 'To compare the performance of liquid-based preparation specimens to classically prepared urine specimens with a malignant diagnosis in the College of American Pathologists Interlaboratory Comparison Program in Nongynecologic Cytology.', 'Participant responses between 2000 and 2007 for urine specimens with a reference diagnosis of high-grade urothelial carcinoma/carcinoma in situ/dysplasia (HGUCA), squamous cell carcinoma, or adenocarcinoma were evaluated. ThinPrep and SurePath challenges were compared with classic preparations (smears, cytospins) for discordant responses.', 'There were 18 288 pathologist, 11 957 cytotechnologist, and 8086 \"laboratory\" responses available. Classic preparations comprised 90% (n = 34 551) of urine challenges; 9% (n = 3295) were ThinPrep and 1% (n = 485) were SurePath. Concordance to the general category of \"positive-malignant\" was seen in 92% of classic preparations, 96.5% of ThinPrep, and 94.6% of SurePath challenges (P<.001). These results were statistically different for the exact reference interpretation of HGUCA (P<.001) but not for adenocarcinoma (P = .22). Cytotechnologists demonstrate statistically better performance for the general category of \"positive-malignant\" compared with pathologists for all urinary slide types and for the exact reference interpretation of HGUCA (94% versus 91.1%; P<.001) but not adenocarcinoma (96.3% versus 95.8%; P = .77) or squamous cell carcinoma (93.6% versus 87.7%; P = .07).']\n\nQuestion: Do liquid-based preparations of urinary cytology perform differently than classically prepared cases?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data show statistically significant differences in concordance rates for the \"positive-malignant\" category and for the exact diagnosis of high-grade urothelial carcinoma between liquid-based (ThinPrep, SurePath) and classic preparations (P<.001). Although the differences are small in magnitude, they are statistically significant and consistent across reviewer types. Therefore, liquid-based preparations perform differently than classically prepared cases.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 529, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 620}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.6659e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_965", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['There is an urgent need to increase opportunistic screening for sexually transmitted infections (STIs) in community settings, particularly for those who are at increased risk including men who have sex with men (MSM). The aim of this qualitative study was to explore whether home sampling kits (HSK) for multiple bacterial STIs are potentially acceptable among MSM and to identify any concerns regarding their use. This study was developed as part of a formative evaluation of HSKs.', 'Focus groups and one-to-one semi-structured interviews with MSM were conducted. Focus group participants (n = 20) were shown a variety of self-sampling materials and asked to discuss them. Individual interviewees (n = 24) had experience of the self-sampling techniques as part of a pilot clinical study. All data were digitally recorded and transcribed verbatim. Data were analysed using a framework analysis approach.', \"The concept of a HSK was generally viewed as positive, with many benefits identified relating to increased access to testing, enhanced personal comfort and empowerment. Concerns about the accuracy of the test, delays in receiving the results, the possible lack of support and potential negative impact on 'others' were raised.\"]\n\nQuestion: Are home sampling kits for sexually transmitted infections acceptable among men who have sex with men?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study indicates that home sampling kits (HSKs) were generally viewed positively by men who have sex with men (MSM), with perceived benefits such as increased access, personal comfort, and empowerment. Although some concerns were raised about accuracy, delays in results, and lack of support, the overall acceptability was positive. Therefore, the most appropriate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 336, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 414}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.1655999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_968", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To compare in vitro fertilization (IVF) outcomes in low responders stimulated with microdose leuprolide protocol (ML) following pretreatment with either oral contraceptive pill (OCP) or luteal estradiol (E2) + GnRH antagonist (E2 + antag) for follicular synchronization prior to controlled ovarian hyperstimulation (COH).', 'This was a retrospective study of 130 women, who were poor responders, undergoing IVF with either OCP/ML or E2+ antag/ML protocols. The main outcome measures were ongoing pregnancy rates, number of oocytes retrieved, and cancellation rate.', 'Both groups were similar in baseline characteristics. There were no significant differences in gonadotropin requirement, cancellation rate, and number of embryos transferred. Ongoing pregnancy rates (40% vs. 15%) were significantly higher in the OCP/ML group. Trends toward greater number of oocytes retrieved (7.7 \u00b1 3.4 vs. 5.9 \u00b1 4.2) and improved implantation rates (20% vs. 12%) were also noted, but these did not reach statistical significance.']\n\nQuestion: Estradiol and Antagonist Pretreatment Prior to Microdose Leuprolide in in Vitro Fertilization. Does It Improve IVF Outcomes in Poor Responders as Compared to Oral Contraceptive Pill?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found significantly higher ongoing pregnancy rates in the oral contraceptive pill (OCP) group compared to the estradiol + antagonist (E2 + antag) group (40% vs. 15%). Although trends favored the OCP group in oocytes retrieved and implantation rates, the key outcome of ongoing pregnancy was statistically superior with OCP pretreatment. Therefore, estradiol and antagonist pretreatment does not improve IVF outcomes as compared to OCP in poor responders.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 369, "output_tokens": 105, "total_tokens": 474}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.6698999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_974", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['Arterial calcification is a significant cardiovascular risk factor in hemodialysis patients. A series of factors are involved in the process of arterial calcification; however, the relationship between malnutrition and arterial calcification is still unclear.', '68 hemodialysis patients were enrolled in this study. Nutrition status was evaluated using modified quantitative subjective global assessment (MQSGA). Related serum biochemical parameters were measured. And the radial artery samples were collected during the arteriovenous fistula surgeries. Hematoxylin/eosin stain was used to observe the arterial structures while Alizarin red stain to observe calcified depositions and classify calcified degree. The expressions of bone morphogenetic protein 2 (BMP2) and matrix Gla protein (MGP) were detected by immunohistochemistry and western blot methods.', '66.18% hemodialysis patients were malnutrition. In hemodialysis patients, the calcified depositions were mainly located in the medial layer of the radial arteries and the expressions of BMP2 and MGP were both increased in the calcified areas. The levels of serum albumin were negatively associated with calcification score and the expressions of BMP2 and MGP. While MQSGA score, serum phosphorus and calcium\\u2009\u00d7\\u2009phosphorus product showed positive relationships with calcification score and the expressions of BMP2 and MGP.']\n\nQuestion: Malnutrition, a new inducer for arterial calcification in hemodialysis patients?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that 66.18% of hemodialysis patients had malnutrition, and higher malnutrition (as indicated by higher MQSGA scores) was positively associated with arterial calcification, BMP2, and MGP expression. Additionally, serum albumin (a marker of good nutrition) was negatively associated with calcification, suggesting malnutrition is linked to increased calcification. Therefore, the evidence supports malnutrition as a potential inducer.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 384, "output_tokens": 97, "total_tokens": 481}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.6964e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_976", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['A side-to-side difference in systolic brachial arterial blood pressure is a common finding in subclavian artery stenosis and is frequently used as a screening tool for subclavian steal syndrome (SSS). It was the goal of this retrospective study to investigate the relationship between different vertebral artery waveform types and the side-to-side difference in systolic blood pressure in patients with sonographically proven SSS.', 'The records of 1860 patients from the Neuroultrasound Laboratory between January 2000 and December 2000 were screened for the diagnosis of SSS in the final ultrasound report. In all patients, bilateral brachial arterial blood pressure was measured in a sitting position prior to the ultrasound examination. Vertebral artery waveforms were classified as (1) systolic deceleration, (2) alternating flow, and (3) complete reversal at rest. Blood pressure difference as calculated by normal-side blood pressure minus lesion-side blood pressure was compared with the 3 Doppler waveform types.', 'SSS was found in 51 of 1860 (2.7%) ultrasonography studies of 49 patients (17 men, 32 women; mean age 65.3 +/- 10.5 years). Two patients (4%) had bilateral SSS. In 3 patients (6%), SSS was related to an innominate artery stenosis. Waveform analysis showed a completely reversed flow in 16 (31%), an alternating flow in 24 (47%), and a systolic deceleration in 11 (22%) cases. Systolic blood pressure difference was significantly higher in the complete reversal and alternating groups than in the systolic deceleration group (P<.001).']\n\nQuestion: Subclavian steal syndrome: can the blood pressure difference between arms predict the severity of steal?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that systolic blood pressure difference between arms was significantly higher in patients with more severe vertebral artery waveform abnormalities (complete reversal and alternating flow) compared to milder forms (systolic deceleration), indicating a correlation between blood pressure difference and severity of steal. This suggests that the inter-arm blood pressure difference can serve as a predictor of the severity of subclavian steal syndrome. Therefore, the evidence supports a positive association.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 469, "output_tokens": 94, "total_tokens": 563}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.2699e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_977", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To assess Internet use amongst young people to determine whether it would be a practical way to provide sex education and information.', 'Year 10 students (aged 14-15 years) from North Nottinghamshire schools were asked to participate in focus groups to discuss the Internet. A series of predefined questions were directed to the whole group to generate debate. Areas explored included: Internet access and site; frequency and purpose of Internet use; websites visited; ideas for a genitourinary medicine (GUM) website. Responses were recorded by a hand count or as individual verbal responses.', \"Thirteen focus groups were held involving 287 students of approximately equal sex distribution. All had access to Internet facilities at school and 224 (78.0%) had access elsewhere. Access was at least once a week by 178 (62.0%) mostly for e-mail, games, chatlines and homework. No one accessed for health information. One hundred and seventy-nine (62.4%) participants said they would use a GUM website. A 'question line' where they could e-mail questions to a health care professional was of interest to 202 (70.4%) participants.\"]\n\nQuestion: Can the Internet be used to improve sexual health awareness in web-wise young people?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The focus group data show that a majority of students (62.4%) would use a genitourinary medicine (GUM) website, and 70.4% were interested in a \"question line\" to ask health professionals, indicating a willingness to engage with sexual health content online. Although no participants currently used the Internet for health information, their frequent Internet use and access suggest potential for online sexual health education. Therefore, the Internet appears to be a practical tool to improve sexual health awareness in this group.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 343, "output_tokens": 111, "total_tokens": 454}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.5453e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_981", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: [\"Currently the choice of breast cancer therapy is based on prognostic factors. The proliferation marker Ki-67 is used increasingly to determine the method of therapy. The current study analyses the predictive value of Ki-67 in foreseeing breast cancer patients' responses to neoadjuvant chemotherapy.\", 'This study includes patients with invasive breast cancer treated between 2008 and 2013. The clinical response was assessed by correlating Ki-67 to histological examination, mammography, and ultrasonography findings.', 'The average Ki-67 value in our patients collectively (n = 77) is 34.9 \u00b1 24.6%. The average Ki-67 value is the highest with 37.4 \u00b1 24.0% in patients with a pCR. The Ki-67 values do not differ significantly among the 3 groups: pCR versus partial pathological response versus stable disease/progress (P = 0.896). However, Ki-67 values of patients with luminal, Her2 enriched, and basal-like cancers differed significantly from each other. Furthermore, within the group of luminal tumors Ki-67 values of patients with versus without pCR also differed significantly.']\n\nQuestion: Can ki-67 play a role in prediction of breast cancer patients' response to neoadjuvant chemotherapy?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that while overall Ki-67 values did not significantly differ among response groups (pCR, partial, stable/progressive disease), Ki-67 levels did differ significantly between molecular subtypes and within luminal tumors based on response. This suggests Ki-67 has some predictive value, particularly in specific subtypes like luminal cancers. Therefore, Ki-67 can play a role in predicting response, albeit in a more nuanced way.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 360, "output_tokens": 99, "total_tokens": 459}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.546e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_982", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To determine the therapeutic effect (alleviation of vascular type headache) and side effects of a slow intravenous metoclopramide infusion over 15 min compared with those effects of a bolus intravenous metoclopramide infusion over 2 min in the treatment of patients with recent onset vascular type headache.', \"All adults treated with metoclopramide for vascular type headache were eligible for entry into this clinical randomised double blinded trial. This study compared the effects of two different rates of intravenous infusion of metoclopramide over a period of 13 months at a university hospital emergency department. During the trial, side effects and headache scores were recorded at baseline (0 min), and then at 5, 15, 30 and 60 min. Repeated measures analysis of variance was used to compare the medication's efficacy and side effects.\", 'A total of 120 patients presenting to the emergency department met the inclusion criteria. Of these, 62 patients (51.7%) were given 10 mg metoclopramide as a slow intravenous infusion over 15 min (SIG group) and 58 patients (48.3%) were given 10 mg metoclopramide intravenous bolus infusion over 2 min (BIG group). 17 of the 58 patients in the BIG group (29.3%) and 4 of the 62 patients (6.5%) in the SIG group had akathisia (p = 0.001). There were no significant differences between the BIG and SIG groups in terms of mean headache scores (p = 0.34) and no adverse reactions in the study period. Metoclopramide successfully relieved the headache symptom(s) of patients in both the BIG and SIG groups.']\n\nQuestion: Intravenous administration of metoclopramide by 2 min bolus vs 15 min infusion: does it affect the improvement of headache while reducing the side effects?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no significant difference in headache relief between the 2-minute bolus and 15-minute infusion (p = 0.34), indicating similar effectiveness. However, the bolus group had a significantly higher incidence of akathisia (29.3% vs 6.5%, p = 0.001), meaning the slower infusion reduced side effects. Therefore, the slower infusion maintains efficacy while reducing adverse effects.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 494, "output_tokens": 96, "total_tokens": 590}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.4674e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_984", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To show the results of treating posterior uveal melanomas with 106Ru plaque beta-ray radiotherapy and to review and discuss the literature concerning the optimal apical dose prescription (100 vs. 160 Gy).', 'Forty-eight patients with uveal melanomas (median height 3.85 mm + 1 mm sclera) were treated with ruthenium plaques. The median apical dose was 120 Gy, the median scleral dose 546 Gy.', 'After 5.8 years of follow-up, the overall 5-year survival rate was 90%, the disease specific 5-year survival rate was 92% (3 patients alive with metastasis). Six percent received a second ruthenium application, 10% of the eyes had to be enucleated. Local control was achieved in 90% of the patients with conservative therapy alone. Central or paracentral tumors showed 50% of the pretherapeutic vision after 4 years, and 80% of the vision was preserved in those with peripheral tumors. The main side effects were mostly an uncomplicated retinopathy (30%); macular degeneration or scarring led to poor central vision in 30% of cases.']\n\nQuestion: Does escalation of the apical dose change treatment outcome in beta-radiation of posterior choroidal melanomas with 106Ru plaques?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study reports a median apical dose of 120 Gy, with good local control (90%) and survival rates, while noting ongoing debate in the literature about optimal dosing (100 vs. 160 Gy). However, no direct comparison within the study shows that higher apical doses significantly improve outcomes. Therefore, based on the provided data, dose escalation does not clearly alter treatment outcomes.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 375, "output_tokens": 90, "total_tokens": 465}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.5625e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_989", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['To assess whether Indigenous Australians age prematurely compared with other Australians, as implied by Australian Government aged care policy, which uses age 50 years and over for population-based planning for Indigenous people compared with 70 years for non-indigenous people.', 'Cross-sectional analysis of aged care assessment, hospital and health survey data comparing Indigenous and non-indigenous age-specific prevalence of health conditions. Analysis of life tables for Indigenous and non-indigenous populations comparing life expectancy at different ages.', 'At age 63 for women and age 65 for men, Indigenous people had the same life expectancy as non-indigenous people at age 70. There is no consistent pattern of a 20-year lead in age-specific prevalence of age-associated conditions for Indigenous compared with other Australians. There is high prevalence from middle-age onwards of some conditions, particularly diabetes (type unspecified), but there is little or no lead for others.']\n\nQuestion: Do Indigenous Australians age prematurely?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The data show that while Indigenous Australians have a lower life expectancy\u2014equivalent to non-Indigenous people at a younger age\u2014there is no consistent 20-year advance in the prevalence of age-associated conditions. This suggests that although health deterioration occurs earlier for some conditions like diabetes, it does not uniformly support the idea of premature aging across all health aspects. Therefore, the evidence does not consistently support the claim that Indigenous Australians age prematurely in a broad biological sense.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 267, "output_tokens": 99, "total_tokens": 366}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.8857e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_99", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['A short course of systemic corticosteroids is an important therapy in the treatment of pediatric asthma exacerbations. Although a 5-day course of oral prednisone or prednisolone has become the most commonly used regimen, dexamethasone has also been used for a shorter duration (1-2 days) with potential for improvement in compliance and palatability. We reviewed the literature to determine if there is sufficient evidence that dexamethasone can be used as an effective alternative in the treatment of pediatric asthma exacerbations in the inpatient setting.', 'A Medline search was conducted on the use of dexamethasone in the treatment of asthma exacerbations in children. The studies selected were clinical trials comparing the efficacy of dexamethasone with prednisone. Meta-analysis was performed examining physician revisitation rates and symptomatic return to baseline.', 'Six completed pediatric clinical trials met the inclusion criteria. All of the pediatric trials found that prednisone is not superior to dexamethasone in treating mild to moderate asthma exacerbations. Meta-analysis demonstrated homogeneity between the dexamethasone and prednisone groups when examining symptomatic return to baseline and unplanned physician revisits after the initial emergency department encounter. Some studies found potential additional benefits of dexamethasone, including improved compliance and less vomiting.']\n\nQuestion: Is dexamethasone an effective alternative to oral prednisone in the treatment of pediatric asthma exacerbations?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The reviewed clinical trials and meta-analysis show that dexamethasone is not inferior to prednisone in treating pediatric asthma exacerbations, with similar outcomes in symptom resolution and revisitation rates. Additionally, dexamethasone may offer advantages such as better compliance and fewer side effects like vomiting. Therefore, it is an effective alternative.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 373, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 446}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.3783e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_991", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['As part of the staging procedure in squamous cell carcinoma of the penis, we assessed the role of ultrasound examination, in particular its role in assessing the extent and the invasion into the corpora.', 'From 1988 until 1992, all patients referred for primary treatment underwent ultrasound assessment with a 7.5 MHz linear array small parts transducer as part of the clinical workup. All ultrasound images were reviewed by one radiologist, without knowledge of the clinical outcome and were compared with the results obtained at histopathologic examination.', 'In 16 patients the primary tumor and in 1 patient a recurrent cancer after primary therapy were examined. All tumors were identified as hypoechoic lesions. Ultrasound examination in the region of the glans was not able to differentiate between invasion of the subepithelial tissue and invasion into the corpus spongiosum, but absence or presence of invasion into the tunica albuginea of the corpus cavernosum was clearly demonstrated. Accurate measurement by ultrasound of maximum tumor thickness was seen in seven of sixteen examinations.']\n\nQuestion: Ultrasound in squamous cell carcinoma of the penis; a useful addition to clinical staging?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The ultrasound was able to clearly identify hypoechoic lesions and determine invasion into the tunica albuginea of the corpus cavernosum, which is critical for staging. However, it had limitations in differentiating early layers of invasion and accurately measured tumor thickness in only 7 out of 16 cases. Despite some limitations, its ability to detect key invasive features supports its value as a useful addition.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 315, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 402}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.1064999999999995e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_995", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['After 34 weeks gestation, summary measures of location for birthweight (e.g means and centiles) increase more slowly for Australian Aborigines than for whites. A similar pattern has been observed for blacks in the US. This study tests whether the reported pattern is due to differential misclassification of gestational age.', 'Simulation was used to measure the potential effect of differential misclassification of gestational age. Reported gestational age data were obtained from Queensland Perinatal Data Collection (QPDC). Estimates of the true distributions of gestational age were obtained by assuming various (plausible) types of misclassification and applying these to the reported distributions. Previous studies and data from the QPDC were used to help specify the birthweight distributions used in the simulations.', 'At full term, the parameters of the birthweight distributions were robust to gestational age misclassification. At preterm, the 10th centiles were robust to misclassification. In contrast, the 90th centiles were sensitive to even minor misclassification. Extreme types of misclassification were required to remove the divergence in median birthweights for Aborigines and whites.']\n\nQuestion: Does gestational age misclassification explain the difference in birthweights for Australian aborigines and whites?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that extreme types of misclassification were required to eliminate the divergence in median birthweights between Australian Aborigines and whites, and the parameters at full term were robust to misclassification. This suggests that typical levels of misclassification are insufficient to explain the observed differences. Therefore, gestational age misclassification does not adequately explain the difference in birthweights.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 330, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 408}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.123e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_997", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['We analyzed the pharmacokinetic-pharmacodynamic relationship of vancomycin to determine the drug exposure parameters that correlate with the efficacy and nephrotoxicity of vancomycin in patients with methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus pneumonia and evaluated the need to use peak concentration in therapeutic drug monitoring (TDM).', 'Serum drug concentrations of 31 hospitalized patients treated with vancomycin for methicillin-resistant S. aureus pneumonia were collected.', 'Significant differences in trough concentration (Cmin)/minimum inhibitory concentration (MIC) and area under the serum concentration-time curve (AUC0-24)/MIC were observed between the response and non-response groups. Significant differences in Cmin and AUC0-24 were observed between the nephrotoxicity and non-nephrotoxicity groups. Receiver operating characteristic curves revealed high predictive values of Cmin/MIC and AUC0-24/MIC for efficacy and of Cmin and AUC0-24 for safety of vancomycin.']\n\nQuestion: Is peak concentration needed in therapeutic drug monitoring of vancomycin?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context indicates that significant differences in efficacy and nephrotoxicity were associated with trough concentration (Cmin), Cmin/MIC, AUC0-24, and AUC0-24/MIC, but not with peak concentration. This suggests that peak concentration does not play a critical role in predicting outcomes, making it unnecessary for routine therapeutic drug monitoring. Therefore, the evidence supports that peak concentration is not needed.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 355, "output_tokens": 111, "total_tokens": 466}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 3.6305e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_998", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['This investigation assesses the effect of platelet-rich plasma (PRP) gel on postoperative pain, swelling, and trismus as well as healing and bone regeneration potential on mandibular third molar extraction sockets.', 'A prospective randomized comparative clinical study was undertaken over a 2-year period. Patients requiring surgical extraction of a single impacted third molar and who fell within the inclusion criteria and indicated willingness to return for recall visits were recruited. The predictor variable was application of PRP gel to the socket of the third molar in the test group, whereas the control group had no PRP. The outcome variables were pain, swelling, and maximum mouth opening, which were measured using a 10-point visual analog scale, tape, and millimeter caliper, respectively. Socket healing was assessed radiographically by allocating scores for lamina dura, overall density, and trabecular pattern. Quantitative data were presented as mean. Mann-Whitney test was used to compare means between groups for continuous variables, whereas Fischer exact test was used for categorical variables. Statistical significance was inferred at P<.05.', 'Sixty patients aged 19 to 35 years (mean: 24.7 \u00b1 3.6 years) were divided into both test and control groups of 30 patients each. The mean postoperative pain score (visual analog scale) was lower for the PRP group at all time points and this was statistically significant (P<.05). Although the figures for swelling and interincisal mouth opening were lower in the test group, this difference was not statistically significant. Similarly, the scores for lamina dura, trabecular pattern, and bone density were better among patients in the PRP group. This difference was also not statistically significant.']\n\nQuestion: Can autologous platelet-rich plasma gel enhance healing after surgical extraction of mandibular third molars?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found that PRP gel significantly reduced postoperative pain, which suggests a beneficial effect on patient comfort. Although improvements in swelling, trismus, and radiographic bone healing were observed in the PRP group, these differences were not statistically significant. Therefore, while there are some positive trends, the evidence is not strong enough to conclusively confirm enhanced healing.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 466, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 545}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 4.0986e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "PubMedQA_999", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: ['The reduced use of sugars-containing (SC) liquid medicines has increased the use of other dose forms, potentially resulting in more widespread dental effects, including tooth wear. The aim of this study was to assess the erosive potential of 97 paediatric medicines in vitro.', 'The study took the form of in vitro measurement of endogenous pH and titratable acidity (mmol). Endogenous pH was measured using a pH meter, followed by titration to pH 7.0 with 0.1-M NaOH.', 'Overall, 55 (57%) formulations had an endogenous pH of<5.5. The mean (+/- SD) endogenous pH and titratable acidity for 41 SC formulations were 5.26 +/- 1.30 and 0.139 +/- 0.133 mmol, respectively; for 56 sugars-free (SF) formulations, these figures were 5.73 +/- 1.53 and 0.413 +/- 1.50 mmol (P>0.05). Compared with their SC bioequivalents, eight SF medicines showed no significant differences for pH or titratable acidity, while 15 higher-strength medicines showed lower pH (P = 0.035) and greater titratable acidity (P = 0.016) than their lower-strength equivalents. Chewable and dispersible tablets (P<0.001), gastrointestinal medicines (P = 0.002) and antibiotics (P = 0.007) were significant predictors of higher pH. In contrast, effervescent tablets (P<0.001), and nutrition and blood preparations (P = 0.021) were significant predictors of higher titratable acidity.']\n\nQuestion: Are sugars-free medicines more erosive than sugars-containing medicines?\n\nOptions: \nA. yes\nB. no\nC. maybe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The study found no statistically significant difference in endogenous pH or titratable acidity between sugars-containing (SC) and sugars-free (SF) formulations (P>0.05). Therefore, the evidence provided does not support the conclusion that sugars-free medicines are more erosive than their sugars-containing counterparts.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 466, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 536}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:05:12.737049+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0002215, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1047", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A variety of this material titles a book by Michael Beloff in which it designates universities like Essex, York, and East Anglia.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The universities named in the query (Essex, York, East Anglia, etc.) are the classic examples of Britain's \"plate-glass universities,\" a term popularized by Michael Beloff's 1968 book of the same title. Plate glass is simply one well-known variety of the material glass, which therefore satisfies every element of the clue.  \n\n\\boxed{glass (plate glass)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 206, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 282}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004475, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1089", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One artist from this country depicted a musician squeezing lemon juice into the eye of a supposedly blind fellow beggar in  The Musician's Brawl  and made several candlelit scenes of Mary Magdalene.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The artist described is Georges de La Tour, a prominent painter from France known for his mastery of chiaroscuro and candlelit religious scenes. The painting *The Musician's Brawl* (also known as *The Hurdy-Gurdy Player's Brawl*) is one of his notable genre works.\n\n\\boxed{France}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 161}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:27.470816+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00012525, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1093", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This genre titles many Sterling Brown poems, such as one about Memphis, one about a riverbank, and one about rent day.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The genre that titles many Sterling Brown poems, including those about Memphis, a riverbank, and rent day, is \"blues.\" Sterling Brown often used the blues form to capture African American life and struggles in his poetry. \n\n\\boxed{blues}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 137}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1235e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1177", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A song in this genre that closes the album  Light as a Feather  opens with the pianist playing the melody of the adagio from the  Concierto de Aranjuez   \n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The album *Light as a Feather* (1973) is a landmark recording by Chick Corea\u2019s Return to Forever. Its closing track, \u201cSpain,\u201d opens with the pianist quoting the famous Adagio theme from Rodrigo\u2019s *Concierto de Aranjuez*; the piece is universally classified as jazz fusion (sometimes called \u201cjazz-rock\u201d or \u201cLatin fusion\u201d).  \n\nThus the genre referenced by \u201cthis genre\u201d is jazz fusion.\n\n\\boxed{jazz fusion (Spain)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 216, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 311}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005075, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1193", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Futurist Gino Severini added Cubist sequins to his depiction of a \"blue\" person in this profession, one of over 100 paintings he made of them.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Gino Severini was fascinated by dancers and created over 100 paintings of them, often blending Futurist and Cubist styles. His work \"The Blue Dancer\" exemplifies this, featuring a dancer adorned with Cubist-inspired sequins and dynamic movement. The profession depicted is a dancer.\n\n\\boxed{dancer}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 166}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3758e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1199", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The winner of a competition to design one of these buildings in Guangzhou ( gwong-joh)  \n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question refers to the Guangzhou Opera House, a prominent architectural landmark. The winning design was created by Zaha Hadid in a competition to design the building. \n\n\\boxed{Zaha Hadid}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 80, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 123}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 9.980000000000001e-06, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1200", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This instrument plays a lullaby-like melody in E major after taking it over from the piano in the first movement of an E minor Brahms chamber piece whose finale's main theme is based on Contrapunctus 13 from  The Art of the Fugue .\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The chamber piece described is Johannes Brahms's Piano Quartet No. 1 in G minor, Op. 25, which features a finale based on Bach's *The Art of the Fugue*. In the first movement, the cello takes over the lyrical second theme in E major from the piano. Therefore, the instrument is the cello.\n\n\\boxed{Cello}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 188}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:27.494104+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0001445, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1212", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Jean Dauberval (\"doe\"-ber-vahl) was known for rehabilitating the \"false\" examples of these techniques, which were reversals of the \"true\" or \"noble\" ones and generally thought to be only suitable for depictions of drunks and sailors.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Jean Dauberval was an 18th-century ballet master best known for elevating character-driven works such as La Fille mal gard\u00e9e. In the period\u2019s hierarchy of dance, \u201cnoble\u201d (danse s\u00e9rieuse) technique reserved certain aerial steps for heroic or aristocratic roles, while their reversed or inverted counterparts were dismissed as \u201cfalse\u201d or grotesque and were therefore confined to comic sailors, drunkards, and peasants. Dauberval\u2019s realistic ballets rehabilitated those reversed steps\u2014cabrioles\u2014thereby legitimizing them for the general repertory.\n\n\\boxed{cabrioles (false/grotesque)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 236, "output_tokens": 125, "total_tokens": 361}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0006075, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1233", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Note to players: artist and type of work required. In one of these paintings, the word \"ADONAI\" is inscribed on St. George's breastplate as he introduces the title jowly canon, whose salvation is signi ed by armrest sculptures of Cain killing Abel and Samson wrenching a lion's jaws apart.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The described scene matches the *Madonna of Canon van der Paele* (c. 1434\u201336), in which St. George presents Joris van der Paele to the enthroned Virgin; \u201cADONAI\u201d appears on the saint\u2019s breastplate and the throne armrests carry the Cain/Abel and Samson/lion reliefs. Because the prompt refers to \u201cone of these paintings\u201d and requires both artist and genre, the common identification is the set of enthroned or donor Madonnas painted by Jan van Eyck (including the Rolin, Lucca, and Dresden versions).  \n\nThus the expected answer is van Eyck Madonnas (or \u201cMadonnas by Jan van Eyck\u201d).\n\n\\boxed{van Eyck Madonnas (w/ donors)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 308, "output_tokens": 707, "total_tokens": 1015}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:35.035213+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0021525, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1242", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This university commissioned Helmut Jahn to design a dormitory that is clad in corrugated steel and divided into six segments.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The university that commissioned Helmut Jahn to design a dormitory clad in corrugated steel and divided into six segments is the Illinois Institute of Technology.\n\nThis dormitory, known as the State Street Village, was designed to accommodate students while reflecting Jahn's modern architectural style.\n\n\\boxed{Illinois Institute of Technology}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 151}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2635e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1276", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Note to players: composer and type of piece required. The key of an unpublished seventh piece from a set of these pieces can be deduced from the pattern of expanding intervals in alternating directions exhibited by the first six, which have the tonics B- lat, C, A, D, G, and E.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given sequence of tonics (B\u266d\u2013C\u2013A\u2013D\u2013G\u2013E) exhibits alternating-direction diatonic intervals whose sizes expand successively (major 2nd up, minor 3rd down, perfect 4th up, perfect 5th down, major 6th up, major 7th down). Continuation of the same rule places the missing seventh tonic on F.  \n\nThe only well-known set whose first six members match these keys exactly, and for which an F-tonic seventh member is known to have remained unpublished, is Bart\u00f3k\u2019s Bagatelles, Op. 6.  \n\nThus the required identification is \u201cBart\u00f3k bagatelles.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{Bart\u00f3k bagatelles (Op.6)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 242, "output_tokens": 151, "total_tokens": 393}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00068, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1301", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a set of five variations on this painting, the words \"EAT,\" \"DIE,\" \"HUG,\" and \"ERR\" encircle its central image superimposed on a red star.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a set of artistic variations featuring the specific four-letter words EAT/DIE/HUG/ERR arranged around a central motif that is itself overlaid on a red star. Those words are a deliberate play on the four-letter motif of Robert Indiana\u2019s iconic 1960s \u201cLOVE\u201d design; Indiana himself produced exactly such a suite of graphic variations in the 1990s. Consequently the original painting referenced is Indiana\u2019s LOVE.\n\n\\boxed{LOVE (R. Indiana)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 219, "output_tokens": 98, "total_tokens": 317}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00051875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_131", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Gender scholars like Judith Tick cite this composer's quip that Impressionism was \"easy music for the sissies\" and obsessive opposition to \"feminine\" music as evidence of misogyny.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The composer referenced here is Charles Ives, whose private writings (as analyzed in Judith Tick's scholarship on American modernism) repeatedly deploy gendered insults to dismiss European Impressionists like Debussy as effeminate or \"sissy\" while championing a hyper-masculine ideal of music. This rhetoric is now routinely cited in gender studies of early-20th-century composition as textbook evidence of misogyny. No other major composer matches both the specific quip and the scholarly citations.\n\n\\boxed{Charles Ives}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 282, "output_tokens": 419, "total_tokens": 701}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:32.749749+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0014, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1322", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This painting was originally displayed facing a depiction of a female model in it costumed as a male matador.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question describes a pair of 1863 paintings by \u00c9douard Manet that shared the same model (Victorine Meurent) and were deliberately hung opposite each other in the Salon des Refus\u00e9s. One work depicts the model dressed as a male bullfighter (\u201cMademoiselle V\u2026 in the Costume of an Espada\u201d); the other is therefore the work referred to by the pronoun \u201cit.\u201d That work is Manet\u2019s Le D\u00e9jeuner sur l\u2019herbe.\n\n\\boxed{Le D\u00e9jeuner sur l'herbe (Manet)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 202, "output_tokens": 108, "total_tokens": 310}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005225, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1327", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Recent performances of this opera have been in luenced by the  ndings of Michael Kaye and Jean-Christophe Keck, who intend their critical edition of it to supersede earlier editions by Choudens and Fritz Oeser.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue refers to an opera with a notoriously complex textual history, owing to the composer's death before completion (and thus multiple competing versions). This matches Offenbach's Les contes d'Hoffmann, whose principal modern critical editions were prepared first by Fritz Oeser and later superseded by the joint work of Michael Kaye and Jean-Christophe Keck. No other opera in the standard repertory fits the named scholars and publishers.\n\n\\boxed{Les contes d'Hoffmann (Tales of Hoffmann)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 226, "output_tokens": 102, "total_tokens": 328}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1343", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Fritz Kreisler convinced his own concert manager to arrange this musician's wildly successful debut 1928 American tour.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Fritz Kreisler, the noted violinist and composer, used his influence with concert manager Arthur Judson to secure an American engagement for a promising young pianist whose European reputation was already rising. That pianist, Vladimir Horowitz, made his U.S. debut with the New York Philharmonic on 12 January 1928, performing Tchaikovsky\u2019s First Piano Concerto to overwhelming acclaim and launching a trans-Atlantic career. No other major musician\u2019s 1928 arrival matches the documented involvement of Kreisler and Judson.\n\n\\boxed{Vladimir Horowitz}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 202, "output_tokens": 109, "total_tokens": 311}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000525, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1348", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The street grid of a campus in this state is o fset from the grid of the surrounding city by 12.25 degrees, inspiring the design of a building which alternates between following the two grids.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The campus described is the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT) in Cambridge, and the building designed to alternate between the two grids is the Ray and Maria Stata Center. The state in which this campus is located is Massachusetts.\n\n\\boxed{Massachusetts}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 147}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:25.653980+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0001005, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1365", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An advocate of this style wrote that buildings should have no unnecessary features and that ornament should only enrich a building's construction in the two \"great rules\" of design he put forth in the book Contrasts.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes two \"great rules\" of design from Augustus Pugin's 1836 manifesto *Contrasts*, which explicitly championed a return to medieval forms over neoclassicism. Those rules are the foundational credo of the Gothic Revival (also called Pointed or Victorian Gothic) style that Pugin, Ruskin, and the Ecclesiological Society promoted in the mid-19th century. Hence the style referenced is Gothic Revival.\n\n\\boxed{Gothic Revival (Pugin)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 221, "output_tokens": 94, "total_tokens": 315}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00051125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1373", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Note to players: artist and type of work required. Francis Bacon painted eight studies based on a destroyed example of one of these paintings, which depict a haunted zombie- gure with a shriveled shadow.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue requires identifying both the artist and the specific works referenced. Francis Bacon repeatedly cited Diego Vel\u00e1zquez\u2019s 1650 Portrait of Pope Innocent X as his primary source, producing dozens of variations (including a well-known series of eight) that transform the seated pontiff into a screaming, distorted \u201czombie\u201d figure whose shadow appears withered or collapsed. The phrase \u201cdestroyed example\u201d alludes to the fact that one of Vel\u00e1zquez\u2019s autograph versions was lost, confirming that the underlying paintings are Vel\u00e1zquez\u2019s portraits of Innocent X.\n\nThus the required answer is Vel\u00e1zquez\u2019s Portrait of Pope Innocent X (or the series of portraits of Innocent X).\n\n\\boxed{Vel\u00e1zquez's Port. of Pope Innocent X\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 222, "output_tokens": 144, "total_tokens": 366}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0006375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1377", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Note to players: composer and type of piece required. In one of these pieces, a pianissimo Un poco meno mosso section begins with the right hand playing tenuto block chords over the le t hand's rapid arpeggiated D dominant seventh chord.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes a specific musical passage (tempo indication, dynamics, and exact texture/voicing of a D7 arpeggio) that occurs inside one member of a larger set. Because the prompt explicitly requires both composer and genre, the set in question must be a well-known, internally varied collection of short solo-piano works by a single composer. Among the standard Romantic and late-Romantic corpora that match these constraints, only Chopin\u2019s nocturnes routinely employ the indicated pianissimo \u201cUn poco meno mosso\u201d middle section with right-hand block chords above a rapid left-hand dominant-seventh arpeggio.\n\nThus the required answer is Chopin\u2019s nocturnes.\n\n\\boxed{Chopin's nocturnes}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 231, "output_tokens": 140, "total_tokens": 371}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00063875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1404", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Scholars in this  eld include Anton Kaes, whose historicist analyses of the in luence of collective memory on German culture include From Hitler to Heimat, which overlaps in subject matter with the major works of Thomas Elsaesser (ELL-zess-er).\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given clue text is a (slightly corrupted) quizbowl-style tossup lead-in. It directly identifies two prominent academics whose work centers on German cinema, collective memory, and the legacy of the Nazi era. The field encompassing their scholarship is therefore film studies (or cinema studies).\n\n\\boxed{film studies}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 231, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 293}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00044375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1408", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The upper right corner of a painting depicting this scene contains a sculpture of two hands, symbolizing the city of Antwerp, near an orange column containing guild symbols such as a bell and an X flanked by two vertical lines on each side.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The description references a painting whose upper-right details explicitly encode the city of Antwerp (the severed-hand emblem) together with the identifying insignia of the local harquebusiers\u2019 guild (the crossbow-like \u201cX\u201d and bell). Those civic and corporate markers appear only on Rubens\u2019s Antwerp altarpiece of the Deposition, confirming both the subject and the artist.  \n\nThus the scene depicted is the Descent from the Cross.\n\n\\boxed{Descent from the Cross (Rubens)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 227, "output_tokens": 96, "total_tokens": 323}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00052375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1427", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Grant Allen essay \"Seven-Year Sleepers\" describes a snail that miraculously came back to life in this building.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Grant Allen essay \"Seven-Year Sleepers\" describes a snail that miraculously came back to life in the British Museum. This incident occurred when a snail, thought to be dead, awoke after being dormant for several years while on display. The correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{British Museum}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 146}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2163999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1445", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: During the 16th century, this city founded four conservatories training young boys that became the model for public music schools throughout Europe.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The city referred to is Naples, which in the 16th century established four conservatories\u2014La Piet\u00e0, Santa Maria di Loreto, Sant'Onofrio, and the Conservatorio dei Poveri di Ges\u00f9 Cristo\u2014that trained young boys in music and became influential models for public music education in Europe. These institutions evolved into leading centers for musical training and helped shape the development of Western classical music. \n\n\\boxed{Naples}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 94, "total_tokens": 181}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5577e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1456", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The words \"Go and set everything aflame\" inspired a painting of this type, a fresco in which Jesus shoots a beam of light at the title saint, which then splits into four rays directed at four continents.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted phrase is a well-known exhortation of St. Ignatius Loyola to his companion St. Francis Xavier. It directly inspired the iconography of the large nave fresco painted by Andrea Pozzo (or, in some attributions, Baciccio) in the Church of the Ges\u00f9, Rome: Christ dispatches a ray of divine light that strikes Xavier and then radiates outward to the four known continents, an image that literally enacts Xavier\u2019s elevation to heavenly glory. Such glorification scenes are conventionally classified in art history as an \u201capotheosis.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{apotheosis (of St. Fr. Xavier)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 223, "output_tokens": 125, "total_tokens": 348}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00059125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1490", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Theodor Adorno was wounded by Walter Benjamin's negative opinion of his fragmentary musical composition in this genre that was inspired by The Adventures of Tom Sawyer.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue refers to a specific biographical incident between Adorno (a trained composer as well as philosopher) and Benjamin. Adorno\u2019s unfinished setting of episodes from *The Adventures of Tom Sawyer* is the 1932\u201333 work *Der Schatz des Indianer-Joe*, explicitly labeled a Singspiel. Benjamin\u2019s dismissive remarks about the piece are documented in their correspondence and wounded Adorno, confirming the genre requested by the question.\n\n\\boxed{Singspiel}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 208, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 297}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004825, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1531", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Graham Bader claimed that a painting titled for an animal of this type shows an animal of another kind engaged in a \"narcissistic circuit\" and staring at the artist's initials in a manner reminiscent of Caravaggio's Narcissus.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The sentence describes an artwork whose title references one animal but whose depicted subject is another animal gazing at the artist's monogram/initials in a reflective surface. This setup is likened to the self-regarding pose in Caravaggio's Narcissus, producing what the cited critic terms a \"narcissistic circuit.\" The type named in the title is therefore the required answer.\n\n\\boxed{swans}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 227, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 306}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00048125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_154", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A Robert Rauschenberg combine named after one of these people is made of a pillow under a box, which is itself under a chicken.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Rauschenberg work in question is the 1955 combine titled Odalisk. Its construction consists of a pillow at the base, a wooden box covered in pictures and fabric in the middle, and a taxidermy rooster (colloquially a chicken) mounted on top. The title is a deliberate pun on \u201codalisque,\u201d the French term for the female harem attendants or concubines who were a staple subject of Orientalist painting; hence \u201cthese people\u201d are odalisques.\n\n\\boxed{odalisques}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 208, "output_tokens": 110, "total_tokens": 318}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000535, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1548", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The writing of this text is depicted in the right panel of an altarpiece housed in a hospital in Bruges, in which its author looks at an inset circle showing a red-cloaked man.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The description matches a right-hand panel from Hans Memling\u2019s altarpiece of the Adoration of the Magi (c. 1479), now in the Old St. John\u2019s Hospital, Bruges. In that panel the canon and chronicler Thomas \u00e0 Kempis is shown composing his devotional treatise while gazing at a visionary tondo of a red-robed figure. Hence the text whose composition is depicted is The Imitation of Christ.\n\n\\boxed{The Imitation of Christ}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 221, "output_tokens": 96, "total_tokens": 317}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00051625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1606", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: French artist ORLAN (or-LAHN) created an edgy, nearly identical version of this painting, renamed so that the last word of its title is \"war.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a well-known work by the French artist ORLAN: an explicit photographic self-portrait that directly appropriates the composition, framing, and title structure of Gustave Courbet\u2019s 1866 canvas but changes the final word to produce the new title \u201cThe Origin of War.\u201d  \nBecause the question asks for the source painting that ORLAN re-created, the answer is therefore Courbet\u2019s original, universally identified as \u201cThe Origin of the World.\u201d  \nNo other canvas satisfies both the visual and titular criteria given.\n\n\\boxed{The Origin of the World (Courbet)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 214, "output_tokens": 115, "total_tokens": 329}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000555, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1636", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This composer's supposed authorship of a serenata titled \"Andromeda Liberata\" caused a feud between Olivier Foures (oh-LIV-yay foo-RAY) and Michael Talbot, the latter of whom is considered the preeminent scholar of this composer.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The composer in question is Antonio Vivaldi. The supposed authorship of the serenata \"Andromeda Liberata\" sparked a scholarly debate between Olivier Foures, who supported its attribution to Vivaldi, and Michael Talbot, a leading Vivaldi expert, who disputed the claim. The disagreement highlighted tensions over authentication methods in musicology.\n\n\\boxed{Antonio Vivaldi}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 196}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6265e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1661", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A painting titled a\u1978er this city contains a low barrier being peered over by a crowd that includes two plump children wearing baseball caps, a reference to the Katzenjammer Kids, and a parody of Dick Tracy, a comic that debuted in one of this city's newspapers.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The painting described is Grant Wood's *American Gothic*, but the correct painting matching all these details\u2014especially the comic references and crowd scene\u2014is *Perry's America* by Roger Rabbit artist Roger Langridge, though the intended answer points to a Mad magazine parody. However, the city referenced is Chicago, home of *The Chicago Tribune*, where Dick Tracy debuted. \n\nThe painting alluded to is likely a *Mad* magazine cover parodying American culture, tied to Chicago.\n\n\\boxed{Chicago}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 118, "output_tokens": 101, "total_tokens": 219}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.8478e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1686", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A concerto for this instrument contains a \"war\" between the alternating keys of F major and E major that is exacerbated by a prominent snare-drum part and that supposedly re ected the bipolar nature of its dedicatee, Aage Oxenvad (AH-geh OX-en-vahd).\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The concerto described is Carl Nielsen's Clarinet Concerto, which features a tonal conflict between F major and E major, symbolizing the turbulent personality of its dedicatee, Aage Oxenvad. The prominent snare drum part adds to the sense of tension and \"war\" throughout the piece. The instrument is the clarinet.\n\n\\boxed{clarinet}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 121, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 197}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6190999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1702", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The inspiration for one song on this album was a walk to a radio station with a man named \"June Eight,\" during which the composer heard music arranged via the aksak system.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question describes an album containing at least one track whose rhythmic organization derives from the aksak (additive, \u201climping\u201d) meters characteristic of Balkan/Turkish folk music. The canonical jazz album that explicitly incorporates such meters\u2014most famously the 9/8 \u201cBlue Rondo \u00e0 la Turk\u201d\u2014is Dave Brubeck\u2019s *Time Out*. Brubeck encountered these rhythms while touring Turkey; the anecdote of the walk with the informant nicknamed \u201cJune Eight\u201d is simply a localized retelling of that same field encounter.\n\nThus the album referenced is *Time Out*.\n\n\\boxed{Time Out (Dave Brubeck Qt.)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 216, "output_tokens": 128, "total_tokens": 344}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00059, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1747", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An unresolved C-sharp dominant 7 chord, which ends the  rst song of one of this composer's cycles, has an ambiguous A-major or F-sharp-minor tonality.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes the opening song (\"Im wundersch\u00f6nen Monat Mai\") of Schumann\u2019s cycle *Dichterliebe*. That song hovers between A major and F\u266f minor and concludes on an unresolved C\u266f\u2077 sonority whose expected resolution is never supplied. No other well-known Lieder composer employs precisely this harmonic device at the start of a cycle.\n\n\\boxed{R. Schumann (Dichterliebe)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 278, "output_tokens": 429, "total_tokens": 707}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:33.739554+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00142, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_176", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Like its composer's opera about Elizabeth of England, this opera's overture is directly taken from that of Aureliano in Palmira.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question refers to an opera by Rossini (the composer of both Aureliano in Palmira and Elisabetta, regina d'Inghilterra) whose overture reuses the same preexisting material. Rossini famously recycled overtures; the sinfonia originally written for Aureliano in Palmira (1813) was next attached to Elisabetta (1815) and then reused once more for the premiere of Il barbiere di Siviglia (1816). Thus the opera described is Il barbiere di Siviglia.\n\n\\boxed{Il barbiere di Siviglia (Rossini)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 208, "output_tokens": 123, "total_tokens": 331}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005675, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1765", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Angela Hewitt's \"world tour\" in 2007 and 2008 was primarily devoted to complete performances of this work.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Angela Hewitt's world tour in 2007 and 2008 was centered around performing Johann Sebastian Bach's *The Well-Tempered Clavier* in its entirety across numerous cities. This ambitious tour included both books of the work, showcasing her deep interpretation and mastery of Bach's preludes and fugues. The tour was widely acclaimed and later released as a recording.\n\n\\boxed{The Well-Tempered Clavier}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 89, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 181}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5519e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1773", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Drawings by Jean-E\u0301tienne Dominique Esquirol (ES-kee-\"roll\") may have inspired a series done by this artist aeer he returned from a stay in England.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes an artist whose post-England work was likely influenced by Esquirol\u2019s psychiatric drawings of mental patients. Th\u00e9odore G\u00e9ricault returned from England in 1821 and soon produced his well-known series of ten portraits of the insane (c. 1822), which scholars have linked to Esquirol\u2019s case studies and illustrations. No other major artist matches both the England sojourn and the Esquirol-inspired \u201cinsane\u201d series.\n\n\\boxed{Th\u00e9odore G\u00e9ricault}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 217, "output_tokens": 101, "total_tokens": 318}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00052375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1791", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A magazine ad of a man in this profession before a blue sky was manipulated by Richard Prince to become the most expensive retouched photograph ever sold at auction.  \n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The photograph in question is part of Richard Prince's \"Untitled (Cowboy)\" series, which features a cowboy from a Marlboro cigarette ad. The original image depicted a cowboy, a symbol of the American West, often associated with the profession of a rancher or cowboy. This retouched photograph became the most expensive photograph ever sold at auction.\n\n\\boxed{cowboy}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 166}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3960999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1813", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Mabel Dodge ran a salon in this state described as a \"garden of Allah\".\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Mabel Dodge ran a famous salon in New Mexico, which she described as a \"garden of Allah\" due to its spiritual and artistic atmosphere. The salon was located in Taos and became a cultural hub for artists, writers, and intellectuals in the early 20th century. \n\n\\boxed{New Mexico}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 77, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 142}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1966999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1832", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A\u774cter moving to America, this man mentored Romare (roh-MAH-ray)\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The man who mentored Romare Bearden after moving to America was the German-born artist George Grosz. Bearden studied under Grosz at the Art Students League of New York during the 1930s.\n\n\\boxed{George Grosz}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 76, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 129}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:25.154647+00:00"}, "cost": 9.85e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1860", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Janis Joplin's version of this standard, which she recorded with Big Brother and the Holding Company and played at Woodstock, added 41 repetitions of the word \"no\" near its end.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The song in question is \"Piece of My Heart,\" originally written by Jerry Ragovoy and Bert Berns and first recorded by Erma Franklin. Janis Joplin's powerful rendition with Big Brother and the Holding Company famously included 41 repetitions of the word \"no\" during the climactic ending. This performance became iconic, especially after her electrifying appearance at Woodstock.\n\n\\boxed{Piece of My Heart}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 187}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5771e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_1898", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: n the fourth and final movement of an F minor piece composed for this ensemble, a fugue climaxes on an unresolved C major chord followed by a bar of silence, then a return of the piece's opening theme.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given clue describes the finale of Beethoven's String Quartet No. 11 in F minor, Op. 95 (\"Serioso\"). Its closing movement contains a fugato whose climax is an unresolved fortissimo C-major chord, a full bar of silence, and then a hushed return of the opening theme (now in the major mode). This identifies the ensemble as the string quartet.\n\n\\boxed{string quartet (Beet. Op.95)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 224, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 313}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005025, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_192", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A collaboration with Jean Cocteau created a work in this art form that reproduced the classic optical illusion of a vase of roses between two kissing faces.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question describes a specific visual work reproducing Rubin's classic figure-ground illusion (a central vase of roses formed by the negative space between two kissing profiles). This matches the definition and techniques of anamorphosis, a category of perspective-based optical art that distorts or hides images so they resolve only from a particular viewpoint or via reflection. Historical records confirm a collaboration between Jean Cocteau and the anamorphic artist J. F. Niceron (or a later practitioner working in the same tradition) that produced exactly such a piece.\n\nThus the art form referenced is anamorphosis.\n\n\\boxed{anamorphosis}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 210, "output_tokens": 123, "total_tokens": 333}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00057, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_209", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A building of this type alternates between using rectangular and hemispherical balconies, and features columns shaped like stacks of bobbins to represent the textile manufacturer who commissioned it.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The description matches a specific exemplar of Catalan Modernisme (the local variant of the international Art Nouveau movement): Casa Mil\u00e0 (\u201cLa Pedrera\u201d) by Antoni Gaud\u00ed, commissioned by the textile magnate Pere Mil\u00e0. Its undulating fa\u00e7ade alternates rectangular and curved balconies, while the interior service court contains the celebrated \u201cbobbin\u201d columns that allude to the client\u2019s industry. Hence the building type referenced is Art Nouveau (or Modernista) architecture.\n\n\\boxed{Art Nouveau (bldg./arch.)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 214, "output_tokens": 104, "total_tokens": 318}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005275, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_218", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the second section of a work titled for this event, the cello re-introduces a fugue subject while the saxophone plays a glissando, which it also plays during the overture over a steady drumbeat.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query is a quizbowl-style tossup clue whose answer is an event, not a musical work. The work in question is John Zorn\u2019s 1992 album *Kristallnacht*, whose movements include an overture (steady drumbeat plus saxophone glissando) and a second section that reintroduces a fugue subject on cello while the saxophone again slides. Because the album is explicitly titled for the 1938 pogrom, the event being asked for is Kristallnacht.\n\n\\boxed{Kristallnacht}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 225, "output_tokens": 108, "total_tokens": 333}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00055125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_268", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Clinton, Tennessee, this architect designed an elevated wooden barn dedicated to Langston Hughes.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a distinctive structure (an elevated wooden barn serving as a library) located at the Alex Haley Farm in Clinton, Tennessee, and dedicated to the poet Langston Hughes. This building is a well-documented adaptive reuse project by Maya Lin, who converted and elevated an existing 1860s barn into the Langston Hughes Library (completed 1999). No other architect matches this specific combination of site, program, and design approach.\n\n\\boxed{Maya Lin}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 198, "output_tokens": 94, "total_tokens": 292}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004825, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_282", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Some of this painting's symbols appear in a comic strip-like sheet of prints titled for the \"Dream and Lie\" of a military leader.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The painting being referred to is Pablo Picasso's *Guernica*, which contains symbols also found in his series titled *Dream and Lie of Franco*. This series of prints features surreal and grotesque imagery involving General Francisco Franco, the Spanish military leader. The symbols from the prints were incorporated into *Guernica* as a protest against the Spanish Civil War.\n\n\\boxed{Guernica}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 166}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4077e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_29", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Several of these objects are connected in a circle and suspended above the ground in Right of Return, one of many sculptures by Marc Andre Robinson made of them.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The objects used in Marc Andre Robinson's sculpture *Right of Return* are wooden chairs. The artist frequently utilizes discarded chairs to explore themes of history, community, and displacement.\n\n\\boxed{chairs}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 127}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:25.583809+00:00"}, "cost": 8.425e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_303", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This artist responded to his friend Anthon van Rappard declaring his work as \"utterly weak\" by angrily writing \"I am always doing what I can't do yet in order to learn how to do it.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The artist who responded to Anthon van Rappard's criticism with that quote is Vincent van Gogh. He frequently corresponded with van Rappard and defended his artistic efforts despite criticism. His quote reflects his determination to grow through challenges.\n\n\\boxed{Vincent van Gogh}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 162}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3213e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_420", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A painting by Magritte depicts one member of this profession smoking his own nose; that work is titled after that profession's \u2018lamp.'\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The painting by Ren\u00e9 Magritte titled *The Son of Man* features a man in a bowler hat with a green apple obscuring his face, but the work referencing smoking a nose is *The Lovers*, though that does not fit. The correct painting is *The Art of Conversation*, but more relevant is *The Fair Captive*, where a man in a suit smokes a pipe while his face is obscured. However, the most famous work matching the description \u2014 a man smoking his own nose \u2014 is actually *The Empire of Light*, but the key clue is the title referencing a profession\u2019s \"lamp.\" That painting is *The Lamp of Diogenes*, referencing the philosopher Diogenes, a Cynic who carried a lamp in daylight searching for an honest man. The profession is philosopher, but the most common answer associated with Magritte\u2019s surreal imagery and the lamp is **fireman**, though that is incorrect. The correct and most common answer to this riddle, based on Magritte\u2019s *The Lamp of Diogenes* and the absurd image of a man smoking his nose, is **philosopher**.\n\n\\boxed{philosopher}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 86, "output_tokens": 237, "total_tokens": 323}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.9806000000000006e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_449", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An essay by Lorraine O'Grady contrasts the \"oppositional\" and \"confrontational\" gazes of the figures in this painting.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question references an essay by Lorraine O'Grady that discusses the \"oppositional\" and \"confrontational\" gazes in a painting, which is most commonly associated with \u00c9douard Manet\u2019s *Olympia*. O'Grady\u2019s analysis focuses on the power dynamics in the painting, particularly the way the Black maid\u2019s gaze challenges the viewer and the white Olympia\u2019s passive yet defiant look. The painting most frequently discussed in this context is *Olympia*.\n\n\\boxed{Olympia}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 109, "total_tokens": 199}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.729e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_47", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A painting set in this state replaces the subjects of Gustave Courbet's The Meeting with its artist, Peter Blake, and two of his colleagues.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The painting described is *Self-Portrait with Richard Hamilton and David Hockney*, which is set in the state of **California**. Peter Blake created this work as a homage to Gustave Courbet's *The Meeting* (also known as *Bonjour, Monsieur Courbet*), replacing the original figures with himself and his fellow pop artists.\n\n\\boxed{California}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 83, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 157}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:26.275241+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00013175, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_472", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One artist who primarily worked in this city painted the four evangelists at the corners of a clock face in this city's cathedral, along with a fresco commemorating the English mercenary John Hawkwood.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The artist described is Paolo Uccello, who painted both the fresco of John Hawkwood and the depiction of the four evangelists on the clock face in Florence Cathedral. These works are located in the Santa Maria del Fiore (Florence Cathedral) in Florence, Italy. \n\n\\boxed{Florence}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 164}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.35e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_510", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The first floor of a building of this complex includes the five-part polyptych\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given clue describes a specific architectural and artistic feature (a five-panel altarpiece displayed on an upper level) that uniquely identifies a well-known Florentine complex. This matches the Museo Nazionale di San Marco (the former Dominican convent of San Marco), whose first floor houses Fra Angelico\u2019s San Marco Altarpiece (c. 1438\u20131443), a five-part polyptych originally commissioned for the convent\u2019s church. No other major site fits the precise combination of \u201cfirst floor,\u201d \u201cbuilding of this complex,\u201d and \u201cfive-part polyptych.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{Museo di San Marco (Florence)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 197, "output_tokens": 126, "total_tokens": 323}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00056125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_515", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An artist's technique of giving depth to these objects by surrounding them with blue outlines was described in a Maurice Merleau-Ponty essay about that artist's \"Doubt.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given clue directly references Maurice Merleau-Ponty's 1945 essay \"C\u00e9zanne's Doubt,\" which analyzes Paul C\u00e9zanne's distinctive approach to still-life painting. C\u00e9zanne famously rendered apples (among other subjects) with modulated blue outlines to create volume, depth, and a sense of emerging form rather than relying on traditional linear perspective. This technique is the most commonly cited example matching the clue's phrasing of \"these objects.\"\n\n\\boxed{apples (C\u00e9zanne's)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 213, "output_tokens": 99, "total_tokens": 312}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00051375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_528", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This composer wrote a chamber opera in which a twelve-note theme played by a piano is transformed and heard again between each of the sixteen scenes.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The composer described is Benjamin Britten, who utilized this structural device in his 1954 chamber opera *The Turn of the Screw*. The twelve-note \"Screw\" theme serves as a recurring musical motif that undergoes variations to bridge the transitions between the opera's sixteen scenes.\n\n\\boxed{Benjamin Britten}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 83, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 149}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:26.317354+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00011975, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_549", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Art Rogers photographed a couple on a park bench holding several of these animals, leading him to sue an artist who created a so-called \"string\" of them based on Rogers' work.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The animals in question are puppies. Art Rogers took a photograph of a couple holding puppies, which was later used without permission by artist Jeff Koons in his sculpture \"String of Puppies,\" leading to a copyright infringement lawsuit. Koons lost the case as the court found substantial similarity and commercial use without fair use justification.\n\n\\boxed{puppies}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 167}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3916e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_563", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 1988 essay by Paul Karasik and Mark Newgarden extensively breaks down a single example in this medium created by Ernie Bushmiller.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question refers to the 1988 essay \"How to Read Nancy,\" which performs a frame-by-frame semiotic breakdown of a single daily strip. Ernie Bushmiller created the long-running newspaper comic strip Nancy, so the medium being analyzed is comic strips (or comics). This matches all details in the prompt exactly.\n\n\\boxed{comic strips (Nancy)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 210, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 282}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004425, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_627", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This director's last interviews, conducted by Canadian filmmaker Damian Pettigrew, were spliced together into the book and film\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The director is Federico Fellini, whose final conversations with Damian Pettigrew were compiled into the documentary *Fellini: I'm a Born Liar* and the accompanying book. These interviews provide a rare, intimate look at his creative process and philosophy toward the end of his life.\n\n\\boxed{Federico Fellini}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 77, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 144}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:06:25.246845+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00011975, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_635", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Ministry of Information commissioned Paul Nash to paint one of these things in his Defence of Albion.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue refers to a WWII-era work by British artist Paul Nash (a war artist employed by the Ministry of Information). \u201cDefence of Albion\u201d depicts the aerial-protection system then in use over Britain, so the object Nash was commissioned to paint is a barrage balloon.  \n\nThis fits the phrasing \u201cone of these things,\u201d which treats the balloon as the common category being asked for.\n\n\\boxed{barrage balloon}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 199, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 282}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00045625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_685", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A man who gained fame for this activity likely modeled for a bronze sculpture exhibited by Arthur Lee at the Armory Show titled The Ethiopian.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes a historical connection to the 1913 Armory Show, where sculptor Arthur Lee exhibited the bronze \"The Ethiopian.\" This work is documented as having been modeled by Jack Johnson, whose celebrity derived from his career as the first African-American world heavyweight champion. The activity referenced is therefore boxing (or prizefighting).\n\n\\boxed{boxing (Jack Johnson model)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 207, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 282}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00044625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_714", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to Mrs. Chambers, a member of this family was buried in periwinkle blue after being poisoned.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue refers to a specific literary reference in Ellen Raskin's *The Westing Game*. In the novel, housekeeper Mrs. Chambers recounts that Violet Westing (daughter of Samuel Westing) was forced into an unwanted engagement, died under suspicious circumstances widely described as poisoning, and was buried in her intended wedding gown of periwinkle blue. This directly identifies the family in question.\n\n\\boxed{Westing family}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 202, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 285}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00046, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_807", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One building in this city features a crossing tower over a trefoil apse that was missing two of its four corner turrets until an 1875 restoration.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The description refers to a distinctive Romanesque church whose trefoil (cloverleaf) east end is crowned by an octagonal crossing tower whose four corner turrets were left incomplete for centuries. That church is St. Maria im Kapitol in Cologne; the missing turrets were finally rebuilt in the 1870s restoration. Because the question asks for the city containing this building, the answer is therefore Cologne.\n\n\\boxed{Cologne}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 212, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 299}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004825, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_815", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a modern touch, this artist selected the moment at which a cup mostly obscures the face of one of the two seated women in a painting titled The Tea, which is similar in theme to this artist's portrait of Mary Dickinson Riddle, Lady at the Tea Table.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The artist described is Mary Cassatt, known for her intimate depictions of women and domestic scenes, particularly involving tea. In *The Tea*, the modern touch refers to the unconventional composition where a cup obscures one woman\u2019s face, emphasizing everyday moments. This aligns with her similar work *Lady at the Tea Table*, confirming her focus on tea-drinking as a social ritual.\n\n\\boxed{Mary Cassatt}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 199}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6594e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_817", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Composer and type of piece required. One of these pieces by this composer opens by twice repeating a dotted falling fifth over an F minor seventh, then three short chords and one long chord a half-step higher.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes the opening motif of a well-known atonal piano work whose first few bars consist of a repeated dotted falling fifth (C\u2013F) sustained over an F-minor-seventh harmony, followed immediately by three staccato chords and one longer chord transposed up a semitone.  \n\nThis distinctive gesture occurs at the beginning of Arnold Schoenberg\u2019s Op. 11 No. 1, one of the set of \u201cThree Piano Pieces.\u201d  \n\nHence the required answer is the composer and the genre of the cycle.\n\n\\boxed{Schoenberg, 3 piano pieces (Op.11)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 221, "output_tokens": 120, "total_tokens": 341}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00057625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_828", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: David Rickert claimed that this specific location was the site of the \"best thing\" Jess Stacy ever did.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "David Rickert referred to the 1938 Benny Goodman Carnegie Hall concert as the site of the \"best thing\" Jess Stacy ever did, highlighting Stacy's legendary piano solo during \"Sing, Sing, Sing.\" This performance is widely celebrated for its improvisational brilliance and emotional depth. The specific location is Carnegie Hall.\n\n\\boxed{Carnegie Hall}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 81, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 154}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3051000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_838", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Paul Tillich described the central man in this work as \"alone but not lonely\" and argued that it is the key image in representing Martin Luther's \"form of the courage to be.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a specific reference in Paul Tillich's theological writings (notably *The Courage to Be*), where he analyzes an image of solitary steadfastness amid existential threats as emblematic of Luther's faith. This directly matches Albrecht D\u00fcrer's 1513 engraving *Knight, Death and the Devil* (also called *The Rider*), whose central armored figure rides forward undeterred by the surrounding symbols of mortality and evil. No other artwork fits Tillich's phrasing or the Luther connection.\n\n\\boxed{Knight, Death & the Devil (D\u00fcrer)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 280, "output_tokens": 459, "total_tokens": 739}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:10:05.503529+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0014975, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_865", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: David Weir argues that this work's image of an  Acherontia  inspired the depiction of an anopheles mosquito that its creator made four years later for a documentary depicting poor mountain-dwelling peasants called  Land Without Bread .\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The work referred to is Luis Bu\u00f1uel's *Un Chien Andalou*, whose surrealist imagery influenced later works by the filmmaker. David Weir suggests that the depiction of an Acherontia (a death's-head moth) in this film inspired Bu\u00f1uel's later portrayal of an anopheles mosquito in *Land Without Bread*. The creator of both works is Luis Bu\u00f1uel.\n\n\\boxed{Un Chien Andalou}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 93, "total_tokens": 201}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6968e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_867", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This man proclaimed that \"modern art can only be born when signs become symbols\" in his analysis of the geometrical aspects of paintings.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quote concerns the shift from representational signs to abstracted, geometrically organized symbols as the basis of modernism, a thesis developed through close analysis of painting structure. This matches Wilhelm Worringer\u2019s 1908 treatise Abstraction and Empathy (and its sequel Formprobleme der Gotik), which explicitly frames the birth of modern art in precisely those geometric-symbolic terms. No other major theorist of the period (Kandinsky, Panofsky, Ghyka, etc.) couples the same phrasing with a sustained geometric reading of historical painting.\n\n\\boxed{Wilhelm Worringer}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 206, "output_tokens": 115, "total_tokens": 321}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000545, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_884", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This English word, which is not a place name, begins the title of a painting commissioned by Girolamo Marcello in which a cupid at the feet of the title nude was painted out by a later artist.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The painting in question is Titian's *Venus of Urbino*, commissioned by Girolamo Marcello. The English word that begins the title and is not a place name is \"Venus,\" referring to the Roman goddess. The cupid in the original painting was later painted out in a subsequent version.\n\n\\boxed{Venus}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 171}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4142e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_941", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A painting by an artist from this country was purchased with money Ernest Hemingway earned in a boxing match and shows a newspaper whose name is cut off at \"L'INTR\" on the title  Farm .\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The painting described is *The Farm* by Joan Mir\u00f3, a Spanish artist. Ernest Hemingway purchased the painting using money he earned from a boxing match, and the newspaper fragment in the artwork shows \"L'INTR,\" likely from \"L'Intransigeant.\" The country of origin for Mir\u00f3 is Spain.\n\n\\boxed{Spain}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 172}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4271000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_946", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A composition with this nickname opens its finale with a soprano soloist singing a wordless pentatonic melody over a drumroll, and features a second-movement trumpet cadenza inspired by its composer hearing a bugler accidentally play a harmonic seventh.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question describes two distinctive features that uniquely match Ralph Vaughan Williams\u2019s Symphony No. 3. The second movement contains an unaccompanied trumpet cadenza whose flattened seventh was deliberately modeled on the \u201cout-of-tune\u201d harmonic that the composer heard a bugler play during World War I. The finale then begins with a wordless soprano vocalise (explicitly marked \u201cpentatonic\u201d in the score) floating above a timpani roll, confirming that the work in question is the one universally known by the nickname \u201cPastoral.\u201d\n\nThus the nickname requested by the question is simply \u201cPastoral.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{Pastoral (VW Sym. 3)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 228, "output_tokens": 129, "total_tokens": 357}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0006075, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_953", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Three walls of an exhibit hall in this country were decorated with a motif including a femme fatale in three-quarter profile representing Lasciviousness and depictions of Typhon and his daughters by an artist who later taught the painter of  Portrait of Wally .\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The exhibit hall with walls decorated by an artist who later taught the painter of *Portrait of Wally* (Egon Schiele) refers to works by Gustav Klimt. Klimt, an Austrian artist, created symbolic murals including allegorical female figures and mythological themes, such as those representing vices and figures like Typhon. The country where this occurred is Austria.\n\n\\boxed{Austria}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 199}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6622999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Fine Arts_997", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The subject of this painting drinks a toast in a portrait made a year earlier that is now in the Isabella Stewart Gardner museum.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query is a riddle identifying a specific artwork based on its subject and a related portrait. The Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum holds Sargent\u2019s 1882\u201383 study \u201cMadame Gautreau Drinking a Toast.\u201d That sitter is the same woman portrayed a year later in Sargent\u2019s 1883\u201384 \u201cMadame X\u201d (Metropolitan Museum of Art). Hence the painting whose subject is described is \u201cMadame X.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{Madame X (Sargent)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 205, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 296}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00048375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_1013", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Massive parades of jeeps called  yipao  honor this country's farmers and are held in cities like Armenia and Calarca\u0301.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The \"yipao\" parades are a cultural tradition in Colombia, where decorated jeeps are showcased to honor coffee farmers. These parades are especially prominent in the Colombian Coffee-Growing Axis, including cities like Armenia and Calarc\u00e1. The correct answer is Colombia.\n\n\\boxed{Colombia}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 88, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 151}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2548e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_1023", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This city was the site of the so-called \"Trefa  (TRAY-fuh)  \n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The city referred to is Cincinnati, where the \"Trefa Banquet\" took place in 1883, marking a significant moment in the history of American Judaism due to the serving of non-kosher food at a Jewish event. This event highlighted the growing divide between traditional and Reform Judaism in the United States. \n\n\\boxed{Cincinnati}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 80, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 154}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.308e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_1100", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A building in this city contains an installation called  Fiori di Como  that consists of more than 2,000 Dale Chihuly-blown glass flowers.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The installation \"Fiori di Como\" by Dale Chihuly is located in Las Vegas. It is situated in the Bellagio Hotel and Casino, where it adorns the lobby with its vibrant, hand-blown glass flowers. \n\n\\boxed{Las Vegas}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 150}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2274000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_1116", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A locomotive passes by one of these animals in a notable diamond-shaped postage stamp from the short-lived Tuvan People's Republic.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes a specific philatelic curiosity: the Tuvan People's Republic (1921\u20131944) produced a series of diamond-shaped stamps, one of which depicts a steam locomotive passing a camel. Because the question is phrased in the \u201cone of these animals\u201d style typical of quiz-bowl or crossword clues, the expected referent is simply the animal shown on that stamp\u2014camels. No other animal appears in the well-documented Tuva locomotive scene, confirming the answer.\n\n\\boxed{camels}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 204, "output_tokens": 103, "total_tokens": 307}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_1148", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Vitousek lab uses a four-million-year chronosequence in this region to understand the successional dynamics of nutrient cycling.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Vitousek lab studies nutrient cycling using a four-million-year chronosequence in Hawaii.\n\nThis long-term ecological research focuses on how soil nutrients and ecosystems change over time on volcanic landscapes.\n\n\\boxed{Hawaii}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 130}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0535e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_1192", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This city is home to a UFO-shaped ice cream parlor called Coppelia, which was founded by a world leader.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The city described is Havana, Cuba. Coppelia is a famous UFO-shaped ice cream parlor founded in 1966 and named after a ballet, inspired by revolutionary leader Che Guevara's interest in making ice cream accessible to all Cubans. It is often associated with the Cuban Revolution's leaders, though not directly founded by Fidel Castro.\n\n\\boxed{Havana}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 83, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 162}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3793e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_1211", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Long tracking shots of this desert are coupled with audio of  lm scholar Lotte Eisner reading from the Popol Vuh in Werner Herzog's early documentary Fata Morgana.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes a key sequence from Werner Herzog's 1971 experimental documentary *Fata Morgana*. That film consists almost entirely of extended tracking shots across the dunes and salt flats of the Sahara (primarily in southern Algeria and Morocco), over which Lotte Eisner recites passages from the Popol Vuh. No other desert is featured in the picture, so the referent is unambiguously the Sahara.\n\n\\boxed{Sahara (desert)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 216, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 304}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00049, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_1252", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: n an e5fort to revitalize a town in this state, sculptor Gary Gre5f placed massive metal statues of pheasants, grasshoppers, and deer along its so called \"Enchanted Highway.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Enchanted Highway is a stretch of road in North Dakota featuring large metal sculptures created by artist Gary Greff to revitalize the area. These sculptures include pheasants, grasshoppers, and deer, among other whimsical figures. The state is North Dakota.\n\n\\boxed{North Dakota}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 168}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3755e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_1334", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In this city in the 1930s, the meteorologist Wilhelm Gustlo f organized a local Nazi party before being shot by the young Jew David Frankfurter, an event described in Gunter Grass's novel Crabwalk.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The city described is Davos, Switzerland, where Wilhelm Gustloff served as the leader of the Nazi Party's Swiss branch until his assassination in 1936. This historical event serves as a central theme in G\u00fcnter Grass's 2002 novel *Crabwalk*.\n\n\\boxed{Davos}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 166}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:08:16.254551+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000124, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_1335", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Emmeline Pankhurst's daughter Sylvia was invited to live in this city in 1956 a ter supporting an anticolonial movement in the 1930s and 1940s.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Sylvia Pankhurst was invited to live in Addis Ababa, Ethiopia, in 1956 after her long-standing support for the Ethiopian resistance against Italian colonization in the 1930s and 1940s. She was a passionate anti-colonial activist and developed strong ties with Emperor Haile Selassie. Her contributions were recognized by the Ethiopian government, which invited her to reside in the capital.\n\n\\boxed{Addis Ababa}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 100, "total_tokens": 204}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.7384e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_1356", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One of this province's \"ten strange wonders\" is a food with an infamously complex name that requires 58 strokes to write.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The food in question is \"bi\u00e1ngbi\u00e1ng mi\u00e0n,\" a type of Chinese noodle known for the complexity of the character \"bi\u00e1ng,\" which requires 58 strokes to write. This dish is associated with Shaanxi province, famous for its unique local cuisine and cultural quirks. \n\n\\boxed{Shaanxi}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 88, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 157}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3148e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_1407", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Local legend holds that Muhammad safely landed in this country at a cove called the Prophet's Hole.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question refers to the first Hijra (flight of persecuted early Muslims from Mecca), who sailed across the Red Sea to safety in the Aksumite kingdom. Historical and local tradition places their landing at a coastal inlet on the territory of the modern state of Eritrea, which is still known as the \u201cProphet\u2019s Hole.\u201d (Ethiopia is sometimes mentioned because of the ancient kingdom\u2019s extent, but the Red-Sea littoral in question lies in present-day Eritrea.)\n\n\\boxed{Eritrea}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 200, "output_tokens": 100, "total_tokens": 300}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_141", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A uranium-containing submarine that ran aground near a naval base in this body of water was nicknamed \"Whiskey on the Rocks.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The submarine incident referred to occurred in the Baltic Sea when the Soviet submarine K-129, a Whiskey-class submarine, ran aground near the Swedish naval base at Karlskrona in 1981. This event became famously known as \"Whiskey on the Rocks\" due to the submarine's class and the location of the grounding. The body of water where this happened is the Baltic Sea.\n\n\\boxed{Baltic Sea}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 94, "total_tokens": 179}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5434999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_1414", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Rotoscoped archival footage of an event that took place in this city is interspersed with eyewitness interviews in a 2016 Kevin Maitland documentary.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The 2016 documentary in question is Keith Maitland's *Tower* (the name \"Kevin\" is evidently a minor transcription error). It reconstructs the 1966 University of Texas clock-tower shooting via rotoscoped archival footage intercut with present-day eyewitness testimony; the event and the film are both set in Austin, Texas. No other city matches the described production.\n\n\\boxed{Austin, TX}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 271, "output_tokens": 309, "total_tokens": 580}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:34.230139+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00111125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_1448", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This peninsula will eventually be connected to the mainland by the planned Parallel Thimble Shoal Tunnel.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue refers to a planned expansion of the Chesapeake Bay Bridge-Tunnel (CBBT) in Hampton Roads, Virginia. The existing CBBT already links the Virginia mainland (near Virginia Beach) to the southern tip of the Eastern Shore via the Thimble Shoal Tunnel and other segments; the parallel tunnel simply adds a second bore for capacity and safety. Thus the peninsula in question is the Eastern Shore of Virginia (the southern portion of the Delmarva Peninsula).\n\n\\boxed{Eastern Shore (VA)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 200, "output_tokens": 103, "total_tokens": 303}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005075, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_1516", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Before directing the London Fire Brigade, James Braidwood organized the  rst modern municipal  re brigade in this city, where he helped  ght an 1824 \"Great Fire\" that destroyed the studio of caricaturist John Kay.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "James Braidwood organized the first modern municipal fire brigade in Edinburgh, where he helped fight the 1824 \"Great Fire\" that destroyed the studio of caricaturist John Kay. He later went on to lead the London Fire Brigade. The correct answer is Edinburgh.\n\n\\boxed{Edinburgh}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 122, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 193}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5762e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_1555", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Welsh immigrants to this region founded a settlement called Y Wladfa (oh lad-vah).\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Welsh settlement known as Y Wladfa (founded in 1865) was established by immigrants in the Chubut Valley of Argentina. This area lies within the broader geographic and cultural region of Patagonia. The name and history are unique to that location and are not associated with Welsh colonies elsewhere.\n\n\\boxed{Patagonia (Chubut, Arg.)}\n\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 199, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 274}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00043625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_1657", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Bally Manufacturing's attempt to corner this city's leisure industry in the 1970s hit a snag when preservationists objected to its planned demolition of the Marlborough\u00c2\u2013Blenheim Hotel.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The city in question is Atlantic City, where Bally Manufacturing planned to build a casino in the 1970s but faced opposition due to the proposed demolition of the historic Marlborough\u2013Blenheim Hotel. Preservationists argued for the protection of the architecturally significant structure, which delayed Bally's plans. This event was part of the larger transformation of Atlantic City into a gambling hub.\n\n\\boxed{Atlantic City}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 187}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5771e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_1707", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: On April 23, lovers in the four provinces of this region celebrate a holiday in which men give women roses in exchange for books.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The holiday described is celebrated on April 23 and involves men giving women roses in exchange for books, which is a tradition associated with Catalonia, Spain. This custom is part of the celebration of Sant Jordi, the patron saint of Catalonia. The region referred to is Catalonia, which includes four provinces: Barcelona, Girona, Lleida, and Tarragona.\n\n\\boxed{Catalonia}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 172}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4677e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_1793", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An art studio in this country employs 4,000 people to create massive monuments for African capitals, such as the African Renaissance Monument in Dakar.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The African Renaissance Monument in Dakar is located in Senegal, but it was actually constructed by a North Korean company, Mansudae Art Studio, which is known for building large monuments in various African countries.\n\nMansudae Art Studio, based in North Korea, employs thousands of workers and has been involved in creating monumental sculptures across Africa.\n\n\\boxed{North Korea}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 167}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4061e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_1812", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Swedish royals were once taken on a \"vice tour\" of one of these places by \"Mayor\" Chuck Connors.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue refers to a historical anecdote about \"Chuck\" Connors (a real-life Tammany Hall figure nicknamed the \"Mayor of Chinatown\"), who in 1898\u20131900 led slumming/vice tours of New York\u2019s Chinatown for visiting European nobility, including Swedish royalty. This directly identifies the category as Chinatowns (plural), the most common answer in quiz contexts such as Jeopardy!.\n\n\\boxed{Chinatowns}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 267, "output_tokens": 456, "total_tokens": 723}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:36.023448+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00147375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_1835", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Li Ying's 2007 documentary about this site opens with footage of a 90-year-old swordsmith at work.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes a documentary by Chinese filmmaker Li Ying that focuses on an ancient Chinese location renowned for its centuries-old tradition of sword-forging. Longquan (in Zhejiang province) is the only site that matches this description, having been a center of sword production since at least the Spring and Autumn period and still home to living master smiths in 2007. No other well-known Chinese historic site (Great Wall, Shaolin, etc.) fits the opening footage of the 90-year-old artisan.\n\n\\boxed{Longquan (China)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 204, "output_tokens": 109, "total_tokens": 313}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005275, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_223", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The world's longest railway platform is found in this country.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The world's longest railway platform is located in India, at Gorakhpur Railway Station. It measures approximately 1,366 meters (4,480 feet) in length. \n\n\\boxed{India}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 71, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 118}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 9.741e-06, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_304", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A boundary dispute with Britain over this state's border was resolved in 1903 and involved determining the exact meaning of vague terms such as \"the mountains parallel to the coast.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The boundary dispute involving vague terms like \"the mountains parallel to the coast\" was resolved in 1903 and pertained to the Alaska-British Columbia border. This dispute arose between the United States and Britain (representing Canada) over the interpretation of the boundary set by the 1825 Anglo-Russian Convention. The arbitration tribunal favored the U.S. position, clarifying the border through the Alaska Panhandle.\n\n\\boxed{Alaska}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 93, "total_tokens": 189}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6116e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_329", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This city contains many yalis, mansions built immediately adjacent to the sea.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The city known for its yalis, which are traditional wooden mansions built along the shoreline, is Istanbul. These historic homes are primarily located along the Bosphorus Strait, offering direct sea access. \n\n\\boxed{Istanbul}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 75, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 122}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0024999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_357", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In this city, a clock with the times of 148 major cities around the globe is topped by a sculpture of an atom and is known as the Urania World Clock.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Urania World Clock, featuring times of 148 major cities and topped by an atomic sculpture, is located in Berlin, Germany. It is a famous landmark situated on Alexanderplatz. \n\n\\boxed{Berlin}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 142}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1416e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_387", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 2010, this country drew international attention by passing an environmentalist act called the Law of the Rights of Mother Earth.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The country that passed the Law of the Rights of Mother Earth in 2010 is Bolivia. This landmark legislation granted nature the same rights as humans, recognizing Earth as a living system with legal rights to exist and thrive. The law drew global attention for its innovative environmental approach.\n\n\\boxed{Bolivia}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 152}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2676999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_388", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This state is home to the second-most densely concentrated surname in the US, Locklear, which comes from the Lumbee people in Robeson County.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The state with the second-most densely concentrated surname Locklear, associated with the Lumbee people in Robeson County, is North Carolina. The Lumbee Tribe is primarily based in Robeson County, and the surname Locklear is especially prevalent among this community. \n\n\\boxed{North Carolina}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 89, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 148}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2219e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_399", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Fauna unique to this region include the llama-like guanaco, the ostrich-like Darwin's rhea, and a rodent called the tuco-tuco.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The region described is the Patagonia region of South America. These animals are characteristic of the vast, arid steppes found in this southern territory.\n\n\\boxed{Patagonia}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 35, "total_tokens": 122}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:08:14.638523+00:00"}, "cost": 7.425e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_407", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Ghost towns in this desert include Kelso, formerly known as \"the town without television,\" and the abandoned silver mining town Calico.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The desert described, containing ghost towns like Kelso and Calico, is the Mojave Desert. Both towns are located in Southern California within this desert region. \n\n\\boxed{Mojave Desert}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 86, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 128}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0306000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_411", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A stacked stone sculpture called an Inuksuk was used as a symbol for one event in this city.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Inuksuk was used as a symbol for the 2010 Winter Olympics, which were held in Vancouver, Canada. This stone sculpture represents guidance and support in Inuit culture and was chosen to reflect the spirit of the Games. \n\n\\boxed{Vancouver}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 81, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 139}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1551e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_438", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Europe's largest indoor aquarium is located in this city, which is home to the art collection of oil magnate Calouste Gulbenkian.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The city described is Lisbon, Portugal. It is home to the Calouste Gulbenkian Museum, which houses the art collection of oil magnate Calouste Gulbenkian, and nearby is the Lisbon Oceanarium, Europe's largest indoor aquarium. \n\n\\boxed{Lisbon}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 89, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 150}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2419000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_529", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This region's Don Juan Pond is named for two helicopter pilots, and not the fictional character.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Don Juan Pond is located in Antarctica's Wright Valley. It is named after Don Juan Pond, a helicopter pilot, and another pilot named John Hickey, combining their names informally. The pond is known for its extremely high salinity, preventing it from freezing despite the cold temperatures.\n\n\\boxed{Antarctica}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 78, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 143}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2038e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_540", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This country's capital is home to the Witches' Market, where healers called yatiri sell various herbs.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Witches' Market is located in La Paz, the capital of Bolivia. This market is known for its traditional healers, or yatiri, who sell herbs, amulets, and other spiritual items. The country in question is Bolivia.\n\n\\boxed{Bolivia}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 82, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 140}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1622e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_557", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 2016, the golden lantern-like cap of a 123-floor \"World Tower\" in this city was finished.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The building described is the Lotte World Tower, which is located in Seoul, South Korea. Its distinctive lantern-like top was completed in 2016.\n\n\\boxed{Seoul}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 125}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:08:14.257602+00:00"}, "cost": 8.125e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_61", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A suburb of a city with this name included an iron mine that lent its name to the daiquiri.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The phrasing indicates that the daiquiri cocktail takes its name from an iron mine located in a suburb (Daiquir\u00ed) of a particular city. That city is Santiago de Cuba, so the name referenced by the query is simply Santiago. (Other cities named Santiago lack any historical connection to either the mine or the cocktail.)\n\n\\boxed{Santiago}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 202, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 272}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004275, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_686", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: It's not Georgia, but a festival with the slogan \"Give Peach a Chance\" is held in this state's city of Ruston.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The festival with the slogan \"Give Peach a Chance\" is held in Ruston, Louisiana, not Georgia. This annual event celebrates local culture and music, playing on the word \"peach\" humorously despite Louisiana not being known for peaches like Georgia. The correct answer is Louisiana.\n\n\\boxed{Louisiana}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 152}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2676999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_830", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Anthropologists like Georg Steindorff investigated traditional homosexual behavior in a town in one of these natural features.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue references anthropological fieldwork (notably by Georg Steindorff) on institutionalized male homosexuality/pederasty in the Egyptian oasis town of Siwa. Siwa lies inside a classic desert oasis, so the \u201cnatural features\u201d referenced by the clue are oases.  \n\nThus the expected answer is the category \u201coases.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{oases}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 264, "output_tokens": 469, "total_tokens": 733}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:38.721420+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0015025, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_856", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A massive 2,000-year-old system for growing this crop was built by the Igorot  (ego-ROTE)  inhabitants of the Ifugao  \n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The massive 2,000-year-old system built by the Igorot people of the Ifugao is for growing rice. This system is known as the Ifugao Rice Terraces, often called the \"Eighth Wonder of the World.\" These terraces were carved into mountain slopes to cultivate rice using sophisticated irrigation methods.\n\n\\boxed{rice}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 168}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4045e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_863", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One of these places in Stockholm is supposedly haunted by the Silverpilen, or \"Silver Arrow\", and features a huge fresco depicting a timeline of human civilization at Rissen.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes a category of locations in Stockholm linked by two distinctive features: the urban legend of the ghost train Silverpilen (which is said to appear only at abandoned or little-used stops on the tunnelbana network) and the large historical fresco at Rissne station. Both details unambiguously identify the Stockholm metro (T-bana) stations as the common set. Hence the answer to the \u201cone of these places\u201d prompt is the Stockholm metro stations themselves.\n\n\\boxed{Stockholm metro stations (T-bana)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 215, "output_tokens": 105, "total_tokens": 320}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00053125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_917", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In this country, the office of the newspaper  Respublika  was firebombed in 2002 shortly after a decapitated dog was hung from that building with the note \"There will be no next time.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The incident involving the firebombing of the Respublika newspaper office and the decapitated dog occurred in Kazakhstan. This was in response to the newspaper's critical reporting and alleged insults toward the president. The country is known for suppressing press freedom, and this event highlighted the dangers faced by journalists there.\n\n\\boxed{Kazakhstan}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 178}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4668e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_939", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An organization based in this European city awards the Wateler Prize and was established after Andrew White convinced Andrew Carnegie to fund a palace.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The organization referred to is the Permanent Court of Arbitration, which is based in The Hague, Netherlands. The Carnegie Foundation, funded by Andrew Carnegie and established through the efforts of Andrew White, built the Peace Palace in The Hague to house this institution. The Wateler Peace Prize is awarded annually by a Dutch foundation based in The Hague.\n\n\\boxed{The Hague}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 159}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3435e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_954", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The brother of a ruler of this country died while defending that ruler's residence of Dasman Palace.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The country in question is Kuwait. The brother of Emir Jaber Al-Ahmad Al-Sabah, Sheikh Faisal Al-Sabah, died while defending Dasman Palace during the Iraqi invasion in 1990. \n\n\\boxed{Kuwait}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 79, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 135}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1208999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_96", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The first recorded use of this river's current name, which may mean \"our boat,\" is by Alvise da Cadamosto (\"all-VEE-say da kah-dah-MOH-stoo\"), who met the damel of Cayor along the coast just to its south.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue refers to a West African river whose mouth lies along the coast of modern Senegal, just south of the historic kingdom of Cayor. Venetian explorer Alvise da Cadamosto, sailing for Portugal in the 1450s, left the first written record of the river\u2019s present-day name while describing his meeting with the damel (ruler) of Cayor. Linguistic evidence identifies that name as \u201cGambia,\u201d plausibly derived from a local phrase meaning \u201cour boat.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{Gambia R. (or Gambie)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 238, "output_tokens": 109, "total_tokens": 347}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00057, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_968", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This city contains a set of nine kinetic art sculptures depicting the Muses by Troy Pillow located at the corners of the namesake intersection of its 9th and 9th neighborhood.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The city described is Salt Lake City, Utah, where the \"9th & 9th\" neighborhood features a series of kinetic art sculptures of the Muses by artist Troy Pillow, installed at the intersection of 9th South and 9th East.\n\nThese sculptures are part of a public art initiative to enhance the cultural vibrancy of the area.\n\n\\boxed{Salt Lake City}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 175}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4716e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Geography_986", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: It was revealed in 2016 that this man corrected the author's factual inaccuracies about the speed of a boat in  The Story of a Shipwrecked Sailor  and a rifle in  Chronicle of a Death Foretold  while serving as an unofficial copy-editor for his friend Gabriel Garci\u0301a\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query is a reference to a 2016 revelation (from letters and interviews published after Garc\u00eda M\u00e1rquez's death) about an unofficial proofreader who fixed specific technical details in two of the author's early works. The individual in question was Germ\u00e1n Vargas Cantillo, a member of the Barranquilla Group and lifelong friend of Garc\u00eda M\u00e1rquez who routinely performed this service. (\u00c1lvaro Mutis and Plinio Apuleyo Mendoza were also close friends but did not perform the copy-editing role described.)\n\n\\boxed{Germ\u00e1n Vargas Cantillo}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 240, "output_tokens": 109, "total_tokens": 349}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005725, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1007", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In this location, President Eisenhower gave a July 4, 1950, speech to Boy Scouts gathered for the first post-war Jamboree.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is the site of the first post-war Boy Scout Jamboree, which was held at Valley Forge, Pennsylvania. President Eisenhower gave a speech there on July 4, 1950, addressing the gathered Scouts. This location is historically significant for its association with both the Revolutionary War and Scouting events.\n\n\\boxed{Valley Forge}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 167}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4032e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1019", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Homeowners in this city were granted a special bread ration called the  panes aedium .\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The \"panes aedium\" was a special bread ration granted to homeowners in ancient Rome. This ration was part of the Roman state's welfare system, particularly during the imperial period, to support citizens, especially in the capital city. The city associated with such rations is Rome.\n\n\\boxed{Rome}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 78, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 142}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1937999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_102", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Max Jones's biography of this man portrays him as a \"martyr to science\" whose death united political radicals.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question is a reference to a specific historical biography, Max Jones's 2003 work *The Last Great Quest*. That book is a scholarly study of Robert Falcon Scott and the Terra Nova expedition; Jones explicitly frames Scott's demise (and the decision to haul scientific specimens to the end) as a \"martyrdom to science\" whose public commemoration briefly bridged Britain's class and political divides, including among radicals. No other figure matches both the biographer and the quoted interpretive language.\n\nThus the man in question is Robert Falcon Scott.\n\n\\boxed{Robert Falcon Scott (Capt. Scott)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 203, "output_tokens": 117, "total_tokens": 320}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00054625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1028", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Objects used to interact with this substance are often inscribed with adinkra symbols by the Akan people and are called mrammou.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes a traditional Akan (Ghanaian) practice involving objects called mrammou. These are the decorated spoons, scoops, or measures used to handle and portion gold dust (the former regional currency), and they are frequently incised with adinkra symbols. Hence the substance in question is gold dust.\n\n\\boxed{gold dust}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 207, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 278}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00043625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1030", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Rebecca Lukens was a pioneering female executive in this industry.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Rebecca Lukens (1794\u20131854) managed the Brandywine Iron Works after her husband's death, turning it into what became the Lukens Steel Company\u2014one of the earliest and largest U.S. producers of boiler plate.  \nShe is therefore recognized as the first woman to lead an industrial corporation, specifically in the iron-and-steel sector.  \nThe industry referenced is consequently the steel (or iron-and-steel) industry.\n\n\\boxed{steel (iron/steel mfg.)}\n\n(The phrasing matches common quiz/crossword clues for this fact.)", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 254, "output_tokens": 512, "total_tokens": 766}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:39.281738+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0015975, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1039", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A kingdom of this people constantly moved between their summer capital of Peiting and their winter capital of Qocho.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The kingdom described is the Uyghur Khaganate, which established a seasonal court moving between Peiting (in the north) and Qocho (in the Tarim Basin) during the 9th century after their migration from Mongolia. This practice reflected their adaptation to the climate and geography of the region. The people are the Uyghurs.\n\n\\boxed{Uyghurs}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 82, "output_tokens": 82, "total_tokens": 164}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4022e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1056", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 1830, this American city was connected to nearby Hamburg by the  Best Friend , the country's first commercially-run passenger steam locomotive.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Best Friend of Charleston was the first commercially operated passenger steam locomotive in the United States, beginning service in 1830. It ran on the South Carolina Canal and Railroad Company line between Charleston and Hamburg, South Carolina. Therefore, the American city connected to Hamburg by this locomotive was Charleston.\n\n\\boxed{Charleston}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 160}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3361000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1058", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Irvine Welsh claimed that one of these things was \"ill-conceived nostalgia\" that was \"wrenched from the rancid prostates of senile, gibbering hippies\".\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quote criticizes an event steeped in 1960s counter-culture nostalgia. Its phrasing (\u201csenile, gibbering hippies,\u201d \u201crancid prostates\u201d) points directly at the 1994 anniversary staging of the original Woodstock festival, which Irvine Welsh publicly derided in exactly those terms. Hence the referent is Woodstock \u201994 (or, more broadly, the series of Woodstock revivals).\n\n\\boxed{Woodstock '94 (revival fest.)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 215, "output_tokens": 93, "total_tokens": 308}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00050125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_106", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a scene first shown in this publication, a man states \"Oh no, my Lord, I assure you that parts of it are excellent!\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quote is a classic reference to the \"curate's egg\" anecdote, in which a junior clergyman is too timid to admit his breakfast egg is spoiled and instead offers the euphemistic reply given in the query. That scene first appeared as a full-page cartoon captioned \"True Humility\" in the British humor magazine Punch (9 November 1895). Consequently the publication named by the query is Punch.\n\n\\boxed{Punch}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 209, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 297}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00048125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1084", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: AT&amp;T executive Frederick Kappel reformed this organization after its public failure in Chicago during Christmas in 1966.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue refers to the 1966 Chicago mail crisis (a massive Christmas-season backlog that publicly exposed the breakdown of manual mail sorting). AT&T chairman Frederick Kappel was then named to lead the Presidential Commission that produced the 1968 Kappel Report; its recommendations were enacted in the Postal Reorganization Act of 1970, converting the old Post Office Department into the independent U.S. Postal Service.  \n\nThus the organization in question is the United States Postal Service (USPS).  \n\n\\boxed{US Postal Service (USPS)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 203, "output_tokens": 108, "total_tokens": 311}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00052375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1087", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Because tagua nuts resemble this substance, the palms on which they are found are named for it.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Tagua nuts are often referred to as \"vegetable ivory\" because they closely resemble elephant ivory in texture and appearance. As a result, the palms that produce them are commonly called ivory palms. The substance they resemble is ivory.\n\n\\boxed{ivory}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 79, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 132}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0908999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1090", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: While running for President, a man in this position released an unprecedented 12 years of his tax returns.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue refers to a historical first during a presidential campaign. George Romney (Mitt Romney\u2019s father) was serving as Governor of Michigan when he released twelve years of tax returns while seeking the 1968 Republican nomination\u2014an action then regarded as unprecedented. The position that satisfies the phrasing \u201ca man in this position\u201d is therefore Governor of Michigan.\n\n\\boxed{Gov. of Michigan (G. Romney)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 201, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 282}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00045375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_11", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: During a referendum on moving this state's capital, Marcus Daly's firm campaigned to keep it in a company town.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question refers to a historical event in Montana, where copper magnate Marcus Daly supported keeping the state capital in Helena, a company-influenced town, during a referendum. His rival, William A. Clark, backed moving the capital to his own company town, Anaconda. The capital remained in Helena.\n\n\\boxed{Montana}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 82, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 151}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2722e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1109", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This man founded a whiskey distillery named after a local strain of moonshine, Valley Tan.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question is a historical trivia item pointing to a 19th-century Utah figure. Valley Tan was the colloquial name for the locally distilled whiskey (and wool cloth) produced in the Utah Territory in the 1850s\u201360s. Orrin Porter Rockwell, the well-known Mormon frontiersman and lawman, operated a Salt Lake City tavern and distillery that commercialized this product under that name.\n\nThus the man referenced is Orrin Porter Rockwell.\n\n\\boxed{Orrin Porter Rockwell}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 199, "output_tokens": 99, "total_tokens": 298}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00049625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1113", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For one of these events, Taro Okamoto created the sculpture  Tower of the Sun , whose interior depicts a Tree of Life  that represents the evolution of animals.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue directly references the iconic Tower of the Sun sculpture (with its interior Tree of Life motif) that Taro Okamoto designed as the symbol of a major international exposition. This work was created exclusively for the 1970 World Exposition held in Osaka, Japan (commonly called Expo \u201970), which celebrated \u201cProgress and Harmony for Mankind.\u201d No other event matches the described artwork or its evolutionary theme.\n\n\\boxed{Expo '70 (Osaka World's Fair)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 214, "output_tokens": 93, "total_tokens": 307}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1135", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Hans Trobst's article \"Fifteen Gallows\" was one of the only foreign reports on purges undertaken by this leader that were justified the following year in his 36-hour speech delivered over six consecutive days.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a specific set of events in early 1959: summary executions of Batista-era officials that drew limited foreign coverage, most notably the article \u201cFifteen Gallows\u201d by German journalist Hans Trobst. Those executions were publicly defended the next year by the Cuban leader in an exceptionally long, multi-day address (a 36-hour speech spread over six consecutive days) that became one of his signature marathon performances. No other twentieth-century figure matches this precise combination of documented purges, the named foreign report, and the distinctive speech length and format.\n\nThus the leader in question is Fidel Castro.\n\n\\boxed{Fidel Castro}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 224, "output_tokens": 127, "total_tokens": 351}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005975, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_114", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When this group was hit with tear gas, the 12-week-old baby Bernard Myers was killed.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a specific historical incident from July 1932, when U.S. Army troops under Douglas MacArthur forcibly evicted the Bonus Army (also called the Bonus Expeditionary Force or BEF) from its Washington, D.C., encampments and used tear gas in the process. Contemporary accounts confirm that two infants, including 12-week-old Bernard Myers, died from the effects of the gas. This event is a standard clue in quiz-bowl or trivia contexts for identifying the Bonus Army.\n\n\\boxed{Bonus Army (marchers/BEF)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 200, "output_tokens": 111, "total_tokens": 311}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005275, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1154", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This object and its \"spider\" support were brought to San Francisco for the opening of the first Transcontinental Telephone Line.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The object referred to is the Liberty Bell. It was transported to San Francisco in 1915 for the Panama-Pacific International Exposition, where it was displayed alongside the \"spider\" support\u2014a special metal cradle designed to prevent further cracking. The bell was included to symbolize national unity, coinciding with the celebration of the first transcontinental telephone line.\n\n\\boxed{Liberty Bell}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4064e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1190", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A city-state on this island sent settlers to Lycia to found Phaselis.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The city-state of Rhodes, located on the island of Rhodes, sent settlers to Lycia to establish the city of Phaselis. This occurred in the 7th century BCE as part of Rhodian maritime expansion. The island of Rhodes is therefore the correct answer.\n\n\\boxed{Rhodes}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 77, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 139}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1667e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1191", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A group of people in this country undergoes the  Soyal  ritual on the winter solstice to \"awaken\" the Sun from its \"sleep\".\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Soyal ritual is practiced by the Hopi people, who are Native Americans primarily residing in the United States. This ceremony is performed during the winter solstice to mark the return of the sun and restore balance in the world. \n\n\\boxed{United States}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 145}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1861e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1216", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a dream from this text, two homosocial companions are represented as a cow who loses her horn and a hornless bull.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a very specific oneiric symbol from Old Norse literature, in which a pair of sworn foster-brothers (f\u00f3stbr\u00e6\u00f0r) appear as a cow that loses a horn and a hornless bull. This emblematic dream occurs in F\u00f3stbr\u00e6\u00f0ra saga, the saga devoted to precisely those two companions (\u00deorgeirr and \u00deorm\u00f3\u00f0r). No other medieval text matches the combination of homosocial protagonists and the exact bovine imagery.\n\n\\boxed{F\u00f3stbr\u00e6\u00f0ra saga}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 206, "output_tokens": 103, "total_tokens": 309}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000515, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1230", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One form of this resource was governed by the precarium, a type of law derived from the word preces meaning \"request.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The resource referred to is land, specifically in the context of early medieval tenure where the precarium was a legal arrangement allowing someone to hold land at the will of the owner, based on a request. This system evolved from the Roman practice where \"preces\" (requests) were made for temporary use of property. The most common answer to the question is land.\n\n\\boxed{land}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 164}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3935e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1243", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 1966, John Gerassi argued that an oligarchical power play was behind a conspiracy exploiting this attitude during which town hall speeches were given by John L. Butler and future senator Frank Church.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes events from mid-1950s Boise, Idaho, in which a morals scandal targeting gay men was deliberately inflamed for political ends. John Gerassi\u2019s 1966 book *The Boys of Boise* explicitly frames the episode as an oligarchic power play that exploited widespread societal prejudice against homosexuality; the cited town-hall appearances by Butler and Church occurred in that context. The attitude being invoked is therefore homophobia (sometimes labeled the \u201cLavender Scare\u201d).\n\n\\boxed{homophobia (Boise scandal)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 220, "output_tokens": 104, "total_tokens": 324}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000535, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_125", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A holder of this title commissioned a set of miniatures to accompany the story collection Tales of a Parrot.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue refers to the illustrated manuscript of the Tuti-nama (Tales of a Parrot), whose earliest Mughal version was produced in the 1560s. That manuscript was commissioned by the emperor Akbar, so the title in question is Mughal emperor (or its near-synonyms Padishah / Great Mughal).  \n\nOther rulers held the same title, but only Akbar is historically linked to this specific artistic commission.\n\n\\boxed{Mughal emperor (Akbar)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 202, "output_tokens": 94, "total_tokens": 296}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1288", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the 1930s, this state's governor proclaimed, \"I am not a liberal.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quote \"I am not a liberal\" is famously attributed to Huey Long, the governor of Louisiana in the 1930s. He made this statement to distance himself from mainstream New Deal liberalism, despite his own populist policies. The state is Louisiana.\n\n\\boxed{Louisiana}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 81, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 141}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1751e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1317", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A preacher from this city's New Bethel Baptist Church became known as The Man with the Million Dollar Voice a ter recording and selling his sermons, such as \"The Eagle Stirreth Her Nest.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The preacher known as \"The Man with the Million Dollar Voice\" was Reverend C.L. Franklin, who served at New Bethel Baptist Church in Detroit, Michigan. He gained fame for recording and selling his powerful sermons, including \"The Eagle Stirreth Her Nest.\" \n\n\\boxed{Detroit}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 163}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.34e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_133", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Before his work on the Enlightenment, progressive historian Carl L.\u00a0Becker proposed a \"dual\" interpretation of this event.\"Radical\" levelling effects of this event are assessed in a 1992 book by Gordon Wood.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The event referred to is the American Revolution. Carl L. Becker proposed a \"dual\" interpretation emphasizing both the struggle for liberty from Britain and the internal social conflict among Americans. Gordon Wood's 1992 book *The Radicalism of the American Revolution* assesses its transformative and leveling effects.\n\n\\boxed{American Revolution}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 176}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4468e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1378", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Carolyn Dean analyzed how the Corpus Christi festival in this modern-day country became a site of resistance as it syncretized with summer solstice celebrations.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Carolyn Dean studied how the Corpus Christi festival in Peru became a site of cultural resistance through its blending with Indigenous summer solstice celebrations, particularly Inti Raymi. This syncretism allowed Andean communities to preserve their traditions under colonial rule. \n\n\\boxed{Peru}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 89, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 147}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2119e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1380", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 2016, this speci c animal's name was given to a newly discovered spaceship in Conway's Game of Life that is only 28 cells and is the  rst to move at a speed of c over ten.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question pertains to a specific discovery in Conway's Game of Life (a well-known 2D cellular automaton). In 2016, a new orthogonal spaceship was found with a minimum population of 28 live cells; it travels at the previously unattained speed of \\(c/10\\) and was accordingly christened the \u201ccopperhead\u201d after the venomous snake of the same name. This matches the description exactly; earlier spaceships (glider, loafer, etc.) differ in speed, size, or discovery date.\n\n\\boxed{copperhead}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 225, "output_tokens": 114, "total_tokens": 339}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00056625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1420", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Loren Graham took the perspective of a member of this profession, Peter Palchinsky, in a history of the early Soviet Union titled for his \"ghost.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Loren Graham's book *The Ghost of the Executed Engineer* tells the story of Peter Palchinsky, a mining engineer and critic of Soviet industrial policies. Palchinsky is portrayed as a figure whose ideas and warnings were ignored, leading to disastrous consequences. The profession central to the narrative is engineering.\n\n\\boxed{engineer}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 159}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.329e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1435", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Richard Kohn's article on \"The Inside Story\" of this event argues that it was largely stage-managed to bolster the case for central government.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The event referred to is the Whiskey Rebellion. Richard Kohn argued that the federal government's response was exaggerated and stage-managed to assert authority and strengthen support for central government power. \n\n\\boxed{Whiskey Rebellion}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 89, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 135}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0919e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1439", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Jonathan Winkler's Nexus explains how the a7termath of this event led to unprecedented integration of private business and government research, while Nicholas Lambert argued that its protagonists were unwilling to threaten their own economic networks.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clues point to a specific pre-WWII historical episode whose economic and communications ramifications have been analyzed by the two named historians. Nicholas Lambert\u2019s *Planning Armageddon* examines British planning for economic warfare and shows that decision-makers ultimately refused to sever the global financial and shipping networks on which Britain itself depended. Jonathan Winkler\u2019s *Nexus* demonstrates that the communications failures exposed by the same conflict produced, in its immediate aftermath, an unprecedented fusion of private-sector infrastructure with U.S. government signals-intelligence programs. Both arguments therefore converge on the First World War as the referent event.\n\n\\boxed{WWI (or equiv.)}\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 221, "output_tokens": 126, "total_tokens": 347}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00059125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1449", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Alan Olmstead and Paul Rhode argued that new varieties of this commodity were responsible for its rise in production, against a controversial book with chapters like \"Feet,\" \"Breath,\" and \"Tongues.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Alan Olmstead and Paul Rhode challenged the arguments made in the controversial book *Time on the Cross* by Robert Fogel and Stanley Engerman, which used unconventional methods to analyze slavery's economics. They argued that improvements in cotton varieties, not slave labor efficiency, drove increased cotton production. The commodity in question is cotton.\n\n\\boxed{cotton}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 118, "output_tokens": 96, "total_tokens": 214}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.7978000000000003e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_149", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a book about this politician's \"intimate world,\" gender researcher Clarence A.\u00a0Tripp claimed that he had homosexual encounters throughout his life.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The politician referenced in the question is Lyndon B. Johnson. Clarence A. Tripp, in his book *The Intimate World of Abraham Lincoln*, made controversial claims about Lincoln, not Johnson. However, the correct answer based on the context of Tripp's work and the subject of his book is Abraham Lincoln.\n\n\\boxed{Abraham Lincoln}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 89, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 161}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3518999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1505", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A venue named for this family employed Oscar Tschirky, a celebrity chef who popularized Thousand Island dressing.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue refers to the ma\u00eetre d'h\u00f4tel Oscar Tschirky, who worked for decades at the Waldorf-Astoria Hotel in New York and is credited with popularizing Thousand Island dressing. That hotel was constructed and named for the Astor family (specifically William Waldorf Astor and John Jacob Astor IV). Thus the family referenced by the question is the Astors.\n\n\\boxed{Astor(s)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 202, "output_tokens": 82, "total_tokens": 284}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004575, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1528", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Daniel Arasse argued that this event amounted to an inverted baptismal rite.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Daniel Arasse interpreted the execution of Louis XVI as an inverted baptismal rite, symbolizing a dark, sacrificial ritual in the context of revolutionary France. He viewed the event as a perverse mirror of religious purification, where blood and death replaced spiritual cleansing. The correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{the execution of Louis XVI}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 75, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 141}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1925e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1549", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Biblioteca Ambrosiana in Milan holds a lock of this woman's hair from which Lord Byron stole a single strand.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The woman is Lucrezia Borgia, whose blonde hair is famously preserved in a reliquary at the Biblioteca Ambrosiana. Lord Byron visited the library in 1816 and was so captivated by the lock that he reportedly stole a single strand.\n\n\\boxed{Lucrezia Borgia}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 77, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 139}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:08:20.057299+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00011225, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1572", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Barry Popik's research revealed that the earliest instances of a phrase pairing these two words were in Christopher Bullock's Cobbler of Preston and Edward Ward's Dancing Devils.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given statement is a quiz clue (in the style of Jeopardy) pointing to the idiomatic phrase that pairs two specific numbers. Etymological research by Barry Popik and others has established that the earliest printed appearances of \u201cat sixes and sevens\u201d occur in Bullock\u2019s 1716 farce and Ward\u2019s 1724 poem. Consequently the two words referenced by the clue are \u201csixes\u201d and \u201csevens.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{at sixes and sevens}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 213, "output_tokens": 98, "total_tokens": 311}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00051125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1616", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A poem criticizing this government program declares that \"the millet is scattered over the ground, the leaves of the sweet potato are withered,\" which was used as evidence to \u2734re a defense minister.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The poem refers to the \"Great Leap Forward\" in China, during which agricultural policies led to widespread famine. The described imagery of scattered millet and withered sweet potato leaves reflects the crop failures and mismanagement under this program. The defense minister criticized was likely Peng Dehuai, who voiced concerns about the policy's failures.\n\n\\boxed{Great Leap Forward}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 174}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.45e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1618", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This body of water occupies the only surviving fragment of the Dura-Europos route map, which was drawn onto the leather portion of a Roman shield.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The body of water depicted on the surviving fragment of the Dura-Europos route map is the Euphrates River. This map, drawn on a leather shield fragment, shows part of a Roman military route that includes the Euphrates. The river was a key geographical feature in the region during the Roman period.\n\n\\boxed{Euphrates}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 167}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4061e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1637", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An oil painting of this battle displayed at the British Museum inaccurately shows an empress on horseback wielding a pistol and depicts Saint George throwing a spear at the losing army.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes a specific anachronism-filled oil painting held by the British Museum, whose iconography (a mounted empress brandishing a firearm plus Saint George hurling a lance) can only refer to the 1444 clash between the Ottoman forces of Murad II and the Polish-Hungarian crusader army of W\u0142adys\u0142aw III. That painting is conventionally titled \u201cThe Battle of Varna,\u201d and the two visual details are well-documented errors introduced by a later European artist. No other historically painted engagement matches both the museum location and the precise inaccuracies cited.\n\n\\boxed{Battle of Varna (1444)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 213, "output_tokens": 121, "total_tokens": 334}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00056875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1654", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Richard Slotkin's Gun\u1978ghter Nation contrasts the Turner thesis with this man's theory of frontier history, concluding that this man's \"progressive\" narrative was more in\u1978uential.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Richard Slotkin contrasts Frederick Jackson Turner's \"frontier thesis\" with the work of Theodore Roosevelt, specifically his multi-volume historical study *The Winning of the West*. Slotkin argues that Roosevelt\u2019s \"progressive\" narrative of national expansion and racial struggle became the more dominant and influential framework for American frontier mythology.\n\n\\boxed{Theodore Roosevelt}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 169}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:08:22.658102+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000131, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1664", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A ruler of this dynasty whose lineage was questioned took out his sword, shouted \"here is my pedigree!,\" and threw gold coins into a crowd; that ruler of this dynasty commissioned scientists to invent the world's first fountain pen.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clues match the Fatimid dynasty in 10th-century North Africa/Egypt. The ruler in question is the caliph al-Mu\u02bfizz li-D\u012bn All\u0101h, who quelled doubts about his claimed descent from F\u0101\u1e6dima by brandishing his sword (\u201cHere is my pedigree!\u201d) and scattering gold coins; the same caliph ordered the construction of the first reservoir-pen (an early fountain pen) that would not leak. No other Islamic dynasty fits both anecdotes simultaneously.\n\n\\boxed{Fatimid (dyn./caliphate)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 225, "output_tokens": 110, "total_tokens": 335}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00055625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_167", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Washington Post claimed that Barack Obama's head of this agency considered resigning because \"there are days where I have literally nothing to do.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question is a reference to a 2012 Washington Post profile of the director of the Selective Service System (the agency responsible for maintaining records of potential military draftees). Because there has been no active draft since 1973, the director at the time reported having essentially no day-to-day responsibilities, prompting the quoted remark about considering resignation. This matches the clue exactly; no other Obama-era agency fits the description.\n\n\\boxed{Selective Service System}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 207, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 298}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00048625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1684", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A city that fought to protect these people built a trebuchet that squared off against a machine called the \"cat,\" inspiring a work by Raimon Escrivan (\"rye-MOAN\" ess-kree-VAHN) in which the two siege engines engage in a mock debate.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a historical episode from the Albigensian Crusade. Toulouse, a center of Cathar (\u201cAlbigensian\u201d) sympathy, deployed a large trebuchet against Simon de Montfort\u2019s siege engine nicknamed \u201cLa Cat\u201d; the ensuing duel inspired Raimon Escrivan\u2019s sirventes in which the two machines debate in verse. The people therefore being protected are the Cathars.\n\n\\boxed{Cathars (Albigensians)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 238, "output_tokens": 90, "total_tokens": 328}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005225, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1689", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The U.S. negotiated a treaty with this tribe to allow the construction of a mail route that was called, like a more northerly route, the Federal Road.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The U.S. negotiated a treaty with the Creek Nation to allow the construction of a mail route known as the Federal Road. This road facilitated communication and travel through Creek territory and was similar to another Federal Road further north. \n\n\\boxed{Creek}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 145}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1803e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1696", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: At a beauty pageant in this city that was held in a basement, a group of women li ed up a banner that read \"don't let them kill us!\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes a secret (and thus illegal) beauty pageant staged in a basement during Iran's 2022\u20132023 protest wave; participants unfurled the banner in question to highlight the regime's lethal crackdowns on women. That event took place in the Iranian capital.  \n\nThus the city referenced by the clue is Tehran.\n\n\\boxed{Tehran}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 212, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 283}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004425, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1709", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: During the papacy of Paul III, the ancient tomb of this Roman's daughter was discovered to contain a well-preserved body and a still-burning lamp.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Roman in question is Marcus Tullius Cicero, whose daughter, Tullia, was said to have been found in a tomb on the Appian Way during the pontificate of Paul III. Legend claims that her body was perfectly preserved and that a lamp had been burning inside the tomb for over 1,500 years.\n\n\\boxed{Cicero}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 86, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 159}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:08:18.400375+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000131, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_171", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A writer from this present-day country was said to have created \"the strongest narcotic\" of his century by saying that history should be written \"as what actually happened.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The writer referred to is Leopold von Ranke, a German historian who famously advocated for history to be written *wie es eigentlich gewesen* (\"as it actually happened\"). This methodological approach became the foundation of modern professional historiography.\n\n\\boxed{Germany}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 88, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 139}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:08:20.778358+00:00"}, "cost": 9.85e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1721", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a speech given in the year of this election, a woman recounted getting beaten in the Montgomery County jail and said \"I question America.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The speech referencing being beaten in Montgomery County jail and saying \"I question America\" was delivered by Fannie Lou Hamer at the 1964 Democratic National Convention. This powerful testimony highlighted the violence and discrimination faced by Black Americans during the civil rights movement. The election year in question is 1964.\n\n\\boxed{1964}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 161}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3577e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1736", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This leader faced scandal when his mistress, B-movie actress Dovie Beams, played their sex tape during a press conference.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The leader in question is Ferdinand Marcos, the former President of the Philippines. The scandal involving his mistress, Dovie Beams, became public when she played a recording of their intimate encounter during a press event. This incident contributed to the growing controversy surrounding his regime.\n\n\\boxed{Ferdinand Marcos}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 147}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2234999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1740", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: During World War I, Hog Island became the largest center for this industry in the world.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "During World War I, Hog Island, located near Philadelphia, was developed as a major shipbuilding site to support the war effort. It became the largest shipbuilding center in the world at the time, focused on constructing cargo ships to transport troops and supplies. The industry in question is shipbuilding.\n\n\\boxed{shipbuilding}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 77, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 143}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2067e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_179", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Thomas Espenshade described the use of the \"repeated trials model\" in this area, which was analyzed as an example of how \"low intensity conflict\" doctrine \"comes home\" in a book on it by Timothy Dunn.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clues point to a specific academic/policy topic: Espenshade modeled the probability of eventual successful entry as a series of independent crossing attempts (the \u201crepeated trials\u201d/geometric distribution), while Dunn\u2019s monograph explicitly treats the same setting as the domestic application of low-intensity conflict doctrine. Both authors focus on the same concrete domain\u2014the enforcement regime along the southern boundary\u2014so the referent of \u201cthis area\u201d is the U.S.\u2013Mexico border (or, equivalently, U.S. Border Patrol operations there).\n\nThus the most concise and commonly accepted answer is the U.S.\u2013Mexico border.\n\n\\boxed{US-Mexico border (patrol/enforcement)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 225, "output_tokens": 129, "total_tokens": 354}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00060375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1797", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Minnesota Congressman John T. Bernard cast the only dissenting vote against a law banning US intervention in this conflict.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "John T. Bernard cast the only dissenting vote against the Neutrality Act of 1937, which aimed to prevent U.S. intervention in foreign conflicts, particularly the Spanish Civil War. His opposition was based on his belief that the U.S. should support the Spanish Republic against fascist-backed forces. The conflict in question is the Spanish Civil War.\n\n\\boxed{Spanish Civil War}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 81, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 161}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3751e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1804", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One of these events came as a surprise to noblemen who fought against supporters of the Constitution of May 3rd.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Constitution of May 3 (1791) was Poland\u2019s response to the First Partition; its defenders fought (and lost) the 1792 Polish\u2013Russian War against the Targowica Confederation. The victorious confederates expected the restoration of the old noble \u201cGolden Freedoms,\u201d but Russia and Prussia instead imposed the Second Partition (1793), which they had not anticipated. Hence the event that \u201ccame as a surprise\u201d is the Second Partition of Poland.\n\n\\boxed{2nd Partition of Poland (1793)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 204, "output_tokens": 106, "total_tokens": 310}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00052, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1828", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Despite having a court order, Autherine Lucy was kicked out of this place.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Autherine Lucy was admitted to the University of Alabama under a court order in 1956, becoming the first African American student to attend the school. Despite the court order, she was expelled shortly after due to \"safety concerns\" amid violent protests. The correct answer is the University of Alabama.\n\n\\boxed{University of Alabama}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 76, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 146}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2396000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_183", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Nowell Myres's archaeological investigations of this kingdom's origins concluded that it was settled from the north, using Nennius's accounts to establish a rough date range.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue pertains to early Anglo-Saxon settlement in Britain. Nennius\u2019s Historia Brittonum records that Hengest dispatched Octha northward to fight the Picts, thereby supplying a mid-fifth-century terminus post quem. J. N. L. Myres\u2019s ceramic and cemetery studies showed that the material culture of the Anglian kingdom of Lindsey (centered on Lincoln) arrived via the Humber rather than by direct North Sea landings, confirming a northern origin for its settlers.\n\nThus the kingdom in question is Lindsey.\n\n\\boxed{Lindsey}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 213, "output_tokens": 106, "total_tokens": 319}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00053125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1836", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to tradition, a \u70a4re in this city that fused metal statues together originated its namesake high-quality bronze.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "According to tradition, the city of Corinth is said to have acquired its namesake \"Corinthian bronze\" after a fire melted various metals together during the city's destruction by the Romans. This alloy was highly prized in antiquity for its unique color and durability.\n\n\\boxed{Corinth}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 78, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 137}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:08:17.581711+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000108, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1859", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In this city, a democratic government under Giuseppe Galletti won popularity by abolishing the macinato tax.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue refers to events in the Papal States during the 1848\u201349 revolutions. After Pius IX fled Rome, a short-lived constitutional regime operated under Prime Minister Giuseppe Galletti; one of its first popular measures was the repeal of the macinato (milling tax). That regime was seated in Rome, which therefore satisfies the phrasing \u201cin this city.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{Rome}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 201, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 279}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00044625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1871", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Samuel Eliot Morison's history of this document argued that Article III, which provided tax support for \"Protestant teachers of piety,\" slipped through without a valid two-thirds vote.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question describes a specific provision (Article III) related to tax support for Protestant religious instructors, which is a distinctive feature of the 1780 Massachusetts Constitution (drafted primarily by John Adams). Historian Samuel Eliot Morison's writings on Massachusetts, including his analysis of the constitutional convention and ratification process, explicitly noted procedural irregularities with that article's two-thirds vote requirement. No other foundational American document (e.g., the U.S. Constitution, Articles of Confederation, or other state constitutions) matches this combination of details.\n\n\\boxed{Mass. Const. (1780)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 215, "output_tokens": 114, "total_tokens": 329}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00055375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_1894", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A speech given about this personal attribute cites how \"Fuentes and McCafiferty\" died side by side with \"Bowie and Crockett\" at the Alamo.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query refers to a famous 1988 Democratic National Convention keynote address (by Texas Governor Ann Richards) that explicitly invokes the cited Alamo defenders as an illustration of the single personal quality they all shared. The surrounding rhetorical context makes clear that the attribute being praised is courage (or bravery), not ethnicity, nationality, or any other trait. This is the only reading that fits both the wording of the question and the historical speech.\n\n\\boxed{courage (bravery)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 215, "output_tokens": 94, "total_tokens": 309}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00050375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_200", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: It's not Babylon, but by the false account in Walter Raleigh's History of the World, this city was called Campsor before it was rebuilt by its founder, an opponent of the Bactrian king Zoroaster and husband of the warrior queen Semiramis.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The city referred to is Nineveh. According to the apocryphal account in Walter Raleigh's *History of the World*, it was once called Campsor and was rebuilt by its founder, Nimrod, who opposed the Bactrian king Zoroaster and was associated with the legendary queen Semiramis. This identification aligns with mythological and pseudo-historical traditions of the time.\n\n\\boxed{Nineveh}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 202}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6893999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_230", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This leader let filmmaker Barbet Schroeder record his cabinet's daily proceedings for a documentary subtitled \"A Self Portrait.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The leader who allowed filmmaker Barbet Schroeder to document his cabinet's daily proceedings in a film subtitled \"A Self Portrait\" was Iranian Prime Minister Amir-Abbas Hoveyda.\n\nThe resulting documentary, \"General Idi Amin Dada: A Self Portrait,\" however, features Ugandan dictator Idi Amin, not Hoveyda\u2014Schroeder gained Amin's cooperation to film his regime.\n\nThus, the correct answer is Idi Amin.\n\n\\boxed{Idi Amin}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 83, "output_tokens": 105, "total_tokens": 188}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6393e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_233", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The composition of these items was regulated by the 1906 Berne Convention.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The 1906 Berne Convention (specifically the International Convention for the Unification of Certain Rules with Respect to Assistance and Salvage at Sea) did not regulate the composition of items. It is likely you are referring to the **1906 Berne Convention on the Prohibition of White Phosphorus in Matches**, which regulated the chemical composition of matchsticks to prevent occupational diseases.\n\n\\boxed{Matches}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 72, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 155}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:08:17.306316+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0001425, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_245", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The \"Hjortspring\" (\"YOTE-spring\") example of these objects is similar to many Bronze Age petroglyphs.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The \"Hjortspring\" boat is an example of a prehistoric Nordic canoe, similar in form to boats depicted in many Bronze Age petroglyphs. These rock carvings often show vessels used in rituals or warfare, matching the Hjortspring find. The correct answer is a type of ancient boat.\n\n\\boxed{boat}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3277000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_262", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This country was dominated for more than a century by the True Whig Party, which once infamously \"won\" an election with fifteen times more votes than eligible voters.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The country described is Liberia, where the True Whig Party maintained political dominance for over a century. The party's control included fraudulent elections, such as one in which votes far exceeded the number of eligible voters. This occurred in the early 20th century, highlighting the lack of democratic integrity during that period.\n\n\\boxed{Liberia}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3774e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_264", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The deadliest building collapse in the United States before the collapse of the Twin Towers occurred in one of these buildings when a walkway collapsed onto a crowded dance floor.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The deadliest building collapse in the U.S. before the Twin Towers was the 1981 collapse of the Hyatt Regency walkway in Kansas City, Missouri. The disaster occurred when two overhead walkways collapsed onto a crowded atrium dance floor, killing 114 people. \n\n\\boxed{Hyatt Regency}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 160}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3361000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_28", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An essay by Gerald Berreman analyzes this institution's conflicts with pushes for \"community development.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The essay by Gerald Berreman analyzes the caste system's conflicts with efforts toward \"community development\" in India. Berreman highlights how social stratification and inequality inherent in the caste system hinder inclusive development. The correct answer is the caste system.\n\n\\boxed{caste system}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 78, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 135}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1238e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_293", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A few months before the outbreak of this war, John Slidell was sent on a diplomatic mission to its eventual losers, who rebuffed him.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "John Slidell was sent by the United States to Mexico in 1845 to negotiate a settlement regarding the annexation of Texas and the border dispute, but the Mexican government refused to receive him. This diplomatic failure served as a primary catalyst for the outbreak of the Mexican-American War.\n\n\\boxed{Mexican-American War}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 152}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:08:20.863178+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000123, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_34", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An uprising sparked by poor policy responses to this event involved the first use of a tricolor flag whose central white color represent religious reconciliation between two other colors.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The described tricolor (green-white-orange) matches the modern Irish flag, whose central white stripe was explicitly adopted to symbolize peace/reconciliation between Catholic (green) and Protestant (orange) populations. That flag made its first public appearance during the Young Irelander Rebellion of 1848. The rebellion itself was a direct reaction to the British government\u2019s inadequate relief measures during the Irish Potato Famine of 1845\u201349.\n\nThus the event referenced in the query is the Irish Potato Famine.\n\n\\boxed{Irish Potato Famine (1845-49)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 211, "output_tokens": 112, "total_tokens": 323}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00054375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_370", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A philandering king belonging to this royal house was married to the Polish Marie Leszczynska, who was the longest-serving queen of her country.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The king described is Louis XV of France, who belonged to the House of Bourbon. Marie Leszczynska was his wife and holds the record as the longest-serving queen consort in French history.\n\n\\boxed{House of Bourbon}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 132}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:08:16.648896+00:00"}, "cost": 9.3e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_391", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: After the final defeat in the Sepoy Mutiny, the last Mughal emperor, Bahadur Shah II, was exiled to this country.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "After the final defeat in the Sepoy Mutiny, the last Mughal emperor, Bahadur Shah II, was exiled to Rangoon, which was in British-controlled Burma (now Myanmar). At the time, Burma was a British colony, making it the destination of his exile. \n\n\\boxed{Burma}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.319e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_404", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a paper with Christos Papadimitriou, this man came up with an algorithm for pancake sorting that was the fastest such algorithm for thirty years.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The man referred to is Bill Gates. In 1979, Bill Gates co-authored a paper with Christos Papadimitriou on pancake sorting, presenting an algorithm that held the record for the fastest solution for decades. \n\n\\boxed{Bill Gates}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 148}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2132e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_416", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Richard Russell led a Senate committee investigating whether a major career setback for this man was constitutional.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Richard Russell led the Senate Armed Services Committee during the 1951 hearings investigating the firing of General Douglas MacArthur by President Harry S. Truman. The committee examined the constitutional authority of the President to relieve a military commander of his duties during the Korean War.\n\n\\boxed{Douglas MacArthur}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 71, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 130}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:08:21.380132+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00010625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_433", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Gatow disaster exacerbated tensions prior to this event.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Gatow air disaster (April 1948) was a mid-air collision between British and Soviet aircraft that sharply raised East-West tensions in occupied Berlin. This directly preceded and helped precipitate the Soviet imposition of the Berlin Blockade two months later. The clue therefore points to the Berlin Blockade (or, less precisely, the ensuing Berlin Airlift) as the event in question.\n\n\\boxed{Berlin Blockade (1948)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 191, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 279}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00045875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_44", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Ken Light sued Richard Taylor over his performance of this action, which led voters to associate John Kerry with Jane Fonda during the 2004 presidential election.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes a notorious 2004 election dirty trick in which a photograph of John Kerry sharing a stage with Jane Fonda was fabricated and widely circulated. The original image had been taken decades earlier by photojournalist Ken Light; graphic artist Richard Taylor was later sued by Light for digitally inserting Kerry into it. That manipulation is the action referred to, universally known as photoshopping.\n\n\\boxed{photoshopping (Kerry/Fonda photo)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 211, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 300}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00048625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_470", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One of the highest-ranking positions in this party, Gauleiter, commanded an entire regional branch of it.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Gauleiter was a high-ranking position in the Nazi Party, responsible for leading a regional division known as a Gau. This role was integral to the party's organizational structure in Nazi Germany. The correct answer is the Nazi Party.\n\n\\boxed{Nazi Party}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 81, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 136}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1251e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_473", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: These laws severely limited the number of town hall meetings to one per year.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question is an identification prompt for a specific set of British parliamentary measures from 1774. Those measures (the Massachusetts Government Act in particular) explicitly capped town meetings at one annual session unless the royal governor granted prior approval. In standard U.S. history curricula the acts are collectively known as the Intolerable Acts (or, less commonly, the Coercive Acts).\n\nThus the most common and correct answer is the Intolerable Acts.\n\n\\boxed{Intolerable Acts (MA Govt Act)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 195, "output_tokens": 101, "total_tokens": 296}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00049625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_49", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An outside supporter of this cause, Frank Abney Hastings, encouraged its proponents to adopt steam technology.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The cause referred to is the Greek War of Independence. Frank Abney Hastings, a British Philhellene, supported the Greek revolutionaries and advocated for the use of steam-powered ships to modernize their naval efforts. The correct answer is the Greek War of Independence.\n\n\\boxed{Greek War of Independence}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 175}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4716e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_490", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This country gained the provinces of Kexholm and Ingria by the terms of the Treaty of Stolbovo.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The country that gained the provinces of Kexholm and Ingria by the Treaty of Stolbovo was Sweden. This treaty, signed in 1617, ended the Ingrian War between Sweden and Russia, significantly expanding Swedish territory in the Baltic region. Russia was forced to cede these territories, marking a major shift in regional power.\n\n\\boxed{Sweden}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 179}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5232e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_494", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: People in this country often clean their teeth with a short stick of wood called a mefakia, which serves as a natural toothbrush.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The country where people traditionally use a *mefakia* (often referred to as *miswak* or *siwak*) to clean their teeth is Ethiopia. This natural toothbrush is derived from the branches of specific trees and is widely used for its oral hygiene benefits.\n\n\\boxed{Ethiopia}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 81, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 142}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:08:16.440808+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00011175, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_504", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This man's son held a Christmas Day feast at Saalfeld where he began to consolidate a rebellion against his father.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue refers to a well-known episode from Salian dynasty history. In December 1104/1105 the future Henry V hosted a Christmas court at Saalfeld expressly to rally German princes for the deposition of his father, Emperor Henry IV; the ensuing civil war ended with Henry IV\u2019s forced abdication in 1105. No other medieval ruler matches both the location and the Christmas timing of the filial revolt.\n\nThus the person alluded to is Henry IV.\n\n\\boxed{Henry IV (HRE)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 203, "output_tokens": 103, "total_tokens": 306}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00051125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_52", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In an instance of this kind of political action, Kiyoshi Kuromiya spread a rumor that he would kill a dog in public, only to show a pamphlet reading \"Congratulations, you saved the life of a dog\" when thousands showed up.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The anecdote describes an attention-grabbing stunt in which a false rumor is deliberately circulated so that a large crowd assembles, only to be confronted with a political or satirical message. Such staged deceptions, intended to expose credulity or publicize a cause, are classically termed hoaxes. Kiyoshi Kuromiya, a Yippie-affiliated activist, repeatedly employed this tactic; the dog-saving pamphlet is simply one documented instance.\n\n\\boxed{hoax (Yippie media hoax)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 291, "output_tokens": 876, "total_tokens": 1167}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:41.944849+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00255375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_537", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Kenneth Westhues said this event was caused by \"workplace mobbing\" and disputed the conclusions of the Massengill Report.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given statement is a clue (in the style of a quizbowl tossup) identifying a specific real-world incident. Kenneth Westhues, a sociologist specializing in workplace mobbing, explicitly applied that framework to the Virginia Tech shootings and criticized the official Massengill Report for overlooking faculty mistreatment of the perpetrator. No other well-known incident matches both the Westhues attribution and the Massengill reference.\n\nThus the event in question is the Virginia Tech massacre.\n\n\\boxed{Virginia Tech massacre (2007)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 207, "output_tokens": 106, "total_tokens": 313}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00052375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_543", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This man's son, Peter, built a house over his father's childhood home, which was known as \"The Locusts.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes a specific piece of trivia about a well-known modern figure whose family home bore the distinctive name \u201cThe Locusts.\u201d Warren Buffett grew up in that house in Omaha; his son Peter later purchased the property and erected a new residence directly on the original foundation. No other prominent individual matches the combination of the son\u2019s name, the house name, and the act of building over the childhood site.\n\n\\boxed{Warren Buffett}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 204, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 292}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000475, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_576", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: During the 2008 running of this event, many objected to the use of Randwick Racecourse in Sydney.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue points to a recurring international event whose 2008 edition was staged in Sydney. Historical records confirm that World Youth Day 2008 culminated with a papal Mass at Randwick Racecourse; the choice of venue drew public objections from anti-gambling and secular groups. No other periodic event matches both the location and the documented controversy.\n\n\\boxed{World Youth Day (2008)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 203, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 281}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00044875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_579", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A character with this name is tasked by the Devil to plow 60 acres in half a day, but is helped by the Devil's daughter and his future wife, Lilith.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes a folkloric pact-with-the-devil episode in which the protagonist must complete an enormous agricultural task (plowing 60 acres in half a day). The Devil\u2019s own daughter secretly aids him and later becomes his bride; that daughter is explicitly named Lilith.  \n\nThe single character who consistently appears in European (chiefly German and Jewish-legenda) variants of this exact narrative is Faust.  \n\nThus the name required by the question is Faust.\n\n\\boxed{Faust}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 215, "output_tokens": 98, "total_tokens": 313}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00051375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_581", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 1950, Hilary Koprowski tested an early version of this thing at Letchworth Village.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Hilary Koprowski tested an early version of the polio vaccine at Letchworth Village in 1950. This was one of the first human trials of a live attenuated polio vaccine. The correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{polio vaccine}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 141}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1664e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_593", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A recent book about this man's \"Black Jesus\" notes the brief but powerful influence of Adam Clayton Powell Sr\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The \"Black Jesus\" reference and the mention of Adam Clayton Powell Sr. point to Adam Clayton Powell Jr., a prominent African American minister and politician. The book in question is likely discussing his legacy and influence, tying in his father's impact. The most common answer is Adam Clayton Powell Jr.\n\n\\boxed{Adam Clayton Powell Jr.}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 82, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 151}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2722e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_598", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This group's anthem was a song called \"Mury\" (MOO-rih), or \"Walls.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The anthem \"Mury\" (Walls) was associated with the Polish anti-communist movement, particularly popularized by the rock band Perfect. It became a symbol of resistance during the Solidarity movement in the 1980s. The group most commonly linked to this anthem in that context is Solidarity.\n\n\\boxed{Solidarity}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 83, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 153}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2893e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_612", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A company operating in the valley of the Kings River built a 62-mile structure to transport these things.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The company built a 62-mile aqueduct to transport water from the Kings River for agricultural and municipal use. This infrastructure project was part of early 20th-century efforts to support irrigation and development in California's Central Valley. \n\n\\boxed{water}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 81, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 135}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1151e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_618", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Jeanne Chall, a notable researcher of this ability, names a test for gauging it along with Edgar Dale.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Jeanne Chall and Edgar Dale are known for their work on readability, particularly the development of the Dale-Chall Readability Formula, which assesses how difficult a text is to understand. This formula evaluates text based on word familiarity and sentence length to determine reading ease. The ability in question is reading comprehension or readability.\n\n\\boxed{readability}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 83, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 153}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2893e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_622", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A presidential candidate in this year did a series of advertisements featuring him informally talking to former baseball player Joe Garagiola.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question refers to a notable U.S. presidential campaign ad series. These informal, conversational spots (sometimes called \u201cCoffee with Nixon\u201d) were produced for Richard Nixon\u2019s 1968 run and featured him chatting with former catcher and broadcaster Joe Garagiola. No other election year matches this specific advertising format.\n\n\\boxed{1968}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 204, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 271}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004225, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_638", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Most of the companies owned by Errett Lobban Cord were in this industry.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Most of the companies owned by Errett Lobban Cord were in the automotive industry. He was a prominent figure in American automobile manufacturing and transportation during the early 20th century, acquiring and leading several well-known car companies.\n\n\\boxed{automotive}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 75, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 128}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0625e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_657", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: After this man was given a cup worth fifty pounds at Peterborough Abbey, he refused to accept the gift unless his friend was given an equal gift.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The anecdote describes an act of loyalty between companions during an 11th-century episode at Peterborough Abbey. The only figure consistently linked to that location and that precise gesture (refusing a costly cup until an equal gift was given to his comrade) is the Anglo-Saxon outlaw Hereward. Later medieval sources that recount Hereward\u2019s career therefore identify him as the man in question.\n\n\\boxed{Hereward the Wake}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 209, "output_tokens": 82, "total_tokens": 291}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00046625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_658", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Adolph Ochs coined a slogan for a business that he owned in this industry, and moved its headquarters to Longacre Square.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Adolph Ochs was the publisher of The New York Times, which he moved to Longacre Square (later renamed Times Square). He coined the slogan \"All the News That's Fit to Print\" for the newspaper. The industry is newspaper publishing.\n\n\\boxed{newspaper}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 143}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1835000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_664", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 2009, a man in this country crashed his car into a parade in an attempt to hit a bus carrying the royal family.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The incident occurred in the Netherlands, where a man drove his car into a parade in 2009, targeting a bus carrying the royal family. This attack took place during the annual Queen's Day celebrations in Apeldoorn. The perpetrator crashed into the parade but failed to hit the royal bus, resulting in multiple casualties among bystanders.\n\n\\boxed{Netherlands}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 89, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3919e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_694", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A banned album in this country whose title translates as Keep the Gate Closed,\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue refers to a specific banned rock album from the communist era (under Enver Hoxha), whose Albanian title \"Mbyllye portat\" literally translates as \"Keep the Gate Closed.\" This makes Albania the only country that fits the phrasing \"in this country.\" No other nation has a documented case matching the translated title and banning incident.\n\n\\boxed{Albania}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 195, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 270}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00043125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_706", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The adjective baluch (bah-LOOCH) sometimes describes varieties of these objects made in response to Soviet and American interventions in Afghanistan.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue points to a specific class of woven textiles whose traditional patterns were altered by 20th-century conflict. Baluch (or Baluchi) weavers, working in the Afghanistan\u2013Pakistan border region, produced rugs whose field designs began to incorporate tanks, helicopters, rifles, and dates of Soviet or American incursions; these pieces are therefore called \u201cBaluch war rugs.\u201d Consequently the objects referenced are simply rugs (or carpets).\n\n\\boxed{rugs (war rugs)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 206, "output_tokens": 94, "total_tokens": 300}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004925, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_712", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The second president of this organization was a former comparative literature professor at Columbia University dismissed by school president Nicholas Murray Butler.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The organization referred to is the NAACP (National Association for the Advancement of Colored People). The second president was Joel Spingarn, a former professor of comparative literature at Columbia University, who was dismissed by Nicholas Murray Butler. \n\n\\boxed{NAACP}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 82, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 137}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1322e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_731", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Many buildings in this country incorporate the quote \"Boys, be ambitious!\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quote \"Boys, be ambitious!\" is famously associated with William S. Clark, an American educator who helped establish Sapporo Agricultural College in Japan. This phrase has since become iconic in Japanese culture, especially in Hokkaido. Many buildings in Japan, particularly in Sapporo, incorporate this quote.\n\n\\boxed{Japan}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 74, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 144}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2254e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_776", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This country's southernmost district of Inagua produces one million tons of salt annually for the Morton Salt company.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The country being referred to is the Bahamas. The southernmost district of Inagua is home to extensive salt ponds that produce about one million tons of salt annually, primarily for the Morton Salt company. This salt production is a major industry for the region.\n\n\\boxed{Bahamas}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 170}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4157999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_784", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A pope with this name opted to remain home after seeing a locust, which sounds similar to the Latin for \"stay in place.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes a historical anecdote in which a pope interpreted the appearance of a locust (Latin *locusta*) as a punning divine command \u201cloco sta\u201d (\u201cstay in the place\u201d) and therefore canceled a journey. That pope was Urban V, who consequently remained in Avignon rather than returning to Rome. Because the question asks for the papal name associated with the incident, the answer is Urban.\n\n\\boxed{Urban}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 269, "output_tokens": 1118, "total_tokens": 1387}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:46.767767+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00313125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_791", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 1900, Charles Morse unsuccessfully attempted to raise the price of this good after monopolizing it in New York City.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In 1900, Charles Morse attempted to corner the market on ice, which he had largely monopolized in New York City, by raising its price. His scheme involved controlling the supply of ice during a particularly hot summer, but it ultimately failed due to public outrage and intervention. The good was ice.\n\n\\boxed{ice}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 86, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 155}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3006e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_8", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Two rivers named for nearby deposits of this substance provide water to the former trade hub of Hotan.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The two rivers near Hotan are named after jade, as the region is historically famous for its jade deposits. These rivers, the White Jade River and the Black Jade River, carry jade fragments from nearby mountains. The substance is jade.\n\n\\boxed{jade}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 79, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 132}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0908999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_812", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Many historians believe that this event was exacerbated by the incompetence of Dr. Willard Bliss.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The event referred to is the assassination of President James A. Garfield. Many historians believe that Dr. Willard Bliss's improper medical treatment, including unsterile procedures, worsened Garfield's condition and ultimately led to his death. The correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{the assassination of James A. Garfield}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 77, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 143}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2067e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_864", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The man delivering this speech sarcastically asked \"Are fleets and armies necessary to a work of love and reconciliation?\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The man delivering this speech was Patrick Henry, and he said this during his \"Give Me Liberty or Give Me Death\" speech in 1775. He used sarcasm to question British intentions, implying that the presence of military forces contradicted any claim of peaceful reconciliation. The correct answer is Patrick Henry.\n\n\\boxed{Patrick Henry}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 81, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 151}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2750999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_882", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An archbishop of this city who presided over and was responsible for implementing the Council of Trent was named Charles Borromeo.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Council of Trent was a significant ecumenical council of the Catholic Church, and its implementation was overseen in part by Archbishop Charles Borromeo in the Archdiocese of Milan.\n\nAlthough the council was held in Trent (now Trento, Italy), Borromeo was the Archbishop of Milan and played a key role in enacting its reforms there.\n\n\\boxed{Milan}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 164}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3935e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_901", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: New York Times  TV critic Jack Gould criticized this person's \"lapse in judgment\" for appearing in a 1959 Good Luck Margarine commercial.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue refers to a specific 1959 TV commercial for Good Luck Margarine that drew public criticism from New York Times critic Jack Gould. The person in question was the respected poet, historian, and Lincoln biographer Carl Sandburg, whose appearance in the ad was viewed as an undignified \u201clapse in judgment.\u201d This matches the historical record of Gould\u2019s column and Sandburg\u2019s documented commercial work.\n\n\\boxed{Carl Sandburg}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 210, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 299}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000485, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_913", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This non-Greek city was briefly ruled by the Duke of Athens, Walter of Brienne. \"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The city is **Florence**, which was ruled by Walter of Brienne, Duke of Athens, during his brief and unpopular tenure as signore in 1342\u20131343. Although he held the title \"Duke of Athens\" due to his family's claims in Greece, he was a French nobleman who governed the Italian city-state.\n\n\\boxed{Florence}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 73, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 152}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:08:17.763662+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00013675, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_926", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A writer from this country wrote about the \"Tiger of the Plains\" in a work arguing for civilization over barbarism.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The \"Tiger of the Plains\" refers to a metaphor used by Domingo Faustino Sarmiento in his work *Facundo*, where he contrasts civilization and barbarism in 19th-century Argentina. Sarmiento, an Argentine writer and president, used the term to describe the violent, authoritarian caudillos who threatened societal progress. The country is Argentina.\n\n\\boxed{Argentina}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 82, "total_tokens": 166}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4164000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_928", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A violent advocate of this cause interpreted a tornado striking Kansas as God's approval for her first-ever protests in Kiowa in 1900.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue refers to Carry Nation (or Carrie A. Nation), whose first saloon-smashing raids occurred in Kiowa, Kansas, in 1900. She explicitly interpreted a tornado that struck Kansas earlier that year as divine endorsement for direct-action protests against alcohol. Her lifelong cause was therefore temperance (the organized movement that later produced national Prohibition).\n\n\\boxed{temperance (mov./Prohibition)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 207, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 287}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00045875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_933", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For this event, a line from \"The Song of the Bell\" was inscribed on a giant bell commissioned by Theodor Lewald.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a giant bell commissioned by German Olympic official Theodor Lewald and bearing an inscription drawn from Schiller\u2019s \u201cDas Lied von der Glocke.\u201d Lewald oversaw preparations for the 1936 Games; the bell in question was cast for the Berlin Olympic Stadium and carried the line \u201cFest steht und treu die Wacht, die Schwart\u201d together with the motto \u201cIch rufe die Jugend der Welt.\u201d No other event matches this precise combination of commissioner, poem, and artifact.\n\nThus the event is the 1936 Summer Olympics (Berlin).\n\n\\boxed{1936 Summer Olympics (Berlin)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 206, "output_tokens": 122, "total_tokens": 328}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_938", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: During this event, parties to the Southeast Mutual Protection Treaty agreed not to obey official decrees.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Southeast Mutual Protection agreement (or Mutual Protection of Southeast China) was negotiated in 1900 by southern Qing governors (notably Li Hongzhang, Liu Kunyi, and Zhang Zhidong) with foreign consuls. It explicitly repudiated the imperial edicts that had declared war on the powers and ordered the extermination of foreigners\u2014an action taken while the Qing court was under Boxer influence in Beijing. Those events collectively constitute the Boxer Rebellion (or Boxer Uprising).\n\n\\boxed{Boxer Rebellion (1900)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 260, "output_tokens": 434, "total_tokens": 694}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:39.435928+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00141, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_978", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: W. C. Handy wrote his first popular blues song for one of these organizations, which was rebuffed by GIs with dynamite charges in the 1946 Battle of Athens.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue refers to political machines (i.e., corrupt urban party organizations controlled by a boss). W. C. Handy\u2019s \u201cMemphis Blues\u201d (originally titled \u201cMr. Crump\u201d) was commissioned for Edward H. Crump\u2019s 1909 mayoral campaign in Memphis; Crump went on to dominate Tennessee politics for decades through exactly this kind of machine. The same Crump-backed machine in McMinn County, Tennessee, was forcibly ousted by returning GIs in the 1946 \u201cBattle of Athens,\u201d an armed confrontation that used dynamite to dislodge deputies barricaded in the county jail.\n\nThus the organizations in question are political machines.\n\n\\boxed{political machines (Crump machine)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 217, "output_tokens": 145, "total_tokens": 362}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00063375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_History_987", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This group's staples include the  kumara , a type of sweet potato.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The group referred to is the M\u0101ori people of New Zealand, who traditionally cultivated and relied on the kumara as a staple food. Kumara, a type of sweet potato, was brought to New Zealand by Polynesian ancestors of the M\u0101ori and has been central to their agriculture and diet for centuries. \n\n\\boxed{M\u0101ori}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 76, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 150}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2795999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_0", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The lines \"Rude, and ungrateful, though my country be,\" in Book 5 of this work alludes to Scipio Africanus as a reference to its author's multiple exiles.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted lines evoke an author's sense of mistreatment by an ungrateful homeland, a sentiment historically linked to Scipio Africanus (who withdrew into voluntary exile after political accusations in Rome). This motif aligns with the biography and poetic voice of Lu\u00eds de Cam\u00f5es, who endured repeated banishments and overseas postings. Consequently the work containing the lines in its fifth book is Cam\u00f5es\u2019s epic Os Lus\u00edadas (The Lusiads).\n\n\\boxed{The Lusiads (Cam\u00f5es)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 219, "output_tokens": 96, "total_tokens": 315}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00051375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1002", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Officials carrying out this European country's policies place an activist on trial in the novel  \n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue phrasing (\"this European country's policies\") is the standard lead-in format for quizbowl-style questions whose answer is a country. It points to Milan Kundera's *The Joke*, whose protagonist Ludvik is prosecuted for a politically incorrect postcard under Czechoslovakia's Stalin-era Communist regime. (Kafka's *The Trial* is ruled out because its setting is deliberately unnamed and the protagonist is not an activist.)\n\n\\boxed{Czechoslovakia}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 196, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 283}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1009", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a poem written in this modern country, the speaker declares \"make me, O Lord, Thy Spinning Wheel Complete\".\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The poem \"Huswifery\" was written by Edward Taylor, a colonial American poet who lived in what is now the United States. The speaker uses the metaphor of a spinning wheel to ask God to transform his soul into a vessel for divine grace.\n\n\\boxed{United States}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 78, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 134}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:18.786750+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0001035, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1015", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This work discusses a solution to the over-hunting of deer offered by a \"true Lover of his Country,\" but cites more approvingly the accounts of a \"very knowing American\" and \"famous Salmanaazor, a Native of the Island Formosa.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The work described is *A Modest Proposal* by Jonathan Swift, though the details mentioned are a misdirection; the essay actually addresses poverty and Irish oppression, not deer hunting. The references to \"Salmanaazor\" and a \"very knowing American\" parody pseudo-scholarly citations common in 18th-century tracts. However, the correct answer to the question, based on the satirical style and cited figures, is:\n\n\\boxed{A Modest Proposal}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 98, "total_tokens": 209}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.7681000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1016", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One poem in this collection exclaims, \"Eclaircise the myths Asiatic!\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted line is taken directly from the poem \"Passage to India,\" which first appeared in the 1871\u201372 expansion of Walt Whitman\u2019s lifelong poetic project. That project is universally known by the title Leaves of Grass, the only collection in which the poem (and therefore the line) appears.  \n\nThus the collection referenced by the question is Leaves of Grass.\n\n\\boxed{Leaves of Grass (Whitman)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 197, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 281}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00045625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1042", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: his character describes how Maurilians prefer visitors to praise postcards of their former scenery over their current, and how Eusapians pose their dead in an identical underground metropolis.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given description matches two specific fictional cities (Maurilia and Eusapia) from Italo Calvino's 1972 novel *Invisible Cities*, in which the character Marco Polo catalogs dozens of imagined locales to Kublai Khan. No other well-known literary work contains these precise vignettes about postcards of a former cityscape or an identical subterranean necropolis.  \n\nThus the question is answered by naming the novel (or its author).  \n\n\\boxed{Invisible Cities (Calvino)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 214, "output_tokens": 96, "total_tokens": 310}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005075, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1045", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A town described by this adjective contains the Weary Gentleman saloon, which is where a drummer and the barkeep discuss the possibility of \"some shootin' \u00c2\u2013 some good shootin'.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given quote matches a scene from Stephen Crane's short story \"The Bride Comes to Yellow Sky,\" which is set in a town of that name containing the Weary Gentleman saloon. The town's name is itself an adjectival phrase, so the adjective in question is the descriptor \"yellow.\" No other adjective is used to characterize the town in the story.\n\n\\boxed{yellow}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 218, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 294}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_105", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The protagonist of a novel in this genre entertains fellow passengers on a stalled train by describing frogs being hunted en masse to supply restaurants with legs.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes a specific embedded anecdote in William Gaddis\u2019s novel *JR* (1975). That novel is a canonical exemplar of postmodern fiction, whose hallmarks include lengthy digressive monologues, nested narratives, and a refusal of conventional linearity\u2014precisely the features that allow a stalled-train monologue about mass frog harvesting to appear. Hence the genre named by the clue is postmodernism (or postmodern fiction).\n\n\\boxed{postmodernism (fic./lit.)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 209, "output_tokens": 93, "total_tokens": 302}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00049375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1052", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Lord Howard helped secure this son of a tailor a seat in Parliament.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question is a historical clue identifying a British MP. Samuel Pepys\u2019s father was a London tailor, and Pepys himself sat in Parliament for Castle Rising (1673) and later Bramber. Contemporary records show that Lord Henry Howard (later 6th Duke of Norfolk) used his family interest to secure the Castle Rising seat for Pepys.\n\nThus the person referenced is Samuel Pepys.\n\n\\boxed{Samuel Pepys}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 194, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 281}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00046, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1055", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Jamaica Kincaid's  Lucy , the title character dreams of being trampled by this poem's subjects after being forced to recite it.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel *Lucy* (1990) draws repeatedly on postcolonial themes of imposed British cultural norms. Early in the narrative, the protagonist is made to memorize and recite Wordsworth\u2019s \u201cI Wandered Lonely as a Cloud,\u201d whose central image is a field of daffodils. She later recounts a nightmare in which those same daffodils trample her\u2014an oneiric reversal of the colonial authority the poem represents.\n\nThus the poem in question is Wordsworth\u2019s \u201cDaffodils.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{Daffodils (Wordsworth)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 208, "output_tokens": 110, "total_tokens": 318}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000535, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1067", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A form of one of these events in African-American tradition provides the title for Yaa Gyasi's (JAH-see's)  \n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue refers to Yaa Gyasi's 2016 debut novel whose title is a single word, \"Homegoing.\" In African-American tradition a \"homegoing\" (or home-going) service is a celebratory funeral rite marking the deceased's passage to the afterlife; therefore the category being defined by the clue is funerals.\n\n\\boxed{funerals (homegoings)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 207, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 283}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00044875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1069", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A character in this play boasts that he \"got the power of death\" after murdering a cat as a child when a priest failed to resurrect his dog.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The anecdote about acquiring the \"power of death\" by strangling a cat after a priest refused to pray for a dead dog is recounted by the defrocked minister Lawrence Shannon in Tennessee Williams's The Night of the Iguana. The speech occurs in Act 2 as Shannon explains the childhood origin of his loss of faith and his subsequent compulsive behavior. No other well-known play contains this specific episode or phrasing.\n\n\\boxed{The Night of the Iguana (Williams)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 211, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 306}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00050125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1071", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A \"poor chap\" who \"always loved larking\" suffers this fate in a Stevie Smith poem that notes \"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted phrases are taken directly from Stevie Smith\u2019s poem \u201cNot Waving but Drowning.\u201d In the poem the \u201cpoor chap\u201d who \u201calways loved larking\u201d is the drowned man whose frantic gestures were misread as playfulness; the title and refrain therefore supply the fate itself. The question is therefore a compact reference to that well-known title.\n\n\\boxed{not waving but drowning}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 203, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 282}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00045125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1073", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A theatrical director named Felix stars in Margaret Atwood's 2016 adaptation of this play,  Hag-Seed .\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question appears to be asking for the play that Margaret Atwood's *Hag-Seed* is an adaptation of. *Hag-Seed* is a modern retelling of William Shakespeare's *The Tempest*. Therefore, the correct answer is *The Tempest*.\n\n\\boxed{The Tempest}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 150}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2535e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1074", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Herbie Hancock played the piano on a \"rhapsody\" named after this character, which appears on an album named for him by Chick Corea.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue points to a 1978 Chick Corea jazz fusion album whose title and thematic inspiration derive from a well-known fictional character; that album contains the track \u201cRhapsody for ___.\u201d Corea\u2019s sideman list for the project includes Herbie Hancock on acoustic piano, confirming the personnel detail. The only character that satisfies every element of the clue is therefore the Mad Hatter.\n\n\\boxed{Mad Hatter}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 210, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 293}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00047, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_109", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a novel written in this format, mosquitoes die upon contact with the \"dumb-ox\" Yanzao due to the massive amounts of pesticides that he spreads around the village of Maqiao.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a specific novel whose structure consists of discrete, alphabetized entries (rather than conventional chapters) that define local terms, customs, and characters from the fictional village of Maqiao. That novel is Han Shaogong\u2019s *A Dictionary of Maqiao* (1996), whose protagonist-narrator records, among many other items, the pesticide-laden \u201cdumb-ox\u201d Yanzao. Consequently the format alluded to is a dictionary.\n\n\\boxed{dictionary}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 220, "output_tokens": 97, "total_tokens": 317}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005175, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1098", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The italicized ending of a poem about one of these places describes a youth who \"gain'd from Heav'n\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given clue is an excerpt from a quizbowl-style tossup on Thomas Gray's \"Elegy Written in a Country Church-Yard.\" Its final section (\"The Epitaph\") is conventionally printed in italics and contains the exact quoted line about the \"youth\" who \"gain'd from Heav'n \u2026 a friend.\" The poem's setting is therefore the category being defined.\n\n\\boxed{churchyards (graveyards)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 204, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 289}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004675, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1108", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In one passage, this process is caused by things like a starched napkin, a clattering spoon, and some uneven paving stones.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes several specific sensory triggers (starched napkin, clattering spoon, uneven paving stones) that appear in Marcel Proust's *In Search of Lost Time*. These are classic examples of the sudden, spontaneous recovery of long-forgotten memories that the narrator experiences, a phenomenon Proust explicitly labels *m\u00e9moire involontaire*. The process is therefore involuntary memory (distinct from both voluntary recollection and the more famous madeleine episode).\n\n\\boxed{involuntary memory (Proust)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 207, "output_tokens": 97, "total_tokens": 304}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00050125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1122", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Eliot Weinberger and Octavio Paz collaborated on a book titled for  19 Ways of Looking at  a poet from this country, analyzing translations of a poem that describes sunlight playing over green moss on a solitary mountain.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The poem described is \"A View of the Mountain Pass\" by Chinese poet Wang Wei, which has been translated and analyzed in various forms. Eliot Weinberger's book *19 Ways of Looking at Wang Wei* examines multiple translations of this poem, originally written in Chinese. The country referred to is China.\n\n\\boxed{China}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 175}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4425999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1127", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This author wondered in his poem \"The Solution\" whether it wouldn't be easier \"for the government /\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The author referred to is Bertolt Brecht, who wrote the poem \"The Solution\" (\"Die L\u00f6sung\" in German). In the poem, he ironically suggests that it might be easier for the government to dissolve the people and elect a new one. This satirical line critiques authoritarian responses to public dissent.\n\n\\boxed{Bertolt Brecht}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 80, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 152}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2879999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1128", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: After a writer from  Wallpaper  magazine described this language as \"one of the ugliest\" in the world, billionaire Johann Rupert pulled several ads in response.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The language in question is Afrikaans. Johann Rupert, a prominent South African businessman, withdrew advertising from Wallpaper magazine after it insulted Afrikaans by calling it \"one of the ugliest\" languages. This sparked national outrage in South Africa, leading to the ad boycott.\n\n\\boxed{Afrikaans}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 155}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2861000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1170", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In this novel, the protagonist's love interest and his boyhood crush Pribislav are linked by their \"Kirghiz eyes\" and by scenes in which they lend him pencils.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The description matches Thomas Mann's 1924 novel *The Magic Mountain* (Der Zauberberg). Its protagonist Hans Castorp is linked to both characters by the shared motif of \"Kirghiz eyes\" (narrow, Asiatic features) and by parallel pencil-lending episodes that carry erotic and symbolic weight. No other novel employs this precise combination of details.\n\n\\boxed{The Magic Mountain (Mann)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 217, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 297}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00047125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1172", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In one story, eight masqueraders dressed as these animals in costumes made of flax and tar are hoisted thirty feet upward by a chain affixed to a pulley and are burnt alive by a torch taken from a caryatid (CARE-yah-tid) .\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a specific scene from Edgar Allan Poe's short story \"Hop-Frog\" (1850). In it, the cruel king and his seven ministers (exactly eight masqueraders) are tricked into wearing highly flammable costumes of flax and tar to resemble orangutans; they are then suspended from a chain and pulley and set ablaze by a torch from a caryatid figure.  \n\nThus the animals referenced are orangutans (sometimes styled \"orang-outangs\" in period spelling).  \n\n\\boxed{orangutans (Hop-Frog)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 233, "output_tokens": 112, "total_tokens": 345}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00057125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1185", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: To visit one of these places, a count disguises himself as the ghost of a nun who was buried alive there.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query is a classic \"what are these X\" style clue (e.g., from quiz bowl, crosswords, or Jeopardy!), so the referent must be a class of locations that fits the described literary incident. The incident itself is a direct allusion to the plot of Matthew Lewis\u2019s gothic novel *The Monk*, in which a nobleman infiltrates a convent by impersonating the ghost of a nun who had been immured alive; the only category that satisfies both the scene and the phrasing \u201cone of these places\u201d is therefore convents (or nunneries).  \n\n\\boxed{convents (nunneries)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 204, "output_tokens": 127, "total_tokens": 331}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005725, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1189", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: character by this name is shown a photograph of a messenger practicing the high jump by the Bridge Inn's landlady.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a very specific scene from Franz Kafka's novel *The Castle*. In that work the Bridge Inn (Br\u00fcckenhof) landlady shows the protagonist a photograph of one of the Count's messengers practicing the high jump, evidently to illustrate the messenger's physical prowess and suitability for castle service. The only character who receives this demonstration is the land-surveyor known simply as K.\n\nThus the name required by the query is K.\n\n\\boxed{K}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 203, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 295}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00048375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1194", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This character's home is suggested to be the \"Great Good Place\" and has \"fairy-tale\" like qualities according to W. H. Auden's essay \"Brothers and Others,\" which argues that this woman appears in an \"Unpleasant Play.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The essay \"Brothers and Others\" (from Auden's *The Dyer's Hand*) analyzes *The Merchant of Venice*, treating Belmont as an idealized \"Great Good Place\" of fairy-tale harmony that contrasts with mercantile Venice. Auden explicitly labels the play \"unpleasant\" because of its unresolved tensions around justice, mercy, and Shylock, and he centers his discussion on the heroine who presides over Belmont. That heroine is therefore Portia.\n\n\\boxed{Portia}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 293, "output_tokens": 439, "total_tokens": 732}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:40.060325+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00146375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1195", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A popular conspiracy theory held by tax protesters is that some parties in court cases do not actually exist since they are identified exclusively through the use of this technique.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question pertains to a fringe legal theory (popular among \"sovereign citizens\" and tax protesters) holding that a court's use of stylized typography creates a fictitious corporate entity rather than referring to a natural person. This is the basis for the so-called \"strawman\" argument, in which only the all-caps version of a name is thought to appear in court filings, contracts, etc. Consequently, the technique in question is the rendering of names in all capital letters.\n\n\\boxed{ALL CAPS names (strawman theory)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 211, "output_tokens": 110, "total_tokens": 321}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00053875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_12", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a novel by this author, a character who thinks he has been poisoned when he is served locally-grown coffee is overthrown in a coup that anticipated a series of real-life coups in this author's home country later the same year.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a scene from Chinua Achebe\u2019s 1966 novel *A Man of the People*, whose corrupt politician Chief Nanga (and the government he serves) is suddenly removed by a military coup. The book appeared in January 1966; Nigeria experienced its first real coup later that month and a second in July, making the fictional event an eerie anticipation of actual history. No other author\u2013country\u2013novel combination matches the coffee-poisoning detail, the coup motif, and the precise chronology.\n\n\\boxed{Chinua Achebe}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 226, "output_tokens": 111, "total_tokens": 337}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00056, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1203", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Seven brothers with this last name all fought at Edgehill, and one of them, John, surrendered Chester to the Parliamentarians.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The seven brothers who fought at the Battle of Edgehill were members of the **Byron** family, and Sir John Byron was the governor who surrendered Chester to Parliament in 1646. The family was famously loyal to the Royalist cause during the English Civil War.\n\n\\boxed{Byron}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 79, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 142}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:14.465691+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00011425, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1204", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One character in this novel skips school every Thursday by wearing an eyepatch and pretending he has to go to the ophthalmologist.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The described behavior matches a specific detail about the character Francis Abernathy in Donna Tartt's 1992 novel. Francis routinely fabricates ophthalmology appointments (complete with an eyepatch) to avoid Thursday classes while concealing other activities from his classmates. No other widely read novel contains this precise recurring ruse, confirming the identification.\n\n\\boxed{The Secret History (Tartt)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 206, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 282}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004475, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1205", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A scene involving one of these objects concludes with the image of a candle used to read a book filled with \"grief and evil\" flaring up then going out forever.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes a literary/filmic scene whose central prop is a sealed, transparent sphere containing a miniature wintry scene; when the sphere is dropped or overturned at the moment of a character's death, the swirling flakes visually echo the extinguishing of the candle that had illuminated a volume explicitly labeled as containing \u201cgrief and evil.\u201d  \n\nThis combination of imagery (miniature weather, sudden darkness, mortality) is classically realized by the snow-globe that falls from Charles Foster Kane\u2019s hand in the opening of Citizen Kane, a motif later echoed in other works that likewise pair the object with a dying reader.  \n\nHence the referent of \u201cthese objects\u201d is snow globes.\n\n\\boxed{snow globes}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 215, "output_tokens": 142, "total_tokens": 357}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00062375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1210", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a poem by this author that opposes the palindromic terms amor and Roma, Tarpeia begs for a retributive \"Rape of the Roman Women.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a specific elegy (Propertius 4.4) whose central conceit is the anagrammatic opposition of *amor* and *Roma*. In that poem Tarpeia, having betrayed the city for love of the Sabine king Tatius, explicitly calls for a retaliatory \u201crape of the Roman women\u201d that would invert the earlier Sabine episode. No other ancient poet treats the Tarpeia myth in precisely these terms.\n\nThus the author in question is Propertius.\n\n\\boxed{Propertius}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 213, "output_tokens": 104, "total_tokens": 317}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00052625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1215", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Margaret Ezell challenged the historical assumptions perpetuated by this character's story in her essay on \"The Myth of [this character].\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Margaret Ezell is a historian of early modern women's writing whose scholarship frequently critiques anachronistic or overly schematic narratives of literary history. One of her best-known interventions is the 1990 essay \"The Myth of Judith Shakespeare,\" which directly attacks the influential parable Virginia Woolf invented in *A Room of One's Own*. Ezell shows how Woolf's tragic fiction of Shakespeare's gifted but doomed sister had been taken as empirical fact by later feminist critics, thereby distorting the actual archival record of women's literary production.\n\nThe character in question is therefore Judith Shakespeare.\n\n\\boxed{Judith Shakespeare}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 205, "output_tokens": 116, "total_tokens": 321}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00054625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1225", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a poem set at this location, the speaker hears \"peals of distant ironical laughter at every word I have written\" and describes himself as \"ba  led, balk'd, bent to the very earth\" in his awareness that \"before all my arrogant poems the real Me stands yet untouch'd, untold, altogether unreach'd.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted lines are taken verbatim from Walt Whitman\u2019s \u201cAs I Ebb\u2019d with the Ocean of Life\u201d (1860). That poem is explicitly situated \u201cat the shores of Paumanok,\u201d Whitman\u2019s recurrent name for Long Island; the speaker addresses the surf, the wind, and the \u201cfish-shaped\u201d island itself while confronting the gap between his written poems and the \u201creal Me.\u201d Consequently the location demanded by the question is Paumanok.\n\n\\boxed{Paumanok (LI shore)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 250, "output_tokens": 100, "total_tokens": 350}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1228", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: At the conclusion of a book by this author, the protagonist receives her diamond engagement ring back from her captors, whose other gi t to her was the 9 millimeter bullet they didn't shoot her with.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes the ending of the 1995 thriller novel *Kiss the Girls*. In it, the surviving victim Kate receives her engagement ring back from the escaped serial killer (along with his parting remark that the bullet he did not fire at her was his other \u201cgift\u201d).  \n\nThe novel belongs to James Patterson\u2019s Alex Cross series, making him the author referenced by the question.  \n\nNo other well-known work matches the precise combination of details (female protagonist, returned diamond ring, spared 9 mm bullet).  \n\n\\boxed{James Patterson}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 283, "output_tokens": 1136, "total_tokens": 1419}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:47.073591+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00319375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_123", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A book by this author discusses the spiritual activism of Mildred Lisette Norman, or Peace Pilgrim, in a chapter on taking a pilgrimage to the Santuario de Chimay\u00f3 (\"san-too-AH-ree-oh de chee-mah-YO\") in New Mexico.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes a specific chapter in Rebecca Solnit's 2000 book *Wanderlust: A History of Walking*, which covers the annual pilgrimage to the Santuario de Chimay\u00f3 and uses that setting to discuss the life and nonviolent activism of Peace Pilgrim (Mildred Norman). No other prominent author matches this precise combination of subject, location, and textual reference.  \n\nThus the author in question is Rebecca Solnit.\n\n\\boxed{Rebecca Solnit}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 234, "output_tokens": 94, "total_tokens": 328}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005275, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1235", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This character addresses the \"dark Hindoo half of nature\" as he watches an animal turn to \"seek intercedings with yon all-quickening sun\" before it dies.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted language is taken directly from Herman Melville\u2019s *Moby-Dick* (chapter 118, \u201cThe Quadrant\u201d). In that scene Captain Ahab, standing on the deck, watches a harpooned whale roll toward the sun in its death throes and apostrophizes the \u201cdark Hindoo half of nature,\u201d thereby revealing both his Promethean defiance and his awareness of cosmic duality. No other character in the novel (or in any other well-known work containing similar imagery) speaks these lines.\n\n\\boxed{Capt. Ahab (Moby-Dick)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 216, "output_tokens": 116, "total_tokens": 332}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00056, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1239", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This food, which pejoratively gave its name to Taiwan's millennial generation, was reclaimed as a badge of honor a ter a 2008 student protest.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The 2008 Wild Strawberry Student Movement protested restrictions on freedom of assembly and explicitly adopted the \u201cstrawberry\u201d label that had been used to disparage Taiwan\u2019s millennials (seen as fragile like the fruit). By turning the epithet into the name of their movement, participants reclaimed it as a positive symbol of youthful activism. Consequently, the food referenced in the clue is the strawberry.\n\n\\boxed{strawberry (gen./movement)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 212, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 301}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1241", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The poem \"To Return to the Trees\" concludes with the image of an \"obdurate almond going under the sand with [one of these things], slowly, by sand grains, by centuries.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted line is the final image of a poem (likely by a modern Arabic poet such as Adonis or Saadi Youssef) that depicts gradual desert burial over geological time. The only noun that completes the line both literally and symbolically\u2014an obdurate almond sinking grain by grain while its dark silhouette is likewise effaced\u2014is \u201cits shadow.\u201d  \n\nThus the completed phrase is the single, most common poetic solution.\n\n\\boxed{its shadow}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 220, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 309}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004975, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1250", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: David Wilbern wrote a psychoanalytic essay on Shakespeare's usage of this word 3ttingly entitled \"Shakespeare's [this word].\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The word is \"Nothing,\" as David Wilbern's influential 1978 essay is titled \"Shakespeare's Nothing.\" This psychoanalytic study explores the recurring motif of \"nothing\" throughout Shakespeare's plays, particularly in relation to gender and sexuality.\n\n\\boxed{Nothing}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 82, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 141}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:18.581528+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000109, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1253", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This poem's author punned on the word for \"meaning\" by adding an extra n to the last word of the phrase \"unser dunkeles Sinngru\u0308n\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given clue describes a distinctive German neologism that puns on \u201cSinn\u201d (meaning) by fusing an extra \u201cn\u201d into the compound \u201cSinngr\u00fcn,\u201d thereby evoking both semantic depth and the evergreen plant name. That exact formation appears at the close of Paul Celan\u2019s 1958 poem \u201cEngf\u00fchrung,\u201d whose final lines read \u201cunser / dunkeles / Sinngr\u00fcn.\u201d No other well-known German-language poem employs this orthographic pun in precisely the cited phrase.\n\nThus the poem whose author is alluded to is \u201cEngf\u00fchrung.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{Engf\u00fchrung (Celan)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 216, "output_tokens": 127, "total_tokens": 343}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1263", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a poem, one of these animals \"believes we may long for one more dream...before we come home to our strange bodies and rise from the dead.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given quote is a clue pointing to a specific animal (or category of animals) featured in a poem. The phrasing around \"strange bodies\" and \"rise from the dead\" is a clear allusion to metamorphosis after a long dormancy, which aligns with cicadas (nymphs emerging as winged adults after 13\u201317 years underground). This fits far better than alternatives such as dogs, butterflies, or mythical creatures.\n\n\\boxed{cicadas}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 213, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 305}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00049625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_127", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The protagonist of a novel by this author is too absorbed in thinking about how Keats felt being spurned by Wordsworth to notice that assassins enter the restaurant he's in and gun down a man at the next table.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes a highly specific scene of literary obsession causing a character to miss a nearby gangland-style killing, which is a signature element of Aleksandar Hemon\u2019s autofictional style. In the novel *Nowhere Man*, the protagonist Pronek is lost in a digression on Keats\u2019s hurt feelings at being slighted by Wordsworth and therefore fails to register the assassins entering the restaurant. No other contemporary author matches both the precise Romantic-era anecdote and the unnoticed shooting.\n\n\\boxed{Aleksandar Hemon}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 284, "output_tokens": 1547, "total_tokens": 1831}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:53.217228+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0042225, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1281", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This author described traveling around London with a companion app programmed with W. G. Sebald's personality in an account of the Olympics for Grantland.com, \"Hard Times in the Uncanny Valley.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The author who wrote the Grantland article \"Hard Times in the Uncanny Valley\" is Brian Phillips. In the piece, he recounts his experiences navigating London during the 2012 Olympics while using a digital companion modeled after the German writer W. G. Sebald.\n\n\\boxed{Brian Phillips}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:21.197810+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00011825, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1283", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This poem's speaker calls on an \"old lecher with a love on every wind\" who has \"reckoned up every unforeknown, unseeing plunge...into the labyrinth of another's being.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted phrases are spoken by the aging poet-persona of W. B. Yeats\u2019s \u201cThe Tower\u201d (1928). In the poem\u2019s second section the speaker explicitly names himself \u201can old lecher with a love on every wind\u201d and then describes the erotic and imaginative risks he has taken as \u201cevery unforeknown, unseeing plunge \u2026 into the labyrinth of another\u2019s being.\u201d  \n\nThus the only poem that matches both the diction and the dramatic situation is Yeats\u2019s \u201cThe Tower.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{The Tower (Yeats)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 219, "output_tokens": 107, "total_tokens": 326}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00054125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1306", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A bureaucrat from this country forges a manuscript about a 17th-century timekeeper to justify the title government agency in the satirical novel  \n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes a plot element from a satirical novel whose title refers to a government agency (a \"ministry\"). The key details\u2014a forged 17th-century manuscript concerning a chronometer or clock\u2014point directly to the Czech novel *The Ministry of Time* (2014) by Hany Rashid. Its protagonist is a Czech bureaucrat, so the country referenced by the clue is the Czech Republic (or Czechia).\n\n\\boxed{Czech Republic}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 209, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 300}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00048875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1307", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This essay argues that from the perspective of the intellect, sin has no essence, but is \"diminution or  less ,\" whereas the conscience feels sin \"as essence,\" viewing it as \"pravity or  bad .\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given text is a partial quotation (with two obvious blanks) describing a philosophical distinction between intellectual and moral views of sin. The first blank must be completed by the noun \"evil\" to yield the standard phrase \"diminution or less evil\"; the second blank must be completed by the suffix \"ness\" to yield the matching noun \"badness.\"  \n\nTogether the restored sentence is a recognizable paraphrase of a passage that appears in several 19th-century theological essays (most often attributed to Coleridge or Kierkegaard).  \n\nThus the single, most common answer expected by the prompt is the pair of missing words.\n\n\\boxed{evil; ness}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 225, "output_tokens": 129, "total_tokens": 354}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00060375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1309", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In an essay by Sigmund Freud, this state is characterized by a cleavage between the critical ego and the ego altered by identification, which is caused by the withdrawing of free libido from an object into the ego.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The state described in the question refers to melancholia, where Freud explains the internal conflict resulting from the loss of a loved object and the subsequent identification with it, leading to self-reproach and depression. The withdrawal of libido from the object into the ego causes a split between the critical agency (superego) and the degraded self-representation. This process is central to Freud's essay \"Mourning and Melancholia.\"\n\n\\boxed{melancholia}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 122, "output_tokens": 118, "total_tokens": 240}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.0461999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1314", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A famous dramatist and translator of this language advocated its classical forms in the \"Epistle on Poetry.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question requires identifying a language based on a historical literary reference. The phrasing points to neoclassical advocacy via an \"Epistle on Poetry,\" which matches the two epistles written by Russian dramatist/translator Alexander Sumarokov (one on poetry, one on language) to promote classical Russian forms. No other language has a comparably direct match for both the authorial figure and the named work.\n\n\\boxed{Russian}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 201, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 287}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00046625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1315", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a novel from this modern-day nation, a relative of Chopin home from Singapore calls the tropics a \"disease\" with no cure and recalls how 4000 Malaysian workers spontaneously went on strike one day at noon.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel described is *The Gift of Rain* by Tan Twan Eng, set in Malaysia and featuring a character with connections to Chopin and Singapore. The reference to 4,000 Malaysian workers going on strike points to historical labor unrest in British Malaya, aligning with the novel\u2019s setting. The nation in question is Malaysia.\n\n\\boxed{Malaysia}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 184}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5297e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1326", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a novel by a later author, this writer is nearly crushed by a falling bed he had rigged to his ceiling, and is ridiculed by the protagonist for the mixed metaphors in a speech he delivers so quietly the audience can't hear him.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clues describe a cameo appearance by an earlier writer (as a character) in a later satirical novel. The inaudible speech full of mixed metaphors is a direct caricature of Colley Cibber\u2019s notoriously inept birthday odes as Poet Laureate; the rigged collapsing bed is an additional comic humiliation invented for the same scene. Both incidents occur in Henry Fielding\u2019s 1741 novel Shamela (a work that repeatedly lampoons Cibber\u2019s Apology and his public persona).\n\nThus the writer in question is Colley Cibber.\n\n\\boxed{Colley Cibber}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 227, "output_tokens": 114, "total_tokens": 341}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00056875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1329", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A ter moving to this city, Zhuang meets her older lover in a movie theater and refers to herself only as \"Z\" in a Xiaolu Guo (SHYAO-lu GWOH) novel.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel described is *A Concise Chinese-English Dictionary for Lovers* by Xiaolu Guo, in which the protagonist, referred to as \"Z,\" moves to London and meets her older lover there. The story unfolds through her experiences learning English and navigating cultural and romantic challenges in the city. The correct answer is London.\n\n\\boxed{London}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 176}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4612999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1345", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This playwright was translated and  rst introduced to the U.S. by an actor who later became a Hollywood star playing Dr. Fu Manchu and Charlie Chan.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The playwright in question is Henrik Ibsen. He was introduced to the U.S. through translations by actor E.A. Sothern, who later gained fame in Hollywood for roles including Dr. Fu Manchu and Charlie Chan. Ibsen is the most common and correct answer given the historical context.\n\n\\boxed{Henrik Ibsen}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 163}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3661e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1349", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This text's \"ethnographic imagination\" is the subject of a book by Carol Dougherty that argues that the description of the creation of an object in this text is a metaphor for the creation of the text itself.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a scholarly analysis of a specific ancient text, and Carol Dougherty's monograph *The Raft of Odysseus* directly matches the phrasing \"ethnographic imagination.\" In that study Dougherty treats the ekphrastic account of Odysseus' raft-building (Odyssey 5) as a self-reflexive metaphor for the poem's own composition. Consequently the text in question is the *Odyssey*.\n\n\\boxed{Odyssey (Hom.)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 224, "output_tokens": 93, "total_tokens": 317}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1359", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a story from this country, a young man bursts a blood vessel a ter being stripped and tied to a table by a crowd that has gathered to watch the killing of 49 steers.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The story described is \"The Slaughterhouse\" (*El Matadero*), a foundational work of Argentine literature written by Esteban Echeverr\u00eda. In this narrative, a young Unitarian is captured, tortured, and eventually dies of rage after being subjected to the brutality of the Federalist supporters at a slaughterhouse.\n\n\\boxed{Argentina}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 160}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:26.106547+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_136", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One of these poems states that the \"burden of a great / sadness\" arises from realizing that \"what one is pursuing now / was / once / nearer, truer, and joined to us / with infinite tenderness.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted passage is a close match to a well-known English rendering of lines 32\u201334 and 67\u201370 of Rainer Maria Rilke\u2019s \u201cEighth Duino Elegy.\u201d No other canonical poem contains this precise formulation about the \u201cburden of a great sadness\u201d that arises from the loss of an earlier, \u201cnearer, truer\u201d intimacy with the open.  \n\nThus the poem referenced is the Eighth Duino Elegy.\n\n\\boxed{8th Duino Elegy (Rilke)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 286, "output_tokens": 727, "total_tokens": 1013}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:44.833509+00:00"}, "cost": 0.002175, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_138", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This play's author wrote that he was resisting the \"bourgeois conception of the immutability of the soul\" by having its characters be \"somewhat lacking in \u2018character.'\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The play described is *Six Characters in Search of an Author*, written by Luigi Pirandello. In his preface to the play, Pirandello explained that he sought to dismantle traditional notions of fixed personality by presenting characters who are fluid and incomplete.\n\n\\boxed{Six Characters in Search of an Author}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 153}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:22.854002+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00011575, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1381", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In one of this author's books, British women style their hair in either ringlets or spit curls to show support for the opposing sides of the Turkish-Serbian War.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes a specific historical and cultural detail from the opening chapters of *Daniel Deronda* (1876), in which fashionable British women signal partisan views on the contemporaneous Eastern Crisis by adopting either \u201cSerbian\u201d ringlets or \u201cTurkish\u201d spit-curls. That novel is the work of George Eliot (Marian Evans), whose fiction is the only major Victorian corpus that incorporates this precise sartorial reference to the 1876 Serbo-Turkish War. No other nineteenth-century novelist matches the combination of date, setting, and topical allusion.\n\n\\boxed{George Eliot}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 213, "output_tokens": 116, "total_tokens": 329}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00055625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1384", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In this play, a man is instructed to crown bowls with freshly shorn wool before pouring out three drink-o ferings from a holy spring and laying olive sprays on the wet ground.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The described ritual matches the instructions given by a local inhabitant to Oedipus for making offerings to the Eumenides (Furies) at their sacred grove. This scene occurs early in Sophocles\u2019 final play, Oedipus at Colonus, and the details (spring water, three libations, freshly shorn wool to \u201ccrown\u201d the bowls, and olive branches) are quoted almost verbatim from the text. No other extant Greek tragedy reproduces this precise sequence of actions performed by a male protagonist.\n\n\\boxed{Oedipus at Colonus (Sophocles)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 217, "output_tokens": 111, "total_tokens": 328}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00054875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1398", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Frederick de Armas argues that a fanciful description of this character with two maids is an ekphrasis of Botticelli's Primavera.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query concerns a specific scholarly claim by Frederick de Armas (a specialist in Golden-Age ekphrasis) linking a literary scene to Botticelli\u2019s Primavera. In that painting Venus stands attended by the three Graces; a parallel \u201cone figure + two maids\u201d grouping therefore points to the heroine of Cervantes\u2019 Persiles, whose fanciful portrait is shown to be a deliberate verbal rendering of the same composition. Hence the character in question is Auristela.\n\n\\boxed{Auristela (Persiles)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 209, "output_tokens": 105, "total_tokens": 314}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00052375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1423", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sarah Brigham's 2016 revival of this play prefaces it with an hour-long monologue titled \"Jinny.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The play being referred to is \"The Waves\" by Virginia Woolf. Sarah Brigham's 2016 revival at the York Theatre Royal added a monologue titled \"Jinny\" as a preface to the performance. The character Jinny is one of the six central figures in Woolf's novel.\n\n\\boxed{The Waves}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 86, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 157}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3206e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1430", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: James and Jorndorf dispute Jansenist readings of this play, citing the lines \"You are in love.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given clue is a partial quizbowl-style tossup (common in academic competitions) whose lead-in references scholarly debates over religious interpretations of a French play. Jansenist readings most commonly attach to works by Moli\u00e8re (especially Tartuffe) or Racine; the quoted dialogue fragment and the scholars named align with the former. Hence the play being asked for is Tartuffe.\n\n\\boxed{Tartuffe (Moli\u00e8re)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 202, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 290}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004725, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1440", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In The Old Curiosity Shop, Nell and her grandfather are taken in by a man of this profession named Mr. Marton.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel in question is Dickens's *The Old Curiosity Shop*. After fleeing Quilp and enduring various hardships on the road, Nell and her grandfather are given shelter in a rural village by its kindly schoolmaster, Mr. Marton, who also employs Nell as an assistant. Thus the profession referenced is schoolmaster (or, equivalently, teacher).\n\n\\boxed{schoolmaster (teacher)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 205, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 282}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00044875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1461", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the introduction to the story this character appears in, the narrator discusses confusions about this character's name and origins, as well as what to title his story, as the four difficulties he faced in writing it.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a narrator who opens by enumerating four compositional obstacles\u2014uncertainty over the protagonist\u2019s baptismal name, uncertainty over his parentage and birth, uncertainty over an appropriate title, and one further meta-difficulty\u2014before proceeding to tell the life story. These exact preoccupations appear at the outset of Laurence Sterne\u2019s novel, whose narrator-protagonist is named Tristram Shandy. No other eighteenth-century fictional autobiography matches the enumerated difficulties so precisely.\n\nThus the character in question is Tristram Shandy.\n\n\\boxed{Tristram Shandy}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 222, "output_tokens": 114, "total_tokens": 336}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1464", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In an essay for Harper's Weekly, this writer recalled a train ride on which she hid the fact that she had a Jewish grandmother from an anti-Semitic colonel who later ordered roast beef hash for lunch.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The writer described in the scenario is Mary McCarthy. In her essay for *Harper's Weekly*, she recounted the anecdote about concealing her Jewish heritage from an anti-Semitic colonel during a train journey. This personal reflection highlights themes of identity and irony, particularly when the colonel ordered roast beef hash, a meal with no dietary restrictions.\n\n\\boxed{Mary McCarthy}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 175}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4599999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1471", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Although this character's creator claimed he was a purely imaginative product, he was partly modeled on David Shipman.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue points to a literary character whose author (James Fenimore Cooper) publicly insisted was invented out of whole cloth. Historical scholarship, however, has established that Cooper drew partial inspiration for the frontier scout from David Shipman, a real-life hunter and trapper who lived near Cooperstown, New York. The figure in question is therefore Natty Bumppo (also known as Leatherstocking, Hawkeye, or Deerslayer).\n\n\\boxed{Natty Bumppo (Leatherstocking)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 201, "output_tokens": 100, "total_tokens": 301}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00050125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1479", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An essay by this author contrasts Titian's skin tones with Van Dyck's, arguing that the latter lack the title property, which is the \"power or passion de ning any object.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The author of the essay is William Hazlitt, and the title property he discusses is \"gusto.\" In his essay *On Gusto*, Hazlitt argues that Titian\u2019s paintings possess this quality of intense vitality, whereas Van Dyck\u2019s work lacks it.\n\n\\boxed{William Hazlitt}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 157}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:26.817259+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000118, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1482", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A poet from this country concluded a poem, \"I am light honed to a still point in the incandescent onrush, a  ne ash in the beast's sudden desiccation when the sun explodes.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted lines resemble the poetic style of Australian poet A.D. Hope, known for his intense, metaphysical imagery and themes of destruction and transcendence. The reference to \"the sun explodes\" and the apocalyptic tone align with Hope's poem \"The Death of the Bird\" and similar works. The most common and correct answer is Australia.\n\n\\boxed{Australia}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 177}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4713000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1485", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This writer criticized the settings of another writer's poems as the products of \"a cook's boy helping the gloomier dwarfs boil toads and snails\" in a series of lectures that begins by asking listeners to \"imagine a man on an island\" who 3nds a box containing all of W. H. Auden's works.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The writer being referred to is C. S. Lewis, who criticized W. H. Auden's poetic settings in a series of lectures. He used the vivid metaphor of \"a cook's boy helping the gloomier dwarfs boil toads and snails\" to express his distaste for the grotesque and fantastical elements in Auden's work. These lectures begin with the thought experiment of a man finding a box containing all of Auden's writings on a deserted island.\n\n\\boxed{C. S. Lewis}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 130, "output_tokens": 108, "total_tokens": 238}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.003e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1489", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Cultural Capital, John Guillory related this poem's \"refunctioning of the commonplace book\" to its subsequent linguistic capital as a means of inculcating literacy in schools.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question points to a specific argument in John Guillory\u2019s *Cultural Capital* (1993), which analyzes how certain canonical texts acquired institutional value as instruments of linguistic pedagogy. Guillory identifies T. S. Eliot\u2019s *The Waste Land* as a modernist \u201crefunctioning of the commonplace book\u201d: its collage of quotations, fragments, and annotations converts the older manuscript practice into a teachable archive of literary English. This formal feature, Guillory shows, supplied the poem with durable \u201clinguistic capital,\u201d allowing it to be installed in school and university syllabi as a privileged vehicle for the inculcation of literacy and cultural literacy alike.\n\nThus the poem in question is *The Waste Land*.\n\n\\boxed{The Waste Land (Eliot)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 216, "output_tokens": 149, "total_tokens": 365}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0006425, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1497", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A novel from this country concludes with the protagonist in a mental asylum imagining himself on Mars where inhabitants only speak the word \"kah-ray-kuh-kuh-ko-kex.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel described is *Solaris* by Stanis\u0142aw Lem, a renowned work of Polish science fiction. The protagonist, after experiencing psychological distress, ends up in a mental facility and imagines being on Mars where the inhabitants speak in a nonsensical phrase resembling \"kah-ray-kuh-kuh-ko-kex.\" This surreal ending is consistent with the philosophical and psychological themes in Lem's writing from Poland.\n\n\\boxed{Poland}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 187}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5915999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1500", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When this character is told \"there is no such thing as abstract morality,\" he decides to live his life \"with due regard to the policeman round the corner.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted dialogue and resulting life philosophy match a key scene late in Samuel Butler\u2019s semi-autobiographical novel *The Way of All Flesh*. After Ernest Pontifex is released from prison and begins to shed his earlier religious scruples, a worldly mentor tells him there is \u201cno such thing as abstract morality\u201d; Ernest immediately adopts the pragmatic rule of simply staying one step ahead of \u201cthe policeman round the corner.\u201d No other major literary character is associated with this precise exchange.\n\n\\boxed{Ernest Pontifex (Way of All Flesh)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 212, "output_tokens": 109, "total_tokens": 321}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1503", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: After Cody is killed in an event of this type, a white-haired \"stickman\" holds Cody in his arms and tells him God loves him at the end of George Saunders's story \"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query is a partial clue (likely from a quiz or crossword) that requires identifying the relevant George Saunders story and the specific calamity that befalls the recurring character Cody. The details match the story \u201cBrad Carrigan, American\u201d (from the collection *In Persuasion Nation*), whose final scene depicts Cody\u2019s death in an aviation disaster followed by the consoling apparition of the white-haired stickman. Consequently the \u201cevent of this type\u201d named by the clue is a plane crash.\n\n\\boxed{plane crash}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 218, "output_tokens": 103, "total_tokens": 321}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00053, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1508", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a story credited to Laurentius Abstemius (law-REN-tee-uss ab-STEE-mee-us), one of these animals allows his daughter to marry a much smaller creature, and the daughter steps on her husband on the wedding night.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a specific fable by Abstemius in which a father elephant consents to his daughter's marriage to a tiny mouse; she accidentally crushes him on their wedding night. This matches the details exactly, so the animals referenced are elephants. The fable is a Renaissance-era moral tale illustrating mismatched unions.\n\n\\boxed{elephants}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 231, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 297}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00045375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1518", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Franz Kafka wrote in a short parable that the \"truth about\" this man was that he exorcised his demons by telling his stories to another man, whom he joined on \"crusades\" that provided a \"great and edifying entertainment to the end of his days.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The man described in Franz Kafka's short parable \"The Truth about Sancho Panza\" is Sancho Panza. Kafka reimagines him not as Don Quixote's squire, but as a wise figure who uses storytelling to exorcise inner demons. The \"crusades\" refer metaphorically to their adventures together.\n\n\\boxed{Sancho Panza}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 193}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5936e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1524", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The centrality of these concepts in Europe began with a translation and commentary written \"in the vulgar language\" by Lodovico Castelvetro.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue refers to a key development in Renaissance literary criticism. Lodovico Castelvetro\u2019s 1570 Italian translation and commentary on Aristotle\u2019s Poetics popularized the doctrine that dramatic action must observe unity of time, place, and action; this formulation quickly became normative across Europe. Consequently, the \u201cconcepts\u201d in question are the three classical (or Aristotelian) unities.\n\n\\boxed{3 classical unities (of drama)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 208, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 294}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000475, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1526", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This language was used to write the novel Memoirs of a Porcupine and an essay addressed to James Baldwin titled Letter to Jimmy.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel *Memoirs of a Porcupine* was written by Alain Mabanckou, and the essay \"Letter to Jimmy\" was also authored by him, both originally in French. Alain Mabanckou is a Francophone writer from the Republic of the Congo, and his works are primarily composed in French. Therefore, the language used is French.\n\n\\boxed{French}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 86, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 167}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4206e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1530", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The stage directions for this play's longest speech prescribe that it be delivered with \"a great deal of action\" to cast a \"hypnotic effect\" over both the listening character and the audience.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question describes a highly specific set of stage directions attached to a single extended monologue, which immediately narrows the field to modern American one-act drama. Among the handful of plays that contain such a lengthy, deliberately mesmeric speech, only Edward Albee\u2019s The Zoo Story matches the quoted phrasing verbatim: Jerry\u2019s \u201cThe Story of Jerry and the Dog\u201d is accompanied by the explicit direction that it be performed \u201cwith a great deal of action\u201d so as to exert a \u201chypnotic effect\u201d on both Peter and the audience. No other canonical play (O\u2019Neill, Albee\u2019s later works, Shaffer, etc.) reproduces both quoted phrases together.\n\nThus the play in question is The Zoo Story.\n\n\\boxed{The Zoo Story}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 220, "output_tokens": 149, "total_tokens": 369}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0006475, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1542", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An essay about this country anecdotally de nes its archetype of the \"Ultimate Peasant\" before describing how changes in this country's culture affected the essayist Richard Cobb.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The essay in question is Richard Cobb's reflection on France, where he describes the \"Ultimate Peasant\" as a cultural archetype. Cobb, a British historian, was deeply influenced by French provincial life and how its evolving culture impacted his personal and academic perspectives. The country central to this discussion is France.\n\n\\boxed{France}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 164}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3587e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1546", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Lisel Mueller wrote that, among postwar Germans who did this activity, she was \"a Briar Rose, a Rip Van Winkle, / a stranger to the beginnings / they make from the stench of evil.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quote is drawn from Lisel Mueller\u2019s poem \u201cCurriculum Vitae,\u201d in which the poet (who emigrated from Germany in 1939) describes her own belatedness and detachment. The lines contrast her Rip-Van-Winkle-like slumber with the work of the postwar German poets who were actively confronting and rebuilding language after the moral catastrophe of the Third Reich. Consequently the activity referenced in the question is writing poetry.\n\n\\boxed{writing poetry (postwar Ger. poets)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 223, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 318}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00051625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1569", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Members of this family title a Peter Ackroyd novel in which the bookseller William Ireland presents them with a lost Shakespeare play called Vortigern.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue refers to Peter Ackroyd\u2019s 2004 novel *The Lambs of London*, whose title characters are the siblings Charles and Mary Lamb. In the plot the forger William Henry Ireland attempts to pass off his fabricated \u201clost Shakespeare play\u201d *Vortigern* on the Lambs and their literary circle. The family name that therefore titles the novel is simply the Lambs.\n\n\\boxed{Lambs (of London)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 209, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 297}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00048125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1575", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In one of this author's poems, the speaker compares a \"catafalqued (KAT-ah-falk'd) king\" and a \"solitary man of war / among these frail vegetables\" to the title \"torpedo from the ocean\" that is \"navigating now / the waters of death.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted phrases match the imagery and diction of Pablo Neruda\u2019s \u201cOde to a Large Tuna in the Market,\u201d in which the fish is apostrophized as both a \u201ccatafalqued king\u201d and a \u201csolitary man of war / among these frail vegetables,\u201d then likened to a \u201ctorpedo from the ocean\u201d now \u201cnavigating now / the waters of death.\u201d Neruda\u2019s characteristic odes to humble market objects therefore identify the author in question.\n\n\\boxed{Pablo Neruda}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 243, "output_tokens": 103, "total_tokens": 346}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00056125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1577", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A character nicknamed a\u29d4er this animal narrates his rise from poverty in a Booker-winning novel framed as a letter to Chinese premier Wen Jiabao.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel referenced here is Aravind Adiga's *The White Tiger* (2008 Man Booker Prize winner). Its narrator/protagonist Balram Halwai is explicitly nicknamed \"the white tiger\" and addresses his life story in the form of a letter to Wen Jiabao. The animal in question is therefore the tiger (specifically the white tiger that supplies the nickname and title).\n\n\\boxed{tiger (white tiger)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 213, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 300}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00048375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1581", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a reimagining of this poem, the speaker warns that \"hunger shall make thy modest zone / and cheat fond death of all but bone\" and offers the addressee \"peace and plenty, bed and board, / that chance employment may afford.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted lines are a clear modern reworking of Marlowe\u2019s pastoral invitation, replacing the original\u2019s beds of roses and singing shepherds with a sober offer of \u201cbed and board\u201d while retaining the same structure of enticement-plus-warning. The distinctive phrase \u201cmodest zone\u201d echoes the Elizabethan imagery of the coy mistress\u2019s girdle, now threatened by hunger rather than time, confirming the source poem.  \n\nThus the poem being reimagined is Marlowe\u2019s \u201cThe Passionate Shepherd to His Love.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{The Passionate Shepherd to His Love (Marlowe)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 233, "output_tokens": 115, "total_tokens": 348}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00057875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1592", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This man idolizes the \"intellectual and virginal manliness\" exempli\u2884ed by St. Sebastian and lives by the motto \"Durchhalten,\" or \"persevere,\" which he borrowed from Frederick the Great.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The description matches the protagonist of Thomas Mann's novella *Death in Venice* (1912). Mann explicitly characterizes Gustav Aschenbach as an ascetic writer who models himself on the \"intellectual and virginal manliness\" of St. Sebastian and who adopts Frederick the Great's motto \"Durchhalten\" as his personal ethic of endurance. No other figure in Mann's oeuvre or in the surrounding literary-historical context fits both the iconographic and the biographical details simultaneously.\n\n\\boxed{Gustav Aschenbach (Death in Venice)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 227, "output_tokens": 107, "total_tokens": 334}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00055125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1596", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Because actions involving this substance and \"the Lip you press\" might \"end in the Nothing all Things end in,\" a poem suggests thinking that \"you are Today what Yesterday / you were\" and that \"tomorrow you shall not be less.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted phrases are taken verbatim from Edward FitzGerald\u2019s translation of The Rub\u00e1iy\u00e1t of Omar Khayy\u00e1m (stanza 43 in the first edition, stanza 47 in later versions). In context, the \u201csubstance\u201d whose contact with \u201cthe Lip you press\u201d is said to \u201cend in the Nothing\u201d is therefore the wine that the poem repeatedly urges the reader to enjoy.  \n\nThus the answer to the query is simply the substance named in the poem.\n\n\\boxed{wine (Rubaiyat)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 229, "output_tokens": 106, "total_tokens": 335}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00055125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1609", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Supposed \"supplements\" to this text, published by Franc\u0327ois Nodot (noh-doh) and Jose\u0301 Marchena, were later shown to be forgeries.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given clue describes a famous literary work whose incomplete surviving manuscripts prompted later attempts at reconstruction. Both Nodot (in 1694) and Marchena (in 1800) published lengthy \u201csupplements\u201d purporting to fill the lacunae; these were exposed as fabrications in the nineteenth century. The work in question is therefore Petronius\u2019 Satyricon.\n\n\\boxed{Satyricon (Petronius)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 216, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 304}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00049, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_161", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Regina Gagnier's (\"GAHN-yay's\") book The Idylls of the Marketplace argues that this author's work functioned as a protest against the commodification of art through notions of utility.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Regina Gagnier's book *The Idylls of the Marketplace* discusses how Oscar Wilde's work served as a protest against the commodification of art and the imposition of utility on artistic expression. Wilde championed aestheticism and the idea of \"art for art's sake,\" directly opposing the notion that art must serve a practical purpose. \n\n\\boxed{Oscar Wilde}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 179}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4971e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1610", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a play, a man with this job encourages people to memorize an anecdote about how 14 foreskins of Christ existed at the time of the Reformation; in that play, Dakin (DAY-kin) blackmails Felix Armstrong to help a man keep his job in this profession, but that man dies in an accident while riding his motorcycle with Irwin.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The man in question is a schoolteacher, as the play described is *The History Boys* by Alan Bennett. The character Hector, a teacher, is the one who encourages students to memorize unusual anecdotes, and he dies in a motorcycle accident with Irwin. Dakin blackmails Armstrong to help Hector keep his job, confirming the profession.\n\n\\boxed{teacher}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 135, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 210}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.7085e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1627", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a novel from this country, a character suffers from \"delirium\" and imagines himself transforming into Thomas Aquinas's Summa Theologica; that novel by an author from this country is dedicated to the \" rst worm\" that gnawed on the narrator's corpse.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel described is *The Posthumous Memoirs of Br\u00e1s Cubas* (also known as *Epitaph of a Small Winner*), written by the Brazilian author Machado de Assis. The narrator, who begins the book by declaring himself a \"deceased author\" rather than an \"author who has died,\" dedicates the work to the worm that first gnawed on his cold flesh.\n\n\\boxed{Brazil}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 197}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:27.445396+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00015675, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1645", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One character created by this author listens to a broadcast about Soviet nuclear testing while agonizing over his decision to dilute the milk being fed to his infant son.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The described scene is a specific flashback in Jonathan Franzen\u2019s 2001 novel *The Corrections*. It occurs early in the book when a young Alfred Lambert, struggling financially, waters down the milk/formula he is feeding his infant son while a radio broadcast reports on Soviet nuclear tests. No other prominent author\u2019s work contains this precise combination of details, confirming Franzen as the referent.\n\n\\boxed{Jonathan Franzen}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 210, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 295}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000475, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1653", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A four-line poem set during this decade discusses a group of men who should be with their sweethearts gathering the \"\u1978owers le\u1978 thick at nightfall in the wood.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The poem described is \"In Flanders Fields\" by John McCrae, written during the First World War in 1915, which places it in the 1910s. The lines evoke imagery of poppies growing among the graves of fallen soldiers, contrasting with the peaceful scene of sweethearts gathering flowers. The correct decade is the 1910s.\n\n\\boxed{1910s}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 90, "total_tokens": 187}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5887e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1665", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This poet wrote that, although \"a prince can make a belted knight, / a marquis, [or a] duke,\" \"the pith of sense and pride of worth / are higher rank than all that.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The poet who wrote these lines is Robert Burns. In his poem \"A Man's a Man for A' That,\" Burns emphasizes the inherent worth of individuals regardless of social rank. The lines reflect his democratic ideals and critique of aristocracy.\n\n\\boxed{Robert Burns}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 159}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2884e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1681", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A play on this title names Michael Gorra's literary biography about the \"making of an American masterpiece.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue refers to Michael Gorra's 2012 study *Portrait of a Novel*, whose title is an explicit variation on Henry James's 1881 novel. That novel is the \"American masterpiece\" whose composition Gorra examines. Hence the title being played upon is *The Portrait of a Lady*.\n\n\\boxed{The Portrait of a Lady}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 201, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 270}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00042375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_169", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This novel enjoins the reader to consult a \"metaphysical professor\" should they \"ever be athirst in the great American desert,\" since \"as everyone knows, meditation and water are wedded forever.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted passage is from Herman Melville's *Moby-Dick*, where the narrator, Ishmael, reflects on the connection between water and contemplation. The novel famously suggests seeking a \"metaphysical professor\" in times of spiritual or existential thirst in the \"great American desert.\" This alludes to the deep philosophical themes interwoven with the sea and meditation in the book.\n\n\\boxed{Moby-Dick}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 188}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5871e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1692", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In this work, \"Knot Taps\" are shown graf ti-ing buildings with the outlines of lovers embracing as if vaporized by the blast at Hiroshima.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The work described is *Watchmen* by Alan Moore and Dave Gibbons, in which the character Rorschach mentions \"Knot Taps\" graffiti depicting embracing figures reminiscent of the Hiroshima shadows. This imagery symbolizes the ever-present threat of nuclear annihilation. The correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{Watchmen}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3131999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1727", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A poem by Richard Brautigan reimagines this event as a rape at the hands of \"an evil  sherman who was dressed in clothes that had no childhood.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a specific Richard Brautigan poem that figuratively recasts a historical turning point in terms of sexual violence perpetrated by an industrialized \u201cevil Sherman.\u201d The only event that aligns with both the military/industrial imagery of Sherman and the reference to machine-made \u201cclothes that had no childhood\u201d is the Industrial Revolution. Brautigan therefore uses the Civil-War general as a symbol of mechanized modernity to dramatize that revolution as a foundational act of violation.\n\n\\boxed{Ind. Rev. (Sherman's March)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 215, "output_tokens": 104, "total_tokens": 319}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00052875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_173", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Apart from \"A,\" this is the first word in the title of a poem that opens: \"I'll tell thee now (dear Love) what thou shalt do /\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The poem is \"A Valediction: of the Book\" by John Donne, which begins with the line, \"I'll tell thee now (dear Love) what thou shalt do.\" Excluding the article \"A,\" the first word of the title is \"Valediction.\"\n\n\\boxed{Valediction}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 88, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 153}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:18.374247+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0001195, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1734", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In this play, a student exits with the sarcastic line \"goodnight, Prometheus,\" prompting another character to speculate that there's \"no such thing\" as \"Prometheus.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted exchange occurs near the end of Act 1 of Willy Russell\u2019s two-hander Educating Rita. A departing pupil sarcastically addresses the alcoholic tutor Frank as \u201cPrometheus,\u201d after which the newly arrived, working-class Rita\u2014still innocent of classical mythology\u2014replies that she has never heard of any such person and wonders whether \u201cthere\u2019s no such thing.\u201d The moment neatly dramatizes the cultural gulf the play explores and is therefore the only work that fits the given dialogue.\n\n\\boxed{Educating Rita}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 214, "output_tokens": 103, "total_tokens": 317}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000525, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1735", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a poem addressed to this man, the speaker sees himself \"as one who sits ashore and longs . . . to visit dolphin-coral in deep seas\"; that sonnet to this man ends by invoking \"Dian (dy-ANN), Queen of Earth, and Heaven, and Hell\" and opens with the speaker \"standing aloof in giant ignorance.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The poem described is John Keats's sonnet \"To Homer,\" which expresses the speaker's longing to fully grasp the epic poet's genius. The speaker feels \"standing aloof in giant ignorance\" because he cannot read the original Greek, leading him to invoke the goddess Diana to help him understand Homer's work.\n\n\\boxed{Homer}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 125, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 198}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:27.567932+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00014075, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1742", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A poem about this event asks \"can you then impute a sinful deed to babes who on their mothers' bosoms bleed?\" and states \"one day everything will be well, that is our hope.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted lines are direct translations from Voltaire's \"Po\u00e8me sur le d\u00e9sastre de Lisbonne\" (1756), which was written in immediate response to the catastrophic earthquake, tsunami, and fires that struck Lisbon on 1 November 1755. The poem uses the suffering of innocents to challenge Leibnizian optimism, matching the supplied excerpts exactly. No other historical event is the subject of this work.\n\n\\boxed{1755 Lisbon earthquake}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 284, "output_tokens": 456, "total_tokens": 740}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:10:06.279245+00:00"}, "cost": 0.001495, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1750", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A Herman Melville essay notes that this story's innocuous title is meant to deceive the \"super cial skimmer of pages,\" who fails to see that this story is \"deep as Dante.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query refers to a specific remark in Herman Melville\u2019s 1850 review essay \u201cHawthorne and His Mosses.\u201d In that essay Melville singles out Hawthorne\u2019s tale \u201cYoung Goodman Brown,\u201d observing that its bland, almost pastoral-sounding title is calculated to mislead \u201cthe superficial skimmer of pages,\u201d while the story itself is in fact \u201cas deep as Dante.\u201d  \n\nNo other Hawthorne story is described by Melville in those exact terms, and the phrasing matches the query verbatim.  \n\nThus the story in question is \u201cYoung Goodman Brown.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{Young Goodman Brown}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 218, "output_tokens": 113, "total_tokens": 331}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000555, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1751", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This poem describes an entity that \"makes the willow shiver in the sun\" for maidens who \"taste / and stray impassioned in the littering leaves.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The poem described is \"The Wind\" by the American poet Richard Wilbur. The lines refer to the wind's personified, transformative effect on the landscape and the people within it.\n\n\\boxed{The Wind}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 86, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 130}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:28.193574+00:00"}, "cost": 8.75e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1752", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An essay by this author recalls a woman wearing a \"dirty crepe-de-Chine (crep-duh-sheen) wrapper\" who tells a bartender that Estelle is the reason she and George Sharp separated.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The essay described is \"Goodbye to All That\" by Joan Didion, in which she recounts a memory of a woman in a dirty crepe-de-Chine wrapper discussing her separation from George Sharp, blaming Estelle. This personal and reflective piece is characteristic of Didion\u2019s early nonfiction, set in New York City. The author is Joan Didion.\n\n\\boxed{Joan Didion}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 184}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5413e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1771", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a job interview, one of this author's characters is asked to translate a note written in French but is too nervous to say that he cannot read the handwriting and insists that doigts (dwah) means \"\u239cngers.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a specific scene involving a nervous job candidate who is asked to translate handwritten French but cannot admit his difficulty with the script, leading him to overconfidently gloss \u201cdoigts\u201d as \u201cfingers.\u201d This episode occurs in Jonathan Franzen\u2019s 2001 novel *The Corrections*, during Chip Lambert\u2019s disastrous interview with a market-research firm. No other contemporary author\u2019s work contains a matching incident, confirming Franzen as the referent.\n\n\\boxed{Jonathan Franzen}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 226, "output_tokens": 97, "total_tokens": 323}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000525, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1780", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The speaker of a poem by this author asks \"whom dost thou worship in this lonely dark corner of a temple with doors all shut?\" and says that God is \"where the tiller is tilling the hard ground and where the pathmaker is breaking stones.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The author of these lines from the poem \"Leave this chanting and singing and telling of beads\" is Rabindranath Tagore. These verses appear in his Nobel Prize-winning collection, *Gitanjali*.\n\n\\boxed{Rabindranath Tagore}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 154}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:28.319450+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000101, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1784", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In David Luke's rhyming translation of this play, one character says \"I'm not a lady and I'm not sweet / I can get home on my own two feet\" in response to the protagonist asking to escort her from confession.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted lines are a direct match for David Luke\u2019s verse rendering of the exchange between Faust and Margarete (Gretchen) immediately after she leaves the confessional in Goethe\u2019s Faust, Part One. No other well-known play exists in a David Luke rhyming translation that contains this scene or these lines.  \n\nThus the work in question is Goethe\u2019s Faust (Part One).\n\n\\boxed{Goethe's Faust (Pt. 1)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 226, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 315}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000505, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1787", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A man who breaks plates without touching them opens a factory that produces this stuff, then builds a railroad to improve its business.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The riddle describes the origin of a specific product and its associated business. The phrase \"breaks plates without touching them\" is a reference to the delicate nature of fine china (porcelain dishware), which can shatter from minor impacts or vibrations. The entrepreneur in question therefore opens a factory to manufacture porcelain and later invests in rail infrastructure to ship the fragile finished goods efficiently.\n\nThis yields the most common solution to the riddle.\n\n\\boxed{porcelain}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 205, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 294}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00047875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1792", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a novel that shares its title with this poem, Dario founds the Edinburgh Fascist Club after immigrating from Sicily to Scotland.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given statement describes a key plot point from a specific novel, whose title is shared with a well-known poem. The unique detail of the Sicilian immigrant Dario founding the Edinburgh Fascist Club directly identifies that novel as James Thomson\u2019s *The City of Dreadful Night* (there is also a 1994 novel of exactly the same title that contains the described episode). Hence the poem referenced by the query must be the same work.\n\n\\boxed{The City of Dreadful Night}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 207, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 302}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00049625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1795", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An essay argues that the \"artificial comedy\" of this century occurs in a \"utopia of gallantry\" unrelated to morality.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given clue matches the central argument of Charles Lamb's 1822 essay \"On the Artificial Comedy of the Last Century,\" in which he defends Restoration playwrights by claiming their work inhabits a self-contained \"Utopia of gallantry\" detached from everyday ethical judgment.  \n\nThe phrasing (\"artificial comedy,\" \"utopia of gallantry\") is taken verbatim from Lamb, making him the unique referent of the question.  \n\nThus the expected answer is the essay's author.\n\n\\boxed{Charles Lamb (On Artif. Comedy)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 206, "output_tokens": 107, "total_tokens": 313}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000525, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1798", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Addressing this place, a character calls himself \"one who brings / A mind not to be changed by place or time,\" since \"The mind is its own place.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quote refers to Satan's declaration in John Milton's *Paradise Lost*, where he asserts mental independence despite being cast into Hell. The place being addressed is Hell, which Satan describes as his new domain. \n\n\\boxed{Hell}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 143}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1603e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_180", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An essay by Rebecca West argues that people cannot be dissuaded from this practice when it seems to their advantage unless they have been brought up with \"common worship\" and \"folk songs.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a specific argument from Rebecca West's writing on loyalty and betrayal (originally an essay that was expanded into the book *The Meaning of Treason*). The quoted phrases about \"common worship\" and \"folk songs\" are taken directly from West's discussion of the social preconditions needed to deter disloyalty. Hence the practice in question is treason.\n\n\\boxed{treason}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 217, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 294}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00046375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1801", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A polio epidemic strikes a summer camp in this state in a 2010 novel whose author claimed it to be his last.  \n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes Philip Roth\u2019s 2010 novel *Nemesis*, which the author publicly stated would be his last. In the book a polio outbreak reaches the boys\u2019 summer camp at which the protagonist is working; that camp is located in the Poconos. The Poconos lie in Pennsylvania, so the state referenced by the clue is Pennsylvania.\n\n\\boxed{Pennsylvania}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 206, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 283}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00045, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1803", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The protagonist of this novel mocks book-reading while arguing against predestination in a speech that repeats his claim to be a racially-pure \"man without a cross.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The description matches a key scene from James Fenimore Cooper\u2019s *The Last of the Mohicans* (1826). In Chapters 3\u20134, Natty Bumppo (Hawkeye) repeatedly calls himself \u201ca man without a cross\u201d while debating David Gamut about Calvinist predestination and dismissing the value of book-learning and psalmody. No other Leatherstocking Tale contains this precise combination of motifs.\n\nThus the novel in question is *The Last of the Mohicans*.\n\n\\boxed{The Last of the Mohicans}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 212, "output_tokens": 106, "total_tokens": 318}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00053, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1820", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A character says that one of these objects \"irked me... it itched me\" after he and another man find one of them on the ground and silently swap three of them back and forth.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a specific scene from Samuel Beckett's play *Waiting for Godot*. Vladimir and Estragon discover Lucky's hat (along with their own), then silently pass the three hats back and forth while trying them on; one of them subsequently complains that a particular hat \"irked me... it itched me.\"  \n\nThis matches the given details exactly (three objects, silent swapping, explicit quotation) and is the most common referent for the phrasing in literary quiz contexts.  \n\n\\boxed{hats (Godot)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 220, "output_tokens": 104, "total_tokens": 324}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000535, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1833", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This character conceives of conversation as a \"served dessert\" of ripe fruits to be piled atop a silver plate signifying his wife's mind.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The description matches a memorable image from Henry James\u2019s *The Portrait of a Lady*. In conversation with Isabel Archer, Gilbert Osmond explicitly figures her mind as a polished silver salver on which he will heap \u201cripe fruits\u201d of cultivated talk, thereby reducing her intellect to a decorative receptacle for his own aesthetic pleasure. No other major literary character employs this precise domestic-metaphorical conceit.\n\n\\boxed{Gilbert Osmond (Portrait of a Lady)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 208, "output_tokens": 90, "total_tokens": 298}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000485, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1843", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a story titled for a man with this name, the narrator gives a brief outline of the plot, then gives the reader the option of meditating on it individually or reading the fuller account, trusting that there will be a moral \"done up neatly, and condensed into the \u70a4nal sentence.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a specific passage from Nathaniel Hawthorne's 1835 short story \"Wakefield,\" in which the narrator summarizes a newspaper anecdote about a man who abandons his wife for twenty years, then explicitly offers the reader the choice of meditating on the outline or continuing to the full narrative whose moral will be \"condensed into the final sentence.\"  \nThe story is therefore titled for its protagonist, making \"Wakefield\" the name in question.  \nNo other well-known tale matches the quoted phrasing or narrative device.\n\n\\boxed{Wakefield}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 240, "output_tokens": 109, "total_tokens": 349}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005725, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1856", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In this poem, a transition between two radically di\u9d01ferent refrains occurs with the line \"The ant's a centaur in his dragon world.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted line is the pivot in Ezra Pound\u2019s Canto LXXXI (from The Pisan Cantos). Immediately before it the poem repeats the refrain \u201cTudor indeed is gone,\u201d while immediately after it the new, antithetical refrain \u201cPull down thy vanity\u201d begins and is reiterated for the remainder of the canto.  \n\nThus the poem that exhibits the described transition between refrains is Canto LXXXI.\n\n\\boxed{Canto LXXXI (Pound)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 212, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 303}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004925, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1879", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a short story, a young man tasked with picking out one of these beings among a group of maidens playing \"hawk and chickens\" is rewarded with a mysterious letter for his father the mayor.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a specific folkloric motif in which a youth must identify one supernatural maiden among many (here disguised as ordinary girls playing a children's game) and is then entrusted with a sealed letter. This matches the plot of multiple Slavic tales featuring rusalki (also spelled rusalky), water or forest spirits who appear as beautiful young women, lure or test mortal men, and sometimes deliver fateful messages to authority figures such as a town mayor. No other class of beings (swan-maidens, vilas, nixies, etc.) consistently combines the exact game, the selection test, and the letter-for-the-mayor reward in the same short-story tradition.\n\n\\boxed{rusalki (rusalky)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 220, "output_tokens": 146, "total_tokens": 366}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00064, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_188", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An Italian prisoner in this novel paces his cell floor on his knees, licking the feet of a brass figurine of Christ.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a highly specific scene involving an Italian inmate performing an act of extreme religious penance in his cell. This matches a passage from Dostoevsky\u2019s semi-autobiographical prison novel (based on his own Siberian incarceration), which catalogs the habits and eccentricities of fellow convicts of various nationalities, including an Italian. No other well-known novel containing prison episodes (Monte Cristo, Resurrection, etc.) contains this precise detail.\n\n\\boxed{The House of the Dead (Dostoevsky)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 267, "output_tokens": 1132, "total_tokens": 1399}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:49.268844+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00316375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1885", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A taxi driver learns about a treacherous act he committed during this historical event in the last past life narrative of Susan Barker's The Incarnations.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel follows a present-day Beijing taxi driver who receives anonymous letters detailing his five previous incarnations across Chinese history. These lives are presented in roughly reverse chronological order, so the final (\u201clast\u201d) narrative concerns the most recent prior life\u2014a young man active during the 1989 student movement. In that section the protagonist learns he betrayed a fellow demonstrator, an act of treachery set against the backdrop of the Tiananmen Square protests.\n\n\\boxed{Tiananmen Sq. protests (1989)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 208, "output_tokens": 101, "total_tokens": 309}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1889", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Lionel Trilling contrasted the liberal reception of this author with that of Henry James in his polemical essay \"Reality in America.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In his essay \"Reality in America,\" Lionel Trilling contrasts the liberal reception of Theodore Dreiser with that of Henry James. He argues that liberals championed Dreiser for his perceived \"reality\" and social concern while unfairly dismissing James for his perceived elitism and lack of engagement with American life.\n\n\\boxed{Theodore Dreiser}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 78, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 145}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:16.714957+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00012, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_1893", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In this novel, a professor tells his students to \"let your thought be the wall,\" then \"let your thought be that that thought the wall.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted exercise in recursive, object-directed thinking is a phenomenological drill drawn from a minor character's backstory in David Foster Wallace's unfinished novel *The Pale King*. In that work a Jesuit instructor directs students first to make their awareness identical with a wall and then to make their awareness identical with the prior act of awareness itself. No other well-known novel contains this precise two-step formulation.\n\n\\boxed{The Pale King (DFW)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 210, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 294}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004725, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_197", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Epistemology of the Closet, Eve Sedgwick writes that this novel anticipates the discourse surrounding the AIDS epidemic by presenting a fantasy of life \"after the homosexual.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query concerns a specific claim in Eve Kosofsky Sedgwick\u2019s *Epistemology of the Closet* (1990). In the chapter devoted to Henry James, Sedgwick reads \u201cThe Beast in the Jungle\u201d as staging a protagonist whose life is organized around the perpetual deferral and eventual erasure of a homosexual possibility; the resulting narrative thereby supplies a pre-AIDS fantasy of a world \u201cafter the homosexual.\u201d No other text Sedgwick treats (Billy Budd, Dorian Gray, etc.) is described in these terms.\n\nThus the novel in question is Henry James\u2019s \u201cThe Beast in the Jungle.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{The Beast in the Jungle (H. James)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 214, "output_tokens": 133, "total_tokens": 347}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0006, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_206", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Three sadistic children in this novel force a rabbit to run as fast as it can, then tug its collapsed body along a string until it nearly dies.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel described is *The Painted Bird* by Jerzy Kosi\u0144ski. In this scene, the children torture the rabbit as a display of their cruelty toward defenseless creatures.\n\n\\boxed{The Painted Bird}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 127}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:17.915436+00:00"}, "cost": 8.55e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_210", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A character created by this author stops believing in the supernatural and hears the speech of birds as mere chatter, after which he blots a manuscript and is imprisoned in a crystal bottle.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The character described is **Nathaniel** from the short story \"The Sandman,\" and the author is **E.T.A. Hoffmann**. In the story, the protagonist's descent into madness and his eventual tragic fate are linked to his obsession with the supernatural and the influence of the sinister Coppelius.\n\n\\boxed{E.T.A. Hoffmann}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 89, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 164}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:23.250744+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00013475, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_217", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This author's attempts to efface the \"realistic sources\" of his works represent an \"intent of undoing,\" according to Stanley Gontarski.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The author described by Stanley Gontarski as having an \"intent of undoing\" in his attempts to efface the realistic sources of his work is Samuel Beckett. Gontarski explores this concept in his critical analysis of Beckett's aesthetic of reduction and his move toward abstraction.\n\n\\boxed{Samuel Beckett}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 148}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:21.654996+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00011575, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_228", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The cover of Sherry Turkle's book Reclaiming Conversation is a reference to an anecdote in this other book, in which the narrator writes that he and his friend \"gradually shoved our chairs farther apart till they touched the wall in opposite corners.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The anecdote describes two people who, lacking anything to talk about, physically retreat from one another until they occupy opposite corners of a room. This scene appears in Jerry Mander\u2019s *Four Arguments for the Elimination of Television* (Argument 2), where Mander uses it to illustrate how the absence of a mediating screen leaves people unable to sustain ordinary face-to-face contact. Turkle\u2019s cover design\u2014two empty chairs pushed against opposite walls\u2014visually cites that passage, thereby linking her argument about digital devices to Mander\u2019s earlier critique of television.\n\n\\boxed{Four Arguments for the Elimination of Television (Mander)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 228, "output_tokens": 124, "total_tokens": 352}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000595, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_234", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Due in part to a developmental disorder that renders her incapable of doing math, an office worker in this country is demoted to cleaning bathrooms in the novel Fear and Trembling by Am\u00e9lie Nothomb.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel *Fear and Trembling* by Am\u00e9lie Nothomb is set in Japan, where the protagonist, a Belgian woman working in a Japanese corporation, faces extreme cultural and professional challenges. Her inability to perform certain tasks, compounded by rigid workplace expectations, leads to her demotion. The country is Japan.\n\n\\boxed{Japan}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 170}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4071e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_237", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A poem compares one of these animals to a person who is \"part woman, three parts a child,\" because she scans to ensure \"that nobody looks\" when her \"feet / Practice a tinker shuffle / Picked up on a street.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted lines are from Paul Muldoon's poem \"Hedgehog,\" which explicitly likens the animal's furtive gait and wariness to \"a person / Who is part woman, three parts a child.\" The reference to a \"tinker shuffle\" further evokes the traditional association between tinkers/gypsies and hedgehogs (which they were known to hunt and cook). No other common animal fits the quoted description.\n\n\\boxed{hedgehogs}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 229, "output_tokens": 93, "total_tokens": 322}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00051875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_24", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A.\u00a0C.\u00a0Bradley argued that this character \"is denied the dignity of verse\" while performing a certain action.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A.C. Bradley's *Shakespearean Tragedy* (1904) analyzes the linguistic texture of the plays and specifically notes that Lady Macbeth, during her sleepwalking scene (Act 5, Scene 1), is \u201cdenied the dignity of verse\u201d and therefore speaks only in broken prose. This observation underscores Bradley\u2019s broader point that Shakespeare reserves verse for moments of heightened tragic dignity and deliberately strips it away here to convey psychological disintegration. No other Shakespearean character matches the quoted phrase or the associated action.\n\n\\boxed{Lady Macbeth (sleepwalking)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 204, "output_tokens": 110, "total_tokens": 314}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00053, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_243", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a story by this author, after the painter Clara Glencairn dies of a stroke, a rival contemporary paints a portrait of her, then never paints again.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question is a standard quiz-bowl style \u201cidentify the author\u201d clue whose sole concrete datum is the anecdote about Clara Glencairn. That anecdote occurs in Silvina Ocampo\u2019s short story \u201cEl retrato mal\u00e9volo\u201d (collected in Los d\u00edas de la noche, 1970), in which a rival painter completes a posthumous portrait of Glencairn and then permanently abandons his art. No other well-known author\u2019s work contains this precise incident, confirming Ocampo as the referent.\n\n\\boxed{Silvina Ocampo}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 214, "output_tokens": 111, "total_tokens": 325}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000545, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_25", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This book's opening word was first rendered in Greek as mataiotes (\"mah-tah-YO-tays\"), which may explain its corruption from an original meaning of \"breath.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The book being referenced is Ecclesiastes, which begins with the word \"Vanity\" in many English translations. This word translates the Hebrew \"hevel,\" meaning \"breath\" or \"vapor,\" and was rendered in the Greek Septuagint as \"mataiotes,\" conveying futility. The opening word's philosophical tone reflects the transient nature of life.\n\n\\boxed{Ecclesiastes}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 180}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5216e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_258", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A play named after this character opens with a crowd carrying olive branches wrapped in wood to ward off the plague.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The play described is *Oedipus Rex* by Sophocles, which opens with Theban citizens bringing olive branches wrapped in wool to appease the gods during a plague. The character after whom the play is named is Oedipus. \n\n\\boxed{Oedipus}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 81, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 141}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1751e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_267", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Denis Diderot revealed his atheism in a letter to a person with this condition.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Denis Diderot revealed his atheism in his 1749 work *Letter on the Blind* (*Lettre sur les aveugles*), which was addressed to a person who was blind. The text explored the philosophical implications of sensory perception and challenged traditional religious views on the existence of God.\n\n\\boxed{blindness}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 72, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 141}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:16.459852+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0001215, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_271", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Richard Wilbur produced the first rhymed English translation of a play by this author, though he did not keep that play's alexandrine couplets.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Richard Wilbur translated Moli\u00e8re's play *Tartuffe*, creating a rhymed English version while abandoning the original French alexandrine couplets. Moli\u00e8re is the most common answer associated with this translation feat. \n\n\\boxed{Moli\u00e8re}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 147}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2061e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_273", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A homeless character created by this author dreams of going to jail on Blackwell's Island for the winter in order to stay warm.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The character Soapy, who attempts to get arrested to secure shelter for the winter, appears in the short story \"The Cop and the Anthem.\" This story was written by the American author O. Henry.\n\n\\boxed{O. Henry}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 80, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 129}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:20.581870+00:00"}, "cost": 9.35e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_278", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Acts 1 and 2 of an early version of this play include a non-speaking ghost character named Innogen.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The play being referred to is *Cymbeline* by William Shakespeare. In early versions of the text, particularly in the First Folio, the character Imogen was mistakenly typeset as \"Innogen,\" and a non-speaking ghost named Innogen appears in the stage directions for Acts 1 and 2. This is now understood as a typographical error or confusion with another name.\n\n\\boxed{Cymbeline}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 82, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 169}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4522000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_294", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Thomas Dekker based his play Satiromastix on the feud between John Marston and this author, which was dubbed \"The War of the Theatres.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The author referenced in the question is Ben Jonson. Thomas Dekker's play *Satiromastix* drew from the satirical conflict between playwrights during the \"War of the Theatres,\" primarily targeting Ben Jonson, who was a central figure in the feud with John Marston. \n\n\\boxed{Ben Jonson}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 162}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3503e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_300", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A speech in this novel claims that although \"no code\" mattered to a poor woman \"before she broke it,\" it \"came crashing down on her afterwards.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted speech concerns the harsh social/sexual double standard applied to a poor unmarried woman (Lena Grove) after she becomes pregnant. This reflection occurs in William Faulkner\u2019s 1932 novel *Light in August*, whose narrator explicitly uses those terms while describing how \u201cno code mattered\u201d to Lena until after she had broken it. No other Faulkner novel (or any other canonical work) contains this precise formulation.\n\n\\boxed{Light in August (Faulkner)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 212, "output_tokens": 93, "total_tokens": 305}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004975, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_321", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The protagonist of this novel kills a man and then pretends to be him to have sex with his lover, this novel's antagonist.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel described is *The Talented Mr. Ripley* by Patricia Highsmith. The protagonist, Tom Ripley, murders Dickie Greenleaf and assumes his identity, eventually engaging with Dickie\u2019s lover, Marge, though not directly having sex with her as part of the deception. The antagonist can be interpreted as Dickie himself or the truth that Tom tries to escape.\n\n\\boxed{The Talented Mr. Ripley}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 86, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 175}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5006e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_324", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In what is considered this author's first poem, he praises the Roman historian Cornelius Nepos, who \"took courage to set forth the whole history of the world in three volumes.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted passage matches the text of Catullus 1 (the dedicatory poem to Cornelius Nepos that opens the surviving collection), in which the poet explicitly compliments Nepos for compressing world history into three rolls.  No other ancient author\u2019s opening poem contains this reference, so the poet in question is Catullus (Gaius Valerius Catullus).  \n\n\\boxed{Catullus (poem 1)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 215, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 302}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00048625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_337", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: At the end of this novel, its protagonist finally begins finishing his dissertation on his ancestor, after he abandoned it during a long period he calls his \"Great Sleep.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The description matches the plot of Robert Penn Warren's *All the King's Men*. Its narrator-protagonist Jack Burden explicitly labels his years-long withdrawal from life and from his historical research as the \"Great Sleep\"; that research is a never-finished dissertation on his ancestor Cass Mastern. The novel's closing pages show Burden returning to the project, now ready to complete it.\n\n\\boxed{All the King's Men}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 213, "output_tokens": 82, "total_tokens": 295}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00047125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_343", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A poem by a writer of this ethnicity asks \"Why are the senators sitting there without legislating?\" and ends by calling the title group of people \"a kind of solution.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The poem described is \"Waiting for the Barbarians\" by the Greek poet Constantine Cavafy. The poem famously concludes by suggesting that the arrival of the barbarians would have been a solution to the political stagnation of the Roman Empire.\n\n\\boxed{Greek}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 88, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 141}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:24.322267+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0001015, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_346", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: William Rothenstein encouraged this author to journey to London, where he nearly lost his only manuscript of a poetry collection on the metro.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The author described is Rabindranath Tagore, who traveled to London in 1912 with his manuscript of *Gitanjali*. He famously left the bag containing his poems on a train, though it was fortunately recovered at the Lost Property Office.\n\n\\boxed{Rabindranath Tagore}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 81, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 141}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:17.385308+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00011025, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_349", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A girl in this play explains that German \"isn't a becoming language\" because she looks \"quite plain\" after her German lesson.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The play described is *The Importance of Being Earnest* by Oscar Wilde. In the play, Cecily Cardew makes this remark to Miss Prism regarding her studies.\n\n\\boxed{The Importance of Being Earnest}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 81, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 126}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:20.065363+00:00"}, "cost": 8.775e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_356", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The first and last stanzas of Philip Larkin's poem \"Annus Mirabilis\" mention this novel before \"The Beatles' first LP.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel mentioned before \"The Beatles' first LP\" in the first and last stanzas of Philip Larkin's \"Annus Mirabilis\" is *Lady Chatterley's Lover*. This reference highlights the cultural significance of the 1960 obscenity trial surrounding the novel's publication. \n\n\\boxed{Lady Chatterley's Lover}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 164}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3789999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_360", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This author depicted a dictator named Kamini, who tries to solve a financial crisis by printing more money, in A Play of Giants.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The author who depicted a dictator named Kamini in *A Play of Giants* is Wole Soyinka. This play satirizes African dictators and their misuse of power, with Kamini representing the absurdity of authoritarian rule. Soyinka, a Nigerian Nobel laureate, is known for his political critiques through drama.\n\n\\boxed{Wole Soyinka}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 86, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 160}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3506e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_369", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A racist in this novel cites Goddard's book The Rise of the Colored Empires to argue that white \"Nordics\" have created \"all the things that go to make civilization.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel in question is *The Great Gatsby* by F. Scott Fitzgerald. The character Tom Buchanan expresses racist views and cites the fictional book *The Rise of the Colored Empires* by Goddard to support white supremacy. This moment highlights the novel\u2019s critique of 1920s American elitism and racial anxiety.\n\n\\boxed{The Great Gatsby}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 177}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4829e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_381", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A play set in this country ends with news of the Actor's suicide, causing Satine to respond that it \"spoiled the song.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue refers to Maxim Gorky's play *The Lower Depths* (1902). Its cast includes the down-and-out characters Satine and the Actor; the play is set in a squalid boarding-house in Russia, and it ends with the Actor's off-stage suicide, prompting Satine's famous line that the death \"spoiled the song.\"\n\nThus the country in question is Russia.\n\n\\boxed{Russia}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 208, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 292}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00047, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_386", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One of this author's title characters declares \"We shall yet make these United States a moral nation!\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quote is spoken by the title character of the 1927 novel *Elmer Gantry*. That novel was written by Sinclair Lewis, whose other title characters (Babbitt, Arrowsmith, Dodsworth, etc.) likewise embody his satirical portraits of American moral and social hypocrisy.  \n\nThus the author referenced by the query is Sinclair Lewis.\n\n\\boxed{Sinclair Lewis}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 199, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 275}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00043875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_40", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A bearded figure in this novel \"wails with the vehemence of the ocean\" as he smites a giant crayfish with a bicycle pump.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel described is *The Third Policeman* by Flann O'Brien, in which a surreal scene involves a bearded figure attacking a giant crayfish with a bicycle pump while wailing \"with the vehemence of the ocean.\" This absurdist moment reflects the novel's darkly comic and philosophical tone.  \n\n\\boxed{The Third Policeman}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3861e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_403", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A main character of a play named for one of these events takes a garland of orange blossoms from her maid and throws them on the floor.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue references Lorca's *Blood Wedding* (*Bodas de sangre*), whose title names one of the events in question. In Act Two the Bride receives a crown of orange blossoms (a traditional wedding symbol) from her servant and angrily casts it to the floor, foreshadowing the violent disruption of the marriage. The same pattern of clues therefore identifies the events as weddings.\n\n\\boxed{weddings (Blood Wedding)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 209, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 293}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00047125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_408", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A character in this novel physically skips from side to side whilst delivering convoluted explanations, and is said to be able to turn black into white.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a specific character trait (physical skipping during convoluted speeches, combined with a talent for rhetorical inversion or sophistry) that matches Koroviev/Fagott in Bulgakov\u2019s The Master and Margarita. Koroviev is repeatedly shown skipping or dancing sideways while delivering deliberately tangled explanations, and the novel\u2019s other characters explicitly note his ability to \u201cturn black into white.\u201d No other widely read novel contains a figure whose mannerisms and reputation align so precisely with the given details.\n\n\\boxed{The Master and Margarita}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 208, "output_tokens": 103, "total_tokens": 311}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005175, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_412", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In one part of this poem, the protagonist has to climb aboard a creature with the wings of a dragon, the tail of a scorpion, and a face of an honest man in order to scale a cliff.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The description matches a key scene in Dante Alighieri's *Inferno* (part of the *Divine Comedy*), where the pilgrim and Virgil must descend a sheer cliff into the circle of fraud by riding the monster Geryon (explicitly depicted with an honest human face, draconic wings, and a venomous scorpion's tail). No other well-known poem contains this precise episode or creature. Thus the poem in question is most commonly identified as Dante's *Inferno*.\n\n\\boxed{Dante's Inferno (Divine Comedy)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 284, "output_tokens": 512, "total_tokens": 796}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:10:07.403252+00:00"}, "cost": 0.001635, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_42", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Osip Mandelstam wrote that this play's cast of characters constituted an \"inexpressive and colorless rebus\" that illustrated its author's tendency to portray \"propinquity with its resultant unpleasantness.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quote is from Osip Mandelstam\u2019s critical writings on Russian drama and directly targets the dramaturgy of Anton Chekhov. Mandelstam\u2019s two chief complaints\u2014colorless, puzzle-like characters and an obsessive focus on the claustrophobia of family relations\u2014map squarely onto the ensemble of The Cherry Orchard (the play in which Chekhov most fully realizes both traits). No other contemporary Russian play fits the description with equal precision.\n\n\\boxed{The Cherry Orchard (Chekhov)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 219, "output_tokens": 98, "total_tokens": 317}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00051875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_431", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The main character of this novel persuades her husband to buy a skinny yellow mule by comparing the sale to the Emancipation Proclamation.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel described is *Their Eyes Were Watching God* by Zora Neale Hurston. The main character, Janie Crawford, persuades her husband, Joe Starks, to buy the mule as an act of compassion, likening its liberation to the Emancipation Proclamation. This moment symbolizes freedom and empathy in the story.\n\n\\boxed{Their Eyes Were Watching God}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 88, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 167}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4147999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_435", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Michel Foucault coined the term \"noso-politics\" in an essay which discusses the integration of public and private administration of this profession during the 18th century.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Michel Foucault used the term \"noso-politics\" to describe the political and administrative management of disease, particularly in the context of medicine and public health. He discussed how the administration of health became intertwined with state power during the 18th century, blurring lines between public and private medical practices. The profession in question is medicine.\n\n\\boxed{medicine}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 172}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4445e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_445", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In an allusion to the Book of Isaiah, this author described a \"cup of trembling\" that glowed and shook as the title character plays the piano at the end of a short story.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The author being referred to is James Baldwin, in his short story \"Sonny's Blues.\" The \"cup of trembling\" is an allusion to Isaiah 51:17, symbolizing suffering and redemption, as the narrator reflects on Sonny's piano playing. The image captures the emotional and spiritual weight of their shared experience.\n\n\\boxed{James Baldwin}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 173}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4457999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_451", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An essay by Edmund Wilson asks why people read stories that focus on these kinds of people.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue refers to Edmund Wilson's well-known 1944 essay \"Why Do People Read Detective Stories?\", which analyzes the appeal of the mystery/detective genre. Such stories center on detectives (or, secondarily, the criminals they pursue) as the focal characters. This matches the phrasing about \"these kinds of people\" exactly, with no other Wilson essay fitting the description.\n\n\\boxed{detectives}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 198, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 279}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00045, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_460", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A novel set at one of these places opens by describing the annual arrival of an \"assembly of station wagons.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted phrase is the famous opening of Don DeLillo's *White Noise*, which depicts the yearly migration of station wagons to the fictional College-on-the-Hill. Because the novel is explicitly set on a college campus, the referent of \"these places\" must be college campuses (or universities). No other common setting matches the specific imagery of the annual station-wagon arrival.\n\n\\boxed{college campuses (White Noise)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 202, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 286}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_475", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: At the end of Zola's novel La bete humaine, Lantier and Pecqueux fall to their deaths from one of these objects.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "At the end of \u00c9mile Zola's novel *La B\u00eate humaine*, Lantier and P\u00e9cqueux die in a train accident, falling from a locomotive during a dramatic confrontation. The \"object\" referred to is a train, which is central to the novel's themes of industrialization and human passion. \n\n\\boxed{train}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 163}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3661e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_479", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This story's protagonist pictures \"a young man under a dripping tree\" and realizes he is imagining shades of the afterlife.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The story described is \"The Dead\" by James Joyce, in which the protagonist, Gabriel Conroy, has a moment of epiphany where he envisions a young man under a tree, symbolizing a connection to the transient nature of life and the afterlife. This image reflects themes of memory, death, and spiritual isolation. The correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{The Dead}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 163}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3864000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_491", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The appendix of a book in this genre includes a poem satirizing \"pious priests\" who attack \"Jack and Nell\" in the name of \"heavenly union.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query refers to Frederick Douglass's 1845 autobiography (full title: Narrative of the Life of Frederick Douglass, an American Slave). Its appendix reprints a Whittier parody that mocks pro-slavery clergymen for invoking \u201cheavenly union\u201d while abusing enslaved people named Jack and Nell. Works of this type constitute the genre known as the slave narrative.\n\n\\boxed{slave narrative}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 214, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 290}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004575, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_50", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Meisei University in Tokyo houses a copy of this document through which a bullet has penetrated half the pages.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The document is the **Gutenberg Bible**. A copy of this 15th-century printed Bible, held at Meisei University, features a bullet hole that passes through approximately half of its pages, likely sustained during a historical conflict.\n\n\\boxed{Gutenberg Bible}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 74, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 132}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:15.440335+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0001055, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_506", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The McGuffey Readers used many passages from this author to teach elocution to American students.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The McGuffey Readers used passages from William Shakespeare to teach elocution to American students. His works were valued for their rich language and dramatic expression, making them ideal for teaching reading and speaking skills. \n\n\\boxed{William Shakespeare}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 79, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 128}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0509e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_509", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a series of lectures, this author argued that \"the king died and then the queen died\" is a story, while \"the king died and then the queen died of grief\" is a plot.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The author who made this distinction between story and plot is E.M. Forster. He explained that a story is a sequence of events in time, while a plot involves causality and motivation. This famous example comes from his 1927 Clark Lectures, later published in \"Aspects of the Novel.\"\n\n\\boxed{E.M. Forster}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 174}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.45e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_514", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This author mourned \"Down, down, down into the darkness of the grave /\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given quote is the opening line of the poem \"Dirge Without Music,\" first published in 1928. Its author is the Pulitzer Prize-winning poet Edna St. Vincent Millay, who uses the verse to mourn the deaths of loved ones. No other well-known writer is associated with this specific phrasing.\n\n\\boxed{Edna St. Vincent Millay}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 197, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 270}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00042875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_534", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An author with this last name responded to the Brexit referendum by writing a 2016 novel that begins \"it was the worst of times, it was the worst of times.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The author is Ali Smith, whose 2016 novel *Autumn* opens with that specific variation of the famous Dickensian line. The novel is the first installment in her \"Seasonal Quartet,\" which explores the political climate of post-Brexit Britain.\n\n\\boxed{Smith}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 147}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:20.855507+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000108, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_542", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a play, one of these objects gradually loses its resemblance to Pan and becomes more Mephistophelean over the span of 14 years.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query is a quizbowl-style clue whose referent is established by two linked details: a dramatic work in which a single artwork ages and moralizes across a fixed interval, and the specific iconographic shift \u201cPan \u2192 Mephistopheles.\u201d Both map directly onto the portrait in theatrical adaptations of Wilde\u2019s *The Picture of Dorian Gray*; the novel\u2019s 18-year span is routinely compressed to 14 years on stage, and the text\u2019s description of the sitter\u2019s hair \u201clos[ing] its resemblance to Pan\u201d and becoming \u201cmore like Mephistopheles\u201d is retained verbatim. Consequently the class of objects named by the clue is portraits (or pictures).\n\n\\boxed{portraits (of Dorian Gray)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 210, "output_tokens": 145, "total_tokens": 355}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_553", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A character in this story describes how he always signs everything so he can hold up the crime to the punishment, see if they match, and determine whether he's been treated fairly.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted description matches a specific passage of dialogue in Alexandre Dumas's novel, in which the character Bertuccio explains his habit of signing his crimes so he can later compare them with any punishment received. This detail is unique to that work and does not appear in other well-known stories that treat similar themes of justice or imprisonment. Consequently, the story referenced by the query is The Count of Monte Cristo.\n\n\\boxed{The Count of Monte Cristo}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 215, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 302}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00048625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_559", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This character is subjected to an older woman's interminable conversation about the contents of a new letter from her niece, which this character escapes having read aloud to her.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a scene of social tedium in a classic English novel: an older, garrulous woman (Miss Bates) has just received a letter from her absent niece (Jane Fairfax) and launches into a rambling oral summary of its contents. The protagonist repeatedly tries to cut the visit short in order to avoid the even longer ordeal of having the letter read aloud verbatim.  \n\nThat scene occurs in Jane Austen\u2019s Emma (chapter 27 and several subsequent visits to the Bates apartment); the only character who fits every detail is therefore the novel\u2019s titular heroine.  \n\nNo other Austen novel, nor any other well-known work of the period, contains a matching incident.\n\n\\boxed{Emma Woodhouse}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 211, "output_tokens": 140, "total_tokens": 351}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00061375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_567", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In one of these works, the title character unwittingly convinces thieving servants of his clairvoyance after he follows sarcastic instructions to buy an alphabet book with a picture of a rooster in it.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The described scene matches a specific episode in Diderot\u2019s Jacques the Fatalist et son ma\u00eetre: after Jacques\u2019s master sarcastically tells him to buy \u201can alphabet with a picture of a rooster,\u201d Jacques returns with exactly that volume; the thieving servants, who have hidden the master\u2019s watch and money, interpret the purchase as proof of clairvoyance and return the stolen items.  \n\nNo other well-known work (Don Quixote, Lazarillo, the Arabian Nights, etc.) contains this precise combination of sarcastic instruction, primer-with-rooster, and duped servants.  \n\nThus the work referenced by the clue is Jacques the Fatalist.\n\n\\boxed{Jacques the Fatalist (Diderot)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 219, "output_tokens": 144, "total_tokens": 363}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00063375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_573", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A man in this play who was interrupted while trying to kill an animal claims to have exterminated only half of a rat.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes a specific, absurd exchange in which one character was interrupted mid-act while attempting to kill a vermin and therefore boasts only of a partial success. This exchange occurs in Harold Pinter\u2019s The Birthday Party, during the menacing interrogation scene in which McCann is questioned by Goldberg about having been stopped while \u201cexterminating\u201d a rat. No other well-known modern play contains a matching line or incident.\n\nThus the play referenced by the question is The Birthday Party.\n\n\\boxed{The Birthday Party}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 205, "output_tokens": 101, "total_tokens": 306}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00050875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_590", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An author from this movement contrasted phrases like \"white napkin\" and \"daylight\" or \"the world\" and \"a purse\" in a text that praises the novels of Matthew Lewis.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query is a tossup-style clue (likely from quiz bowl) whose answer is a literary/artistic movement. The key details are an author belonging to that movement, a text praising Matthew Lewis (author of the Gothic novel The Monk), and specific contrasting phrases that appear inside that text.\n\nThose phrases are taken directly from Andr\u00e9 Breton\u2019s Anthology of Black Humour (1940), whose entry on Lewis explicitly juxtaposes \u201cwhite napkin\u201d with \u201cdaylight,\u201d \u201cthe world\u201d with \u201ca purse,\u201d etc., to illustrate the convulsive, black-humor imagery Breton prized. Breton is the central theorist and practitioner of Surrealism; the anthology itself is a canonical Surrealist document. Hence the movement referenced by \u201cthis movement\u201d is Surrealism.\n\n\\boxed{Surrealism}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 218, "output_tokens": 160, "total_tokens": 378}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0006725, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_601", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A character in this play remembers a time when his son hit him in the face, before exclaiming \"Rotten kid!\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given clue is a standard trivia-style prompt (e.g., from quiz bowl or a similar knowledge test) whose expected referent is the title of the dramatic work in which the described scene occurs.  \n\nThe incident matches a flashback monologue delivered by the father, John Cleary, in Frank D. Gilroy\u2019s 1964 play The Subject Was Roses; after returning from military service, his son Timmy strikes him during an argument, prompting the exclamation \u201cRotten kid!\u201d  \n\nNo other well-known American play contains this precise combination of action and quoted line, confirming the identification.\n\n\\boxed{The Subject Was Roses}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 205, "output_tokens": 123, "total_tokens": 328}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00056375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_605", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: After a writer was banned in this country, a fellow poet wrote the lines \"only the trees know the pain as they stand still erect\u2026 their branches dry like wire.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The lines are from the poem \"The Trees\" by the Kenyan writer **Jared Angira**, which was written in response to the banning of the writer **Ng\u0169g\u0129 wa Thiong'o** in Kenya. The poem reflects the atmosphere of political repression and the silencing of voices during that period.\n\n\\boxed{Kenya}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 155}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:25.605256+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00012375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_620", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One member of this title group asserts that all militaries must be \"the finest in the world\" although navies are measured by tonnage.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The phrasing of the query is characteristic of a quizbowl-style clue, which points to a group sharing an identical proper name (i.e., a \u201ctitle group\u201d). Both states that bear that name routinely issue propaganda or official statements claiming to field \u201cthe strongest/finest military in the world,\u201d yet objective naval rankings are performed by aggregate tonnage\u2014a metric that separates the two claimants. The only polity pair that satisfies every element of the clue is therefore the two Koreas.\n\n\\boxed{the (two) Koreas}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 208, "output_tokens": 104, "total_tokens": 312}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00052, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_628", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A poem about one of these animals describes how it \"drops the silver chain of sound\" after it \"rises and begins to round.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted lines are taken directly from George Meredith\u2019s 1881 poem \u201cThe Lark Ascending,\u201d which opens with the skylark\u2019s characteristic spiraling flight and continuous song. Because the poem is explicitly about this bird, the animals referenced by the clue are larks (most commonly skylarks).  \n\n\\boxed{skylarks (larks)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 208, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 278}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000435, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_651", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 2004, the author of this play wrote a prequel in which one of its characters is slapped across the face by his wife Ann.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue identifies a well-known one-act play whose author later supplied it with an explicit prequel. In 2004 Edward Albee wrote the curtain-raiser \u201cHomelife,\u201d in which the protagonist Peter (the same character who later appears in the park in \u201cThe Zoo Story\u201d) is struck across the face by his wife Ann. The two pieces were subsequently performed together under the joint title \u201cPeter and Jerry,\u201d confirming that \u201cThe Zoo Story\u201d is the original work referenced.\n\nThus the play in question is The Zoo Story.\n\n\\boxed{The Zoo Story}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 210, "output_tokens": 113, "total_tokens": 323}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000545, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_653", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This person is actually the title character of the novel The Prince of India by Lew Wallace, in which he helps bring about the fall of Constantinople.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes the protagonist of Lew Wallace's 1893 novel *The Prince of India*, a historical romance centered on the 1453 fall of Constantinople. That protagonist is the legendary Wandering Jew (also called Salathiel or the Wandering Israelite), who is granted immortality after the Crucifixion and later appears in Constantinople as an Indian prince. The identification is confirmed by standard literary references to the work and by the novel's own plot summary.\n\n\\boxed{Wandering Jew (Salathiel)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 209, "output_tokens": 101, "total_tokens": 310}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00051375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_656", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A poet with this surname wrote about flowers that have \"forgotten\" their \"Eastern origin\" and become \"decent\" and \"reticent\" in America in a poem that describes them as \"False Blue, White, Purple.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted phrases identify the opening of Amy Lowell\u2019s poem \u201cLilacs,\u201d which personifies the flowers as having \u201cforgotten\u201d their \u201cEastern origin\u201d and adopted the restrained demeanor (\u201cdecent,\u201d \u201creticent\u201d) of New England. Because the poet\u2019s surname is therefore the required answer, the solution is Lowell.\n\n\\boxed{Lowell}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 227, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 297}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00045875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_659", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Insisting on the centrality of \"intellectual freedom,\" this essay cites at length Arthur Quiller-Couch's argument that \"the poor poet has not in these days, nor has had for two hundred years, a dog's chance.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted passage matches Virginia Woolf's extended discussion of the material and social conditions needed for literary creation. In the relevant section of the text, Woolf explicitly invokes \"intellectual freedom\" as a prerequisite for poetry and then reproduces Quiller-Couch's remark about the \"poor poet\" at length. No other well-known essay of the period centers this precise citation in the service of that argument.\n\nThus the work in question is Woolf's *A Room of One's Own*.\n\n\\boxed{A Room of One's Own (Woolf)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 226, "output_tokens": 107, "total_tokens": 333}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00055, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_667", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: While staying in this city, a man hears the story of Curran, a circus manager whose passion was founding a church exclusively for dogs.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The city being referenced is Dublin, as the story of Curran, a circus manager wanting to found a church for dogs, is a fictional anecdote associated with Dublin's eccentric tales. This story is often linked to the character of Curran in James Joyce's *Ulysses*, set in Dublin. \n\n\\boxed{Dublin}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 157}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3177e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_673", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A character who lives in this province envisions traveling with Banga on journeys to the sun and the moon.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes a character (likely a young girl) living in a Philippine province who imagines fantastical journeys alongside her banga (the distinctive clay pot traditionally balanced on the head). This directly matches the well-known Kalinga folktale tradition and its associated cultural imagery, in which the banga itself functions as a companion or vessel for such imagined travels to the sun and moon. No other Philippine province aligns with both the geographic setting and the specific banga motif.\n\n\\boxed{Kalinga}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 202, "output_tokens": 100, "total_tokens": 302}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005025, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_681", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Virginia Woolf highlighted a symbolic passage in this novel in which a plain earthenware pot allows the reader to see into the human soul.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question points to a specific observation by Virginia Woolf about the power of an everyday object in fiction. In her 1919 essay on Daniel Defoe, Woolf singles out the famous scene in which Robinson Crusoe painstakingly fashions a simple earthenware pot; she treats the pot as a transparent window onto the castaway\u2019s inner life, revealing the elemental human need for order, security, and self-sufficiency. No other novel matches this precise conjunction of Woolf\u2019s commentary and the symbolic vessel she describes.\n\nThus the novel in question is Robinson Crusoe.\n\n\\boxed{Robinson Crusoe}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 206, "output_tokens": 117, "total_tokens": 323}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00055, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_692", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a play set in this country, a woman opts to ride through town on a chair carried by two men instead of riding in a car; that woman earlier pulled an emergency cord to stop the \"Flying Dutchman.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The play described is *The Visit* by Friedrich D\u00fcrrenmatt, which is set in Switzerland. The woman who rides in a chair and stops the \"Flying Dutchman\" is Claire Zachanassian, and the setting of the fictional town of G\u00fcllen is in a German-speaking European country, commonly understood to be Switzerland. \n\n\\boxed{Switzerland}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 179}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4913000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_697", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a 2000 novel by Joyce Carol Oates, this real-life person is murdered by a government agent called the Sharpshooter.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The 2000 novel by Joyce Carol Oates is *Blonde*, a fictionalized account of Marilyn Monroe's life. In the novel, Marilyn Monroe is portrayed as being murdered by a government agent known as the Sharpshooter, reflecting conspiracy theories about her death. The real-life person in question is Marilyn Monroe.\n\n\\boxed{Marilyn Monroe}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 89, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 164}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3819e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_704", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In this work, a man is impressed into filling trenches dug by rebels in a nearby neighborhood.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given statement is a plot clue pointing to a specific literary work (likely drawn from an identification quiz, exam, or trivia set). The scene matches a key episode in Graham Greene's *The Power and the Glory*, in which the unnamed priest is conscripted by Red Shirts (the novel's secular rebels) to help fill in trenches containing the bodies of executed Cristeros.  \n\nNo other widely taught novel contains this precise incident, confirming the identification.\n\n\\boxed{The Power and the Glory (Greene)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 199, "output_tokens": 104, "total_tokens": 303}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00050875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_728", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a poem dedicated to his mother, this author described a felled chestnut tree as \"a soul ramifying and forever / silent, beyond silence listened for.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The author of the poem \"The Chestnut Tree,\" which contains the lines describing a felled tree as \"a soul ramifying and forever / silent, beyond silence listened for,\" is Seamus Heaney. The poem was written as a tribute to his mother, Margaret Kathleen Heaney.\n\n\\boxed{Seamus Heaney}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 150}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:24.360534+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00011875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_740", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A character created by this author contrasts \"spiritually married\" and \"spiritually unmarried\" men while defending socialism to Mr. Ferrenby.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted dialogue is spoken by Amory Blaine during a train-car debate near the end of the novel *This Side of Paradise*. Because Amory is a fictional creation of F. Scott Fitzgerald, the author referenced by the clue is Fitzgerald.\n\n\\boxed{F. Scott Fitzgerald}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 209, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 264}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00039875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_757", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A novel about this profession ends with Henry Wiggen lamenting \"from here on in, I rag nobody\" after Bruce Pearson dies of Hodgkin's disease.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes the final scene of Mark Harris's 1956 novel *Bang the Drum Slowly* (the second book in the Henry Wiggen tetralogy). In that novel Wiggen, a major-league pitcher, narrates the final season of his teammate and roommate Bruce Pearson, a catcher dying of Hodgkin's lymphoma; the quoted lament is the book's closing sentence. The shared profession of the two central characters is therefore baseball player (or, more narrowly, major-league baseball player).\n\n\\boxed{baseball player (Bang the Drum Slowly)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 211, "output_tokens": 111, "total_tokens": 322}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00054125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_758", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: At one point, a man tells the head of this place that he is holding his \"tool\" in his hand while lying under a blanket, implying that he is pleasuring himself rather than meditating.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The described scene involves a pun on the word \"tool\" (a meditation prop vs. a euphemism for genitalia) and takes place in a setting where residents are expected to meditate under blankets. Such a setting is classically a monastery (typically Buddhist or Zen), whose head is an abbot or similar superior. This matches the details exactly and is the most common cultural referent for the situation.\n\n\\boxed{monastery (abbot's)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 282, "output_tokens": 907, "total_tokens": 1189}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:48.941290+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00262, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_761", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Henry Green's novel Loving, Raunce, a character with this profession, begins a relationship with his younger coworker Edith.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Raunce is a butler in Henry Green's novel *Loving*. He works at a country house and develops a romantic interest in Edith, a younger housemaid. His profession is central to the social dynamics of the story.\n\n\\boxed{butler}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 86, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 140}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1506e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_763", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In this poem, one of the speakers recounts how she was beaten and stripped of her mantle by the \"sentinels of the walls\" making their rounds in the city.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The description matches a specific passage in the Song of Songs (also called the Song of Solomon or Canticles), in which the female speaker recounts being assaulted by the city watchmen after searching for her lover at night (5:7). This erotic poem, traditionally attributed to Solomon and forming part of the Hebrew Bible/Old Testament, is the only text that contains these precise narrative details. No other well-known poem reproduces the same episode with the sentinels \u201cof the walls.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{Song of Songs (5:7)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 215, "output_tokens": 107, "total_tokens": 322}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00053625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_771", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This character fondly recalls \"the triumphant conviction of strength, the heat of life in the handful of dust\" associated with the title attribute in a short story that concludes with his first vision of the East.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The character is Marlow, who reflects on the \"triumphant conviction of strength\" while contemplating the \"heart of darkness\" in Joseph Conrad's novella. The story concludes with Marlow's vision of the Thames leading into the \"heart of an immense darkness\" as he looks toward the East.\n\n\\boxed{Marlow}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 161}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:24.852418+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000124, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_780", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One of these people becomes a hero by saving a boy from drowning in a novel in which these people are impressed by a man's ability to shoot pheasants on the wing.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes a specific scene from Turgenev\u2019s *Fathers and Sons*. Bazarov (a nihilist) impresses the Kirsanov household by effortlessly shooting pheasants on the wing; later, the same nihilist circle is shown when Arkady\u2019s friend saves a peasant boy from drowning and is briefly lionized as a hero. Thus the group referred to by \u201cthese people\u201d is the nihilists.\n\n\\boxed{nihilists}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 277, "output_tokens": 1994, "total_tokens": 2271}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:58.272508+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00533125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_782", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Giles Allen sued the owners of this location for transporting a building from his land to this place while he was on vacation.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question refers to a famous incident from Elizabethan theater history. In 1598, while Giles Allen (the landlord) was away, the Lord Chamberlain's Men dismantled The Theatre in Shoreditch and carried its timbers across the Thames to construct the new Globe on Bankside; Allen later sued the company for theft of the building materials. Thus the location in question is the Globe Theatre.\n\n\\boxed{Globe Theatre (Bankside)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 266, "output_tokens": 538, "total_tokens": 804}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:10:07.294098+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0016775, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_795", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An analogue of this figure is said to be the only one of the giant race of the jentillak (JEN-tee-lahk) to survive the arrival of Christianity.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes Olentzero, the last surviving member of the jentillak (a race of Basque giants said to have vanished with the arrival of Christianity). Olentzero is a folkloric Christmas gift-bringer whose role and attributes are directly analogous to those of the modern Santa Claus/Father Christmas figure.  \n\nThus the referent of \u201cthis figure\u201d is Santa Claus.  \n\n\\boxed{Santa Claus}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 218, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 302}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004825, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_803", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a short story set in this country, a ten-year-old girl stops brushing her teeth to preserve the feeling of the candy she receives from the title character, a botany professor.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question requires identifying the country where a short story unfolds, with the plot centered on its title character (a botany professor) who gives candy to a 10-year-old girl; she then deliberately stops brushing her teeth so the sensation will linger.  \n\nThis matches the distinctive story \u201cO Professor de Bot\u00e2nica,\u201d whose author (Lygia Fagundes Telles) and setting are Brazilian; the narrative detail about the candy is sufficiently idiosyncratic to rule out other candidates.  \n\nHence the country in question is Brazil.\n\n\\boxed{Brazil}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 217, "output_tokens": 109, "total_tokens": 326}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00054375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_81", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A poem set \"at the fourth watch\" opens with the striking image of \"the mountains disgorging\" this object.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The poem described is \"The Fourth Watch\" by the Chinese poet Du Fu, which features the striking image of the mountains disgorging the moon. This imagery is a hallmark of his evocative landscape poetry.\n\n\\boxed{the moon}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 79, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 127}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:22.669329+00:00"}, "cost": 9.175e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_811", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In an essay, this author wondered at the pre-modern \"dry truthfulness\" with which Homer recorded the unequal value of the arms exchanged by Diomedes and Glaucus.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The author who famously discussed the \"dry truthfulness\" of Homer\u2019s account of the exchange between Diomedes and Glaucus is Erich Auerbach. He analyzes this passage in the opening chapter of his seminal work of literary criticism, *Mimesis: The Representation of Reality in Western Literature*.\n\n\\boxed{Erich Auerbach}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 160}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:07:25.202901+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0001275, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_829", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A poem addressed to this type of person notes that \"A honey tongue, a heart of gall, Is fancy's spring, but sorrow's fall.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted lines come from Sir Walter Raleigh\u2019s \u201cThe Nymph\u2019s Reply to the Shepherd,\u201d a direct rejoinder to Marlowe\u2019s \u201cThe Passionate Shepherd to His Love.\u201d In that poem the nymph systematically dismantles the shepherd\u2019s idyllic promises, declaring that \u201cA honey tongue, a heart of gall / Is fancy\u2019s spring, but sorrow\u2019s fall.\u201d The addressee is therefore explicitly a shepherd.\n\n\\boxed{shepherd}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 210, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 298}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004825, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_833", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A character in this novel is beaten to demonstrate that \"definitions belonged to the definers\u2014not the defined.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel being referenced is *Beloved* by Toni Morrison, in which Sethe is brutally beaten to assert control and power over her identity. This act symbolizes how those in power (the \"definers\") impose definitions and ownership on others (the \"defined\"). The correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{Beloved}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 80, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 146}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2280000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_842", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This novel's narrator laments that \"whatever lithophanic eternities\" might be provided for him cannot erase his deeds, leaving him nothing but the \"very local palliative of articulate art.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted passage employs characteristically Nabokovian diction (\u201clithophanic eternities,\u201d \u201clocal palliative of articulate art\u201d) and is spoken by a posthumous narrator who reflects on the limits of both immortality and artistic consolation. These elements converge uniquely in the 1972 novel Transparent Things, whose ghostly narrator comments on the life and death of Hugh Person from beyond the grave. No other Nabokov work (Pale Fire, Lolita, Ada) contains this precise phrasing or narrative situation.\n\nThus the novel in question is Transparent Things.\n\n\\boxed{Transparent Things (Nabokov)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 218, "output_tokens": 119, "total_tokens": 337}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00057, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_845", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This man wrote an article about the employees at the Office of Economic Opportunity in San Francisco, whom he dubbed \"Flak Catchers\" taking abuse from \"mau-mauers.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The man who wrote the article about the employees at the Office of Economic Opportunity in San Francisco, referring to them as \"Flak Catchers\" dealing with \"mau-mauers,\" was Tom Wolfe. This piece, titled \"The Me Decade and the Third Great Awakening,\" showcased his signature style of New Journalism. The term \"mau-mauers\" was used controversially to describe aggressive activists.\n\n\\boxed{Tom Wolfe}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 90, "total_tokens": 186}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5816e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_861", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This character owned a loom decorated with a picture of Apollo changing his course, and used it to depict the quarrel between Atreus and Thyestes.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The character described is Arachne, a skilled weaver in Greek mythology who challenged Athena to a weaving contest. Her loom depicted various myths, including Apollo altering his course and the conflict between Atreus and Thyestes. Arachne's hubris led to her transformation into a spider by Athena.\n\n\\boxed{Arachne}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 162}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3532e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_876", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Late in a play, this character reverses an insult about being called a \"squashed cabbage leaf.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query refers to a key moment in George Bernard Shaw\u2019s *Pygmalion*. Early in the play Professor Higgins insults the flower-girl Eliza Doolittle by calling her \u201ca squashed cabbage leaf.\u201d In the final act she deliberately hurls the same phrase back at him, thereby \u201creversing\u201d the insult and demonstrating her new social and verbal equality.\n\nThus the character in question is Eliza Doolittle.\n\n\\boxed{Eliza Doolittle (Pygmalion)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 200, "output_tokens": 99, "total_tokens": 299}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004975, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_881", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: After browsing a library containing Paracelsus and Roger Bacon, a woman in this story weeps against the cover of a journal recording how all the projects of a man's life have fallen short of their aims.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The described scene matches a pivotal moment in Nathaniel Hawthorne\u2019s short story \u201cThe Birth-Mark.\u201d Georgiana, while alone in Aylmer\u2019s laboratory, examines his folio of alchemical writings (explicitly naming Paracelsus, Cornelius Agrippa, and Roger Bacon) and then discovers his private journal, whose entries record a lifetime of failed experiments; she weeps over the volume\u2019s cover in recognition of her husband\u2019s thwarted ambitions. No other Hawthorne tale or contemporaneous work reproduces this precise sequence of library, journal, and weeping.\n\n\\boxed{The Birth-Mark (Hawthorne)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 222, "output_tokens": 115, "total_tokens": 337}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000565, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_885", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The protagonist of a novel titled for this entity is forced to pose for visitors at the Museum of Natural Wonders and is pursued by Ridgeway.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The novel described is *The Underground Railroad* by Colson Whitehead. The protagonist, Cora, is referred to as the \"entity\" in the metaphorical sense, as the novel personifies the Underground Railroad itself. However, the most common answer to this question, based on the phrasing and context, is the **Underground Railroad**.\n\n\\boxed{Underground Railroad}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 195}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6483999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_889", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the second stanza of a poem addressed to one of these things, the speaker says \"I would, before my time to go, / Sing of old Eire and the ancient ways.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted lines are from W. B. Yeats\u2019s \u201cTo the Rose upon the Rood of Time,\u201d whose opening and closing apostrophes make clear that the poem is addressed to a rose. In quiz-bowl or crossword contexts the same lines are conventionally used as a clue for the answer \u201croses.\u201d  \n\nThus the referent of \u201cthese things\u201d is roses.\n\n\\boxed{roses}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 218, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 298}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004725, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_891", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The brother of the title character of Roddy Doyle's novel  Paddy Clarke Ha Ha Ha  is nicknamed for this character, whose daughter Yasmin falls in love with an American called \"Somebody\" in a John Barth novel.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The nickname refers to \"Sinbad,\" the brother of Paddy Clarke in Roddy Doyle's novel. Sinbad is also the name of the sailor from the Arabian Nights, whose daughter Yasmin appears in John Barth's *The Last Voyage of Somebody the Sailor*, where she falls in love with the protagonist, \"Somebody.\" The correct and most common answer is:\n\n\\boxed{Sinbad}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 187}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5626e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_898", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This character suggests that every man \"see to the restoration of his own land\" in a refusal to join men with \"sheets and hoods and night-galloping horses.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The character described is Atticus Finch from Harper Lee's *To Kill a Mockingbird*. He refuses to join the Ku Klux Klan and advocates for individual moral responsibility, urging each man to \"see to the restoration of his own land\" rather than engage in secretive, hateful acts. This moment reflects his commitment to justice and personal integrity.\n\n\\boxed{Atticus Finch}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 171}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4373999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_906", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The opening two words \"Smart lad\" in this poem's third quatrain are both stressed, breaking the otherwise iambic tetrameter of the poem.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given statement is a specific identifying clue about a well-known lyric poem written in quatrains. The only poem that matches the metrical detail (regular iambic tetrameter interrupted by the spondaic \u201cSmart lad\u201d at the start of the third stanza) is A. E. Housman\u2019s \u201cTo an Athlete Dying Young.\u201d\n\nThus the answer required by the query is the title (or author + title) of that poem.\n\n\\boxed{To an Athlete Dying Young (Housman)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 213, "output_tokens": 103, "total_tokens": 316}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00052375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_916", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In one story by this author, the 104-year-old general George Poker Sash dies onstage in a wheelchair at a graduation before his granddaughter Sally collects her diploma.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The described scene is the climax of Flannery O\u2019Connor\u2019s short story \u201cA Late Encounter with the Enemy,\u201d in which the centenarian Confederate veteran General George Poker Sash collapses during his granddaughter Sally\u2019s college graduation. O\u2019Connor\u2019s recurring Southern Gothic motifs\u2014grotesque elderly figures, mordant humor, and sudden death\u2014make the identification unmistakable. No other author matches both the specific character names and the precise episode.\n\n\\boxed{Flannery O'Connor}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 213, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 308}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00050375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_920", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This character makes a \"great and edifying entertainment\" out of the adventures of his demon in a Kafka parable revealing the \"Truth about\" this character.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question refers to a Kafka parable titled \"The Truth about Sancho Panza,\" in which Kafka reimagines Don Quixote's squire, Sancho Panza, as the wise figure who deliberately employs Don Quixote (the demon) as a form of \"great and edifying entertainment.\" In this reinterpretation, Sancho Panza is not the fool but the enlightened one who uses the adventures to maintain spiritual balance. The character in question is thus Sancho Panza.\n\n\\boxed{Sancho Panza}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 108, "total_tokens": 199}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.7261e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_930", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Characters in this novel make banana jam despite it being illegal for being \"too thin for jelly and too thick for jam.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted description of illegal banana jam matches a key plot point from Arundhati Roy\u2019s 1997 novel, in which the characters operate a pickle factory that also produces the nonconforming preserve. No other well-known work of fiction contains this specific legal and culinary detail.  \n\nThus the novel in question is *The God of Small Things*.\n\n\\boxed{The God of Small Things}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 204, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 281}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004475, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_948", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This poet declared that \"two poetries are ever competing, a cooked and a raw\" in an acceptance speech for a 1960 National Book Award.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The poet who stated that \"two poetries are ever competing, a cooked and a raw\" in his 1960 National Book Award acceptance speech was Robert Lowell. He used this metaphor to describe the tension between highly crafted, formal poetry (\"cooked\") and more spontaneous, confessional styles (\"raw\"). This speech is often seen as a pivotal moment in the development of confessional poetry.\n\n\\boxed{Robert Lowell}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 178}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5131999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_966", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In this country, a slaughterhouse where the workers drink blood employs Kurt, whose friends share Lola's diary after her suicide.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question appears to reference elements from the novel *Lola & Milla* by Andreas Steinh\u00f6fel, which is set in Germany. The surreal and symbolic details\u2014such as workers drinking blood and the sharing of Lola's diary\u2014align with the novel's themes and setting. Therefore, the country in question is Germany.\n\n\\boxed{Germany}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 186}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5671e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_974", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A man who engages in this activity with \"pure Teutonic pleasure\" is one of the two subjects of John McPhee's \"double profile\"  Levels of the Game .\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The activity referred to is playing tennis. The two subjects of John McPhee's \"Levels of the Game\" are Clark Graebner and Arthur Ashe, with Graebner described as playing with \"pure Teutonic pleasure.\" The correct answer is tennis.\n\n\\boxed{tennis}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 156}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2815999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Literature_980", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: To worship a god represented by these animals, a character recites nonsense lineages such as \"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query provides an incomplete clue describing a fictional religious practice (nonsense genealogies recited to honor a deity whose form or avatars are the animals in question). This is a recognizable reference to the feline cult in Neil Gaiman\u2019s Sandman story \u201cA Dream of a Thousand Cats,\u201d where cats worship a great feline goddess and intone absurd ancestral lists. Hence the animals are cats.\n\n\\boxed{cats (Gaiman's Sandman)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 198, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 285}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000465, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_10", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The brother of Julian Barnes, Jonathan Barnes, has written about this school of thought in works titled for its \"toils\" and \"modes.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question points to philosopher Jonathan Barnes (brother of novelist Julian Barnes), whose scholarship focuses on Hellenistic philosophy. His books *The Toils of Scepticism* and *The Modes of Scepticism* (the latter co-authored with Julia Annas) analyze the argumentative strategies and \u201cmodes\u201d (e.g., those of Agrippa) employed by the Pyrrhonian sceptics. The school of thought in question is therefore ancient scepticism (or Pyrrhonism).\n\n\\boxed{skepticism (Pyrrhonism)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 209, "output_tokens": 107, "total_tokens": 316}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00052875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_1129", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Meinong's jungle consists of items that do not exist but still have a form of this property.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Meinong's theory of objects posits a distinction between existence (a spatiotemporal property) and the broader notion of being, which encompasses subsistence for ideal or abstract entities. Nonexistent objects (e.g., golden mountains or round squares) are therefore granted a Sosein, or \"being-so,\" allowing them to possess properties without existing. This populates Meinong's \"jungle\" with items that have a attenuated form of being.\n\n\\boxed{being (Sosein)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 200, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 295}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_1224", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This book argues that the automation of labor turns \"apparatuses we once handled freely\" into \"shells...as...belong to the body of the turtle.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted argument is a direct reference to Hannah Arendt\u2019s analysis of modern labor and technology. In *The Human Condition* (especially Part IV, \u201cWork\u201d), Arendt observes that automation converts once-manipulable instruments into prosthetic \u201cshells\u201d fused to the worker, much as a turtle\u2019s shell is fused to its body. No other major text on automation employs this precise imagery or phrasing.\n\nThus the book in question is *The Human Condition*.\n\n\\boxed{The Human Condition (Arendt)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 214, "output_tokens": 99, "total_tokens": 313}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000515, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_1246", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An opponent of this theory argued that the answer to the question \"What is the aim of chess?\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question fragment refers to a philosophical debate (likely over game formalism or similar theories) in which an opponent points out that chess has a single, obvious objective. That objective is to checkmate the opponent\u2019s king, which is the universally accepted definition found in the rules of chess and in standard gameplay descriptions.\n\nAny deeper strategic goals (capturing material, controlling the center, etc.) are merely means to that end. Hence the most common, concise answer to the question is simply \u201ccheckmate.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{checkmate opponent's king}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 200, "output_tokens": 107, "total_tokens": 307}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005175, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_1270", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In one paper, this philosopher muses that realism solves Nelson Goodman's new \"riddle of induction\" by positing \"perfectly natural\" properties that \"carve nature at the joints.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The philosopher referred to is David Lewis, who proposed that realism about \"perfectly natural\" properties can address Nelson Goodman's new riddle of induction by providing a metaphysical basis for projectible predicates.\n\nLewis argued that these natural properties, which \"carve nature at the joints,\" allow for a principled distinction between genuine patterns and accidental regularities.\n\n\\boxed{David Lewis}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 175}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4658e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_1342", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A pragmatist interpretation of this text was illustrated through the example of a judge who applies precedents to decide on tort law in A Spirit of Trust, an analytic re-con guring of this text by Robert Brandom.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given clue describes a philosophical work subjected to a pragmatist reinterpretation. Brandom's *A Spirit of Trust* (2019) is explicitly framed as a neo-analytic, inferentialist reworking of Hegel's *Phenomenology of Spirit*; its central running example of a common-law judge extending tort precedents is used to illustrate the recognitive, historical, and normative dimensions of Spirit. Hence the referent of \u201cthis text\u201d is Hegel's *Phenomenology*.\n\n\\boxed{Phen. of Spirit (Hegel)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 223, "output_tokens": 106, "total_tokens": 329}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00054375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_135", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A work by this thinker analyzes the difference between the Greek verbs archein and prattein to illustrate how rulers have monopolized the strength of others, creating a \"delusion of extraordinary strength.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The thinker described is Hannah Arendt, who in her work *The Human Condition* examines the Greek verbs *archein* (to begin, to rule) and *prattein* (to act) to explore how political action and leadership have been distorted. She argues that rulers have historically monopolized the capacity for action, fostering a false perception of singular, extraordinary power. This analysis aligns with her critique of how authority and action are misunderstood in modern politics.\n\n\\boxed{Hannah Arendt}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 104, "total_tokens": 201}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.7287e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_1355", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: These concepts title a Philip Fisher intellectual history which discusses their \"abolition of privacy.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question is a quiz-style clue pointing to a specific book title consisting of two concepts. Philip Fisher's monograph *The Vehement Passions* centers on the Aristotelian pair pity and fear (sometimes rendered \u201cpity and terror\u201d), arguing that these vehement passions produce an \u201cabolition of privacy\u201d by dissolving the boundary between self and other. No other Fisher title matches the phrasing, confirming that the two concepts named in the clue are pity and fear.\n\n\\boxed{pity & fear (vehement passions)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 197, "output_tokens": 100, "total_tokens": 297}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00049625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_1403", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An essay titled for this question discusses a prior text as the possible origin of an ongoing \"critical ontology of ourselves\" and cites Baudelaire to sketch a four-point outline of the related \"attitude of modernity.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given description matches Michel Foucault's 1984 essay \"What Is Enlightenment?\", which opens by positioning Kant's 1784 text of the same name as the starting point of an unfinished \"critical ontology of ourselves.\" Foucault then turns to Baudelaire's writings on modernity to enumerate four constitutive attitudes (awareness of the present as heroic, ascetic elaboration of the self, ironic heroism, and the invention of the self as a work of art). This yields the quiz-bowl-style answer \"What Is Enlightenment?\"\n\n\\boxed{What Is Enlightenment? (Foucault)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 222, "output_tokens": 112, "total_tokens": 334}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005575, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_143", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This work argues that scientific laws are used as \"inference-tickets\" between factual statements as part of its argument that not all indicative sentences report facts.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The description matches Gilbert Ryle's well-known account of nomological statements. In that work Ryle explicitly characterizes scientific laws as \u201cinference-tickets\u201d that license transitions between particular factual assertions rather than themselves stating additional facts; this is part of his broader claim that many well-formed indicative sentences (including law-statements and dispositional attributions) do not function as reports of empirical fact. The same thesis appears in several of Ryle\u2019s essays, but it receives its most influential and extended treatment in The Concept of Mind.\n\n\\boxed{The Concept of Mind (Ryle)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 210, "output_tokens": 113, "total_tokens": 323}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000545, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_1446", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One section of this book lists the restrictions imposed by the Hindu caste system on the chandala and finds that \"undying chandala hatred\" has been disguised as love.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The book described is likely *The Annihilation of Caste* by B.R. Ambedkar, which critically examines the Hindu caste system and its oppressive structures. In it, Ambedkar discusses how the chandala (or Dalit) communities have been systematically marginalized and how religious texts often mask social oppression as spiritual duty. The correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{The Annihilation of Caste}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 178}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5044999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_1458", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A thinker described how complex \"molecular\" versions of these entities arise from four \"incidents,\" which he listed in tables of opposites and correlatives.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes a logical system in which atomic propositions combine into compound (\u201cmolecular\u201d) ones. The four \u201cincidents\u201d are precisely the relations (contradictories, contraries, subcontraries, subalterns) displayed in the traditional square of opposition and its associated tables of correlatives. These relations were classically used to generate the full set of molecular propositions from the four basic categorical forms, making \u201cpropositions\u201d the entity referred to.\n\n\\boxed{propositions}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 210, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 305}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_1480", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This thinker argued that because theoretical statements are not translatable into statements about the immediate objects of experience without a loss of meaningful content, \"descriptivist\" interpretations of theories inevitably collapse into \"instrumentalist\" interpretations.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question concerns a philosopher of science who analyzed the semantics of theories in terms of the observational-theoretical distinction. The key claim is that any attempt to treat a theory as a literal description of unobservables (descriptivism) must fail once it is granted that theoretical statements cannot be fully reconstructed in an observational vocabulary; the only remaining coherent option is therefore to treat theories merely as predictive instruments (instrumentalism). This exact line of argument appears in Carl G. Hempel\u2019s \u201cThe Theoretician\u2019s Dilemma\u201d (1958), which therefore identifies the thinker in question.\n\n\\boxed{C. G. Hempel}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 223, "output_tokens": 124, "total_tokens": 347}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00058875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_1537", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A mode of analysis based on these entities was pioneered in a book subtitled for the \"study of the history\" of one of them, which uses the principles of continuity and plentitude to analyze a concept that was developed in an Alexander Pope poem; that book, which advocated for a \"history\" of these entities, is The Great Chain of Being by Arthur Lovejoy.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given paragraph is a quizbowl-style tossup clue whose structure points to the entities being analyzed. Lovejoy's 1936 monograph explicitly calls for (and exemplifies) a \"history of ideas,\" treating the Great Chain of Being as a composite of simpler, persistent \"unit-ideas\" whose development can be traced via the principles of plenitude and continuity (the latter drawn from Pope). Hence the entities in question are unit-ideas (or simply ideas).\n\n\\boxed{unit-ideas (ideas)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 256, "output_tokens": 101, "total_tokens": 357}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005725, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_1540", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Fred Dretske (DRET-\"ski\") used the example of the possibility of a zebra being a cleverly disguised mule to illustrate his \"relative alternatives\" theory of this concept.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question pertains to epistemology, specifically Fred Dretske's relevant-alternatives account (sometimes phrased with the near-synonym \"relative\"). In that account, an agent can be said to know a proposition \\(P\\) provided she can eliminate all contextually relevant alternatives to \\(P\\); far-fetched possibilities (such as a zebra being a painted mule) are simply irrelevant to the truth of the knowledge claim. Hence the concept illustrated by the example is knowledge itself.\n\n\\boxed{knowledge (rel. alt. theory)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 216, "output_tokens": 106, "total_tokens": 322}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000535, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_1570", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This book argues that nonsense shouldn't be understood as gibberish but rather as something that lies beyond the limits of sense.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The description matches the core argument of Wittgenstein's early philosophy, in which meaningful language is bounded by logical form and \"the limits of the world.\" Any attempt to speak about ethics, aesthetics, or metaphysics falls outside those bounds and is therefore classified as nonsense\u2014not mere gibberish or error, but something that can only be shown rather than said. This is the central claim of the Tractatus Logico-Philosophicus (especially propositions 6.4\u20137).\n\n\\boxed{Tractatus Logico-Philosophicus (Wittgenstein)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 203, "output_tokens": 106, "total_tokens": 309}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00051875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_1588", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: With Michael Maccoby, this thinker studied the social character of peons, free campesinos, and entrepreneurs in a Mexican village.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The thinker who studied the social character of peons, free campesinos, and entrepreneurs in a Mexican village with Michael Maccoby is Erich Fromm. Their collaborative research was published in the book *Social Character in a Mexican Village* (1970), which applied Fromm's psychoanalytic and sociological theories to understand how economic roles shape personality. \n\n\\boxed{Erich Fromm}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 172}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4677e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_1640", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This is the  rst word in the title of a book whose second title concept is de ned as a necessarily destructive rupture that changes an existing order and that creates a new order; that book claims this concept cannot be conceptualized as a \"one\" and must be understood as a \"pure multiple,\" and that book also uses Zermelo\u00c2\u2013Frankel theory to make the claim that mathematics is the study of this concept, and the study of this concept \"is a situation.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The book described is *Being and Event* by Alain Badiou. The first word in the title is \"Being,\" and the concept discussed\u2014defined as a destructive rupture creating a new order, understood as a \"pure multiple\"\u2014is central to Badiou's use of set theory (Zermelo\u2013Fraenkel) to argue that mathematics is the science of being qua being. The study of being, for Badiou, \"is a situation.\"\n\n\\boxed{Being}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 156, "output_tokens": 101, "total_tokens": 257}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.1176000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_1651", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A book titled a\u1978er this concept illustrates an old conception of it with the con\u1978ict between the \"king of the vultures\" and an \"animal of prey stronger than the rest.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question describes a passage from J.S. Mill's *On Liberty* that contrasts an older, purely negative conception of liberty (protection from the \"king of the vultures\" ruler) with newer, positive limits on authority. The book is therefore titled after the concept of liberty itself. This matches the quoted language exactly and is the standard referent in philosophy and political-theory quiz contexts.\n\n\\boxed{liberty}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 223, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 306}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00048625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_1667", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a 1998 book proposing a \"theory\" of this phenomenon, Bernard Baars proposed a computational architecture for it called the \"global workspace theory.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Bernard Baars proposed the \"global workspace theory\" to explain consciousness. This theory likens consciousness to a global workspace in the brain where information is broadcast and made available to various cognitive processes. The phenomenon in question is consciousness.\n\n\\boxed{consciousness}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 144}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1731999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_1775", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One character in this work dies in a ditch while waiting for a messenger to return from a diviner.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a specific plot point involving a death by misadventure (in a ditch, while awaiting news from an oracle/diviner). This matches a minor episode recounted in Wole Soyinka\u2019s play *Death and the King\u2019s Horseman*, whose central action revolves around ritual suicide, divination, and messengers carrying intelligence between the worlds of the living and the dead.  \n\nNo other well-known work (Greek tragedy, Brecht, Shakespeare, Achebe, etc.) contains an incident that aligns on all three details simultaneously.  \n\nThus the work in question is *Death and the King\u2019s Horseman*.\n\n\\boxed{Death & the King's Horseman (Soyinka)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 201, "output_tokens": 133, "total_tokens": 334}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00058375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_1818", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This philosopher used a pressure-pad-activated statue of Neptune that threatened oncomers with his trident as a model for the mechanistic nature of the body.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The description matches Ren\u00e9 Descartes' famous analogy (drawn from his visits to the Royal Gardens at Saint-Germain-en-Laye) between hydraulic automata and the mechanistic operations of the body. In works such as the Treatise on Man, Descartes explicitly invokes pressure-activated statues\u2014including one of Neptune wielding a trident\u2014to illustrate how sensory input, nerves, and muscular action can be explained purely in terms of physical causation without invoking a non-material soul for non-human animals or the body\u2019s automatic functions. No other early-modern philosopher is recorded as having used this particular garden-statue example.\n\n\\boxed{Descartes (Ren\u00e9)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 210, "output_tokens": 121, "total_tokens": 331}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000565, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_1841", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 1986 book argued that this character's repeated use of the word exaiphnes (ex-ah-EEF-nace) makes his central image \"the lightning bolt,\" which \u754clashes like the sun in \"later paintings of Turner.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query is a quizbowl-style clue pointing to a specific literary/philosophical character. The Greek adverb \\(\\text{exaiphnes}\\) (\u201csuddenly\u201d) is repeatedly foregrounded in a 1986 monograph whose central thesis equates that word with the image of the lightning bolt; the same monograph links the bolt\u2019s sudden solar flare to the late Turner canvases. Those motifs converge uniquely on the protagonist of Nietzsche\u2019s *Thus Spoke Zarathustra*, whose signature declarations (\u201cI am lightning,\u201d \u201cthe \u00dcbermensch shall be like lightning\u201d) and abrupt, epiphanic appearances are repeatedly signaled by the same adverb in Nietzsche\u2019s German rendering. No other figure satisfies every element of the clue.\n\n\\boxed{Zarathustra (Nietzsche)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 229, "output_tokens": 150, "total_tokens": 379}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00066125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_1857", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In an essay from The Interpretation of Cultures, Cli\u9d01ford Geertz distinguished the \"interest theory\" of this concept from its \"strain theory\" while analyzing it \"as a Cultural System.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In his essay \"Ideology as a Cultural System,\" Clifford Geertz contrasts the \"interest theory\" and the \"strain theory\" to explain the social function of ideology. He argues that these theories view ideology as a response to either social conflict or psychological tension.\n\n\\boxed{Ideology}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 153}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:59:33.851347+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000112, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_325", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A book about this concept likens it to the capacity to chop, possessed by an axe, and the power of sight, possessed by an eye.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question references Aristotle's treatise *De Anima* (On the Soul). In Book II, Aristotle explicitly employs the axe/chopping and eye/sight analogies to define soul as the form or first actuality of a natural body that has life potentially. Thus the concept in view is simply the soul (or Aristotelian psyche).\n\n\\boxed{soul (Aristotle/De Anima)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 210, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 285}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00045, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_342", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Fictional \"epistles\" named for this school of thought were popular throughout the Roman empire.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue refers to the Cynic epistles, a well-known body of pseudepigraphic letters (many composed in the Roman period) that purport to be written by or about famous Cynic philosophers such as Diogenes and Crates. These fictional letters were widely circulated and read throughout the Roman Empire as vehicles for Cynic moral teaching. No other ancient school (Stoic, Epicurean, etc.) produced a comparable corpus of \u201cschool-named\u201d epistles.\n\n\\boxed{Cynicism (Cynics)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 199, "output_tokens": 103, "total_tokens": 302}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00050625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_373", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This man justified the acquisition of property as long as that property is not left to spoil and \"enough and as good\" are left for others.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The man described is John Locke, who argued that individuals can acquire private property through labor, as long as they do not take more than they can use without spoiling it, and \"enough and as good\" remains for others. This principle is central to his theory of property in the *Second Treatise of Government*. His justification laid the foundation for liberal views on property rights.\n\n\\boxed{John Locke}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 89, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 172}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4619e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_458", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This man claims that he is not a politician because a daimon, or divine sign, has always come to him and stopped him from becoming one.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The man referred to is Socrates, who claimed that a divine sign, or daimonion, often warned him against engaging in politics. He used this as a reason for not pursuing a political career, believing the sign would not have consistently opposed it if it were right for him. This is well-documented in Plato's dialogues, particularly in the \"Apology.\"\n\n\\boxed{Socrates}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 173}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4690000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_464", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In one book, this philosopher defined the state as the \"march of God in the world.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The philosopher who described the state as the \"march of God in the world\" is Georg Wilhelm Friedrich Hegel. This quote reflects his view of the state as the embodiment of rationality and ethical life. \n\n\\boxed{Hegel}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 79, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 130}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0709e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_499", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Mandukya Upanishad (mon-DOOK-yuh oo-PA-ni-shad) describes how the middle letter in the word \"A-U-M\" represents this activity, which is known as \"svapna.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The middle letter \"U\" in \"A-U-M\" represents the dream state, known as \"svapna,\" according to the Mandukya Upanishad. This state is associated with the subtle body and internal experiences during sleep. \n\n\\boxed{dreaming}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3367999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_518", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This book proposes that Socrates dies at the moment of the death verdict and considers his response to the verdict as his last words.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query requires identifying a modern interpretive monograph (not a primary source such as Plato\u2019s Apology) whose central thesis is that Socrates\u2019 philosophical death occurs at the pronouncement of the death sentence, rendering his subsequent remarks his \u201clast words.\u201d  \n\nBrickhouse & Smith\u2019s Socrates on Trial advances precisely this claim: after the jury\u2019s final verdict Socrates is already \u201cdead\u201d in the civic and existential sense, so the speech that follows functions as a posthumous address.  \n\nNo other widely cited study (Guardini, Wilson, Kofman, etc.) frames the chronology in exactly these terms.\n\n\\boxed{Socrates on Trial (Brickhouse/Smith)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 205, "output_tokens": 132, "total_tokens": 337}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00058625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_569", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A book about this subject is in the form of dialogues at the Orti Oricellari between Florentine aristocrats like Lord Fabrizio Colonna.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The book described is *The Prince* by Niccol\u00f2 Machiavelli, which is sometimes confused with his other work, *Discourses on Livy*. However, the work presented as dialogues at the Orti Oricellari involving Florentine aristocrats such as Fabrizio Colonna is *The Art of War* (also known as *Dell'arte della guerra*). This dialogue features Colonna as a central figure discussing military tactics and political theory.\n\n\\boxed{The Art of War}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 107, "total_tokens": 200}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.7303e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_611", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This philosopher disagreed with Kant's assessment that human beings are driven to ethical actions thanks to a categorical imperative due to its egoistic nature.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The philosopher in question is Arthur Schopenhauer, whose 1840 essay \"On the Basis of Morality\" directly attacks Kant's framework. Schopenhauer contends that the categorical imperative, despite its universalist rhetoric, reduces to an egoistic hypothetical (i.e., \"I ought to act this way lest I contradict my own rational nature\"), thereby grounding ethics in self-interest rather than genuine compassion for others. This critique aligns precisely with the query's phrasing and is the standard historical reference.\n\n\\boxed{Schopenhauer}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 269, "output_tokens": 438, "total_tokens": 707}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:44.824610+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00143125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_642", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Bernard Williams interprets the use of \"I\" in this work to refer to the reader, a view he put forth in a book about its author's \"Project of Pure Inquiry.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue identifies a work by Descartes, given Williams's book *Descartes: The Project of Pure Enquiry*. Williams's reading of the first-person pronoun in that work treats it as an impersonal, representative \u201cI\u201d that any rational reader can occupy while performing the meditation. The text that fits is therefore Descartes\u2019s *Meditations on First Philosophy*.\n\n\\boxed{Meditations (Descartes)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 215, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 294}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00046625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_646", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This philosopher argued that Hegel founded an anti-metaphysical tradition and helped turn philosophy into a literary genre in a book that contrasts Nietzsche's and Heidegger's achievements in self-creation with that of Proust.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The philosopher who argued that Hegel founded an anti-metaphysical tradition and helped turn philosophy into a literary genre, while contrasting Nietzsche, Heidegger, and Proust in terms of self-creation, is Richard Rorty. This argument appears in his book *Contingency, Irony, and Solidarity*, where he reinterprets philosophical traditions through a literary and pragmatic lens. Rorty emphasizes narrative and self-creation over systematic metaphysics.\n\n\\boxed{Richard Rorty}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 103, "total_tokens": 208}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.7755e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_675", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Percy Shelley wrote a \"Discourse on the Manners of the Ancient Greeks\" to accompany his translation of this work.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question refers to a specific translation by Percy Bysshe Shelley. Shelley produced an 1818 English version of Plato\u2019s *Symposium* (which he titled *The Banquet*) and prefaced it with the essay \u201cA Discourse on the Manners of the Ancient Greeks Relative to the Subject of Love,\u201d written to address the homoerotic content of the dialogue for a contemporary audience. No other classical work is associated with this particular essay and translation.\n\nThus the work in question is Plato\u2019s *Symposium*.\n\n\\boxed{Plato's Symposium (The Banquet)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 204, "output_tokens": 114, "total_tokens": 318}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00054, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_683", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: John B. Cobb wrote an introduction to theological approaches based on the metaphysics of this philosopher, whose ideas were also extended to theology by Charles Hartshorne.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "John B. Cobb wrote an introduction to theological approaches based on the metaphysics of Alfred North Whitehead, whose process philosophy was foundational to process theology. Charles Hartshorne further developed and extended Whitehead's ideas within a theological context. \n\n\\boxed{Alfred North Whitehead}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 149}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2261e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_738", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An essay about this type of person argues that \"to say that Pierre Dupont does not exist is not at all the same as saying\" that some of these people don't exist in a discussion of proper names.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted argument concerns the semantics of proper names (a classic topic in analytic philosophy), using \"Pierre Dupont\" as a placeholder for any common name. The key distinction drawn is that denying the existence of a particular referent is not equivalent to denying that anyone bearing that name exists at all. This directly identifies the category under discussion as namesakes (i.e., people who share a name).\n\nThus the answer is namesakes.\n\n\\boxed{namesakes}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 221, "output_tokens": 90, "total_tokens": 311}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00050125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_790", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This book compares modern society to a \"sorcerer who is no longer able to control the powers of the nether world whom he has called up by his spells.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quoted passage is a well-known rhetorical flourish from Karl Marx and Friedrich Engels, describing how the bourgeoisie unleashes productive forces it cannot ultimately master. It appears verbatim in their 1848 work (Part I), not in later texts such as Capital. Hence the book in question is the Communist Manifesto.\n\n\\boxed{Communist Manifesto (Marx/Engels)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 214, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 286}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004475, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_871", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The process of \"spiritualization\" that constitutes this philosopher's theory of memory resembles that of an earlier philosopher but rejects that philosopher's notion of the  wahm   (WAH-hmm) , or estimative faculty.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue points to a medieval scholastic philosopher whose account of memory (as the storage of \"intentions\" extracted via a process of progressive \"spiritualization,\" or dematerialization, from sensible forms) is modeled on Avicenna\u2019s faculty psychology. Avicenna, however, located that extraction in a distinct inner sense he called wahm (estimatio). The thinker in question adopts the overall schema of spiritualization while denying the existence of any such separate estimative faculty, instead attributing the work to the cogitative power (vis cogitativa) or particular reason. That description fits Thomas Aquinas exactly.\n\n\\boxed{Thomas Aquinas}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 287, "output_tokens": 847, "total_tokens": 1134}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:50.507175+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00247625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_894", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A character advocates this ideology while he and another character lie by a haystack, before nearly attacking the other when he compares a maple leaf to a butterfly.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The described scene matches a passage in Turgenev\u2019s Fathers and Sons in which Arkady and Bazarov recline beside a haystack. Bazarov expounds his nihilist creed (rejection of all received authority, aestheticism, and romantic sentiment), then angrily rounds on Arkady for likening a maple leaf to a butterfly\u2014an observation Bazarov regards as precisely the sort of empty poeticism nihilism exists to destroy. No other widely referenced literary episode unites these exact details and the named ideology.\n\n\\boxed{nihilism (Fathers & Sons)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 211, "output_tokens": 116, "total_tokens": 327}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00055375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_91", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One essay argues that this thinker discovered the survival of \"obligation\" long after the abandonment of the framework of divine law that made it \"really intelligible.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The phrasing of the clue points to a specific diagnostic insight in the history of ethics: someone noticed that deontic concepts such as \u201cobligation\u201d or \u201cduty\u201d had become semantically orphaned once the theistic-legal framework that originally rendered them intelligible had been discarded. That diagnosis is classically associated with Nietzsche\u2019s account of the \u201cdeath of God,\u201d in which Christian moral language lingers on as a ghostly residue. An essay making this attribution therefore identifies the thinker in question as Nietzsche.\n\n(The same observation is later elaborated by Anscombe, but the clue\u2019s wording\u2014\u201cone essay argues that this thinker discovered\u201d\u2014treats the insight as a discovery attributed to the thinker rather than as Anscombe\u2019s own thesis.)\n\nThus the answer required by the clue is Nietzsche.\n\n\\boxed{Nietzsche}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 210, "output_tokens": 156, "total_tokens": 366}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0006525, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_940", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This book introduced the term \"sortal\" to describe the abstract idea behind a genus, and contends that species and genus terms only describe nominal essences.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The book that introduced the term \"sortal\" and discussed nominal essences in relation to species and genus is *An Essay Concerning Human Understanding* by John Locke. In this work, Locke argues that our classifications reflect nominal, rather than real, essences. The term \"sortal\" was later derived from his discussion of how we sort objects into kinds.\n\n\\boxed{An Essay Concerning Human Understanding}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 173}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4690000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_952", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In  On the Genealogy of Morals , Nietzsche asks \"Who is right \u00c2\u2013 [this man] or Stendhal?\" in ridiculing this man's assertion that beautiful things give satisfaction without interest.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Nietzsche is referring to Immanuel Kant in this passage from *On the Genealogy of Morals*, where he critiques Kant's view on aesthetic judgment. Stendhal, in contrast, emphasized passion and desire in beauty, opposing Kant's disinterestedness. Nietzsche sides with Stendhal against Kant, ridiculing Kant's assertion.\n\n\\boxed{Kant}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 176}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4670999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_993", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This text portrays a series of transitions from Sense-certainty to Perception to Understanding.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement directly references the opening sections of G.W.F. Hegel's *Phenomenology of Spirit* (1807), whose first three chapters are explicitly titled \"Sense-Certainty,\" \"Perception,\" and \"Force and the Understanding.\" These chapters trace the dialectical movement of consciousness through precisely those successive shapes. No other canonical philosophical text employs this exact sequence of terms.\n\n\\boxed{Phen. of Spirit (Hegel)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 196, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 280}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000455, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1026", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a 1976 experiment that exactly recapitulated theory, Robert Trivers and Hope Hare found that these individuals weighed almost exactly three times as much as their counterparts.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question refers to Trivers and Hare's 1976 test of worker-queen conflict over sex allocation in Hymenoptera. Because of haplodiploidy, workers are three times more related to full sisters (\\(r = 3/4\\)) than to brothers (\\(r = 1/4\\)), so they are predicted to bias colony investment in reproductives at a 3:1 female-to-male ratio. Trivers and Hare confirmed the prediction by measuring dry weights of alates across many ant species and finding that the biomass of new queens was almost exactly three times that of males.\n\nThus the individuals in question are the female reproductives.\n\n\\boxed{female alates (vs \u2642 ants)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 213, "output_tokens": 147, "total_tokens": 360}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00063375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1040", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Two of Lipinski's four \"rules of five\" restrict how much a drug candidate can participate in this effect.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The effect referred to is hydrogen bonding. Two of Lipinski's rules of five limit the number of hydrogen bond donors (no more than 5) and hydrogen bond acceptors (no more than 10) in a drug candidate. These restrictions help predict oral bioavailability.\n\n\\boxed{hydrogen bonding}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 82, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 146}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2222e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1063", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Holonomic constraints take a function of the position variables and the time and set it equal to this number.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Holonomic constraints are equations that involve the position variables and time, and they are set equal to zero. Therefore, the function of the position variables and time is constrained to be zero. \n\n\\boxed{0}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 151}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2315999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1085", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The extent to which this phenomenon is observed is given by \" e  to the negative  d , times sinh  (sinch)  \n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given expression matches the functional form of a screened interaction (typically a Yukawa/Coulomb potential modified by geometry-dependent hyperbolic factors). Such expressions arise in Debye\u2013H\u00fcckel or Thomas\u2013Fermi treatments once the Poisson equation is linearized and solved for a slab, film or layered geometry; the resulting potential between the boundaries therefore decays as \\(e^{-d}\\) multiplied by a \\(\\operatorname{sinh}\\) (or \\(\\operatorname{sinch}\\)) term that encodes the finite thickness. Consequently the phenomenon quantified by the formula is screening.\n\n\\boxed{screening\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 208, "output_tokens": 115, "total_tokens": 323}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005475, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1095", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Jacobus Kapteyn was the first to use \"statistical\" data from this concept, and not \"secular\" data to gauge the layout of stars in the sky.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The phrasing of the query indicates that the unknown concept yields two distinct categories of data (statistical versus secular) that Kapteyn applied to stellar-distribution problems. Those two categories correspond exactly to the classic astronomical techniques known as statistical parallax and secular parallax, both of which are derived from proper-motion measurements. Consequently the concept itself is parallax.\n\n\\boxed{parallax (stat./secular)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 216, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 294}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000465, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1107", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: While sticking her head out of a giant one of these objects, Signora Zenobia is decapitated in Edgar Allan Poe's story \"A Predicament\".\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In Edgar Allan Poe's short story \"A Predicament,\" Signora Zenobia is decapitated while sticking her head out of a giant clock. The scene is a grotesque and satirical moment in the narrative, where the clock's descending weights sever her head. The correct answer is a clock.\n\n\\boxed{clock}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 160}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3332e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1112", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This phenomenon's namesake \"wedge\" appears red in color due to backscattering from a light source whose zenith angle is in between 10 and 20 degrees.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The described phenomenon is the \"Belt of Venus,\" a pinkish or reddish glow seen above the horizon opposite the Sun during twilight. The \"wedge\" appears red due to backscattering of sunlight by the atmosphere when the Sun is just below the horizon, with a zenith angle between 10 and 20 degrees. This atmospheric optical phenomenon is commonly observed during civil twilight.\n\n\\boxed{Belt of Venus}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 184}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5616e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1133", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Russell Schaedler names a group of eight common bacterial species that live in this habitat.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue refers to the well-known \"Schaedler flora\" (later refined as altered Schaedler flora), a defined consortium of eight bacterial taxa isolated and named by Russell Schaedler in the 1960s. These taxa were selected precisely because they represent the dominant, stable members of the normal murine intestinal microbiota and are still used today to colonize gnotobiotic mice. Consequently, the habitat named in the clue is the mouse gut (or murine gastrointestinal tract).\n\n\\boxed{murine gut (Schaedler flora)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 198, "output_tokens": 110, "total_tokens": 308}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005225, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1138", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Alfve\u0301n's  (all-VANE's)  theorem uses the idealized form of this law to prove that magnetic field lines exactly coincide with the streamlines in a plasma.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Alfv\u00e9n's theorem relies on the concept of \"frozen-in\" magnetic flux, which is derived from the ideal magnetohydrodynamic (MHD) version of Ohm's law. This law describes the relationship between the electric field, the plasma velocity, and the magnetic field in a perfectly conducting fluid.\n\n\\boxed{Ohm's law}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:03:46.147980+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0001325, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1145", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A normed space named after these objects defines the notion of these objects' size.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question refers to a normed space, which is a mathematical concept used in functional analysis. In such a space, the norm defines the \"size\" or magnitude of elements, typically vectors. The most common objects for which size is defined in this context are vectors.\n\n\\boxed{vectors}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 76, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 137}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1496e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1149", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The power that can be extracted from a windmill depends on this function of the wind speed.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The power extractable from wind follows directly from the kinetic energy per unit time of the moving air mass. Kinetic energy scales with \\(v^2\\), while the mass flux through any fixed area scales with an additional factor of \\(v\\), yielding the overall dependence \\(P \\propto v^3\\). This is expressed in the standard wind-power equation \\(P = \\frac12\\rho A v^3\\).\n\nThus the function in question is the cube (third power) of wind speed.\n\n\\boxed{cube (v\u00b3)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 199, "output_tokens": 105, "total_tokens": 304}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00051125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1164", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Glucose sensors work by colorimetrically monitoring the formation of this compound when glucose is oxidized.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Glucose sensors work by monitoring the formation of hydrogen peroxide (H\u2082O\u2082) when glucose is oxidized by the enzyme glucose oxidase. This reaction produces H\u2082O\u2082, which can be detected colorimetrically through a coupled reaction that generates a colored product. The intensity of the color is proportional to the glucose concentration.\n\n\\boxed{hydrogen peroxide}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 80, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 157}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3379999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1168", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Christopher Fairburn advocates the use of 16 to 20 sessions of cognitive behavior therapy to treat these types of conditions.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Christopher Fairburn is a leading researcher on the application of CBT to eating disorders (particularly his CBT-E model for bulimia nervosa and related conditions). Standard protocols he has developed and tested prescribe 16\u201320 sessions, matching the clue exactly. Thus the referent of \u201cthese types of conditions\u201d is eating disorders.\n\n\\boxed{eating disorders (bulimia)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 204, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 275}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004325, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1184", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A generalization of one of this man's namesake objects uses a linear combination of orthogonal versions of a Bessel function to solve PDEs in cylindrical coordinates.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes a person with multiple namesake mathematical objects, one of which (the Fourier series) admits a well-known generalization. That generalization replaces the usual orthogonal trigonometric basis with an orthogonal basis of Bessel functions, yielding the Fourier\u2013Bessel series that furnishes separated solutions of the Helmholtz or wave equation in cylindrical coordinates. The only figure whose names match both the original object and its cylindrical generalization is therefore Fourier.\n\n\\boxed{Fourier}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 209, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 296}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00047875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1217", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One of these geologic features contains a unique mineral whose closest relatives are picrite and komatiite and whose type locality is the Meimecha-Kotuj province.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question refers to a rock type (meimechite) whose type locality lies in the Meimecha-Kotui region of northern Siberia; meimechite is an ultramafic volcanic rock whose nearest relatives are indeed picrite and komatiite. That region forms part of the larger Siberian Traps large igneous province, the only geologic feature among common candidates that hosts meimechite. Hence the feature singled out by the question is the Siberian Traps.\n\n\\boxed{Siberian Traps}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 213, "output_tokens": 103, "total_tokens": 316}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00052375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1222", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Application of sodium amide to a ben\u00c2\u00b7zyl\u00c2\u00b7ic version of these compounds can lead to ortho alkylation in the Sommelet-Hauser rearrangement.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Sommelet\u2013Hauser rearrangement is a base-promoted [2,3]-sigmatropic shift that converts a benzyl quaternary ammonium salt into an ortho-substituted benzylamine. Sodium amide deprotonates the ammonium salt at the benzylic position to generate the requisite nitrogen ylide; the \u201cbenzylic version\u201d phrasing in the clue therefore identifies the parent compounds as quaternary ammonium salts (or \u201cquats\u201d). This matches the historical literature exactly and rules out related but mechanistically distinct species such as sulfonium salts or simple amines.\n\n\\boxed{quaternary ammonium salts (quats)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 213, "output_tokens": 120, "total_tokens": 333}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00056625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1232", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Electrons in e-sub-g orbitals do not contribute to orbital angular momentum because the e-sub-g orbitals cannot transform between each other under this operation.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given statement is a standard explanation from ligand-field theory for quenching of orbital angular momentum in the \\(e_g\\) set. The angular-momentum operators transform as rotations (proper rotations of the point group); the two \\(e_g\\) functions (\\(d_{x^2-y^2}\\) and \\(d_{z^2}\\)) belong to the same irreducible representation but are not interconverted by any such rotation, so matrix elements \\(\\langle e_g|\\hat{L}|e_g\\rangle\\) vanish. In contrast, the \\(t_{2g}\\) set is closed under rotations, allowing nonzero orbital angular momentum.\n\nThus the missing operation is rotation (or a proper rotation such as \\(C_4\\)).\n\n\\boxed{rotation (C4/proper rot.)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 271, "output_tokens": 751, "total_tokens": 1022}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:53.592787+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00221625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1236", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A normal example of these sequences has an underlying sigma  eld equal to sigma of the sign of the W function; that one named for Azema is subject to Kurtz's theorem, which states that one of these things converges if the \"Z-hat t\" operator for it is self-adjoint.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question references stochastic processes, sigma-fields, and convergence theorems tied to self-adjoint operators, with specific mention of the Azema martingale and Kurtz's theorem. These concepts are most commonly associated with \"martingales\" in probability theory. The Azema martingale is a well-known example, and Kurtz's theorem relates to convergence of certain processes under operator conditions.\n\n\\boxed{martingales}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 123, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 211}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.7533e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1240", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Perturbative expansion of one type of this system in terms of two coupling constants with a  xed ratio produces an equation of motion where the second time derivative of the more slowly changing variable is proportional to the partial derivative of an e1\u20442fective potential with respect to that variable.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given statement is a precise description of the Born\u2013Oppenheimer (BO) procedure. In the molecular Hamiltonian the electron\u2013nuclear mass ratio supplies a small parameter \\(\\varepsilon\\); a second coupling constant (the strength of the electron\u2013nuclear interaction) is held in fixed proportion to \\(\\varepsilon\\). A systematic perturbative expansion in this ratio separates the fast electronic motion from the slow nuclear motion and yields an effective potential \\(V_{\\rm eff}(R)\\) for the nuclei. The resulting nuclear equation of motion is then simply\n\\[\nM\\ddot R=-\\partial V_{\\rm eff}/\\partial R,\n\\]\nwhich is the defining dynamical content of the BO approximation.\n\nThus the object named by the clue is the Born\u2013Oppenheimer approximation.\n\n\\boxed{Born-Oppenheimer approx.\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 239, "output_tokens": 158, "total_tokens": 397}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00069375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1255", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An algorithm named the \"big O of log n\" algorithm performs this task, and requires that all inputs be written in the form of A x plus B y plus C equals zero.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The form \\(Ax + By + C = 0\\) is simply a rewriting of the classic two-variable linear Diophantine equation \\(Ax + By = C\\). The only polynomial-time algorithm that solves this equation over the integers (via the extended Euclidean algorithm) has running time \\(O(\\log n)\\) where \\(n\\) is the magnitude of the coefficients; hence the facetious name \u201cbig-O-of-log-n algorithm.\u201d No other common computational task matches both the stated complexity and the required input representation.\n\n\\boxed{solving lin. Dioph. eq. (Ax+By=C)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 217, "output_tokens": 119, "total_tokens": 336}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00056875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_126", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 2002, Duke University lost the right to use one of these devices after losing a patent case against its inventor, former Duke professor John Madey.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The device in question is the \"free-electron laser.\" John Madey, a former Duke professor, invented the free-electron laser and won a patent case against Duke University in 2002, resulting in the university losing rights to use the device.\n\n\\boxed{free-electron laser}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 155}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2803000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1297", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A structure H will be a substructure of a series-parallel construct if and only if all of these things for H do not include the wheel designated by W-sub-four.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given statement is a characterization theorem from structural graph theory. Series-parallel graphs (also called partial 2-trees) are defined via series and parallel compositions starting from a single edge; equivalently, they are the graphs that exclude \\(K_4\\) (equivalently \\(W_4\\)) as a minor. Consequently the stated \u201cif and only if\u201d condition holds exactly.\n\n\\boxed{true}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 214, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 295}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00047, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1312", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This technique can be used to determine the oxygen environment of hepta\u00c2\u00b7valent neptunium compounds, in particular whether oxygen ligands are bridging or not.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a specialized spectroscopic method capable of probing the local electronic and coordination environment around Np(VII) centers. Because 237Np M\u00f6ssbauer spectroscopy is uniquely sensitive to isomer shifts and quadrupole splittings that differ markedly between terminal and bridging oxo ligands, it directly distinguishes bridging versus non-bridging oxygen atoms without requiring long-range crystallographic order. Other common techniques (EXAFS, vibrational spectroscopy, 17O NMR) supply supporting but less definitive information on this specific structural question for Np(VII) compounds.\n\n\\boxed{237Np M\u00f6ssbauer spec. (or equiv.)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 212, "output_tokens": 121, "total_tokens": 333}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005675, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1338", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An error-correction scheme that relies on values constructed by using non-singular projective curves defined over one of these constructs is the Goppa code.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Goppa code is an error-correcting code that is constructed using algebraic structures defined over finite fields. Specifically, it relies on non-singular projective curves over finite fields to generate the code. The most common and correct answer is finite fields.\n\n\\boxed{finite fields}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 150}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.239e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1360", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the Lambda-CDM model, the accelerating expansion of the universe begins at a scale factor equal to this function of omega-sub-matter over two omega-sub-lambda.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In the Lambda-CDM model, the transition from decelerated to accelerated expansion occurs when the scale factor $ a $ satisfies $ a = \\left( \\frac{\\Omega_{m,0}}{2\\Omega_{\\Lambda,0}} \\right)^{1/3} $. This marks the point where dark energy begins to dominate over matter, leading to accelerated expansion. The most common and correct answer is the cube root expression.\n\n\\boxed{\\left( \\frac{\\Omega_{m}}{2\\Omega_{\\Lambda}} \\right)^{1/3}}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 119, "total_tokens": 213}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.8574e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_139", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: At a molar ratio of 1, this quantity and enthalpy can be estimated from isothermal titration calorimetry curves.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quantity referred to is the binding constant (or association constant), which, along with enthalpy, can be directly estimated from isothermal titration calorimetry (ITC) data at a molar ratio of 1. ITC measures heat changes during molecular interactions, allowing simultaneous determination of binding affinity and enthalpy. These parameters are typically derived by fitting the titration curve to a binding model.\n\n\\boxed{binding constant}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 90, "total_tokens": 177}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5176999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1412", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A de3nition of this quantity that takes the form of the Euler-Lagrange equations includes the expression \"the negative gradient\" of quantity \"scalar potential minus the dot product of velocity and vector potential,\" close quantity, minus \"the total derivative of vector potential.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quantity described is the **Lorentz force**, which arises from the Lagrangian of a charged particle in an electromagnetic field. The expression provided corresponds to the force term derived from the Euler-Lagrange equations using the generalized potential $U = q(\\phi - \\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{A})$.\n\n\\boxed{Lorentz force}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 179}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:03:48.181890+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0001335, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1473", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When Evan Priestley was part of this organization, he developed the Phabricator collaboration tool, which is used for code reviews.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Evan Priestley developed Phabricator while he was part of Facebook (now Meta). He created the tool during his time at the company to streamline code review and software collaboration. \n\n\\boxed{Facebook}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 85, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 128}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0334999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1519", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Determining this quantity for a system can be done using only the core velocity dispersion if one uses King's method, also known as core  tting.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quantity being referred to is the **mass** of a stellar system, such as a globular cluster. King's method, or core fitting, uses the observed core radius and central velocity dispersion to model the system's density profile and estimate its total mass. This technique assumes dynamical equilibrium and a specific form for the distribution function.\n\n\\boxed{mass}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 163}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3690000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1582", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A frequency for these particles contains a factor of the cube root of \"six pi squared times number density.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given expression matches the Fermi wavevector \\(k_F = (6\\pi^2 n)^{1/3}\\) that appears for spinless (or fully spin-polarized) fermions. Any characteristic frequency built from this wavevector\u2014most commonly the Fermi frequency \\(\\omega_F = \\hbar k_F^2/2m\\)\u2014therefore contains precisely the stated factor. The particles in question are therefore fermions.\n\n\\boxed{fermions (Fermi gas)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 201, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 292}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00047875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1615", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This quantity and the second virial coef\u2734cient can be estimated by extrapolating a Zimm plot to \"theta equals zero.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Zimm plot is constructed from multi-angle static light-scattering data on polymer solutions. Its double extrapolation (zero angle and zero concentration) yields the intercept \\(1/M_w\\), while the concentration dependence of the \\(\\theta=0\\) intercepts directly supplies the second virial coefficient \\(A_2\\). Consequently the quantity obtained together with \\(A_2\\) by the \\(\\theta\\to0\\) extrapolation is the weight-average molecular weight.\n\n\\boxed{weight-av. mol. wt. (Mw)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 206, "output_tokens": 99, "total_tokens": 305}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000505, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_168", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For Dirichlet (\"DEE-ree-klet\") boundary conditions, this quantity is given by the volume integral of the charge density times the Green's function.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question pertains to solutions of Poisson's equation \\(\\nabla^2\\Phi=-\\rho/\\varepsilon_0\\) (electrostatics) via Green's functions. When Dirichlet boundary conditions are imposed and the potential vanishes on the boundary surface, the Green's function \\(G(\\mathbf{r},\\mathbf{r}')\\) itself vanishes on that surface; the unique solution inside the volume then reduces exactly to the indicated integral\n\\[\n\\Phi(\\mathbf{r})=\\int G(\\mathbf{r},\\mathbf{r}')\\rho(\\mathbf{r}')\\,dV'.\n\\]\nHence the quantity defined by the integral is the electrostatic (scalar) potential.\n\n\\boxed{electrostatic potential (w/ V=0 on bdry)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 209, "output_tokens": 138, "total_tokens": 347}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00060625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1680", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An inhibitor of calcineurin (cal-sih-NOOR-in) named for this disease's candidate region suppresses V\u00c2\u00b7E\u00c2\u00b7G\u00c2\u00b7F, which is why people with this disease rarely get solid tumors.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The disease described is **Down syndrome** (also known as Trisomy 21). The calcineurin inhibitor mentioned is **Down syndrome candidate region 1 (DSCR1)**, also known as RCAN1, which inhibits VEGF-mediated angiogenesis and contributes to the lower incidence of solid tumors in individuals with this condition.\n\n\\boxed{Down syndrome}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 176}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:03:48.753410+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00013525, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1700", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Metallocenes can be synthesized by reacting a cyclo\u00c2\u00b7penta\u00c2\u00b7diene sandwich complex of this element with a metal halide.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The synthesis of metallocenes (e.g., chromocene or vanadocene) via transmetallation commonly employs a Cp-transfer reagent that is itself a metallocene. The reagent in question must therefore be a true sandwich complex (Cp\u2082M) that is sufficiently ionic/covalent to react cleanly with a metal halide MX\u2099. Magnesocene (Cp\u2082Mg) satisfies these criteria and is the reagent most frequently cited for this purpose in both preparative and industrial contexts.\n\nThus the element is magnesium.\n\n\\boxed{Mg (magnesium)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 270, "output_tokens": 811, "total_tokens": 1081}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:56.125267+00:00"}, "cost": 0.002365, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1710", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Localizing a subset S of a ring gives every element of S this property.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In commutative algebra, localization of a ring \\(R\\) at a multiplicative subset \\(S\\) is the universal construction that formally adjoins inverses for every element of \\(S\\). Consequently, the canonical homomorphism \\(R\\to S^{-1}R\\) sends each \\(s\\in S\\) to a unit (i.e., an invertible element) of the localized ring. This is the defining property conferred on \\(S\\) by the localization functor.\n\n\\boxed{being a unit (invertible)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 196, "output_tokens": 97, "total_tokens": 293}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1724", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Nitrogen  xation is assayed by an experiment in which this compound is reduced.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Nitrogen fixation is commonly assayed by the acetylene reduction assay, in which nitrogenase enzyme reduces acetylene to ethylene.\n\nThe compound reduced in this experiment is acetylene.\n\n\\boxed{acetylene}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 77, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 124}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0167e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_174", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Examining the spectrum of a quantization of the classical Hamiltonian \"H equals xp\" yields a result similar to this statement according to the Berry\u2013Keating conjecture.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Berry\u2013Keating conjecture posits a hypothetical quantum Hamiltonian whose eigenvalues are precisely the imaginary parts of the nontrivial zeros of the Riemann \\(\\zeta\\) function. The simplest classical Hamiltonian that reproduces the correct asymptotic counting of those zeros is \\(H=xp\\). Consequently, any quantization of \\(H=xp\\) whose spectrum is real and simple is equivalent to the assertion that all nontrivial zeros lie on the critical line \\(\\operatorname{Re}(s)=1/2\\), i.e., the Riemann hypothesis.\n\n\\boxed{Riemann hypothesis (\u03b6 zeros on Re(s)=1/2)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 211, "output_tokens": 113, "total_tokens": 324}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00054625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1790", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a 1984 book co-written with Ann Druyan, Carl Sagan suggested that Earth is at the heart of over a trillion of these objects.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The 1984/1985 book in question is *Comet*, co-authored by Sagan and Druyan. In it they describe the spherical Oort cloud hypothesized to surround the solar system, containing (by their estimate) more than a trillion individual bodies whose collective center is the Sun\u2014and therefore Earth. The objects referenced are therefore simply comets.\n\n\\boxed{comets (Oort cloud)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 272, "output_tokens": 644, "total_tokens": 916}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:52.992218+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00195, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1800", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This scientist is often credited with devising a problem in which a customer either stays in a waiting room or tries to wake up the namesake person if no one else is getting a haircut.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query references the classic \"sleeping barber\" synchronization problem from operating systems and concurrency theory. In this setup, a barber (the namesake figure) sleeps when idle, while arriving customers either occupy a seat in the waiting room or wake the barber if no haircut is underway. Edsger Dijkstra is the researcher most commonly credited with formulating the problem (along with related concurrency examples such as the dining philosophers).\n\n\\boxed{Edsger Dijkstra}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 217, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 305}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00049125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_181", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Some of these devices feature glass fibers that are woven together into an absorbent mat to protect a component that nowadays is often made by mixing sulfuric acid and fumed silica.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question describes a category of devices in which two alternative technologies are used to immobilize the electrolyte for safety and low maintenance. One technology (AGM) employs a woven glass-fiber mat that both absorbs the liquid electrolyte and physically protects the plates; the other (gel) forms a semisolid electrolyte by mixing sulfuric acid with fumed silica. Both technologies therefore belong to the same broad class of devices\u2014valve-regulated or sealed lead-acid batteries\u2014making that class the referent of \u201cthese devices.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{VRLA/SLA (lead-acid) batteries}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 213, "output_tokens": 112, "total_tokens": 325}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00054625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1826", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a coordinate system devised by the IAU in 1958, the distribution of neutral hydrogen emissions was used to determine the \"equator\" of this structure.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The coordinate system devised by the IAU in 1958 is the galactic coordinate system, which is based on the plane of the Milky Way. The distribution of neutral hydrogen (H I) emissions was used to define the galactic equator, as these emissions trace the plane of the Galaxy. Therefore, the structure referred to is the Milky Way.\n\n\\boxed{Milky Way}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 175}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4774e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1848", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Using a perturbative expansion in this quantity to perform a canonical change of variables on the Lagrangian of light-cone Yang-Mills theory reproduces the CSW selection rules.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement refers to the construction of the MHV (or CSW) Lagrangian for pure Yang-Mills theory. Light-cone gauge Yang-Mills naturally splits into a self-dual (SD) sector whose only vertices are MHV and an anti-self-dual (ASD) deformation. A field redefinition that puts the SD sector into a free form is constructed order-by-order as a power series in the ASD coupling; the resulting interaction vertices are then precisely the CSW vertices, automatically enforcing the CSW helicity selection rules.\n\nThus the quantity in question is the ASD Yang-Mills coupling.\n\n\\boxed{ASD coupling (g_\u00af)}\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 212, "output_tokens": 131, "total_tokens": 343}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005925, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_185", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The subgroup of these objects that is connected to the identity is doubly covered by the group SL(2,C)\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The double cover relation follows because the Lie algebra \\(\\mathfrak{sl}(2,\\mathbb{C})\\) is isomorphic to the complexification of \\(\\mathfrak{so}(1,3)\\), while the kernel of the covering homomorphism \\(\\mathrm{SL}(2,\\mathbb{C})\\to\\mathrm{SO}^+(1,3)\\) is precisely the two-element center \\(\\{\\pm I\\}\\). Consequently the connected component of the identity inside the full Lorentz group \\(\\mathrm{O}(1,3)\\) is the restricted Lorentz group \\(\\mathrm{SO}^+(1,3)\\), which is the image of this covering. The objects in the question are therefore the elements of the Lorentz group (or, equivalently, Lorentz transformations).\n\n\\boxed{Lorentz group (SO+(1,3))\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 202, "output_tokens": 153, "total_tokens": 355}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000635, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1858", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One of these animals presented to King George II was called the Indian Monster and was reportedly fed hard boiled eggs.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The phrasing \"one of these animals\" indicates the query is seeking the common name of a category/species rather than an individual specimen. Historical records of exotic-animal gifts to George II identify the specimen in question as an Indian rhinoceros (the first living rhino seen in Britain since Roman times), popularly billed as the \u201cIndian Monster\u201d and maintained on a diet that included hard-boiled eggs. Hence the animals referenced are rhinoceroses.\n\n\\boxed{rhinoceroses (Indian rhinos)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 202, "output_tokens": 99, "total_tokens": 301}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1892", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A form of this property manifests as the destruction of anti-nodal coherence peaks in the local density of states spectra of under-doped cuprate superconductors.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The property described relates to the suppression of coherence peaks in the local density of states due to the presence of competing orders or strong correlations in under-doped cuprate superconductors. This phenomenon is most commonly associated with the pseudogap phase. The destruction of anti-nodal coherence peaks is a hallmark feature of the pseudogap.\n\n\\boxed{pseudogap}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 167}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4061e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_198", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The ammonia-rich clays on this body's surface suggest that it migrated to its current location some time after its formation.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The ammonia-rich clays found on the surface of this dwarf planet suggest that it formed in the outer solar system before migrating to the asteroid belt. This body is the largest object in the asteroid belt and is classified as a dwarf planet.\n\n\\boxed{Ceres}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 79, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 133}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:03:47.834491+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00010075, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_229", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The genotype of this compound's receptor significantly correlates with disease subtype in leprosy patients.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The genotype of the **vitamin D** receptor (VDR) has been significantly correlated with susceptibility to and the clinical subtype of leprosy. Variations in the VDR gene influence the immune response to *Mycobacterium leprae*, affecting whether a patient develops the tuberculoid or lepromatous form of the disease.\n\n\\boxed{Vitamin D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 71, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 141}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:03:47.856068+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00012275, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_283", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The moment-generating function of a random variable X is defined as the expectation value of this function of X times t.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The moment-generating function of a random variable \\( X \\) is defined as \\( \\mathbb{E}[e^{tX}] \\), the expected value of \\( e^{tX} \\). This function is used to generate moments of the distribution of \\( X \\) by taking derivatives with respect to \\( t \\) at \\( t = 0 \\). The correct and most common answer is:\n\n\\boxed{e^{tX}}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 83, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 175}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5093e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_292", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The rate of this process can be measured through the use of an acetylene reduction assay.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The acetylene reduction assay is commonly used to measure nitrogen fixation, as nitrogenase enzymes in certain bacteria reduce acetylene to ethylene. This process is a proxy for estimating the activity of nitrogen fixation in soil or plant-associated microbes. \n\n\\boxed{nitrogen fixation}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 78, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 135}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1238e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_308", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This phenomenon is exhibited by the rotation of a water wheel with leaky buckets.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The described setup is a classic physical analogy for the Poynting\u2013Robertson drag: each \u201cbucket\u201d (dust grain) loses mass while moving tangentially, so the departing water (re-radiated photons) carries away angular momentum and produces a net torque that causes the wheel (orbit) to decay inward. This torque arises because the re-emitted radiation is aberrated in the particle\u2019s frame, exactly mirroring the offset between the leaking water\u2019s velocity vector and the bucket\u2019s radial position. Hence the phenomenon named by the clue is the Poynting\u2013Robertson effect.\n\n\\boxed{Poynting-Robertson effect}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 195, "output_tokens": 127, "total_tokens": 322}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00056125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_354", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Some cells in this structure can become hyperpolarized when the activation of the G-protein transducin triggers phospho-di-ester-ase to cleave cGMP.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The structure described is the retina, specifically the photoreceptor cells (rods and cones). When light activates transducin, it leads to the activation of phosphodiesterase, which reduces cGMP levels, causing hyperpolarization of the photoreceptor cells. This process occurs in the retina.\n\n\\boxed{retina}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 166}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3816e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_364", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The relativistic kinetic energy of a photon equals this quantity times the speed of light.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The relativistic energy-momentum relation for any particle is \\(E^2 = (pc)^2 + (mc^2)^2\\). A photon has \\(m = 0\\), so its total energy reduces exactly to \\(E = pc\\). Because a photon has zero rest mass, this total energy is identical to its relativistic kinetic energy, yielding \\(K = pc\\).\n\nThus the missing quantity is simply the photon\u2019s momentum magnitude \\(p\\).\n\n\\boxed{momentum (p)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 196, "output_tokens": 96, "total_tokens": 292}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000485, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_37", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 2006 paper by Mark Shriver posited an instance of this phenomenon by studying ASIP, OCA2, and other skin pigmentation-related genes in European and East Asian populations.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The phenomenon described is **convergent evolution**, which refers to the independent evolution of similar traits in unrelated or distantly related lineages. Mark Shriver's research highlighted how different genetic mutations in the *ASIP* and *OCA2* genes independently led to the evolution of lighter skin pigmentation in European and East Asian populations.\n\n\\boxed{Convergent evolution}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 167}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:03:48.003192+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000133, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_43", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Treating this operation as an automorphism is the first step in constructing the adjoint representation of a Lie (\"lee\") group.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The construction of the adjoint representation \\(\\operatorname{Ad}\\) of a Lie group \\(G\\) begins with the conjugation (inner automorphism) map\n\\[\nc_g(h)=ghg^{-1}.\n\\]\nEach \\(c_g\\) is a group automorphism of \\(G\\); differentiating at the identity then yields a Lie-algebra automorphism of \\(\\mathfrak{g}\\), which is precisely \\(\\operatorname{Ad}(g)\\). Hence the operation being treated as an automorphism is conjugation.\n\n\\boxed{conjugation (inner auto.)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 203, "output_tokens": 102, "total_tokens": 305}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00050875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_450", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In these locations, smaller species evolve to get larger and larger species become smaller, according to Foster's rule.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Foster's rule (also called the \"island rule\") describes a specific pattern of size evolution in isolated populations: smaller-bodied species tend toward gigantism while larger-bodied species tend toward dwarfism. This pattern is driven by the unique resource constraints, reduced predation, and limited competition that characterize islands (or other insular environments). Hence the locations referenced in the question are simply islands.\n\n\\boxed{islands (isl. rule)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 202, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 286}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_474", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This planet's shepherd moon Pan is located within this planet's Encke Gap.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The planet with the shepherd moon Pan located within its Encke Gap is Saturn. Pan orbits inside the Encke Gap in Saturn's A Ring and helps maintain the gap through gravitational interactions. \n\n\\boxed{Saturn}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 75, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 120}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 9.825e-06, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_492", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Note to moderator: Take a second to read the pronunciation guides and the answerline.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The message contains moderator instructions and meta-prompting but no actual quizbowl-style question, clue, or query with a factual answer. Without content to evaluate against pronunciation guides or an answerline, no specific response can be determined.  \nThe most common handling in such cases is to note the omission rather than fabricate content.\n\n\\boxed{none}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 197, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 265}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00041625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_53", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Hardware-enforced control-flow integrity requires a \"shadow\" version of this structure.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Hardware-enforced control-flow integrity uses a \"shadow\" stack to protect return addresses. This structure stores return addresses separately from the main stack to prevent tampering. The correct answer is the stack.\n\n\\boxed{stack}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 75, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 120}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 9.825e-06, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_550", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An algorithm for this problem that classifies bases as either witnesses or liars is named for Solovay and Strassen.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Solovay\u2013Strassen algorithm is a classic Monte Carlo procedure that solves the decision problem of determining whether an odd integer \\(n\\) is prime. It works by selecting random bases \\(a\\) and testing the equality between the Jacobi symbol \\((a/n)\\) and \\(a^{(n-1)/2} \\bmod n\\); failure of the equality yields a deterministic compositeness witness, while consistent success leaves open the possibility that \\(a\\) is a \u201cliar.\u201d Consequently the underlying problem the algorithm addresses is primality testing.\n\n\\boxed{primality testing (of n)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 203, "output_tokens": 118, "total_tokens": 321}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00054875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_572", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This body contains a so-called \"mountain in a moat\" whose origin is unknown.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The phrase \"mountain in a moat\" is a descriptive term for the central peak inside a lunar impact crater (a ring-shaped depression whose floor forms the \"moat\"). Such features are well-documented across the Moon's surface, and the origin of certain examples remains incompletely explained by current models of crater formation. No other celestial or terrestrial body matches the wording as precisely or commonly.\n\n\\boxed{the Moon}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 198, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 281}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000455, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_580", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Laughlin wavefunction is used to study this effect for filling factors of one over an odd integer.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Laughlin wavefunction is a variational ansatz introduced to describe strongly correlated 2D electron states in a perpendicular magnetic field. It is constructed to be totally antisymmetric and to produce an incompressible quantum liquid precisely when the Landau-level filling factor equals \\(1/m\\) for odd integers \\(m\\). These filling factors correspond to the primary series of the fractional quantum Hall effect (FQHE), thereby accounting for the observed fractional quantization of the Hall conductance.\n\n\\boxed{fractional quantum Hall effect (FQHE)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 201, "output_tokens": 101, "total_tokens": 302}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00050375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_607", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One of these constructs named for Banach and Mazur can be used to define Baire spaces.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Banach-Mazur game is a topological game named for Stefan Banach and Stanis\u0142aw Mazur, which can be used to characterize Baire spaces. In this game, two players alternately choose nested open sets, and the outcome relates to whether a given set is comeager. A space is a Baire space if and only if the second player has a winning strategy in the Banach-Mazur game.\n\n\\boxed{Banach-Mazur game}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 79, "output_tokens": 98, "total_tokens": 177}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5408999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_613", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This statement can be derived from Lagrange's identity when the time derivative of the scalar G function is equal to zero.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query pertains to a result in the calculus of variations applied to time-independent Lagrangians. Lagrange's identity supplies the general relation between the total time derivative of a scalar function \\(G(q,\\dot{q})\\) and the Euler\u2013Lagrange operator. Setting \\(\\mathrm{d}G/\\mathrm{d}t=0\\) immediately reduces that relation to the first integral\n\\[\nL-\\dot{q}\\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial\\dot{q}}=\\text{const},\n\\]\nwhich is precisely Beltrami\u2019s identity.\n\nThus the statement referenced by the query is Beltrami\u2019s identity.\n\n\\boxed{Beltrami identity\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 203, "output_tokens": 125, "total_tokens": 328}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00056625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_619", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A subset of this set of numbers corresponds to the surreal numbers with birthdays earlier than omega; those surreal numbers are the dyadic type of this number.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes a set of numbers whose subset (the dyadic rationals) coincides exactly with the class of surreal numbers whose birthdays are the finite ordinals, i.e., all ordinals strictly less than \\(\\omega\\). Those dyadic rationals are by definition the dyadic instances of the ordinary rational numbers; hence the set in question is the set of rational numbers.\n\nThis identification follows at once from the standard inductive construction of the surreal numbers: on day \\(n\\) one adjoins the arithmetic mean of each previously created pair, generating precisely the dyadics of denominator \\(2^n\\); the union over all finite days is therefore the dyadic rationals, a subset of \\(\\mathbb{Q}\\).\n\nNo other familiar number system (reals, integers, etc.) satisfies both the \u201csubset\u201d and the \u201cdyadic type\u201d clauses simultaneously.\n\n\\boxed{rational numbers (dyadics)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 210, "output_tokens": 180, "total_tokens": 390}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0007125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_634", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The difference in this quantity between two systems can be determined using the Bennett acceptance ratio.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Bennett acceptance ratio (BAR) method is an optimized, overlap-sampling estimator derived from the Metropolis acceptance criterion. It is used in statistical mechanics to compute the equilibrium free-energy difference \\(\\Delta F\\) (or \\(\\Delta A\\)) between two thermodynamic states from the same set of forward and reverse energy samples. Consequently, the quantity whose difference is obtained by BAR is free energy.\n\n\\boxed{free energy (\u0394F)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 197, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 282}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00045875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_640", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This theorem is the m-equals-one case of the empire problem.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The theorem that represents the $m=1$ case of the empire problem is the **Four Color Theorem**. This theorem states that any map on a plane can be colored with at most four colors such that no two adjacent regions share the same color. The empire problem generalizes this by considering maps where each \"empire\" consists of $m$ non-contiguous regions.\n\n\\boxed{Four Color Theorem}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 68, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 149}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:03:44.462236+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0001385, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_643", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Smooth muscle relaxation is thought to be promoted by this hormone in its namesake \"block\" on the myometrium.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The hormone associated with promoting smooth muscle relaxation in the myometrium is progesterone. It acts to suppress contractions during pregnancy by maintaining uterine quiescence. This effect is commonly referred to as the \"progesterone block.\"\n\n\\boxed{Progesterone}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 83, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 140}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1593e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_679", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Chris Freiling argued that this statement is false because it is equivalent to the negation of his axiom of symmetry.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes a well-known argument from set theory: Freiling's 1986 paper introduced an axiom of symmetry (a probabilistic statement about functions from the reals to countable sets of reals) and proved it equivalent to the negation of CH. Hence the statement whose falsity Freiling asserted is precisely the continuum hypothesis (\\(2^{\\aleph_0}=\\aleph_1\\)).\n\nThis identification is corroborated by standard references in infinitary combinatorics and by the fact that no other classical statement (e.g., AC or GCH) bears the cited equivalence.\n\n\\boxed{continuum hypothesis (CH)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 202, "output_tokens": 123, "total_tokens": 325}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00056, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_691", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A group with this name can be represented by Specht modules or by Young tableaux with n boxes and n\u00a0distinct entries.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given description matches the representation theory of the symmetric group \\(S_n\\). Its irreducible representations (Specht modules) over fields of characteristic zero are constructed from Young diagrams, and the natural action of \\(S_n\\) on the set of all fillings of those diagrams by \\(n\\) distinct labels realizes the regular representation. Consequently the group in question is the symmetric group (equivalently, the permutation group on \\(n\\) letters).\n\n\\boxed{symmetric group (S_n)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 205, "output_tokens": 96, "total_tokens": 301}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00049625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_71", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Measurements of these particles violated the Leggett inequalities that are implied by nonlocal realism in a 2007 study by Anton Zeilinger's group.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Measurements of entangled photons violated the Leggett inequalities in the 2007 study by Anton Zeilinger's group. This demonstrated that quantum mechanics cannot be explained by nonlocal realistic theories. The correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{photons}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 144}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1761e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_72", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Any continuous positive definite function that maps 0 to 1 can serve as a function known by this word due to Bochner's theorem.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "According to Bochner's theorem, any continuous positive definite function that maps 0 to 1 is the characteristic function of some probability distribution. Such functions are known as characteristic functions in probability theory. \n\n\\boxed{characteristic}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 134}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0877e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_739", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Finding the largest number of rooks on an m-by-n chessboard with k squares removed such that none of the rooks attack each other can be solved by reducing to this problem.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The non-attacking-rook placement task on a board with forbidden squares is exactly the problem of selecting a maximum set of positions such that each row and each column is used at most once. This is modeled by a bipartite graph whose two parts are the rows and the columns, with an edge present precisely when the corresponding square has not been removed. The size of a maximum set of non-attacking rooks is therefore identical to the size of a maximum matching in this graph, which can be computed by any standard bipartite-matching algorithm (Hopcroft\u2013Karp, flow-based methods, etc.).\n\nThus the original combinatorial question reduces directly to the maximum-bipartite-matching problem.\n\n\\boxed{max bipartite matching\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 217, "output_tokens": 141, "total_tokens": 358}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00062375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_750", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The ylide made by the reaction of this compound with methyl iodide, followed by subsequent deprotonation, is used to cyclopropanate double bonds.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The described transformation generates a sulfur ylide (Corey\u2013Chaykovsky reagent) that transfers a methylene unit to electron-deficient alkenes, forming cyclopropanes. The only common, commercially available precursor that undergoes clean S-methylation with MeI followed by deprotonation to furnish such an ylide is dimethyl sulfide. Other sulfides (e.g., tetrahydrothiophene) are occasionally employed for specialized ylides, but dimethyl sulfide is the standard reagent referenced in this context.\n\n\\boxed{(CH3)2S (dimethyl sulfide)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 211, "output_tokens": 109, "total_tokens": 320}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00053625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_766", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Two ways of measuring this quantity are Lipschitz equivalent if they are bounded between constant multiples of each other.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question describes a property of metrics where two measures are considered equivalent if each is bounded above and below by constant multiples of the other. This is the definition of Lipschitz equivalence, which applies to metrics. The quantity being measured in this context is a **metric**.\n\n\\boxed{metric}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 81, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 142}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1850999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_792", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The first element of the signature of a number field is the number of embeddings of the field in this set.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The signature \\((r_1,r_2)\\) of a number field \\(K/\\mathbb{Q}\\) of degree \\(n\\) records the possible embeddings \\(K\\hookrightarrow\\mathbb{C}\\). Exactly \\(r_1\\) of those embeddings land inside the subfield \\(\\mathbb{R}\\subset\\mathbb{C}\\), while the remaining \\(2r_2\\) embeddings come in conjugate pairs. Consequently the first entry of the signature is defined to be the number of real embeddings, i.e., embeddings into the set \\(\\mathbb{R}\\).\n\n\\boxed{\u211d (reals)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 202, "output_tokens": 115, "total_tokens": 317}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00054, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_796", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: BzK photometry is used to classify galaxies by this phenomenon, which, along with redshift, characterizes Lyman-break galaxies.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "BzK selection is a two-color technique (using BzK filters) that separates high-redshift galaxies into the two broad categories of star-forming versus passively evolving on the basis of their rest-frame optical/UV colors. Lyman-break galaxies are defined by precisely the same pair of properties: a known redshift plus the presence of vigorous, dust-obscured star formation that produces a strong UV continuum. Consequently the single phenomenon that both the BzK classification and the LBG definition isolate is star formation (or star-forming activity).\n\n\\boxed{star formation (sSFR/Balmer break)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 204, "output_tokens": 120, "total_tokens": 324}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000555, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_804", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Cohn, Kleinberg, Szegedy, and Umans provided a group theoretic approach to this task that re-derives an earlier algorithm for it that Virginia Williams improved upon in 2011.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The task referred to is matrix multiplication. Cohn, Kleinberg, Szegedy, and Umans developed a group-theoretic framework that re-derives the Coppersmith-Winograd algorithm, which Virginia Williams improved upon in 2011 to achieve a faster matrix multiplication time bound. The correct answer is matrix multiplication.\n\n\\boxed{matrix multiplication}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 179}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4913000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_819", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Haloketones of this type can react upon the addition of an aqueous base to form a cyclopropanone intermediate that subsequently rearranges to form a carboxylic acid.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given statement matches the key mechanistic features of the Favorskii rearrangement: an \\(\\alpha\\)-haloketone treated with aqueous base proceeds through a cyclopropanone intermediate that ring-opens to deliver a carboxylic acid (or ester if alkoxide is used).  \n\nNo other common named reaction of haloketones (e.g., Ramberg\u2013B\u00e4cklund, quasi-Favorskii) invokes this exact cyclopropanone pathway under basic aqueous conditions.  \n\nThus the most concise and standard answer to the implied query (\u201cname the reaction\u201d) is the Favorskii rearrangement.\n\n\\boxed{Favorskii rearr. (\u03b1-haloketone)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 213, "output_tokens": 131, "total_tokens": 344}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00059375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_843", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the Debye\u2013H\u00fcckel equation, the log of the activity coefficient is proportional to this parameter to the negative three-halves power, times the square root of ionic strength.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Debye\u2013H\u00fcckel limiting law takes the explicit form\n\\[\n\\log\\gamma_i=-A z_i^2\\sqrt{I},\n\\]\nwhere the prefactor \\(A\\) is given (in conventional units) by\n\\[\nA\\propto(\\varepsilon T)^{-3/2}.\n\\]\nConsequently \\(\\log\\gamma\\) is proportional to the single composite quantity \\(\\varepsilon T\\) raised to the power \\(-3/2\\) (multiplied by \\(\\sqrt{I}\\)). In the great majority of textbook and quiz-bowl statements of this dependence the quantity singled out is therefore the dielectric constant of the solvent.\n\n\\boxed{dielectric const. (of solvent)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 217, "output_tokens": 131, "total_tokens": 348}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00059875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_849", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A field that is \"formally [this adjective]\" can be equipped with an ordering to become an ordered field.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A field that is \"formally real\" can be equipped with an ordering to become an ordered field. This means that -1 cannot be expressed as a sum of squares in the field. The term \"formally real\" is the standard terminology in field theory for such fields.\n\n\\boxed{real}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 82, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 144}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2021999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_888", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Cancers of this organ are assessed by the RMI score, which depends on the concentration of the biomarker CA-125.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Cancers of the ovary are assessed by the RMI (Risk of Malignancy Index) score, which incorporates the level of the biomarker CA-125, along with ultrasound findings and menopausal status. CA-125 is commonly elevated in epithelial ovarian cancers. Therefore, the organ in question is the ovary.\n\n\\boxed{ovary}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3977e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_90", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The real line under the K-topology is Hausdorff and has this property, but is neither regular nor normal.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The K-topology on \\(\\mathbb{R}\\) is generated by the usual open intervals together with basis elements of the form \\((a,b) \\setminus K\\), where \\(K=\\{1/n:n\\in\\mathbb{Z}_+\\}\\). This topology is strictly finer than the Euclidean topology, so \\(\\mathbb{R}_K\\) remains hereditarily Lindel\u00f6f (any open cover admits a countable subcover, which can be refined using the countability of \\(K\\) and the Lindel\u00f6f property of the usual line). The same example is known to fail regularity (the point \\(0\\) and the closed set \\(K\\) cannot be separated by disjoint open sets), hence also fails normality.\n\nThus the missing property is precisely the Lindel\u00f6f property.\n\n\\boxed{Lindel\u00f6f\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 203, "output_tokens": 160, "total_tokens": 363}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00065375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_918", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This quantity is linearly related to a type of enthalpy in the Evans\u00c2\u2013Polanyi principle.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quantity linearly related to a type of enthalpy in the Evans\u2013Polanyi principle is the activation energy. This principle states that the activation energy for a reaction is linearly proportional to the reaction enthalpy. Thus, the correct answer is activation energy.\n\n\\boxed{activation energy}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 82, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 144}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2021999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_967", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Like loops, these things are often unrolled such that the items stored within them fit into a single unit of memory to improve cache performance.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question draws an analogy to loop unrolling (a standard compiler optimization) and refers to a data-structure technique with the same goal and terminology. In an unrolled linked list each node stores a small array of elements sized to occupy exactly one cache line; the \u201cunrolling\u201d therefore packs multiple items together, cutting pointer overhead and improving spatial locality exactly as the question describes. No other common structure (plain arrays, trees, hash tables, etc.) is conventionally described by the verb \u201cunrolled\u201d in this cache-oriented sense.\n\n\\boxed{linked lists (unrolled)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 208, "output_tokens": 116, "total_tokens": 324}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00055, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_98", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a paper subtitled \"The Endless Dispute,\" Jacob Rempel summarized the difficulty of determining the evolutionary origin of the head of animals in this phylum due to the nebulous nature of the pre-oral region and the labrum.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The phylum in question is Arthropoda, as the debate over the evolutionary origin of the head, particularly concerning the labrum and pre-oral region, is a well-known issue in arthropod biology. Jacob Rempel's paper discusses the uncertainty in homologizing these structures across arthropods and their relatives. The most common answer to this context is Arthropoda.\n\n\\boxed{Arthropoda}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 195}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6338999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_994", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: It has nothing to do with magnetic fields, but the Biot\u00c2\u2013Savart  (byoh-sah-VARR)  law can be used to derive this force in a theory derived by Ludwig Prandtl.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue points to Prandtl's lifting-line theory in finite-wing aerodynamics. In that framework a vortex filament produces a velocity perturbation that is evaluated with the identical line-integral expression as the Biot\u2013Savart law of magnetostatics; the resulting downwash tilts the local lift vector and thereby generates a streamwise force component known as induced drag. (The same mathematics is unrelated to electromagnetic fields.)\n\nThus the force referenced by the clue is induced drag.\n\n\\boxed{induced drag (on finite wing)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 224, "output_tokens": 104, "total_tokens": 328}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00054, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1033", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to the Lockean proviso, this  specific resource  should only be consumed such that enough is left for others.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Lockean proviso states that one may appropriate resources only if there is \"enough and as good\" left for others. This principle is most commonly applied to natural resources, particularly land, in the context of property rights. The most specific resource implied in this context is land.\n\n\\boxed{land}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 147}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2264e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1036", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A case in which Susan Guillory Phipps sued the state of Louisiana to change this kind of designation is described in Omi and Winant's book on \"formations\" of this concept.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The case described involves Susan Guillory Phipps challenging Louisiana's racial classification system, specifically her designation as \"Black\" under the state's one-drop rule. This case is discussed in Omi and Winant's *Racial Formation in the United States*, which analyzes the social and political formations of race. The concept in question is \"race.\"\n\n\\boxed{race}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 175}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4629e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1130", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a theory developed by Lev Vygotsky, the ability of a child to learn unaided goes through a form of this process.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question refers to Lev Vygotsky's concept of the Zone of Proximal Development (ZPD), which describes the difference between what a learner can do without help and what they can achieve with guidance. The process in question is \"scaffolding,\" where support is provided to help the child move through the ZPD. However, the ability to learn unaided improves through the process of internalization.\n\n\\boxed{internalization}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 88, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 179}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5348e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1220", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One passage of this text criticizes the communists who believe they have found the \"deliverance from our evils,\" claiming that the abolition of private property will only lead to increased \"prerogative in the  eld of sexual relationships.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given passage is a direct reference to a critique of Marxist ideas in section V of Freud's 1930 work. There, Freud concedes that abolishing private property might reduce certain economic sources of aggression, yet immediately counters that sexual rivalry and \"prerogative in the field of sexual relationships\" would remain ineradicable. Hence the text in question is unambiguously *Civilization and Its Discontents*.\n\n\\boxed{Civ. & its Discontents (Freud)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 289, "output_tokens": 783, "total_tokens": 1072}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:56.482952+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00231875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1248", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a classic experiment on this process, participants were divided into two groups, which both watched a video of a job interview; one group was told the job was \"submariner,\" while the other was told it was \"astronaut.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The experiment described is a classic study on **confirmation bias** (or sometimes referred to as **hypothesis testing**). Participants tended to ask questions that would confirm their preconceived notions about the personality traits required for the specific job roles.\n\n\\boxed{Confirmation bias}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 152}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:00:31.698063+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000103, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1273", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Individuals possess \"contradictory\" forms of this construct according to a model designed by Erik Olin Wright.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Erik Olin Wright's model of class analysis describes how individuals may have \"contradictory\" class locations, particularly in relation to their relationship to labor and capital. These contradictory class locations arise when people share characteristics of more than one class, such as managers who supervise workers but are also employees themselves. The construct in question is \"class.\"\n\n\\boxed{class}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 81, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 156}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3250999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1279", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A world in which all agents demonstrate the \"hyperbolic absolute\" version of this behavior was used by Stiglitz and Cass to derive the two fund separation theorem.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The two-fund separation theorem (due to Cass and Stiglitz) states that all investors will optimally hold a combination of two mutual funds whenever every agent\u2019s indirect utility exhibits hyperbolic absolute risk aversion (HARA) with a common exponent parameter. HARA is simply the indicated functional family of utility functions, so the underlying \u201cbehavior\u201d referenced by the query is risk aversion.  \n\nThus the term that completes the statement is risk aversion.\n\n\\boxed{risk aversion (HARA)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 213, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 308}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00050375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1282", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This country's \"sung points\" are analyzed as \"melodic machetes\" in Jennie Smith's When the Hands are Many.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The country referred to is Haiti. In her ethnography *When the Hands are Many*, Jennie Smith analyzes the \"sung points\" (pwen) of Haitian peasant communities as tools for social and political resistance.\n\n\\boxed{Haiti}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 82, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 131}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:00:29.224688+00:00"}, "cost": 9.4e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1358", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This condition appears as an adjective in the title of a book that rejects the so-called \"domestic analogy\" and suggests the possibility of a \"neo-medievalist\" system of \"overlapping structures.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The phrasing matches Hedley Bull's classic IR text *The Anarchical Society* (1977). That work explicitly rejects the \u201cdomestic analogy,\u201d explores the possibility of \u201cneo-medieval\u201d overlapping authorities, and treats international politics as occurring under the structural condition of anarchy (rendered adjectivally in the title). Hence the condition in question is anarchy.\n\n\\boxed{anarchy (anarchical)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 220, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 300}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000475, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1370", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Laryngeals and the sound represented by this letter of the Latin alphabet were deleted in Szemere\u0301nyi's (seh-meh-\"RAIN\"-yee's) law.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Szemere\u0301nyi's law describes the loss of word-final long vowels before a word-final resonant followed by a word-final sibilant, specifically resulting in the deletion of the laryngeal and the letter **s**. This sound change is a well-known feature of Proto-Indo-European phonology as reconstructed by Oswald Szemer\u00e9nyi.\n\n\\boxed{s}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 173}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:00:28.874296+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0001445, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1386", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 2012, a seminal text on this phenomenon was criticized by James Forman, who cited Vanessa Barker's research on its \"politics.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The phenomenon referred to is mass incarceration in the United States. James Forman Jr. critiqued the political analysis in works like Michelle Alexander's *The New Jim Crow* (2012), referencing Vanessa Barker's research on the politics of punishment. The correct answer is: \n\n\\boxed{mass incarceration}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 156}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2960999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1396", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Per Baltzer Overgaard analyzed this type of action as a signaling game whose objective is to show possession of resources.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Per Baltzer Overgaard analyzed **conspicuous consumption** as a signaling game whose objective is to show possession of resources. This concept aligns with economic theories where individuals display wealth to signal status. \n\n\\boxed{conspicuous consumption}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 82, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 134}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1021999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1399", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Global mutagenesis using these entities was used to determine the minimal genome for the  rst synthetic organism Mycoplasma laboratorium.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The minimal genome for *Mycoplasma laboratorium* was determined using global mutagenesis via **transposons** (specifically, transposon mutagenesis). This technique allowed researchers to identify essential genes by disrupting them and observing which mutations were lethal to the organism.\n\n\\boxed{transposons}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 76, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 133}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:00:28.227264+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0001045, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1438", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Terry Bouton argues that the rate of this action eclipsed 37ty percent for many Pennsylvania counties in the decade a7ter the Revolutionary War, pursuant to a deliberate state-building project.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes a key argument from Terry Bouton's *Taming Democracy*, which analyzes post-Revolutionary Pennsylvania records. Bouton shows that, as part of a deliberate counter-revolutionary project to concentrate wealth and power, county sheriffs seized and auctioned the farms or property of more than 37 % of taxpayers in many localities during the 1780s. The action that fits the statistic and the historical context is therefore sheriff's sales (or the equivalent contemporary term, property foreclosures via tax and debt enforcement).\n\n\\boxed{sheriff's sales (PA farm foreclosures)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 218, "output_tokens": 117, "total_tokens": 335}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000565, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1460", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Heterogeneity across firms is behind a productivity shift in a model of this phenomenon created by Marc Melitz.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question refers to Marc Melitz's canonical 2003 model of trade with heterogeneous firms. In that framework, opening to trade (i.e., trade liberalization) induces a within-industry productivity shift because only the most productive firms export while the least productive firms exit. Firm heterogeneity is therefore the mechanism that generates the aggregate productivity gain, exactly as described.\n\nThus the phenomenon being modeled is trade liberalization.\n\n\\boxed{trade liberalization (Melitz 2003)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 201, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 293}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00048125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1472", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An army led by a member of this ethnic group was formed by a meeting in Bilpam, which is the name given to the headquarters of that army.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The ethnic group referred to is the Dinka people, as the Sudan People's Liberation Army (SPLA) was formed by John Garang and other leaders primarily from this group. The headquarters of the SPLA was famously established at Bilpam in Ethiopia.\n\n\\boxed{Dinka}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 143}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:00:30.521365+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0001095, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1478", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Grodzinsky and Reinhart argued against Grimshaw and Rosen that this grammatical phenomenon can only be understood as innate if it is processed by a di ferent module than co-reference.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query concerns a specific debate in the acquisition literature on Chomsky's binding theory. Grimshaw & Rosen (1990) claimed that children's (apparent) knowledge of Principles A/B already demonstrates innateness. Grodzinsky & Reinhart (1993) countered that such a claim is warranted only if the syntactic relation of binding is representationally and computationally segregated from the pragmatic relation of coreference (the latter being handled by a separate extra-syntactic module, e.g., Reinhart's Rule-I). Hence the grammatical phenomenon at issue is binding (specifically, Principle B effects).\n\n\\boxed{Principle B/binding (vs. coref.)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 278, "output_tokens": 672, "total_tokens": 950}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:57.685248+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0020275, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1496", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Greenwood et al. found that freewheel running prevents this phenomenon in rats by attenuating the activity of serotonin neurons in the dorsal raphe nucleus during stressful situations.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Greenwood et al. found that voluntary exercise prevents **learned helplessness** in rats by modulating the activity of serotonin neurons in the dorsal raphe nucleus. This phenomenon refers to the state where an organism exposed to uncontrollable stressors ceases to attempt escape even when opportunities arise.\n\n\\boxed{learned helplessness}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 86, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 145}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:00:30.125939+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00011, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1515", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a 2001 paper contrasting this value with \"prices,\" Greg Mankiw (MAN-\"cue\") and Ricardo Reis (\"race\") proposed that its \"stickiness\" could be used to construct an alternative to the Phillips curve.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The 2001 Mankiw-Reis paper is explicitly titled \u201cSticky Information Versus Sticky Prices,\u201d and it advances a model in which information (rather than prices) adjusts slowly, thereby generating an expectations-based alternative to the New Keynesian Phillips curve.  \nThe phrasing \u201ccontrasting this value with \u2018prices\u2019\u201d and the reference to \u201cits stickiness\u201d therefore identify the contrasted term as information.  \nNo other economic variable fits both the cited paper and the wording of the clue.\n\n\\boxed{information (sticky info.)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 226, "output_tokens": 105, "total_tokens": 331}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000545, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1584", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This book argues that, while the sciences of nature were born from the practices of investigation, the sciences of man arose from examination.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The phrasing in the query is a near-verbatim description of Michel Foucault\u2019s argument in *Discipline and Punish* (1975). There Foucault contrasts the emergence of the natural sciences (rooted in practices of empirical investigation and inquiry) with the human sciences (which, he claims, arose from the disciplinary technique of the examination that simultaneously observes, normalizes, and documents individuals). No other well-known work matches this specific contrast between \u201cinvestigation\u201d and \u201cexamination.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{Discipline & Punish (Foucault)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 206, "output_tokens": 108, "total_tokens": 314}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005275, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1619", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 1999 book cataloguing the \"languages\" of this continent was written by Marianne Mithun.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The book referenced is *The Languages of Native North America* by Marianne Mithun, published in 1999, which catalogs the indigenous languages of North America. This work focuses specifically on the linguistic diversity of Native American languages across North America. Therefore, the continent in question is North America.\n\n\\boxed{North America}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 84, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 153}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2864e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1628", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An essay arguing that the adoption of this practice was bad notes that progressivists seem to believe that this practice led to the creation of the Parthenon and the Mass in B Minor.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes Jared Diamond's well-known 1987 essay \"The Worst Mistake in the History of the Human Race,\" which contends that the shift to agriculture produced worse health, nutrition, and social outcomes for humans. The essay explicitly mocks the \"progressivist\" view that agriculture was a necessary precondition for later cultural achievements such as the Parthenon and Bach's Mass in B Minor. Hence the practice in question is agriculture (or, equivalently, farming).\n\n\\boxed{agriculture (J. Diamond essay)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 280, "output_tokens": 483, "total_tokens": 763}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:53.839251+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0015575, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_165", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A target value for one form of this quantity that is especially useful during periods of crisis can be found with the McCallum rule.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The McCallum rule is a monetary-policy rule (an alternative to the Taylor rule) that prescribes a target growth rate for the monetary base. The monetary base is simply the narrowest form (M0) of the broader money supply; because it can still be observed and controlled even when interest-rate channels break down, the rule is especially useful in crisis periods. Hence the referent of \u201cthis quantity\u201d is the money supply.\n\n\\boxed{money supply (M0/base)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 206, "output_tokens": 96, "total_tokens": 302}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004975, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1655", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a section of a paper titled \"The Problem Illustrated Anew,\" this man used an example from a law case in which a confectioner's mortars and pestles caused vibrations that prevented a doctor from using a stethoscope to examine patients; that paper by this man was published a few weeks before a Guido Calabresi article setting forth similar thoughts about liability rules in automobile accidents and is one of several of his papers that cite the case Sturges v. Bridgman.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The man described is Ronald Coase, known for his seminal work on externalities and the Coase Theorem. The example from \"The Problem of Social Cost\" involving the confectioner and the doctor references Sturges v. Bridgman, a case he frequently cited. His paper was indeed published shortly before Guido Calabresi's similar analysis, aligning with the context provided.\n\n\\boxed{Ronald Coase}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 160, "output_tokens": 90, "total_tokens": 250}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.0359999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1725", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In an oligopolistic market, the time series plot of this value may take on a sawtooth shape as a result of dynamic equilibria, as predicted by the theory of \"Edgeworth cycles.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The value described in the context of Edgeworth cycles in an oligopolistic market is price. In such markets, firms may engage in repeated price competition, leading to cyclical patterns of price cuts and recoveries, creating a sawtooth pattern in the time series of prices. This phenomenon is known as Edgeworth price cycles.\n\n\\boxed{price}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 175}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4541999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1743", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Before a front vowel, the Proto-Greek labiovelar \"k\u00c2\u00b7w\" became the sound represented by this letter.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Proto-Greek labiovelars (*k\u02b7, etc.) are known to have undergone conditioned splits in the development to Ancient Greek. One of the regular outcomes is that *k\u02b7 yields /t/ immediately before a front vowel (e.g., *penk\u02b7e > \u03c0\u03ad\u03bd\u03c4\u03b5). That coronal stop is represented by the letter tau.\n\nThus the required answer is tau (\u03c4).\n\n\\boxed{tau (\u03c4)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 206, "output_tokens": 87, "total_tokens": 293}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000475, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1755", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One economist disputed traditional approaches to this situation by formulating eight design principles, including the use of \"graduated sanctions\"; that economist, Elinor Ostrom, wrote a book that offered governing methods in response to this situation.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The situation described refers to the management of shared resources that are prone to depletion by individual users acting in their own self-interest. Elinor Ostrom famously addressed this in her seminal work, *Governing the Commons*, by challenging the idea that such resources must be managed by the state or privatized.\n\n\\boxed{Tragedy of the commons}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 166}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:00:32.508101+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000129, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1844", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The so-called \"father\" of this kind of \u70a4rm was a French immigrant who earned the nickname \"the General\" for supervising R&amp;D for the U.S. Army during World War II.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue describes Georges Doriot, a French immigrant who rose to brigadier general while overseeing U.S. Army R&D in World War II. After the war he founded American Research and Development Corporation, the first institutional venture-capital firm, and is universally recognized as \u201cthe father of venture capital.\u201d The malformed token \u201c\u70a4rm\u201d is therefore resolved as \u201cfirm,\u201d yielding the referent \u201cventure capital firm.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{venture capital firm}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 222, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 311}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1847", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This approach was used by Albrecht and Axell to develop a model that assumes two types of sellers with different reservation prices.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given statement describes a classic result from the equilibrium search literature in economics (specifically, models of wage or price dispersion). Albrecht and Axell (1984) generate an equilibrium distribution of posted prices by combining costly search with an exogenous two-point distribution of seller costs (i.e., reservation prices). This is the canonical illustration of what the literature therefore labels the \u201cheterogeneity approach.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{heterogeneity approach (2-type res. prices)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 204, "output_tokens": 90, "total_tokens": 294}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00048, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1852", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Japanese economic anthropologist Naoki Kasuga argued that a type of these phenomena did not presuppose a \"parts-and-whole image.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question phrasing indicates a \"common link\" style query whose referent is a category of phenomena discussed in economic anthropology. Kasuga's work (drawing on actor-network theory and related ontological debates) explicitly treats networks as lacking any presupposed \"parts-and-whole\" hierarchy; they are instead flat, emergent assemblages. This matches the quoted argument exactly and rules out near-synonyms such as \"economies,\" \"markets,\" or \"multiplicities.\"\n\n\\boxed{networks}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 206, "output_tokens": 94, "total_tokens": 300}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004925, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1891", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A monograph on this subject argues that it relies on five \"sociological presuppositions,\" such as \"man's aim in life is happiness,\"and five \"myths,\" such as that of \"the Youth;\" that book distinguishes its \"agitative\" from its \"integrative\" form, which is made necessary by technology.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The described monograph refers to \"Propaganda\" by Jacques Ellul, which analyzes propaganda as a sociological phenomenon relying on underlying presuppositions and myths. Ellul distinguishes between agitative propaganda (used to incite action or revolution) and integrative propaganda (used to maintain social order, especially in technologically advanced societies). The subject of the monograph is propaganda.\n\n\\boxed{propaganda}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 127, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 211}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.7417000000000003e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_196", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The ability to vocalize this action is heavily limited within the Pama\u2013Nyungan language family.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question is a reference to a known linguistic feature of (many) Australian Aboriginal languages in the Pama\u2013Nyungan family: they lack direct lexical equivalents for refusal. As a result, the speech act of negation/refusal cannot readily be vocalized and must instead be conveyed indirectly or via circumlocution. This produces the surface phrasing \u201cthe ability to vocalize this action [refusing / saying \u2018no\u2019] is heavily limited.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{saying \"no\" (refusing)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 200, "output_tokens": 99, "total_tokens": 299}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004975, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_2", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An injunctive message can block a negative outcome of this process through the \"boomerang effect.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement refers to a well-known finding from Cialdini\u2019s research on norm-based persuasion. When a purely descriptive norm is communicated (e.g., \u201cmost people use X amount of energy\u201d), individuals already behaving better than the norm can increase their consumption\u2014the classic boomerang effect. Pairing the descriptive information with an injunctive norm (approval or disapproval) eliminates this unintended backlash, thereby protecting the desired outcome of the social-norms intervention.\n\nThus the \u201cprocess\u201d named in the prompt is social-norms marketing (or descriptive-norm feedback).\n\n\\boxed{social-norms mktg (descr. norms fbk)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 201, "output_tokens": 128, "total_tokens": 329}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00057125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_224", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A social scientist with this surname found that relative community sizes are key to explaining why the Chewa and Tumbuka ethnic groups have better relations in Zambia than in Malawi.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The social scientist is Daniel Posner, who analyzed this phenomenon in his book *Institutions and Ethnic Politics in Africa*. He argued that the different sizes of the Chewa and Tumbuka groups relative to the national population in each country determine whether they are treated as political allies or rivals.\n\n\\boxed{Posner}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 88, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 153}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:00:28.800847+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0001195, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_280", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The best-known work of Francis Moore Lapp\u00e9 is dedicated to developing more environmentally-friendly ways to use this commodity.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The clue refers to Frances Moore Lapp\u00e9\u2019s landmark 1971 book *Diet for a Small Planet*. That work is devoted to showing how the global food supply (especially grain and plant protein) can be used far more efficiently and with far less environmental damage than the prevailing practice of feeding grain to livestock. Hence the commodity in question is food (or, more narrowly, grain/protein).\n\n\\boxed{food (grain/protein)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 203, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 291}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00047375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_312", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Hotelling's lemma shows this quantity is equal to the derivative of another function.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Hotelling's lemma applies to a firm's differentiable profit function \\(\\pi(p, w)\\) in producer theory. Differentiating this function with respect to each output or input price directly recovers the corresponding profit-maximizing net supply (or factor demand) quantity. Thus the lemma equates the economically relevant quantity\u2014supply\u2014to the indicated derivative.\n\n\\boxed{supply (fn./net output)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 196, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 271}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0004325, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_339", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A book by William Sumner concludes that different groups defined by this concept owe very little to one another.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The phrasing of the question directly matches the central thesis of William Graham Sumner's 1883 book *What Social Classes Owe to Each Other*. In that work Sumner applies a strict laissez-faire argument to argue that individuals belonging to one social stratum have no inherent obligations toward those in another. The concept that therefore defines the groups in question is social class (or simply class).\n\n\\boxed{social class (class)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 200, "output_tokens": 82, "total_tokens": 282}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000455, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_401", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: William Julius Wilson's book When Work Disappears argues that the disappearance of blue-collar jobs from this country's cities contributes to urban poverty.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is true. In *When Work Disappears*, William Julius Wilson argues that the decline of manufacturing and blue-collar employment in inner cities led to a rise in joblessness, which subsequently fueled concentrated poverty and social dislocation.\n\n\\boxed{True}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 83, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 135}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:00:30.460996+00:00"}, "cost": 9.875e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_415", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Daniel Burnham led a movement in the early 20th-century that advocated beautifying these places in order to instill civic loyalty.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Daniel Burnham was a leading figure in the City Beautiful movement, which aimed to beautify cities through grand public spaces, monumental architecture, and improved urban planning to promote civic pride and social order. This movement targeted urban centers, particularly American cities, to instill civic loyalty through aesthetic and functional improvements. The places he sought to beautify were cities.\n\n\\boxed{cities}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 87, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 163}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3777e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_453", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This phenomenon is efficient in directed search models but may be inefficient in random search.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question pertains to search-and-matching models in labor economics. In random-search frameworks, agents' uncoordinated decisions (e.g., how intensively to search while employed) typically generate congestion or thick-market externalities that violate the Hosios condition and produce inefficient outcomes. In directed/competitive-search settings, wage posting or market utility posting internalizes those externalities, restoring constrained efficiency for the same decisions. Hence the phenomenon that satisfies this efficiency contrast is on-the-job search.\n\n\\boxed{on-the-job search (w/ free entry)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 196, "output_tokens": 105, "total_tokens": 301}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005075, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_465", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: As part of an investigative article for Mother Jones, Shane Bauer spent four months working in one of these places in Winnfield, Louisiana.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Shane Bauer worked undercover at a private prison operated by Corrections Corporation of America (now CoreCivic) in Winnfield, Louisiana, for his Mother Jones investigation. His expos\u00e9 detailed the harsh conditions and systemic issues within the facility. The correct answer is a private prison.\n\n\\boxed{private prison}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 86, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 148}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2306e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_482", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Japan, spirits named \"mizu\" or \"water\" people of this type are honored in a funeral ceremony invoking a bodhisattva whose statues are commonly found on roadsides and graveyards named Jizo.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The spirits referred to are unborn children, particularly those lost through miscarriage, stillbirth, or abortion, known as \"mizuko,\" meaning \"water child.\" These spirits are honored in the mizuko kuy\u014d ceremony, where Jizo statues\u2014commonly found by roadsides and in graveyards\u2014are adorned with offerings like red hats and toys. Jizo, as a bodhisattva, is believed to protect these vulnerable souls in the afterlife.\n\n\\boxed{mizuko}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 103, "output_tokens": 102, "total_tokens": 205}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.7513000000000003e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_57", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 1985 book argues that this concept's \"essentialist\" form results from a lack of correspondence between economic and social understandings of class, and must be combatted through a dual \"war of maneuver\" and a \"war of position.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question describes arguments from Laclau and Mouffe's Hegemony and Socialist Strategy (1985). That work invokes Gramsci's paired military metaphors to describe how socialists should counter the reduction of all political subjects to an assumed working-class core. The same non-correspondence between economic position and ideological interpellation is precisely what Laclau and Mouffe identify as the origin of an \"essentialist\" conception of populism; hence the referent of the question is populism.\n\n\\boxed{populism}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 229, "output_tokens": 102, "total_tokens": 331}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00054125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_641", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: It's not in the Caucasus, but languages in this country reportedly have bilabially trilled voiceless alveolar affricates.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The rare phonetic segment in question is the voiceless alveolar affricate with simultaneous bilabial trill, commonly notated [t\u032a\u0299\u0325] or [t\u0299\u0325]. This segment is documented in the Chapacuran language Wari\u2019 (and a few neighboring Amazonian varieties) spoken inside Brazil; it does not occur in any Caucasian language. Hence the country referenced by the clue is Brazil.\n\n\\boxed{Brazil}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 205, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 291}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00047125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_693", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Eastern Armenian is a rare example of a language that uses this feature for contrast in word-final positions.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question is a linguistic clue referring to a rare phonemic contrast preserved in Eastern Armenian (but neutralized in most languages). Stops in this language have a three-way laryngeal distinction (voiced, voiceless unaspirated, voiceless aspirated); the last two series remain contrastive even word-finally because release and aspiration cues are retained. Hence the feature in question is aspiration (or, equivalently, the contrast between aspirated and unaspirated voiceless stops).\n\n\\boxed{aspiration (final C contrast)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 200, "output_tokens": 103, "total_tokens": 303}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0005075, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_724", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This man befriended Dr. Saxton Pope while receiving treatment for various diseases, and he taught Pope the skills that were later honored by the Pope and Young Club.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The man who befriended Dr. Saxton Pope and taught him traditional hunting and archery skills was Ishi, the last member of the Yahi tribe. Ishi's expertise in bow-making and archery greatly influenced Pope, whose legacy, along with Art Young, led to the founding of the Pope and Young Club, which promotes ethical big game hunting. The skills Ishi preserved are honored by the club's dedication to fair chase and conservation.\n\n\\boxed{Ishi}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 97, "total_tokens": 190}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.6303e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_741", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The short film Unnecessary Fuss shows horrific injuries inflicted on one of these beings.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The short film *Unnecessary Fuss* documents footage of animal cruelty involving baboons at the University of Pennsylvania's Head Injury Clinic. The film was created by PETA using stolen tapes to expose the mistreatment of these primates during head injury research.\n\n\\boxed{baboons}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 70, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 127}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:00:29.215422+00:00"}, "cost": 0.000103, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_754", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An effect named for this economist holds that decreases in prices will cause interest rates to fall, leading to an increase in investment.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The described mechanism matches the Keynes effect, in which a fall in the price level raises real money balances, shifts the LM curve rightward, lowers the equilibrium interest rate, and thereby stimulates investment spending. This transmission channel is conventionally attributed to J. M. Keynes and is distinct from the Pigou (real-balance) effect on consumption. Hence the economist named in the question is Keynes.\n\n\\boxed{Keynes}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 205, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 288}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00046375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_77", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An essay by Joane Nagel analyzes the role of the \"patriotic\" form of this concept in the rise of nationalism.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question points to a specific scholarly analysis of how nationalism is constructed through gender. Joane Nagel's well-known essay \"Masculinity and Nationalism\" (1998) explicitly examines the role of the \"patriotic\" variant of masculinity in forging national identities and movements. No other concept fits the phrasing or the cited author's body of work.\n\nThus, the answer is masculinity.\n\n\\boxed{masculinity}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 205, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 286}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00045875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_806", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: John McCall developed a field of economics around people who perform this action based on the mathematical theory of optimal stopping.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question refers to the application of optimal stopping theory (e.g., the secretary problem) to labor markets. John McCall's seminal 1970 model formalized job search theory, in which unemployed workers sequentially receive wage offers and must decide whether to accept or continue searching. Thus the action performed by the agents in this field of economics is searching for a job (or job hunting).\n\n\\boxed{job searching (search theory)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 203, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 289}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00046875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_896", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Open economies allow for foreign firms to establish a controlling interest in domestic companies, known as the foreign direct type of this activity.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question refers to the type of economic activity where foreign firms gain controlling interest in domestic companies. This is known as foreign direct investment (FDI). The blank is best filled with \"investment.\"\n\n\\boxed{investment}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 167}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3626e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_902", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Michael Walzer popularized a thought experiment in which these figures must potentially violate fundamental morality in pursuit of a greater good, the problem of \"dirty hands.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The thought experiment described refers to political leaders or rulers who may have to commit morally questionable acts for the sake of a greater political good, a concept known as \"the problem of dirty hands.\" Michael Walzer discussed this in the context of political morality, focusing on figures like politicians or statesmen. The most common answer is \"politicians.\"\n\n\\boxed{politicians}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 165}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.389e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_907", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Herfindahl Index calculates how well this condition is being met in an industry.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Herfindahl-Hirschman Index (HHI) is computed as the sum of squared market shares of all firms in an industry. A lower HHI value indicates greater dispersion of shares (i.e., more firms of roughly equal size), which corresponds directly to the degree to which competitive conditions are satisfied. Thus the index quantifies how well the economic condition of competition is being met.\n\n\\boxed{competition (mkt conc./perf. comp.)\n}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 197, "output_tokens": 93, "total_tokens": 290}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00047875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_965", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An 1893 book refutes the \"happiness hypothesis\" and offers explanations for the function, causes, and abnormal forms of one phenomenon affecting this concept.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given statement describes a book that refutes the notion that a certain phenomenon arises solely from happiness, while also analyzing that phenomenon's evolutionary role, triggers, and pathologies (e.g., hysterical or neurological variants).  \n\nThese elements collectively point to laughter as the phenomenon in question, making the affected concept humor.  \n\n(The most common concise answer to the query is therefore simply the word \"humor.\")\n\n\\boxed{humor}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 212, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 296}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000475, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_982", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Phebe Cramer showed that Israeli kids who grew up during war were more likely to demonstrate these things than their older peers, in a study of them \"in action\".\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Phebe Cramer is a developmental psychologist whose research centers on the maturation of ego defenses (e.g., denial, projection, identification) across childhood. In a study conducted during the 1991 Gulf War, she compared Israeli children who had lived under missile attack with age-matched peers; the younger cohort displayed reliably higher rates of immature defenses, which she interpreted as defenses \u201cin action.\u201d Thus the phrase \u201cthese things\u201d refers to defense mechanisms.\n\n\\boxed{defense mechanisms (immature ones)}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 213, "output_tokens": 99, "total_tokens": 312}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00051375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_10198", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Sasha had to do a group project, so she set up a meeting with her group to discuss the project in detail.\n\nQuestion: Why did Sasha set up a meeting?\n\nOptions: \nA. Yell at her group members\nB. Discuss the project\nC. figure out the direction to take\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Sasha set up a meeting to talk about the project with her group, which means she wanted to communicate and plan together. The most direct reason based on the context is to discuss the project in detail. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 120, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 174}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.392e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_10992", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: When all the towels were handed out, Ash accidentally got Cameron's towel.\n\nQuestion: How would you describe Ash?\n\nOptions: \nA. be unhappy about the mix\nB. very neutral\nC. someone who needs a towel\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "C. someone who needs a towel\n\nAsh received Cameron's towel, which implies Ash was expecting or in need of a towel. The context focuses on the distribution of towels, suggesting Ash is one of the people who needed one. \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 159}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2826e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_11868", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Jordan was in a city. Jordan suddenly heard a sound.\n\nQuestion: How would you describe Jordan?\n\nOptions: \nA. scared\nB. busy at work\nC. a cautious person\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given context supplies no details about Jordan's feelings, job, or character, so none of the options can be inferred. Selecting any choice would require an unsupported assumption. The only defensible response is therefore that no option is correct.\n\n\\boxed{none}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 219, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 271}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00040375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_12792", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Ash told Sydney about the thing she had forgotten when she left college.\n\nQuestion: What does Ash need to do before this?\n\nOptions: \nA. listen to ash\nB. meet up with Sydney\nC. ignore Sydney's phone calls\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Ash needs to meet up with or contact Sydney in order to remind her of something she forgot. Therefore, the most logical action Ash must take before telling her is to meet up with Sydney. Listening to Ash or ignoring calls doesn't fit the context of initiating the communication.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 168}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3667999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_12968", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Jordan has a large collection of stamps, but it is too big. Jordan got rid of the collection altogether.\n\nQuestion: How would you describe Jordan?\n\nOptions: \nA. anger that he discarded the entire stamp collection\nB. unattached to material things\nC. regret that he got rid of the stamp collection\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Jordan chose to get rid of a large collection altogether, which suggests a lack of strong attachment to possessions. This action indicates a willingness to let go of material items without apparent hesitation. Therefore, the best description is that Jordan is unattached to material things.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 123, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 180}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4433e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_13225", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Quinn was the goalie on the soccer team and tried to block a shot.\n\nQuestion: What would others sitting in the stands do?\n\nOptions: \nA. would tell Quinn to let the ball go\nB. would jump up and scream\nC. a great athlete\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Others in the stands would likely react emotionally to an exciting moment like a shot on goal. They would probably jump up and scream in anticipation or excitement. This is a common fan reaction during intense moments in sports.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 161}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2823e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_13366", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Kai checked their mail and found out that they had some packages.\n\nQuestion: How would you describe Kai?\n\nOptions: \nA. surprised and curious\nB. quite angry\nC. interested in their mail\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely answer is \\boxed{C}. Receiving packages is a routine event that typically generates interest in what has arrived. Options A and B imply strong emotional reactions that are not supported by the neutral context provided.", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 142}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:00:33.848992+00:00"}, "cost": 8.925e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_13810", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: After spending the whole day studying, Sasha decided to watch TV and get Chinese food.\n\nQuestion: What will Sasha want to do after studying?\n\nOptions: \nA. Complete his reading\nB. decided to watch TV\nC. decided to study food\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Sasha finished studying and made plans to watch TV and get Chinese food. The question asks what Sasha wants to do after studying, and one of the activities mentioned is watching TV. Therefore, the most accurate answer based on the context is that Sasha decided to watch TV.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 170}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3809999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_1453", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Lee's friend had to pain the fence around the yard.  Lee help his friend paint it.\n\nQuestion: How could Lee be described?\n\nOptions: \nA. selfish\nB. very, very lazy\nC. helpful\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Lee helped his friend paint the fence, which shows he supported his friend with a task. This behavior demonstrates a willingness to assist. Therefore, Lee could be described as helpful.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 41, "total_tokens": 146}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1555e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_14652", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Sasha improved her performance a lot after she listened to the teacher.\n\nQuestion: What did Sasha do before this?\n\nOptions: \nA. ignore her teacher\nB. watch TV all day\nC. listen to the teacher\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Sasha improved her performance after listening to the teacher, which implies that her prior behavior was different. The improvement suggests she previously did not listen or follow the teacher's advice. Therefore, the most likely answer is that she ignored her teacher before.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 104, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2783999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_14695", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Austin reached their goals and decided to celebrate by throwing a big party at the local country club.\n\nQuestion: How would you describe Austin?\n\nOptions: \nA. cares about treating his friends\nB. doesn't want anyone else to have food\nC. as happy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}\n\nAustin is described as happy because they reached their goals and chose to celebrate with a big party. Celebrating a personal achievement is a common expression of joy and satisfaction.", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 38, "total_tokens": 149}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:00:34.758442+00:00"}, "cost": 8.475e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_15288", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: It was Kai's favorite song and they liked every time they heard it play.\n\nQuestion: How would you describe Kai?\n\nOptions: \nA. excited afterwards\nB. pleased afterwards\nC. As someone who likes the song\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question asks how to describe Kai based on their reaction to hearing their favorite song. Since the context emphasizes that Kai likes the song every time they hear it, the best description is directly about their ongoing feeling toward the song. Therefore, the most accurate answer is that Kai is someone who likes the song.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 105, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 172}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4155e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_15322", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Riley went to visit their friend Tracy who is in the hospital.\n\nQuestion: What will happen to Riley?\n\nOptions: \nA. be upset\nB. be happy\nC. freak out\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Riley is visiting a friend in the hospital, which suggests a concern for Tracy's well-being. While Riley might feel worried, the act of visiting indicates care and support rather than extreme distress. The most likely response is a moderate emotional reaction.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 153}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": n