of immediately grabbing his gun in response to seeing one suggests a readiness to confront or match aggression. This behavior aligns more with a combative demeanor rather than calm or neutral behavior. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 145}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1629e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_25568", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Addison layered Casey's hair when they asked for a new type of haircut.\n\nQuestion: What does Addison need to do before layering the hair?\n\nOptions: \nA. shave off the hair\nB. give a sample look of the style\nC. cut more peoples hair\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Before layering hair, it's important to show the client a sample or visual of the desired style to ensure alignment and approval. This helps avoid misunderstandings and ensures the client is happy with the intended result. Shaving off the hair or cutting other people's hair is not a necessary prerequisite.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 180}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4665e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_25951", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Casey got the things together so they would be prepared for school.\n\nQuestion: What does Casey need to do before this?\n\nOptions: \nA. have their things prepared for school\nB. know what they need\nC. be ready for school\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Casey needs to know what they need before gathering the things for school. Without knowing the required items, they wouldn't be able to prepare effectively. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{B}.", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 151}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1939e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_26846", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Remy added a new gem to their collection. Soon they would have them all.\n\nQuestion: What will Remy want to do next?\n\nOptions: \nA. collect all the gems\nB. sell all the gems\nC. needed to find the gems\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Remy is actively adding gems to their collection, indicating a goal of gathering them all. The context suggests a desire to complete the set rather than dispose of or search for them. Therefore, Remy will most likely want to continue collecting.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 166}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3352e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_26973", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Jordan was gambling and saw that he could win more.\n\nQuestion: How would you describe Jordan?\n\nOptions: \nA. glad he took a chance\nB. win\nC. someone who gambles often\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question asks how to describe Jordan based on the context that he was gambling and saw he could win more. This suggests a characteristic or trait about Jordan, not just a momentary outcome. The most fitting description is that he is someone who engages in gambling regularly.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 160}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3070999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_27023", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Sasha went to the store for a new jacket. It was the wrong color but she bought it anyways.\n\nQuestion: What did Sasha do?\n\nOptions: \nA. liked it\nB. bought a new skirt\nC. went to the store\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Sasha went to the store to buy a new jacket, which indicates her action was visiting the store. Even though the jacket was the wrong color, she still bought it, but the question asks what Sasha *did*, not how she felt. The best answer reflecting her action is that she went to the store.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 178}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4639e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_27231", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Aubrey was given a present by Sydney who decided to come and give them one.\n\nQuestion: What's going to happen with Aubrey?\n\nOptions: \nA. be mad that Sydney gave them a bad gift\nB. want to fight Sydney for bringing a present\nC. thank Sydney for being very nice to them\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Aubrey received a present from Sydney, who made the effort to come and give it to them. This suggests a positive and thoughtful gesture from Sydney. Therefore, the most likely response from Aubrey is gratitude.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 124, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 173}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3704e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_28285", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Ash attempted to take Addison's test which was harder.\n\nQuestion: How would you describe Ash?\n\nOptions: \nA. like a failure\nB. wanting to take a harder test\nC. intelligent\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Ash attempted to take Addison's test, which was described as harder, suggesting Ash was seeking a greater challenge. This indicates motivation and a willingness to tackle difficult tasks. Therefore, the most accurate description is that Ash is wanting to take a harder test.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 156}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2699999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_28639", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Ash developed their skills as a computer programmer so they could get a better job.\n\nQuestion: How would you describe Ash?\n\nOptions: \nA. ambitious\nB. capable and proud\nC. lazy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Ash worked to improve their skills with the goal of advancing their career, which shows drive and determination. This behavior best reflects ambition.  \n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 33, "total_tokens": 133}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.04e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_28828", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Ash tickled Kendall's fancy dog's stomach and gave her a huge treat.\n\nQuestion: How would you describe Ash?\n\nOptions: \nA. generous\nB. bad with animals\nC. angry\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Ash is described as tickling the dog's stomach and giving her a large treat, which shows kindness and generosity toward the animal. This behavior reflects a generous and caring attitude rather than anger or discomfort around animals. Therefore, the best description of Ash is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 157}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2800000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_29169", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Alex told Robin they had to leave because it was time to do home work.\n\nQuestion: What will Robin want to do next?\n\nOptions: \nA. Enforce the rule set in place\nB. Make them obey rules\nC. go home\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Robin was told it was time to leave because they needed to do homework, implying that going home is the next logical step. The question asks what Robin will want to do next, and the most direct response to the situation is to go home. Options A and B involve enforcing rules, which doesn't align as closely with Robin's likely personal next action.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 187}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.551e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_30036", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Jordan was tired and decided to wander off and hurt people at the fair.\n\nQuestion: How would you describe Jordan?\n\nOptions: \nA. a hopeful man who hopes to be the next ted bundy\nB. an evil person that should be on the deathbed\nC. just confused lately\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context describes Jordan as tired and acting out by hurting people, which suggests internal struggle rather than inherent evil or a clear criminal aspiration. Option C acknowledges this possible emotional confusion without jumping to extreme conclusions. Therefore, the most balanced and likely accurate description is:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 119, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 176}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4149000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_30913", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Sydney got home late after partying all night with their friends.\n\nQuestion: How would you describe Sydney?\n\nOptions: \nA. exhausted\nB. feeling drunk\nC. wiped out\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}\n\nWhile all options describe a state of fatigue or impairment, \"exhausted\" is the most neutral and encompassing term for someone who has been partying all night. Options B and C are more specific or informal, but \"exhausted\" directly addresses the physical state resulting from a lack of sleep.", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 158}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:00:44.835734+00:00"}, "cost": 0.0001195, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_31357", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Ash was sitting around the fire pit and only a little fire was going. Ash added gas to the flame to really get it going.\n\nQuestion: What does Ash need to do before this?\n\nOptions: \nA. keep close watch on the fire\nB. needed to go outside\nC. needed to go inside\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Ash needed to go outside to access the fire pit, as fire pits are typically located outdoors. Since Ash was sitting around the fire pit, it implies the action takes place outside, so going outside would be necessary before tending to the fire.  \nTherefore, the most logical action Ash needed to do before this is go outside.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 123, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 195}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5933e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_32014", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Sasha wanted to get good at ballet. Sasha improved their performance by practicing every day.\n\nQuestion: What will Sasha want to do next?\n\nOptions: \nA. practice more\nB. wanted to get good at ballet\nC. be lazy instead\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Sasha has shown consistent effort to improve at ballet by practicing every day, indicating a strong commitment to getting better. It is logical that Sasha would continue this positive behavior to further enhance their skills. Therefore, the most likely next step is to continue practicing.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 166}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3439e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_32670", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Riley had just turned 14 and spent at least two hours in the bathroom getting ready every day. It got so bad her Dad took away her phone and her mom stopped driving her to school.\n\nQuestion: What happened to Riley?\n\nOptions: \nA. stopped getting rides to school\nB. won an Emmy\nC. was run over by a reindeer\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Riley's parents took disciplinary actions because she was spending too much time getting ready. Her mom stopped driving her to school, which means Riley no longer received rides. This matches option A.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 133, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 177}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3843e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_33370", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Tracy just got her driver's license and a new car. Tracy was driving to school now.\n\nQuestion: What does Tracy need to do before this?\n\nOptions: \nA. pass her driver's test\nB. get to school\nC. get to class\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Tracy needed to pass her driver's test before she could legally drive to school. Getting to school and getting to class happen after obtaining a license. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 155}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2251999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_33779", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Kai stayed home from work, so Kai spent several hours online doing nothing.\n\nQuestion: How would you describe Kai?\n\nOptions: \nA. guilty\nB. productive\nC. lazy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Kai stayed home from work and spent time online doing nothing, which suggests a lack of activity or effort. This behavior aligns most closely with the description of being lazy. Therefore, the most accurate choice is:\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 146}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1786999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_34238", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Mark offered Austin chocolate cake with sprinkles. Austin wanted ice cream instead.\n\nQuestion: How would you describe Austin?\n\nOptions: \nA. satisfied\nB. frustrated\nC. delighted\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Austin wanted ice cream instead of the chocolate cake, which indicates he did not get what he desired. This suggests he was not satisfied or delighted with the offer. Therefore, the most accurate description is that he was frustrated.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 147}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1887e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_4716", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Jesse called Carson's friend to find out if they might like to go to the zoo with them.\n\nQuestion: What will happen to Carson's friend?\n\nOptions: \nA. enthusiastic about the trip\nB. go to the zoo with Carson\u00b4s friend\nC. go to the zoo alone\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question asks what will happen to Carson's friend, based on Jesse calling them to invite them to the zoo. The most logical outcome is that Carson's friend will accept the invitation and go to the zoo with Jesse and Carson. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A} \n\nCarson's friend is likely to be enthusiastic about the trip, which best reflects a positive response to the invitation. Option B is incorrect because it suggests the friend would go with themselves, and C contradicts the context of a shared outing.", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 118, "output_tokens": 108, "total_tokens": 226}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.9178000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_4822", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Ash used a model to represent the story of his family tree.\n\nQuestion: How would you describe Ash?\n\nOptions: \nA. thoughtful\nB. boring\nC. lazy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Ash used a model to represent his family tree, which shows effort and intention in preserving and sharing his family's story. This indicates thoughtfulness and care in presenting something meaningful. Therefore, the best description is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 143}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1545e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_5673", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Jordan loved fire but this time he went too far and set his house on fire, he had to call the fire department.\n\nQuestion: How would you describe Jordan?\n\nOptions: \nA. dangerous\nB. a good neighbor\nC. embarrassed that the house was on fire\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Jordan's action of setting his house on fire due to his love for fire suggests reckless behavior, which aligns most closely with being dangerous. While he might also feel embarrassed, the description emphasizes his actions rather than emotions. Being a good neighbor is inconsistent with the situation described.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 176}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4265e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_6527", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Ash is relaxing and having a good day off work.\n\nQuestion: How would you describe Ash?\n\nOptions: \nA. hardworking\nB. relaxed\nC. easily angered\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Ash is described as \"relaxing and having a good day off work,\" which suggests a calm and content state. This best aligns with the option that reflects a current emotional state of ease. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 141}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1344999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_7241", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Jan will never see Sasha after she moves from France because of her new work in Washington, D.C.\n\nQuestion: What will happen to Sasha and Jan?\n\nOptions: \nA. depressed\nB. lonely\nC. live in different countries\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context states that Jan will never see Sasha after she moves from France to Washington, D.C., indicating a permanent separation due to geography. This means they will be living in different countries\u2014France and the United States. Therefore, the most accurate outcome is that they will live in different countries.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 108, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 173}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4167999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_7411", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Remy bought a new dog for Alex and gave to to him on his birthday.\n\nQuestion: What will happen to Remy?\n\nOptions: \nA. become a dog owner\nB. give the dog to Alex\nC. sell the dog\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Remy bought the dog and gave it to Alex, so he is not keeping it. Therefore, Remy will not become a dog owner or sell the dog after the gift. The action that happens to Remy is completing the act of giving the dog to Alex.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 122, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 182}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4662e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_7682", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Jesse was glad to have Bailey's support.\n\nQuestion: What will happen to Jesse?\n\nOptions: \nA. thank Bailey\nB. provide jesse support\nC. do\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Jesse was glad to have Bailey's support, which suggests Jesse appreciates the help. It is natural to respond to support with gratitude. Therefore, Jesse will most likely thank Bailey.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 138}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1044999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_7839", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Riley had gone to the store to buy liquor for a party they were having that evening.\n\nQuestion: What does Riley need to do after this?\n\nOptions: \nA. make sure they had a fun party\nB. go to checkout\nC. serve alcohol at the party\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "After buying liquor at the store, the next immediate step Riley needs to take is to complete the purchase by going to checkout. This step logically follows selecting items and precedes using the alcohol at the party. Options A and C occur later and are not immediate next steps.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 175}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4164999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_7915", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Jordan really wanted it and saved up for a long time to be able to buy it.\n\nQuestion: How would you describe Jordan?\n\nOptions: \nA. a forgetful person\nB. a focused person\nC. a cold person\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Jordan demonstrated determination by saving for a long time to achieve a goal, which shows persistence and concentration. This behavior aligns best with being focused. Therefore, the most accurate description is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 150}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1896999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_827", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Ash needed more room and moved Cameron over an inch.\n\nQuestion: What does Ash need to do before this?\n\nOptions: \nA. walk away\nB. stay still\nC. gently shove Cameron over\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Ash needed to move Cameron, which implies some action was required to create more room. \"Gently shove Cameron over\" aligns with the action described. Therefore, the most logical preceding action is C.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 148}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1870999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_8557", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Ash raised and supported him. Their parents had been dead since they were kids.\n\nQuestion: What does Ash need to do before this?\n\nOptions: \nA. accept the job before her\nB. remain closely connected\nC. send him to college\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Based on the context provided, Ash raised and supported him after their parents died, which implies a long-term commitment to his upbringing and education. Among the choices, sending him to college is a logical step in the process of raising and supporting a sibling into adulthood.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 166}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:00:44.044993+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00011525, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SocialiQA_9152", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Jordan studied for a week for the big test that they had coming up.\n\nQuestion: How would you describe Jordan?\n\nOptions: \nA. smart\nB. forgetful\nC. over\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Jordan studied for a week for the test, which shows dedication and preparation. This behavior suggests they are likely responsible and academically inclined. Therefore, the best description among the options is \"smart.\"\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 144}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1558e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4430", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: The man turned on the faucet.\n\nQuestion: what's the effect of this?\n\nOptions: \nA. The toilet filled with water.\nB. Water flowed from the spout.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "When a man turns on the faucet, it typically results in water coming out of the spout. This is the direct and expected effect of that action. The toilet filling with water is unrelated to turning on a faucet.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 144}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1645e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4434", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: The hamburger meat browned.\n\nQuestion: what's the cause for this?\n\nOptions: \nA. The cook froze it.\nB. The cook grilled it.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The browning of hamburger meat is typically caused by cooking at high heat, such as grilling. Freezing meat would not cause it to brown; instead, it preserves the meat. Therefore, the most likely cause is that the cook grilled it.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 147}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2061e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4439", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: The man drank heavily at the party.\n\nQuestion: what's the effect of this?\n\nOptions: \nA. He had a headache the next day.\nB. He had a runny nose the next day.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely effect of drinking heavily at a party is experiencing a headache the next day, commonly known as a hangover. A runny nose is less directly related to alcohol consumption. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 151}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2171e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4440", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: The bowling ball knocked over the bowling pins.\n\nQuestion: what's the cause for this?\n\nOptions: \nA. The man rolled the bowling ball down the alley.\nB. The man dropped the bowling ball on his foot.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The cause of the bowling ball knocking over the pins is that it was rolled down the alley, which is the standard action in bowling. Dropping the ball on a foot would not result in the ball reaching the pins. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 126, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 191}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.5446e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4442", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: My computer crashed.\n\nQuestion: what's the effect of this?\n\nOptions: \nA. I installed new speakers.\nB. I lost all my data.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The crash of a computer can result in data loss, especially if there was no backup or proper shutdown. Installing new speakers is unrelated to a system crash. Therefore, the most likely effect is losing data.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 136}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.099e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4445", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: The judge pounded the gavel.\n\nQuestion: what's the cause for this?\n\nOptions: \nA. The courtroom broke into uproar.\nB. The jury announced its verdict.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely cause for a judge pounding a gavel is to restore order in a chaotic environment. Therefore, an uproar in the courtroom is the standard reason for this action.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 134}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:00:38.615932+00:00"}, "cost": 8.35e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4448", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: The cook's eyes watered.\n\nQuestion: what's the cause for this?\n\nOptions: \nA. He ran out of onions.\nB. He cut an onion.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The cook's eyes watered because cutting an onion releases chemicals that irritate the eyes, causing tears. This is a common reaction when preparing onions in cooking.  \nTherefore, the most likely cause is that he cut an onion.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 145}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1803e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4452", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: I put my hands under the running faucet.\n\nQuestion: what's the effect of this?\n\nOptions: \nA. The soap rinsed off my hands.\nB. The water splashed in my face.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "When hands are placed under a running faucet, the primary effect is that water flows over them, which would rinse off any soap present. Option A describes a direct and logical consequence of placing hands under running water. Option B is less likely unless specific splashing conditions are mentioned, which are not indicated here.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 166}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.37e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4456", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: My view of the movie screen was blocked.\n\nQuestion: what's the cause for this?\n\nOptions: \nA. The couple behind me was whispering.\nB. A tall person was sitting in front of me.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely cause for a blocked view of the movie screen is a tall person sitting in front of you, as this physically obstructs the line of sight. Option A, whispering, might be annoying but does not block the view. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 162}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3242e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4460", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: The secretary put the caller on hold.\n\nQuestion: what's the effect of this?\n\nOptions: \nA. The caller's phone lost reception.\nB. The caller waited on the line.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The secretary putting the caller on hold means the caller was temporarily paused in the conversation and asked to wait. This action does not affect phone reception but requires the caller to stay on the line until the secretary returns. Therefore, the correct effect is that the caller waited on the line.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 159}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3087e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4461", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: The woman walked with crutches.\n\nQuestion: what's the cause for this?\n\nOptions: \nA. She shaved her legs.\nB. She broke her leg.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The woman likely uses crutches because of a physical injury that affects her ability to walk normally. Shaving her legs would not cause mobility issues, but breaking her leg would explain the need for crutches. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 140}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1332000000000001e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4463", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: The clock chimed.\n\nQuestion: what's the cause for this?\n\nOptions: \nA. It was the top of the hour.\nB. The hour seemed to drag on.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The chiming of a clock is typically a signal that marks the beginning of a new hour. Option A directly explains this common function of clocks, while Option B refers to a subjective feeling of time passing slowly, which does not cause a clock to chime. Therefore, the most likely cause is that it was the top of the hour.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 95, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 169}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4145e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4469", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: The man grew old.\n\nQuestion: what's the effect of this?\n\nOptions: \nA. His hair turned gray.\nB. He sold his belongings.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The natural effect of a man growing old is often visible in physical changes such as hair color. Gray hair is a common sign of aging, making it a direct consequence. Selling belongings is not inherently linked to aging in the same way.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 143}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1690000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4470", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: The friends decided to share the hamburger.\n\nQuestion: what's the effect of this?\n\nOptions: \nA. They cut the hamburger in half.\nB. They ordered fries with the hamburger.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely effect of the friends deciding to share the hamburger is that they divided it so each could eat part of it. Cutting the hamburger in half is a direct result of sharing. Ordering fries is unrelated to the act of sharing the hamburger.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 152}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2387e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4472", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: The pair of students came under scrutiny by the teacher.\n\nQuestion: what's the cause for this?\n\nOptions: \nA. The students both received excellent grades.\nB. Their responses on the assignment were identical.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely cause for the students coming under scrutiny is that their responses on the assignment were identical, which could suggest cheating or unauthorized collaboration. Identical responses raise suspicion, whereas excellent grades alone would not typically lead to scrutiny. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 153}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2370999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4474", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: The journalist wrote a biography about the humanitarian's life.\n\nQuestion: what's the cause for this?\n\nOptions: \nA. The humanitarian was difficult for the journalist to interview.\nB. The journalist was intrigued by the humanitarian's work.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The journalist writing a biography suggests a strong interest in the subject's life and achievements. Option B indicates that the journalist was intrigued by the humanitarian's work, which is a logical reason to write a biography. Option A implies difficulty in interviewing, which does not explain the cause for writing the biography.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 170}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3925999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4475", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: The man defied the authorities of the church.\n\nQuestion: what's the effect of this?\n\nOptions: \nA. He donated money to the church.\nB. He was excommunicated from the church.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Defying the authorities of the church typically results in disciplinary action, especially in historical or religious contexts. Excommunication is a common consequence for such defiance. Therefore, the most likely effect is that he was excommunicated.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 151}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2171e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4483", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: The boy threw a temper tantrum.\n\nQuestion: what's the cause for this?\n\nOptions: \nA. His brother took his toys from him.\nB. He shared his toys with his brother.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely cause of a temper tantrum is frustration or anger, often due to something being taken away or not getting one's way. Option A describes a situation that would likely provoke such a reaction, while Option B describes a positive behavior that would not typically lead to a tantrum. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 169}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4029e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4485", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: The boy skipped dinner.\n\nQuestion: what's the cause for this?\n\nOptions: \nA. His mother cooked his favorite meal.\nB. He ate a big lunch.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The boy skipped dinner, which suggests he was not hungry. Option B, \"He ate a big lunch,\" provides a logical reason for skipping dinner. Option A would likely encourage the boy to eat, not skip.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 93, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 142}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1503e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4499", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: The couple was happy to see each other.\n\nQuestion: what's the effect of this?\n\nOptions: \nA. They kissed.\nB. They rested.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context indicates the couple was happy to see each other, which suggests a positive and affectionate reaction. Among the options, kissing is a common expression of happiness and affection in such a situation. Resting does not directly relate to the emotion of happiness upon reunion.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 90, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 148}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2190000000000002e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4500", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: The woman asked the man to leave.\n\nQuestion: what's the cause for this?\n\nOptions: \nA. He insulted her.\nB. He thanked her.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The context indicates that the woman asked the man to leave, implying a negative interaction. Option A, \"He insulted her,\" provides a plausible reason for her wanting him to leave. Option B, \"He thanked her,\" is unlikely to result in such a request.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 151}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2431999999999999e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4503", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: The seasons changed from summer to autumn.\n\nQuestion: what's the effect of this?\n\nOptions: \nA. People evacuated their homes.\nB. Leaves fell from the trees.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The change from summer to autumn typically results in cooler temperatures and changes in foliage. One common effect is that leaves fall from deciduous trees as part of the seasonal cycle. This makes option B the most accurate.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 142}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1474e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4506", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: The lobbyist persuaded the legislature to support the bill.\n\nQuestion: what's the effect of this?\n\nOptions: \nA. The president vetoed the bill.\nB. The legislature passed the bill.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The lobbyist successfully persuaded the legislature to support the bill, which implies increased likelihood of legislative approval. Therefore, the most direct effect is that the legislature passed the bill. The president's veto is not indicated in the context.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 148}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1957999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4507", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: My closet was messy.\n\nQuestion: what's the effect of this?\n\nOptions: \nA. I organized it.\nB. I decorated it.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question asks for the effect of the closet being messy. A messy closet would more likely lead to organizing it rather than decorating it. Therefore, the most logical effect is that I organized it.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 88, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 133}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.0748e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4510", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Everyone in the class turned to stare at the student.\n\nQuestion: what's the cause for this?\n\nOptions: \nA. The student's phone rang.\nB. The student took notes.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely cause for everyone in the class turning to stare at the student is an unexpected or disruptive event. A ringing phone would draw sudden attention, while taking notes is a normal, unremarkable action. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 97, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 152}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2387e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4513", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: Political violence broke out in the nation.\n\nQuestion: what's the effect of this?\n\nOptions: \nA. Many citizens relocated to the capitol.\nB. Many citizens took refuge in other territories.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Political violence often leads people to flee affected areas in search of safety. Option B reflects this response, as citizens would likely seek refuge in safer, often neighboring or foreign, territories. Option A is less plausible, as relocating to the capital might not be safe during political unrest.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 161}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.3229e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4518", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: The woman contacted the real estate agent.\n\nQuestion: what's the cause for this?\n\nOptions: \nA. The woman planned to buy a condo.\nB. The woman needed to clean her house.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The woman likely contacted the real estate agent to discuss buying property, which aligns with planning to buy a condo. Option B, needing to clean her house, is unrelated to the services a real estate agent provides. Therefore, the most logical cause is A.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 157}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.2829e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4520", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: I lit the candle.\n\nQuestion: what's the effect of this?\n\nOptions: \nA. Wax dripped off the candle.\nB. The wax on the candle hardened.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Lighting a candle causes the wax to melt due to the heat of the flame, which often results in wax dripping down the side of the candle. Option A describes a common and immediate effect of lighting a candle. Option B, in contrast, describes a cooling process that would occur after the candle is extinguished, not while it is lit.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 169}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.4174e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4526", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: I tidied up my house.\n\nQuestion: what's the cause for this?\n\nOptions: \nA. I was swamped with work.\nB. I was expecting company.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The most likely cause for tidying up the house is preparing for visitors. Option B, \"I was expecting company,\" directly explains why someone would clean their house. Option A suggests being too busy, which makes cleaning less likely.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 94, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 146}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 1.1873999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_10005", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Britons are by far the biggest adopters of contactless payments in Europe as the use of the system continues to climb across the continent, new figures reveal. More than one billion contactless transactions worth \u20ac12.6billion took place in Europe over the last 12 months \u2013 a three-fold increase when compared to the same period in 2014, according to Visa Europe. Britain is the country with the highest number of contactless transactions, with 52.6million worth more than \u20ac330million made in March alone, followed by Poland and Czech Republic, with 49.7million and 13.9million transactions respectively. This rapid growth in the UK was fuelled in part by the launch of contactless payments on Transport for London services last September, Visa Europe said.\n@highlight\nThe UK issues the highest number of contactless cards\n@highlight\nBritons made 52.6million transactions worth more than \u20ac330million in March\n@highlight\nSome 1.1billion contactless transactions worth \u20ac12.6billion were made by Visa cardholders across Europe in the last 12 months\nQuery: Across the continent, 131million Visa contactless cards are carried in the pockets and purses of consumers, of which 49.6million are in the @placeholder.\n\nOptions : A. Poland\nB. Transport for London\nC. Britons\nD. Visa\nE. Czech Republic\nF. UK\nG. Visa Europe\nH. Britain\nI. Europe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{UK}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 367, "output_tokens": 5, "total_tokens": 372}, "provider": "Google", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:00:39.993322+00:00"}, "cost": 9.925e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_10013", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: In a world where computers are increasingly powerful and are concealed within ever more glossy slabs of aluminum, the Raspberry Pi (RPi) offers surprising proof for the virtue of moderation. Resembling little more than a credit card-sized scrap of exposed circuit board, the RPi is a fully programmable PC that runs a free, open-source Linux operating system, plugs into any TV, can power 3D graphics, connects to the Internet and, with a little ingenuity, be used to create your own personalized robot slave. The computer's miniature frame is crowded with two USB ports, an SD card slot, an Ethernet connection and microchip in the middle -- all powered by a universal USB mobile charger.\n@highlight\nThe Raspberry Pi is a credit-card sized computer that costs little more than a textbook\n@highlight\nOriginally designed to encourage school children to learn programming skills\n@highlight\nThe mini-PC now hugely popular with DIY geeks, who have used it to power their own creations\nQuery: It turned out there was a voracious appetite -- particularly among a growing class of @placeholder geeks -- for a cheap, easily-programmable, open-source piece of hardware that would allow them to let their imaginations run wild.\n\nOptions : A. Raspberry Pi\nB. Ethernet\nC. Internet\nD. USB\nE. Linux\nF. RPi\nG. DIY\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The passage directly states that the mini-PC \"now hugely popular with DIY geeks, who have used it to power their own creations.\" This matches the query's reference to a \"growing class of @placeholder geeks\" who embraced the device for open-ended, imaginative projects. Among the given options, only \"DIY\" completes the sentence in a way that is both factually accurate to the source text and semantically coherent.\n\n\\boxed{DIY}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 457, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 546}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00079375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_10093", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Despite complaints that Google Glass was too bulky and nerdy, rumours suggest the tech giant will release a new version with a larger prism display. The Enterprise Edition (EE) is also said to include an Intel Atom processor for improved performance and battery life. Some users of Glass, which was pulled in January following poor sales and mixed reviews, complained of eye strain after prolonged use. This may explain why Google might have decided to include a larger screen in its next design, 9to5Google reported. It\u2019s rumoured that final iterations of the EE include a prism that extends further, allowing wearers to glance upwards and focus on the screen more comfortably than before.\n@highlight\nRumours suggest Google will release a new version of Google Glass, dubbed the Enterprise Edition, with a larger prism display\n@highlight\nImproved screen could help to reduce eye strain for wearers\n@highlight\nSmart specs are also said to include an Intel Atom processor for improved performance and battery life compared to the previous version\n@highlight\nSome users of Glass, which was pulled in January following poor sales and mixed reviews, complained of eye strain after prolonged use\nQuery: The previous @placeholder headset was launched in a beta version under the firm's Explorer programme.\n\nOptions : A. Google\nB. Google Glass\nC. Intel Atom\nD. Smart\nE. Glass\nF. EE\nG. Enterprise Edition\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query requires identifying the referent for \"@placeholder\" in the given sentence. The passage introduces the original product by its full name (\"Google Glass\") and explicitly contrasts it with the rumoured new Enterprise Edition (EE). The Explorer programme was the beta launch vehicle for that original product.  \n\nSubstituting option B therefore yields the only grammatically and referentially coherent sentence:  \n\"The previous Google Glass headset was launched in a beta version under the firm's Explorer programme.\"  \n\nAll other options either produce redundancy, semantic mismatch, or an incomplete product name.\n\n\\boxed{Google Glass}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 463, "output_tokens": 113, "total_tokens": 576}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00086125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_10484", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: In the ancient Inca kingdom, the wheel was yet to be invented, iron was foreign and steel was unheard of. So when the Incas needed to travel across the Andes, they did so on handwoven rope bridges, stretched over gorges and rivers. Five hundred years later, just one of the Inca rope bridges remains: the Keshwa Chaca, which\u00a0spans the Apurimac River near Huinchiri, Peru, in the Province of Canas. Dangerous work: Local villagers work on renewing the Keshwa Chaca - the last Inca rope bridge - in the Andes near Huinchiri, Peru Incredible skill: The 90ft long Keshwa Chaca remains thanks to local villagers who rebuild the bridge each year using the same techniques as their Inca ancestors\n@highlight\nInca kingdom in the Andes was connected via handwoven rope bridges\n@highlight\nToday, only one bridge remains - the Keshwa Chaca near Huinchiri, Peru\n@highlight\nThe 90ft-long bridge is rebuilt by villagers over three days every June, before gradually\u00a0disintegrating\u00a0each time\n@highlight\nLocals use the same techniques to make the rope as their Inca ancestors\nQuery: The last @placeholder disappeared in the early 17th century, and over the years their bridges followed.\n\nOptions : A. Andes\nB. Inca\nC. Peru\nD. Incas\nE. Apurimac River\nF. Keshwa Chaca\nG. Huinchiri\nH. Canas\nI. Province\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query requires filling the placeholder in the sentence \"The last @placeholder disappeared in the early 17th century, and over the years their bridges followed.\"  \n\nThe passage describes the Inca kingdom and its rope-bridge network. After the Spanish conquest, Inca political authority ended (with the final resistance crushed by the early 17th century). Once the Incas themselves were gone as a ruling people, the bridges they had maintained gradually disappeared as well.  \n\nGrammatically, the possessive \"their\" is plural, matching the plural noun \"Incas\" rather than the singular \"Inca.\" None of the other listed options (geographic names, the single surviving bridge, etc.) can serve as the antecedent of \"their bridges.\"  \n\nThus the required word is exactly the option text \"Incas.\"\n\n\\boxed{Incas}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 501, "output_tokens": 165, "total_tokens": 666}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00103875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_10591", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Scientologists hold a 'blackmail file' on John Travolta to stop him leaving the faith, which includes 'damaging material' from his sessions with auditors at the church, it has been claimed. A documentary investigating the religion and its secret California-based headquarters features a number of allegations about how members are threatened and tortured in prison-style camps and cut off from their family if they decide to leave Scientology. Others belonging to the most senior order of the faith have been forced to play musical chairs to the sound of Queen's Bohemian Rhapsody in a fight to secure a chair to stay in the church, it was claimed.\n@highlight\nGoing Clear documentary claims to reveal secrets of Scientology religion\n@highlight\nIt alleges the church has a 'blackmail file' on John Travolta from auditing sessions and\u00a0members are thrown into 'The Hole' to confess their crimes and vie for places by playing musical chairs to Bohemian Rhapsody\n@highlight\nSylvia 'Spanky' Taylor, who once acted as the intermediary between the church and John Travolta, said people were punished with 30 hours labour\n@highlight\nScientologists rejected allegations saying they are from 'admitted liars'\nQuery: The documentary also claimed @placeholder chiefs hold a 'black PR package' on Travolta, with all the disclosures he made during auditing sessions.\n\nOptions : A. Queen\nB. California\nC. John Travolta\nD. Sylvia 'Spanky' Taylor\nE. Scientologists\nF. Clear\nG. The Hole\nH. Bohemian Rhapsody\nI. Scientology\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query requires filling the placeholder in the sentence \"The documentary also claimed @placeholder chiefs hold a 'black PR package' on Travolta...\" to produce a grammatically coherent and factually consistent statement drawn from the passage.  \n\nThe passage opens with the explicit claim that \"Scientologists hold a 'blackmail file'\" (also glossed as a \"black PR package\") containing Travolta's auditing disclosures. Among the listed options, only \"Scientology\" yields the well-formed noun phrase \"Scientology chiefs.\" The remaining options either produce ungrammatical strings (\"Queen chiefs,\" \"The Hole chiefs,\" etc.) or refer to entities that the passage never describes as holding such a file.  \n\nThus the single option that satisfies both syntactic and semantic constraints is Scientology.\n\n\\boxed{Scientology}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 506, "output_tokens": 160, "total_tokens": 666}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0010325, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_10724", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: In among all the pomp and ceremony surrounding the Apple Music launch, the firm has quietly killed off its Home Sharing feature, outraging many users. Before the iOS 8.4 update, Home Sharing let people share their iTunes music with other iOS devices on the same Wi-Fi network and was a favourite among families. But since Apple rolled out the software the feature has seemingly vanished and there has been no word as to why, leading to angry tweets and forum posts. The iOS 8.4 update was released to add the Apple Music app to phones and tablets. It also redesigned the music player and tweaked the iTunes Store.\n@highlight\nReports about the demise of Home Sharing appeared on Twitter this week\n@highlight\nAlthough Apple hasn't confirmed the change, it is likely to have been removed because it rivalled Apple's Family plan on Apple Music\n@highlight\nFor $14.99 a month, a family of six can share an Apple Music subscription\n@highlight\nThis is similar to what Home Sharing offered for free on any Wi-Fi network\nQuery: Many disgruntled users have also taken to the @placeholder support forums to complain about the changes.\n\nOptions : A. Wi\nB. iTunes Store\nC. Twitter\nD. Fi\nE. Home Sharing\nF. Apple Music\nG. Apple\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query requires identifying the missing term in the sentence \"Many disgruntled users have also taken to the @placeholder support forums to complain about the changes.\"  \n\nThe passage explicitly references \"angry tweets and forum posts\" in connection with user complaints about the removal of Home Sharing. It further highlights that reports appeared on Twitter, but the query's phrasing specifically uses the term \"support forums.\"  \n\nAmong the given options, only \"Apple\" produces a coherent, contextually accurate phrase (\"Apple support forums\") that aligns with the described user complaints. Other options either create nonsensical phrases (e.g., \"Twitter support forums\") or do not fit the sentence structure.  \n\nThus the correct option text is Apple.  \n\n\\boxed{Apple}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 517, "output_tokens": 810, "total_tokens": 1327}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:59.312048+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00267125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_11037", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Fast food giant Domino\u2019s is selling \u2018Frankenfood\u2019 pizzas to customers while claiming to be \u2018GM-free\u2019 on its website. It has emerged that their \u2018thin and crispy\u2019 pizza bases have been made using genetically modified soya bean oil and maize flour since February. Waitrose has also been selling imported American confectionery which contains GM sugar beet and a soya derivative and Marks & Spencer has been stocking American sauces and cookies containing GM soya and corn \u2013 even though the firm has previously boasted about not using GM ingredients. Fast food giant Domino\u2019s is selling \u2018Frankenfood\u2019 pizzas to customers while claiming to be \u2018GM-free\u2019 on its website\n@highlight\n'Thin and crispy' pizza bases made using GM soya bean oil and maize flour since February\n@highlight\nWaitrose selling imported US confectionery containing GM sugar beet and soya derivative\n@highlight\nMarks & Spencer has been stocking American sauces and cookies that contain GM soya and corn\n@highlight\nThe double-dealing has been identified by the campaign group GM Freeze\nQuery: And a Waitrose spokesman insisted that any GM ingredients in @placeholder chocolate stocked by the store were \u2018clearly labelled\u2019.\n\nOptions : A. US\nB. Thin\nC. Domino\nD. Domino\u2019s\nE. GM\nF. Waitrose\nG. Marks & Spencer\nH. Frankenfood\nI. American\nJ. GM Freeze\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query requires identifying the single word that best completes the given sentence as a factual reference to the supplied passage. The passage states that Waitrose sells \u201cimported American confectionery\u201d containing GM ingredients. Because confectionery includes chocolate, the adjective that directly modifies \u201cchocolate\u201d while preserving the passage\u2019s wording is \u201cAmerican.\u201d  \n\nNo other option satisfies both the syntactic slot (\u201c\u2026 chocolate\u201d) and the explicit lexical choice in the source text.  \n\nThus the correct option text is American.\n\n\\boxed{I. American}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 470, "output_tokens": 102, "total_tokens": 572}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0008425, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_11207", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) Selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors, known as SSRIs, are the most common type of antidepressants prescribed to pregnant women. Yet a new study indicates that when taken during pregnancy, the drugs are associated with a higher risk of language disorders, including dyslexia, in offspring. The children of women who took SSRIs while pregnant have a 37% greater risk of speech or language disorders compared with the children of depressed but unmedicated mothers, the researchers say. In practical terms, if a depressed mother did not take antidepressants, her child's risk of being diagnosed with a speech or language disorder would be about 1%, but if she took an SSRI, it would increase to 1.37%, explained Dr. Alan Brown, lead author of the study and a professor of psychiatry and epidemiology at Columbia University Medical Center.\n@highlight\nKids of pregnant women who took SSRIs have a higher risk of speech disorders, a study finds\n@highlight\n6% to 10% of pregnant women worldwide are exposed to antidepressants, author says\nQuery: The first \"exposure\" group included 15,596 mothers who purchased @placeholder once or more before or during pregnancy.\n\nOptions : A. Alan Brown\nB. Columbia University Medical Center\nC. SSRI\nD. SSRIs\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The passage discusses the risks associated with taking SSRIs (a class of antidepressants) during pregnancy. The query sentence describes a study cohort of mothers who purchased medication, which aligns directly with the drug class referenced throughout the passage (SSRIs).  \n\nOptions A and B can be ruled out immediately, as neither refers to a purchasable medication. Between the remaining choices, the plural form SSRIs is the only one that fits the sentence grammatically and contextually (\u201cpurchased SSRIs once or more\u201d).  \n\nThus the placeholder is filled by the text of option D.\n\n\\boxed{SSRIs}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 441, "output_tokens": 118, "total_tokens": 559}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00084625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_11394", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Good news has arrived for stranded holidaymakers after Virgin Australia and Jetstar officially announced that conditions were safe to resume flights to and from Bali. Earlier on Saturday, Indonesian officials declared Denpasar Airport safe to reopen as the cloud of ash from the eruption of Mount Raung drifted away. Virgin sent an observation flight to the airport to have visual confirmation and determine whether conditions were suitable for flights to operate before giving the all-clear. The airline said scheduled flights out of Denpasar would go ahead on Saturday evening and it plans to continue operations in and out of the Indonesian island on Sunday.\n@highlight\nVirgin Australia and Jetstar has confirmed it is able to resume flights\n@highlight\nThey announced the conditions were safe to operate to and from Bali\n@highlight\nStrong winds  pushed the ash cloud away from the airport on Saturday\n@highlight\nAn eruption from\u00a0Mount Raung caused the large ash cloud to form\n@highlight\nThe cloud caused visibility issue and can effect engine electronics\n@highlight\nIt caused thousands of Australians to be stranded at Denpasar airport\nQuery: The ash grounded planes from Virgin, @placeholder, Garuda and AirAsia on Friday.\n\nOptions : A. Mount Raung\nB. Denpasar\nC. Virgin Australia\nD. Bali\nE. Virgin\nF. Australians\nG. Indonesian\nH. Jetstar\nI. Denpasar Airport\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "H. Jetstar\n\n\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 344, "output_tokens": 11, "total_tokens": 355}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.5524e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_11554", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Apple's latest tablet comes in a smaller, pocketable, gripable, adorable new travel size. But the iPad Mini is more than just a smaller face -- it's a whole new product with its own killer features and disappointments. Joining the iPhone and 10-inch iPad in Apple's iOS lineup, the 7.8-inch iPad enters a crowded market of 7-inch tablets. Here's a closer look at the Mini and how it stacks up against its competitors. The body Applying the patented Apple shrink-ray wasn't the only change to the iPad body. The unibody shell is smooth and rounded on the back and edges -- more so than the 10-inch iPad. The lack of sharp edges makes it more confortable to hold in your hands.\n@highlight\nThe iPad Mini hits the spot with its perfectly portable size, but the price tag is high\n@highlight\nBuyers could be disappointed by the lack of a retina display on the Mini\n@highlight\niPad Mini is great for consuming content, but 10-inch iPad is still best as a PC replacement\nQuery: The choice between @placeholder products largely depends on what you're going to use the device for.\n\nOptions : A. PC\nB. iPhone\nC. Mini\nD. iPad Mini\nE. iOS\nF. iPad\nG. Apple\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The passage concludes by contrasting the iPad Mini (ideal for media consumption) with the larger 10-inch iPad (better suited as a PC replacement). This directly supports the query sentence, which refers to a choice between those two specific products.  \n\nThe matching text drawn from the supplied options is therefore \u201ciPad Mini and iPad.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{iPad Mini and iPad}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 457, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 534}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00076375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_11580", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: The EU's migration chief has urged European leaders to stop thinking about whether accepting refugees into their country will affect the next election. Dimitris Avramopoulos hinted that EU heads of state is letting their worry about how their actions in response to the migration crisis will be seen by voters cloud their humanitarian judgement. The 62-year-old said EU leaders should think more like the Commission, which does not need to be re-elected and therefore does not take into account how their actions might change public opinion. Avramopoulois is European Commissioner for Migration, Home Affairs and Citizenship and has served as both Defence and Foreign Minister in Greece as well as Mayor of Athens.\n@highlight\nDimitris Avramopoulos said EU leaders must stop thinking of next election\n@highlight\nEU Migration chief said to stop thinking about 'political cost' of refugees\n@highlight\nSaid reason for delay in action on crisis was that EU was taken by surprise\nQuery: 'The @placeholder is here for five years to do its job and we did it with vision, responsibility and commitment.\n\nOptions : A. Greece\nB. EU Migration\nC. Said\nD. EU\nE. Dimitris Avramopoulos\nF. Commission\nG. Citizenship\nH. European\nI. Athens\nJ. Avramopoulois\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query requires identifying the word or phrase that logically fills the blank in the given sentence. The passage explicitly contrasts EU leaders (who must face re-election) with the Commission (whose members serve fixed five-year terms and therefore need not factor electoral consequences into their decisions).  \n\nThe sentence supplied in the query directly echoes this contrast: it refers to an entity that \u201cis here for five years to do its job,\u201d which matches the Commission\u2019s mandate. Among the listed options, only \u201cCommission\u201d satisfies both the semantic content of the passage and the syntactic requirements of the blank.  \n\nThus the correct choice is Commission.\n\n\\boxed{Commission}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 448, "output_tokens": 127, "total_tokens": 575}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0008775, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_11586", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) For several weeks now, city and state officials have traded barbs over who is ultimately responsible for the toxic water that's inundated Flint, Michigan. On Thursday, the feds said they both are. In an emergency administrative order, the Environmental Protection Agency slammed the city of Flint, the Michigan Department of Environmental Quality and the State of Michigan, saying they are all responsible for the lead contamination in the city's water. Their responses to the crisis, the EPA said, were \"inadequate to protect public health.\" EPA administrator resigns \"There are serious, ongoing concerns with delays, lack of adequate transparency, and capacity to safely manage the drinking water system,\" the agency said in a press release.\n@highlight\nThe EPA says the city of Flint and the state of Michigan are among those responsible for the water crisis\n@highlight\nThe agency's regional administrator who oversees Flint has resigned\n@highlight\nCongress may hold a hearing on the incident\nQuery: The emergency order also means the EPA will start doing its own lead testing in @placeholder's water system.\n\nOptions : A. Michigan\nB. EPA\nC. Michigan Department of Environmental Quality\nD. State of Michigan\nE. Flint\nF. Congress\nG. Environmental Protection Agency\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The passage centers on the Flint water crisis and the EPA's emergency order, which assigns responsibility for lead contamination specifically to the city's water system (along with state-level agencies). The query sentence refers to the EPA beginning its own testing in that same water system, so the placeholder must be filled by the city in question.\n\nThis eliminates all other options, which refer to agencies or entities that are not the direct location of the affected water system.\n\n\\boxed{Flint}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 495, "output_tokens": 584, "total_tokens": 1079}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:35:57.999209+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00207875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_11849", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Airlines have been forced to cancel another day of flights to Denpasar as volcanic ash continues to make its way over Bali's airspace. By 1pm, Jetstar had announced all of Thursday's flights to the holiday island had been stopped, assuring it would resume them as soon as the Volcanic Ash Advisory Centre deemed it safe to do so. Virgin has meanwhile cancelled all flights bound for Bali from Australia for both Thursday and Friday. The carrier said it would make a decision about resuming the flights headed to Australia from Denpasar midday Friday. 'Unfavourable winds have pushed the ash cloud close to Denpasar Airport over the last day and we're not satisfied it is safe to operate services in these conditions,' a statement from Jetstar said.\n@highlight\nJetstar has called off all of Thursday's flights to the holiday island\n@highlight\nVirgin has  cancelled all flights bound for Bali  for both Thursday and Friday\n@highlight\nThey will\u00a0resume flights when Volcanic Ash Advisory Centre deems it safe\n@highlight\nIt comes as winds bring ash from the Mount Raung volcano over Denpasar\nQuery: Jestar customers have been urged to check the status of their flight on Jetstar.com before travelling to airports while @placeholder is directing passengers to change their booking to another flight, which can be made at no extra charge in the next 14 days unless they prefer a full travel credit.\n\nOptions : A. Mount Raung\nB. Denpasar\nC. Australia\nD. Bali\nE. Virgin\nF. Jetstar\nG. Volcanic Ash Advisory Centre\nH. Denpasar Airport\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "E. Virgin\n\n\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 401, "output_tokens": 9, "total_tokens": 410}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.9370999999999994e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_11915", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Jenson Button's miserable Formula One season continued in Bahrain after he failed to start the Bahrain Grand Prix. The British driver was set to start from the back of the grid after he broke down in qualifying. But despite frantic work from his McLaren team to get his car ready in time for the race in Sakhir, Button was forced to watch from the sidelines. Jenson Button (left) waves to fans during the drivers parade before the start of the Bahrain Grand Prix 'The engine is not broken,' said McLaren chairman Ron Dennis. 'What we have is the data in the Energy Recovery System is not clean and the chances of it failing are quite high so it is probably best not to run it.'\n@highlight\nJenson Button was set to start from the back of the grid after mechanical\u00a0 failure in\u00a0qualifying\n@highlight\nDespite frantic work from McLaren mechanics, they were unable to get his car on to the grid leaving Button to watch from the sidelines\n@highlight\nIt was only the third race of the last 272 staged that he has missed\nQuery: Button jumps out of his McLaren\u00a0after failing to complete the qualifying session in @placeholder\n\nOptions : A. Sakhir\nB. Energy Recovery System\nC. Bahrain\nD. Bahrain Grand Prix\nE. Jenson Button\nF. Formula One\nG. Button\nH. McLaren\nI. Ron Dennis\nJ. Grand Prix\nK. British\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query requires filling the placeholder in a sentence describing the location of Button's failed qualifying session. The passage states that Button broke down during qualifying for the race in Sakhir (the specific circuit hosting the Bahrain Grand Prix).  \n\nThis matches option A directly, as Sakhir is the only location explicitly tied to the on-track activity. Bahrain (option C) refers only to the broader country/GP name and is therefore less precise for the required slot. All remaining options are either people, teams, or non-location entities and cannot grammatically or semantically complete the phrase \"in @placeholder.\"\n\n\\boxed{A. Sakhir}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 477, "output_tokens": 124, "total_tokens": 601}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00090625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_11950", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (ArsTechnica) -- The Federal Communications Commission is releasing the details of its new net neutrality Order in stages. Although the FCC's new ban on \"unreasonable discrimination\" for wired ISPs allows certain kinds of traffic discrimination (not all bits need be equal), the agency made clear after Tuesday's meeting that \"paid prioritization\" deals with Internet companies are unlikely to be allowed. Critics had worried that the new Order would only affect outright website blocking, leaving paid prioritization untouched (or even implicitly sanctioned). \"Pay for Priority Unlikely to Satisfy 'No Unreasonable Discrimination' Rule,\" advises one subheading of the new net neutrality rules. Ed Whitacre's dream of directly charging Google and Yahoo to \"use his pipes\" -- a key event in starting the entire net neutrality debate -- appears to be dashed.\n@highlight\nThe FCC's new rules forbid Internet providers from blocking lawful content\n@highlight\nCritics worried that the new Order would leave paid prioritization untouched\n@highlight\nFCC: Reasonable network management shall not constitute unreasonable discrimination\nQuery: \"Even open Internet skeptics acknowledge that pay for priority may disadvantage non-commercial uses of the network, which are typically less able to pay for priority, and for which the @placeholder is a uniquely important platform.\"\n\nOptions : A. Google\nB. Internet\nC. ISPs\nD. Yahoo\nE. new Order\nF. Ed Whitacre\nG. FCC\nH. Unreasonable Discrimination' Rule\nI. ArsTechnica\nJ. Federal Communications Commission\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 373, "output_tokens": 6, "total_tokens": 379}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.7082999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_12028", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Banish the tumour and cure the disease. That\u2019s what a Delhi-based think-tank close to the RSS is set to do by posing a serious legal challenge to Kashmir\u2019s \u2018special\u2019 provisions. The Delhi-based Jammu and Kashmir Study Centre (JKSC) is gearing up to target Article 35A, an outgrowth powered by Article 370 of the Constitution, which gives J&K special status. Article 35A allows the state to grant special privileges and rights to its permanent residents, and not to others living there, the think-tank says. To scrap these special provisions, the Jammu and Kashmir Study Centre (JKSC) has decided to approach the Supreme Court. On July 11, the organisation will formally announce at a seminar in Delhi the date for filing the petition.\n@highlight\nThe Jammu and Kashmir Study Centre, based in Delhi, is challenging Article 35A\n@highlight\nThe amendment is powered by Article 370 of the Constitution, which gives J&K special status\n@highlight\nIt lets the state grant privileges and rights to permanent residents, but not others\nQuery: RSS national executive member Arun Kumar is one of the advisers with the petitioner @placeholder.\n\nOptions : A. Jammu and Kashmir Study Centre\nB. JKSC\nC. Article 370\nD. RSS\nE. J&K\nF. Supreme Court\nG. Delhi\nH. Constitution\nI. Article 35A\nJ. Kashmir\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The passage identifies the Delhi-based Jammu and Kashmir Study Centre (JKSC) as the organization preparing to file a petition in the Supreme Court to challenge Article 35A. This organization is therefore the petitioner referenced in the query.  \n\nThe query\u2019s placeholder must be filled by the name of that petitioner. Among the listed options, only \u201cJammu and Kashmir Study Centre\u201d matches the entity described in the passage as the actor filing the petition.  \n\n(The abbreviated form JKSC is also used in the passage, but the full name is the primary designation given when the organization is introduced and is therefore the most direct match for the placeholder.)\n\n\\boxed{Jammu and Kashmir Study Centre}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 475, "output_tokens": 135, "total_tokens": 610}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00093125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_12136", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: George Osborne should spread austerity over a longer period than currently planned to avoid damaging the economy, a leading global watchdog has claimed. The Chancellor looks set to use next month's Budget - the first since the Tories' dramatic election victory last month - to outline plans to balance the books by 2018-19. But the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development suggested that the cuts required in 2016 and 2017 to return Britain to the black may be too harsh. The OECD urged the government to even out austerity over a longer period to 'lower its impact on growth'. Despite the warning, the Paris based think-tank said it again expects Britain to be the fastest growing major economy in the world this year.\n@highlight\nOsborne planning to balance the books by 2018-19 with deep cuts\n@highlight\nOECD warns the spending cuts should be spread over a longer period\n@highlight\nDowngrades\u00a0UK growth to 2.4% \u00a0but still stronger than the rest of the G7\nQuery: 'The Chancellor should heed the @placeholder's warnings that 'continued weak productivity' could lead to 'a higher-than-expected budget deficit'.\n\nOptions : A. Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development\nB. George Osborne\nC. Budget\nD. Downgrades\u00a0UK\nE. Tories\nF. OECD\nG. Britain\nH. Paris\nI. Osborne\nJ. G7\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The passage identifies the source of the austerity warning as the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development (subsequently abbreviated OECD). The query\u2019s placeholder refers to the same entity issuing an additional warning on productivity and the deficit; therefore the concise, conventional label used throughout the text is OECD.\n\n\\boxed{OECD}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 534, "output_tokens": 1051, "total_tokens": 1585}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:36:02.040744+00:00"}, "cost": 0.003295, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_12184", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: The identity of the kissing couple immortalized in the throes of passions in Times Square on VJ Day, 1945 has been thrown into doubt after a new scientific theory disproved all existing accounts. More than a dozen people claimed to be either the the sailor or the nurse shown passionately embracing as the news broke of the end of the Second World War after Japan's surrender. But according to a team of astronomers, none of their accounts can be true. The scientists say they have managed to pinpoint the time of the shot by analyzing the shadows in the image - and their result does not match any of the stories put forward.\n@highlight\nSailor and a nurse were immortalized in photograph from August 14, 1945\n@highlight\nWas published in Life magazine - but photographer didn't get their names\n@highlight\nMore than a dozen people have claimed they were in the image\n@highlight\nScientists have now debunked some stories via astronomy\n@highlight\nSay they have pinned time of image to 5:51pm - which does not match any leading stories\nQuery: He remembers tearing through @placeholder kissing everyone in sight from sheer excitement.\n\nOptions : A. Second World War\nB. Japan\nC. Life\nD. Sailor\nE. Times Square\nF. VJ Day\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{Times Square}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 330, "output_tokens": 6, "total_tokens": 336}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:00:52.098347+00:00"}, "cost": 9.15e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_12215", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: George Osborne today refused to match Labour's pledge not to increase VAT as a row erupted over how to balance the books after the election. The Chancellor declined to give a 'cast-iron guarantee'\u00a0to match Labour's pledge not to increase VAT over the five years of the next Parliament. It came after Labour's shadow chancellor Ed Balls that Conservatives had a history of raising VAT after elections despite saying they had no plans to do so during the campaign. Scroll down for video Chancellor George Osborne declined to give a 'cast-iron guarantee' to match Labour's pledge not to increase VAT from 20 per cent over the five years of the next Parliament\n@highlight\nLabour's Ed Balls unveils poster warning Tories will hike VAT again\n@highlight\nOsborne used first Budget in 2010 to increase rate from 17.5% to 20%\n@highlight\nChancellor insists his plans to balance books do not require new increase\n@highlight\nBut he\u00a0repeatedly\u00a0refused to match Labour's promise ahead of election\nQuery: Mr Balls claimed the @placeholder 'have a secret plan to raise VAT again'\n\nOptions : A. George Osborne\nB. Budget\nC. Ed Balls\nD. Tories\nE. Parliament\nF. Osborne\nG. Labour\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 326, "output_tokens": 5, "total_tokens": 331}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.3645999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_12315", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: NASA has given the people of Earth a rare treat: A color mosaic that captures not only Saturn, but also the tiny dots of Earth and other planets in the background. The panorama, released Tuesday, was captured by the Cassini spacecraft on July 19, when the sun slipped behind the ringed planet. Earth appears as a bright blue dot to Saturn's lower right, just above Saturn's outer, halo-like E-ring. Venus is a dot to the upper left, with Mars appearing as a faint red dot above and to the left of Venus. This is the first image in which Saturn, its moons and rings, and Earth, Venus and Mars are all visible, NASA said. The image -- a panorama of 141 wide-angle pictures -- covers 404,880 miles across Saturn and its ring system.\n@highlight\nImage is Cassini's first showing Saturn, rings, moons, Earth, Venus and Mars at same time\n@highlight\nThe collage is panorama of 141 wide-angle pictures taken July 19\n@highlight\nImage was possible that day because Saturn obstructed spacecraft's view of sun\nQuery: Cassini images showing both Saturn and Earth are rare because the sun is so close to Earth, that targeting the blue planet would damage @placeholder's sensors, NASA says.\n\nOptions : A. Saturn\nB. Venus\nC. Cassini\nD. Earth\nE. NASA\nF. Cassini spacecraft\nG. Mars\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query describes why Cassini rarely images both Saturn and Earth together. From Saturn's vantage point, Earth lies very close to the Sun in the sky; therefore any camera pointing that includes Earth would also point almost directly at the Sun. Prolonged exposure to direct sunlight would overheat or permanently damage the spacecraft's sensitive imaging instruments.  \n\nThe only entity whose sensors are at risk is the spacecraft itself. Among the listed options, \u201cCassini\u201d is the concise, conventional name for that spacecraft and produces the grammatically natural phrase \u201cCassini\u2019s sensors.\u201d All other choices (Saturn, Venus, Earth, NASA, Mars, or the longer \u201cCassini spacecraft\u201d) are either celestial bodies, organizations, or stylistically redundant.\n\nThus the completed sentence reads:  \n\u201cCassini images showing both Saturn and Earth are rare because the sun is so close to Earth that targeting the blue planet would damage Cassini\u2019s sensors, NASA says.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{C. Cassini}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 473, "output_tokens": 193, "total_tokens": 666}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00107375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_12352", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) -- The small, black-and-white newspaper ad offered a discount: Nine holes of golf for $9.11 -- on September 11. The management of a Wisconsin golf course said the idea was to remember the victims of the September 11, 2001, attacks, but the ad turned into a public relations disaster on social media. By Tuesday, TumbleDown Trails Golf Course was reporting death threats. The golf course in Verona, Wisconsin, placed an advertisement in Monday's Wisconsin State Journal offering to \"commemorate\" the 12th anniversary of the terror attacks with \"9 holes with cart for only $9.11 per person or 18 holes with cart for only $19.11!\"\n@highlight\nSocial media erupts after course offers discount to \"commemorate\" terror attacks\n@highlight\nOffer: $9.11 for nine holes, $19.11 for 18 holes\n@highlight\nManagement apologizes on Facebook, reports death threats\n@highlight\nCourse may be closed on Wednesday due to security concerns\nQuery: By Tuesday afternoon, many @placeholder commenters were defending the course.\n\nOptions : A. Wisconsin\nB. Facebook\nC. Verona\nD. CNN\nE. Wisconsin State Journal\nF. TumbleDown Trails Golf Course\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The passage describes a public relations crisis that played out on social media after the golf course placed its advertisement. One of the bullet-point highlights explicitly states that management \u201capologizes on Facebook,\u201d indicating that the platform where public reaction (both negative and defensive) occurred was Facebook.  \n\nThe sentence to be completed therefore reads naturally as \u201cmany Facebook commenters were defending the course,\u201d making \u201cFacebook\u201d the only option that fits the context supplied by the passage.\n\n\\boxed{Facebook}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 444, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 539}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0007925, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_12469", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: At the end of last year Apple overtook sales of Android devices for the first time since 2012. And in a bid to fuel this trend further, the Californian tech giant is reportedly planning to extend its\u00a0recycling\u00a0and trade-in scheme to include rival handsets. Reports claim Android, as well as BlackBerry and potentially Windows Phone customers, will be able to exchange their handsets for gift cards and credit towards Apple products. Apple is reportedly planning to extend the recycling and trade-in scheme it launched in 2013 (pictured) to include rival handsets. Reports claim Android, as well as BlackBerry and potentially Windows Phone customers, will be able to exchange their handsets for gift cards and credit towards an Apple product\n@highlight\nApple launched its iPhone Reuse and Recycle trade-in scheme in 2013\n@highlight\nIt gives Apple credit to put towards the purchase of a new device\n@highlight\nSources said Apple will soon accept non-iOS devices on this program\n@highlight\nThis includes Android, Windows Phone and BlackBerry handsets\n@highlight\nEmployees are being trained in the changes now and the scheme is expected to launch 'in the coming weeks'\nQuery: The amount of credit depends on the device and its condition, and its likely that figures for Android handsets, which are typically much cheaper than @placeholder phones, will be low under the scheme.\n\nOptions : A. Android\nB. Windows Phone\nC. Californian\nD. BlackBerry\nE. Recycle\nF. iPhone Reuse\nG. non-iOS\nH. Apple\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query sentence discusses relative pricing of handsets in the context of Apple's trade-in program. Android devices are described as typically lower-cost than the premium devices being traded in for Apple credit.  \n\nThe only option that produces a coherent, factually accurate completion is therefore \"Apple\" (i.e., \"much cheaper than Apple phones\"). All other choices either repeat the subject of the clause, name rival platforms, or insert irrelevant program titles.\n\n\\boxed{H. Apple}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 504, "output_tokens": 93, "total_tokens": 597}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.0008625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_12613", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: It's the social and health crisis plaguing almost one million Japanese people. The sufferers of 'Hikikomori' \u2013 mostly young men - have such severe social withdrawal they isolate themselves in their bedroom, in some cases for years. One of the few hikikomori experts in Japan, Dr Takahiro Kato, suffered from the condition as a student and is now working to prevent it from having a widespread affect on the next generation. Dr Kato, who is studying hikikomori with a team of experts at Kyushu University in Fukuoka, said he had seen cases so severe that some men in their 50s had been withdrawn from society for more than 30 years.\n@highlight\n'Hikikomori' is a social and health crisis affect almost one million Japanese\n@highlight\nSufferers have such severe social withdrawal they isolate themselves in their bedroom, in some cases for years\n@highlight\nDoctors are working to stop it having a major affect on the next generation\nQuery: 'It\u2019s one reason why @placeholder have many more hikikomori compared to western society.'\n\nOptions : A. Hikikomori\nB. Sufferers\nC. Japan\nD. Kato\nE. Kyushu University\nF. Fukuoka\nG. Japanese\nH. Takahiro Kato\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query requires filling @placeholder in the sentence \"It\u2019s one reason why @placeholder have many more hikikomori compared to western society.\"  \n\nThe passage establishes that hikikomori is a phenomenon concentrated in Japan (affecting ~1 million Japanese people) and contrasts it implicitly with other societies. Among the given options, only \"Japanese\" produces a grammatically well-formed sentence that matches this meaning: \"why Japanese have many more hikikomori \u2026\".  \n\nAll other candidates are either singular (\"Japan,\" \"Kato,\" etc.) and would require \"has,\" or are semantically incoherent in the slot.  \n\nThus the correct option text is Japanese.\n\n\\boxed{Japanese}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 447, "output_tokens": 135, "total_tokens": 582}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00089625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_12894", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Microsoft's Windows 10 software has only been available in its final form for a few hours - but experts have already warned of a major security risk in the software. The feature is designed to easily let people share wifi passwords with friends. However, experts say the feature actually automatically shares your wifi passwords with all Outlook, Skype and Facebook contacts who also use Windows 10. To change your settings, go to Network settings then Manage Wi-Fi settings (Settings > Network & Internet > Wi-Fi > Manage Wi-Fi Settings). There, you can choose which contacts you share Wi-Fi settings with.\n@highlight\nFeature designed to easily let people share wifi passwords with friends.\n@highlight\nExperts say the feature is 'an accident waiting to happen'\nQuery: 'In practice \u2013 @placeholder have, somewhere, an enormous database full of people's passwords.\n\nOptions : A. Windows 10\nB. Facebook\nC. Wi\nD. Skype\nE. Microsoft\nF. Fi\nG. Fi Settings\nH. Outlook\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "E. Microsoft\n\n\\boxed{E. Microsoft}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 269, "output_tokens": 12, "total_tokens": 281}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.0298999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_13086", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) The long awaited La Ni\u00f1a, which was first predicted by the Climate Prediction Center (CPC) back in April, has finally arrived in the Pacific Ocean, NOAA announced Thursday -- and it's expected to stick around through the winter. La Ni\u00f1a conditions, which are characterized by below-normal sea surface temperatures in the tropical Pacific, were observed during October and have persisted into November -- prompting the CPC to raise the ENSO Alert System from a La Ni\u00f1a Watch to a La Ni\u00f1a Advisory. La Ni\u00f1a, much like its warmer counterpart, El Ni\u00f1o, have far reaching global impacts extending beyond the Pacific Ocean.\n@highlight\nLa Ni\u00f1a is characterized by a cooling of ocean waters in the Pacific\n@highlight\nThe climate pattern is likely to worsen drought in the southeastern US\nQuery: It will be interesting to see if this @placeholder can slow down the rapidly rising global temperatures and prevent 2016 from outpacing 2015 and becoming the third consecutive hottest year for the planet.\n\nOptions : A. US\nB. NOAA\nC. Climate Prediction Center\nD. La Ni\u00f1a\nE. El Ni\u00f1o\nF. Pacific\nG. ENSO Alert System\nH. CPC\nI. La Ni\u00f1a Advisory\nJ. Pacific Ocean\nK. La Ni\u00f1a Watch\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The passage describes the arrival of La Ni\u00f1a and explicitly notes that it is defined by cooling sea-surface temperatures in the tropical Pacific. Because the placeholder refers to a phenomenon that could plausibly counteract rising global temperatures, the only entity among the listed options that produces a cooling effect is La Ni\u00f1a. All other candidates are either organizations (NOAA, CPC), monitoring systems (ENSO Alert System), or the opposing warm phase (El Ni\u00f1o), none of which would slow planetary warming.\n\nThus the placeholder is filled by the text of option D.\n\n\\boxed{La Ni\u00f1a}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 445, "output_tokens": 114, "total_tokens": 559}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00084125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_13287", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) The Force was with Los Angeles. The board of directors for the Lucas Museum of Narrative Art announced Tuesday that the City of Angels will be the site for the $1 billion facility that will house George Lucas' personal art collection. The city's Exposition Park will be the home of the futuristic building, which is sure to be a draw for \"Star Wars\" fans and architecture geeks alike. Los Angeles beat out San Francisco for the site. In a statement, the board said, \"Settling on a location proved to be an extremely difficult decision precisely because of the desirability of both sites and cities.\"\n@highlight\nChicago was the original site for the Lucas Museum of Narrative Art\n@highlight\nFilmmaker George Lucas has a trove of art and \"Star Wars\" memorabilia\nQuery: @placeholder is a magnet for the region and accessible from all parts of the city.\n\nOptions : A. Exposition Park\nB. City of Angels\nC. San Francisco\nD. Star Wars\nE. Lucas Museum of Narrative Art\nF. George Lucas\nG. Force\nH. Chicago\nI. Los Angeles\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "A. Exposition Park\n\n\\boxed{A. Exposition Park}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 295, "output_tokens": 16, "total_tokens": 311}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.2545e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_13409", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: A group of Belgian holidaymakers who were heading to the French Alps for a few days of skiing wound up being taken on a major detour thanks to their coach driver\u2019s sat-nav mistake. The driver wasn\u2019t familiar with the route to La Plagne, a popular destination for ski tourists, and mistakenly drove the tour group to the South of France after selecting the wrong destination on his GPS. Instead of entering La Plagne into his sat-nav, the driver entered Plagne, located in the French Pyrenees, putting the group of 50 holidaymakers on a nearly 800-mile detour, Belgian media reported. The tourists were travelling to La Plagne in the French Alps, but were driven towards the South of France\n@highlight\nGroup of 50 holidaymakers were travelling to La Plagne in the French Alps\n@highlight\nTheir coach driver selected Plagne, in the French Pyrenees, as destination\n@highlight\nThe driver turned around in Toulouse after realising his error\n@highlight\nTour group arrived at La Plagne nearly 24 hours behind schedule\nQuery: By the time the driver realised his mistake the group was already in Toulouse, nearly 425 miles south-west of @placeholder.\n\nOptions : A. French\nB. Alps\nC. French Pyrenees\nD. Toulouse\nE. Plagne\nF. La Plagne\nG. French Alps\nH. Belgian\nI. South of France\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query requires identifying the location of which Toulouse is described as being nearly 425 miles to the southwest.  \n\nThe passage states that the intended destination was La Plagne (in the French Alps) and that the driver realized the error only after reaching Toulouse. Geographically, Toulouse lies well to the southwest of La Plagne; the 425-mile figure is therefore the distance between those two points.  \n\nNo other option satisfies the directional and factual constraints of the sentence:  \n- \u201cFrench Alps\u201d or \u201cFrench Pyrenees\u201d are regions, not the specific destination referenced.  \n- \u201cPlagne\u201d is the erroneous destination the driver actually entered.  \n- The remaining choices are either too vague or refer to places that do not lie northeast of Toulouse.  \n\nHence the placeholder must be filled by \u201cLa Plagne.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{F. La Plagne}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 471, "output_tokens": 172, "total_tokens": 643}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00101875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_13469", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: A solar system including five Earth-sized planets has been discovered which is so ancient it was born not long after the dawn of time - and experts say it could help find life on planets far older than we expected. The system's parent star, named Kepler-444, is 117 light years from Earth and 11.2 billion years old. When the sun-like star was formed out of a primordial cloud of gas and dust, the universe was just a fifth of its current age. Astronomers made the discovery after trawling through four years' worth of data collected by Nasa's Kepler space telescope.\n@highlight\nSolar system's parent star, named Kepler-444, is 117 light years from Earth\n@highlight\n11.2 billion-year-old star formed when the universe was a fifth of its age\n@highlight\nFive Earth-sized planets orbit the star with years equivalent to 10 days\n@highlight\nFind shows Earth-sized planets have formed throughout universe's history\nQuery: However, the chances of an advanced race of beings living on any of the planets are remote, despite @placeholder being\u00a025 per cent smaller and 700 degrees cooler than the sun.\n\nOptions : A. Kepler\nB. Nasa\nC. Astronomers\nD. Solar\nE. Earth\nF. Five Earth\nG. Kepler-444\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The sentence requires a subject that can be directly compared to the Sun in terms of size and temperature. The passage identifies the parent star of the system as Kepler-444 and explicitly describes it as \u201csun-like,\u201d establishing the necessary contrast. Substituting any of the other listed entities (Kepler, Nasa, Astronomers, Solar, Earth, or Five Earth) yields a grammatically or semantically incoherent statement. Consequently, the placeholder is filled by the star\u2019s proper name.\n\n\\boxed{Kepler-444}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 451, "output_tokens": 102, "total_tokens": 553}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00081875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_13747", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) \"Yessssss!\" was my reaction to hearing the news that the U.S. Food and Drug Administration intends to regulate e-cigarettes, hookahs, vape pens, e-pipes and other electronic nicotine delivery products. As a family physician, I often have patients ask me about e-cigarettes. Some have seen advertisements and are wondering what they are; some have simply heard that e-cigarettes are safer than traditional cigarettes and want to know if this is true. E-cigarettes are included in the category of ENDS -- Electronic Nicotine Delivery Systems -- products that use a liquid containing nicotine and varying amounts of flavor, glycerin, propylene glycol and other ingredients. This liquid is heated into an aerosol that users then smoke. It is often referred to as \"vaping.\"\n@highlight\nJennifer Caudle says FDA regulation of electronic nicotine delivery systems is overdue\n@highlight\nMore research needed on long-term effects, especially as youth use skyrockets, she says\nQuery: The effect of e-cigarettes and @placeholder on children is also an issue -- especially given the growth of e-cigarette use among teens in recent years.\n\nOptions : A. Yessssss!\nB. Electronic Nicotine Delivery Systems\nC. FDA\nD. Jennifer Caudle\nE. CNN\nF. U.S. Food and Drug Administration\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 335, "output_tokens": 6, "total_tokens": 341}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.4384999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_13776", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) World leaders touch down in the Chinese city of Hangzhou this week for the G20 summit and Beijing is determined it will proceed without a hitch. Factories are shuttered, skies are clear and security is tight. Local residents have been given seven days extra vacation time and discounted tours to destinations outside the city to ensure Hangzhou is free of crowds and traffic. Meanwhile, thousands of migrant workers have left the city due to the halt in their work lives and the growing inconvenience caused by G20 preparation measures. What will be discussed at the summit? How has China prepared? And why is it in Hangzhou anyway?\n@highlight\nPollution, residents cleared out in preparation for China's big G20 debut in Hangzhou\n@highlight\nChina wants to focus on economic issues, rather than the South China Sea dispute\nQuery: The Hangzhou summit has been called another \"milestone\" for a rising @placeholder, keen to show its growing dominance on the world stage.\n\nOptions : A. Chinese\nB. Beijing\nC. South China Sea\nD. Hangzhou\nE. G20\nF. China\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 293, "output_tokens": 6, "total_tokens": 299}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.1402999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_14200", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Connellsville, PennsylvaniaJudy Keller, 69, has always relied on Highlands Hospital for medical care, just as her parents did before her. When she walks through the halls, she recognizes faces from the community and even from her days working as a school teacher. The 64-bed facility, she says, is a mainstay of this rural Southwest Pennsylvania town. \"This hospital all my life has been here,\" said Keller, now retired. \"[It] helps a lot of people who don't have adequate health care coverage \u2014 and I don't know what they would do without it.\" Aside from providing health care to a largely poor population, it provides hundreds of jobs in a town that locals say never recovered after industries such as coal mining and glass manufacturing disappeared.\n@highlight\nAffordable Care Act helped vital but financially troubled rural hospitals\n@highlight\nA full repeal of the law could signal their death knell\nQuery: Despite that, @placeholder CFO Andursky said he barely noticed the increase \u2014 the threat of closure is a \"daily concern,\" he said.\n\nOptions : A. Southwest Pennsylvania\nB. Affordable Care Act\nC. PennsylvaniaJudy Keller\nD. Connellsville\nE. Keller\nF. Highlands Hospital\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 314, "output_tokens": 6, "total_tokens": 320}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.2893999999999998e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_14224", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) So much for a warm and fuzzy Valentine's Day. About 20 cities across the East endured record-breaking cold Sunday, forecasters say. New York City's temperature plummeted to 1 below zero at Central Park, shattering the record of 2 degrees, set during World War I. Boston reported 9 below. Toronto's temperature reached 16 below over the weekend. And those are just the real temperatures. Factor in strong winds, and states from northern Pennsylvania to Maine felt wind chills well, well below zero. In all, more than 75 million people from the Midwest to the Eastern Seaboard are expected to be affected by snow and freezing rain into Tuesday.\n@highlight\nRecord-low temperatures are reported Sunday in some cities\n@highlight\nPart of Interstate 65 in Indiana is closed after multiple crashes\n@highlight\nSnow and freezing rain are impacting more than 75 million people into Tuesday\nQuery: At least three people died in the pileup on @placeholder 78, Pennsylvania State Police said.\n\nOptions : A. Interstate\nB. Central Park\nC. Valentine's Day\nD. Indiana\nE. New York City\nF. East\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 307, "output_tokens": 6, "total_tokens": 313}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.2397e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_14310", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) -- After downloading the latest iPhone, iPod touch and iPad operating system, iOS 6, the fun part is excitedly poking around and hunting for what's new. Find subtle design changes, like the phone's key pad, or set up new features, like Facebook integration. You might even use Siri again for the first time in a while to test its improved sports and restaurant knowledge. If you have an iPhone 3GS, 4 or 4S, a fourth generation iPod touch, or an iPad 2 or the new iPad, you can upgrade to iOS 6. Go to your settings screen, tap General and then Software Update. Keep in mind that some features are limited to the most recent models.\n@highlight\nNew operating system update for the iPhone, iPad and iPod touch has gained and lost features\n@highlight\nApple's new Maps app drops Google data, including public transit directions, adds turn-by-turn\n@highlight\nVoice assistant Siri adds movie, sports and restaurant data\nQuery: Flyover is only available on the iPhone 4S and later, @placeholder 2 and later, and the iPod touch.\n\nOptions : A. iPhone 3GS\nB. General\nC. Software Update\nD. Google\nE. iPhone\nF. Facebook\nG. iOS\nH. iPod touch\nI. iPad\nJ. Apple\nK. Siri\nL. Maps\nM. CNN\nN. 4S\nO. iOS 6\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 364, "output_tokens": 5, "total_tokens": 369}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.6343999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_14349", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) With just two weeks until Congress is expected to leave town, the fate of roughly 700,000 young immigrants still hangs in the balance. And, it could be up to Senate Democrats now to decide whether they will make protections for the Deferred Action for Childhood Arrivals (DACA) program recipients a condition of their support for a must-pass spending bill or punt the issue to next year when they still have months to work it out. There's a whole host of issues that must be dealt with by the end of the year including reauthorizing a spying program, funding disaster relief and paying for the Children's Health Insurance Program, which has all sparked questions about whether Democrats will insist DACA also be included in that list of year-end spending priorities.\n@highlight\nDemocrats have repeatedly called for a fix to the ending of the DACA program\n@highlight\nThe party may have the most leverage as part of their year-end negotiations\nQuery: The President had spoken favorably in September about DACA recipients and pushed @placeholder to reach a deal, but in recent weeks ne has taken to hardline rhetoric on illegal immigration and blaming Democrats for crime.\n\nOptions : A. Children's Health Insurance Program\nB. Deferred Action for Childhood Arrivals\nC. Democrats\nD. DACA\nE. Congress\nF. Senate\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query requires identifying the entity that the President pushed to reach a DACA deal. The passage opens by framing the entire issue around the congressional calendar (\"With just two weeks until Congress is expected to leave town\") and repeatedly identifies Congress as the body that must act on year-end spending legislation that could include DACA protections.  \n\nThe sentence structure of the query contrasts the President\u2019s earlier constructive appeal with his later hard-line rhetoric; the natural recipient of that appeal, given the legislative timetable described, is therefore Congress. Among the supplied options, only \u201cCongress\u201d fits this role without redundancy or contradiction.  \n\nThus the placeholder is filled by the text of option E.\n\n\\boxed{Congress}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 448, "output_tokens": 138, "total_tokens": 586}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000905, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_14820", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) There were more reported cases of sexually transmitted diseases last year than ever before in the United States, according to the latest STD surveillance report by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention. The annual report, which was released on Wednesday, showed that the rates of chlamydia, gonorrhea, and syphilis -- the three most commonly reported STDs in the nation -- increased between 2014 and 2015, reaching an all-time high. Reported cases of primary and secondary syphilis rose by 19%, gonorrhea cases rose by 12.8%, and chlamydia cases rose by 5.9%, from 2014. All three STDs are curable with antibiotics, but most infections go undiagnosed and untreated, according to the CDC.\n@highlight\nChlamydia, gonorrhea and syphilis rates hit an all-time high last year, new report shows\n@highlight\n\"We have reached a decisive moment for the nation,\" CDC official says\nQuery: Scientists at the @placeholder warned in July that the bacterium that causes gonorrhea, called Neisseria gonorrhoeae, is developing resistance to the antibiotic drugs used to treat it.\n\nOptions : A. United States\nB. STD\nC. CDC\nD. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\nE. Chlamydia\nF. STDs\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The passage discusses rising STD rates based on a CDC report and quotes a CDC official. The query sentence requires an organization whose scientists could issue a warning about gonorrhea resistance; the only entity in the passage that fits this role is the CDC (introduced in full on first mention and then abbreviated).  \n\nAll other options are either generic terms (STD, STDs), unrelated diseases (Chlamydia), or geographic references (United States) that do not match the required slot.  \n\nThus the placeholder is filled by the text \u201cCDC\u201d.\n\n\\boxed{CDC}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 508, "output_tokens": 1050, "total_tokens": 1558}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:36:02.319533+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00326, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_14964", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: A million homes in\u00a0Morocco\u00a0could soon be powered by a mega solar plant capable of providing energy at all hours of the day and night. Instead of using the standard photovoltaic solar cells, Ouarzazate's power station will use Concentrated Solar Power (CSP) - a technology that harnesses sunlight to melt salt and power a steam turbine. The plant, called Noor1, is expected to open next month and will be the first of four stations to be set up in the region. Once complete, the establishment will be the largest CSP farm in the world. The Ouarzazate plant is part of Morocco's strategy to produce 42 per cent of its energy from renewable sources by 2020 - a goal that has been praised by the UN.\n@highlight\nThe Ouarzazate plant will be the biggest solar thermal plant in the world\n@highlight\nIt will use a technology known as Concentrate Solar Power (CSP)\n@highlight\nCSP harnesses sunlight to melt salt and power a steam turbine\n@highlight\nMorocco plans to get 42 per cent of its energy from renewables by 2020\nQuery: While solar thermal power methods such as @placeholder only work in very hot countries, solar energy at large is experiencing more widespread use worldwide as the photovoltaic panels' price is progressively falling.\n\nOptions : A. Ouarzazate\nB. Concentrate Solar Power\nC. Morocco\nD. UN\nE. Concentrated Solar Power\nF. CSP\nG. Noor1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query requires filling @placeholder in a sentence about solar thermal methods. The passage describes the relevant technology as one that \"harnesses sunlight to melt salt and power a steam turbine,\" explicitly naming it \"Concentrated Solar Power (CSP).\"  \n\nThis matches option E exactly (including correct spelling), and the resulting sentence is both grammatical and faithful to the source text. Options B (misspelled) and F (abbreviation) are close but inferior; the remaining choices name places or organizations rather than the method itself.  \n\nThus the text of the single best option is Concentrated Solar Power.\n\n\\boxed{Concentrated Solar Power}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 555, "output_tokens": 1193, "total_tokens": 1748}, "provider": "xAI", "model_used": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "requested_model": "x-ai/grok-4.3", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T16:36:04.753559+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00367625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_14974", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: One way or another, Chile's Copa America semi-final with Peru will be settled in Santiago on Monday night, but the two nations will continue to bicker long after the full-time whistle. Whether the debate centres on cocktails or overhead kicks, agreeing to disagree is the only thing these two rivals will concede to one another. And the clash  - the most important in almost 20 years - will re-open old wounds in what is one of football's fiercest yet little-known rivalries. The animosity dates back to the four-year War of the Pacific at the end of the nineteenth century, hence its tag as the 'Pacific Clasico'. The 1879-1883 conflict, which also involved Bolivia, was fought over the supply of nitrates and ended with Chile annexing large parts of its neighbours' territory.\n@highlight\nChile and Peru meet in the semi-finals of the Copa America\n@highlight\nThe two nations have had animosity ever since the War of the Pacific\n@highlight\nThey also disagree on where the local spirit Pisco\u00a0originates\u00a0from\n@highlight\nChile are favourites for the clash after impressing during the tournament\nQuery: Perhaps not, but don't expect the respective fans to come together for a glass of @placeholder afterwards, either.\n\nOptions : A. Copa America\nB. War of the Pacific\nC. Santiago\nD. Peru\nE. Bolivia\nF. Chile\nG. Pisco\nH. Pacific Clasico\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query sentence refers to a post-match drink that fans of the two teams would be unlikely to share, given their long-standing disagreements. The passage (and its accompanying highlights) explicitly notes that Chile and Peru disagree about the origins of the local spirit Pisco.  \n\nThis matches option G exactly; none of the other listed entities fits the context of a shared glass after the match.  \n\nThus the placeholder is resolved by the single word \u201cPisco.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{Pisco}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 477, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 572}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00083375, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_15366", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: William Tallon was more than just the Queen Mother\u2019s favourite servant. He rose from impoverished beginnings to become her confidant and close friend. As the first part of a remarkable new biography revealed last week, Tallon was also a predatory homosexual who breached Royal security by bringing young men back to Clarence House at night. And he made powerful enemies. Here, in the final extract of Backstairs Billy, we reveal that courtiers took their revenge by banishing him from the Queen Mother\u2019s side, shamefully disregarding her wish that he should be allowed to live at Clarence House for the rest of his life.\n@highlight\nQueen Mother's royal courtier William Tallon was known as Backstairs Billy\n@highlight\nRose from impoverished beginnings to become her confidant and friend\n@highlight\nBut he also breached protocol and brought young men to Clarence House\n@highlight\nOther courtiers took revenge by banishing him from Queen Mother's side\n@highlight\nAlso denied her request that he should be allowed to live at Clarence House for the rest of his life\nQuery: For years he had organised lunches and dinners for the @placeholder, but he had never had to make his own meals.\n\nOptions : A. Royal\nB. Mother\nC. Queen\nD. Queen Mother\nE. Clarence House\nF. Tallon\nG. William Tallon\nH. Backstairs Billy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The passage centers on William Tallon (Backstairs Billy) and his long service to the Queen Mother. The pronoun \u201che\u201d in the query sentence therefore refers to Tallon, who is described throughout as the Queen Mother\u2019s confidant and servant. The only phrase that both fits the syntactic slot after \u201cfor the\u201d and is consistent with the surrounding narrative is \u201cQueen Mother.\u201d All other options are either too vague, refer to the wrong person, or name a location rather than the individual for whom Tallon organized meals.\n\nThus the completed sentence reads naturally and accurately: \u201cFor years he had organised lunches and dinners for the Queen Mother, but he had never had to make his own meals.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{Queen Mother}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 461, "output_tokens": 145, "total_tokens": 606}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00093875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_15745", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) You will be able to test yourself at home for a genetic predisposition for certain diseases, thanks to a new ruling from the US Food and Drug Administration. On Thursday, the FDA gave 23andMe permission to market its Personal Genome Service genetic health risk tests for 10 diseases. It is the first direct-to-consumer genetic test the FDA has allowed to provide that information. The tests can look for a genetic predisposition to conditions; the 10 approved Thursday are Parkinson's; late-onset Alzheimer's; celiac disease; a movement disorder called early-onset primary dystonia; a disorder that elevates your risk for lung and liver disease called Alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency; a blood clotting disorder Factor XI deficiency; an organ and tissue disorder called Gaucher disease type 1; a red blood cell condition known as G6PD; hereditary hemochromatosis, an iron overload disorder; and hereditary thrombophilia, a blood clot disorder.\n@highlight\n23andMe gets FDA approval to market its genetic tests for 10 diseases\n@highlight\nThese tests do not give a diagnosis but suggest whether you have a predisposition\nQuery: Environmental factors and lifestyle choices probably influence whether someone will get a disease like late-onset @placeholder's.\n\nOptions : A. US Food and Drug Administration\nB. Alpha-1\nC. Personal Genome Service\nD. G6PD\nE. Alzheimer\nF. Gaucher\nG. FDA\nH. Parkinson\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 374, "output_tokens": 5, "total_tokens": 379}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.7054e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_15955", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) According to a recent survey, 72% of Americans think coconut oil is a healthy food. But despite popular health claims about coconut oil, a report from the American Heart Association recently advised against its use, stating that it increases LDL cholesterol (a cause of cardiovascular disease) and has no known offsetting effects. \"There are many claims being made about coconut oil being wonderful for lots of different things, but we really don't have any evidence of long-term health benefits,\" said Dr. Walter C. Willett, professor of epidemiology and nutrition at the Harvard T.H. Chan School of Public Health. How exactly, then, does coconut oil rank among oils?\n@highlight\nCoconut oil increases LDL cholesterol, a cause of cardiovascular disease\n@highlight\nBut coconut oil does a particularly nice job of raising HDL, the \"good\" cholesterol\nQuery: Still, though the increase in @placeholder seen with consumption of coconut oil may offset some of the disease risk, it's still not as good as consuming unsaturated oils, which not only raise HDL but lower LDL, according to Willett.\n\nOptions : A. LDL\nB. American Heart Association\nC. Americans\nD. Walter C. Willett\nE. HDL\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "E. HDL\n\n\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 316, "output_tokens": 11, "total_tokens": 327}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.3535999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_16116", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: When Suleiman the Magnificent died, his heart and body were buried in separate locations. His embalmed body was laid to rest at mosque in Istanbul and the rest was hidden in a secret location. Now, archaeologists believe they have unearthed the tomb that holds the heart and organs from the great ruler of the Ottoman Empire. 'We have data which all points in the same direction,'said Norbet Pap head of the department of Political Geography, Regional and Development Studies at the University of Pecs in Hungary at a presentation of the latest findings. 'That is why we say 'in all certainty,' because there is no sign pointing in another direction.'\n@highlight\nTeam used historical records and archives to search for location of tomb\n@highlight\nDecorative elements resemble those where his body is\n@highlight\nSuleiman's death at Szigetvar was kept secret for 48 days\n@highlight\nExcavation work at the site would restart in April\nQuery: Until his death at age 71, Suleiman was the @placeholder's longest-ruling sultan.\n\nOptions : A. Suleiman\nB. Norbet Pap\nC. Szigetvar\nD. Regional and Development Studies\nE. University of Pecs\nF. Istanbul\nG. Political Geography\nH. Hungary\nI. Magnificent\nJ. Ottoman Empire\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "J. Ottoman Empire\n\n\\boxed{J. Ottoman Empire}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 343, "output_tokens": 14, "total_tokens": 357}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.5752999999999996e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_16180", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Since the mid-1990s, Rs 1,500 crore has been spent to clean up the dying Yamuna, but it all has gone down the drain. Now the water you drink is expected to give a new lease of life to the once fabled river. For the first time in history, Delhi may get its share of Yamuna water, treated and supplied to households, from the river itself. The Capital has so far been getting water diverted from the river to Western Yamuna Canal (WYC) in Haryana. This meets Delhi\u2019s 70 per cent drinking water needs. A high-powered committee headed by the secretary, ministry of water resources, Shashi Shekhar, has recommended this move to the National Green Tribunal (NGT) to ensure fresh water flow in the river.\n@highlight\nCommittee says Yamuna river will remain a 'sewer' unless action is taken\n@highlight\nIt will take time for the river to revive, but Green Tribunal supports plan\nQuery: Even now the canal water is deposited at Palla in @placeholder and collected at Wazirabad before it is cleaned up and supplied.\n\nOptions : A. Western Yamuna Canal\nB. WYC\nC. Haryana\nD. Shashi Shekhar\nE. National Green Tribunal\nF. Green Tribunal\nG. The Capital\nH. Delhi\nI. Committee\nJ. Rs\nK. Yamuna\nL. NGT\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The passage describes how Delhi currently receives its drinking water via diversion into the Western Yamuna Canal (WYC) located in Haryana. That diverted canal water then enters Delhi at the upstream monitoring point of Palla before being collected farther downstream at the Wazirabad barrage for treatment.  \n\nBecause both Palla and Wazirabad lie inside Delhi, the only phrase that correctly completes the sentence \u201cdeposited at Palla in \u2026 and collected at Wazirabad\u201d is the place name \u201cDelhi.\u201d All other listed options either name entities outside Delhi or are not place names at all.\n\nThus the required text is Delhi.\n\n\\boxed{Delhi}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 473, "output_tokens": 127, "total_tokens": 600}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00090875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_16546", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: After months of speculation Microsoft has officially announced its Windows 10 software will launch globally on 29 July. The Washington-based firm said Windows 7 and Windows 8.1 users will have one year from this date to take advantage of the free upgrade. And once a device is upgraded to Windows 10, Microsoft said it will continue to keep it up-to-date for the supported lifetime of the device at no cost. For other Windows users, or people who don't currently run a version of the firm's operating system, they will need to pay for the software. Microsoft hasn't announced pricing but details leaked on a reseller over the weekend suggest it will start at $109.99 for the Home edition, and $149.99 for the Professional version.\n@highlight\nMicrosoft said software will launch across all 190 regions on the same day\n@highlight\nIt will power PCs, phones and connected devices such as bank machines and medical equipment, along with the firm's Xbox One console\n@highlight\nWindows 7 and 8.1 users will have a year from 29 July to get free upgrade\n@highlight\nAnd Microsoft will support the software for the lifetime of the device\nQuery: Although the new software won't be formally released until next year, analysts already consider its success crucial for @placeholder and Satya Nadella.\n\nOptions : A. Xbox One\nB. Windows 8.1\nC. Windows 7\nD. Windows 10\nE. Microsoft\nF. PCs\nG. Windows\nH. Washington\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 388, "output_tokens": 6, "total_tokens": 394}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.8148e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_16687", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Users\u00a0of Microsoft's new Windows 10 software were elated to find the firm had brought back solitaire, the famous free game. In its latest incarnation it boasts more features and can even track your stats. However, there is just one problem - to play without ads, users have to pay Microsoft $10 a year, every year. Experts have describe the decision as odd. 'Netflix charges you $7.99 per month for thousands of streaming movies and TV shows, Spotify, Slacker, Rdio and others charge about $10 per month for unlimited music,' said Mark Hachman of PC World. 'And Microsoft? They want you to pay $1.50 per month to remove ads from Solitaire.'\n@highlight\nFree game was a popular part of earlier windows versions\n@highlight\nNew Version charges users $10 a year for ad free\u00a0Solitaire\u00a0games\n@highlight\nExperts say the feature is 'an accident waiting to happen'\nQuery: '@placeholder itself is free, so complaining too much about this might seem ungracious,' said Hachman.\n\nOptions : A. Windows 10\nB. Solitaire\nC. Rdio\nD. Netflix\nE. Microsoft\nF. PC World\nG. Slacker\nH. New Version\nI. Mark Hachman\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query requires identifying the referent of \"@placeholder\" in the given quote from Mark Hachman.  \n\nThe passage explicitly describes solitaire as \"the famous free game\" and notes that the only paid element is the optional ad-removal subscription. Hachman's remark therefore contrasts the free base product with the optional fee, making \"Solitaire\" the only noun that fits the placeholder both semantically and contextually. All other options either refer to paid services (Netflix, Rdio, etc.) or to entities that are not described as free in the text.  \n\nThus the completed sentence reads naturally: \"Solitaire itself is free, so complaining too much about this might seem ungracious.\"\n\n\\boxed{B. Solitaire}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 446, "output_tokens": 143, "total_tokens": 589}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000915, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_16724", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Apple promised it would offer an Android version of its music service in autumn. And it seems it is on track, if leaked images spotted by German website Mobile Geeks are anything to go by. Screenshots seem to show Apple Music features including Beats 1 Radio and the built-in social network Apple Music Connect, as well as Android hallmarks such as sliding sidebars. Shots of the beta version of the app show the 'For Me' recommendations page as well as features not currently available on the iOS version, such as the ability to change the size of the cache used to store music offline, 9to5Mac reported.\n@highlight\nLeaked screenshots were spotted by German website Mobile Geeks\n@highlight\nSeem to show standard Apple Music features including Beats 1 Radio and the built-in social network Apple Music Connect with Android functionality\n@highlight\nApple has previously said the service will launch on Android this autumn\nQuery: It noted the design still looks like an @placeholder product, but the functions are geared towards Android, rather than iPhone users.\n\nOptions : A. For Me\nB. Beats 1 Radio\nC. German\nD. Android\nE. Apple Music Connect\nF. Apple Music\nG. Mobile Geeks\nH. Apple\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query sentence describes a contrast between the app's overall appearance (which resembles something familiar from Apple) and its functionality (which has been adapted specifically for Android users).  \n\nThe passage repeatedly references the beta app as an Apple product that is being ported to Android, and it explicitly notes features that differ from the existing iOS version. Substituting \u201cApple\u201d for the placeholder produces the coherent statement \u201cthe design still looks like an Apple product, but the functions are geared towards Android,\u201d which matches both the wording of the query and the information supplied in the passage.  \n\nNo other option yields a grammatically or contextually plausible sentence.\n\n\\boxed{H. Apple}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 439, "output_tokens": 132, "total_tokens": 571}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00087875, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_16736", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Nasa has selected a variety of companies to work on projects to create advanced space technologies, including faster methods of propulsion. Other projects to be worked on include improved habitats for humans, and small satellites to explore deep space. And one of the companies in the 12 Next Space Technologies for Exploration Partnerships (NextStep) says they have an engine that could get humans to Mars in just 39 days. Scroll down for video Nasa has selected a variety of companies to work on projects to create advanced space technologies, including a faster method of propulsion known as Vasimr (illustrated), which could apparently get to Mars in a matter of weeks, not months\n@highlight\nCompany in Texas has been asked to develop its revolutionary engine\n@highlight\nAd Astra's Vasimr engine could apparently get to Mars in 39 days\n@highlight\nIt is one of 12 advanced technology projects to be funded by Nasa\n@highlight\nOthers include new types of habitation and small deep space satellites\nQuery: Whether an engine such as @placeholder could shorten the time it would take to cover the distance, though, remains to be seen.\n\nOptions : A. Nasa\nB. Ad Astra\nC. NextStep\nD. Texas\nE. Mars\nF. Next Space Technologies for Exploration Partnerships\nG. Vasimr\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query is a cloze-style sentence that must be completed by the single most appropriate term from the supplied options.  \n\nThe passage repeatedly identifies one specific propulsion technology\u2014the Vasimr engine developed by Ad Astra\u2014as the candidate system that \u201ccould get humans to Mars in just 39 days.\u201d The query\u2019s phrasing (\u201can engine such as \u2026\u201d) directly echoes that claim and therefore calls for the name of the engine itself.  \n\nAll other options are either organizations (Nasa, Ad Astra, NextStep), geographic references (Texas), or broader program names; none of them denotes an engine. Consequently the only term that can grammatically and semantically occupy the placeholder is \u201cVasimr.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{Vasimr}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 451, "output_tokens": 143, "total_tokens": 594}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00092125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_17584", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: America's largest internet providers have been accused off ripping off customers and 'throttling' their internet connections. Major providers, including AT&T, Time Warner and Verizon, are all slowing users, many slowing to the speed of a dial up connection at times - despite recent net neutrality rulings which outlaw such practices. Researchers analysed online tests taken by 300,00 people in major cities. This test measures whether interconnection points are experiencing problems. It runs speed measurements from your (the test user\u2019s) ISP, across multiple interconnection points, detecting degraded performance. They says the evidence collected points to slowdowns for users on the networks of five of the largest Internet access providers \u2014 AT&T, CenturyLink, Comcast, Time Warner Cable and Verizon \u2014 which represent 75 percent of all U.S. wireline households\n@highlight\nReport analysed results from 300,000 internet users in major cities\n@highlight\nFound AT&T, Time Warner and Verizon \u00a0all slowed data speeds at times\nQuery: 'In truth, the big phone and cable companies are terrified that so many people are performing the speed tests and compiling data on what ails the @placeholder.,' he said.\n\nOptions : A. Time Warner Cable\nB. AT&T\nC. U.S.\nD. Internet\nE. Verizon\nF. America\nG. Comcast\nH. Time Warner\nI. CenturyLink\nJ. ISP\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D. Internet}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 355, "output_tokens": 8, "total_tokens": 363}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.6005e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_17691", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Nasa wants to land the first humans on Mars in 2035, and to do that, it needs the world's toughest parachute. Its latest plan is to use a large inflatable 'flying saucer' that will slow a spacecraft down after piercing through the thin Martian atmosphere. Dubbed the density supersonic decelerator (LDSD), the space agency plans to conduct an ambitious test flight of its design on Wednesday at 1:30pm (5:30pm GMT). The LDSD is unique in its design, using a donut-shaped inflatable decelerator to create atmospheric drag. When attached to the exterior of a capsule travelling at Mach 4 it will be capable of slowing it down to Mach 2, where a regular parachute can then deploy.\n@highlight\nThe saucer is known as the low density supersonic decelerator\n@highlight\nThe test flight will take place on Wednesday at 1:30pm ET (5:30 GMT)\n@highlight\nInflatable saucer is 5ft (4.6 metres) wide, weighing 7,000lbs (3.200kg)\n@highlight\nThe parachute was torn apart in when it deployed in a flight last year\nQuery: Last June, to simulate the @placeholder atmosphere on Earth, the LDSD was lifted to a height of 23 miles (37km) by a high-altitude balloon.\n\nOptions : A. Martian\nB. Nasa\nC. LDSD\nD. Inflatable\nE. GMT\nF. Mars\nG. Mach 2\nH. Mach 4\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 399, "output_tokens": 6, "total_tokens": 405}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.8928999999999997e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_17871", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) Prepare to say goodbye to Cassini. In the early morning hours of September 15, NASA's 13-year mission exploring Saturn and its moons will come to an end as the spacecraft deliberately dives into Saturn's atmosphere and plunges itself into the planet. Even then, Cassini will transmit new data about the planet's composition as long as its antenna remains pointed toward Earth, with the assist from small thrusters. No spacecraft has ever been so close to Saturn. \"You can think of Cassini as the first Saturn probe,\" said Linda Spilker, Cassini project scientist. The Ion and Neutral Mass Spectrometer will act as the \"nose\" of the spacecraft, directly sampling the composition and structure of the atmosphere -- something that can't be done from orbit, said Hunter Waite, team lead for the spectrometer.\n@highlight\nThe NASA Cassini mission ends Friday after 13 years observing the Saturn system\n@highlight\nCassini data has revealed groundbreaking discoveries about Saturn and its moons\nQuery: While many other options were considered -- such as \"parking\" the spacecraft in orbit around @placeholder -- they didn't want to risk Cassini colliding with any of Saturn's moons.\n\nOptions : A. Saturn\nB. NASA Cassini\nC. Cassini\nD. Ion and Neutral Mass Spectrometer\nE. Linda Spilker\nF. Hunter Waite\nG. NASA\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query requires identifying the most logical referent for the placeholder based on context from the passage. The passage describes the deliberate decision to end the Cassini mission by plunging the spacecraft into Saturn itself. This choice was made precisely to eliminate any possibility of the probe later colliding with (and potentially contaminating) any of Saturn\u2019s moons.  \n\nConsequently, the phrase \u201cparking the spacecraft in orbit around \u2026\u201d must refer to Saturn; any other listed entity is either a person, an instrument aboard Cassini, or an organization and would not fit the orbital context.  \n\nThus the placeholder is correctly filled by the text \u201cSaturn.\u201d\n\n\\boxed{Saturn}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 463, "output_tokens": 129, "total_tokens": 592}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00090125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_17965", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) Long-term use of acetaminophen during pregnancy was associated with twice the risk of attention-deficit hyperactivity disorder in children, according to a study published Monday in the journal Pediatrics. However, two experts believe that the data do not support these findings. Acetaminophen, also known as paracetamol, is the active ingredient in Tylenol and hundreds of over-the-counter and prescription medicines, according to the US Food and Drug Administration. It is commonly prescribed during pregnancy to relieve pain and fever, with an estimated 65% of pregnant women in America using the drug, according to the US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention.\n@highlight\nResearchers collected data from about 95,000 mothers with children born between 1999 and 2009\n@highlight\nLong-term acetaminophen use in pregnancy is related to more than a twofold increase in risk for ADHD in children\n@highlight\nThe data does not support their conclusions, other experts say\nQuery: No evidence of a cause-effect relationship between the drug and @placeholder was found, Ystr\u00f8m and his colleagues concluded.\n\nOptions : A. US Food and Drug Administration\nB. Acetaminophen\nC. Long\nD. Pediatrics\nE. America\nF. Tylenol\nG. ADHD\nH. US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query sentence refers to the conclusion of experts (Ystr\u00f8m et al.) who reviewed the study findings. The study itself reported an association between long-term acetaminophen use and ADHD risk, but the experts explicitly stated that the data showed no causal link.  \n\nAmong the given options, only \u201cADHD\u201d completes the sentence in a way that is consistent with the passage. All other options are either organizations, drug names, or unrelated terms that do not fit the logical or factual context.  \n\nThus the correct option text is ADHD.\n\n\\boxed{ADHD}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 440, "output_tokens": 110, "total_tokens": 550}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000825, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_18033", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Arkansas' Supreme Court on Friday afternoon stopped any more same-sex marriages in the state, a court spokeswoman said, leaving the legal status of more than 400 gay and lesbian couples who got marriage licenses in limbo. This development stems from 21 couples' legal challenge of Amendment 83 to the Arkansas Constitution, arguing that it violates their federal and state rights of equal protection and privacy. Pulaski County Circuit Judge Chris Piazza ruled in their favor last Friday. But same-sex marriage was back up in the air after the state Supreme Court said Wednesday it couldn't decide whether to grant an emergency stay because Piazza's decision was \"not final.\"\n@highlight\nA state judge in Arkansas earlier struck down same-sex marriage ban\n@highlight\nArkansas Supreme Court grants a stay, thus preventing more such marriages\n@highlight\nStatus of couples who got marriage licenses is unclear\nQuery: @placeholder, at least, was issuing marriage licenses to same-sex couples by Thursday afternoon.\n\nOptions : A. Arkansas Supreme Court\nB. Supreme Court\nC. Arkansas\nD. Chris Piazza\nE. Amendment 83\nF. Piazza\nG. Arkansas Constitution\nH. Pulaski County\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 308, "output_tokens": 6, "total_tokens": 314}, "provider": "openrouter", "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 2.2468e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_18362", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Their wild ways might already be the talk of Newport high society, but don't assume we've seen the best of Lillian and Beatrice Bellacourt quite yet. Because as these wine-swigging, bed-hopping sisters enter the limelight, their scandalous lifestyles are becoming exposed in all their debauched detail. We're talking sex, drugs and buckets of money \u2013 with a touch of incest thrown in for good measure. Not your average society darling, fame-hungry Lady Lillian isn't afraid to let down her perfectly coiffed hair, with her daringly extravagant soir\u00e9es. To keep up with this upper-class party girl, you'll find yourself downing glasses of cocaine-wine, dodging a gun-toting matriarch and quite possibility getting into a fist-fight with a blind and deaf lady.\n@highlight\nFictional content sponsored by Comedy Central\nQuery: Not to be outdone by her sister's escapades, @placeholder indulges in a few exploits of her own, including daring sexual dalliances.\n\nOptions : A. Newport\nB. Lady Lillian\nC. Comedy Central\nD. Lillian\nE. Beatrice Bellacourt\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The passage describes the scandalous exploits of the Bellacourt sisters in Newport, with the bulk of the specific details (cocaine-wine, extravagant soir\u00e9es, etc.) attached to Lady Lillian. The query sentence is structured as a follow-on that attributes additional exploits to the other sister\u2014the one whose behavior has not yet been enumerated.  \n\nThat sister is Beatrice Bellacourt, making option E the only choice that satisfies both the referential logic of the sentence and the content of the passage.  \n\n\\boxed{Beatrice Bellacourt}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 409, "output_tokens": 108, "total_tokens": 517}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00078125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_18477", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) People are often surprised to learn that Shelby Payne has type 1 diabetes -- because her identical twin sister, Sydney, does not. \"Everyone's like, 'Wow, how in the world does (my sister) not have it?' \" said Payne, 23, who once played forward on Stanford's soccer team, like her sister. \"They can't really fathom it.\" Though experts agree that genetics influence who gets type 1 diabetes, Payne's story suggests that something other than genes must also be at play. And some researchers are focusing in on one family of viruses in particular. A new study from Finland joins decades of research suggesting that enteroviruses, which include over 100 individual virus types, may play a key role in triggering type 1 diabetes, which has no cure.\n@highlight\nType 1 diabetes is an autoimmune condition, which may be triggered by factors that are not genetic\n@highlight\nEnteroviruses, known to affect the gut, may be a key player in the development of type 1 diabetes\nQuery: @placeholder and her sister have also enrolled in TrialNet, a diabetes research network studying ways to prevent and delay type 1 diabetes.\n\nOptions : A. Enteroviruses\nB. Type 1\nC. Payne\nD. Finland\nE. Sydney\nF. Stanford\nG. Shelby Payne\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The passage introduces Shelby Payne as the individual with type 1 diabetes and explicitly identifies her identical twin sister Sydney as the unaffected sibling. The query sentence requires a subject who \u201cand her sister\u201d enrolled in TrialNet; only Shelby Payne satisfies this referential relationship.  \n\n- Option C (\u201cPayne\u201d) is merely a surname fragment and does not appear as a standalone referent in the passage.  \n- Option E (\u201cSydney\u201d) would produce the nonsensical phrase \u201cSydney and her sister.\u201d  \n- All remaining options (A, B, D, F) are entities or concepts that lack any sibling relationship.  \n\nConsequently, the sole grammatically and contextually coherent filler is the full name given in the passage.\n\n\\boxed{Shelby Payne}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 454, "output_tokens": 147, "total_tokens": 601}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.000935, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_18633", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: The Earth experienced its hottest month of March since record-keeping began in 1880. There's been no break from the globe's record heat - the first three months of 2015 have all set new high temperature marks. Last month's average temperature soared to 56.4\u00b0F (13.6\u00b0C), which is 1.5\u00b0F (0.85\u00b0C) above the average for the 20th century. Last month's average temperature of 56.4\u00b0F (13.6\u00b0C) was the hottest March on record, averaging 1.5\u00b0F (0.85\u00b0C) above the average for the 20th century. This was the highest for March in the 1880\u20132015 record, surpassing the previous record of 2010 by 0.09\u00b0F (0.05\u00b0C). Pictured is how the high temperatures affected different regions of the world\n@highlight\nWorld experience average temperatures of 56.4\u00b0F (13.6\u00b0C) last month - 1.5\u00b0F above average for the 20th century\n@highlight\nFirst 3 months of 2015 have set new high temperature marks, and the trend could continue throughout the year\n@highlight\nScientists warn fossil fuels are pushing greenhouse gas into the atmosphere, leading to increased temperatures\n@highlight\nBut El Ni\u00f1o, a blob of record hot water in the Northeast Pacific Ocean, could also be driving up temperatures\nQuery: 'Many climate prediction models show this weak @placeholder continuing into summer.'\n\nOptions : A. 56.4\u00b0F\nB. F (13.6\u00b0C\nC. Earth\nD. Northeast Pacific Ocean\nE. El Ni\u00f1o\nF. 0.09\u00b0F\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query requires identifying the noun phrase that logically completes the placeholder in the given sentence (\"Many climate prediction models show this weak @placeholder continuing into summer\").  \n\nThe passage explicitly introduces El Ni\u00f1o as a climatic phenomenon (\"a blob of record hot water\") that can vary in strength and that is already being discussed as a possible driver of the observed temperature anomalies. Substituting \"El Ni\u00f1o\" yields the coherent statement \"this weak El Ni\u00f1o continuing into summer,\" which is a standard meteorological observation.  \n\nAll other options produce semantically or grammatically ill-formed sentences:  \n- temperature values (A, B, F) cannot \"continue into summer\";  \n- geographic or planetary nouns (C, D) likewise fail to fit the predicate.  \n\nHence the only option that satisfies both the syntactic frame and the scientific context supplied by the passage is E.  \n\n\\boxed{El Ni\u00f1o}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 528, "output_tokens": 172, "total_tokens": 700}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00109, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_18766", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Everyone has that friend who instigates a wild night out, encourages you to have one drink too many, but gets you home in one piece. Now there's a 'smart beer mug' that does a similar thing. Fitted with sensors, the ePint lights up when it is empty, keeps track of the number of drinks its user has sunk and can even suggest ordering a cab at the end of the night. Start-up Xtreme Tech, based in Los Angeles, California, is raising money to put the gadget into production on Kickstarter. The firm audaciously describes its invention as 'Vegas in a cup'.\n@highlight\nePint contains sensors, LEDs and a Bluetooth chip to link to a phone\n@highlight\nIt lights up to show when it is empty or when a sports team has scored\n@highlight\nApp features let users play drinking games and even order a cab home\n@highlight\nGadget is available to pre-order via Kickstarter from $30 (\u00a320)\nQuery: The ePint also has a built-in weight sensor to track how much liquid it is holding, accelerometers and @placeholder that flash and change colour, as well as a bottle opener so it can be filled with beer quickly.\n\nOptions : A. App\nB. Kickstarter\nC. Bluetooth\nD. California\nE. LEDs\nF. Gadget\nG. Los Angeles\nH. Vegas\nI. Xtreme Tech\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query requires filling in the @placeholder based on details from the passage. The passage explicitly states that the ePint contains \"sensors, LEDs and a Bluetooth chip,\" and that \"It lights up to show when it is empty.\"  \n\nThis directly matches the query's description of components that \"flash and change colour.\" Among the given options, only LEDs fits this description and context (the other options refer to unrelated elements such as the company name, location, or app features).  \n\nThus, the correct option text is LEDs.\n\n\\boxed{LEDs}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 475, "output_tokens": 113, "total_tokens": 588}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00087625, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_9449", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: She won an Oscar for playing Elizabeth II in the 2006 film The Queen. Now, Helen Mirren has once again scored a major award for playing her Royal Highness - this time for the play The Audience - at the 2015 Tony Awards in New York City on Sunday night. It also marked the 69-year-old's first ever Tony Award win, which is considered to be U.S. theater's highest honor. The Tony Award meant that Mirren was only a Grammy Award away from gaining so-called EGOT status as the winner of an Emmy, Grammy, Oscar and Tony - a distinction shared by only 12 entertainers.\n@highlight\nHelen Mirren wins for Best Leading Actress in a Play for portrayal of Queen Elizabeth II in The Audience\n@highlight\nThe Curious Incident of the Dog in the Night-Time scores five awards including Best Play and Best Leading Actor in a Play\n@highlight\nFun Home ties for lead with five awards including \u00a0Best Musical, Best Book of a Musical, Best Score, Best Director and Best Leading Actor in a Musical\n@highlight\nTommy Tune accepts Lifetime Achievement Award marking his 10th Tony Award\nQuery: 'Your Majesty, you did it again,' @placeholder said as she accepted her first Tony Award.\n\nOptions : A. Best Leading Actress\nB. Best Leading Actor\nC. Tommy Tune\nD. The Queen\nE. Elizabeth II\nF. Lifetime Achievement Award\nG. Grammy Award\nH. Tony Award\nI. Helen Mirren\nJ. New York City\nK. The Audience\nL. Best Book of a Musical\nM. Tony Awards\nN. Best Musical\nO. Tony\nP. Emmy\nQ. Best Score\nR. Oscar\nS. Best Director\nT. U.S.\nU. Best Play\nV. Royal Highness\nW. Curious Incident of the Dog in the Night\nX. EGOT\nY. Grammy\nZ. Mirren\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{Helen Mirren}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 469, "output_tokens": 7, "total_tokens": 476}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:00:40.926759+00:00"}, "cost": 0.00012775, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_9518", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) It's official -- El Ni\u00f1o is dead. But its demise doesn't necessarily mean we're done with wild weather. The recent climate event -- characterized by warming waters in the eastern Pacific Ocean -- has been one of the strongest ever recorded, and its impact has been felt far and wide. Record smashing temperatures hit Thailand, Laos and Cambodia. In Malaysia, lakes dried up and vegetables withered. Weak monsoons and killer heatwaves left India barren and praying for rain. Storms pounded the Californian coast, leaving apartments teetering on cliff edges as backyards dropped into the ocean. The weather system may even have contributed to the spread of Zika by creating conditions that helped mosquito populations thrive.\n@highlight\nThe temperature of the Pacific has cooled, signaling the end of the El Ni\u00f1o part of the cycle\n@highlight\nExperts say there is a 75% chance of a La Ni\u00f1a pattern forming by the end of 2016\nQuery: According to Dr. Santoso, the risk for a strong @placeholder is enhanced following a strong El Ni\u00f1o, such as the one we just had over the last year.\n\nOptions : A. Malaysia\nB. La Ni\u00f1a\nC. El Ni\u00f1o\nD. Zika\nE. Laos\nF. India\nG. Cambodia\nH. Californian\nI. Thailand\nJ. Pacific\nK. Pacific Ocean\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{La Ni\u00f1a}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 338, "output_tokens": 7, "total_tokens": 345}, "provider": "Google AI Studio", "model_used": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "requested_model": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "invoked_at": "2026-08-05T17:00:39.172594+00:00"}, "cost": 9.5e-05, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_9533", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: If Jenson Button has competed in a British Grand Prix for the last time, it can conclusively be said that his association with it was jinxed. He has never so much as had a podium in 16 attempts, and his brief participation in yesterday\u2019s race was fittingly disastrous. He crashed out on the first lap. \u2018I am disappointed, obviously,\u2019 said the 2009 world champion. \u2018In front of your home crowd you want to put on a good show and I wasn\u2019t able to do that after a turn-three incident and that is a shame.\u2019 Button started 18th on the grid, as McLaren-Honda continue to struggle for speed and reliability, and was ensnared in a collision involving the two Lotus cars.\n@highlight\nJenson Button's 16th British Grand Prix lasted less than 20 seconds\n@highlight\nButton's\u00a0miserable\u00a0luck at the race continued in a pile up at turn three\n@highlight\nIt is the first time since 2002 that Button has failed to finish three races\nQuery: But it was not total doom and gloom at @placeholder, with Alonso scoring his first point of the season.\n\nOptions : A. Honda\nB. British Grand Prix\nC. Jenson Button\nD. Button\nE. McLaren\nF. Lotus\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The passage focuses on Jenson Button\u2019s poor performance at the British Grand Prix while driving for the McLaren-Honda team. The query sentence supplies a contrasting positive note (Alonso scoring a point) that logically applies to Button\u2019s team rather than to any individual driver, the race itself, or a rival constructor. Among the listed options, only \u201cMcLaren\u201d produces a grammatically and contextually coherent sentence (\u201c\u2026 at McLaren, with Alonso scoring his first point of the season\u201d). All other choices yield nonsensical or semantically mismatched results.\n\nThus the placeholder is filled by the text of option E.\n\n\\boxed{McLaren}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 451, "output_tokens": 127, "total_tokens": 578}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00088125, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_9693", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Marking one of England\u2019s most stunning military victories always takes something special. The Battle of Agincourt, where Henry V\u2019s outnumbered army defeated the French against the odds, got just that at a rousing service to commemorate its 600th anniversary yesterday. Henry\u2019s sword, normally kept safely in a museum, was back in the thick of the action, solemnly carried through Westminster Abbey at the start before being placed on the High Altar. Later came high drama as an armour-clad thespian, his forehead spattered with stage-blood, delivered the English king\u2019s inspiring \u2018We few, we happy few, we band of brothers\u2019 speech from Shakespeare\u2019s Henry the Fifth, the play which immortalised the battle.\n@highlight\nCommemoration took place in central London in remembrance of clash\n@highlight\nBattle took place in a farmer's field in northern France on October 25, 1415\n@highlight\nSmall band of English and Welsh archers beat vast French 